BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20210404T171500
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20210404T174500
DTSTAMP:20261004T164458Z
UID:7smpmlv1pj58uotfn7shoac3hc@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Chicago:20210404T171500
CREATED:20210403T191642Z
DESCRIPTION:<b>What you did well:</b><br>As always\, super good at doing in
  record time ! Keep it up.<br><b><br></b><br><b>What we worked on and what 
 to practice:</b><br><br><b>Alignments: </b>3 basic alignments: Arrow Line\,
  Barrel of the Gun\, Final Position<br><b>Keeping the ¨T¨ </b>- or what I s
 ometimes call ¨Balance¨ - You´re always keeping the balance front/back\, to
 wards target/away from target - revolving around an imaginary pole running 
 from the top of your head into the ground.<br><br><b>at Set </b>-&nbsp\;<br
 >o #1 Arrow Line : maintained throughout the shot :<br>o Draw wrist straigh
 t in line with arrow in two planes - from your view and from the camera vie
 w\,&nbsp\;<br>o Draw shoulder level with bow shoulder throughout<br>o Set p
 osture&nbsp\;<br>o Fix head\, and maintain throughout - quads\, glutes\, co
 re tight\, knees locked<br><br><b>at Top of Set Up</b> -&nbsp\;<br>o Draw h
 and should be at about mouth height<br><b>to Bottom of Set Up -</b>&nbsp\;<
 br>o Draw hand comes down and in to between bow shoulder and neck at should
 er height<br>o #2 Set Barrel of the Gun (grip\, bow arm\, bow shoulder\, ba
 ck shoulder)<br><br><b>Draw to Load</b>&nbsp\;<br>o Use angular motion by m
 oving LAN2 directly behind you (towards your parked car) resulting in draw 
 scapula moving closer and over your spine<br><br>Keep <b>bow</b> level (not
  pointing to the sky) and vertical (not canted) throughout\; it moves in a 
 straight line up and comes back down to Aim - not off to the side or in an 
 arc.<br><br><b>Expand/Aim&nbsp\;</b><br>o Visual focus: On aiming<br>o Ment
 al focus: Think of where you want to end up - at Final Position\, which is 
 a result of continued internal back compression and chest expansion (bow wr
 ist\, bow arm\, bow shoulder\, upper back muscles\, draw shoulder\, to draw
  elbow) (all invisible internal movements)<br><br><b>Release&nbsp\;</b><br>
 o result of 95% back tension<br>o String release synchronized with flicking
  bow hand down\, keeping V and thumb pointing toward target and index finge
 r flicks down to point at ground\, other three fingers still curled in on t
 hemselves.<br><br><b>Follow-through:</b>&nbsp\;<br>o Achieve #3 Final Posit
 ion<br>o Draw hand and wrist should remain in same position as at Release\,
  not drop to shoulder\, but come around to back of neck naturally&nbsp\;<br
 >o Think of a disc with your head in the center and your draw arm on top of
  the disc coming around at Follow Through<br>o Arms stay up and drop togeth
 er after arrow hits the paper<br><br>Enough for now. I´ll see you Tuesday!
LAST-MODIFIED:20210511T185751Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Jake
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
