CREATED:20230125T012039Z
DESCRIPTION:<b><i>This class has been canceled due to cold temperatures and
  wind chill forecasted at &lt\; 50F\, Also fewer than 4 people registered f
 or the class\, which is the minimum required to hold the class. This happen
 s from time to time. From our experience\, you will enjoy your time at arch
 ery more when the temperature and wind conditions are more favorable. Pleas
 e register or email Coach Racae with a substitute time\, or request a refun
 d.</i></b><br><br>REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to adult\, juniors 8+\, and pa
 rents! Please read all the info below and in the registration and waivers.<
 br><br>More information\, registration forms and waivers are available at <
 a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com"><u><u><u><u>www.archerytraini
 ngcenter.com</u></u></u></u></a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE of these f
 orms:<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeciOgkyuKTLZ5_Z
 aWCEyQKYSX1fWGpP5qakhT6OuAc6jJ_FQ/viewform"><u>2023 Outdoor 1: First-time C
 lass for Adults</u></a>  OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1
 FAIpQLSc_bYEFoE4oXkcm0T6fZK99fu_q6lL8wZGClXyfa1GZbahh-g/viewform"><u>2023 O
 utdoor 1: First-time Class for Juniors and Parents</u></a><br><br>Sign up f
 or just ONE Outdoor 1 class\, because most people graduate out of this clas
 s into Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br><br>Your name will be added bel
 ow and your place reserved on a first registered and paid basis and after w
 e receive 3 things:  <br><b>2023 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM   +  MEMBERSHI
 P AND WAIVERS PACKET +   FEE</b><b><br></b><u></u><br><u></u><b>USA Archery
  Level 4 NTS Coach Racae Meyer</b><b><br></b><br><b>Registered archers </b>
 at 9m on 40-cm target face unless otherwise noted:<u></u><br><u></u><br><b>
 Target Assignments:</b><br> <br>4A. <br>4B. <br><br>5A. <br>5B. <br><br>6A.
  <b>Greg Q.\, </b>16 - pd<br>6B. <br><br>7A. <br>7B. <br><br>8A. <br>8B. <b
 r><br>9A. <br>9B. <br><br>10A. <br>10B.<br><br>Space will be limited to 10-
 15 archers per session depending on the number of family groups in attendan
 ce or in accordance with CDC Guidelines. <br>Each person will have a target
  stand\, except after 10 people have registered\, members may be assigned t
 o share a target stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will b
 e allowed on the field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae. <br
 >Parents of juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator. <
 br>Parents of juniors 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with
  their child for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ pare
 nt) is accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-time Class. <br><br>We will acce
 pt a limited number of kids under 12 into the program each semester\, depen
 ding on the total  number of archers in all the classes. If you join before
  the limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the progra
 m and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2. If y
 ou are under 12\, registered and paid after the cut off\, your fee will be 
 returned to you. <br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three ti
 mes before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make 
 it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows. <br>Adults 
 don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessor
 ies packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for 
 Outdoor 2. ($18) Please pay for this at the field\, as our stock fluctuates
  because of dealer supply fluctuations<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and s
 tring loop)\, optional but really needed to practice form\, warm up before 
 classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will b
 e posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not r
 ecognize your final score\, because it will have been averaged by taking yo
 ur recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrows yo
 u shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a f
 ull round score. After the last first-time class each weekend\, final score
 s may also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more info
 rmation before your next class.
