 ld need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their child for greater safety.<
 br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into each Outdoor
  1: First-time Class. <br><br>We will accept a limited number of kids under
  12 into the program each semester\, depending on the total  number of arch
 ers in all the classes. If you join before the limit is reached\, and are y
 ounger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take other Outdoor 1 classe
 s as needed and later join Outdoor 2. If you are under 12\, registered and 
 paid after the cut off\, your fee will be returned to you. <br><br>Juniors 
 may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying to get into
  Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on averag
 e about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows. <br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to gra
 duate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\
 , fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($18) Please pay for t
 his at the field\, as our stock fluctuates because of dealer supply fluctua
 tions<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but really
  needed to practice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of
  each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a 
 complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, becau
 se it will have been averaged by taking your recorded score from your score
 card\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, 
 and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round score. After the last f
 irst-time class each weekend\, final scores may also be sent to all Outdoor
  1 participants in an email with more information before your next class.
