UID:756qfpt673tgka0nlukv43ra9o@google.com
CREATED:20210613T054636Z
DESCRIPTION:Registered Archers:<br>Once you are shooting at 20m\, your goal
  is to get to the next distance (+10m) by shooting 320 pts at your present 
 distance on a 122-cm target in one round of 36 arrows until you reach your 
 tournament distance as listed here:<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbs
 p\; &nbsp\; Masters: (50+) 60m&nbsp\;<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &n
 bsp\; &nbsp\; Seniors (21-50+) 70m<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp
 \; &nbsp\; Juniors (18-20) 70m&nbsp\;<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &n
 bsp\; &nbsp\; Cadets (15-17) 60m&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &
 nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; Cubs (13-14) 50m&nbsp\;<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &
 nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; Bowman (10-12) 30m.<br><br>1. Nate H.\, 20m on 122-c
 m target face<br>2.<br>3. Lily R.\, 20m on 122-cm target face<br>4..<br>5.<
 br>6.<br>7.<br>8.<br>9.<br>10.<br><br>OVERVIEW:<br>These Outdoor Target Arc
 hery recreational classes prepare you to shoot at longer and longer distanc
 es until you reach your USA Archery tournament distance (see below)\, while
  learning the National Training System\, which is the most highly researche
 d biomechanical method of shooting taught out at the Olympic Training Cente
 r. You will be shooting with other archers in group sessions\, so you can a
 ll learn together and from each other.<br><br>PREREQUISITE:<br>Some archery
  experience and your own recurve archery equipment is required.<br><br>OPEN
  TO ADULTS / JUNIORS / PARENTS (with experience and own recurve archery equ
 ipment)<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the
  field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae.<br>Space will be li
 mited to a maximum of 10 archers per session or in accordance with CDC Guid
 elines.<br><br>NO DROP INS:<br>You cannot just drop in\, because the number
  of archers on the shooting line is very limited and we are observing CDC g
 uidelines with social distancing.<br><br>DATES: Start Dates: MAY 15 (Adults
 ) or JUNE 12 (Juniors 10+)<br>&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nb
 sp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;Ending Date: AUGUST 14
 <br><br>ADDRESSES:<br>OUTDOOR FIELD SOUTH: 2310 Bliss Spillar Road\, Mancha
 ca\, TX 78652<br>MAILING: Archery Training Center\, Inc.\, PO Box 93216\, A
 ustin\, TX 78709<br><br>E-MAIL:&nbsp\;<a href="mailto:archerytrainingcenter
 austin@gmail.com">archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a><br><br>PHONE/TE
 XT: 512 975 1850<br><br>CAPACITY: 10 archers per class or in accordance wit
 h CDC guidelines<br>AGES: 10 - 80+ years old (See start dates above)<br>DIS
 TANCES: 9m\, 13.5m\, 18m\, 20m-70m<br>BOWS: Recurves<br>(If you are not a r
 ecurve archer\, but would like to learn to shoot a recurve bow\, please sta
 y tuned to our Instagram for announcements of the re-opening of our in-pers
 on First-time Classes\, or register online for a few Virtual NTS Form class
 es with Coach Racae.)<br><br>EQUIPMENT:<br>These classes are for archers wh
 o have their own equipment\, consisting of at least a recurve bow\, 12 alum
 inum or carbon arrows\, armguard\, finger tab\, hip or field quiver. (If yo
 u need to change your equipment or order your own\, please contact Coach Ra
 cae at&nbsp\;<a href="mailto:archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com">archery
 trainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a>. She will specify what you´ll need and h
 elp you order it\, so you buy the correct equipment for your strength and e
 xperience.)<br><br>INSTRUCTOR / COACH:<br>USA Archery Level 2 Instructor Te
 d Aanstoos<br><br>CLASS TIMES:<br>These are the days/times that are availab
 le to you. (Additional sessions will be added in future.)<br><br>SAT: 9:00-
 10:30pm<br>WED: 9:00-10:30pm<br>Please check&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.arch
 erytrainingcenter.com/calendar">www.archerytrainingcenter.com/calendar</a>&
 nbsp\;before registering!<br><br>DAYS CLOSED:<br>The outdoor range is close
 d\, gates locked\, and targets stored away except during the above class ti
 mes.<br><br>ENROLLMENT IS ON A FIRST-RECEIVED AND PAID BASIS.<br>Complete t
 he Outdoor Target Archery Registration Form under Adults or Juniors at&nbsp
 \;<a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrainingcenter.
 com</a><br><br>ATTENDANCE RECOMMENDATIONS:<br>Recreational archers have no 
 attendance requirements\, but we would recommend attending at least twice a
  week to improve faster.<br><br>FEES:<br>All fees are payable in advance of
  the class to secure your place in the class.<br>$30/archer for each 1.5-hr
  training session OR<br>$115/mo (for 1 training session/week) OR<br>$213/mo
  (for 2 training sessions/week)<br>+ Enrollment fee: $20 (always due once p
 er semester)<br><br>WEATHER:<br>Archers need to practice in all weather\, e
 xcept when there is lightning.<br><br>REFUNDS\, CREDITS\, and SUBSTITUTIONS
 :<br>Substitutions or credits will be applied if we cancel a class due to w
 eather conditions or instructor illness or if the 24-hr notice is met.<br>T
 here are no refunds for paid classes missed during the summer\, except in t
 he case of injury\, long-term illness\, unforeseen move out of the Austin a
 rea\, or being expelled for a safety violation.<br><br>24-HR NOTICE:<br>If 
 you let us know within 24 hours of the class that you will miss the class\,
  you can substitute another class and use your fee as long as there are pla
 ces left in that class during the semester. If you notify us less than 24 h
 ours in advance of the class that you will need to cancel (except for sudde
 n illness)\, or you do a "no-show"\, you'll forfeit your fee.<br><br>ILLNES
 S or INJURY: In the case of physical injury or long-term illness\, we requi
 re a doctor's note saying that you are unable to practice archery\, and the
 n a doctor's note saying that you are again fit to return to archery\, befo
 re you will be allowed back in class or a refund/credit issued.<br><br>MEMB
 ERSHIP IN USA ARCHERY:<br>Membership in USA Archery is now REQUIRED to part
 icipate in JOAD and Adult Training.<br>You can attend 2 sessions before joi
 ning USAA\, but then we'll need to see your membership card BEFORE WE CAN H
 AND OUT ANY USA ARCHERY STAR PINS to you during Master Challenge Weeks!<br>
 If you would like to see the benefits of USAA membership:&nbsp\;<a href="ht
 tp://www.teamusa.org/USA-Archery/Membership/Membership-Benefits">http://www
 .teamusa.org/USA-Archery/Membership/Membership-Benefits</a><br>JOIN USA ARC
 HERY:&nbsp\;<a href="https://www.usarchery.org/memberships/become-a-member"
 >https://www.usarchery.org/memberships/become-a-member</a><br><br>SAFE SPOR
 TS:<br>PARENTS PLEASE NOTE: We are part of the US Olympic Committee's Safe 
 Sport program\, so we minimally require one other adult besides the instruc
 tor to be present at all times. Please plan to stay with your child or take
  turns with other parents staying whenever necessary to fulfill this requir
 ement. THANKS!<br><br>SIGN AND RETURN THESE OUTDOOR WAIVERS:<br>The followi
 ng documents and waivers will be part of your Registration and Waiver Packe
 t. You will need to sign these documents before we add your name to those s
 hooting in the class:<br>o Membership Form<br>o Safety Rules<br>o Release o
 f Liability Waiver<br>o Supervision Policy (Under 18)<br>o Medical Release<
 br>o Photo/Video Release<br>o COVID-19 Guidelines<br>o Outdoor Field Rules 
 of Participation<br><br>VACCINATIONS:<br>We do not at this time require arc
 hers to be vaccinated\, but we would like to know if you have been\, so we 
 can take it into consideration when deciding on issues such as masks and so
 cial distancing and abiding by the CDC Guidelines. All our instructors have
  been fully vaccinated of their own accord.<br><br>QUESTIONS?<br>E-mail us 
 at&nbsp\;<a href="mailto:archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com">archerytrai
 ningcenteraustin@gmail.com</a>&nbsp\;or<br>Call/Text us at 512 975 1850<br>
 <br>*NTS = National Training System (which is used for training the USA Oly
 mpic team!)<br>*JDT = Junior Dream Team (top 20 Junior archers in the USA!)
 <br>*JOAD = Junior Olympic Archery Development
