DTSTART:20220728T000000Z
DTEND:20220728T023000Z
DTSTAMP:20261004T164458Z
UID:4pgjfe9qnv44hconcb9pos9cd7@google.com
CREATED:20220519T051748Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><br><table><tbody><tr><td>July 27\, 8:00 pm E
 T</td><td><b>Targeting Optimal Performance</b></td><td>Gabriele Wulf\, Ph.D
 .</td></tr><tr><td>July 27\, 9:10 pm ET</td><td><b>Mindfulness and the Olym
 pic Archer</b></td><td>Peter Haberl\, Ed.D.</td></tr></tbody></table><u></u
 ><br><u></u>To register\, log in to your&nbsp\;<a href="http://usarchery.sp
 ort80.com/"><u><u>USA Archery member account</u></u></a>\, select Conferenc
 es on the left and click 2022 USA Archery Virtual&nbsp\;Symposium.<br><br>T
 his year’s&nbsp\;<a href="https://www.usarchery.org/coaches/virtual-symposi
 um"><u>USA Archery Virtual Symposium</u></a>&nbsp\;brings coaches\, athlete
 s\, parents\, and club leaders insights and information from world-renowned
  athletes\, coaches\, and subject matter experts. The Virtual Symposium wil
 l feature 7 sessions between July and&nbsp\;August.<br><p>This year’s sympo
 sium will take a look at evidence-based performance and coaching methods an
 d the information will be applicable to intermediate to elite athletes\, co
 aches and parents. Participants will hear from world renowned experts in ar
 chery\, coach education\, motor learning and control and sports psychology.
  Gabriele Wulf\, Ph. D. who is one of the leading experts in motor control 
 and learning will share her OPTIMAL Theory of Motor Learning. Wade Gilbert\
 , Ph.D. will share how to build trust in coaching\, and Lanny Bassham of Me
 ntal Management System will explore Parenting Champions. Dr. Peter Haberl f
 rom the U.S. Olympic and Paralympic Committee will open our minds to the be
 nefits of Mindfulness in&nbsp\;Archery.</p><p>Archery specific topics this 
 year will include Movement Analysis with National Head Coach KiSik Lee\, Fi
 eld Archery Tips and Tricks with Team USA archers Paige Pearce and Brady El
 lison\, Target Panic with Joel Turner of Shot IQ\, Selecting the Right Equi
 pment with Heather Pfeil from Lancaster Archery Academy\, and promoting and
  marketing your club with Scott Booth\, host of Raising an Archer&nbsp\;pod
 cast.</p><p>Sessions will be recorded and sent to all registered participan
 ts if you miss the live time or want to review a session. Sponsors includin
 g Black Rifle Coffee Company and Xero Shoes will be providing giveaway prod
 ucts for lucky&nbsp\;participants.</p><p>Contact USA Archery Education and 
 Training Manager Guy Krueger at&nbsp\;<a href="mailto:gkrueger@usarchery.or
 g"><u>gkrueger@usarchery.org</u></a>&nbsp\;for more&nbsp\;information.<br><
 /p><u></u></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20220708T221853Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:USA Archery Virtual Symposium - Series 4
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
