 br>10A. <b>Judy K</b>.\, adult - pd - <b>substituted 2/19</b><br>10B. <b>Ma
 ggie K</b>.\, 8\, on 60-cm target face - pd - <b>substituted 2/19</b><br><b
 r>Space will be limited to 10-15 archers per session depending on the numbe
 r of family groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC Guidelines. <br>
 Each person will have a target stand\, except after 10 people have register
 ed\, members may be assigned to share a target stand.<br>The archer and a m
 aximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field until further notice o
 r approved by Coach Racae. <br>Parents of juniors 10+ can sign up as an arc
 her or watch as a spectator. <br>Parents of juniors 8-9 years old need to r
 egister\, pay\, and shoot with their child for greater safety.<br><br>A max
 imum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-ti
 me Class. <br><br>We will accept a limited number of kids under 12 into the
  program each semester\, depending on the total  number of archers in all t
 he classes. If you join before the limit is reached\, and are younger than 
 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed 
 and later join Outdoor 2. If you are under 12\, registered and paid after t
 he cut off\, your fee will be returned to you. <br><br>Juniors may need to 
 take Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 b
 y scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pt
 s/end of 3 arrows. <br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into O
 utdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingerslin
 g)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($18) Please pay for this at the f
 ield\, as our stock fluctuates because of dealer supply fluctuations<br>fp 
 = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but really needed to p
 ractice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoo
 r 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a complete rou
 nd (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, because it will h
 ave been averaged by taking your recorded score from your scorecard\, divid
 ing by the number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then mul
 tiplying that by 30 to get a full round score. After the last first-time cl
 ass each weekend\, final scores may also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participa
