DESCRIPTION:REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to adult\, juniors 8+\, and parents!
  Please read all the info below and in the registration and waivers.<br><br
 >More information\, registration forms and waivers are available at <a href
 ="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com"><u><u><u><u>www.archerytrainingcent
 er.com</u></u></u></u></a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE of these forms:<
 br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeciOgkyuKTLZ5_ZaWCEyQ
 KYSX1fWGpP5qakhT6OuAc6jJ_FQ/viewform"><u>2023 Outdoor 1: First-time Class f
 or Adults</u></a>  OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQL
 Sc_bYEFoE4oXkcm0T6fZK99fu_q6lL8wZGClXyfa1GZbahh-g/viewform"><u>2023 Outdoor
  1: First-time Class for Juniors and Parents</u></a><br><br>Sign up for jus
 t ONE Outdoor 1 class\, because most people graduate out of this class into
  Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br><br>Your name will be added below and
  your place reserved on a first registered and paid basis and after we rece
 ive 3 things:  <br><b>2023 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM   +  MEMBERSHIP AND 
 WAIVERS PACKET +   FEE</b><b><br></b><u></u><br><u></u><b>USA Archery Level
  4 NTS Coach Racae Meyer</b><b><br></b><br><b>Registered archers </b>at 9m 
 on 40-cm target face unless otherwise noted:<u></u><br><u></u><br><b>Target
  Assignments:</b><br> <br>4A. <br>4B. <br><br>5A. <br>5B. <br><br>6A. <b>Ke
 vin C</b>.\, adult - pd - <b> 69 pts</b> -&gt\; Outdoor 2<br>6B. <br><br>7A
 . <b>Byron C.</b>\, adult - pd - <b>90 pts </b>-&gt\; Outdoor 2<br>7B. <br>
 <br>8A. <b>Constance W.\, </b>adult - pd - <b>34 pts </b>-&gt\; Outdoor 2<b
 r>8B. <br><br>9A. <b>Gabrielle W.\, </b>14<b> - </b>pd - <b> 59 pts </b>-&g
 t\; Outdoor 2<br>9B. <br><br>10A. <b>Liam W.\, </b>10\, on 60-cm target fac
 e - pd - <b>91 pts </b>-&gt\; Outdoor 2<br>10B.<br><br>Space will be limite
 d to 10-15 archers per session depending on the number of family groups in 
 attendance or in accordance with CDC Guidelines. <br>Each person will have 
 a target stand\, except after 10 people have registered\, members may be as
 signed to share a target stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectato
 r will be allowed on the field until further notice or approved by Coach Ra
 cae. <br>Parents of juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a spec
 tator. <br>Parents of juniors 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and sh
 oot with their child for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old
  (+ parent) is accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-time Class. <br><br>We w
 ill accept a limited number of kids under 12 into the program each semester
 \, depending on the total  number of archers in all the classes. If you joi
 n before the limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in th
 e program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor
  2. If you are under 12\, registered and paid after the cut off\, your fee 
 will be returned to you. <br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or 
 three times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´
 ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows. <br
 >Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = 
 accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be nee
 ded for Outdoor 2. ($18) Please pay for this at the field\, as our stock fl
 uctuates because of dealer supply fluctuations<br>fp = form pack (stretchba
 nd and string loop)\, optional but really needed to practice form\, warm up
  before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your score
 s will be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you m
 ay not recognize your final score\, because it will have been averaged by t
 aking your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the number of a
 rrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to
  get a full round score. After the last first-time class each weekend\, fin
 al scores may also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with m
 ore information before your next class.
