DESCRIPTION:REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to adult\, juniors 8+\, and parents!
  Please read all the info below and in the registration and waivers.<br><br
 >More information\, registration forms and waivers are available at <a href
 ="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com"><u><u><u>www.archerytrainingcenter.
 com</u></u></u></a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE of these forms:<br><a h
 ref="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeciOgkyuKTLZ5_ZaWCEyQKYSX1fW
 GpP5qakhT6OuAc6jJ_FQ/viewform">2023 Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Adults<
 /a>  OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSc_bYEFoE4oXkc
 m0T6fZK99fu_q6lL8wZGClXyfa1GZbahh-g/viewform">2023 Outdoor 1: First-time Cl
 ass for Juniors and Parents</a><br><br>Sign up for just ONE Outdoor 1 class
 \, because most people graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after the 
 first lesson.<br><br>Your name will be added below and your place reserved 
 on a first registered and paid basis and after we receive 3 things:  <br><b
 >2023 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM   +  MEMBERSHIP AND WAIVERS PACKET +   FE
 E</b><b><br></b><u></u><br><b>USA Archery Level 3 NTS Coach Lindsay Rerecic
 h</b><br><b>See </b><a href="https://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/who-we-a
 re"><u>https://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/who-we-are</u></a><b><br></b><
 br><b>Registered archers </b>at 9m on 40-cm target face unless otherwise no
 ted:<u></u><br><u></u><br><b>Target Assignments:</b><br><u></u><b><br></b>5
 A. <b>Rich I.\, </b>adult\, <b>USAA - </b>pd - <b>106 pts -&gt\; Outdoor 2<
 /b><br>5B.<br><br>6A. <b>Jeremy P.\, </b>adult - pd - <b>92 pts -&gt\; Outd
 oor 2</b><br>6B.<br><br>7A. <b>Haneen A.\, </b>adult - pd - <b>90 pts -&gt\
 ; Outdoor 2</b><br>7B.<br><br>8A.  <b>Jackie R.\, </b>16 - pd <b>-&gt\; Out
 door 1 </b><br>8B.<br><br>9A.  <b>Maddie M.\, </b>11 - pd - <b>84 pts -</b>
 &gt\; <b>Outdoor 2 (substituted for 4/8)</b><br>9B.<br><br>10A.<br>10B.<br>
 <br>Space will be limited to 10-15 archers per session depending on the num
 ber of family groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC Guidelines. <b
 r>Each person will have a target stand\, except after 10 people have regist
 ered\, members may be assigned to share a target stand.<br>The archer and a
  maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field until further notice
  or approved by Coach Racae. <br>Parents of juniors 10+ can sign up as an a
 rcher or watch as a spectator. <br>Parents of juniors 8-9 years old need to
  register\, pay\, and shoot with their child for greater safety.<br><br>A m
 aximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-
 time Class. <br><br>We will accept a limited number of kids under 12 into t
 he program each semester\, depending on the total  number of archers in all
  the classes. If you join before the limit is reached\, and are younger tha
 n 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as neede
 d and later join Outdoor 2. If you are under 12\, registered and paid after
  the cut off\, your fee will be returned to you. <br><br>Juniors may need t
 o take Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2
  by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 
 pts/end of 3 arrows. <br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into
  Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersl
 ing)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($18) Please pay for this at the
  field\, as our stock fluctuates because of dealer supply fluctuations<br>f
 p = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but really needed to
  practice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outd
 oor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a complete r
 ound (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, because it will
  have been averaged by taking your recorded score from your scorecard\, div
 iding by the number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then m
 ultiplying that by 30 to get a full round score. After the last first-time 
 class each weekend\, final scores may also be sent to all Outdoor 1 partici
 pants in an email with more information before your next class.
