DESCRIPTION:REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to adult\, juniors 8+\, and parents!
  Please read all the info below and in the registration and waivers.<br><br
 >More information\, registration forms and waivers are available at <a href
 ="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com"><u><u><u><u>www.archerytrainingcent
 er.com</u></u></u></u></a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE of these forms:<
 br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeciOgkyuKTLZ5_ZaWCEyQ
 KYSX1fWGpP5qakhT6OuAc6jJ_FQ/viewform"><u>2023 Outdoor 1: First-time Class f
 or Adults</u></a>  OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQL
 Sc_bYEFoE4oXkcm0T6fZK99fu_q6lL8wZGClXyfa1GZbahh-g/viewform"><u>2023 Outdoor
  1: First-time Class for Juniors and Parents</u></a><br><br>Sign up for jus
 t ONE Outdoor 1 class\, because most people graduate out of this class into
  Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br><br>Your name will be added below and
  your place reserved on a first registered and paid basis and after we rece
 ive 3 things:  <br><b>2023 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM   +  MEMBERSHIP AND 
 WAIVERS PACKET +   FEE</b><b><br></b><u></u><br><u></u><b>USA Archery Level
  4 NTS Coach Racae Meyer</b><b><br></b><br><b>Registered archers </b>at 9m 
 on 40-cm target face unless otherwise noted:<u></u><br><u></u><br><b>Target
  Assignments:</b><br><br>5. <b>Victor C.\, </b>adult - pd - substituted for
  5/14<b> - 97 pts -&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br><br>6. <b>Glenda C.\, </b>adult -
  pd - substituted for 5/14<b> </b>-&gt\; <b>Outdoor 2</b><b><br></b><br>7. 
 <b>Alejandro C.\, </b>adult - pd - <b>140 pts -&gt\; Outdoor 2<br></b><br>8
 . <b>Aaron C.\, </b>adult - pd - substituted for 5/14 <b>- 54 pts -&gt\; Ou
 tdoor 2</b><br><br>9. <b>Jonathan W.\, </b>adult - pd - <b>? pts</b> - <b>O
 utdoor 2 </b><br><br>10. <b>Joseph-Junen F</b>.\, 12\, on 60-cm target face
  - pd - <b>substituted for 5/7 -177 pts -&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br><br>Space w
 ill be limited to 10-15 archers per session depending on the number of fami
 ly groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC Guidelines. <br>Each pers
 on will have a target stand\, except after 10 people have registered\, memb
 ers may be assigned to share a target stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of
  one spectator will be allowed on the field until further notice or approve
 d by Coach Racae. <br>Parents of juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or wa
 tch as a spectator. <br>Parents of juniors 8-9 years old need to register\,
  pay\, and shoot with their child for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of o
 ne 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-time Class.
  <br><br>We will accept a limited number of kids under 12 into the program 
 each semester\, depending on the total  number of archers in all the classe
 s. If you join before the limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´
 ll stay in the program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later
  join Outdoor 2. If you are under 12\, registered and paid after the cut of
 f\, your fee will be returned to you. <br><br>Juniors may need to take Outd
 oor 1 two or three times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring
  50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 
 3 arrows. <br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.
 <br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, whic
 h will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($18) Please pay for this at the field\, as
  our stock fluctuates because of dealer supply fluctuations<br>fp = form pa
 ck (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but really needed to practice f
 orm\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class
 \, your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 ar
 rows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, because it will have been 
 averaged by taking your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by th
 e number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying 
 that by 30 to get a full round score. After the last first-time class each 
 weekend\, final scores may also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an
  email with more information before your next class.
