DESCRIPTION:REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to adult\, juniors 8+\, and parents!
  Please read all the info below and in the registration and waivers.<br><br
 >More information\, registration forms and waivers are available at <a href
 ="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com"><u><u><u><u>www.archerytrainingcent
 er.com</u></u></u></u></a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE of these forms:<
 br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeciOgkyuKTLZ5_ZaWCEyQ
 KYSX1fWGpP5qakhT6OuAc6jJ_FQ/viewform"><u>2023 Outdoor 1: First-time Class f
 or Adults</u></a>  OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQL
 Sc_bYEFoE4oXkcm0T6fZK99fu_q6lL8wZGClXyfa1GZbahh-g/viewform"><u>2023 Outdoor
  1: First-time Class for Juniors and Parents</u></a><br><br>Sign up for jus
 t ONE Outdoor 1 class\, because most people graduate out of this class into
  Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br><br>Your name will be added below and
  your place reserved on a first registered and paid basis and after we rece
 ive 3 things:  <br><b>2023 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM   +  MEMBERSHIP AND 
 WAIVERS PACKET +   FEE</b><b><br></b><u></u><br><u></u><b>USA Archery Level
  4 NTS Coach Racae Meyer</b><b><br></b><br><b>Registered archers </b>at 9m 
 on 40-cm target face unless otherwise noted:<u></u><br><u></u><br><b>Target
  Assignments:</b><br> <br>4A. <b>Chris K.\, </b>adult - pd<br>4B. <br><br>5
 A. <br>5B. <br><br>6A. <br>6B. <br><br>7A. <br>7B. <br><br>8A. <br>8B. <br>
 <br>9A. <br>9B. <br><br>10A. <br>10B.<br><br>Space will be limited to 10-15
  archers per session depending on the number of family groups in attendance
  or in accordance with CDC Guidelines. <br>Each person will have a target s
 tand\, except after 10 people have registered\, members may be assigned to 
 share a target stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be 
 allowed on the field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae. <br>P
 arents of juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator. <br
 >Parents of juniors 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with t
 heir child for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent
 ) is accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-time Class. <br><br>We will accept
  a limited number of kids under 12 into the program each semester\, dependi
 ng on the total  number of archers in all the classes. If you join before t
 he limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program 
 and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2. If you
  are under 12\, registered and paid after the cut off\, your fee will be re
 turned to you. <br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three time
 s before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it
  as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows. <br>Adults do
 n´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessorie
 s packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for Ou
 tdoor 2. ($18) Please pay for this at the field\, as our stock fluctuates b
 ecause of dealer supply fluctuations<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and str
 ing loop)\, optional but really needed to practice form\, warm up before cl
 asses ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be 
 posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not rec
 ognize your final score\, because it will have been averaged by taking your
  recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrows you 
 shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a ful
 l round score. After the last first-time class each weekend\, final scores 
 may also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more inform
 ation before your next class.
