 KYSX1fWGpP5qakhT6OuAc6jJ_FQ/viewform"><u>2023 Outdoor 1: First-time Class f
 or Adults</u></a>  OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQL
 Sc_bYEFoE4oXkcm0T6fZK99fu_q6lL8wZGClXyfa1GZbahh-g/viewform"><u>2023 Outdoor
  1: First-time Class for Juniors and Parents</u></a><br><br>Sign up for jus
 t ONE Outdoor 1 class\, because most people graduate out of this class into
  Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br><br>Your name will be added below and
  your place reserved on a first registered and paid basis and after we rece
 ive 3 things:  <br><b>2023 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM   +  MEMBERSHIP AND 
 WAIVERS PACKET +   FEE</b><b><br></b><u></u><br><u></u><b>USA Archery Level
  4 NTS Coach Racae Meyer</b><b><br></b><br><b>Registered archers </b>at 9m 
 on 40-cm target face unless otherwise noted:<u></u><br><u></u><br><b>Target
  Assignments:</b><br> <br>4A. <br>4B. <br><br>5A. <br>5B. <br><br>6A. <br>6
 B. <br><br>7A. <br>7B. <br><br>8A. <br>8B. <br><br>9A. <br>9B. <br><br>10A.
  <br>10B.<br><br>Space will be limited to 10-15 archers per session dependi
 ng on the number of family groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC G
 uidelines. <br>Each person will have a target stand\, except after 10 peopl
 e have registered\, members may be assigned to share a target stand.<br>The
  archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field until f
 urther notice or approved by Coach Racae. <br>Parents of juniors 10+ can si
 gn up as an archer or watch as a spectator. <br>Parents of juniors 8-9 year
 s old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their child for greater safet
 y.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into each Outd
 oor 1: First-time Class. <br><br>We will accept a limited number of kids un
 der 12 into the program each semester\, depending on the total  number of a
 rchers in all the classes. If you join before the limit is reached\, and ar
 e younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take other Outdoor 1 cla
 sses as needed and later join Outdoor 2. If you are under 12\, registered a
 nd paid after the cut off\, your fee will be returned to you. <br><br>Junio
 rs may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying to get i
 nto Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on ave
 rage about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows. <br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to 
 graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingert
 ab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($18) Please pay fo
 r this at the field\, as our stock fluctuates because of dealer supply fluc
 tuations<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but rea
 lly needed to practice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end
  of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we did not finish
  a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, be
 cause it will have been averaged by taking your recorded score from your sc
 orecard\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average
 \, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round score. After the las
 t first-time class each weekend\, final scores may also be sent to all Outd
 oor 1 participants in an email with more information before your next class
 .
