DESCRIPTION:This class has been canceled due not meeting the registration m
 inimum of four archers. It´s Memorial Day Weekend\, and everyone is busy go
 ing other places!<br>Sign up for a future class\, and we´ll look forward to
  seeing you soon!<br><br>REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to adult\, juniors 8+\,
  and parents! Please read all the info below and in the registration and wa
 ivers.<br><br>More information\, registration forms and waivers are availab
 le at <a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com"><u><u><u><u>www.archer
 ytrainingcenter.com</u></u></u></u></a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE of 
 these forms:<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeciOgkyu
 KTLZ5_ZaWCEyQKYSX1fWGpP5qakhT6OuAc6jJ_FQ/viewform"><u>2023 Outdoor 1: First
 -time Class for Adults</u></a>  OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/form
 s/d/e/1FAIpQLSc_bYEFoE4oXkcm0T6fZK99fu_q6lL8wZGClXyfa1GZbahh-g/viewform"><u
 >2023 Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Juniors and Parents</u></a><br><br>Si
 gn up for just ONE Outdoor 1 class\, because most people graduate out of th
 is class into Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br><br>Your name will be ad
 ded below and your place reserved on a first registered and paid basis and 
 after we receive 3 things:  <br><b>2023 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM   +  ME
 MBERSHIP AND WAIVERS PACKET +   FEE</b><b><br></b><u></u><br><u></u><b>USA 
 Archery Level 4 NTS Coach Racae Meyer</b><b><br></b><br><b>Registered arche
 rs </b>at 9m on 40-cm target face unless otherwise noted:<u></u><br><u></u>
 <br><b>Target Assignments:</b><br> <br>4A. <br>4B. <br><br>5A. <b>Karen C.\
 , </b>adult\, pd - fee refunded 5/28<br>5B. <b>Kirstie L.</b>\, adult\, pd 
 - fee refunded 5/28<br><br>6A. <b>Alex C.\, </b>adult\, pd - fee refunded 6
 /7<br>6B. <br><br>7A. <br>7B. <br><br>8A. <br>8B. <br><br>9A. <br>9B. <br><
 br>10A. <br>10B.<br><br>Space will be limited to 10-15 archers per session 
 depending on the number of family groups in attendance or in accordance wit
 h CDC Guidelines. <br>Each person will have a target stand\, except after 1
 0 people have registered\, members may be assigned to share a target stand.
 <br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field 
 until further notice or approved by Coach Racae. <br>Parents of juniors 10+
  can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator. <br>Parents of juniors 8
 -9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their child for greate
 r safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into ea
 ch Outdoor 1: First-time Class. <br><br>We will accept a limited number of 
 kids under 12 into the program each semester\, depending on the total  numb
 er of archers in all the classes. If you join before the limit is reached\,
  and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take other Outdoo
 r 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2. If you are under 12\, regis
 tered and paid after the cut off\, your fee will be returned to you. <br><b
 r>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying t
 o get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score
  on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows. <br>Adults don´t need a minimum sc
 ore to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, 
 fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($18) Please
  pay for this at the field\, as our stock fluctuates because of dealer supp
 ly fluctuations<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, optional 
 but really needed to practice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At 
 the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we did not
  finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final sco
 re\, because it will have been averaged by taking your recorded score from 
 your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot to get an arrow 
 average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round score. After 
 the last first-time class each weekend\, final scores may also be sent to a
 ll Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more information before your nex
 t class.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230607T154123Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:CANCELED: OUTDOOR 1: First-time Class
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
