DESCRIPTION:REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to adult\, juniors 8+\, and parents!
  Please read all the info below and in the registration and waivers.<br><br
 >More information\, registration forms and waivers are available at <a href
 ="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com"><u><u><u>www.archerytrainingcenter.
 com</u></u></u></a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE of these forms:<br><a h
 ref="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeciOgkyuKTLZ5_ZaWCEyQKYSX1fW
 GpP5qakhT6OuAc6jJ_FQ/viewform">2023 Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Adults<
 /a>  OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSc_bYEFoE4oXkc
 m0T6fZK99fu_q6lL8wZGClXyfa1GZbahh-g/viewform">2023 Outdoor 1: First-time Cl
 ass for Juniors and Parents</a><br><br>Sign up for just ONE Outdoor 1 class
 \, because most people graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after the 
 first lesson.<br><br>Your name will be added below and your place reserved 
 on a first registered and paid basis and after we receive 3 things:  <br><b
 >2023 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM   +  MEMBERSHIP AND WAIVERS PACKET +   FE
 E</b><b><br></b><u></u><br><u></u><b>USA Archery Level 3 Coach Lindsay Rere
 cich</b><b><br></b><br><b>Registered archers </b>at 9m on 40-cm target face
  unless otherwise noted:<u></u><br><u></u><br><b>Target Assignments:</b><br
 ><u></u><b><br></b>5A. <b>Hunter S.\, </b>adult - pd -<b>69 / 47 pts -&gt\;
  Outdoor 2</b><br>5B.<br><br>6A.<br>6B.<br><br>7A. <b>Thomas B</b>.\, adult
  - pd <b>85 / 146 pts -&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br>7B. <b>Andrew B</b>.\, 9\, on
  60-cm target face - pd <b>136 / 103 - WOW!! on to Outdoor 2</b><br><br>8A.
 <br>8B.<br><br>9A.<br>9B.<br><br>10A.<br>10B.<br><br>Space will be limited 
 to 10-15 archers per session depending on the number of family groups in at
 tendance or in accordance with CDC Guidelines. <br>Each person will have a 
 target stand\, except after 10 people have registered\, members may be assi
 gned to share a target stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator 
 will be allowed on the field until further notice or approved by Coach Raca
 e. <br>Parents of juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a specta
 tor. <br>Parents of juniors 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoo
 t with their child for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (
 + parent) is accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-time Class. <br><br>We wil
 l accept a limited number of kids under 12 into the program each semester\,
  depending on the total  number of archers in all the classes. If you join 
 before the limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the 
 program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2
 . If you are under 12\, registered and paid after the cut off\, your fee wi
 ll be returned to you. <br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or th
 ree times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll
  make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows. <br>A
 dults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = ac
 cessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be neede
 d for Outdoor 2. ($18) Please pay for this at the field\, as our stock fluc
 tuates because of dealer supply fluctuations<br>fp = form pack (stretchband
  and string loop)\, optional but really needed to practice form\, warm up b
 efore classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores 
 will be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may
  not recognize your final score\, because it will have been averaged by tak
 ing your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arr
 ows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to g
 et a full round score. After the last first-time class each weekend\, final
  scores may also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with mor
 e information before your next class.
