DESCRIPTION:REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to adult\, juniors 8+\, and parents!
  Please read all the info below and in the registration and waivers.<br><br
 >More information\, registration forms and waivers are available at <a href
 ="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com"><u><u><u><u>www.archerytrainingcent
 er.com</u></u></u></u></a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE of these forms:<
 br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeciOgkyuKTLZ5_ZaWCEyQ
 KYSX1fWGpP5qakhT6OuAc6jJ_FQ/viewform"><u>2023 Outdoor 1: First-time Class f
 or Adults</u></a>  OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQL
 Sc_bYEFoE4oXkcm0T6fZK99fu_q6lL8wZGClXyfa1GZbahh-g/viewform"><u>2023 Outdoor
  1: First-time Class for Juniors and Parents</u></a><br><br>Sign up for jus
 t ONE Outdoor 1 class\, because most people graduate out of this class into
  Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br><br>Your name will be added below and
  your place reserved on a first registered and paid basis and after we rece
 ive 3 things:  <br><b>2023 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM   +  MEMBERSHIP AND 
 WAIVERS PACKET +   FEE</b><b><br></b><u></u><br><u></u><b>USA Archery Level
  4 NTS Coach Racae Meyer</b><b><br></b><br><b>Registered archers </b>at 9m 
 on 40-cm target face unless otherwise noted:<u></u><br><u></u><br><b>Target
  Assignments:</b><br> <br>4A. <b>Chris K.\, </b>adult - pd  - <b>112 pts </
 b><b>-&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br>4B. <br><br>5A. <b>Sophia P.</b>\, adult - pd 
 - <b>84 pts </b><b>-&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br>5B. <br><br>6A. <b>Aaron P.</b>\
 , adult - pd - <b>110 pts </b><b>-&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br>6B. <br><br>7A. <b
 >Dustin R</b>.\, adult - pd - <b> 105 pts </b><b>-&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br>7B
 . <br><br>8A. <b>Arianne R.\, </b> adult - pd - <b>90 pts </b><b>-&gt\; Out
 door 2</b><br>8B. <br><br>9A. <b>Elyssa W.\, </b>adult - pd - <b>140 pts </
 b><b>-&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br>9B. <br><br>10A. <b>Viviana B</b>.\, 15 - pd -
  <b> 97 pts -&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br>10B.<br><br>Space will be limited to 10
 -15 archers per session depending on the number of family groups in attenda
 nce or in accordance with CDC Guidelines. <br>Each person will have a targe
 t stand\, except after 10 people have registered\, members may be assigned 
 to share a target stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will 
 be allowed on the field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae. <b
 r>Parents of juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator. 
 <br>Parents of juniors 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot wit
 h their child for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ par
 ent) is accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-time Class. <br><br>We will acc
 ept a limited number of kids under 12 into the program each semester\, depe
 nding on the total  number of archers in all the classes. If you join befor
 e the limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the progr
 am and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2. If 
 you are under 12\, registered and paid after the cut off\, your fee will be
  returned to you. <br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three t
 imes before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make
  it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows. <br>Adults
  don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accesso
 ries packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for
  Outdoor 2. ($18) Please pay for this at the field\, as our stock fluctuate
 s because of dealer supply fluctuations<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and 
 string loop)\, optional but really needed to practice form\, warm up before
  classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will 
 be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not 
 recognize your final score\, because it will have been averaged by taking y
 our recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrows y
 ou shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a 
 full round score. After the last first-time class each weekend\, final scor
 es may also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more inf
 ormation before your next class.
