 WAIVERS PACKET +   FEE</b><b><br></b><u></u><br><u></u><b>USA Archery Level
  4 NTS Coach Racae Meyer</b><b><br></b><br><b>Registered archers </b>at 9m 
 on 40-cm target face unless otherwise noted:<u></u><br><u></u><br><b>Target
  Assignments:</b><br> <br>4A. <b>Anastasia A.\, </b>adult\, pd - <b>41 pts 
 -&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br>4B. <br><br>5A. <b>Sara N.\,</b> adult\, pd - <b>55
  pts -&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br>5B.<br><br>6A. <b>Izaak Z.\,</b> 14\, on 40-cm
  target face\, pd - <b>DNF</b><br>6B. <b>Thaddeus Z.</b>\, adult\, pd - <b>
 175 pts</b><br><br>7A.<b> Nikolas Z.\, </b>12\, on 60-cm target face - <b>4
 2 pts -&gt\; Outdoor 2 ! (special  pass)</b><br>7B. <br><br>8A. <b>Emma H.\
 ,</b> 9\, adult\, pd -<b> 53 pts -&gt\; Outdoor 2 !</b><br>8B. <br><br>9A. 
 <b>Susan H.\,</b> 9\, on 60-cm target face - <b>56 pts -&gt\; Outdoor 2 !</
 b><br>9B. <br><br>10A. <b>Lavender M</b>.\, adult\, pd - <b>96 pts -&gt\; O
 utdoor 2 !</b><br>10B. <b>Charlotte A.\, </b>8\, on 60-cm target face - <b>
 84 pts -&gt\; Outdoor 2 !</b><br><br>Space will be limited to 10-15 archers
  per session depending on the number of family groups in attendance or in a
 ccordance with CDC Guidelines. <br>Each person will have a target stand\, e
 xcept after 10 people have registered\, members may be assigned to share a 
 target stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed 
 on the field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae. <br>Parents o
 f juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator. <br>Parents
  of juniors 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their chi
 ld for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is acc
 epted into each Outdoor 1: First-time Class. <br><br>We will accept a limit
 ed number of kids under 12 into the program each semester\, depending on th
 e total  number of archers in all the classes. If you join before the limit
  is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take
  other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2. If you are und
 er 12\, registered and paid after the cut off\, your fee will be returned t
 o you. <br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times before
  qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon
  as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows. <br>Adults don´t need
  a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet
  (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2.
  ($18) Please pay for this at the field\, as our stock fluctuates because o
 f dealer supply fluctuations<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string loop
 )\, optional but really needed to practice form\, warm up before classes ($
 4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. 
 If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize y
 our final score\, because it will have been averaged by taking your recorde
 d score from your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot to 
 get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round 
 score. After the last first-time class each weekend\, final scores may also
  be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more information be
 fore your next class.
