DESCRIPTION:We unfortunately are canceling the Outdoor 1: First-time Class 
 on Sat.\, 2/18\, due to low temperatures and wind chill being forecasted at
  below 50F during the time of the class. <br>From our experience\, you'll e
 njoy your first archery class a lot more under better conditions. Please em
 ail us with a substituted date or request a refund. (There is 1 place left 
 in the Sunday 2/19 Outdoor 1 class\, if you'd like to come to that one inst
 ead\, please email Coach Racae at <a href="mailto:archerytrainingcenteraust
 in@gmail.com">archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a>)<br>We're so sorry 
 to disappoint you\, but are really looking forward to meeting and coaching 
 you\, and having a great time together soon!<br>Have a great weekend!<br><b
 r>REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to adult\, juniors 8+\, and parents! Please re
 ad all the info below and in the registration and waivers.<br><br>More info
 rmation\, registration forms and waivers are available at <a href="http://w
 ww.archerytrainingcenter.com"><u><u><u>www.archerytrainingcenter.com</u></u
 ></u></a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE of these forms:<br><a href="https
 ://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeciOgkyuKTLZ5_ZaWCEyQKYSX1fWGpP5qakhT6
 OuAc6jJ_FQ/viewform">2023 Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Adults</a>  OR<br
 ><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSc_bYEFoE4oXkcm0T6fZK99f
 u_q6lL8wZGClXyfa1GZbahh-g/viewform">2023 Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Ju
 niors and Parents</a><br><br>Sign up for just ONE Outdoor 1 class\, because
  most people graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after the first less
 on.<br><br>Your name will be added below and your place reserved on a first
  registered and paid basis and after we receive 3 things:  <br><b>2023 OUTD
 OOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM   +  MEMBERSHIP AND WAIVERS PACKET +   FEE</b><b><b
 r></b><u></u><br><u></u><b>USA Archery Level 3 Coach Lindsay Rerecich</b><b
 ><br></b><br><b>Registered archers </b>at 9m on 40-cm target face unless ot
 herwise noted:<u></u><br><u></u><br><b>Target Assignments:</b><br><u></u><b
 ><br></b>4A. <b>Robert A.\, </b>adult - giftcard - moved from 1/21 - moved 
 to 3/25<br>4B.<br><br>5A. <b>Danielle DeG.\, </b>adult - pd (substituted fo
 r 1/28) moved to 2/19<br>5B. <b>Josh I.\, </b>adult - pd (substituted for 1
 /28) moved to 2/19<br><br>6A. <b>Stevency T.\, </b>adult - pd - moved to 2/
 19<br>6B.<br><br>7A. <b>Alexiss C.\, </b>adult - pd - moved to 2/26<br>7B. 
 <b>Irvin L.\, </b>adult - pd - moved to 2/26<br><br>8A. <b>Brian F.\, </b>a
 dult - pd - (substituted for 2/11) - moved to 4/1<br>8B.<br><br>9A. <b>Alea
 h L</b>.\, adult - pd - <b>need substitute date</b><br>9B. <b>Kristen T.\, 
 </b>adult - pd - <b>need waivers</b><br><br>10A. <b>Thomas B.\, </b>adult -
  pd - (substituted for 2/11) - moved to 2/25<br>10B. <b>Andrew B.\, </b>9\,
  on 60-cm target face - pd (substituted for 2/11) - moved to 2/25<br><br>Sp
 ace will be limited to 10-15 archers per session depending on the number of
  family groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC Guidelines. <br>Each
  person will have a target stand\, except after 10 people have registered\,
  members may be assigned to share a target stand.<br>The archer and a maxim
 um of one spectator will be allowed on the field until further notice or ap
 proved by Coach Racae. <br>Parents of juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer 
 or watch as a spectator. <br>Parents of juniors 8-9 years old need to regis
 ter\, pay\, and shoot with their child for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum
  of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-time C
 lass. <br><br>We will accept a limited number of kids under 12 into the pro
 gram each semester\, depending on the total  number of archers in all the c
 lasses. If you join before the limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\,
  you´ll stay in the program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and 
 later join Outdoor 2. If you are under 12\, registered and paid after the c
 ut off\, your fee will be returned to you. <br><br>Juniors may need to take
  Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by sc
 oring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/en
 d of 3 arrows. <br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdo
 or 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\,
  which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($18) Please pay for this at the field
 \, as our stock fluctuates because of dealer supply fluctuations<br>fp = fo
 rm pack (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but really needed to pract
 ice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 
 class\, your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (
 30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, because it will have 
 been averaged by taking your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing 
 by the number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multipl
 ying that by 30 to get a full round score. After the last first-time class 
 each weekend\, final scores may also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants 
 in an email with more information before your next class.
