 ="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com"><u><u><u><u>www.archerytrainingcent
 er.com</u></u></u></u></a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE of these forms:<
 br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeciOgkyuKTLZ5_ZaWCEyQ
 KYSX1fWGpP5qakhT6OuAc6jJ_FQ/viewform"><u>2023 Outdoor 1: First-time Class f
 or Adults</u></a>  OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQL
 Sc_bYEFoE4oXkcm0T6fZK99fu_q6lL8wZGClXyfa1GZbahh-g/viewform"><u>2023 Outdoor
  1: First-time Class for Juniors and Parents</u></a><br><br>Sign up for jus
 t ONE Outdoor 1 class\, because most people graduate out of this class into
  Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br><br>Your name will be added below and
  your place reserved on a first registered and paid basis and after we rece
 ive 3 things:  <br><b>2023 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM   +  MEMBERSHIP AND 
 WAIVERS PACKET +   FEE</b><b><br></b><u></u><br><u></u><b>USA Archery Level
  4 NTS Coach Racae Meyer</b><b><br></b><br><b>Registered archers </b>at 9m 
 on 40-cm target face unless otherwise noted:<u></u><br><u></u><br><b>Target
  Assignments:</b><br> <br>4A. <br>4B. <br><br>5A. <b>Jeremy P.\, </b>adult\
 , pd - substituted for 4/2<br>5B. <br><br>6A. <b>Jennifer Q.\, </b>adult - 
 pd - substituted for 4/8\, substituted 5/13<br>6B. <b>Uzair Q.\, </b>adult 
 - pd - substituted for 4/8\, substituted 5/13<br><br>7A. <br>7B. <br><br>8A
 . <br>8B. <br><br>9A. <br>9B. <br><br>10A. <br>10B.<br><br>Space will be li
 mited to 10-15 archers per session depending on the number of family groups
  in attendance or in accordance with CDC Guidelines. <br>Each person will h
 ave a target stand\, except after 10 people have registered\, members may b
 e assigned to share a target stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spec
 tator will be allowed on the field until further notice or approved by Coac
 h Racae. <br>Parents of juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a 
 spectator. <br>Parents of juniors 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, an
 d shoot with their child for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year
 -old (+ parent) is accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-time Class. <br><br>
 We will accept a limited number of kids under 12 into the program each seme
 ster\, depending on the total  number of archers in all the classes. If you
  join before the limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay i
 n the program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Out
 door 2. If you are under 12\, registered and paid after the cut off\, your 
 fee will be returned to you. <br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two
  or three times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. 
 You´ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.
  <br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>a
 p = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be
  needed for Outdoor 2. ($18) Please pay for this at the field\, as our stoc
 k fluctuates because of dealer supply fluctuations<br>fp = form pack (stret
 chband and string loop)\, optional but really needed to practice form\, war
 m up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your s
 cores will be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, y
 ou may not recognize your final score\, because it will have been averaged 
 by taking your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the number 
 of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 3
 0 to get a full round score. After the last first-time class each weekend\,
  final scores may also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email wi
 th more information before your next class.
