DESCRIPTION:REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to adult\, juniors 8+\, and parents!
  Please read all the info below and in the registration and waivers.<br><br
 >More information\, registration forms and waivers are available at <a href
 ="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com"><u><u><u>www.archerytrainingcenter.
 com</u></u></u></a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE of these forms:<br><a h
 ref="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeciOgkyuKTLZ5_ZaWCEyQKYSX1fW
 GpP5qakhT6OuAc6jJ_FQ/viewform">2023 Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Adults<
 /a>  OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSc_bYEFoE4oXkc
 m0T6fZK99fu_q6lL8wZGClXyfa1GZbahh-g/viewform">2023 Outdoor 1: First-time Cl
 ass for Juniors and Parents</a><br><br>Sign up for just ONE Outdoor 1 class
 \, because most people graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after the 
 first lesson.<br><br>Your name will be added below and your place reserved 
 on a first registered and paid basis and after we receive 3 things:  <br><b
 >2023 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM   +  MEMBERSHIP AND WAIVERS PACKET +   FE
 E</b><b><br></b><u></u><br><u></u><b>USA Archery Level 3 Coach Lindsay Rere
 cich</b><b><br></b><br><b>Registered archers </b>at 9m on 40-cm target face
  unless otherwise noted:<u></u><br><u></u><br><b>Target Assignments:</b><br
 ><br>5A. <b>Ryan C.\, </b>adult - pd - <b>149 pts</b><br>5B. <b>Naveen N.</
 b>\, adult - pd - <b>40 pts</b><br><br>6A. <b>Laura S</b>.\, adult - pd - <
 b>90 pts</b><br>6B. <br><br>7A. <b>Lauren K.\, </b>adult - pd - <b>92 pts</
 b><br>7B. <b>Alex B.\, </b>adult - pd - <b>141 pts</b><br><br>8A. <b>Eric D
 .\, </b>adult - pd - <b>50 pts</b><br>8B. <br><br>9A. <b>Stephanie M.\, </b
 >adult - pd - <b>64 pts</b><br>9B. <b>Grace P.\, </b>15 - pd - <b>64 pts</b
 ><br><br>10B. <b>Matt N.\, </b>adult - pd - <b>98 pts</b><br>10A. <b>Kelly 
 H.\, </b>adult - pd - <b>75 pts</b><br><b><br></b><br><b>Rob A.\, </b>adult
  - substituted 2/18 due to injury off site<b><br></b><br>Space will be limi
 ted to 10-15 archers per session depending on the number of family groups i
 n attendance or in accordance with CDC Guidelines. <br>Each person will hav
 e a target stand\, except after 10 people have registered\, members may be 
 assigned to share a target stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one specta
 tor will be allowed on the field until further notice or approved by Coach 
 Racae. <br>Parents of juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a sp
 ectator. <br>Parents of juniors 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and 
 shoot with their child for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-o
 ld (+ parent) is accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-time Class. <br><br>We
  will accept a limited number of kids under 12 into the program each semest
 er\, depending on the total  number of archers in all the classes. If you j
 oin before the limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in 
 the program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdo
 or 2. If you are under 12\, registered and paid after the cut off\, your fe
 e will be returned to you. <br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two o
 r three times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. Yo
 u´ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows. <
 br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap 
 = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be n
 eeded for Outdoor 2. ($18) Please pay for this at the field\, as our stock 
 fluctuates because of dealer supply fluctuations<br>fp = form pack (stretch
 band and string loop)\, optional but really needed to practice form\, warm 
 up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your sco
 res will be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you
  may not recognize your final score\, because it will have been averaged by
  taking your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the number of
  arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 
 to get a full round score. After the last first-time class each weekend\, f
 inal scores may also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with
  more information before your next class.
