 r>Parents of juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator. 
 <br>Parents of juniors 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot wit
 h their child for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ par
 ent) is accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-time Class. <br><br>We will acc
 ept a limited number of kids under 12 into the program each semester\, depe
 nding on the total  number of archers in all the classes. If you join befor
 e the limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the progr
 am and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2. If 
 you are under 12\, registered and paid after the cut off\, your fee will be
  returned to you. <br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three t
 imes before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make
  it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows. <br>Adults
  don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accesso
 ries packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for
