CREATED:20230125T012039Z
DESCRIPTION:<b>This class is canceled due to temperatures and wind chill be
 ing forecasted at below 50F with high northerly winds during the time of th
 e class. From our experience\, you'll enjoy your first archery class a lot 
 more under better conditions. Please email us with a substituted date or re
 quest a refund. Sorry to disappoint you!</b><br><br>REGISTER NOW !<br><br>O
 pen to adult\, juniors 8+\, and parents! Please read all the info below and
  in the registration and waivers.<br><br>More information\, registration fo
 rms and waivers are available at <a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.
 com"><u><u><u><u>www.archerytrainingcenter.com</u></u></u></u></a>.<br><br>
 Register here using ONE of these forms:<br><a href="https://docs.google.com
 /forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeciOgkyuKTLZ5_ZaWCEyQKYSX1fWGpP5qakhT6OuAc6jJ_FQ/viewfor
 m"><u>2023 Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Adults</u></a>  OR<br><a href="h
 ttps://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSc_bYEFoE4oXkcm0T6fZK99fu_q6lL8wZGC
 lXyfa1GZbahh-g/viewform"><u>2023 Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Juniors an
 d Parents</u></a><br><br>Sign up for just ONE Outdoor 1 class\, because mos
 t people graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<
 br><br>Your name will be added below and your place reserved on a first reg
 istered and paid basis and after we receive 3 things:  <br><b>2023 OUTDOOR 
 1 REGISTRATION FORM   +  MEMBERSHIP AND WAIVERS PACKET +   FEE</b><b><br></
 b><u></u><br><u></u><b>USA Archery Level 4 NTS Coach Racae Meyer</b><b><br>
 </b><br><b>Registered archers </b>at 9m on 40-cm target face unless otherwi
 se noted:<u></u><br><u></u><br><b>Target Assignments:</b><br> <br>4A. <br>4
 B. <br><br>5A. <br>5B. <br><br>6A. <br>6B. <br><br>7A. <br>7B. <br><br>8A. 
 <br>8B. <br><br>9A. <b>William McK.\, </b>adult - pd - substituted 2/25<br>
 9B. <br><br>10A. <b>Emerie McK.\, </b>10\, on 60-cm target face - pd - subs
 tituted 2/25<br>10B.<br><br>Space will be limited to 10-15 archers per sess
 ion depending on the number of family groups in attendance or in accordance
  with CDC Guidelines. <br>Each person will have a target stand\, except aft
 er 10 people have registered\, members may be assigned to share a target st
 and.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the fi
 eld until further notice or approved by Coach Racae. <br>Parents of juniors
  10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator. <br>Parents of junio
 rs 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their child for gr
 eater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted int
 o each Outdoor 1: First-time Class. <br><br>We will accept a limited number
  of kids under 12 into the program each semester\, depending on the total  
 number of archers in all the classes. If you join before the limit is reach
 ed\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take other Ou
 tdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2. If you are under 12\, r
 egistered and paid after the cut off\, your fee will be returned to you. <b
 r><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifyi
 ng to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you s
 core on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows. <br>Adults don´t need a minimu
 m score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguar
 d\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($18) Pl
 ease pay for this at the field\, as our stock fluctuates because of dealer 
 supply fluctuations<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, optio
 nal but really needed to practice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br
 >At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we did
  not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final
  score\, because it will have been averaged by taking your recorded score f
 rom your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot to get an ar
 row average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round score. Af
 ter the last first-time class each weekend\, final scores may also be sent 
 to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more information before your
  next class.
