DESCRIPTION:REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to adult\, juniors 8+\, and parents!
  Please read all the info below and in the registration and waivers.<br><br
 >More information\, registration forms and waivers are available at <a href
 ="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com"><u><u><u><u>www.archerytrainingcent
 er.com</u></u></u></u></a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE of these forms:<
 br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeciOgkyuKTLZ5_ZaWCEyQ
 KYSX1fWGpP5qakhT6OuAc6jJ_FQ/viewform"><u>2023 Outdoor 1: First-time Class f
 or Adults</u></a>  OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQL
 Sc_bYEFoE4oXkcm0T6fZK99fu_q6lL8wZGClXyfa1GZbahh-g/viewform"><u>2023 Outdoor
  1: First-time Class for Juniors and Parents</u></a><br><br>Sign up for jus
 t ONE Outdoor 1 class\, because most people graduate out of this class into
  Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br><br>Your name will be added below and
  your place reserved on a first registered and paid basis and after we rece
 ive 3 things:  <br><b>2023 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM   +  MEMBERSHIP AND 
 WAIVERS PACKET +   FEE</b><b><br></b><u></u><br><u></u><b>USA Archery Level
  4 NTS Coach Racae Meyer</b><b><br></b><br><b>Registered archers </b>at 9m 
 on 40-cm target face unless otherwise noted:<u></u><br><u></u><br><b>Target
  Assignments:</b><br> <br>4A. <b>Carlos C.\, </b>adult - pd - <b>148 pts </
 b>-&gt\; Outdoor 2<br>4B. <br><br>5A. <b>Alicia C.\, 12?</b>\, on 60-cm tar
 get face - pd - <b>95 pts</b> -&gt\; Outdoor 2<br>5B. <br><br>6A. <b>Jackie
  R.\, </b>16 - pd - <b>70 pts </b>-&gt\; Outdoor 2<br>6B. <br><br>7A. <br>7
 B. <br><br>8A. <br>8B. <br><br>9A. <br>9B. <br><br>10A. <br>10B.<br><br>Spa
 ce will be limited to 10-15 archers per session depending on the number of 
 family groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC Guidelines. <br>Each 
 person will have a target stand\, except after 10 people have registered\, 
 members may be assigned to share a target stand.<br>The archer and a maximu
 m of one spectator will be allowed on the field until further notice or app
 roved by Coach Racae. <br>Parents of juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer o
 r watch as a spectator. <br>Parents of juniors 8-9 years old need to regist
 er\, pay\, and shoot with their child for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum 
 of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-time Cl
 ass. <br><br>We will accept a limited number of kids under 12 into the prog
 ram each semester\, depending on the total  number of archers in all the cl
 asses. If you join before the limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, 
 you´ll stay in the program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and l
 ater join Outdoor 2. If you are under 12\, registered and paid after the cu
 t off\, your fee will be returned to you. <br><br>Juniors may need to take 
 Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by sco
 ring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end
  of 3 arrows. <br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoo
 r 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, 
 which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($18) Please pay for this at the field\
 , as our stock fluctuates because of dealer supply fluctuations<br>fp = for
 m pack (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but really needed to practi
 ce form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 c
 lass\, your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (3
 0 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, because it will have b
 een averaged by taking your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing b
 y the number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiply
 ing that by 30 to get a full round score. After the last first-time class e
 ach weekend\, final scores may also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants i
 n an email with more information before your next class.
