DESCRIPTION:REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to adult\, juniors 8+\, and parents!
  Please read all the info below and in the registration and waivers.<br><br
 >More information\, registration forms and waivers are available at <a href
 ="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com"><u><u><u>www.archerytrainingcenter.
 com</u></u></u></a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE of these forms:<br><a h
 ref="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeciOgkyuKTLZ5_ZaWCEyQKYSX1fW
 GpP5qakhT6OuAc6jJ_FQ/viewform">2023 Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Adults<
 /a>  OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSc_bYEFoE4oXkc
 m0T6fZK99fu_q6lL8wZGClXyfa1GZbahh-g/viewform">2023 Outdoor 1: First-time Cl
 ass for Juniors and Parents</a><br><br>Sign up for just ONE Outdoor 1 class
 \, because most people graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after the 
 first lesson.<br><br>Your name will be added below and your place reserved 
 on a first registered and paid basis and after we receive 3 things:  <br><b
 >2023 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM   +  MEMBERSHIP AND WAIVERS PACKET +   FE
 E</b><b><br></b><u></u><br><b>USA Archery Level 3 NTS Coach Lindsay Rerecic
 h</b><br><b>See </b><a href="https://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/who-we-a
 re"><u>https://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/who-we-are</u></a><b><br></b><
 br><b>Registered archers </b>at 9m on 40-cm target face unless otherwise no
 ted:<u></u><br><u></u><br><b>Target Assignments:</b><br><u></u><b><br></b>5
 A. <b>Robert A.\, </b>adult - giftcard - moved from 1/21 - substituted for 
 2/18<br>5B. <b>Christophe R</b>.\, adult - pd<br><br>6A. <b>Spencer B</b>.\
 , adult - pd<br>6B. <b>Anisha M.</b>\, adult - pd - need waivers<br><br>7A.
  <b>Greg Q.</b>\, 16 - pd<br>7B. <b>Steven S.</b>\, adult - pd<br><br>8A. <
 b>Chandler S</b>.\, 12\, on 60-cm target face - pd<br>8B. <br><br>9A. <b>Ch
 ysawndra S</b>.\, adult - pd<br>9B. <b>Wendy S</b>.\, 9\, on 60-cm target f
 ace - pd<br><br>10A. <b>Everett S</b>.\, 9\, on 60-cm target face - pd<br>1
 0B.<br><br>Space will be limited to 10-15 archers per session depending on 
 the number of family groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC Guideli
 nes. <br>Each person will have a target stand\, except after 10 people have
  registered\, members may be assigned to share a target stand.<br>The arche
 r and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field until further
  notice or approved by Coach Racae. <br>Parents of juniors 10+ can sign up 
 as an archer or watch as a spectator. <br>Parents of juniors 8-9 years old 
 need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their child for greater safety.<br>
 <br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into each Outdoor 1:
  First-time Class. <br><br>We will accept a limited number of kids under 12
  into the program each semester\, depending on the total  number of archers
  in all the classes. If you join before the limit is reached\, and are youn
 ger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take other Outdoor 1 classes a
 s needed and later join Outdoor 2. If you are under 12\, registered and pai
 d after the cut off\, your fee will be returned to you. <br><br>Juniors may
  need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying to get into Ou
 tdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on average a
 bout 5 pts/end of 3 arrows. <br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to gradua
 te into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, f
 ingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($18) Please pay for this
  at the field\, as our stock fluctuates because of dealer supply fluctuatio
 ns<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but really ne
 eded to practice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of ea
 ch Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a com
 plete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, because 
 it will have been averaged by taking your recorded score from your scorecar
 d\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and
  then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round score. After the last firs
 t-time class each weekend\, final scores may also be sent to all Outdoor 1 
 participants in an email with more information before your next class.
