DESCRIPTION:<i>Sorry to disappoint you\, but the heat index is already 105F
  at 12:50pm today\, Mon 6/26\, and it´s only going up today and all week! J
 ust too dangerous out there.. </i><i>I´m canceling the open range\, and all
  the evening weekday classes this week.</i><br><i>Shooting really great sho
 ts with great form is reduced under these conditions\, so it is a much bett
 er use of your time\, if you spend the time working in front of your mirror
 s with your stretchbands/string loops\, and trying to understand / feel / d
 o the NTS shot cycle. </i><br><i>See you on the weekend. We´ve got two out 
 of three archer tents up\, and four really nice new dark blue pop-up tents 
 for spectators\, so it should be fine in the mornings on Saturday and Sunda
 y. I´m looking forward to seeing you then!</i><br>                         
                 <i><b>Coach Racae </b></i><br><b><br></b><br><b>REGISTER NO
 W !</b><br>This class is open to <b>adults\, juniors\, and parents</b> <b>w
 ho have taken and graduated out of Outdoor 1: First-time Class and are shoo
 ting at distances of 9m to 70m</b>. It is a mixed class of different distan
 ces. .<br><br><b>Sign up any time for as many or as few Outdoor 2-9 Classes
  as you like.</b><br><br>PLEASE NOTE: Class start and end times will shift 
 depending on daylight\, weather\, and temperature conditions. Classes requi
 re a minimum of 4 archers:<br>Jan\, Feb:   6:00 pm - 7:30 pm (in the dark\,
  depending on temperatures/chill factor)<br>Mar-May:  6:00 pm - 7:30 pm<br>
 Jun-Aug:   6:30 pm - 8:00 pm (depending on temperatures/heat index)<br>Sept
 -Dec:  6:00 pm - 7:30 pm (partially in the  dark!)<br><br><b>Register at on
 e of these links depending on your level:</b><br><a href="https://docs.goog
 le.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfeoHL9-iDkbFJnbIH2Ad1y3Z74wtnfR31CQ7PdSahRoelhGg/v
