DESCRIPTION:This class has been canceled due to low registrations\, probabl
 y because it´s Memorial Day weekend\, school´s out\, and it´s the beginning
  of summer!<br>We look forward to seeing you some other Saturday!<br><br>RE
 GISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to adult\, juniors 8+\, and parents! Please read a
 ll the info below and in the registration and waivers.<br><br>More informat
 ion\, registration forms and waivers are available at <a href="http://www.a
 rcherytrainingcenter.com"><u><u><u>www.archerytrainingcenter.com</u></u></u
 ></a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE of these forms:<br><a href="https://d
 ocs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeciOgkyuKTLZ5_ZaWCEyQKYSX1fWGpP5qakhT6OuAc
 6jJ_FQ/viewform">2023 Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Adults</a>  OR<br><a 
 href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSc_bYEFoE4oXkcm0T6fZK99fu_q6
 lL8wZGClXyfa1GZbahh-g/viewform">2023 Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Junior
 s and Parents</a><br><br>Sign up for just ONE Outdoor 1 class\, because mos
 t people graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<
 br><br>Your name will be added below and your place reserved on a first reg
 istered and paid basis and after we receive 3 things:  <br><b>2023 OUTDOOR 
 1 REGISTRATION FORM   +  MEMBERSHIP AND WAIVERS PACKET +   FEE</b><b><br></
 b><u></u><br><b>USA Archery Level 4 NTS Coach Racae Meyer and other instruc
 tors/coaches.</b><br><b>See </b><a href="https://www.archerytrainingcenter.
 com/who-we-are"><u>https://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/who-we-are</u></a>
 <b><br></b><br><b>Registered archers </b>at 9m on 40-cm target face unless 
 otherwise noted:<u></u><br><u></u><br><b>Target Assignments:</b><u></u><br>
 5A.<br>5B.<br><br>6A. <b>Alex C.\, </b>adult\, pd - need substitute date<br
 >6B.<br><br>7A. <br>7B.<br><br>8A. <br>8B.<br><br>9A.<br>9B.<br><br>10A.<br
 >10B.<br><br><b>Abby Y.\, </b>11\, on 60-cm target face\, pd - sprained ank
 le - need substitute class<br><br>Space will be limited to 10-15 archers pe
 r session depending on the number of family groups in attendance or in acco
 rdance with CDC Guidelines. <br>Each person will have a target stand\, exce
 pt after 10 people have registered\, members may be assigned to share a tar
 get stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on 
 the field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae. <br>Parents of j
 uniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator. <br>Parents of
  juniors 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their child 
 for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accept
 ed into each Outdoor 1: First-time Class. <br><br>We will accept a limited 
 number of kids under 12 into the program each semester\, depending on the t
 otal  number of archers in all the classes. If you join before the limit is
  reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take ot
 her Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2. If you are under 
 12\, registered and paid after the cut off\, your fee will be returned to y
 ou. <br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times before qu
 alifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as
  you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows. <br>Adults don´t need a 
 minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (a
 rmguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($
 18) Please pay for this at the field\, as our stock fluctuates because of d
 ealer supply fluctuations<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\,
  optional but really needed to practice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<
 br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If 
 we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your
  final score\, because it will have been averaged by taking your recorded s
 core from your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot to get
  an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round sco
 re. After the last first-time class each weekend\, final scores may also be
  sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more information befor
 e your next class.
