DESCRIPTION:Registered Archers:<br>1. Kevin B.\, 18m on 40cm target face<br
 >2. Yuhan X.\, 9m on 60-cm target face - paid<br>3.<br>4..<br>5.<br>6.<br>7
 .<br>8.<br>9.<br>10.<br><br>OVERVIEW:<br>These Outdoor Target Archery recre
 ational classes prepare you to shoot at longer and longer distances until y
 ou reach your USA Archery tournament distance (see below)\, while learning 
 the National Training System\, which is the most highly researched biomecha
 nical method of shooting taught out at the Olympic Training Center. You wil
 l be shooting with other archers in group sessions\, so you can all learn t
 ogether and from each other.<br><br>PREREQUISITE:<br>Some archery experienc
 e and your own recurve archery equipment is required.<br><br>OPEN TO ADULTS
  / JUNIORS / PARENTS (with experience and own recurve archery equipment)<br
 >The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field unt
 il further notice or approved by Coach Racae.<br>Space will be limited to a
  maximum of 10 archers per session or in accordance with CDC Guidelines.<br
 ><br>NO DROP INS:<br>You cannot just drop in\, because the number of archer
 s on the shooting line is very limited and we are observing CDC guidelines 
 with social distancing.<br><br>DATES: Start Dates: MAY 15 (Adults) or JUNE 
 12 (Juniors 10+)<br>&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\
 ;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;Ending Date: AUGUST 14<br><br>AD
 DRESSES:<br>OUTDOOR FIELD SOUTH: 2310 Bliss Spillar Road\, Manchaca\, TX 78
 652<br>MAILING: Archery Training Center\, Inc.\, PO Box 93216\, Austin\, TX
  78709<br><br>E-MAIL:&nbsp\;<a href="mailto:archerytrainingcenteraustin@gma
 il.com">archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a><br><br>PHONE/TEXT: 512 97
 5 1850<br><br>CAPACITY: 10 archers per class or in accordance with CDC guid
 elines<br>AGES: 10 - 80+ years old (See start dates above)<br>DISTANCES: 9m
 \, 13.5m\, 18m\, 20m-70m<br>BOWS: Recurves<br>(If you are not a recurve arc
 her\, but would like to learn to shoot a recurve bow\, please stay tuned to
  our Instagram for announcements of the re-opening of our in-person First-t
 ime Classes\, or register online for a few Virtual NTS Form classes with Co
 ach Racae.)<br><br>EQUIPMENT:<br>These classes are for archers who have the
 ir own equipment\, consisting of at least a recurve bow\, 12 aluminum or ca
 rbon arrows\, armguard\, finger tab\, hip or field quiver. (If you need to 
 change your equipment or order your own\, please contact Coach Racae at&nbs
 p\;<a href="mailto:archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com">archerytrainingce
 nteraustin@gmail.com</a>. She will specify what you´ll need and help you or
 der it\, so you buy the correct equipment for your strength and experience.
 )<br><br>INSTRUCTOR / COACH:<br>USA Archery Level 2 Instructor Ted Aanstoos
 <br><br>CLASS TIMES:<br>These are the days/times that are available to you.
  (Additional sessions will be added in future.)<br><br>SAT: 9:00-10:30pm<br
 >WED: 9:00-10:30pm<br>Please check&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.archerytrainin
 gcenter.com/calendar">www.archerytrainingcenter.com/calendar</a>&nbsp\;befo
 re registering!<br><br>DAYS CLOSED:<br>The outdoor range is closed\, gates 
 locked\, and targets stored away except during the above class times.<br><b
 r>ENROLLMENT IS ON A FIRST-RECEIVED AND PAID BASIS.<br>Complete the Outdoor
  Target Archery Registration Form under Adults or Juniors at&nbsp\;<a href=
 "http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrainingcenter.com</a><br
 ><br>ATTENDANCE RECOMMENDATIONS:<br>Recreational archers have no attendance
  requirements\, but we would recommend attending at least twice a week to i
 mprove faster.<br><br>FEES:<br>All fees are payable in advance of the class
  to secure your place in the class.<br>$30/archer for each 1.5-hr training 
 session OR<br>$115/mo (for 1 training session/week) OR<br>$213/mo (for 2 tr
 aining sessions/week)<br>+ Enrollment fee: $20 (always due once per semeste
 r)<br><br>WEATHER:<br>Archers need to practice in all weather\, except when
  there is lightning.<br><br>REFUNDS\, CREDITS\, and SUBSTITUTIONS:<br>Subst
 itutions or credits will be applied if we cancel a class due to weather con
 ditions or instructor illness or if the 24-hr notice is met.<br>There are n
 o refunds for paid classes missed during the summer\, except in the case of
  injury\, long-term illness\, unforeseen move out of the Austin area\, or b
 eing expelled for a safety violation.<br><br>24-HR NOTICE:<br>If you let us
  know within 24 hours of the class that you will miss the class\, you can s
 ubstitute another class and use your fee as long as there are places left i
 n that class during the semester. If you notify us less than 24 hours in ad
 vance of the class that you will need to cancel (except for sudden illness)
 \, or you do a "no-show"\, you'll forfeit your fee.<br><br>ILLNESS or INJUR
 Y: In the case of physical injury or long-term illness\, we require a docto
 r's note saying that you are unable to practice archery\, and then a doctor
 's note saying that you are again fit to return to archery\, before you wil
 l be allowed back in class or a refund/credit issued.<br><br>MEMBERSHIP IN 
 USA ARCHERY:<br>Membership in USA Archery is now REQUIRED to participate in
  JOAD and Adult Training.<br>You can attend 2 sessions before joining USAA\
 , but then we'll need to see your membership card BEFORE WE CAN HAND OUT AN
 Y USA ARCHERY STAR PINS to you during Master Challenge Weeks!<br>If you wou
 ld like to see the benefits of USAA membership:&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.t
 eamusa.org/USA-Archery/Membership/Membership-Benefits">http://www.teamusa.o
 rg/USA-Archery/Membership/Membership-Benefits</a><br>JOIN USA ARCHERY:&nbsp
 \;<a href="https://www.usarchery.org/memberships/become-a-member">https://w
 ww.usarchery.org/memberships/become-a-member</a><br><br>SAFE SPORTS:<br>PAR
 ENTS PLEASE NOTE: We are part of the US Olympic Committee's Safe Sport prog
 ram\, so we minimally require one other adult besides the instructor to be 
 present at all times. Please plan to stay with your child or take turns wit
 h other parents staying whenever necessary to fulfill this requirement. THA
 NKS!<br><br>SIGN AND RETURN THESE OUTDOOR WAIVERS:<br>The following documen
 ts and waivers will be part of your Registration and Waiver Packet. You wil
 l need to sign these documents before we add your name to those shooting in
  the class:<br>o Membership Form<br>o Safety Rules<br>o Release of Liabilit
 y Waiver<br>o Supervision Policy (Under 18)<br>o Medical Release<br>o Photo
 /Video Release<br>o COVID-19 Guidelines<br>o Outdoor Field Rules of Partici
 pation<br><br>VACCINATIONS:<br>We do not at this time require archers to be
  vaccinated\, but we would like to know if you have been\, so we can take i
 t into consideration when deciding on issues such as masks and social dista
 ncing and abiding by the CDC Guidelines. All our instructors have been full
 y vaccinated of their own accord.<br><br>QUESTIONS?<br>E-mail us at&nbsp\;<
 a href="mailto:archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com">archerytrainingcenter
 austin@gmail.com</a>&nbsp\;or<br>Call/Text us at 512 975 1850<br><br>*NTS =
  National Training System (which is used for training the USA Olympic team!
 )<br>*JDT = Junior Dream Team (top 20 Junior archers in the USA!)<br>*JOAD 
 = Junior Olympic Archery Development
