BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20190921T163000Z
DTEND:20190921T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20261004T164458Z
UID:1k1ooli0mhk0gu0vcs4ob2bbl3@google.com
CREATED:20190912T203905Z
DESCRIPTION:THANKS SO MUCH for giving us the opportunity to share your spec
 ial day!\nIt helps our Junior Olympic Archery program (JOAD) a lot when you
  introduce your friends to the fun of Olympic target archery!\n\nWHAT AGES?
 \n10 years old and above. (We do adult birthday parties\, too!)\nChildren n
 ot participating must be supervised by an adult from your party.\n\nHOW MAN
 Y ARCHERS?\nMax. of 10 archers. \n\nWHAT DAYS and TIMES ARE AVAILABLE?\nFir
 st check www.archerytrainingcenter.com/calendar to make sure another party 
 or individuals have not already booked the time you would like to come.\n\n
 SAT/SUN: 11:30am-2:00pm \n(You will be occupying the time slot usually rese
 rved for the Sat/Sun Indoor 1: First-time Class) Book early!\nT/W/F: 2:30-5
 :00pm \n\nWHAT ARE THE MINIMUM FEES to reserve the range for my group?\n$28
 0 on weekends (11:30am-2:00pm)\n$250 on T/W/F (2:30-5:00pm)\n\nHOW LONG ARE
  THE BIRTHDAY PARTIES?\nBirthday parties are usually about 2-1/2 hours. Ple
 ase arrive at least 15 min. before the party begins.\n\nHOW FAR IN ADVANCE 
 SHOULD I BOOK?\nAt least 2-3 weeks in advance. \n\nHOW DO I KNOW IF MY BIRT
 HDAY PARTY IS BOOKED?\nLook at the Calendar at www.archerytrainingcenter.co
 m a few hours after you submit the form below\, to make sure your party is 
 registered on the Calendar for the day/time you wanted. (We will contact yo
 u by email to confirm before putting it up on the Calendar.)\n\nCONTACTS AN
 D WAIVERS\nEach participant (or the parent of a junior archer) will need to
  fill out and sign the Membership form\, Release of Liability Waiver\, and 
 Photo Release. The Safety Rules must also be reviewed with the junior arche
 r and signed before class. These will be emailed to the coordinator. If som
 e parents accompany the archer to the birthday party\, they can sign the fo
 rms at the range. ALL FORMS MUST BE SUBMITTED BEFORE THE ARCHER WILL BE ALL
 OWED TO ENTER THE RANGE.\n\nARRIVALS\nWe all start together. It is importan
 t for everyone to arrive 15 min. before the party begins\, so we can start 
 on time. If some people are late\, we may start 15 minutes or so late\, whi
 ch will mean less shooting for everyone. We would recommend carpooling from
  another location\, so everyone arrives on time.\n\nPARKING\nThere is limit
 ed parking for a max. of 10 cars outside our range. If you'll need more par
 king\, please carpool from another nearby public parking location (shopping
  center\, etc.).\n\nPARTY AGENDA\nYou can see photos of birthday parties on
  our Instagram.\nThe party will be an abbreviated version of the Indoor 1 F
 irst-time Class. We will enforce the safety rules\, so everyone should read
  them carefully. \nAfter everyone learns the basics\, they'll start shootin
 g. It's impossible to just "let them shoot" as soon as they arrive\, becaus
 e (besides the safety factor)\, they just wouldn't hit anything\, and would
  become very frustrated...so a basic lesson in good form is essential for t
 hem in order to enjoy shooting. \nAfter everyone shoots for a while at the 
 very large target faces\, we'll put up balloons on the wall\, and all the a
 rchers will try to hit theirs. If some balloons remain\, they can take them
  home\, or watch as the best archer of the day or the birthday boy/girl/adu
 lt tries to hit them. Everyone cheers! The balloons are always a big hit an
 d create a lot of laughter. \n\nAWARDS\nEveryone will receive a Personal Be
 st award and\, if they score and shoot 50+ pts.\, also a Qualifier Certific
 ate\, which means they are then members of USA Archery's Junior Olympic pro
 gram or Adult Training Program\, and can join the regularly scheduled class
 es (Indoor 2 classes on the Calendar). \n\nWHAT WE PROVIDE\nWe provide all 
 archery equipment\, balloons (to shoot at)\, bottled water\, napkins. \nYou
  can see photos of the interior of our facility on Google. The white round 
 tables with red/blue/black chairs in the area adjacent to the archery range
  will seat 15 participants comfortably. \n\nWHAT YOU COULD BRING\nYou can b
 ring whatever other refreshments and food you like. Most bring easy-to-eat 
 cupcakes\, doughnuts\, cookies\, cake\, soft drinks\, orange juice\, etc.  
 (There are lots of photos online of archery-decorated deserts!) \nPlease al
 so remember to bring the cutlery\, plates\, cups\, etc.\, and\, of course\,
  PRESENTS!\n\nWHEN SHOULD THEY EAT?\nAFTER the shooting and archery photos\
 , otherwise there are sticky fingers on the equipment\, delays\, etc. (You 
 could set the tables while the archers are shooting.) Most prefer to do the
  archery part separately\, and go home or to a restaurant for the "cake and
  presents" part\, as there is often another archery class starting immediat
 ely after the archers finish shooting.\n\nPHOTOS\nWe will be taking photos 
 throughout the event and group shots of all the archers in front of the tar
 get wall\, when they shoot a bull´s-eye\, and at the end on the podiums. Us
 ually we post them on our Instagram and Facebook social media pages to enco
 urage others to come for a great time. If you do not want us to take photos
  of participants in your event\, each participant should refrain from signi
 ng the Photo/Video Release Waiver. Most of the time everyone signs the waiv
 ers\, but it is totally up to each of you whether you do so or not.\n\nCLEA
 N UP\nThere will be trashcans available for your use. Please clean and wipe
  off the tables and pick up any items or food from the range that need to b
 e thrown away\, unless the coach instructs otherwise. There may be a class 
 immediately after your party\, so we appreciate your help cleaning up!\n\nP
 ICK UP\nEvery archer is to leave the range immediately after the birthday p
 arty. Our instructor(s) may be coaching another class immediately after you
 r party\, or turning off the lights and air-conditioning\, locking the rang
 e\, and leaving the building\, so the birthday party organizer needs to mak
 e sure that if one or more of your guest junior archers has not been picked
  up immediately after the party\, you stay with them until they are picked 
 up. Please have their parents' contact numbers so you can get in touch with
  them for instructions\, if necessary.\n\nSAFE SPORTS:\nParents please note
  we are part of the US Olympic Committee's Safe Sport program\, so we minim
 ally require one other adult besides the instructor to be present at all ti
 mes. Please plan to stay with your child or take turns with other parents s
 taying whenever necessary to fulfill this requirement. THANKS!\n\nQUESTIONS
 ...?\nIf you have any questions at any time before your event\, just email 
 us at archerytrainingcenteraustin.com\, call us at 512 975 1850\, or talk w
 ith us at the archery range. \n\nYou're all going to have a great time !!!
LAST-MODIFIED:20190919T152302Z
LOCATION:10203 Old Manchaca Rd\, Austin\, TX 78748\, USA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Birthday Party ! - Karen
