 wed on the field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae. <br>Paren
 ts of juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator. <br>Par
 ents of juniors 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their
  child for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is
  accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-time Class. <br><br>We will accept a l
 imited number of kids under 12 into the program each semester\, depending o
 n the total  number of archers in all the classes. If you join before the l
 imit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and 
 take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2. If you are
  under 12\, registered and paid after the cut off\, your fee will be return
 ed to you. <br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times be
 fore qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as 
 soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows. <br>Adults don´t 
 need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories pa
 cket (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoo
 r 2. ($18) Please pay for this at the field\, as our stock fluctuates becau
 se of dealer supply fluctuations<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string 
 loop)\, optional but really needed to practice form\, warm up before classe
 s ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be post
 ed. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recogni
 ze your final score\, because it will have been averaged by taking your rec
 orded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot
  to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full ro
 und score. After the last first-time class each weekend\, final scores may 
 also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more informatio
 n before your next class.
