  C</b>.\, adult - pd - substituted 5/14<br>4B. <b>Victor C</b>.\, adult - p
 d - substituted 5/14<br><br>5A. <b>Aaron C</b>.\, adult - pd  - substituted
  5/14<br>5B. <br><br>6A. <b>Emery B.</b>\, 15\, pd - substituted 5/13<br><b
 r>7A. <b>Joseph-Junen F</b>.\, 12\, on 60-cm target face - pd - substituted
  5/21<br>7B. <br><br>8A. <br>8B. <br> <br>9A.<b> </b><br>9B. <br><br>10A. <
 br>10B.<br><br>Space will be limited to 10-15 archers per session depending
  on the number of family groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC Gui
 delines. <br>Each person will have a target stand\, except after 10 people 
 have registered\, members may be assigned to share a target stand.<br>The a
 rcher and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field until fur
 ther notice or approved by Coach Racae. <br>Parents of juniors 10+ can sign
  up as an archer or watch as a spectator. <br>Parents of juniors 8-9 years 
 old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their child for greater safety.
 <br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into each Outdoo
 r 1: First-time Class. <br><br>We will accept a limited number of kids unde
 r 12 into the program each semester\, depending on the total  number of arc
 hers in all the classes. If you join before the limit is reached\, and are 
 younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take other Outdoor 1 class
 es as needed and later join Outdoor 2. If you are under 12\, registered and
  paid after the cut off\, your fee will be returned to you. <br><br>Juniors
  may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying to get int
 o Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on avera
 ge about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows. <br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to gr
 aduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab
 \, fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($18) Please pay for 
 this at the field\, as our stock fluctuates because of dealer supply fluctu
 ations<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but reall
 y needed to practice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end o
 f each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a
  complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, beca
 use it will have been averaged by taking your recorded score from your scor
 ecard\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\,
  and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round score. After the last 
 first-time class each weekend\, final scores may also be sent to all Outdoo
 r 1 participants in an email with more information before your next class.
