DESCRIPTION:This class is for archers who would like to learn how to fletch
  their arrows and set up their new bow. (We do not fletch your arrows for y
 ou after you order your own equipment.)<br><br>Coach Racae will be holding 
 these sessions periodically\, as archers receive their equipment\, so if yo
 u miss tonight's session\, you can schedule another session with me sometim
 e more convenient for you. <br><br><b>Registered: </b><br><b>Valerie W.</b>
 <br><b>Zach S.</b><br><b>Abby Y.<br></b><br>Please note\, class times are f
 or coaching form/mental preparation\; there is not time to set up your new 
 bow or fletch your new arrows\, so you need to make a separate time with me
  to learn how to do that.<br><br>In preparation for tonight's session:<br>Y
 ou must have received the following equipment for each class. If you are st
 ill waiting on some equipment\, email Coach Racae\, so she can bring a subs
 titute\, if possible.<br><br>You can <b>bring snacks/drinks to eat or share
 </b> before the arrow fletching class begins.<ul><li><b>Arrow Fletching: 6:
 00-6:45:  Fee: $30/archer\;</b> <b>$25/archer for 2</b> attending\; <b>$20/
 archer for 3 or more </b>attending.<ul><li>Arrow shafts: Carbons (outdoors)
 \; Aluminums (indoors)</li><li>Points</li><li>Vanes (outdoors) or Feathers 
 (indoors)</li><li>Nocks</li><li>Stick glue for points</li><li>Torch for glu
 ing points in</li><li>Gas for torch</li><li>Adhesive glue for feathers / va
 nes</li><li>Fletching jig - for three/vanes feathers initially</li><li>Flet
 ching jig - for one feather/vane replacements in future</li><li>Fletching j
 ig - for spinwings (for outdoors advanced)</li><li>Measuring arrow (optiona
 l)</li><li>Other: Very fine sand paper (for aluminum shafts)</li><li>Shaft 
 cleaner (alcohol or other)</li><li>Arrow saw (only if you personally need t
 o cut your arrows\, otherwise you can use ours)</li></ul></li><li><b>Bow Se
 t Up: 6:45-8:00: Fee: $60/archer</b>\; <b>$40/archer for 2</b> attending\; 
 <b>$30/archer for 3 </b>attending\; <b>$25/archer for 4 or more</b> attendi
 ng.<br><ul><li>Riser</li><li>Limbs</li><li>String</li><li>Nok set - or do a
  tie-on nocking point via video (<a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=M
 FI17QKYc2g">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MFI17QKYc2g</a>) before coming 
 to class</li><li>Nocking pliers (for brass nok set\, not tie-ons)</li><li>B
 ow square</li><li>Bow scale (optional\, but preferred)</li><li>Stringer</li
 ><li>Rest (stick-on or magnetic)</li><li>Cushion Plunger (if you bought mag
 netic rest)</li><li>Clicker (if Coach Racae says you're ready for one)</li>
 <li>Sight</li><li>Stabilizer</li><li>Bow stand</li><li>Backpack with arrow 
 tube</li><li>Tools: <ul><li>Allen keys that came with equipment</li><li>Phi
 lips screw driver</li><li>Scissors</li><li>Utility knife</li><li>Pliers/ pi
 ncers</li></ul></li><li>Sharpie</li></ul></li></ul>
