CREATED:20230125T012039Z
DESCRIPTION:REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to adult\, juniors 8+\, and parents!
  Please read all the info below and in the registration and waivers.<br><br
 >More information\, registration forms and waivers are available at <a href
 ="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com"><u><u><u><u>www.archerytrainingcent
 er.com</u></u></u></u></a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE of these forms:<
 br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeciOgkyuKTLZ5_ZaWCEyQ
 KYSX1fWGpP5qakhT6OuAc6jJ_FQ/viewform"><u>2023 Outdoor 1: First-time Class f
 or Adults</u></a>  OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQL
 Sc_bYEFoE4oXkcm0T6fZK99fu_q6lL8wZGClXyfa1GZbahh-g/viewform"><u>2023 Outdoor
  1: First-time Class for Juniors and Parents</u></a><br><br>Sign up for jus
 t ONE Outdoor 1 class\, because most people graduate out of this class into
  Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br><br>Your name will be added below and
  your place reserved on a first registered and paid basis and after we rece
 ive 3 things:  <br><b>2023 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM   +  MEMBERSHIP AND 
 WAIVERS PACKET +   FEE</b><b><br></b><u></u><br><u></u><b>USA Archery Level
  4 NTS Coach Racae Meyer</b><b><br></b><br><b>Registered archers </b>at 9m 
 on 40-cm target face unless otherwise noted:<u></u><br><u></u><br><b>Target
  Assignments:</b><br> <br>4A. <br>4B. <br><br>5A. <b>Derek F.\, </b>adult\,
  pd - <b>77 pts </b>-&gt\; to Outdoor 2<br>5B. <b>Laura F.\, </b>adult\, pd
  - <b>81 pts </b>(corrected)-&gt\; to Outdoor 2<br><br>6A. <b>Christophe B.
 \, </b>adult - pd - <b>160 pts</b>-&gt\; to Outdoor 2<br>6B. <br><br>7A. <b
 >Alexiss C.\, </b>adult - pd - <b>34 pts</b>-&gt\; to Outdoor 2<br>7B. <b>I
 rvin L.\, </b>adult - pd - <b>80 pts</b>-&gt\; to Outdoor 2<br><br>8A. <b>R
 oque P.\, </b>adult - pd - <b>80 pts</b>-&gt\; to Outdoor 2<br> for<br>9A. 
 <b>Yumeng L.\, </b>adult - pd - ? pts -&gt\; to Outdoor 2<br>9B. <br><br>10
 A. <b>Kaitlyn McN.\, </b>15\, on 60-cm target face - pd - <b>substituted 1/
 28 -&gt\; to Outdoor 2</b><br>10B.<br><br>Space will be limited to 10-15 ar
 chers per session depending on the number of family groups in attendance or
  in accordance with CDC Guidelines. <br>Each person will have a target stan
 d\, except after 10 people have registered\, members may be assigned to sha
 re a target stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be all
 owed on the field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae. <br>Pare
 nts of juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator. <br>Pa
 rents of juniors 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with thei
 r child for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) i
 s accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-time Class. <br><br>We will accept a 
 limited number of kids under 12 into the program each semester\, depending 
 on the total  number of archers in all the classes. If you join before the 
 limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and
  take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2. If you ar
 e under 12\, registered and paid after the cut off\, your fee will be retur
 ned to you. <br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times b
 efore qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as
  soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows. <br>Adults don´t
  need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories p
 acket (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdo
 or 2. ($18) Please pay for this at the field\, as our stock fluctuates beca
 use of dealer supply fluctuations<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string
  loop)\, optional but really needed to practice form\, warm up before class
 es ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be pos
 ted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recogn
 ize your final score\, because it will have been averaged by taking your re
 corded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrows you sho
 t to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full r
 ound score. After the last first-time class each weekend\, final scores may
  also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more informati
 on before your next class.
