DESCRIPTION:USA Archery certified Level 2-4 coach or instructor coaches wil
 l provide form rectification\, mental coaching\, and equipment tuning and a
 dvice.<br>Fee: $52/two-hour class/archer or multi-class discount pack.<br><
 br>1. <b>Hannah T</b>\, USAA\, pd -  Recorded equipment measurements. Score
 d 273 @ 30m\, but with two bonus ends to sub for first two ends (moved sigh
 t the wrong direction) 299 final score. Qualified for <b>40m</b>.<i><b>(Wow
 ! Congratulations! CR) </b></i>- 2 hrs<br>2. <b>Abby Y.</b> - Scored 299 @ 
 40m. Qualified for <b>50m</b>. Working on a strong bow arm and having good 
 posture in the shoulders before the set-up. <i><b>(Wow! Congratulations! CR
 ) </b></i>- 2 hrs<br>3. <b>Ellie Y.</b> - Working on a cleaner anchor/expan
 sion/release-follow-through with a flat wrist. strapped a beiter arm guard 
 to the inside of her wrist as a physical cue for a couple ends. <i>(Good id
 ea! CR)  </i>- 2 hrs<br>4. <b>Luke T</b>. USAA\, pd - Recorded equipment me
 asurements. Arrows are getting very short and will be too short with form c
 orrections. Adopted a shoelace finger sling and worked on grip (pushing and
  letting the bow drop instead of grasping the bow).- 2 hrs<br>5. <br>6. <br
 >7. <br>8. <br>9. <br>10.
