UID:6m85n9p7f8r10ei2bk98ou5afr@google.com
CREATED:20220519T051637Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><br><table><tbody><tr><td>July 12\, 2:00 pm E
 T</td><td><b>The Art of Storytelling in Coaching</b>&nbsp\;</td><td>Alexand
 er Grabner-Jarlung</td></tr><tr><td>July 12\, 8:00 pm ET</td><td><b>Buildin
 g Trust in Coaching</b></td><td><br>Dr. Wade Gilbert\, Ph.D.<br><br></td></
 tr></tbody></table>To register\, log in to your&nbsp\;<a href="http://usarc
 hery.sport80.com/"><u><u>USA Archery member account</u></u></a>\, select Co
 nferences on the left and click 2022 USA Archery Virtual&nbsp\;Symposium.<u
 ></u><br><u></u><br><u></u><br><u></u>This year’s&nbsp\;<a href="https://ww
 w.usarchery.org/coaches/virtual-symposium"><u>USA Archery Virtual Symposium
 </u></a>&nbsp\;brings coaches\, athletes\, parents\, and club leaders insig
 hts and information from world-renowned athletes\, coaches\, and subject ma
 tter experts. The Virtual Symposium will feature 7 sessions between July an
 d&nbsp\;August.<br><p>This year’s symposium will take a look at evidence-ba
 sed performance and coaching methods and the information will be applicable
  to intermediate to elite athletes\, coaches and parents. Participants will
  hear from world renowned experts in archery\, coach education\, motor lear
 ning and control and sports psychology. Gabriele Wulf\, Ph. D. who is one o
 f the leading experts in motor control and learning will share her OPTIMAL 
 Theory of Motor Learning. Wade Gilbert\, Ph.D. will share how to build trus
 t in coaching\, and Lanny Bassham of Mental Management System will explore 
 Parenting Champions. Dr. Peter Haberl from the U.S. Olympic and Paralympic 
 Committee will open our minds to the benefits of Mindfulness in&nbsp\;Arche
 ry.</p><p>Archery specific topics this year will include Movement Analysis 
 with National Head Coach KiSik Lee\, Field Archery Tips and Tricks with Tea
 m USA archers Paige Pearce and Brady Ellison\, Target Panic with Joel Turne
 r of Shot IQ\, Selecting the Right Equipment with Heather Pfeil from Lancas
 ter Archery Academy\, and promoting and marketing your club with Scott Boot
 h\, host of Raising an Archer&nbsp\;podcast.</p><p>Sessions will be recorde
 d and sent to all registered participants if you miss the live time or want
  to review a session. Sponsors including Black Rifle Coffee Company and Xer
 o Shoes will be providing giveaway products for lucky&nbsp\;participants.</
 p><p>Contact USA Archery Education and Training Manager Guy Krueger at&nbsp
 \;<a href="mailto:gkrueger@usarchery.org"><u>gkrueger@usarchery.org</u></a>
 &nbsp\;for more&nbsp\;information.</p><u></u></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260404T082256Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:USA Archery Virtual Symposium - Series 3
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
