DESCRIPTION:To be nominated to the 2020 US Olympic Archery Team\, archers m
 ust compete in the Trials as set by USA Archery and the US Olympic Committe
 e.&nbsp\;<br>For the Tokyo 2020 Games\, there are four stages of the Trials
 .<br><b><i>Participation is open to any USA Archery member who is also a ci
 tizen of the United States.</i></b><br>Archers wanting to participate in th
 e Trials need to complete a separate registration and be registered in the 
 Recurve Senior division.<br>This is your chance to earn a spot on Team USA!
  Compete with the best of the best on the Road to Tokyo!<br>Trials particip
 ants receive a special commemorative t-shirt from the event and memories fo
 r a lifetime!<br><b>Stage 1</b>: <b>Aug 15-16</b> during the 135th US Natio
 nal Target Championships. (Registration is now open)&nbsp\;<br><b>Stage 2: 
 Sept 28\, 30\, Oct. 1</b>&nbsp\;during the Texas Shootout. (Registration is
  now open)<br><b>Stage 3: April 8-11\, 2020 </b>in Chula Vista\, CA<br><b>S
 tage 4: May 25-26\, 2020</b>&nbsp\;during the Gator Cup in Newberry\, FL
LAST-MODIFIED:20260404T082256Z
