UID:0o9dvvobno916qei1hov49v170@google.com
CREATED:20250331T144839Z
DESCRIPTION:Level 3 NTS Coach Joel (203-232-8331)<br><br>USA Archery certif
 ied Level 2-4 coach or instructor coaches will provide form rectification\,
  mental coaching\, and equipment tuning and advice.<br>Fee: $52/two-hour cl
 ass/archer or multi-class discount pack.<br><br>Class opened with a discuss
 ion on the key points for SET. I took form videos for the archers and uploa
 ded to their respective shared folders on Google\, including Coach Jake.<br
 ><br>1. <b> (distance?) Abby Y.</b> 13\, 2 hrs - Working on keeping the hea
 d from turning and leaning forward into the anchor and keeping the bow shou
 lder relaxed and down. <br><span>2.</span><span>(</span><b>40m</b><span>)</
 span><span> </span><b>Miles G.</b><span>\, 12\, USAA\, ob\, pd - 2 hrs -</s
 pan><span> </span><i>Working on the back end of the shot--coiling to get to
  full alignment\, expanding through the shot with back tension and completi
 ng the "T". Discussed having a bit of a more stable stance by widening feet
  and positioning them in NTS shape instead of a V pointing opposite ways fr
 om the shooting line</i><span>.</span><br><span>3. (</span><b>30m?) Hannah 
 T</b><span>\, adult\, USAA\, pd - 2 hrs - </span><i>Working on keeping the 
 bow shoulder tucked back and down. Identified a little bit more coiling nee
 ded to get to full alignment at holding.</i><br>4 (<b>30m</b>) <b>Sophie D<
 /b>.\,f - 2 hrs- <i>Working on keeping the bow shoulder down. Finding a sol
 id anchoring point. Discussed relaxing the fingers for the release instead 
 in squeezing the fingers at the end of the shot. Lowered bow weight to 28# 
 (maxed out the tiller bolts) and raised brace height to just under 9" to he
 lp make holding and alignment a little easier to get to.</i><br>5. (<b>20m<
 /b>) <b>Anna P</b> - 2 hrs - <i>Working on not drawing down across the face
  and lifting head to tuck draw hand into anchor position\, instead getting 
 the end of the setup below the chin and then draw to load/anchor up under t
 he jaw. Discussed coiling and reaching barrel-of-the-gun alignment by the e
 nd of setup to help get to full alignment at holding.</i><br>6. (<b>30m</b>
 ) <b>Colby K.!</b> - 2 hrs - <i>Discussed the very tense draw hand when rel
 easing. Also discussed the high draw shoulder and draw elbow that leads to 
 a release/follow-through motion that is more downward vertical motion than 
 it is a opening up rotationally around the "pole"</i><br><br><b>Luke T.\, <
 /b>DNA
LAST-MODIFIED:20250425T063020Z
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Outdoor 4+ Training Class w/ Coach Joel
