DESCRIPTION:To be nominated to the 2020 US Olympic Archery Team\, archers m
 ust compete in the Trials as set by USA Archery and the US Olympic Committe
 e. \nFor the Tokyo 2020 Games\, there are four stages of the Trials.\nParti
 cipation is open to any USA Archery member who is also a citizen of the Uni
 ted States.\nArchers wanting to participate in the Trials need to complete 
 a separate registration and be registered in the Recurve Senior division.\n
 This is your chance to earn a spot on Team USA! Compete with the best of th
 e best on the Road to Tokyo!\nTrials participants receive a special commemo
 rative t-shirt from the event and memories for a lifetime!\nStage 1: Aug 15
 -16 during the 135th US National Target Championships. (Registration is now
  open) \nStage 2: Sept 28\, 30\, Oct. 1 during the Texas Shootout. (Registr
 ation is now open)\nStage 3: April 8-11\, 2020 in Chula Vista\, CA\nStage 4
 : May 25-26\, 2020 during the Gator Cup in Newberry\, FL
LAST-MODIFIED:20260404T082256Z
LOCATION:Newberry\, FL
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Stage 4: Olympic Trials - POSTPONED to June 15-16
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
