CREATED:20190417T193641Z
DESCRIPTION:\n8-10 people\n\nWe are very happy to host a Corporate Team Arc
 hery Event for your group! \n\nThese sessions are proving to be very popula
 r\, and we appreciate the opportunity. \nOur indoor corporate archery tourn
 aments may be coming up soon!\n\nA few of the corporations which schedule e
 vents with us are:\nFacebook\, Intel\, Dell\, AMD\, Samsung\, Home Away\, N
 ational Instruments\, Texas Mutual Insurance\, Electronic Arts\, ERCOT\, Ve
 ctra Networks\, Austin Children's Advocacy\, Glatfelder Insurance\, Kerbey 
 Lane\, RackSpace\, Abilitie\, Black Locus\, Boosterthon\, WP Engine\, Camp 
 Gladiator\, Marriott International\, Zimmer Biomet\, Austin Gastroenterolog
 y\, Yeti\, RetailMeNot\, Tableau Software\, Four Hands and others. \n\nWe a
 lso would like to thank your company for its vital\, indirect support of US
 A Archery's Junior Olympic Archery Development (JOAD) program! Support like
  yours grows Olympians! \n\nBelow is a typical agenda for a Corporate Team 
 Event with us\, and some other general info\, which may make things run mor
 e smoothly. \n\nCAPACITY: 1-20 participants. 10 places on the shooting line
 . If you'll have over 10 participants\, we will form two shooting lines\; e
 ven numbers are best\, so we can create teams of two.\n\nDAYS CLOSED: \nMON
 DAYS and THURSDAYS\nJAN 1-5: Happy Holidays!\nAPRIL 21: Happy Easter !\nMAY
  12: Happy Mother´s Day!\n\nAGENDA (approx.- depends on number and pace of 
 participants)\n\n1:00 Arrival\; waivers (to be signed by participants over 
 18 years old or adults/parents/guardians)\n1:15 Selecting two-person teams\
 ; equipment review and selection (bows\, arrows\, finger tabs\, arm guards\
 , targets\, etc.)\n1:55 Safety rules\; whistle system\n2:00 Break\n2:10 For
 m (positions) training (stance\, nocking\, hooking/gripping\, set\, mindset
 \, set-up\, drawing\, anchor\, loading\, aiming\, expanding\, release)\n2:4
 5 Ranking Round - shooting in teams\; quantity of arrows will depend on num
 ber and pace of participants\n3:45 Olympic Round: Based on ranking round\; 
 each team picks a country to represent\; all teams progress in a match play
  to the Gold\, Silver\, and Bronze medal matches\, with other teams cheerin
 g them on!\n4:15 Awards Ceremony and podium presentations\, photos!\n\nSCHE
 DULING:\nWe can schedule a corporate team event on T/W/Th/F during the day 
 for a max. of 20 people\, pending your confirmation. If you would prefer an
 other day or time\, please tell us\, and we'll do our best to accommodate y
 ou. Sundays 11:00am-2:00pm are also available\, if booked at least two week
 s in advance.\n\nTIME NEEDED:\nIt's best to allow at least 3 hrs. for a tea
 m of up to 10\, and about 3.5-4 hours for more than 10 participants\, since
  we'll need to form two lines of shooting. We may run over by as much as 30
  minutes\, depending on everyone's arrival and ability. If this will be a p
 roblem\, please let us know\, so we can pace the event carefully.\n\nARRIVA
 LS: We'll all start together\, so please have everyone arrive on time or to
 gether. \n\nPARKING: We have limited parking space for about 8-10 vehicles.
  Some corporations decide to park at a nearby shopping center parking lot\,
  and then "carpool" to the archery range.\n\nFEE: There is a minimum fee of
  $250 for 1-10 people\, and then $25/person for 11-20 people. We can accomm
 odate 20 people for $500. If your company requires a separate written recei
 pt for accounting purposes\, please tell us in advance so we can have one r
 eady for you.\n\nPAYMENT: When you arrive at the range\, you can pay for th
 e session individually or by corporate check payable to Archery Training Ce
 nter\, or by credit card (+4%). All fees must be paid before the session be
 gins. \n\nREFUNDS: If you pay in advance of arrival\, a refund will be issu
 ed only for cancellations or reductions in attendees in writing when you gi
 ve us notice not less than 24 hours before the session begins.\n\nEQUIPMENT
 : We provide all equipment necessary during the Corporate Team Event.\n\nDR
 ESS RECOMMENDATIONS: Flat shoes are best\, as we stand a lot and throw our 
 weight forward a little\, so balance and weight distribution is important. 
 The bowstring can get slowed or entangled in your clothing or hair\, so wea
 ring tighter fitting clothes\, no wide skirts\, shirts without buttons on t
 he front pockets and tying your hair back is preferable. Longer brim baseba
 ll caps often prevent the string from reaching your face\, so shorter brims
  are better. In the winter on very cold days\, please dress in layers\, as 
 it may be chilly in the indoor range.\n\nWAIVERS: There will be waivers for
  each archer to fill out and sign when they first come in\, and before ente
 ring the range. All signees must be at least 18 years old. For those under 
 18\, a parent/guardian will need to sign for them. \n\nSPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS
 : Please let us know if there are any special concepts you would like us to
  emphasize\, or any other considerations which you would like us to take in
 to account.\n\nOLYMPIC TARGET ARCHERY LINKS: \nHere are some links\, which 
 you and your group may find interesting before you get to the session.\n\nh
 ttp://www.usarchery.org \nhttp://www.olympic.org/archery \nhttp://www.world
 archery.org\nhttp://www.youtube.com/archerytv\n\nThe YouTube videos showing
  the top American male archer\, Brady Ellison\, competing with the top Kore
 an archer\, KU Bonchan\, in the Rio Olympics Men's Semi Final Match is the 
 best we've seen in 20 years! You have to watch every shot.\n\nTHANK YOU for
  your interest in and support of Olympic target archery. We know you'll all
  really enjoy being part of the Olympic Round at the end of your training!!
 \n\nWe look forward to your time with us.\n\nIf you'd like to discuss your 
 reservation in more detail\, please call Coach Racae Meyer 512 975 1850 at 
 your convenience.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260404T082256Z
LOCATION:10203 Old Manchaca Rd.\, Austin\, TX 78748
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Corporate Team Event - Samsung - Leslie
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
