CREATED:20150217T230442Z
DESCRIPTION:We'd be very happy to host a team-building archery event for yo
 ur corporate group. These sessions are proving to be very popular\, and we 
 appreciate the opportunity!   We also would like to thank your group for yo
 ur vital and indirectly support of USA Archery's Junior Olympic Archery Dev
 elopment (JOAD) program! Support like yours grow Olympians!  Here is a samp
 le agenda for your team building event with us\, and some other general inf
 o\, which may make things run more smoothly.   Agenda (approx.- depends on 
 pace of participants) 1:30 Arrival\; waivers 1:45 Selecting two-person team
 s\; equipment selection 2:00 Safety rules\; whistle system 2:10 Form (posit
 ions) training 2:30 Learning loading\, aiming\, expanding\, release 2:45 Ra
 nking Round - shooting in teams\; quantity of arrows will depend on pace of
  class 3:30 Olympic Round: Based on ranking round\; each team picks a count
 ry to represent\; all teams progress in a match play to the Gold\, Silver\,
  and Bronze medal matches\, with other teams cheering them on! 4:00 Awards 
 Ceremony and podium presentations\, photos!  SCHEDULING: We will schedule y
 our group\, pending your confirmation. It's best to allow about 3 hrs.\, as
  we may run over by as much as 30 minutes\, depending on everyone's arrival
 s and abilities. If this will be a problem\, please let us know.  ARRIVALS:
   We'll all start together\, so it's good to have everyone arrive on time o
 r together. (You may want to carpool from where you're having lunch\, as th
 ere is limited parking at our facilities for a max. of 8-10 cars.)  FEE:   
  For a first-time team-building approx. 3-hr session\, there is a minimum f
 ee of $125 for 1-5 people\, and then $25/person for 6-20 people.   PAYMENT:
  When you arrive at the range\, you can pay for the session individually or
  by corporate check payable to Archery Training Center\, or by credit card 
 (+2.75%).  EQUIPMENT:    We provide all equipment necessary.   WAIVERS:  Th
 ere will be waivers for each archer to fill out and sign when they first co
 me in\, and before entering the range.  SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS:    Also\, ple
 ase let us know if there are any special concepts you would like us to emph
 asize to help you build your team. After the initial "learning how to shoot
 " part\, there will be time for team games\, which everyone always enjoys. 
  ARCHERY LINKS:  Here are some links\, which you and your team may find int
 eresting before you get to the the team-building lesson.  <http://www.usarc
 hery.org>  http://www.olympic.org/archery  http://www.worldarchery.org http
 ://www.youtube.com/archerytv  The YouTube videos showing the USA Men/Women 
 Recurve team in Turkey are particularly exciting\, as are the 2012 Olympics
 : Men's Recurve Team Gold Medal Match and the Women's Individual Recurve Br
 onze Medal Match.  Thank you for your interest in Olympic target archery\, 
 and we know you'll all really enjoy being part of the Olympic Round at the 
 end of your training!!  We look forward to your time with us.  If you'd lik
 e to discuss this in more detail\, please call 512 436 8813 at your conveni
 ence.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260404T082256Z
LOCATION:10203 Old Manchaca Rd\, Austin\, TX 78748\, USA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Corporate Team - Creative One Group
TRANSP:OPAQUE
