DESCRIPTION:<i><b>Thank you for your support of our Olympic Target Archery 
 programs for adults and juniors!</b></i><b><br></b><br><b>WAIVERS:</b> Ever
 yone needs to <b>sign the waivers in advance </b>of arriving at the range\,
  so we are not delayed in starting. Here's the link <a href="https://docs.g
 oogle.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSe4nVUxh99Vi50BKWFl9swZ4fephhjHBHtHpxx7G7I7KIiw5
 A/viewform?usp=preview" target="_blank"><u><b>2025 Waivers for Corporate Te
 am Building Events</b></u></a><br><br><b>DIRECTIONS:</b> <b>Google Map "Don
 ut Taco Palace"</b> to find us quickly - We are right next door in Unit 102
 . (Some people are still being misdirected.) There is a target on the glass
  door and the unit is facing 290W service road going west on the corner of 
 Industrial Oaks Blvd and 290W. <br><br><b>ARRIVAL</b>: For a 7:00 pm start\
 , please <b>arrive by 6:45 pm</b>\, because we will all be starting togethe
 r at 7:00 pm. <br><br><b>CARPOOLING / PARKING:</b> Please meet and carpool 
 earlier from another location or from a big box store parking lot across th
 e highway (like Target or At Home on the corner of Mopac and 290W). It's ea
 sy and convenient to do. (Parking in front of the range and along Industria
 l Oaks Blvd may be limited\, depending on the number of participants.)<br><
 br><b>DRESS RECOMMENDATIONS: </b><br>Flat athletic shoes are best\, as we w
 ill be throwing our weight forward a little\, so balance and weight distrib
 ution is important. The bowstring can get slowed or entangled in your cloth
 ing or hair\, so wearing tightly fitting clothes\, no wide skirts\, shirts 
 without buttons on the front pockets and tying your hair back is preferable
 . Longer brim baseball caps often prevent the string from reaching your fac
 e\, so shorter brims or bucket hats are better. <br>:<br><b>All participant
 s need to complete waivers online before the event.</b><br><b>Here is the d
 irect link to complete: </b><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAI
 pQLSe4nVUxh99Vi50BKWFl9swZ4fephhjHBHtHpxx7G7I7KIiw5A/viewform?usp=preview" 
 target="_blank"><u><b>2025 Waivers for Corporate Team Building Events</b></
 u></a><br><br>Waivers have been received from those shown below in <b>bold 
 with (W)</b><br><b>Last update: 5/21/25 at 7:10 pm</b><ol><li><b>Tyrone H. 
 (W)</b></li><li><b>Patrick T. (W)</b></li><li><b>Haoyang L (W)</b><br></li>
 <li><b>Franck M. (W)</b></li><li><b>Jan O. (W)</b></li><li><b>Eduard D. (W)
 </b></li><li><b>Aryeh R. (W)</b></li><li><b>Steve W. (W)</b></li><li><b>Phi
 llipp M. (W)</b></li><li><b>Alok C (W)</b></li><li><b>Mohan N. (W)</b></li>
 <li><b>Grady L. (W)</b></li><li><b>Joel D. (W)</b></li><li><b>Kord B. (W)</
 b></li><li><b>Miguel G. (W)</b></li></ol>
