DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><br><table><tbody><tr><td>July 9\, 4:00 pm ET</td><t
 d><b>Myth Busters - Archery Edition</b></td><td>Kristy Wapniarski and Andy 
 Neville</td></tr><tr><td>July 9\, 5:15 pm ET</td><td><b>Parenting Champions
 </b></td><td>Lanny Bassham</td></tr></tbody></table></html-blob><br><html-b
 lob><br></html-blob><br><html-blob>To register\, log in to your&nbsp\;<a hr
 ef="http://usarchery.sport80.com/"><u><u>USA Archery member account</u></u>
 </a>\, select Conferences on the left and click 2022 USA Archery Virtual&nb
 sp\;Symposium.<u></u><br><u></u><br><u></u><br><u></u>This year’s&nbsp\;<a 
 href="https://www.usarchery.org/coaches/virtual-symposium"><u>USA Archery V
 irtual Symposium</u></a>&nbsp\;brings coaches\, athletes\, parents\, and cl
 ub leaders insights and information from world-renowned athletes\, coaches\
 , and subject matter experts. The Virtual Symposium will feature 7 sessions
  between July and&nbsp\;August.<br><p>This year’s symposium will take a loo
 k at evidence-based performance and coaching methods and the information wi
 ll be applicable to intermediate to elite athletes\, coaches and parents. P
 articipants will hear from world renowned experts in archery\, coach educat
 ion\, motor learning and control and sports psychology. Gabriele Wulf\, Ph.
  D. who is one of the leading experts in motor control and learning will sh
 are her OPTIMAL Theory of Motor Learning. Wade Gilbert\, Ph.D. will share h
 ow to build trust in coaching\, and Lanny Bassham of Mental Management Syst
 em will explore Parenting Champions. Dr. Peter Haberl from the U.S. Olympic
  and Paralympic Committee will open our minds to the benefits of Mindfulnes
 s in&nbsp\;Archery.</p><p>Archery specific topics this year will include Mo
 vement Analysis with National Head Coach KiSik Lee\, Field Archery Tips and
  Tricks with Team USA archers Paige Pearce and Brady Ellison\, Target Panic
  with Joel Turner of Shot IQ\, Selecting the Right Equipment with Heather P
 feil from Lancaster Archery Academy\, and promoting and marketing your club
  with Scott Booth\, host of Raising an Archer&nbsp\;podcast.</p><p>Sessions
  will be recorded and sent to all registered participants if you miss the l
 ive time or want to review a session. Sponsors including Black Rifle Coffee
  Company and Xero Shoes will be providing giveaway products for lucky&nbsp\
 ;participants.</p><p>Contact USA Archery Education and Training Manager Guy
  Krueger at&nbsp\;<a href="mailto:gkrueger@usarchery.org"><u>gkrueger@usarc
 hery.org</u></a>&nbsp\;for more&nbsp\;information.</p><u></u></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260404T082256Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:USA Archery Virtual Symposium - Series 2
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
