DESCRIPTION:10 people<br><br>We are very happy to host a Corporate Team Arc
 hery Event for your group on a mutually convenient date.&nbsp\;<br><br>Thes
 e sessions are proving to be very popular\, and we appreciate the opportuni
 ty!&nbsp\;<br><br>A few of the corporations which schedule events with us a
 re:<br>Facebook\, Intel\, Dell\, AMD\, Samsung\, Home Away\, National Instr
 uments\, Texas Mutual Insurance\, Electronic Arts\, ERCOT\, Vectra Networks
 \, Austin Children's Advocacy\, Glatfelder Insurance\, Kerbey Lane\, RackSp
 ace\, Abilitie\, Black Locus\, Boosterthon\, WP Engine\, Camp Gladiator\, M
 arriott International\, Zimmer Biomet\, Austin Gastroenterology\, Yeti\, Re
 tailMeNot\, Tableau Software\, Wikibuy/Capital One\, Managed by Q\, GTS Tec
 hnology Solutions\, Spiceworks\, Burlebo and others.&nbsp\;<br><br>We also 
 would like to thank your company for its vital\, indirect support of USA Ar
 chery's Junior Olympic Archery Development (JOAD) program! Support like you
 rs grows Olympians!&nbsp\;<br><br>Please read the following information.<br
 >Below is a typical agenda for a Corporate Team Event with us\, and some ot
 her general info\, which may make things run more smoothly.&nbsp\;<br><br>C
 APACITY: 1 to 30 participants. 10 places on the shooting line. If you'll ha
 ve over 10 participants\, even numbers are best\, so we can create teams of
  two or even three.<br><br>DAYS CLOSED:&nbsp\;<br>MONDAYS and THURSDAYS (bu
 t we do open for Corporate Team Events!)<br>JAN 1-3: Happy Holidays!<br>MAR
  17-20 : Spring Break !<br>APRIL 11 + 12: Easter Weekend<br>MAY 6 : Coach R
 acae´s birthday !<br>MAY 10: Happy Mother´s Day!<br>MAY 24-JUNE 5 - Summer 
 Vacation 1<br><br>AGENDA (approx.- depends on number and pace of participan
 ts)<br><br>1:00 Arrival\; waivers (to be signed by participants over 18 yea
 rs old or adults/parents/guardians)<br>1:15 Selecting two-person teams\; eq
 uipment review and selection (bows\, arrows\, finger tabs\, arm guards\, ta
 rgets\, etc.)<br>1:55 Safety rules\; whistle system<br>2:00 Break<br>2:10 F
 orm (positions) training (stance\, nocking\, hooking/gripping\, set\, minds
 et\, set-up\, drawing\, anchor\, loading\, aiming\, expanding\, release)<br
 >2:45 Ranking Round: Shooting in teams\; quantity of arrows will depend on 
 number and pace of participants<br>3:45 Olympic Round: Based on ranking rou
 nd\; each team picks a country to represent\; all teams progress in a match
  play to the Gold\, Silver\, and Bronze medal matches\, with other teams ch
 eering them on!<br>4:15 Awards Ceremony and podium presentations\, photos!<
 br><br>SCHEDULING:<br>We can schedule a corporate team event on M/T/W/Th/F 
 during the day for a max. of 30 people\, pending your confirmation. If you 
 would prefer another day or time\, please tell us\, and we'll do our best t
 o accommodate you. Sundays 11:00am-2:00pm are also available\, if booked at
  least two weeks in advance for up to 10 people..<br><br>TIME NEEDED:<br>It
 's best to allow at least 3 hrs. for a team of up to 10\, and about 3.5-4 h
 ours for more than 10 participants\, since we'll need to form two lines of 
 shooting. We may run over by as much as 30 minutes\, depending on everyone'
 s arrival and ability. If this will be a problem\, please let us know\, so 
 we can pace the event carefully.<br><br>ARRIVALS: We'll all start together\
 , so please have everyone arrive on time or together.&nbsp\;<br><br>PARKING
 : We have LIMITED parking space for about 8-10 vehicles. Some corporations 
 decide to park at a nearby shopping center parking lot\, and then "carpool"
  to the archery range.<br><br>FEE: There is a minimum fee of $250 for 1-10 
 people\, and then $25/person for 11-30 people. We can accommodate 20 people
  for $500 and 30 people for $750. If your company requires a separate writt
 en receipt for accounting purposes\, please tell us in advance so we can ha
 ve one ready for you.<br><br>PAYMENT: When you arrive at the range\, you ca
 n pay for the session individually or by corporate check payable to Archery
  Training Center\, or by credit card (+4%). All fees must be paid before th
 e session begins.&nbsp\;<br><br>REFUNDS: If you pay in advance of arrival\,
  a refund will be issued only for cancellations or reductions in attendees 
 in writing when given notice not less than 24 hours before the session begi
 ns.<br><br>EQUIPMENT: We provide all equipment necessary during the Corpora
 te Team Event.<br><br>DRESS RECOMMENDATIONS: Flat shoes are best\, as we st
 and a lot and throw our weight forward a little\, so balance and weight dis
 tribution is important. The bowstring can get slowed or entangled in your c
 lothing or hair\, so wearing tighter fitting clothes\, no wide skirts\, shi
 rts without buttons on the front pockets and tying your hair back is prefer
 able. Longer brim baseball caps often prevent the string from reaching your
  face\, so shorter brims are better. In the winter on very cold days\, plea
 se dress in layers\, as it may be chilly in the indoor range.<br><br>WAIVER
 S: There will be waivers for each archer to fill out and sign when they fir
 st come in\, and before entering the range. All signees must be at least 18
  years old. For those under 18\, a parent/guardian will need to sign for th
 em.&nbsp\;<br><br>SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS: Please let us know if there are any
  special concepts you would like us to emphasize\, or any other considerati
 ons which you would like us to take into account.<br><br>OLYMPIC TARGET ARC
 HERY LINKS:&nbsp\;<br>Here are some links\, which you and your group may fi
 nd interesting before you get to the session.<br><br><a href="http://www.us
 archery.org">http://www.usarchery.org</a>&nbsp\;<br><a href="http://www.oly
 mpic.org/archery">http://www.olympic.org/archery</a>&nbsp\;<br><a href="htt
 p://www.worldarchery.org">http://www.worldarchery.org</a><br><a href="http:
 //www.youtube.com/archerytv">http://www.youtube.com/archerytv</a><br><br>Th
 e YouTube videos showing the top American male archer\, Brady Ellison\, com
