DESCRIPTION:We're very happy to host a Corporate Team Archery Event for you
 r group on a mutually convenient date. \n\nThese sessions are proving to be
  very popular\, and we appreciate the opportunity! \nBook now so you're rea
 dy for our indoor corporate archery tournaments!\n\nA few of the corporatio
 ns which schedule events with us are:\n\nFacebook\, Intel\, Dell\, AMD\, Sa
 msung\, Home Away\, National Instruments\, Texas Mutual Insurance\, Electro
 nic Arts\, ERCOT\, Vectra Networks\, Austin Children's Advocacy\, Glatfelde
 r Insurance\, Kerbey Lane\, RackSpace\, Abilitie\, Black Locus\, Boostertho
 n\, WP Engine\, Camp Gladiator\, Marriott International\, Zimmer Biomet\, A
 ustin Gastroenterology\, Yeti\, RetailMeNot\, Tableau Software and others. 
 \n\nWe also would like to thank your company for its vital\, indirect suppo
 rt of USA Archery's Junior Olympic Archery Development (JOAD) program! Supp
 ort like yours grows Olympians! \n\nBelow is a typical agenda for a Corpora
 te Team Event with us\, and some other general info\, which may make things
  run more smoothly. \n\nCAPACITY: Up to 20 participants. If you'll have ove
 r 10 participants\, even numbers are best\, so we can create teams of two\,
  with up to 10 people on the shooting line at once.\n\nDAYS CLOSED: \nMONDA
 YS and THURSDAYS\nJAN 1-5: Happy Holidays!\nAPRIL 21: Happy Easter !\nMAY 1
 2: Happy Mother´s Day!\nMAY 26-JUNE 7 - Summer Vacation 1\nJUNE 16 - Happy 
 Father´s Day!\nAUG 11 - 24th ANNUAL ARCHERS OF THE YEAR POTLUCK BANQUET 5:3
 0-7:30pm - Mark your calendars NOW!\nAUG 12-23 - Summer Vacation 2\n\nTYPIC
 AL AGENDA (approx.- depends on arrival time\, number and pace of participan
 ts)\n\n1:00 Arrival\; waivers (to be signed by participants over 18 years o
 ld or adults/parents/guardians)\n1:15 Introduction\n1:25 Selecting two-pers
 on teams\; equipment review and selection (bows\, arrows\, finger tabs\, ar
 m guards\, targets\, etc.)\n1:55 Safety rules\; whistle system\n2:00 Break\
 n2:10 Form (positions) training (stance\, nocking\, hooking/gripping\, set\
 , mindset\, set-up\, drawing\, anchor\, loading\, aiming\, expanding\, rele
 ase\, follow-through)\n2:45 Ranking Round - shooting in teams\; quantity of
  arrows will depend on number and pace of participants\n3:45 Olympic Round:
  Based on ranking round\; each team picks a country to represent\; all team
 s progress in a match play to the Gold\, Silver\, and Bronze medal matches\
 , with other teams cheering them on!\n4:15 Awards Ceremony and podium prese
 ntations\, photos!\n\nSCHEDULING:\nWe can schedule a corporate team event o
 n T/W/Th during the day for a max. of 20 people\, pending your confirmation
 . If you would prefer another day or time\, please tell us\, and we'll do o
 ur best to accommodate you. Sundays 11:00am-2:00pm are also available\, if 
 booked at least two weeks in advance.\n\nTIME NEEDED:\nIt's best to allow a
 t least 3 hrs. for a team of up to 10\, and about 3.5-4 hours for more than
  10 participants\, since we'll need to form two lines of shooting. We may r
 un over by as much as 30 minutes\, depending on everyone's arrival and abil
 ity. If this will be a problem\, please let us know\, so we can pace the ev
 ent carefully.\n\nARRIVALS: We'll all start together\, so please have every
 one arrive on time or together. \n\nPARKING: We have limited parking space 
 for about 8-10 vehicles. Some corporations decide to park at a nearby shopp
 ing center parking lot\, and then "carpool" to the archery range.\n\nFEE: T
 here is a minimum fee of $250 for 1-10 people\, and then $25/person for 11-
 20 people. We can accommodate 20 people for $500. If your company requires 
 a separate written receipt for accounting purposes\, please tell us in adva
 nce so we can have one ready for you.\n\nPAYMENT: When you arrive at the ra
 nge\, you can pay for the session individually or by corporate check payabl
 e to Archery Training Center\, or by credit card (+4%). All fees must be pa
 id before the session begins. \n\nREFUNDS: If you pay in advance of arrival
 \, a refund will be issued only for cancellations or reductions in attendee
 s in writing when given notice not less than 24 hours before the session be
 gins.\n\nEQUIPMENT: We provide all equipment necessary during the Corporate
  Team Event.\n\nDRESS RECOMMENDATIONS: Flat shoes are best\, as we stand a 
 lot and throw our weight forward a little\, so balance and weight distribut
 ion is important. The bowstring can get slowed or entangled in your clothin
 g or hair\, so wearing tighter fitting clothes\, no wide skirts\, shirts wi
 thout buttons on the front pockets and tying your hair back is preferable. 
 Longer brim baseball caps often prevent the string from reaching your face\
 , so shorter brims are better. In the winter on very cold days\, please dre
 ss in layers\, as it may be chilly in the indoor range.\n\nWAIVERS: There w
 ill be waivers for each archer to fill out and sign when they first come in
 \, and before entering the range. All signees must be at least 18 years old
 . For those under 18\, a parent/guardian will need to sign for them. \n\nSP
 ECIAL INSTRUCTIONS: Please let us know if there are any special concepts yo
 u would like us to emphasize\, or any other considerations which you would 
 like us to take into account.\n\nOLYMPIC TARGET ARCHERY LINKS: \nHere are s
 ome links\, which you and your group may find interesting before you get to
  the session.\n\nhttp://www.usarchery.org \nhttp://www.olympic.org/archery 
 \nhttp://www.worldarchery.org\nhttp://www.youtube.com/archerytv\n\nThe YouT
 ube videos showing the top American male archer\, Brady Ellison\, competing
  with the top Korean archer\, KU Bonchan\, in the Rio Olympics Men's Semi F
 inal Match is the best we've seen in 20 years! You have to watch every shot
 .\n\nTHANK YOU for your interest in and support of Olympic target archery. 
 We know you'll all really enjoy being part of the Olympic Round at the end 
 of your training!!\n\nWe look forward to your time with us.\n\nIf you'd lik
 e to discuss your reservation in more detail\, please call Coach Racae Meye
 r 512 975 1850 at your convenience.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260404T082256Z
LOCATION:10203 Old Manchaca Road\, Austin\, TX 78748
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Corporate Team Event - Intel 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
