DESCRIPTION:8 people\n\nWe'd be very happy to host a Corporate Team Archery
  Event for your group on a mutually convenient date. \n\nThese sessions are
  proving to be very popular\, and we appreciate the opportunity! \nBook now
  so you're ready for our indoor corporate archery tournaments!\n\nA few of 
 the corporations which schedule events with us are:\nFacebook\, Intel\, Del
 l\, AMD\, Samsung\, Home Away\, National Instruments\, Texas Mutual Insuran
 ce\, Electronic Arts\, ERCOT\, Vectra Networks\, Austin Children's Advocacy
 \, Glatfelder Insurance\, Kerbey Lane\, RackSpace\, Abilitie\, Black Locus\
 , Boosterthon\, WP Engine\, Camp Gladiator\, Marriott International\, Zimme
 r Biomet\, Austin Gastroenterology\, Yeti\, RetailMeNot\, Tableau Software 
 and others. \n\nWe also would like to thank your company for its vital\, in
 direct support of USA Archery's Junior Olympic Archery Development (JOAD) p
 rogram! Support like yours grows Olympians! \n\nBelow is a typical agenda f
 or a Corporate Team Event with us\, and some other general info\, which may
  make things run more smoothly. \n\nCAPACITY: 1-20 participants. 10 places 
 on the shooting line. If you'll have over 10 participants\, we will form tw
 o shooting lines\; even numbers are best\, so we can create teams of two.\n
 \nDAYS CLOSED: \nMONDAYS and THURSDAYS\nJAN 1-5: Happy Holidays!\nAPRIL 21:
  Happy Easter !\nMAY 12: Happy Mother´s Day!\n\nAGENDA (approx.- depends on
  number and pace of participants)\n\n1:00 Arrival\; waivers (to be signed b
 y participants over 18 years old or adults/parents/guardians)\n1:15 Selecti
 ng two-person teams\; equipment review and selection (bows\, arrows\, finge
 r tabs\, arm guards\, targets\, etc.)\n1:55 Safety rules\; whistle system\n
 2:00 Break\n2:10 Form (positions) training (stance\, nocking\, hooking/grip
 ping\, set\, mindset\, set-up\, drawing\, anchor\, loading\, aiming\, expan
 ding\, release)\n2:45 Ranking Round - shooting in teams\; quantity of arrow
 s will depend on number and pace of participants\n3:45 Olympic Round: Based
  on ranking round\; each team picks a country to represent\; all teams prog
 ress in a match play to the Gold\, Silver\, and Bronze medal matches\, with
  other teams cheering them on!\n4:15 Awards Ceremony and podium presentatio
 ns\, photos!\n\nSCHEDULING:\nWe can schedule a corporate team event on T/W/
 Th/F during the day for a max. of 20 people\, pending your confirmation. If
  you would prefer another day or time\, please tell us\, and we'll do our b
 est to accommodate you. Sundays 11:00am-2:00pm are also available\, if book
 ed at least two weeks in advance.\n\nTIME NEEDED:\nIt's best to allow at le
 ast 3 hrs. for a team of up to 10\, and about 3.5-4 hours for more than 10 
 participants\, since we'll need to form two lines of shooting. We may run o
 ver by as much as 30 minutes\, depending on everyone's arrival and ability.
  If this will be a problem\, please let us know\, so we can pace the event 
 carefully.\n\nARRIVALS:  We'll all start together\, so please have everyone
  arrive on time or together. \n\nPARKING: We have limited parking space for
  about 8-10 vehicles. Some corporations decide to park at a nearby shopping
  center parking lot\, and then "carpool" to the archery range.\n\nFEE:  The
 re is a minimum fee of $250 for 1-10 people\, and then $25/person for 11-20
  people. We can accommodate 20 people for $500. If your company requires a 
 separate written receipt for accounting purposes\, please tell us in advanc
 e so we can have one ready for you.\n\nPAYMENT: When you arrive at the rang
 e\, you can pay for the session individually or by corporate check payable 
 to Archery Training Center\, or by credit card (+4%). All fees must be paid
  before the session begins. \n\nREFUNDS: If you pay in advance of arrival\,
  a refund will be issued only for cancellations or reductions in attendees 
 in writing when you give us notice not less than 24 hours before the sessio
 n begins.\n\nEQUIPMENT:  We provide all equipment necessary during the Corp
 orate Team Event.\n\nDRESS RECOMMENDATIONS: Flat shoes are best\, as we sta
 nd a lot and throw our weight forward a little\, so balance and weight dist
 ribution is important. The bowstring can get slowed or entangled in your cl
 othing or hair\, so wearing tighter fitting clothes\, no wide skirts\, shir
 ts without buttons on the front pockets and tying your hair back is prefera
 ble.  Longer brim baseball caps often prevent the string from reaching your
  face\, so shorter brims are better. In the winter on very cold days\, plea
 se dress in layers\, as it may be chilly in the indoor range.\n\nWAIVERS:  
 There will be waivers for each archer to fill out and sign when they first 
 come in\, and before entering the range. All signees must be at least 18 ye
 ars old. For those under 18\, a parent/guardian will need to sign for them.
  \n\nSPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS:    Please let us know if there are any special c
 oncepts you would like us to emphasize\, or any other considerations which 
 you would like us to take into account.\n\nOLYMPIC TARGET ARCHERY LINKS: \n
 Here are some links\, which you and your group may find interesting before 
 you get to the session.\n\nhttp://www.usarchery.org \nhttp://www.olympic.or
 g/archery \nhttp://www.worldarchery.org\nhttp://www.youtube.com/archerytv\n
 \nThe YouTube videos showing the top American male archer\, Brady Ellison\,
  competing with the top Korean archer\, KU Bonchan\, in the Rio Olympics Me
 n's Semi Final Match is the best we've seen in 20 years! You have to watch 
 every shot.\n\nTHANK YOU for your interest in and support of Olympic target
  archery. We know you'll all really enjoy being part of the Olympic Round a
 t the end of your training!!\n\nWe look forward to your time with us.\n\nIf
  you'd like to discuss your reservation in more detail\, please call Coach 
 Racae Meyer 512 975 1850 at your convenience.
