CREATED:20250403T204318Z
DESCRIPTION:<br><b>Alex</b> - <i>At 18m at the field. Just really wanted to
  shoot and score to earn USA Archery Star Pins. Initially tried to do ancho
 r for longer\, but it was frustrating and intermittent. As he gets older\, 
 call his attention to how better form relates to tighter groups\, more cons
 istent scores. Almost shooting instinctively\, but he said he is aiming wit
 h the sight in the middle of the target. Succeeded in scoring enough for th
 e Black and Blue pins. Main emphasis is keeping his enthusiasm up while slo
 wly introducing the steps of shooting as he matures and gets stronger and s
 hoots at longer distances. He's going to be great!</i><br><i><br></i><br><b
 >Alejandro</b>  -  <i>Swaying  forward improved. Worked on increasing back 
 tension by moving right shoulder blade closer to the spine through angular 
 motion until it can't go any further while scooping and pushing up and out 
 towards the target with the bow arm. Lift the bow with your hands\, reducin
 g stress in arms and shoulders at TRANSFER. Slowly began to feel back tensi
 on\, but needs more practice. Practiced exaggerating RELEASE and FOLLOW-THR
 U to feel the difference in how the mid-back moves. Maxing out equally with
  tension and direction towards the target and back and around for FOLLOW-TH
 RU. Improved dynamics.<br></i>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260404T082256Z
LOCATION:5446 W US Hwy 290 Service Rd\, Unit 102\, Austin\, TX 78735\, USA
