UID:4ja96ttk161dj8u53j84hhqmvn@google.com
CREATED:20200110T204646Z
DESCRIPTION:7 people\n\nWe are very happy to host a Corporate Team Archery 
 Event for your group on a mutually convenient date. \n\nThese sessions are 
 proving to be very popular\, and we appreciate the opportunity! \n\nA few o
 f the corporations which schedule events with us are:\nFacebook\, Intel\, D
 ell\, AMD\, Samsung\, Home Away\, National Instruments\, Texas Mutual Insur
 ance\, Electronic Arts\, ERCOT\, Vectra Networks\, Austin Children's Advoca
 cy\, Glatfelder Insurance\, Kerbey Lane\, RackSpace\, Abilitie\, Black Locu
 s\, Boosterthon\, WP Engine\, Camp Gladiator\, Marriott International\, Zim
 mer Biomet\, Austin Gastroenterology\, Yeti\, RetailMeNot\, Tableau Softwar
 e\, Wikibuy/Capital One\, Managed by Q\, GTS Technology Solutions\, Spicewo
 rks and others. \n\nWe also would like to thank your company for its vital\
 , indirect support of USA Archery's Junior Olympic Archery Development (JOA
 D) program! Support like yours grows Olympians! \n\nPlease read the followi
 ng information.\nBelow is a typical agenda for a Corporate Team Event with 
 us\, and some other general info\, which may make things run more smoothly.
  \n\nCAPACITY: 1 to 30 participants. 10 places on the shooting line. If you
 'll have over 10 participants\, even numbers are best\, so we can create te
 ams of two or even three.\n\nDAYS CLOSED: \nMONDAYS and THURSDAYS (but we d
 o open for Corporate Team Events!)\nJAN 1-3: Happy Holidays!\nMAR 17-20 : S
 pring Break !\nAPRIL 11 + 12: Easter Weekend\nMAY 6 : Coach Racae´s birthda
 y !\nMAY 10: Happy Mother´s Day!\nMAY 24-JUNE 5 - Summer Vacation 1\n\nAGEN
 DA (approx.- depends on number and pace of participants)\n\n1:00 Arrival\; 
 waivers (to be signed by participants over 18 years old or adults/parents/g
 uardians)\n1:15 Selecting two-person teams\; equipment review and selection
  (bows\, arrows\, finger tabs\, arm guards\, targets\, etc.)\n1:55 Safety r
 ules\; whistle system\n2:00 Break\n2:10 Form (positions) training (stance\,
  nocking\, hooking/gripping\, set\, mindset\, set-up\, drawing\, anchor\, l
 oading\, aiming\, expanding\, release)\n2:45 Ranking Round: Shooting in tea
 ms\; quantity of arrows will depend on number and pace of participants\n3:4
 5 Olympic Round: Based on ranking round\; each team picks a country to repr
 esent\; all teams progress in a match play to the Gold\, Silver\, and Bronz
 e medal matches\, with other teams cheering them on!\n4:15 Awards Ceremony 
 and podium presentations\, photos!\n\nSCHEDULING:\nWe can schedule a corpor
 ate team event on M/T/W/Th/F during the day for a max. of 30 people\, pendi
 ng your confirmation. If you would prefer another day or time\, please tell
  us\, and we'll do our best to accommodate you. Sundays 11:00am-2:00pm are 
 also available\, if booked at least two weeks in advance for up to 10 peopl
 e..\n\nTIME NEEDED:\nIt's best to allow at least 3 hrs. for a team of up to
  10\, and about 3.5-4 hours for more than 10 participants\, since we'll nee
 d to form two lines of shooting. We may run over by as much as 30 minutes\,
  depending on everyone's arrival and ability. If this will be a problem\, p
 lease let us know\, so we can pace the event carefully.\n\nARRIVALS:  We'll
  all start together\, so please have everyone arrive on time or together. \
 n\nPARKING: We have LIMITED parking space for about 8-10 vehicles. Some cor
 porations decide to park at a nearby shopping center parking lot\, and then
  "carpool" to the archery range.\n\nFEE:  There is a minimum fee of $250 fo
 r 1-10 people\, and then $25/person for 11-30 people. We can accommodate 20
  people for $500 and 30 people for $750. If your company requires a separat
 e written receipt for accounting purposes\, please tell us in advance so we
  can have one ready for you.\n\nPAYMENT: When you arrive at the range\, you
  can pay for the session individually or by corporate check payable to Arch
 ery Training Center\, or by credit card (+4%). All fees must be paid before
  the session begins. \n\nREFUNDS: If you pay in advance of arrival\, a refu
 nd will be issued only for cancellations or reductions in attendees in writ
 ing when given notice not less than 24 hours before the session begins.\n\n
 EQUIPMENT:  We provide all equipment necessary during the Corporate Team Ev
 ent.\n\nDRESS RECOMMENDATIONS: Flat shoes are best\, as we stand a lot and 
 throw our weight forward a little\, so balance and weight distribution is i
 mportant. The bowstring can get slowed or entangled in your clothing or hai
 r\, so wearing tighter fitting clothes\, no wide skirts\, shirts without bu
 ttons on the front pockets and tying your hair back is preferable.  Longer 
 brim baseball caps often prevent the string from reaching your face\, so sh
 orter brims are better. In the winter on very cold days\, please dress in l
 ayers\, as it may be chilly in the indoor range.\n\nWAIVERS:  There will be
  waivers for each archer to fill out and sign when they first come in\, and
  before entering the range. All signees must be at least 18 years old. For 
 those under 18\, a parent/guardian will need to sign for them. \n\nSPECIAL 
 INSTRUCTIONS:    Please let us know if there are any special concepts you w
 ould like us to emphasize\, or any other considerations which you would lik
 e us to take into account.\n\nOLYMPIC TARGET ARCHERY LINKS: \nHere are some
  links\, which you and your group may find interesting before you get to th
 e session.\n\nhttp://www.usarchery.org \nhttp://www.olympic.org/archery \nh
 ttp://www.worldarchery.org\nhttp://www.youtube.com/archerytv\n\nThe YouTube
  videos showing the top American male archer\, Brady Ellison\, competing wi
 th the top Korean archer\, KU Bonchan\, in the Rio Olympics Men's Semi Fina
 l Match is the best we've seen in 20 years! You have to watch every shot.\n
 \nTHANK YOU for your interest in and support of Olympic target archery. We 
 know you'll all really enjoy being part of the Olympic Round at the end of 
 your training!!\n\nWe look forward to your time with us.\n\nIf you'd like t
 o discuss your reservation in more detail\, please call Coach Racae Meyer 5
 12 975 1850 at your convenience.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260404T082256Z
LOCATION:10203 Old Manchaca Rd\, Austin\, TX 78748\, USA
