DESCRIPTION:16 participants <br><br>If you'd like to register for a Corpora
 te Team Event\, just fill out the fields at this link:<br><a href="https://
 docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSc2Lh5MTw61OLmxV93RlHO58HEOBhrnYycyQIqEKrb
 _QsaQLg/viewform">2018 Corporate Team Event</a><br>See you soon!<br><br>We'
 d be very happy to host a Corporate Team Archery Event for your group on a 
 mutually convenient date.&nbsp\;<br>These sessions are proving to be very p
 opular\, and we appreciate the opportunity!&nbsp\;<br>Book now so you're re
 ady for our indoor corporate archery tournaments!<br><br>A few of the corpo
 rations which schedule events with us are Facebook\, Intel\, Dell\, AMD\, H
 ome Away\, National Instruments\, Texas Mutual Insurance\, Electronic Arts\
 , ERCOT\, Vectra Networks\, Austin Children's Advocacy\, Glatfelder Insuran
 ce\, Kerbey Lane\, RackSpace\, Abilitie\, Black Locus\, Boosterthon\, WP En
 gine\, and others.&nbsp\;<br><br>We also would like to thank your company f
 or its vital\, indirect support of USA Archery's Junior Olympic Archery Dev
 elopment (JOAD) program! Support like yours grows Olympians!&nbsp\;<br><br>
 Please read the following information and fill in the fields at the bottom.
 <br>Below is a typical agenda for a Corporate Team Event with us\, and some
  other general info\, which may make things run more smoothly.&nbsp\;<br><b
 r>CAPACITY: 10 places on the shooting line. 1-20 participants. If you'll ha
 ve over 10 participants\, even numbers are best\, so we can create teams of
  two.<br><br>AGENDA (approx.- depends on number and pace of participants)<b
 r><br>1:00 Arrival\; waivers (to be signed by participants over 18 years ol
 d or adults/parents/guardians)<br>1:15 Selecting two-person teams\; equipme
 nt review and selection (bows\, arrows\, finger tabs\, arm guards\, targets
 \, etc.)<br>1:55 Safety rules\; whistle system<br>2:10 Form (positions) tra
 ining (stance\, nocking\, hooking/gripping\, set\, mindset\, set-up\, drawi
 ng\, anchor\, loading\, aiming\, expanding\, release)<br>2:45 Ranking Round
  - shooting in teams\; quantity of arrows will depend on number and pace of
  participants<br>3:45 Olympic Round: Based on ranking round\; each team pic
 ks a country to represent\; all teams progress in a match play to the Gold\
 , Silver\, and Bronze medal matches\, with other teams cheering them on!<br
 >4:15 Awards Ceremony and podium presentations\, photos!
LAST-MODIFIED:20260404T082324Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Corporate Team Event - Marriott Corp.
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
