DESCRIPTION:<b>WAIVERS:</b> Everyone needs to <b>sign the waivers in advanc
 e </b>of arriving at the range\, so we are not delayed in starting. Here's 
 the link: <a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdYr3Yh5msvPHC_
 -ukFsifcvhYXRrzVRvcdyP4Ybx9O5zgUug/viewform" target="_blank"><u><u><u><u><u
 ><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u>2024 Corporate Team Events Waivers Pac
 ket</u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></a>
   As each participant signs the waivers\, it will be indicated on the calen
 dar\, so you will be aware of what we have received. <br><br><b>DIRECTIONS:
 </b> <b>Google Map "Donut Taco Palace"</b> to find us quickly - We are righ
 t next door in Unit 102. (Some people are still being misdirected.) There i
 s a target on the glass door and the unit is facing 290W service road going
  west on the corner of Industrial Oaks Blvd and 290W. <br><br><b>ARRIVAL</b
 >: For a 1:00 pm start\, please <b>arrive by 12:45 pm</b>\, because we need
  to start together at 1:00 pm. <br><br><b>CARPOOLING / PARKING:</b> Please 
 meet and carpool earlier from another location or from a big box store park
 ing lot across the highway (like Target or At Home on the corner of Mopac a
 nd 290W). It's easy and convenient to do. (Parking in front of the range an
 d along Industrial Oaks Blvd may be limited\, depending on the number of pa
 rticipants.)<br><br><b>DRESS RECOMMENDATIONS: </b><br>Flat athletic shoes a
 re best\, as we will be throwing our weight forward a little\, so balance a
 nd weight distribution is important. The bowstring can get slowed or entang
 led in your clothing or hair\, so wearing tightly fitting clothes\, no wide
  skirts\, shirts without buttons on the front pockets and tying your hair b
 ack is preferable. Longer brim baseball caps often prevent the string from 
 reaching your face\, so shorter brims or bucket hats are better.<br><br><b>
 All participants need to complete waivers online before the event.</b><br><
 b>Here is the direct link to complete: </b><a href="https://docs.google.com
 /forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdYr3Yh5msvPHC_-ukFsifcvhYXRrzVRvcdyP4Ybx9O5zgUug/viewfor
 m" target="_blank"><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u
 >2024 Corporate Team Events Waivers Packet</u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u><
 /u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></a>  <br><br>Waivers have been 
 received from those shown below in <b>bold with (W). </b>Last update: 12/6 
 @ 10:00 am<br><br><ol><li><b>Melissa J. (W)</b></li><li><b>Tom G. </b><u></
 u><u></u><b>(W)</b></li><li><b>Paul N. </b><u></u><u></u><b>(W)</b></li><li
 ><b>Jessica K. </b><u></u><u></u><b>(W)</b></li><li><b>Caleb S</b>. <b>(W)<
 /b></li><li><b>Ryan B. (W)</b></li><li><b>Morgan H. </b><b>(W)</b></li><li>
 <b>Randall L. (W)</b></li><li><b>Randall S. </b><b>(W)</b></li><li><b>Chris
  B</b>. <b>(W)</b></li><li>Jerel R.</li><li>Dan R.</li></ol><p><u></u></p><
