DESCRIPTION:<i><b>Thank you for your support of our Olympic Target Archery 
 programs for adults and juniors!</b></i><b><br></b><br><b>WAIVERS:</b> Ever
 yone needs to <b>sign the waivers in advance </b>of arriving at the range\,
  so we are not delayed in starting. Here's the link <a href="https://docs.g
 oogle.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfzW_yYiWOQmAtPOWF8W6pu6m72zrgf3nnQtYjCuAOA5p9iV
 Q/viewform" target="_blank"><b>2025 Waivers for Corporate Team Events</b></
 a><br><br><b>DIRECTIONS:</b> <b>Google Map "Donut Taco Palace"</b> to find 
 us quickly - We are right next door in Unit 102. (Some people are still bei
 ng misdirected.) There is a target on the glass door and the unit is facing
  290W service road going west on the corner of Industrial Oaks Blvd and 290
 W. <br><br><b>ARRIVAL</b>: For a 1:00 pm start\, please <b>arrive by 12:45 
 pm</b>\, because we will all be starting together at 1:00 pm. <br><br><b>CA
 RPOOLING / PARKING:</b> Please meet and carpool earlier from another locati
 on or from a big box store parking lot across the highway (like Target or A
 t Home on the corner of Mopac and 290W). It's easy and convenient to do. (P
 arking in front of the range and along Industrial Oaks Blvd may be limited\
 , depending on the number of participants.)<br><br><b>DRESS RECOMMENDATIONS
 : </b><br>Flat athletic shoes are best\, as we will be throwing our weight 
 forward a little\, so balance and weight distribution is important. The bow
 string can get slowed or entangled in your clothing or hair\, so wearing ti
 ghtly fitting clothes\, no wide skirts\, shirts without buttons on the fron
 t pockets and tying your hair back is preferable. Longer brim baseball caps
  often prevent the string from reaching your face\, so shorter brims or buc
 ket hats are better. <br>:<br><b>All participants need to complete waivers 
 online before the event.</b><br><b>Here is the direct link to complete: </b
 ><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfzW_yYiWOQmAtPOWF8W6pu6
 m72zrgf3nnQtYjCuAOA5p9iVQ/viewform" target="_blank"><u><b>2025 Waivers for 
 Corporate Team Events</b></u></a> <br><br>Waivers have been received from t
 hose shown below in <b>bold with (W)</b><br><i>(Updated: 4/9/25 at 2:30 pm)
 </i><ol><li><b>Gerald H. </b><b>(W) 158 pts</b> <b> </b>(averaged)</li><li>
 <b>Tatum H. </b><b>(W) - 141 pts</b></li><li><b>Dan I. </b><b>(W) - 138 pts
 </b></li><li><b>Olivia H. </b><b>(W) - 110 pts </b><b> </b>(averaged) </li>
 <li><b>Adrian L. </b><b>(W) - 91 pts</b></li><li><b>Evelyn B. (W) - 55 pts 
 </b>(averaged) </li><li><br></li><li><br></li><li><br></li><li><br></li><li
 ><br></li><li>.</li><li>.</li><li>..</li></ol>
