UID:0544i3vrdcv5goesrmoudrmdd7@google.com
CREATED:20200127T150945Z
DESCRIPTION:10 people<br><br>We are very happy to host a Corporate Team Arc
 hery Event for your group on a mutually convenient date.&nbsp\;<br><br>Thes
 e sessions are proving to be very popular\, and we appreciate the opportuni
 ty!&nbsp\;<br><br>A few of the corporations which schedule events with us a
 re:<br>Facebook\, Intel\, Dell\, AMD\, Samsung\, Home Away\, National Instr
 uments\, Texas Mutual Insurance\, Electronic Arts\, ERCOT\, Vectra Networks
 \, Austin Children's Advocacy\, Glatfelder Insurance\, Kerbey Lane\, RackSp
 ace\, Abilitie\, Black Locus\, Boosterthon\, WP Engine\, Camp Gladiator\, M
 arriott International\, Zimmer Biomet\, Austin Gastroenterology\, Yeti\, Re
 tailMeNot\, Tableau Software\, Wikibuy/Capital One\, Managed by Q\, GTS Tec
 hnology Solutions\, Spiceworks and others.&nbsp\;<br><br>We also would like
  to thank your company for its vital\, indirect support of USA Archery's Ju
 nior Olympic Archery Development (JOAD) program! Support like yours grows O
 lympians!&nbsp\;<br><br>Please read the following information.<br>Below is 
 a typical agenda for a Corporate Team Event with us\, and some other genera
 l info\, which may make things run more smoothly.&nbsp\;<br><br>CAPACITY: 1
  to 30 participants. 10 places on the shooting line. If you'll have over 10
  participants\, even numbers are best\, so we can create teams of two or ev
 en three.<br><br>DAYS CLOSED:&nbsp\;<br>MONDAYS and THURSDAYS (but we do op
 en for Corporate Team Events!)<br>JAN 1-3: Happy Holidays!<br>MAR 17-20 : S
 pring Break !<br>APRIL 11 + 12: Easter Weekend<br>MAY 6 : Coach Racae´s bir
 thday !<br>MAY 10: Happy Mother´s Day!<br>MAY 24-JUNE 5 - Summer Vacation 1
 <br><br>AGENDA (approx.- depends on number and pace of participants)<br><br
 >1:00 Arrival\; waivers (to be signed by participants over 18 years old or 
 adults/parents/guardians)<br>1:15 Selecting two-person teams\; equipment re
 view and selection (bows\, arrows\, finger tabs\, arm guards\, targets\, et
 c.)<br>1:55 Safety rules\; whistle system<br>2:00 Break<br>2:10 Form (posit
 ions) training (stance\, nocking\, hooking/gripping\, set\, mindset\, set-u
 p\, drawing\, anchor\, loading\, aiming\, expanding\, release)<br>2:45 Rank
 ing Round: Shooting in teams\; quantity of arrows will depend on number and
  pace of participants<br>3:45 Olympic Round: Based on ranking round\; each 
 team picks a country to represent\; all teams progress in a match play to t
 he Gold\, Silver\, and Bronze medal matches\, with other teams cheering the
 m on!<br>4:15 Awards Ceremony and podium presentations\, photos!<br><br>SCH
 EDULING:<br>We can schedule a corporate team event on M/T/W/Th/F during the
  day for a max. of 30 people\, pending your confirmation. If you would pref
 er another day or time\, please tell us\, and we'll do our best to accommod
 ate you. Sundays 11:00am-2:00pm are also available\, if booked at least two
  weeks in advance for up to 10 people..<br><br>TIME NEEDED:<br>It's best to
  allow at least 3 hrs. for a team of up to 10\, and about 3.5-4 hours for m
 ore than 10 participants\, since we'll need to form two lines of shooting. 
 We may run over by as much as 30 minutes\, depending on everyone's arrival 
 and ability. If this will be a problem\, please let us know\, so we can pac
 e the event carefully.<br><br>ARRIVALS: We'll all start together\, so pleas
 e have everyone arrive on time or together.&nbsp\;<br><br>PARKING: We have 
 LIMITED parking space for about 8-10 vehicles. Some corporations decide to 
 park at a nearby shopping center parking lot\, and then "carpool" to the ar
 chery range.<br><br>FEE: There is a minimum fee of $250 for 1-10 people\, a
 nd then $25/person for 11-30 people. We can accommodate 20 people for $500 
 and 30 people for $750. If your company requires a separate written receipt
  for accounting purposes\, please tell us in advance so we can have one rea
 dy for you.<br><br>PAYMENT: When you arrive at the range\, you can pay for 
 the session individually or by corporate check payable to Archery Training 
 Center\, or by credit card (+4%). All fees must be paid before the session 
 begins.&nbsp\;<br><br>REFUNDS: If you pay in advance of arrival\, a refund 
 will be issued only for cancellations or reductions in attendees in writing
  when given notice not less than 24 hours before the session begins.<br><br
 >EQUIPMENT: We provide all equipment necessary during the Corporate Team Ev
 ent.<br><br>DRESS RECOMMENDATIONS: Flat shoes are best\, as we stand a lot 
 and throw our weight forward a little\, so balance and weight distribution 
 is important. The bowstring can get slowed or entangled in your clothing or
  hair\, so wearing tighter fitting clothes\, no wide skirts\, shirts withou
 t buttons on the front pockets and tying your hair back is preferable. Long
 er brim baseball caps often prevent the string from reaching your face\, so
  shorter brims are better. In the winter on very cold days\, please dress i
 n layers\, as it may be chilly in the indoor range.<br><br>WAIVERS: There w
 ill be waivers for each archer to fill out and sign when they first come in
 \, and before entering the range. All signees must be at least 18 years old
 . For those under 18\, a parent/guardian will need to sign for them.&nbsp\;
 <br><br>SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS: Please let us know if there are any special c
 oncepts you would like us to emphasize\, or any other considerations which 
 you would like us to take into account.<br><br>OLYMPIC TARGET ARCHERY LINKS
 :&nbsp\;<br>Here are some links\, which you and your group may find interes
 ting before you get to the session.<br><br><a href="http://www.usarchery.or
 g">http://www.usarchery.org</a>&nbsp\;<br><a href="http://www.olympic.org/a
 rchery">http://www.olympic.org/archery</a>&nbsp\;<br><a href="http://www.wo
 rldarchery.org">http://www.worldarchery.org</a><br><a href="http://www.yout
 ube.com/archerytv">http://www.youtube.com/archerytv</a><br><br>The YouTube 
 videos showing the top American male archer\, Brady Ellison\, competing wit
 h the top Korean archer\, KU Bonchan\, in the Rio Olympics Men's Semi Final
  Match is the best we've seen in 20 years! You have to watch every shot.<br
 ><br>THANK YOU for your interest in and support of Olympic target archery. 
 We know you'll all really enjoy being part of the Olympic Round at the end 
 of your training!!<br><br>We look forward to your time with us.<br><br>If y
 ou'd like to discuss your reservation in more detail\, please call Coach Ra
 cae Meyer 512 975 1850 at your convenience.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260404T082256Z
LOCATION:10203 Old Manchaca Rd\, Austin\, TX 78748\, USA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Corporate Team Event - RxSaver by RetailMeNot - Rustin
TRANSP:OPAQUE
