CREATED:20190722T143151Z
DESCRIPTION:up to 20 people\n\nWe're very happy to host a Corporate Team Ar
 chery Event for your group on a mutually convenient date. \n\nThese session
 s are proving to be very popular\, and we appreciate the opportunity! \nBoo
 k now so you're ready for our indoor corporate archery tournaments!\n\nA fe
 w of the corporations which schedule events with us are:\n\nFacebook\, Inte
 l\, Dell\, AMD\, Samsung\, Home Away\, National Instruments\, Texas Mutual 
 Insurance\, Electronic Arts\, ERCOT\, Vectra Networks\, Austin Children's A
 dvocacy\, Glatfelder Insurance\, Kerbey Lane\, RackSpace\, Abilitie\, Black
  Locus\, Boosterthon\, WP Engine\, Camp Gladiator\, Marriott International\
 , Zimmer Biomet\, Austin Gastroenterology\, Yeti\, RetailMeNot\, Tableau So
 ftware and others. \n\nWe also would like to thank your company for its vit
 al\, indirect support of USA Archery's Junior Olympic Archery Development (
 JOAD) program! Support like yours grows Olympians! \n\nBelow is a typical a
 genda for a Corporate Team Event with us\, and some other general info\, wh
 ich may make things run more smoothly. \n\nCAPACITY: Up to 20 participants.
  If you'll have over 10 participants\, even numbers are best\, so we can cr
 eate teams of two\, with up to 10 people on the shooting line at once.\n\nD
 AYS CLOSED: \nMONDAYS and THURSDAYS\nJAN 1-5: Happy Holidays!\nAPRIL 21: Ha
 ppy Easter !\nMAY 12: Happy Mother´s Day!\nMAY 26-JUNE 7 - Summer Vacation 
 1\nJUNE 16 - Happy Father´s Day!\nAUG 11 - 24th ANNUAL ARCHERS OF THE YEAR 
 POTLUCK BANQUET 5:30-7:30pm - Mark your calendars NOW!\nAUG 12-23 - Summer 
 Vacation 2\n\nTYPICAL AGENDA (approx.- depends on arrival time\, number and
  pace of participants)\n\n1:00 Arrival\; waivers (to be signed by participa
 nts over 18 years old or adults/parents/guardians)\n1:15 Introduction\n1:25
  Selecting two-person teams\; equipment review and selection (bows\, arrows
 \, finger tabs\, arm guards\, targets\, etc.)\n1:55 Safety rules\; whistle 
 system\n2:00 Break\n2:10 Form (positions) training (stance\, nocking\, hook
 ing/gripping\, set\, mindset\, set-up\, drawing\, anchor\, loading\, aiming
 \, expanding\, release\, follow-through)\n2:45 Ranking Round - shooting in 
 teams\; quantity of arrows will depend on number and pace of participants\n
 3:45 Olympic Round: Based on ranking round\; each team picks a country to r
 epresent\; all teams progress in a match play to the Gold\, Silver\, and Br
 onze medal matches\, with other teams cheering them on!\n4:15 Awards Ceremo
 ny and podium presentations\, photos!\n\nSCHEDULING:\nWe can schedule a cor
 porate team event on T/W/Th during the day for a max. of 20 people\, pendin
 g your confirmation. If you would prefer another day or time\, please tell 
 us\, and we'll do our best to accommodate you. Sundays 11:00am-2:00pm are a
 lso available\, if booked at least two weeks in advance.\n\nTIME NEEDED:\nI
 t's best to allow at least 3 hrs. for a team of up to 10\, and about 3.5-4 
 hours for more than 10 participants\, since we'll need to form two lines of
  shooting. We may run over by as much as 30 minutes\, depending on everyone
 's arrival and ability. If this will be a problem\, please let us know\, so
  we can pace the event carefully.\n\nARRIVALS: We'll all start together\, s
 o please have everyone arrive on time or together. \n\nPARKING: We have lim
 ited parking space for about 8-10 vehicles. Some corporations decide to par
 k at a nearby shopping center parking lot\, and then "carpool" to the arche
 ry range.\n\nFEE: There is a minimum fee of $250 for 1-10 people\, and then
  $25/person for 11-20 people. We can accommodate 20 people for $500. If you
 r company requires a separate written receipt for accounting purposes\, ple
 ase tell us in advance so we can have one ready for you.\n\nPAYMENT: When y
 ou arrive at the range\, you can pay for the session individually or by cor
 porate check payable to Archery Training Center\, or by credit card (+4%). 
 All fees must be paid before the session begins. \n\nREFUNDS: If you pay in
  advance of arrival\, a refund will be issued only for cancellations or red
 uctions in attendees in writing when given notice not less than 24 hours be
 fore the session begins.\n\nEQUIPMENT: We provide all equipment necessary d
 uring the Corporate Team Event.\n\nDRESS RECOMMENDATIONS: Flat shoes are be
 st\, as we stand a lot and throw our weight forward a little\, so balance a
 nd weight distribution is important. The bowstring can get slowed or entang
 led in your clothing or hair\, so wearing tighter fitting clothes\, no wide
  skirts\, shirts without buttons on the front pockets and tying your hair b
 ack is preferable. Longer brim baseball caps often prevent the string from 
 reaching your face\, so shorter brims are better. In the winter on very col
 d days\, please dress in layers\, as it may be chilly in the indoor range.\
 n\nWAIVERS: There will be waivers for each archer to fill out and sign when
  they first come in\, and before entering the range. All signees must be at
  least 18 years old. For those under 18\, a parent/guardian will need to si
 gn for them. \n\nSPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS: Please let us know if there are any 
 special concepts you would like us to emphasize\, or any other consideratio
 ns which you would like us to take into account.\n\nOLYMPIC TARGET ARCHERY 
 LINKS: \nHere are some links\, which you and your group may find interestin
 g before you get to the session.\n\nhttp://www.usarchery.org \nhttp://www.o
 lympic.org/archery \nhttp://www.worldarchery.org\nhttp://www.youtube.com/ar
 cherytv\n\nThe YouTube videos showing the top American male archer\, Brady 
 Ellison\, competing with the top Korean archer\, KU Bonchan\, in the Rio Ol
 ympics Men's Semi Final Match is the best we've seen in 20 years! You have 
 to watch every shot.\n\nTHANK YOU for your interest in and support of Olymp
 ic target archery. We know you'll all really enjoy being part of the Olympi
 c Round at the end of your training!!\n\nWe look forward to your time with 
 us.\n\nIf you'd like to discuss your reservation in more detail\, please ca
 ll Coach Racae Meyer 512 975 1850 at your convenience.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260404T082256Z
LOCATION:10203 Old Manchaca Rd\, Austin\, TX 78748\, USA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Corporate Team Event - Wikibuy / Capital One - Susan
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
