DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><br><b>2022 Winter/Spring Schedule and Goals for Out
 door 2-9 (9m to 70m):&nbsp\;</b><br>&nbsp\;<br><b>FEBRUARY</b><br><b>&nbsp\
 ; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>12-18</b>&nbsp\;Welcome Back: Understanding&nbsp\; 
 NTS Concepts&nbsp\;<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>19-25</b>&nbsp\;NTS
  Steps 1+2: STANCE + NOCK&nbsp\;<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>26 - M
 AR 4: MASTER CHALLENGE TOURNAMENT WEEK (Pin Shoot)</b><br><b>MARCH</b><br><
 b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;5-11</b>&nbsp\;NTS Step 3: HOOK &amp\; GRIP&nbsp\;
 <br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;12-18</b>&nbsp\; NTS Step 4: SET&nbsp\;&nbsp\
 ;<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;<b>19-25&nbsp\;</b>NTS Step 5: SET-UP&nbsp\;<br
 ><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>26 - APR 1: MASTER CHALLENGE TOURNAMENT W
 EEK (Pin Shoot)</b><br><b>APRIL</b><br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;2-8</b>&nb
 sp\; NTS Step 6 DRAW to LOAD&nbsp\;<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;9-15&nbsp\
 ;</b>&nbsp\;NTS Step 7 ANCHOR&nbsp\;<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;<b>16-22&nbs
 p\;</b>NTS Step 8 TRANSFER to HOLD<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;23-29&nbsp\
 ;</b>NTS Step 9 EXPAND / AIM&nbsp\;<b><br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>30 
 - MAY 6: MASTER CHALLENGE TOURNAMENT WEEK (Pin Shoot)</b><br><b>MAY</b><br>
 <b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>7-13&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</b>NTS Step 10 RELEASE 
 + FOLLOW-THROUGH<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>14-20</b>&nbsp\; NTS S
 tep 11: FEEDBACK + Putting it all together!<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</
 b><b>21/22 : END OF SEMESTER TOURNAMENT WEEKEND (Pin Shoot)</b><br><br>Each
  week the focus of your lessons will be on particular Steps of Shooting of 
 the NTS (National Training System) shot cycle\, to help you focus and impro
 ve your form\, which\, as we all know\, leads to greater precision (tight g
 roups of arrows) and ultimately greater accuracy (tight groups of arrows de
 ad center).<br><br>Your goal is always to replicate the NTS step(s) mindful
 ly and consistently on every shot.<br><br>You do not need to score in every
  class. In fact\, it would be more beneficial to you if you scored only dur
 ing Master Challenge Tournament Weeks\, which happen the last week of each 
 month. This is because working on the NTS Steps of Shooting (your form) is 
 more easily done without the distraction of the target face or scoring\, an
 d you will improve faster.<br><br>As you reach higher levels\, you will lea
 rn the NTS Steps in progressively greater detail.<br>The NTS Steps are cumu
 lative with each step most successfully completed if the previous steps hav
 e been completed well.&nbsp\;<br><br>Your ability to learn and understand t
 he NTS Steps\, and use deep focus on these Steps while shooting outdoors an
 d while using your stretchband/string loop at home to reinforce form poisit
 ions will propel you to higher levels fast!<br><br><b>Goals by the end of t
 he semester (May 22):&nbsp\;</b><br>See Coach Racae´s email ¨2022 New Year´
 s Goals¨</html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260404T082256Z
