UID:2qqms496fm3ngos1rdkfp5u4er@google.com
CREATED:20190626T185752Z
DESCRIPTION:10 people\n\nWe'd be very happy to host a Corporate Team Archer
 y Event for your group on a mutually convenient date. \n\nThese sessions ar
 e proving to be very popular\, and we appreciate the opportunity! \nBook no
 w so you're ready for our indoor corporate archery tournaments!\n\nA few of
  the corporations which schedule events with us are:\nFacebook\, Intel\, De
 ll\, AMD\, Samsung\, Home Away\, National Instruments\, Texas Mutual Insura
 nce\, Electronic Arts\, ERCOT\, Vectra Networks\, Austin Children's Advocac
 y\, Glatfelder Insurance\, Kerbey Lane\, RackSpace\, Abilitie\, Black Locus
 \, Boosterthon\, WP Engine\, Camp Gladiator\, Marriott International\, Zimm
 er Biomet\, Austin Gastroenterology\, Yeti\, RetailMeNot\, Tableau Software
  and others. \n\nWe also would like to thank your company for its vital\, i
 ndirect support of USA Archery's Junior Olympic Archery Development (JOAD) 
 program! Support like yours grows Olympians! \n\nPlease read the following 
 information and fill in the fields at the bottom.\nBelow is a typical agend
 a for a Corporate Team Event with us\, and some other general info\, which 
 may make things run more smoothly. \n\nCAPACITY: 1-20 participants. 10 plac
 es on the shooting line. If you'll have over 10 participants\, even numbers
  are best\, so we can create teams of two.\n\nDAYS CLOSED: \nMONDAYS and TH
 URSDAYS\nJAN 1-5: Happy Holidays!\nAPRIL 21: Happy Easter !\nMAY 12: Happy 
 Mother´s Day!\nMAY 26-JUNE 7 - Summer Vacation 1\nJUNE 16 - Father´s Day!\n
 AUG 11 - 24th ANNUAL ARCHERS OF THE YEAR POTLUCK BANQUET 5:30-7:30pm - Mark
  your calendars NOW!\nAUG 12-23 - Summer Vacation 2\n\nAGENDA (approx.- dep
 ends on number and pace of participants)\n\n1:00 Arrival\; waivers (to be s
 igned by participants over 18 years old or adults/parents/guardians)\n1:15 
 Selecting two-person teams\; equipment review and selection (bows\, arrows\
 , finger tabs\, arm guards\, targets\, etc.)\n1:55 Safety rules\; whistle s
 ystem\n2:00 Break\n2:10 Form (positions) training (stance\, nocking\, hooki
 ng/gripping\, set\, mindset\, set-up\, drawing\, anchor\, loading\, aiming\
 , expanding\, release\, follow-through)\n2:45 Ranking Round - shooting in t
 eams\; quantity of arrows will depend on number and pace of participants\n3
 :45 Olympic Round: Based on ranking round\; each team picks a country to re
 present\; all teams progress in a match play to the Gold\, Silver\, and Bro
 nze medal matches\, with other teams cheering them on!\n4:15 Awards Ceremon
 y and podium presentations\, photos!\n\nSCHEDULING:\nWe can schedule a corp
 orate team event on T/W/Th during the day for a max. of 20 people\, pending
  your confirmation. If you would prefer another day or time\, please tell u
 s\, and we'll do our best to accommodate you. Sundays 11:00am-2:00pm are al
 so available\, if booked at least two weeks in advance.\n\nTIME NEEDED:\nIt
 's best to allow at least 3 hrs. for a team of up to 10\, and about 3.5-4 h
 ours for more than 10 participants\, since we'll need to form two lines of 
 shooting. We may run over by as much as 30 minutes\, depending on everyone'
 s arrival and ability. If this will be a problem\, please let us know\, so 
 we can pace the event carefully.\n\nARRIVALS: We'll all start together\, so
  please have everyone arrive on time or together. \n\nPARKING: We have limi
 ted parking space for about 8-10 vehicles. Some corporations decide to park
  at a nearby shopping center parking lot\, and then "carpool" to the archer
 y range.\n\nFEE: There is a minimum fee of $250 for 1-10 people\, and then 
 $25/person for 11-20 people. We can accommodate 20 people for $500. If your
  company requires a separate written receipt for accounting purposes\, plea
 se tell us in advance so we can have one ready for you.\n\nPAYMENT: When yo
 u arrive at the range\, you can pay for the session individually or by corp
 orate check payable to Archery Training Center\, or by credit card (+4%). A
 ll fees must be paid before the session begins. \n\nREFUNDS: If you pay in 
 advance of arrival\, a refund will be issued only for cancellations or redu
 ctions in attendees in writing when given notice not less than 24 hours bef
 ore the session begins.\n\nEQUIPMENT: We provide all equipment necessary du
 ring the Corporate Team Event.\n\nDRESS RECOMMENDATIONS: Flat shoes are bes
 t\, as we stand a lot and throw our weight forward a little\, so balance an
 d weight distribution is important. The bowstring can get slowed or entangl
 ed in your clothing or hair\, so wearing tighter fitting clothes\, no wide 
 skirts\, shirts without buttons on the front pockets and tying your hair ba
 ck is preferable. Longer brim baseball caps often prevent the string from r
 eaching your face\, so shorter brims are better. In the winter on very cold
  days\, please dress in layers\, as it may be chilly in the indoor range.\n
 \nWAIVERS: There will be waivers for each archer to fill out and sign when 
 they first come in\, and before entering the range. All signees must be at 
 least 18 years old. For those under 18\, a parent/guardian will need to sig
 n for them. \n\nSPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS: Please let us know if there are any s
 pecial concepts you would like us to emphasize\, or any other consideration
 s which you would like us to take into account.\n\nOLYMPIC TARGET ARCHERY L
 INKS: \nHere are some links\, which you and your group may find interesting
  before you get to the session.\n\nhttp://www.usarchery.org \nhttp://www.ol
 ympic.org/archery \nhttp://www.worldarchery.org\nhttp://www.youtube.com/arc
 herytv\n\nThe YouTube videos showing the top American male archer\, Brady E
 llison\, competing with the top Korean archer\, KU Bonchan\, in the Rio Oly
 mpics Men's Semi Final Match is the best we've seen in 20 years! You have t
 o watch every shot.\n\nTHANK YOU for your interest in and support of Olympi
 c target archery. We know you'll all really enjoy being part of the Olympic
  Round at the end of your training!!\n\nWe look forward to your time with u
 s.\n\nIf you'd like to discuss your reservation in more detail\, please cal
 l Coach Racae Meyer 512 975 1850 at your convenience.
