DESCRIPTION:<b>NTS Step 7: Anchor </b>(See details in email)<br>Stabilizes 
 the back of the arrow by providing two consistent connections\, one with un
 derside of the jaw and one with the nose\, while continuing angular motion\
 , which results in 90% back tension.<br><ol><li>Head in final fixed positio
 n</li><li>Maintain previous positions</li><li>LAN 2 direction of movement</
 li><li>Draw side:<ul><li><span>Hand </span><ul><li>Knuckle</li><li>Index fi
 nger</li><li>Little finger</li><li>Thumb</li></ul></li><li>Wrist</li><li>Fo
 rearm<br></li><li>Nose</li><li>Teeth</li><li>Elbow</li><li>Scapula</li></ul
 ></li><li>No gap</li><li>String position on jaw and nose</li><li>No aiming<
 /li></ol><br><br><b><br></b><br><b><br></b>\n\nJoin with Google Meet: https
 ://meet.google.com/trc-oast-vhz\n\nLearn more about Meet at: https://suppor
 t.google.com/a/users/answer/9282720
