UID:cgomae1ic4rm4b9ncdgjib9kcks64bb160pj2bb2cpijeohp6hijcchgcc@google.com
CREATED:20190309T002855Z
DESCRIPTION:<b>PRIVATE LESSONS</b><br><br>We train all our archers in Olymp
 ic target archery\, and specifically in the National Training System (NTS)\
 , as researched and instructed at the Olympic Training Center in Chula Vist
 a\, CA by National Coach KiSik Lee and practiced by the resident athletes a
 nd US national archery teams.<br><br>Private lessons with Coach Racae are a
 vailable to adults and juniors at different levels of experience\, most can
  be one or two hours long\, and are intensive.&nbsp\;<br><br><b>Times</b><b
 r>Private lessons are available at times listed below\, which are adjacent 
 to regularly scheduled classes.&nbsp\;<br>(Check the website calendar first
  to make sure the time is not already booked).&nbsp\;<br>Tues/Wed: 3:00-5:3
 0 PM<br>Fri: 6:00-8::30pm<br>Sat: 6:00-7:00 PM<br>Sun: 10:30-11:30 AM<br>If
  you prefer a time outside of the hours listed above\, but still not during
  regularly scheduled class hours\, an additional $25/hr fee will be added t
 o the regular fee below.<br><br><b>Contact </b>Coach Racae at archerytraini
 ngcenteraustin@gmail.com or call 512 975 1850<br>to request a time after se
 lecting one of the following types of private lessons:&nbsp\;<br><br><b>Eva
 luation</b> : 1 hrs : Fee: $50/hr<br>For recurve archers with at least one 
 year of experience. Your positions will be analyzed with a view to placing 
 you within the ATCI ongoing classes at the level you have attained. Your sc
 ores will be of secondary consideration. How coachable and open to change y
 ou are is important. If you have a coach at present\, it is necessary for y
 ou to inform your coach that you are coming to us for an evaluation\, you’l
 l need to give us your coach’’s name\, so we can discuss your goals and pri
 orities with him/her. If you do not have a coach at present or have not lea
 rned or practiced the NTS method of shooting before\, the NTS is different 
 from “straight shooting”\, and requires more strength to execute\, usually 
 resulting in fewer injuries and stronger\, more powerful shots for the same
  bow weight.<br><br><b>NTS Overview</b>: (age: 10+) : 2 hrs : Fee: $100<br>
 For beginning archers with experience of less than one (1) year who want an
  overview of the NTS (the form) and are ready to receive\, understand\, and
  implement a lot of information and instruction in a very short period of t
 ime\, with repetitive drills on the NTS form positions.&nbsp\;<br><br><b>NT
 S Review:</b> (age 10+) : 1 or 2 hrs: Fee: $50/hr<br>For archers at any lev
 el who are regular attendees of the group classes and who feel they need mo
 re one-on-one time with Coach Racae to better know\, understand\, and imple
 ment the NTS form positions.<br><b><br></b><br><b>NTS Details: </b>(age: 10
 +) : 1 or 2 hrs: Fee: $50/hr<br>For archers at Indoor 3A (13.5m) level or a
 bove\, who are regular attendees of the group classes\, want their form to 
 be evaluated in detail\, and are willing to work on the NTS form positions 
 in order to break through to a higher level or prepare for the annual  Comp
 etitive Archery Program (CAP) Draft Tournament\, where the minimum qualifyi
 ng score (MQS) is 250 pts at 18m.<br><br><b>Mental Management</b> (coming s
 oon) : 1 or 2 hrs: Fee: $75/hr<br>For archers at any level who believe they
  would benefit from understanding what to think\, and when to think it\, ho
 w to adopt a better attitude\, more positive outlook\, and appropriate focu
 s. There are many elements\, so each of these private lessons will cover th
 ose areas that will be of most benefit to you personally\, based on your go
 als.&nbsp\;<br><br><b>Goal Setting</b> (coming soon) : 1 or 2 hrs: Fee: $75
 /hr<br>For archers at any level who want to have a detailed structure to th
 eir training. Be prepared to answer a lot of questions in advance of the le
 sson in order to set specific goals and then work on what is needed to do n
 ow to reach your ultimate goal! Join our 2028 Team heading for the Olympics
  in LA!
LAST-MODIFIED:20260404T082256Z
LOCATION:10203 Old Manchaca Rd
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Private Lesson/Evaluation with Coach Racae - Schneider
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20220623
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20220624
DTSTAMP:20261004T164458Z
UID:6ak4ubjvkruai047l341f5heni@google.com
CREATED:20220603T213817Z
DESCRIPTION:<b>2022 Summer Schedule and Goals for Outdoor 2-9 (9m to 70m)</
 b><br><b><br></b><br><b>Goals by the end of the summer semester (Aug 14):&n
 bsp\;</b><br>Make a list of what you want to accomplish<b><br></b>&nbsp\;<b
 r><b>JUNE</b><br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>2-5</b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &n
 bsp\; Welcome Back: Understanding&nbsp\; NTS Concepts \; Mental Program<br>
 <b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>9-12</b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; NTS Steps 1+2: STA
 NCE + NOCK&nbsp\;<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\;&nbsp\;<b>16-19&nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b>NTS S
 tep 3: HOOK &amp\; GRIP&nbsp\;<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; 25/</b><b>26&nbsp\; JU
 NE ATCI MASTER CHALLENGE TOURNAMENT (Pin Shoot)</b><br><b>JULY</b><br><b>&n
 bsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;6/30-7/3&nbsp\;</b>NTS Step 4: SET\; NTS Step 5: SET-U
 P&nbsp\;<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;7-10</b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;NTS St
 ep 6 DRAW to LOAD&nbsp\;<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;<b>14-17&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</
 b>NTS Step 7 ANCHOR&nbsp\;<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>21-24&nbsp\;
 &nbsp\;</b>NTS Step 8 TRANSFER to HOLD<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;30/31&n
 bsp\; JULY ATCI MASTER CHALLENGE TOURNAMENT (Pin Shoot)</b><br><b>AUGUST</b
 ><br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;4-7</b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;NTS St
 ep 9 EXPAND / AIM&nbsp\;<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;11-14</b>&nbsp\; NTS 
 Step 10 RELEASE + FOLLOW-THROUGH<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;<b>18-21</b>&nbs
 p\;<b>&nbsp\;</b>NTS Step 11: FEEDBACK + Putting it all together!<b><br>&nb
 sp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>27/28&nbsp\; AUGUST ATCI MASTER CHALLENGE TOURNA
 MENT (Pin Shoot)</b><br><br>Each week the focus of your lessons will be on 
 particular Steps of Shooting of the NTS (National Training System) shot cyc
 le\, to help you focus and improve your form\, which\, as we all know\, lea
 ds to greater and consistent precision (tight groups of arrows) and ultimat
 ely greater accuracy (tight groups of arrows dead center).<br><br>Your goal
  is always to replicate the NTS step(s) mindfully and consistently on every
  shot. If you stay in the present just doing what you need to do as you nee
 d to it\, your conscious mind will be occupied\, instead of random thoughts
  entering your head or you being distracted by emotional or environmental e
 lements. You´ll need to build up your mental program alongside your form kn
 owledge\, so when your body is trained to shoot excellent shots\, your self
  image and subsonscious support you\, instead of undermining you. Confidenc
 e and consistency in form and mind are major goals.<br><br>You do not need 
 to score in every class. In fact\, it would be more beneficial to you if yo
 u scored only during Master Challenge Tournament Weeks\, which happen the l
 ast week of each month. This is because working on the NTS Steps of Shootin
 g (your form) is more easily done without the distraction of the target fac
 e or scoring\, and you will improve faster.<br><br>As you reach higher leve
 ls\, you will learn the NTS Steps in progressively greater detail.<br>The N
 TS Steps are cumulative with each step most successfully completed if the p
 revious steps have been completed well.&nbsp\;<br><br>Your ability to learn
  and understand the NTS Steps\, and use deep focus on these Steps while sho
 oting outdoors and while using your stretchband/string loop at home to rein
 force form poisitions will propel you to higher levels fast!
LAST-MODIFIED:20260404T082256Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:FORM FOCUS: NTS Steps 1-3 Review
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
