  outdoor competitive archers on Wed 4:00-8:00. Check the calendar\, and whe
 n a time has already been booked by another archer\,\, select an adjacent t
 ime. <span>Send an email to Coach Racae with a date and time.</span><span> 
 (Competitive archers should register for a private lesson at least once per
  month.)</span></i><br><i>30 min : $65</i><br><i>60 min: $125</i><br><br>Gr
 eat progress! Well done\, Adrianne! <br><b>Today's Notes:</b><br>Worked on 
 (in order of shot sequence):<br>3. GRIP: Angle of knuckles to ledge\, broad
 ness of back of hand\, tension in pinkie. Pressure point deep within grip. 
 Grabbing bow. Sync release soon.<br>4. SET Too straight - core tight\, ches
 t down\, shoulders down\, back and level\; weight balanced<br>5. SET UP: Bo
 w arm: Push and scoop to keep bow shoulder down\, confirming shoulder stays
  down\, increases draw length\; <br>Draw shoulder: Stays down while raising
 <br>Draw forearm: Level<br>More coiling to line up shoulders with bow arm. 
 <br>Bow arm needs strengthening. Practice holding bow in T alignment in 30-
 sec reps\, 60-sec rest\, repeat until form starts going off or shaking<br>6
 . DRAW TO LOAD: Too much in upper shoulders\, reduce tension\, shift tensio
 n into mid back (mid and lower traps). Draw by coiling\, not arms. Standing
  against outside corner and against wall to feel movement of scapula pushin
 g out from wall. Need to feel scapula movement better. LAN 2 movement and d
 irection. See photos of scapulae positions in Inside the Archer book.<br>7.
  ANCHOR - Draw elbow too high\, should ideally be in line with arrow. After
  setting height of forearm near neck\, just lift forearm and hand o Anchor 
 and hand to anchor position (not elbow)<br>8. TRANSFER TO HOLD - Alignment 
 needs to improve earlier in order to do a good Transfer to Hold. Practice H
 olding SPT<br>7. EXPAND/AIM - Arrow too long for clicker\, even with presen
 t improvements in alignments\, but we will wait for better alignment instea
 d of cutting arrows. Not yet ready for clicker.<br>8. RELEASE/FOLLOW-THRU: 
 Draw hand flies out upon Release. Tighten bicep.  F/T - more arm than back 
 tension.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260404T082256Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Private Lesson with Coach Racae - Adrianne
TRANSP:OPAQUE
