DTSTAMP:20261004T164458Z
UID:7c1ucl3gpfoe8cg7ejloirr9fm@google.com
CREATED:20190326T191705Z
DESCRIPTION:\nTHANKS SO MUCH for giving us the opportunity to share your sp
 ecial day!\nIt helps our Junior Olympic Archery program (JOAD) a lot when y
 ou introduce your friends to the fun of Olympic target archery!\n\nPLEASE R
 EAD THE INFO BELOW - AND THEN FILL OUT THE FORM AT THE BOTTOM\n\nHere are a
  few things that may help you plan....\n\nADDRESSES:\nRANGE:    10203 OLD M
 anchaca Rd.\, Austin\, TX 78748\nMAILING:  Archery Training Center\, Inc.\,
  PO Box 93216\, Austin\, TX 78709\n\nE-MAIL: archerytrainingcenteraustin@gm
 ail.com\n\nTIMES OPEN:\nPlease drop in during business hours to visit.\nCHE
 CK THE ONLINE CALENDAR before coming in case class schedules and opening ti
 mes have changed.\nYou'll need to be registered in a class in order to use 
 the range.\nSUNDAYS:       11:30am-6:00pm\nTUESDAYS:       5:30pm-8:30pm\nW
 EDNESDAYS: 5:30pm-8:30pm\nTHURSDAYS:    6:00pm-8:30pm (when there is a firs
 t-time class)\nSATURDAYS:   11:30am-6:00pm\n(We are OPEN during Spring Brea
 k: March 12-16)\n\nWHAT AGES?\n10 years old and above. (We do adult birthda
 y parties\, too!)\nChildren not participating must be supervised by an adul
 t from your party.\n\nHOW MANY ARCHERS?\nMax. of 10 archers. \n\nWHAT DAYS 
 and TIMES ARE AVAILABLE?\nFirst check www.archerytrainingcenter.com/calenda
 r to make sure another party or individuals have not already booked the tim
 e you would like to come. We sometimes use the range for open practice on F
 riday evenings\, but this time slot is available to you instead.\n\nSAT/SUN
 : 11:30am-2:00pm \n(You will be occupying the time slot usually reserved fo
 r the Indoor 1: First-time Class) Book early!\nT/W: 2:30-5:00pm \nTH: 3:00-
 8:30pm\nM/F: 3:00-8:30 pm \nOn the days when are usually closed\, we will o
 pen the facility for your party for a higher fee.\n\nWHAT ARE THE MINIMUM F
 EES to reserve the range for my group?\n$250 on weekends (11:30am-2:00pm)\n
 $250 on T/W (2:30-5:00pm)\n$280 on TH (3:00-8:30pm)\n$280 on M/F (3:00-8:30
 pm)\n\nHOW DO I PAY IN ADVANCE?\nAfter we confirm your birthday party date 
 by placing it on the Calendar at www.archerytrainingcenter.com\, \nthe birt
 hday party organizer pays the total fees in advance.\nWe accept cash or che
 cks by mail or in person and credit cards (+4%) by phone or in person.\nPle
 ase make your check payable to "Archery Training Center\, Inc." and give it
  to us at the range or mail it to us at:\nArchery Training Center\, Inc.\, 
 PO Box 93216\, Austin\, TX 78709-3216\n\nHOW LONG ARE THE BIRTHDAY PARTIES?
 \nBirthday parties are usually about 2-1/2 hours. Please arrive at least 15
  min. before the party begins.\n\nHOW FAR IN ADVANCE SHOULD I BOOK?\nAt lea
 st 2-3 weeks in advance. \n\nHOW DO I KNOW IF MY BIRTHDAY PARTY IS BOOKED?\
 nLook at the Calendar at www.archerytrainingcenter.com a few hours after yo
 u submit the form below\, to make sure your party is registered on the Cale
 ndar for the day/time you wanted. (We will contact you by email to confirm 
 before putting it up on the Calendar.)\n\nCONTACTS AND WAIVERS\nEach partic
 ipant (or the parent of a junior archer) will need to fill out and sign the
  Membership form\, Release of Liability Waiver\, and Photo Release. The Saf
 ety Rules must also be reviewed with the junior archer and signed before cl
 ass. These 4 forms are available under Indoor 1 Documents at http://www.arc
 herytrainingcenter.com/classes/recreational. If some parents accompany the 
 archer to the birthday party\, they can sign the forms at the range. ALL FO
 RMS MUST BE SUBMITTED BEFORE THE ARCHER WILL BE ALLOWED TO ENTER THE RANGE.
 \n\nARRIVALS\nWe all start together. It is important for everyone to arrive
  15 min. before the party begins\, so we can start on time. If some people 
 are late\, we may start 15 minutes or so late\, which will mean less shooti
 ng for everyone. We would recommend carpooling from another location\, so e
 veryone arrives on time.\n\nPARKING\nThere is limited parking for a max. of
  10 cars outside our range. If you'll need more parking\, please carpool fr
 om another nearby public parking location (shopping center\, etc.).\n\nPART
 Y AGENDA\nThe party will be an abbreviated version of the Indoor 1 First-ti
 me Class. We will enforce the safety rules\, so everyone should read them c
 arefully. \nAfter everyone learns the basics\, they'll start shooting. It's
  impossible to just "let them shoot" as soon as they arrive\, because (besi
 des the safety factor)\, they just wouldn't hit anything\, and would become
  very frustrated...so a basic lesson in good form is essential for them in 
 order to enjoy shooting. \nAfter everyone shoots for a while or scores 50 p
 ts. at 9m\, we'll put up balloons on the wall\, and all the archers will tr
 y to hit theirs. If some balloons remain\, they can take them home\, or wat
 ch as the best archer of the day or the birthday boy/girl/adult tries to hi
 t them. Everyone cheers! The balloons are always a big hit and create a lot
  of laughter. \n\nAWARDS\nEveryone will receive a Personal Best award and\,
  if they shot 50+ pts.\, also a Qualifier Certificate\, which means they ar
 e then members of USA Archery's Junior Olympic program or Adult Training Pr
 ogram\, and can join the regularly scheduled classes (Indoor 2 classes on t
 he Calendar). Later in future classes\, if they would like to earn USA Arch
 ery Star Pins\, they'll need to join USA Archery at https://usarchery.sport
 80.com/register/membership?id_add_on=246 .\n\nWHAT WE PROVIDE\nWe provide a
 ll archery equipment\, balloons (to shoot at)\, bottled water\, napkins. \n
 You can see photos of the interior of our facility on our website. The whit
 e round tables with red/blue/black chairs in the area adjacent to the arche
 ry range will seat 10-13 participants comfortably. \n\nWHAT YOU COULD BRING
 \nYou can bring whatever other refreshments and food you like. Most bring e
 asy-to-eat cupcakes\, doughnuts\, cookies\, cake\, soft drinks\, orange jui
 ce\, etc.  (There are lots of photos online of archery-decorated deserts!) 
 \nPlease also remember to bring the cutlery\, plates\, cups\, etc.\, and\, 
 of course\, PRESENTS!\n\nWHEN SHOULD THEY EAT?\nAFTER the shooting and arch
 ery photos\, otherwise there are sticky fingers on the equipment\, delays\,
  etc. (You could set the tables while the archers are shooting.) Most prefe
 r to do the archery part separately\, and go home or to a restaurant for th
 e "cake and presents" part\, as there is often another archery class starti
 ng immediately after the archers finish shooting.\n\nPHOTOS\nJust some poin
 ters on taking archery photos in our indoor range\, which we've learned fro
 m years of experience photographing archers. We hope these help you take gr
 eat photos and fill your scrapbook with wonderful memories of your son\, da
 ughter\, relative or friend on their birthday! \noGenerally: Pay close atte
 ntion to the background in your photos (which should be the target wall whe
 never possible\, since it's more colorful and will remind you that it was a
 n archery party) and the overhead lighting (should be a few feet in front o
 f the subject\, so the light is more even on their faces\, not directly ove
 rhead creating shadows.)\noGroup photo: Take a group shot with everyone sta
 nding at the target wall. Good to do after the target faces are on the wall
  but before the archers start shooting and/or after we add the balloons.\no
 Archers shooting: Stand in the middle room at the far window to take photos
  of the archers through the window while they are shooting. Do NOT ask an a
 rcher with an arrow in his/her bow to turn towards you so you can take a ph
 oto – very dangerous!\noParent/child photo: Have each parent and child stan
 d together at the target wall in front of their target with arrows in it\, 
 and turn around and smile at you while you take a photo of them.\noArrows i
 n the wall: When the archers go to the target wall to pull their arrows\, s
 tand on the very far right at the target wall in the vacant space\, and pho
 to everyone's arrows sticking out from the wall and also photo them pulling
  their arrows!\noBirthday photo: Take a photo with everyone seated at the t
 ables before they start eating – with the birthday person sitting in front 
 of their cake!\noPodium photo: Often we ranking everyone who has participat
 ed\, and have the gold\, silver\, and bronze medallists stand on the podium
 s at the end of the party.\n\nCLEAN UP\nThere will be trashcans available f
 or your use. Please clean and wipe off the tabl
LAST-MODIFIED:20260404T082324Z
LOCATION:10203 Old Manchaca Rd.\, Austin\, TX 78748
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Birthday Party! Noam ! 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
