DESCRIPTION:This class is only for adults at 9m + 13.5m\n\nPREREQUISITE:\nI
 NDOOR 1: First-time Class:\n   Click the Sign Up button at the top of www.a
 rcherytrainingcenter.com\n   Saturdays: 11:00am-1:30pm (Fee: $25/cl)\n   Su
 ndays: 11:00am-1:30pm (Fee: $25/cl)\n\nENROLLMENT LINKS at:\nhttp://www.arc
 herytrainingcenter.com/classes\n\nATTENDEES TONIGHT (Paid in advance):\n1. 
 Deborah P. (adult 13.5m)\n2.\n3.\n4.\n5.\n6.\n7.\n8.\n9.\n10.\n\nPER CLASS 
 FEE: $20/hr\nSundays: \n10:00am-11:00am\n6:00pm-7:00pm\n\nUSA Archery's Adu
 lt Training Program (ATP) follows a similar path to the Junior Olympic Arch
 ery Development (JOAD) program. \n\nYour first step is to take an Indoor 1:
  First-time Class for Adults. Just click the link or the Sign Up button at 
 the top of this website. \n\nEveryone starts out in our Recreational progra
 m at 9 meters. As you improve you progress to 13.5 meters then on to 18 met
 ers indoors. You'll shoot outdoors at longer distances after completing tra
 ining indoors at 18m.\n\nWe welcome adult recurve and compound Olympic targ
 et archers at all levels of experience. \nRecurve archers attend any of the
  group classes above or book private lessons with Coach Dan. \nCompounds ar
 e coached in private lessons only with Coach Dan.\n\nWhen you decide that y
 ou are interested in competing you'll apply to join USA Archery Level 4 NTS
  and JDT Coach Alex Meyer's Competitive Archery Program (CAP).\n\nExperienc
 ed competitive archers need to be evaluated for advanced placement in eithe
 r the Progressive Program or recommendation to the Competitive Archery Prog
 ram with Coach Alex.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260512T052633Z
LOCATION:10203 OLD Manchaca Road\, Austin\, TX 78748
