DESCRIPTION:REMINDER:  Everyone needs to come to at least one Training Clas
 s per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (All indoor classes are trai
 ning classes.)<br><br>If you are not a coach/instructor\, the fees are:  <b
 r><br>Outdoor Training Class (OTC): $52/class or multi-class pack <br><br>I
 ndoor Training Class (ITC): $43/class or multi-class pack or unlimited pack
 <br><br>Open Practice (OP): ($50/mo)  <br><br>If you are a coach/instructor
 \, you have received an email from Coach Racae outlining your fees.<br><br>
 During the summer (May 31-Aug 31)\, at least 5 archers need to register by 
 <br>8:00 am on Thursdays (for Saturdays) and <br>8:00 am on Fridays (for Su
 ndays) <br>for Coach Racae to coach the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class. In the 
 case of low or late registrations or cancellations\, another coach/instruct
 or\, when available\, will coach the session as a Training Class or oversee
  it as an Open Practice instead. If this is not possible\, then the class m
 ay need to be cancelled.<br><br>Add your name to the Target Assignment List
  below or submit the above completed form.<br>Focus primarily on perfecting
  your form\, <br>slowly increasing your physical strength and draw weight\,
  <br>strengthening your mental program\, <br>determining your average and p
 ersonal best\, <br>understanding the spread between the two\, and working o
 n closing it.<br><br>You need your own equipment <br>Competition recurve bo
 w\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar
  assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling
 \, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not
  be added until you reach a higher level\, but you should order them in adv
 ance.) <br><br>Wear your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br>When you score 288 
 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the n
 ext distance until you reach your competition distance<br>If you trained ou
 tdoors in the 2024 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot
 .<br><br>Target arrangements may vary each session\, depending on who atten
 ds and distances needed.<br>Target 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition dist
 ance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent practice
  in between classes.<br>Target 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition distance
 ) <br>Target 3 at 50m<br>Target 4+5 at 40m (U15 competition distance) <br>T
 arget 6+7+8 at 30m (U13 competition distance) <br>Targets 9 at 20m (for tho
 se who have shot at 18m indoors or with Coach Racae's approval)<br>Target 1
 0 at 13.5m (for those who have just graduated from indoors at 9m)<br><br>Id
 eally\, we want to practice with two archers/target to replicate competitio
 n conditions as much as possible.<br><br>Target Assignments:<br>Targets are
  assigned outdoors in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\,<br
 >so add your name next to your distance below. <br>If you need help or have
  questions\, email/text Coach Racae<br>(Dotted lines represent tent poles d
 ividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)<br>----------------------------------<br>1A
 . (70m)<br>1B<br><br>2A. (60m)  <b>Nick E.\, 219 pts</b><br>2B<br><br>3A. (
 50m)  <br>----------------------------------<br>3B<br><br>4A. (40m) <b>Finn
  E. </b>(Scorecard?)<br>4B. <b>Adrianne M.</b> <b>271 + 291 = 562 pts - CON
 GRATULATIONS! -&gt\; Outdoor 7 at 50m !!!</b><br>--------------------------
 --------<br>5A. (40m) <b>Luke T. 206 pts </b>- (use horizontal 20-70m score
 card next time)<br>5B. <br><br>6A. (40m) <b>Anna P. - 273 pts</b><br>------
 ----------------------------<br>6B. <br><br>7A. (30m)<br>7B. <br>----------
 ------------------------ <br>8A. (30m)<br>8B. <br><br>9A. (20m) <b>Lexi - 2
 37 pts</b><br>----------------------------------<br>9B. <b>Rhys - 174 pts</
 b><br><br>10A. (18m) <b>Anush - 131 pts </b>on 60-cm target face<br>10B
