DESCRIPTION:New 2025 Fees (See below)<br><br>If you have been with us for a
  while\, and have been given access to the ATCI Calendar via an email from 
 Coach Racae\, just add the archer´s name under Registered Archers below.<br
 >For newer archers\, register using the 2025 INDOOR 2-6 at 9m Registration 
 form<br><br>SCHEDULE :<br>​Register for ​​as many as your schedule and budg
 et allows to progress faster:<br>Sat/Sun 4:00-5:30 pm - <br>T/Th  5:00-6:30
  pm  and  <br>T/W/Th   6:30-8\;:00 pm<br>​Weekdays: Juniors usually come to
  the 5:00 pm class\, and adults to the 6:30 class\, but all classes are ope
 n to both adults and juniors.<br><br>Always check this calendar just before
  driving to class in case there are last-minutes changes or cancellations!<
 br><br>USA Archery Level 4 NTS Coach Racae Meyer<br><br>After you graduate 
 out of Indoor 1\, sign up for 2025 INDOOR 2-6 at 9m<br><br>Registered arche
 rs:<br>1. <b>Amy N</b>\, USAA\, pd - 1.5 hrs - <i>Moved to 66" bow due to l
 onger draw length and sight window too small on 62" to see the sight beyond
  the riser</i>. <i>Worked on reducing lateral bow movement due to bow arm m
 ovement and sight position\; more coiling and angular motion\; improving al
 ignments</i><br>2. <b>Anna P</b>\, USAA\, pd - 1.5 hrs - <i>Form looking in
 creasingly better and strong. Worked on improving final alignments\; no inc
 rease in weight until final draw-side alignment achieved. Fivics rest arm r
 epeatedly stuck but turning nock so bottom feather more to the left away fr
 om rest stopped it and groups also improved. </i><br>3.<br>4.<br>5.<br>6.<b
 r><br><b>Hannah T</b>\, USAA\, paid - DNA<br><br>NEW 2025 Winter/Spring Fee
 s <br><br>SINGLE Class Fees per archer for one Indoor 2-6 class:<br>$31 for
  1 hr (arrive 30 min after class starts or leave 30 min before class ends)<
 br>$43 for 1.5 hrs<br><br>MULTI-Class Discount Packets<br>  9 hours : $250 
 (six 1.5-hr classes)<br> 12 hours : $320 (eight 1.5-hr classes)<br> 18 hour
 s : $460 (twelve 1.5-hr classes) <br><br>There are 8 places on the shooting
  line\, and we sometimes have double lines depending on attendance.<br><br>
 Sign in/out upon arrival/departure<br>For single classes\, book and pay in 
 advance.<br>For multi-class discount packs\, pay in advance and book when y
 ou are sure of the dates.<br>Coaching and whistle commands at all times.<br
 >Instruction in the National Training System.<br>Unfair games depending on 
 attendance.<br><br>Please note: Youths &lt\;12 y.o. should not shoot more t
 han 100 arrows/day!<br><br>Prerequisites for Indoor 2: <br>Adults: No min. 
 score in Indoor 1 <br>Juniors: 50 pts in Indoor 1<br>Scores needed at 9m to
  advance to Indoor 3-6 and Outdoor 3-6:<br><br>                 On 40-cm   
                On 60-cm<br>               target face                 targe
 t face<br>Indoor 3:          230 pts                240 pts           -&gt\
 ; Outdoor 3 at 13.5m<br>Indoor 4:          250 pts                260 pts  
          -&gt\; Outdoor 4 at 18m/20m<br>Indoor 5:          270 pts         
