DESCRIPTION:To register for this class\, you will have already completed an
 d graduated out of Outdoor 1: First-time Class\, Outdoor 2 at 9m\, and Outd
 oor 3 at 13.5m\, and your distance will be at least 20m.<br>Register here: 
 <a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfF-EGKsMPSlfPLuLe3aLkqTh
 TFZs0qqb8zleJ_0W3B6Xn7mA/viewform">2021 Outdoor 4-9 at 20m-70m</a><br><br>R
 egistered Archers:<br>1. Kevin B.\, 18m on 40cm target face - substitute fo
 r canceled 7/10<br>2. Yuhan X.\, 9m on 60-cm target face - paid<br>3.&nbsp\
 ;&nbsp\;Lindsay L. at 30m on 122-cm target face - paid but didn't come<br>4
 .. Andrew M. at 20m on 122-cm target face - paid?<br>5.<br>6.<br>7.<br>8.<b
 r>9.<br>10.<br><br>OVERVIEW:<br>These Outdoor Target Archery recreational c
 lasses prepare you to shoot at longer and longer distances until you reach 
 your USA Archery tournament distance (see below)\, while learning the Natio
 nal Training System\, which is the most highly researched biomechanical met
 hod of shooting taught out at the Olympic Training Center. You will be shoo
 ting with other archers in group sessions\, so you can all learn together a
 nd from each other.<br><br>PREREQUISITE:<br>Some archery experience and you
 r own recurve archery equipment is required.<br><br>OPEN TO ADULTS / JUNIOR
 S / PARENTS (with experience and own recurve archery equipment)<br>The arch
 er and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field until furthe
 r notice or approved by Coach Racae.<br>Space will be limited to a maximum 
 of 10 archers per session or in accordance with CDC Guidelines.<br><br>NO D
 ROP INS:<br>You cannot just drop in\, because the number of archers on the 
 shooting line is very limited and we are observing CDC guidelines with soci
 al distancing.<br><br>DATES: Start Dates: MAY 15 (Adults) or JUNE 12 (Junio
 rs 10+)<br>&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&
 nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;Ending Date: AUGUST 14<br><br>ADDRESSES:<
 br>OUTDOOR FIELD SOUTH: 2310 Bliss Spillar Road\, Manchaca\, TX 78652<br>MA
 ILING: Archery Training Center\, Inc.\, PO Box 93216\, Austin\, TX 78709<br
 ><br>E-MAIL:&nbsp\;<a href="mailto:archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com">a
 rcherytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a><br><br>PHONE/TEXT: 512 975 1850<br
 ><br>CAPACITY: 10 archers per class or in accordance with CDC guidelines<br
 >AGES: 10 - 80+ years old (See start dates above)<br>DISTANCES: 9m\, 13.5m\
 , 18m\, 20m-70m<br>BOWS: Recurves<br>(If you are not a recurve archer\, but
  would like to learn to shoot a recurve bow\, please stay tuned to our Inst
 agram for announcements of the re-opening of our in-person First-time Class
 es\, or register online for a few Virtual NTS Form classes with Coach Racae
 .)<br><br>EQUIPMENT:<br>These classes are for archers who have their own eq
 uipment\, consisting of at least a recurve bow\, 12 aluminum or carbon arro
 ws\, armguard\, finger tab\, hip or field quiver. (If you need to change yo
 ur equipment or order your own\, please contact Coach Racae at&nbsp\;<a hre
 f="mailto:archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com">archerytrainingcenterausti
 n@gmail.com</a>. She will specify what you´ll need and help you order it\, 
 so you buy the correct equipment for your strength and experience.)<br><br>
 INSTRUCTOR / COACH:<br>USA Archery Level 2 Instructor Ted Aanstoos<br><br>C
 LASS TIMES:<br>These are the days/times that are available to you. (Additio
 nal sessions will be added in future.)<br><br>SAT: 9:00-10:30pm<br>WED: 9:0
 0-10:30pm<br>Please check&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.c
 om/calendar">www.archerytrainingcenter.com/calendar</a>&nbsp\;before regist
 ering!<br><br>DAYS CLOSED:<br>The outdoor range is closed\, gates locked\, 
 and targets stored away except during the above class times.<br><br>ENROLLM
 ENT IS ON A FIRST-RECEIVED AND PAID BASIS.<br>Complete the Outdoor Target A
 rchery Registration Form under Adults or Juniors at&nbsp\;<a href="http://w
 ww.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrainingcenter.com</a><br><br>ATTE
 NDANCE RECOMMENDATIONS:<br>Recreational archers have no attendance requirem
 ents\, but we would recommend attending at least twice a week to improve fa
 ster.<br><br>FEES:<br>All fees are payable in advance of the class to secur
 e your place in the class.<br>$30/archer for each 1.5-hr training session O
 R<br>$115/mo (for 1 training session/week) OR<br>$213/mo (for 2 training se
 ssions/week)<br>+ Enrollment fee: $20 (always due once per semester)<br><br
 >WEATHER:<br>Archers need to practice in all weather\, except when there is
  lightning.<br><br>REFUNDS\, CREDITS\, and SUBSTITUTIONS:<br>Substitutions 
 or credits will be applied if we cancel a class due to weather conditions o
 r instructor illness or if the 24-hr notice is met.<br>There are no refunds
  for paid classes missed during the summer\, except in the case of injury\,
  long-term illness\, unforeseen move out of the Austin area\, or being expe
 lled for a safety violation.<br><br>24-HR NOTICE:<br>If you let us know wit
 hin 24 hours of the class that you will miss the class\, you can substitute
  another class and use your fee as long as there are places left in that cl
 ass during the semester. If you notify us less than 24 hours in advance of 
 the class that you will need to cancel (except for sudden illness)\, or you
  do a "no-show"\, you'll forfeit your fee.<br><br>ILLNESS or INJURY: In the
  case of physical injury or long-term illness\, we require a doctor's note 
 saying that you are unable to practice archery\, and then a doctor's note s
 aying that you are again fit to return to archery\, before you will be allo
 wed back in class or a refund/credit issued.<br><br>MEMBERSHIP IN USA ARCHE
 RY:<br>Membership in USA Archery is now REQUIRED to participate in JOAD and
  Adult Training.<br>You can attend 2 sessions before joining USAA\, but the
 n we'll need to see your membership card BEFORE WE CAN HAND OUT ANY USA ARC
 HERY STAR PINS to you during Master Challenge Weeks!<br>If you would like t
 o see the benefits of USAA membership:&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.teamusa.or
 g/USA-Archery/Membership/Membership-Benefits">http://www.teamusa.org/USA-Ar
 chery/Membership/Membership-Benefits</a><br>JOIN USA ARCHERY:&nbsp\;<a href
 ="https://www.usarchery.org/memberships/become-a-member">https://www.usarch
 ery.org/memberships/become-a-member</a><br><br>SAFE SPORTS:<br>PARENTS PLEA
 SE NOTE: We are part of the US Olympic Committee's Safe Sport program\, so 
 we minimally require one other adult besides the instructor to be present a
 t all times. Please plan to stay with your child or take turns with other p
 arents staying whenever necessary to fulfill this requirement. THANKS!<br><
 br>SIGN AND RETURN THESE OUTDOOR WAIVERS:<br>The following documents and wa
 ivers will be part of your Registration and Waiver Packet. You will need to
  sign these documents before we add your name to those shooting in the clas
 s:<br>o Membership Form<br>o Safety Rules<br>o Release of Liability Waiver<
 br>o Supervision Policy (Under 18)<br>o Medical Release<br>o Photo/Video Re
 lease<br>o COVID-19 Guidelines<br>o Outdoor Field Rules of Participation<br
 ><br>VACCINATIONS:<br>We do not at this time require archers to be vaccinat
 ed\, but we would like to know if you have been\, so we can take it into co
 nsideration when deciding on issues such as masks and social distancing and
  abiding by the CDC Guidelines. All our instructors have been fully vaccina
 ted of their own accord.<br><br>QUESTIONS?<br>E-mail us at&nbsp\;<a href="m
 ailto:archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com">archerytrainingcenteraustin@gm
 ail.com</a>&nbsp\;or<br>Call/Text us at 512 975 1850<br><br>*NTS = National
  Training System (which is used for training the USA Olympic team!)<br>*JDT
  = Junior Dream Team (top 20 Junior archers in the USA!)<br>*JOAD = Junior 
 Olympic Archery Development
