 . (Some people are still being misdirected.) There is a target on the glass
  door and the unit is facing 290W service road going west on the corner of 
 Industrial Oaks Blvd and 290W. <br><br><b>ARRIVAL</b>: For a 1:30 pm start\
 , please <b>arrive by 1:15 pm</b>\, because we need to start together at 1:
 30 pm. <br><br><b>CARPOOLING / PARKING:</b> Please meet and carpool earlier
  from another location or from a big box store parking lot across the highw
 ay (like Target or At Home on the corner of Mopac and 290W). It's easy and 
 convenient to do. (Parking in front of the range and along Industrial Oaks 
 Blvd may be limited\, depending on the number of participants.)<br><br><b>D
 RESS RECOMMENDATIONS: </b><br>Flat athletic shoes are best\, as we will be 
 throwing our weight forward a little\, so balance and weight distribution i
 s important. The bowstring can get slowed or entangled in your clothing or 
 hair\, so wearing tightly fitting clothes\, no wide skirts\, shirts without
  buttons on the front pockets and tying your hair back is preferable. Longe
 r brim baseball caps often prevent the string from reaching your face\, so 
 shorter brims or bucket hats are better.<br><br><b>All participants need to
  complete waivers online before the event.</b><br><b>Here is the direct lin
 k to complete: </b><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfsWlv
 FJhlvEMDPIw2f8-x-Lwpwd06cVxvA7PGw-lgmRnD00w/viewform?usp=dialog" target="_b
 lank">2026 Waives/Membership Packet for Corporate Team Events</a>  <br><br>
 Waivers have been received from those shown below in <b>bold with (W) - </b
 ><br><b>Last update: Thurs 2/26/26 at 11:55 pm CST:</b><ol><li><b>Alexxa R.
 </b> <b>(W)</b></li><li><b>Jared J. </b> <b>(W)</b></li><li><b>Travis C.</b
 > <b>(W)</b></li><li><b>Manuel O. (W)</b></li><li><b>Blake D.</b> <b>(W)</b
 > tbc</li><li><b>Sonia D</b>. <b>(W</b>) tbc</li><li>Gary M. - DNA</li></ol
 >
