DESCRIPTION:<b>Wednesday\, June 26\, 1:30-4:30 pm</b><br><br><b>WAIVERS:</b
 > Everyone needs to <b>sign the waivers in advance </b>of arriving at the r
 ange\, so we are not delayed in starting. Here's the link: <a href="https:/
 /docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdYr3Yh5msvPHC_-ukFsifcvhYXRrzVRvcdyP4Ybx
 9O5zgUug/viewform" target="_blank"><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u>2
 024 Corporate Team Events Waivers Packet</u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u
 ></u></u></u></u></a>  <br><br><b>DIRECTIONS:</b> <b>Google Map "Donut Taco
  Palace"</b> to find us quickly - We are right next door in Unit 102. (Some
  people are still being misdirected.) There is a target on the glass door a
 nd the unit is facing 290W service road going west on the corner of Industr
 ial Oaks Blvd and 290W. <br><br><b>ARRIVAL</b>: For a 1:30 pm start\, pleas
 e <b>arrive by 1:15 pm</b>\, because we need to start together at 1:30 pm. 
 <br><br><b>CARPOOLING / PARKING:</b> Please meet and carpool earlier from a
 nother location or from a big box store parking lot across the highway (lik
 e Target or At Home on the corner of Mopac and 290W). It's easy and conveni
 ent to do. (Parking in front of the range and along Industrial Oaks Blvd ma
 y be limited\, depending on the number of participants.)<br><br><b>DRESS RE
 COMMENDATIONS: </b><br>Flat athletic shoes are best\, as we will be throwin
 g our weight forward a little\, so balance and weight distribution is impor
 tant. The bowstring can get slowed or entangled in your clothing or hair\, 
 so wearing tightly fitting clothes\, no wide skirts\, shirts without button
 s on the front pockets and tying your hair back is preferable. Longer brim 
 baseball caps often prevent the string from reaching your face\, so shorter
  brims or bucket hats are better. <br>:<br><b>All participants need to comp
 lete waivers online before the event.</b><br><b>Here is the direct link to 
 complete: </b><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdYr3Yh5msv
 PHC_-ukFsifcvhYXRrzVRvcdyP4Ybx9O5zgUug/viewform" target="_blank"><u><u><u><
 u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u>2024 Corporate Team Events Waivers Packet</
 u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></a>  <br><br><b>(ave
 raged) </b>means your score in the first round divided by the number of arr
 ows you shot and multiplied by 30 arrows to get an official 30-arrow round 
 score.<br><br>Waivers have been received from those shown below in <b>bold 
 with (W)</b><br><b><br></b>1. <b>Anand R. </b><b>(W)  </b>104 pts (averaged
 )<br>2. <b>Gordon G </b>.<b>(W) </b>88 pts<br>3. <b>Norman T. (W) </b>84 pt
 s (averaged)<br>4. <b>Achuta T. (W) </b>43 pts (averaged)<br>5. <b>Minh C</
 b>. <b>(W) </b>71 pts (averaged)<br>6. <b>Efron H. </b><b>(W) </b>59 pts (a
 veraged)<br>7. <b>Madhur J. </b><b>(W) </b>56 pts<br>8. <b>Tao C. </b><b>(W
 ) </b>45 pts (averaged)<br>9. <b>Ashish N. </b><b>(W) </b>30 pts (averaged)
