DESCRIPTION:<span><span><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u
 ></u><u></u><u></u>REGISTER NOW !<br /><br />Open to adult\, juniors 8+\, a
 nd parents! Please read all the info below and in the registration and waiv
 ers.<br /><br />More information\, registration forms and waivers are avail
 able at <a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com"><u>www.archerytraini
 ngcenter.com</u></a>.<br /><br />Register here using ONE of these forms:<br
  /><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfcwG419ZK9XmA4-JlXM-z
 hjhvSPCF8NCwWJlzFP2w-gRliUw/viewform"><u>2022 Winter/Spring Outdoor 1: Firs
 t-time Class for Juniors + Parents</u></a>  OR<br /><a href="https://docs.g
 oogle.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSe-YxPKAMTxiC7kVt6fZuQJeidXENYq_iV4rWj1RaXdLhPoe
 w/viewform"><u>2022 Winter/Spring Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Adults</u
 ></a><br /><br />Sign up for just one Outdoor 1 class\, because most junior
 s 11+ and all adults graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after the fi
 rst lesson.<u></u><br /><br /><b>Your name will be added below and your pla
 ce reserved on a</b> <b>first registered and paid basis and after we receiv
 e 3 things</b>:  <br />2022 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM + WAIVERS + FEE<br 
 /><br /><b>Registered archers </b>at 9m on 40-cm FITA target face:<br /><b>
 Target Assignments:</b><br />1. <b>Tristyn C</b>.\, adult - pd - <b>157 pts
 </b><br />2. <b>Jacob E.</b>\, adult - pd - <b>120 pts</b><br />3. <b>Steph
 en S.\, </b>adult - pd - <b>148 pts</b><u></u><br /><u></u>4. <b>Gabriel C.
 \, </b>adult - pd -<b>?</b><br />5. <u></u><b>Leticia M.</b>\, adult - pd -
  <b>93 pts</b><br /><u></u>6. <b>Christopher C.\, </b>adult - pd - <b>110 p
 ts</b><u></u><br /><u></u>7. <b>Ingram J.\, </b>12\, - pd - <b>178 pts -&gt
 \; Outdoor 2</b><br />8<u></u>. <b>Jia L.\, </b>mom - pd - <b>63 pts</b><br
  /><u></u>9A. <b>Kelvin L</b>.\, dad - pd - <b>74 pts</b><u></u><br /><u></
 u>9B. <b>Henry L</b>.\, 8 - pd - <b>22 pts -&gt\; Outdoor 1</b><br /><u></u
 >10A. <b>Han L.\, </b>dad - pd - rescheduled from 4/10 - <b>123 pts</b><br 
 />10B. <b>Gianna L.\, </b>8 - pd - rescheduled from 4/10 - <b>68 pts -&gt\;
  Outdoor 2</b><br /><br />Space will be limited to 10-15 archers per sessio
 n depending on the number of family groups in attendance or in accordance w
 ith CDC Guidelines. <br />Each person will have a target stand\, except aft
 er 10 people have registered\, two members from the same family will share 
 one target stand.<br />The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be al
 lowed on the field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae. <br />P
 arents of juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator. Par
 ents of juniors 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their
  child for greater safety.<br /><br />A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent
 ) is accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-time Class. <br /><br />We will ac
 cept a limited number of kids under 12 into the program each semester\, dep
 ending on the total  number of archers in all the classes. If you join befo
 re the limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the prog
 ram and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2. If
  you are under 12\, registered and paid after the cut off\, your fee will b
 e returned to you. <br /><br />Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or th
 ree times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll
  make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows. <br /
 >Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br /><br />a
 p = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be
  needed for Outdoor 2. ($15)<br />fp = form pack (stretchband and string lo
 op)\, optional but really needed to practice form\, warm up before classes 
 ($4)<br /><br />At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be po
 sted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recog
 nize your final score\, because it will have been averaged by taking your r
 ecorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrows you sh
 ot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full 
 round score. After the last class on the weekend\, final scores will also b
 e sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more information befo
 re your next class.<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u>
 <u></u><u></u></span></span>
