DESCRIPTION:Registration form: OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m<br><br><br>REMINDER
 :  Everyone needs to come to at least one Training Class per week to be abl
 e to attend Open Practice. (All indoor classes are training classes.)<br><b
 r>If you are not a coach/instructor\, the fees are:  <br>Outdoor Training C
 lass (OTC): $52/class or multi-class pack <br>Indoor Training Class (ITC): 
 $43/class or multi-class pack or unlimited pack<br>Open Practice (OP): ($50
 /mo)  <br><br>If you are a coach/instructor\, you have received an email fr
 om Coach Racae outlining your fees.<br><br>During the summer (May 31-Aug 31
 )\, at least 5 archers need to register by <br>8:00 am on Thursdays (for Sa
 turdays) and <br>8:00 am on Fridays (for Sundays) <br>for Coach Racae to co
 ach the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class. In the case of low or late registration
 s or cancellations\, another coach/instructor\, when available\, will coach
  the session as a Training Class or oversee it as an Open Practice instead.
  If this is not possible\, then the class may need to be cancelled.During t
 he summer (May 31-Aug 31)\, at least 5 archers need to register by 8:00 am 
 on Thursdays (for Saturdays) and 8:00 am on Fridays (for Sundays) for Coach
  Racae to coach the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class . In the case of low or late
  registrations or cancellations\, another coach/instructor\, when available
 \, will coach the session as a Training Class or oversee it as an Open Prac
 tice instead. If this is not possible\, then the class may need to be cance
 lled.<br><br>Add your name to the Target Assignment List below or submit th
 e above completed form.<br>Focus primarily on perfecting your form\, <br>sl
 owly increasing your physical strength and draw weight\, <br>strengthening 
 your mental program\, <br>determining your average and personal best\, <br>
 understanding the spread between the two\, and working on closing it.<br><b
 r>You need your own equipment <br>Competition recurve bow\, sight\, stabili
 zer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker
 \, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field qui
 ver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added until you
  reach a higher level\, but you should order them in advance.) <br><br>Wear
  your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow r
 ound on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the next distance until 
 you reach your competition distance<br>If you trained outdoors in the 2024 
 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.<br><br>Target arr
 angements may vary each session\, depending on who attends and distances ne
 eded.<br>Target 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should always
  stay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent practice in between classes
 .<br>Target 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition distance) <br>Target 3 at 5
 0m<br>Target 4+5 at 40m (U15 competition distance) <br>Target 6+7+8 at 30m 
 (U13 competition distance) <br>Targets 9 at 20m (for those who have shot at
  18m indoors or with Coach Racae's approval)<br>Target 10 at 13.5m (for tho
 se who have just graduated from indoors at 9m)<br><br>Ideally\, we want to 
 practice with two archers/target to replicate competition conditions as muc
 h as possible.<br><br>Target Assignments:<br>Targets are assigned outdoors 
 in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\,<br>so add your name n
 ext to your distance below. <br>If you need help or have questions\, email/
 text Coach Racae<br>(Dotted lines represent tent poles dividing Targets 3\,
  6\, and 9.)<br>----------------------------------<br>1A. (70m)<br>1B<br><b
 r>2A. (60m)  <br>2B<br><br>3A. (50m)  <b>Nick E</b>\, adult\, pd - <b>288 p
 ts -&gt\; Outdoor 8 at 60m ! CONGRATULATIONS!</b><br>----------------------
 ------------<br>3B<br><br>4A. (40m) <b>Adrianne M</b>\, adult - <b>273 + 23
 5 = 508 pts </b>(2 rounds)<br>4B. <b>Anna P</b>\, adult\, pd - <b>270+ 265 
 = 535 pts </b>(2 rounds)<br>----------------------------------<br>5A. (40m)
  <b>Sophie D\,</b> adult\, f - <b>256 pts </b>(one round)<br>5B. <b>Colby K
 .</b>!!! adult\, USAA\, pd - <b> 229 + 197 = 426 pts </b>(2 rounds)<br><br>
 6A. (<b>40m</b>) <b>Finn E - 215 pts </b>(one round)<br>-------------------
 ---------------<br>6B. <br><br>7A. (30m)<br>7B. <br>-----------------------
 ----------- <br>8A. (30m)<br>8B. <br><br>9A. (20m) <b>Rhys E - 46 + 100 = 1
 46 pts </b>(2 rounds)<br>----------------------------------<br>9B. <b>Lexi 
 E</b>. 16\, pd - <b>246 + 233 = 479 pts </b>(2 rounds)<br><br>10A. (13.5m)<
 b> Emma A.</b>\, 13\, on 60-cm target face\, pd - <b>247 pts -&gt\; Outdoor
  4 at 20m ! CONGRATULATIONS!</b><br>10B  <b>Anush  M\, </b>12\, on 60-cm ta
 rget face\, pd - <b>185 + 185 = 370 pts </b>(2 rounds)
