DESCRIPTION:<i>This class has been cancelled due to the persistent rain.!</
 i><br><i><br></i><br><b>REMINDER</b>:  Everyone needs to come to at least o
 ne Training Class per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (All indoor 
 classes are training classes.)<br><br>If you are not a coach/instructor\, t
 he fees are:  <ul><li><b>Outdoor Training Class (OTC)</b>: $52/class or mul
 ti-class pack </li><li><b>Indoor Training Class (ITC)</b>: $43/class or mul
 ti-class pack or unlimited pack</li><li><b>Open Practice (OP)</b>: ($50/mo)
   </li></ul>If you are a coach/instructor\, you have received an email from
  Coach Racae outlining your fees.<br><br>During the summer (May 31-Aug 31)\
 , at least 5 archers need to register by <br>8:00 am on Thursdays (for Satu
 rdays) and <br>8:00 am on Fridays (for Sundays) <br>for Coach Racae to coac
 h the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class. <span>In the case of low or late registra
 tions or cancellations\, another coach/instructor\, when available\, will c
 oach the session as a Training Class or oversee it as an Open Practice inst
 ead. If this is not possible\, then the class may need to be cancelled.</sp
 an><br><br>Add your name to the Target Assignment List below or submit the 
 above completed form.<br>Focus primarily on perfecting your form\, <br>slow
 ly increasing your physical strength and draw weight\, <br>strengthening yo
 ur mental program\, <br>determining your average and personal best\, <br>un
 derstanding the spread between the two\, and working on closing it.<br><br>
 You need your own equipment <br>Competition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilize
 r\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\,
  chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quive
 r\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added until you r
 each a higher level\, but you should order them in advance.) <br><br>Wear y
 our ATCI shirt to training.<br><br>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow rou
 nd on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the next distance until yo
 u reach your competition distance<br>If you trained outdoors in the 2024 se
 ason\, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.<br><br>Target arran
 gements may vary each session\, depending on who attends and distances need
 ed.<br>Target 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should always s
 tay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent practice in between classes.<
 br>Target 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition distance) <br>Target 3 at 50m
 <br>Target 4+5 at 40m (U15 competition distance) <br>Target 6+7+8 at 30m (U
 13 competition distance) <br>Targets 9 at 20m (for those who have shot at 1
 8m indoors or with Coach Racae's approval)<br>Target 10 at 13.5m (for those
  who have just graduated from indoors at 9m)<br><br>Ideally\, we want to pr
 actice with two archers/target to replicate competition conditions as much 
 as possible.<br><br>Target Assignments:<br>Targets are assigned outdoors in
  advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\,<br>so add your name nex
 t to your distance below. <br>If you need help or have questions\, email/te
 xt Coach Racae<br>(Dotted lines represent tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6
 \, and 9.)<br>----------------------------------<br>1A. (70m)<br>1B<br><br>
 2A. (60m)  <br>2B<br><br>3A. (50m) <br>----------------------------------<b
 r>3B<br><br>4A. (40m) <br>4B. <br>----------------------------------<br>5A.
  (40m)<br>5B. <br><br>6A. (30m)<br>----------------------------------<br>6B
 . <br><br>7A. (30m) <b>Sofia W.</b><br>7B. <br>----------------------------
 ------ <br>8A. (30m)<br>8B. <br><br>9A. (20m)<br>--------------------------
 --------<br>9B. <br><br>10A. (13.5m)<br>10B
