DESCRIPTION:REMINDER:  Everyone needs to come to at least one Training Clas
 s per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (All indoor classes are trai
 ning classes.)\n\nIf you are NOT a coach/instructor\, the fees are:  \nOutd
 oor Training Class (OTC): $52/class or multi-class pack \nIndoor Training C
 lass (ITC): $43/class or multi-class pack or unlimited pack\nOpen Practice 
 (OP): ($50/mo)  \nIf you are a coach/instructor\, you have received an emai
 l from Coach Racae outlining your fees.\n\nDuring the summer (May 31-Aug 31
 )\, at least 5 archers need to register by \n8:00 am on Thursdays (for Satu
 rdays) and \n8:00 am on Fridays (for Sundays) \nfor Coach Racae to coach th
 e Outdoor 3-9 Training Class. \nIn the case of low or late registrations or
  cancellations\, another coach/instructor\, when available\, will coach the
  session as a Training Class or oversee it as an Open Practice instead. If 
 this is not possible\, then the class may need to be cancelled.\n\nAdd your
  name to the Target Assignment List below or submit the above completed for
 m.\nFocus primarily on perfecting your form\, \nslowly increasing your phys
 ical strength and draw weight\, \nstrengthening your mental program\, \ndet
 ermining your average and personal best\, \nunderstanding the spread betwee
 n the two\, and working on closing it.\n\nYou need your own equipment \nCom
 petition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arro
 ws\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, finge
 rtab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker an
 d side rods may not be added until you reach a higher level\, but you shoul
 d order them in advance.) \n\nWear your ATCI shirt to training.\n\nWhen you
  score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm target face you'll move ba
 ck to the next distance until you reach your competition distance\nIf you t
 rained outdoors in the 2024 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance
  you shot.\n\nTarget arrangements may vary each session\, depending on who 
 attends and distances needed.\nTarget 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition d
 istance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent pract
 ice in between classes.\nTarget 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition distanc
 e) \nTarget 3 at 50m\nTarget 4+5 at 40m (U15 competition distance) \nTarget
  6+7+8 at 30m (U13 competition distance) \nTargets 9 at 20m (for those who 
 have shot at 18m indoors or with Coach Racae's approval)\nTarget 10 at 13.5
 m (for those who have just graduated from indoors at 9m)\n\nIdeally\, we wa
 nt to practice with two archers/target to replicate competition conditions 
 as much as possible.\n\nTarget Assignments:\nTargets are assigned outdoors 
 in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\,\nso add your name nex
 t to your distance below. \nIf you need help or have questions\, email/text
  Coach Racae\n(Dotted lines represent tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, a
 nd 9.)\n----------------------------------\n1A. (70m)\n1B\n\n2A. (60m)  \n2
 B\n\n3A. (50m)  Nick E\n----------------------------------\n3B\n\n4A. (40m)
  Finn E\n4B.  Adrianne M. adult\, pd\n----------------------------------\n5
 A. (40m) Luke T\, 16\, pd\n5B. Anna P\, adult\, pd\n\n6A. (30m)\n----------
 ------------------------\n6B. \n\n7A. (30m)\n7B. \n------------------------
 ---------- \n8A. (30m)\n8B. \n\n9A. (20m) Rhys E\n-------------------------
 ---------\n9B. \n\n10A. (13.5m)\n10B
LAST-MODIFIED:20260512T052633Z
