DESCRIPTION:RetailMeNot registration: 11 people\n\n\nGeneral Information:\n
 We'd be very happy to host a Corporate Team Archery Event for your group on
  a mutually convenient date. \n\nThese sessions are proving to be very popu
 lar\, and we appreciate the opportunity! \nBook now so you're ready for our
  indoor corporate archery tournaments!\n\nA few of the corporations which s
 chedule events with us are:\nFacebook\, Intel\, Dell\, AMD\, Samsung\, Home
  Away\, National Instruments\, Texas Mutual Insurance\, Electronic Arts\, E
 RCOT\, Vectra Networks\, Austin Children's Advocacy\, Glatfelder Insurance\
 , Kerbey Lane\, RackSpace\, Abilitie\, Black Locus\, Boosterthon\, WP Engin
 e\, Camp Gladiator\, Marriott International\, Zimmer Biomet\, Austin Gastro
 enterology\, and others. \n\nWe also would like to thank your company for i
 ts vital\, indirect support of USA Archery's Junior Olympic Archery Develop
 ment (JOAD) program! Support like yours grows Olympians! \n\nPlease read th
 e following information and fill in the registration form\, which can be fo
 und under Classes on our website.\nBelow is a typical agenda for a Corporat
 e Team Event with us\, and some other general info\, which may make things 
 run more smoothly. \n\nCAPACITY: 10 places on the shooting line. 1-20 parti
 cipants. If you'll have over 10 participants\, even numbers are best\, so w
 e can create teams of two.\n\nDAYS CLOSED: \nMONDAYS and FRIDAYS\nJAN 1-5: 
 Happy Holidays!\nAPRIL 21: Happy Easter !\nMAY 12: Happy Mother´s Day!\n\nA
 GENDA (approx.- depends on number and pace of participants)\n\n1:00 Arrival
 \; waivers (to be signed by participants over 18 years old or adults/parent
 s/guardians)\n1:15 Selecting two-person teams\; equipment review and select
 ion (bows\, arrows\, finger tabs\, arm guards\, targets\, etc.)\n1:55 Safet
 y rules\; whistle system\n2:10 Form (positions) training (stance\, nocking\
 , hooking/gripping\, set\, mindset\, set-up\, drawing\, anchor\, loading\, 
 aiming\, expanding\, release)\n2:45 Ranking Round - shooting in teams\; qua
 ntity of arrows will depend on number and pace of participants\n3:45 Olympi
 c Round: Based on ranking round\; each team picks a country to represent\; 
 all teams progress in a match play to the Gold\, Silver\, and Bronze medal 
 matches\, with other teams cheering them on!\n4:15 Awards Ceremony and podi
 um presentations\, photos!\n\nSCHEDULING:\nWe can schedule a corporate team
  event on T/W/Th during the day for a max. of 20 people\, pending your conf
 irmation. If you would prefer another day or time\, please tell us\, and we
 'll do our best to accommodate you. \n\nTIME NEEDED:\nIt's best to allow at
  least 3 hrs. for a team of up to 10\, and about 3.5-4 hours for more than 
 10 participants\, since we'll need to form two lines of shooting. We may ru
 n over by as much as 30 minutes\, depending on everyone's arrival and abili
 ty. If this will be a problem\, please let us know\, so we can pace the eve
 nt carefully.\n\nARRIVALS:  We'll all start together\, so please have every
 one arrive on time or together. \n\nPARKING: We have limited parking space 
 for about 8-10 vehicles. Some corporations decide to park at a nearby shopp
 ing center parking lot\, and then "carpool" to the archery range.\n\nFEE:  
 There is a minimum fee of $280 for 1-10 people\, and then $25/person for 11
 -20 people. We can accommodate 20 people for $530. If your company requires
  a separate written receipt for accounting purposes\, please tell us in adv
 ance so we can have one ready for you.\n\nPAYMENT: When you arrive at the r
 ange\, you can pay for the session individually or by corporate check payab
 le to Archery Training Center\, or by credit card (+4%). All fees must be p
 aid before the session begins. \n\nREFUNDS: If you pay in advance of arriva
 l\, a refund will be issued only for cancellations or reductions in attende
 es in writing when given notice not less than 24 hours before the session b
 egins.\n\nEQUIPMENT:  We provide all equipment necessary during the Corpora
 te Team Event.\n\nDRESS RECOMMENDATIONS: Flat shoes are best\, as we stand 
 a lot and throw our weight forward a little\, so balance and weight distrib
 ution is important. The bowstring can get slowed or entangled in your cloth
 ing or hair\, so wearing tighter fitting clothes\, no wide skirts\, shirts 
 without buttons on the front pockets and tying your hair back is preferable
 .  Longer brim baseball caps often prevent the string from reaching your fa
 ce\, so shorter brims are better. In the winter on very cold days\, please 
 dress in layers.\n\nWAIVERS:  There will be waivers for each archer to fill
  out and sign when they first come in\, and before entering the range. All 
 signees must be at least 18 years old. For those under 18\, a parent/guardi
 an will need to sign for them. \n\nSPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS:    Please let us k
 now if there are any special concepts you would like us to emphasize\, or a
 ny other considerations which you would like us to take into account.\n\nOL
 YMPIC TARGET ARCHERY LINKS: \nHere are some links\, which you and your grou
 p may find interesting before you get to the session.\n\nhttp://www.usarche
 ry.org \nhttp://www.olympic.org/archery \nhttp://www.worldarchery.org\nhttp
 ://www.youtube.com/archerytv\n\nThe YouTube videos showing the top American
  male archer\, Brady Ellison\, competing with the top Korean archer\, KU Bo
 nchan\, in the Rio Olympics Men's Semi Final Match is the best we've seen i
 n 20 years! You have to watch every shot.\n\nTHANK YOU for your interest in
  and support of Olympic target archery. We know you'll all really enjoy bei
 ng part of the Olympic Round at the end of your training!!\n\nWe look forwa
 rd to your time with us.\n\nIf you'd like to discuss your reservation in mo
 re detail\, please call Coach Racae Meyer 512 975 1850 at your convenience.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260404T082343Z
LOCATION:10203 OLD Manchaca Rd.\, Austin\, 78748
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Corporate Team Event - RetailMeNot - Nick
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
