DESCRIPTION:This class is only for adults at 9m + 13.5m\n\nPREREQUISITE:\nI
 NDOOR 1: First-time Class:\n   Click the Sign Up button at the top of www.a
 rcherytrainingcenter.com\n   Saturdays: 11:00am-1:30pm (Fee: $25/cl)\n   Su
 ndays: 11:00am-1:30pm (Fee: $25/cl)\n\nENROLLMENT LINKS at:\nhttp://www.arc
 herytrainingcenter.com/classes\n\nATTENDEES TONIGHT (Paid in advance):\n1. 
 Helen Y. \n2. Suzanne J.\n3.\n4.\n5.\n6.\n7.\n8.\n9.\n10.\n\nPER CLASS FEE:
  $20/hr\nSundays: \n10:00am-11:00am\n6:00pm-7:00pm\n\nUSA Archery's Adult T
 raining Program (ATP) follows a similar path to the Junior Olympic Archery 
 Development (JOAD) program. \n\nYour first step is to take an Indoor 1: Fir
 st-time Class for Adults. Just click the link or the Sign Up button at the 
 top of this website. \n\nEveryone starts out in our Recreational program at
  9 meters. As you improve you progress to 13.5 meters then on to 18 meters 
 indoors. You'll shoot outdoors at longer distances after completing trainin
 g indoors at 18m.\n\nWe welcome adult recurve and compound Olympic target a
 rchers at all levels of experience. \nRecurve archers attend any of the gro
 up classes above or book private lessons with Coach Dan. \nCompounds are co
 ached in private lessons only with Coach Dan.\n\nWhen you decide that you a
 re interested in competing you'll apply to join USA Archery Level 4 NTS and
  JDT Coach Alex Meyer's Competitive Archery Program (CAP).\n\nExperienced c
 ompetitive archers need to be evaluated for advanced placement in either th
 e Progressive Program or recommendation to the Competitive Archery Program 
 with Coach Alex.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260512T052633Z
LOCATION:10203 OLD Manchaca Road\, Austin\, TX 78748
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:ADULT TRAINING at 9m + 13.5m
TRANSP:OPAQUE
