DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20250622T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20250622T110000
DTSTAMP:20261004T164458Z
UID:02fc55apdd5qigpb3kq47gis7s_R20250607T140000@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Chicago:20250622T090000
CREATED:20250501T180249Z
DESCRIPTION:<i>This class has been changed to an Open Practice run by Instr
 uctors Anna\, Adrianne\, and Sophia. It is not a Training Class (TC). (Coac
 h Racae not be in attendance or coaching\, as five archers did not register
  for it 48 hours in advance.).</i><br><br>REMINDER:  Everyone needs to come
  to at least one Training Class per week to be able to attend Open Practice
 . (All indoor classes are training classes.)<br><br>If you are not a coach/
 instructor\, the fees are:  <br>    * Outdoor Training Class (OTC): $52/cla
 ss or multi-class pack <br>    * Indoor Training Class (ITC): $43/class or 
 multi-class pack or unlimited pack<br>    * Open Practice (OP): ($50/mo)  <
 br>If you are a coach/instructor\, you have received an email from Coach Ra
 cae outlining your fees.<br><br>During the summer (May 31-Aug 31)\, at leas
 t 5 archers need to register by <br>8:00 am on Thursdays (for Saturdays) an
 d <br>8:00 am on Fridays (for Sundays) <br>for Coach Racae to coach the Out
 door 3-9 Training Class. In the case of low or late registrations or cancel
 lations\, another coach/instructor\, when available\, will coach the sessio
 n as a Training Class or oversee it as an Open Practice instead. If this is
  not possible\, then the class may need to be cancelled.<br><br>Add your na
 me to the Target Assignment List below or submit the above completed form.<
 br>Focus primarily on perfecting your form\, <br>slowly increasing your phy
 sical strength and draw weight\, <br>strengthening your mental program\, <b
 r>determining your average and personal best\, <br>understanding the spread
  between the two\, and working on closing it.<br><br>You need your own equi
 pment <br>Competition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 1
 2 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, arm
 guard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc
 . (Clicker and side rods may not be added until you reach a higher level\, 
 but you should order them in advance.) <br><br>Wear your ATCI shirt to trai
 ning.<br><br>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm targe
 t face you'll move back to the next distance until you reach your competiti
 on distance<br>If you trained outdoors in the 2024 season\, you'll return t
 o the farthest distance you shot.<br><br>Target arrangements may vary each 
 session\, depending on who attends and distances needed.<br>Target 1 at 70m
  (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can
  use it for independent practice in between classes.<br>Target 2 at 60m (U1
 8 + Masters competition distance) <br>Target 3 at 50m<br>Target 4+5 at 40m 
 (U15 competition distance) <br>Target 6+7+8 at 30m (U13 competition distanc
 e) <br>Targets 9 at 20m (for those who have shot at 18m indoors or with Coa
 ch Racae's approval)<br>Target 10 at 13.5m (for those who have just graduat
 ed from indoors at 9m)<br><br>Ideally\, we want to practice with two archer
 s/target to replicate competition conditions as much as possible.<br><br>Ta
 rget Assignments:<br>Targets are assigned outdoors in advance to reduce con
 fusion and delay on the day\,<br>so add your name next to your distance bel
 ow. <br>If you need help or have questions\, email/text Coach Racae<br>(Dot
 ted lines represent tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)<br>--------
 --------------------------<br>1A. (70m)<br>1B<br><br>2A. (60m)  <br>2B<br><
