UID:6rlj9eigabegus16aetmh9bvlg@google.com
CREATED:20190402T152548Z
DESCRIPTION:\n14 people\nWe'd be very happy to host a Corporate Team Archer
 y Event for your group on a mutually convenient date. \n\nThese sessions ar
 e proving to be very popular\, and we appreciate the opportunity! \nBook no
 w so you're ready for our indoor corporate archery tournaments!\n\nA few of
  the corporations which schedule events with us are:\nFacebook\, Intel\, De
 ll\, AMD\, Samsung\, Home Away\, National Instruments\, Texas Mutual Insura
 nce\, Electronic Arts\, ERCOT\, Vectra Networks\, Austin Children's Advocac
 y\, Glatfelder Insurance\, Kerbey Lane\, RackSpace\, Abilitie\, Black Locus
 \, Boosterthon\, WP Engine\, Camp Gladiator\, Marriott International\, Zimm
 er Biomet\, Austin Gastroenterology\, Yeti\, RetailMeNot\, Tableau Software
  and others. \n\nWe also would like to thank your company for its vital\, i
 ndirect support of USA Archery's Junior Olympic Archery Development (JOAD) 
 program! Support like yours grows Olympians! \n\nBelow is a typical agenda 
 for a Corporate Team Event with us\, and some other general info\, which ma
 y make things run more smoothly. \n\nCAPACITY: 1-20 participants. 10 places
  on the shooting line. If you'll have over 10 participants\, we will form t
 wo shooting lines\; even numbers are best\, so we can create teams of two.\
 n\nDAYS CLOSED: \nMONDAYS and THURSDAYS\nJAN 1-5: Happy Holidays!\nAPRIL 21
 : Happy Easter !\nMAY 12: Happy Mother´s Day!\n\nAGENDA (approx.- depends o
 n number and pace of participants)\n\n1:00 Arrival\; waivers (to be signed 
 by participants over 18 years old or adults/parents/guardians)\n1:15 Select
 ing two-person teams\; equipment review and selection (bows\, arrows\, fing
 er tabs\, arm guards\, targets\, etc.)\n1:55 Safety rules\; whistle system\
 n2:00 Break\n2:10 Form (positions) training (stance\, nocking\, hooking/gri
 pping\, set\, mindset\, set-up\, drawing\, anchor\, loading\, aiming\, expa
 nding\, release)\n2:45 Ranking Round - shooting in teams\; quantity of arro
 ws will depend on number and pace of participants\n3:45 Olympic Round: Base
 d on ranking round\; each team picks a country to represent\; all teams pro
 gress in a match play to the Gold\, Silver\, and Bronze medal matches\, wit
 h other teams cheering them on!\n4:15 Awards Ceremony and podium presentati
 ons\, photos!\n\nSCHEDULING:\nWe can schedule a corporate team event on T/W
 /Th/F during the day for a max. of 20 people\, pending your confirmation. I
 f you would prefer another day or time\, please tell us\, and we'll do our 
 best to accommodate you. Sundays 11:00am-2:00pm are also available\, if boo
 ked at least two weeks in advance.\n\nTIME NEEDED:\nIt's best to allow at l
 east 3 hrs. for a team of up to 10\, and about 3.5-4 hours for more than 10
  participants\, since we'll need to form two lines of shooting. We may run 
 over by as much as 30 minutes\, depending on everyone's arrival and ability
 . If this will be a problem\, please let us know\, so we can pace the event
  carefully.\n\nARRIVALS: We'll all start together\, so please have everyone
  arrive on time or together. \n\nPARKING: We have limited parking space for
  about 8-10 vehicles. Some corporations decide to park at a nearby shopping
  center parking lot\, and then "carpool" to the archery range.\n\nFEE: Ther
 e is a minimum fee of $250 for 1-10 people\, and then $25/person for 11-20 
 people. We can accommodate 20 people for $500. If your company requires a s
 eparate written receipt for accounting purposes\, please tell us in advance
  so we can have one ready for you.\n\nPAYMENT: When you arrive at the range
 \, you can pay for the session individually or by corporate check payable t
 o Archery Training Center\, or by credit card (+4%). All fees must be paid 
 before the session begins. \n\nREFUNDS: If you pay in advance of arrival\, 
 a refund will be issued only for cancellations or reductions in attendees i
 n writing when you give us notice not less than 24 hours before the session
  begins.\n\nEQUIPMENT: We provide all equipment necessary during the Corpor
 ate Team Event.\n\nDRESS RECOMMENDATIONS: Flat shoes are best\, as we stand
  a lot and throw our weight forward a little\, so balance and weight distri
 bution is important. The bowstring can get slowed or entangled in your clot
 hing or hair\, so wearing tighter fitting clothes\, no wide skirts\, shirts
  without buttons on the front pockets and tying your hair back is preferabl
 e. Longer brim baseball caps often prevent the string from reaching your fa
 ce\, so shorter brims are better. In the winter on very cold days\, please 
 dress in layers\, as it may be chilly in the indoor range.\n\nWAIVERS: Ther
 e will be waivers for each archer to fill out and sign when they first come
  in\, and before entering the range. All signees must be at least 18 years 
 old. For those under 18\, a parent/guardian will need to sign for them. \n\
 nSPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS: Please let us know if there are any special concepts
  you would like us to emphasize\, or any other considerations which you wou
 ld like us to take into account.\n\nOLYMPIC TARGET ARCHERY LINKS: \nHere ar
 e some links\, which you and your group may find interesting before you get
  to the session.\n\nhttp://www.usarchery.org \nhttp://www.olympic.org/arche
 ry \nhttp://www.worldarchery.org\nhttp://www.youtube.com/archerytv\n\nThe Y
 ouTube videos showing the top American male archer\, Brady Ellison\, compet
 ing with the top Korean archer\, KU Bonchan\, in the Rio Olympics Men's Sem
 i Final Match is the best we've seen in 20 years! You have to watch every s
 hot.\n\nTHANK YOU for your interest in and support of Olympic target archer
 y. We know you'll all really enjoy being part of the Olympic Round at the e
 nd of your training!!\n\nWe look forward to your time with us.\n\nIf you'd 
 like to discuss your reservation in more detail\, please call Coach Racae M
 eyer 512 975 1850 at your convenience.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260404T082343Z
LOCATION:10203 Old Manchaca Rd.\, Austin\, TX 78748
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Corporate Team Event - Four Hands
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
