DESCRIPTION:For archers in Outdoor 2-9.<br><br><b>Tournament Week</b><br>Fo
 r one week each month during Tournament Week\, you shoot for score and subm
 it your scores to Coach Racae. Score in your regular classes or come to the
  tournament on Tournament Saturday.<br><br><b>Tournament Saturday</b><br>On
  the last day of tournament week\, Saturday\, Coach Racae will conduct the 
 Saturday Outdoor 4-9 class as a tournament with scoring and little to no co
 aching\, so you realize what you know and can do on your own and learn to t
 rust yourself to adapt and succeed.&nbsp\;<br><br><b>Master Challenge</b><b
 r>While you´re shooting in the tournament&nbsp\; Coach Racae will look at y
 our form and assess how much attention to form you can remember to do while
  shooting in a tournament. You can earn Mastered Tags for each step of the 
 form you have consistently done at your level. As you progress through high
 er levels\, the level of detail required will increase and additional posit
 ions will be added.<br><br><b>USA Archery Star Pins</b><br><b>If you are a 
 member of USA Archery</b>\, Tournament Saturday is often called a ¨Pin Shoo
 t¨\, when you can earn your USA Archery Star Pins based on the scores you o
 btain. Look at the bottom of your scorecard to see how many points you´ll n
 eed to receive a Star Pin.<br><br><b>Winners´ Pot and Fees</b><br>Archers i
 n Outdoor 4-9 participate in Tournament Week by entering one of the followi
 ng tournaments and paying $5.00 towards the Winners´ Pot. Winners will be a
 nnounced by email and Instagram following Tournament Saturday.&nbsp\;<br>Ar
 chers participating in Tournament Saturday or attending any Outdoor 2-9 cla
 sses will also pay $30 for their place on the shooting line\, unless they a
 lso take virtual lessons once or twice a week with Coach Racae\, in which c
 ase\, their fee is $10.<br><br>Enter one of these tournaments:<br><b>Outdoo
 r 2 + 3 Tournament :&nbsp\;</b><br>For beginners at 9m and 13.5m - One or t
 wo rounds (depending on your strength) of 10 ends of 3 arrows each for a to
 tal of 30 arrows.<br><b>Outdoor 4-9 Tournament:&nbsp\;</b><br>For more adva
 nced archers at 20m+ - Two rounds of 6 ends of 6 arrows each for a total of
  72 arrows shot on 122-cm target faces
LAST-MODIFIED:20260404T082324Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:TOURNAMENT + MASTER CHALLENGE WEEK
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
