CREATED:20250501T180249Z
DESCRIPTION:<b>REMINDER</b>:  Everyone needs to come to at least one Traini
 ng Class per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (All indoor classes a
 re training classes.)<br><br>If you are not a coach/instructor\, the fees a
 re:  <br><ul><li><b>Outdoor Training Class (OTC)</b>: $52/class or multi-cl
 ass pack </li><li><b>Indoor Training Class (ITC)</b>: $43/class or multi-cl
 ass pack or unlimited pack</li><li><b>Open Practice (OP)</b>: ($50/mo)  </l
 i></ul>If you are a coach/instructor\, you have received an email from Coac
 h Racae outlining your fees.<br><br>During the summer (May 31-Aug 31)\, at 
 least 5 archers need to register by <br>8:00 am on Thursdays (for Saturdays
 ) and <br>8:00 am on Fridays (for Sundays) <br>for Coach Racae to coach the
  Outdoor 3-9 Training Class. <span>In the case of low or late registrations
  or cancellations\, another coach/instructor\, when available\, will coach 
 the session as a Training Class or oversee it as an Open Practice instead. 
 If this is not possible\, then the class may need to be cancelled.</span><b
 r><br>Add your name to the Target Assignment List below or submit the above
  completed form.<br>Focus primarily on perfecting your form\, <br>slowly in
 creasing your physical strength and draw weight\, <br>strengthening your me
 ntal program\, <br>determining your average and personal best\, <br>underst
 anding the spread between the two\, and working on closing it.<br><br>You n
 eed your own equipment <br>Competition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, p
 lunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, ches
 t protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, a
 rrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added until you reach 
 a higher level\, but you should order them in advance.) <br><br>Wear your A
 TCI shirt to training.<br><br>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on
  the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the next distance until you rea
 ch your competition distance<br>If you trained outdoors in the 2024 season\
 , you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.<br><br>Target arrangemen
 ts may vary each session\, depending on who attends and distances needed.<b
 r>Target 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should always stay a
 t 70m so Jake can use it for independent practice in between classes.<br>Ta
 rget 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition distance) <br>Target 3 at 50m<br>T
 arget 4+5 at 40m (U15 competition distance) <br>Target 6+7+8 at 30m (U13 co
 mpetition distance) <br>Targets 9 at 20m (for those who have shot at 18m in
 doors or with Coach Racae's approval)<br>Target 10 at 13.5m (for those who 
 have just graduated from indoors at 9m)<br><br>Ideally\, we want to practic
 e with two archers/target to replicate competition conditions as much as po
 ssible.<br><br>Target Assignments:<br>Targets are assigned outdoors in adva
 nce to reduce confusion and delay on the day\,<br>so add your name next to 
 your distance below. <br>If you need help or have questions\, email/text Co
 ach Racae<br>(Dotted lines represent tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, an
 d 9.)<br>----------------------------------<br>1A. (70m)<br>1B<br><br>2A. (
 60m)  <br>2B<br><br>3A. (50m)  Joseph F.\, 14\, USAA\, pd - Please reschedu
 le<br>----------------------------------<br>3B<br><br>4A. (40m) <br>4B. <br
 >----------------------------------<br>5A. (40m)<br>5B. <br><br>6A. (30m)<b
 r>----------------------------------<br>6B. <br><br>7A. (30m)<br>7B. <br>--
 -------------------------------- <br>8A. (30m)<br>8B. <br><br>9A. (20m)<br>
 ----------------------------------<br>9B. <br><br>10A. (13.5m)<br>10B
LAST-MODIFIED:20260512T052633Z
