CREATED:20250501T180249Z
DESCRIPTION:REMINDER:  Everyone needs to come to at least one Training Clas
 s per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (All indoor classes are trai
 ning classes.)\n\nIf you are not a coach/instructor\, the fees are:  \n    
 * Outdoor Training Class (OTC): $52/class or multi-class pack \n    * Indoo
 r Training Class (ITC): $43/class or multi-class pack or unlimited pack\n  
   * Open Practice (OP): ($50/mo)  \nIf you are a coach/instructor\, you hav
 e received an email from Coach Racae outlining your fees.\n\nDuring the sum
 mer (May 31-Aug 31)\, at least 5 archers need to register by \n8:00 am on T
 hursdays (for Saturdays) and \n8:00 am on Fridays (for Sundays) \nfor Coach
  Racae to coach the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class. In the case of low or late 
 registrations or cancellations\, another coach/instructor\, when available\
 , will coach the session as a Training Class or oversee it as an Open Pract
 ice instead. If this is not possible\, then the class may need to be cancel
 led.\n\nAdd your name to the Target Assignment List below.\nFocus primarily
  on perfecting your form\, \nslowly increasing your physical strength and d
 raw weight\, \nstrengthening your mental program\, \ndetermining your avera
 ge and personal best\, \nunderstanding the spread between the two\, and wor
 king on closing it.\n\nYou need your own equipment \nCompetition recurve bo
 w\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar
  assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling
 \, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not
  be added until you reach a higher level\, but you should order them in adv
 ance.) \n\nWear your ATCI shirt to training.\n\nWhen you score 288 pts in a
  36-arrow round on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the next dist
 ance until you reach your competition distance\nIf you trained outdoors in 
 the 2024 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.\n\nTarge
 t arrangements may vary each session\, depending on who attends and distanc
 es needed.\nTarget 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should alw
 ays stay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent practice in between clas
 ses.\nTarget 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition distance) \nTarget 3 at 50
 m\nTarget 4+5 at 40m (U15 competition distance) \nTarget 6+7+8 at 30m (U13 
 competition distance) \nTargets 9 at 20m (for those who have shot at 18m in
 doors or with Coach Racae's approval)\nTarget 10 at 13.5m (for those who ha
 ve just graduated from indoors at 9m)\n\nIdeally\, we want to practice with
  two archers/target to replicate competition conditions as much as possible
 .\n\nTarget Assignments:\nTargets are assigned outdoors in advance to reduc
 e confusion and delay on the day\,\nso add your name next to your distance 
 below. \nIf you need help or have questions\, email/text Coach Racae\n(Dott
 ed lines represent tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)\n-----------
 -----------------------\n1A. (70m) Jake L.\n1B Adam M.\n\n2A. (70m) Ted H\n
 2B. \n\n3A. (60m) Nick E.   I’m in!\n----------------------------------\n3B
  \n\n4A. (50m) Adrianne M adult\, USAA (transfer from Aug 3) \, pd\n4B. \n-
 ---------------------------------\n5A. (50m) \n5B. Joseph F\, 14\, USAA\, p
 d\n\n6A. (40m) Hannah T\, USAA\, pd\n----------------------------------\n6B
 .  \n\n7A. (40m)  Luke\, 16\, USAA\, Pd\n7B. \n----------------------------
 ------ \n8A. (30m) Emma A.\, 13\, USAA\, pd\n8B. \n\n9A. (20m) Chi C.\, adu
 lt\, USAA\,\n----------------------------------\n9B. Anush K\, \n\n10A. (13
 .5m) Logan C.\, 8\, USAA\, \n10B
LAST-MODIFIED:20260512T052633Z
LOCATION:2324 Bliss Spillar Rd\, Manchaca\, TX 78652\, USA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m - Coach Racae (Confirmed)
TRANSP:OPAQUE
