DESCRIPTION:Registration form: OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m<br><br>REMINDER:  E
 veryone needs to come to at least one Training Class (TC) per week to be ab
 le to attend Open Practice. (All indoor classes are training classes.)<br><
 br>If you are not a coach/instructor\, the fees are:  <br>    * Outdoor Tra
 ining Class (OTC): $52/class or multi-class pack <br>    * Indoor Training 
 Class (ITC): $43/class or multi-class pack or unlimited pack<br>    * Open 
 Practice (OP): ($50/mo)  <br>If you are a coach/instructor\, you have recei
 ved an email from Coach Racae outlining your fees.<br><br>During the summer
  (May 31-Aug 31)\, at least 5 archers need to register by <br>8:00 am on Th
 ursdays (for Saturdays) and <br>8:00 am on Fridays (for Sundays) <br>for Co
 ach Racae to coach the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class. <br>In the case of low o
 r late registrations or cancellations\, another coach/instructor\, when ava
 ilable\, will coach the session as a Training Class or oversee it as an Ope
 n Practice instead. If this is not possible\, then the class may need to be
  cancelled.<br><br>Add your name to the Target Assignment List below or sub
 mit the above completed form.<br>Focus primarily on perfecting your form\, 
 <br>slowly increasing your physical strength and draw weight\, <br>strength
 ening your mental program\, <br>determining your average and personal best\
 , <br>understanding the spread between the two\, and working on closing it.
 <br><br>You need your own equipment <br>Competition recurve bow\, sight\, s
 tabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, c
 licker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or fie
 ld quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added unt
 il you reach a higher level\, but you should order them in advance.) <br><b
 r>Wear your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br>When you score 288 pts in a 36-a
 rrow round on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the next distance 
 until you reach your competition distance<br>If you trained outdoors in the
  2024 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.<br><br>Targ
 et arrangements may vary each session\, depending on who attends and distan
 ces needed.<br>Target 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should 
 always stay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent practice in between c
 lasses.<br>Target 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition distance) <br>Target 
 3 at 50m<br>Target 4+5 at 40m (U15 competition distance) <br>Target 6+7+8 a
 t 30m (U13 competition distance) <br>Targets 9 at 20m (for those who have s
 hot at 18m indoors or with Coach Racae's approval)<br>Target 10 at 13.5m (f
 or those who have just graduated from indoors at 9m)<br><br>Ideally\, we wa
 nt to practice with two archers/target to replicate competition conditions 
 as much as possible.<br><br>Target Assignments:<br>Targets are assigned out
 doors in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\,<br>so add your 
 name next to your distance below. <br>If you need help or have questions\, 
 email/text Coach Racae<br>(Dotted lines represent tent poles dividing Targe
 ts 3\, 6\, and 9.)<br>----------------------------------<br>1A. (70m)<br>1B
 <br><br>2A. (60m)  <b>Joel Y</b>\, adult\, pd <br>2B<br><br>3A. (50m) <b> A
 bby Y</b>\, 13\, pd <br>----------------------------------<br>3B.<b> Joseph
  F</b>\, 14\, pd<br><br>4A. (40m) <b>Erika OG\,</b> adult\, pd<br>4B. <b>Ja
