CREATED:20190606T155648Z
DESCRIPTION:We'd be very happy to host a Corporate Team Archery Event for y
 our group on a mutually convenient date. \n\nThese sessions are proving to 
 be very popular\, and we appreciate the opportunity! \nBook now so you're r
 eady for our indoor corporate archery tournaments!\n\nA few of the corporat
 ions which schedule events with us are:\nFacebook\, Intel\, Dell\, AMD\, Sa
 msung\, Home Away\, National Instruments\, Texas Mutual Insurance\, Electro
 nic Arts\, ERCOT\, Vectra Networks\, Austin Children's Advocacy\, Glatfelde
 r Insurance\, Kerbey Lane\, RackSpace\, Abilitie\, Black Locus\, Boostertho
 n\, WP Engine\, Camp Gladiator\, Marriott International\, Zimmer Biomet\, A
 ustin Gastroenterology\, Yeti\, RetailMeNot\, Tableau Software and others. 
 \n\nWe also would like to thank your company for its vital\, indirect suppo
 rt of USA Archery's Junior Olympic Archery Development (JOAD) program! Supp
 ort like yours grows Olympians! \n\nBelow is a typical agenda for a Corpora
 te Team Event with us\, and some other general info\, which may make things
  run more smoothly. \n\nCAPACITY: 1-20 participants. 10 places on the shoot
 ing line. If you'll have over 10 participants\, even numbers are best\, so 
 we can create teams of two in two lines..\n\nDAYS CLOSED: \nMONDAYS and THU
 RSDAYS\nJAN 1-5: Happy Holidays!\nAPRIL 21: Happy Easter !\nMAY 12: Happy M
 other´s Day!\nMAY 26-JUNE 7 - Summer Vacation 1\nJUNE 16 - Father´s Day!\nA
 UG 11 - 24th ANNUAL ARCHERS OF THE YEAR POTLUCK BANQUET 5:30-7:30pm - Mark 
 your calendars NOW!\nAUG 12-23 - Summer Vacation 2\n\nAGENDA (approx.- depe
 nds on number and pace of participants)\n\n1:00 Arrival\; waivers (to be si
 gned by participants over 18 years old or adults/parents/guardians)\n1:15 S
 electing two-person teams\; equipment review and selection (bows\, arrows\,
  finger tabs\, arm guards\, targets\, etc.)\n1:55 Safety rules\; whistle sy
 stem\n2:00 Break\n2:10 Form (positions) training (stance\, nocking\, hookin
 g/gripping\, set\, mindset\, set-up\, drawing\, anchor\, loading\, aiming\,
  expanding\, release\, follow-through)\n2:45 Ranking Round - shooting in te
 ams\; quantity of arrows will depend on number and pace of participants\n3:
 45 Olympic Round: Based on ranking round\; each team picks a country to rep
 resent\; all teams progress in a match play to the Gold\, Silver\, and Bron
 ze medal matches\, with other teams cheering them on!\n4:15 Awards Ceremony
  and podium presentations\, photos!\n\nSCHEDULING:\nWe can schedule a corpo
 rate team event on T/W/Th during the day for a max. of 20 people\, pending 
 your confirmation. If you would prefer another day or time\, please tell us
 \, and we'll do our best to accommodate you. Sundays 11:00am-2:00pm are als
 o available\, if booked at least two weeks in advance.\n\nTIME NEEDED:\nIt'
 s best to allow at least 3 hrs. for a team of up to 10\, and about 3.5-4 ho
 urs for more than 10 participants\, since we'll need to form two lines of s
 hooting. We may run over by as much as 30 minutes\, depending on everyone's
  arrival and ability. If this will be a problem\, please let us know\, so w
 e can pace the event carefully.\n\nARRIVALS:  We'll all start together\, so
  please have everyone arrive on time or together. \n\nPARKING: We have limi
 ted parking space for about 8-10 vehicles. Some corporations decide to park
  at a nearby shopping center parking lot\, and then "carpool" to the archer
 y range.\n\nFEE:  There is a minimum fee of $250 for 1-10 people\, and then
  $25/person for 11-20 people. We can accommodate 20 people for $500. If you
 r company requires a separate written receipt for accounting purposes\, ple
 ase tell us in advance so we can have one ready for you.\n\nPAYMENT: When y
 ou arrive at the range\, you can pay for the session individually or by cor
 porate check payable to Archery Training Center\, or by credit card (+4%). 
 All fees must be paid before the session begins. \n\nREFUNDS: If you pay in
  advance of arrival\, a refund will be issued only for cancellations or red
 uctions in attendees in writing when given notice not less than 24 hours be
 fore the session begins.\n\nEQUIPMENT:  We provide all equipment necessary 
 during the Corporate Team Event.\n\nDRESS RECOMMENDATIONS: Flat shoes are b
 est\, as we stand a lot and throw our weight forward a little\, so balance 
 and weight distribution is important. The bowstring can get slowed or entan
 gled in your clothing or hair\, so wearing tighter fitting clothes\, no wid
 e skirts\, shirts without buttons on the front pockets and tying your hair 
 back is preferable.  Longer brim baseball caps often prevent the string fro
 m reaching your face\, so shorter brims are better. In the winter on very c
 old days\, please dress in layers\, as it may be chilly in the indoor range
 .\n\nWAIVERS:  There will be waivers for each archer to fill out and sign w
 hen they first come in\, and before entering the range. All signees must be
  at least 18 years old. For those under 18\, a parent/guardian will need to
  sign for them. \n\nSPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS:    Please let us know if there ar
 e any special concepts you would like us to emphasize\, or any other consid
 erations which you would like us to take into account.\n\nOLYMPIC TARGET AR
 CHERY LINKS: \nHere are some links\, which you and your group may find inte
 resting before you get to the session.\n\nhttp://www.usarchery.org \nhttp:/
 /www.olympic.org/archery \nhttp://www.worldarchery.org\nhttp://www.youtube.
 com/archerytv\n\nThe YouTube videos showing the top American male archer\, 
 Brady Ellison\, competing with the top Korean archer\, KU Bonchan\, in the 
 Rio Olympics Men's Semi Final Match is the best we've seen in 20 years! You
  have to watch every shot.\n\nTHANK YOU for your interest in and support of
  Olympic target archery. We know you'll all really enjoy being part of the 
 Olympic Round at the end of your training!!\n\nWe look forward to your time
  with us.\n\nIf you'd like to discuss your reservation in more detail\, ple
 ase call Coach Racae Meyer 512 975 1850 at your convenience.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260404T082343Z
LOCATION:10203 Old Manchaca Rd\, Austin\, TX 78748\, USA
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Corporate Team Event - Intel - Jay
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
