UID:4n9d98n77foknse5o8arbo1vi8@google.com
CREATED:20220102T020608Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><b>Tournaments are held at the end of each calendar 
 month at 1:30-3:30pm on Saturdays and Sundays\,</b> weather permitting.&nbs
 p\;If you are new to our program\, come and try it\, so you will be more co
 mfortable and better prepared next month!<br><br>The only differences betwe
 en the regular training sessions and the tournaments are that we are more c
 losely reproducing tournament conditions\, which include:<br><ul><li>No coa
 ching while you are on the shooting line (but\, as in a real tournament\, y
 ou can always ask the coach for help in between the ends.) This is your cha
 nce to find out how well you can do the form on your own.</li><li>You will 
 shoot more arrows :&nbsp\; Practice arrows + Two rounds -&nbsp\;60 arrows a
 t 9m and 13.5m or 72 arrows at 20m-70m</li><li>You will score every arrow f
 or two rounds.&nbsp\;</li><li>The ends will be timed. You´ll have 4 min to 
 shoot 6 arrows.</li><li>Everyone will be shooting at close-to-regular tourn
 ament spacing so there will be two archers on each target about 3 ft apart.
 </li><li>There will be a maximum of 20 archers on the shooting line at the 
 same time. Awesome! (Lots of arrow flying towards the targets!)</li></ul><b
 r><b>Outside of the tournament weeks</b>\, each week the focus of your less
 ons will be on particular Steps of Shooting of the NTS (National Training S
 ystem) shot cycle\, to help you focus and improve your form\, which\, as we
  all know\, leads to greater precision (tighter groups of arrows) and ultim
 ately greater accuracy (tight groups of arrows dead center).<br><b><br></b>
 <br><b>FEBRUARY</b><br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>12-18</b>&nbsp\;Wel
 come Back: Understanding&nbsp\; NTS Concepts&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br><b>&nbsp\; &n
 bsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>19-25</b>&nbsp\;NTS Steps 1+2: STANCE + NOCK&nbsp\;&nbs
 p\;<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>26 - MAR 4: MASTER CHALLENGE TOURNA
 MENT WEEK (Pin Shoot)</b><br><b>MARCH</b><br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;5-11
 </b>&nbsp\;NTS Step 3: HOOK &amp\; GRIP&nbsp\; &nbsp\;<u></u><br><u></u>&nb
 sp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;<b>12-18&nbsp\;</b>NTS Step 4: SET<u></u><br><u></u><b>
 &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;19-25</b>&nbsp\;<u></u>NTS Step 5: SET-UP&nbsp\;&nbs
 p\;<br><u></u><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>26 - APR 1: MASTER CHALLENGE
  TOURNAMENT WEEK (Pin Shoot)</b><br><b>APRIL</b><br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbs
 p\;2-8</b>&nbsp\;<u></u>NTS Step 6 DRAW to LOAD&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;<br><
 u></u><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;9-15&nbsp\;</b><u></u>NTS Step 7 ANCHOR&nbs
 p\; &nbsp\;<br><u></u><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;16-22&nbsp\;</b><u></u>NTS 
 Step 8 TRANSFER to HOLD<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;<b>23-29&nbsp\;</b>NTS St
 ep 9 EXPAND / AIM<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;30 - MAY 6: MASTER CHALLENGE
  TOURNAMENT WEEK (Pin Shoot)</b><br><u></u><b>MAY</b><br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\;
  &nbsp\;</b><b>7-13&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</b>NTS Step 10 RELEASE and FOLLOW-THROUGH
 <br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>14-20</b>&nbsp\;<u></u>NTS Step 11 Fee
 dback and Putting it all together!<br><u></u><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b>
 <b>21/22 : END OF SEMESTER TOURNAMENT WEEKEND (Pin Shoot)</b><br><br>Your g
 oal is always to replicate the NTS step(s) mindfully and consistently on ev
 ery shot.<br><br>You do not need to score every class. In fact\, it would b
 e more beneficial to you if you scored only during Master Challenge Tournam
 ent Weeks\, which happen the last week of each month. This is because worki
 ng on the NTS Steps of Shooting (your form) is more easily done without the
  distraction of the target face or scoring\, and you will improve faster.<b
 r><br>As you reach higher levels\, you will learn the NTS Steps in progress
 ively greater detail.<br>The NTS Steps are cumulative with each step most s
 uccessfully completed if the previous steps have been completed mindfully.&
 nbsp\;<br><br>Your ability to learn and understand the NTS Steps\, and use 
 deep focus on these Steps while shooting outdoors and while using your stre
 tchband/string loop at home will propel you to higher levels fast!<br><br><
 b>Goals by the end of the semester (May 22):&nbsp\;</b><br>See Coach Racae´
 s email ¨2022 New Year´s Goals¨<u></u><u></u></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260404T082324Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:ATCI OUTDOOR 2-9 MASTER CHALLENGE TOURNAMENT (Pin Shoot)
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
