DESCRIPTION:Registration form: OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m<br><br>REMINDER:  E
 veryone needs to come to at least one Training Class per week to be able to
  attend Open Practice. (All indoor classes are training classes.)<br><br>If
  you are not a coach/instructor\, the fees are:  <br>Outdoor Training Class
  (OTC): $52/class or multi-class pack <br>Indoor Training Class (ITC): $43/
 class or multi-class pack or unlimited pack<br>Open Practice (OP): ($50/mo)
   <br>If you are a coach/instructor\, you have received an email from Coach
  Racae outlining your fees.<br><br>Coach Racae will coach the Outdoor 3-9 T
 raining Classes on Saturdays and Sundays\, when at least 5 archers register
  by <br>8:00 am on Thursdays (for Saturdays) and <br>8:00 am on Fridays (fo
 r Sundays) <br>In the case of low or late registrations or cancellations\, 
 another coach/instructor\, when available\, will coach the session as a Tra
 ining Class or oversee it as an Open Practice instead. If this is not possi
 ble\, then the class may need to be cancelled.<br>Add your name to the Targ
 et Assignment List below.<br>Focus primarily on perfecting your form\, <br>
 slowly increasing your physical strength and draw weight\, <br>strengthenin
 g your mental program\, <br>determining your average and personal best\, <b
 r>understanding the spread between the two\, and working on closing it.<br>
 <br>You need your own equipment <br>Competition recurve bow\, sight\, stabi
 lizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, click
 er\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field q
 uiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added until y
 ou reach a higher level\, but you should order them in advance.) <br><br>We
 ar your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow
  round on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the next distance unti
 l you reach your competition distance<br>If you trained outdoors in the 202
 4 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.<br><br>Target a
 rrangements may vary each session\, depending on who attends and distances 
 needed.<br>Target 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should alwa
 ys stay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent practice in between class
 es.<br>Target 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition distance) <br>Target 3 at
  50m<br>Target 4+5 at 40m (U15 competition distance) <br>Target 6+7+8 at 30
 m (U13 competition distance) <br>Targets 9 at 20m (for those who have shot 
 at 18m indoors or with Coach Racae's approval)<br>Target 10 at 13.5m (for t
 hose who have just graduated from indoors at 9m)<br><br>Ideally\, we want t
 o practice with two archers/target to replicate competition conditions as m
 uch as possible.<br><br>Target Assignments:<br>Targets are assigned outdoor
 s in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\,<br>so add your name
  next to your distance below. <br>If you need help or have questions\, emai
 l/text Coach Racae<br>(Dotted lines represent tent poles dividing Targets 3
 \, 6\, and 9.)<br>----------------------------------<br>1A. (<b>70m</b>)<br
 >1B<br><br>2A. (<b>60m</b>)  Nick E\, adult\, USAA\, <b>248 pts</b><br>2B<b
 r><br>3A. (<b>50m</b>)  Adrianne M\, adult USAA\, transfer (8/17) 251 + 248
  = <b>499 pts</b><br>----------------------------------<br>3B<br><br>4A. (<
 b>40m</b>) Luke T\, 16 USAA\, Pd<br>4B.  <b>Finn E\, </b>13\, USAA\, pd -  
