DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20190302T113000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20190302T140000
DTSTAMP:20261004T164458Z
UID:3n1c5aq0spleejr16ahe408mr4@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Chicago:20190302T113000
CREATED:20181219T185313Z
DESCRIPTION:\nAinsley B.\, 11\nDan B\, parent\nAlissa B.\, parent\nMaggie S
 .\, 10\nDaniela C.\, 10\; \nChloe McK. 10\; \nMaddie L.\, 11\; Berit 11\; \
 nMarissa McG.\, 10\; \nWillow R.\,11\n\nTHANKS SO MUCH for giving us the op
 portunity to share your special day!\nIt helps our Junior Olympic Archery p
 rogram (JOAD) a lot when you introduce your friends to the fun of Olympic t
 arget archery!\n\nHere are a few things that may help you plan....\n\n\nADD
 RESSES:\nRANGE:    10203 OLD Manchaca Rd.\, Austin\, TX 78748\nMAILING:  Ar
 chery Training Center\, Inc.\, PO Box 93216\, Austin\, TX 78709\n\nE-MAIL: 
 archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com\n\nDAYS CLOSED: \nMONDAYS and FRIDAYS
 \nAPRIL 21: HAPPY EASTER !\nMAY 12: MOTHER´S DAY !\n\nTIMES OPEN:\nPlease d
 rop in during business hours and between classes to visit.\nSUNDAYS:       
 11:30am-6:00pm\nTUESDAYS:       5:30pm-8:30pm\nWEDNESDAYS: 5:30pm-8:30pm\nT
 HURSDAYS:    6:00pm-8:30pm (when there is a first-time class)\nSATURDAYS:  
  11:30am-6:00pm\n(We are OPEN during the above times during Spring Break: M
 arch 18-22)\n\nWHAT AGES?\n10 years old and above. (We do adult birthday pa
 rties\, too!)\nChildren not participating must be supervised by an adult fr
 om your party. Additional parents may be asked to help oversee archers on t
 he line.\n\nHOW MANY ARCHERS?\nMax. of 10 archers. \n\nWHAT DAYS and TIMES 
 ARE AVAILABLE?\nFirst check www.archerytrainingcenter.com/calendar to make 
 sure another party or individuals have not already booked the time you woul
 d like to come.\n\nSAT/SUN: 11:30am-2:00pm \n(You will be occupying the tim
 e slot usually reserved for the Indoor 1: First-time Class) Book early!\nT/
 W: 2:30-5:00pm \nTH: 5:00-7:30pm\nM/F: 3:00-5:30 pm (We are usually closed 
 on these days\, but we will open the facility for your party for a higher f
 ee.)\n\n\nWHAT ARE THE MINIMUM FEES to reserve the range for my group?\n$25
 0 on weekends (11:30am-2:00pm)\n$250 on T/W (2:30-5:00pm)\n$350 on M/Th/F (
 2.5 hrs between 1:00-6:00pm)\n\nHOW DO I PAY IN ADVANCE?\nAFTER you fill in
  the 2019 Birthday Parties form online\, we will confirm your birthday part
 y date by sending you a confirmation email\, and placing your birthday part
 y on the Calendar at www.archerytrainingcenter.com. AFTER we confirm\, the 
 birthday party organizer pays the total fees in advance. If you need to can
 cel\, you must give us at least 24 hours´ notice in order to receive a full
  refund. Less than 24 hours´ notice will entitle you to only a 50% refund.\
 nNEW!! You can now also pay at www.PayPal.Me/atciaustin . (Please add 4% an
 d make sure to wait for confirmation of the date/time before paying! Refere
 nce your party´s name and date on the payment.)\nWe also accept cash or che
 cks by mail or in person and credit cards (+4%) by phone or in person.\nPle
 ase make your check payable to "Archery Training Center\, Inc." and give it
  to us at the range or mail it to us at:\nArchery Training Center\, Inc.\, 
 PO Box 93216\, Austin\, TX 78709-3216\n\nHOW LONG ARE THE BIRTHDAY PARTIES?
 \nBirthday parties are usually about 2-1/2 hours. Please arrive at least 15
  min. before the party begins.\n\nHOW FAR IN ADVANCE SHOULD I BOOK?\nAt lea
 st 2-3 weeks in advance. \n\nHOW DO I KNOW IF MY BIRTHDAY PARTY IS BOOKED?\
 nLook at the Calendar at www.archerytrainingcenter.com a few hours after yo
 u submit the form below\, to make sure your party is registered on the Cale
 ndar for the day/time you wanted. (We will contact you by email to confirm 
 before putting it up on the Calendar.)\n\nCONTACTS AND WAIVERS\nEach partic
 ipant (or the parent of a junior archer) will need to fill out and sign the
  Membership form\, Release of Liability Waiver\, and Photo Release. The Saf
 ety Rules must also be reviewed with the junior archer and signed before cl
 ass. These 4 Indoor 1 Documents will be sent to you by email when we confir
 m. If some parents accompany the archer to the birthday party\, they can si
 gn the forms at the range. ALL FORMS MUST BE SUBMITTED BEFORE THE ARCHER WI
 LL BE ALLOWED TO ENTER THE RANGE.\n\nARRIVALS\nWe all start together. It is
  important for everyone to arrive 15 min. before the party begins\, so we c
 an start on time. If some people are late\, we may start 15 minutes or so l
 ate\, which will mean less shooting for everyone. We would recommend carpoo
 ling from another location\, so everyone arrives on time.\n\nPARKING\nThere
  is limited parking for a max. of 10 cars outside our range. If you'll need
  more parking\, please carpool from another nearby public parking location 
 (shopping center\, etc.).\n\nPARTY AGENDA\nThe party will be an abbreviated
  version of the Indoor 1 First-time Class. We will enforce the safety rules
 \, so everyone should read them carefully. \nAfter everyone learns the basi
 cs\, they'll start shooting. It's impossible to just "let them shoot" as so
 on as they arrive\, because (besides the safety factor)\, they just wouldn'
 t hit anything\, and would become very frustrated...so a basic lesson in go
 od form is essential for them in order to enjoy shooting. \nAfter everyone 
 shoots for a while or scores 50 pts. at 9m\, we'll put up balloons on the w
 all\, and all the archers will try to hit theirs. If some balloons remain\,
  they can take them home\, or watch as the best archer of the day or the bi
 rthday boy/girl/adult tries to hit them. Everyone cheers! The balloons are 
 always a big hit and create a lot of laughter. \n\nAWARDS\nEveryone will re
 ceive a Personal Best award and\, if they shoot 50+ pts.\, also a Qualifier
  Certificate\, which means they are then members of USA Archery's Junior Ol
 ympic program or Adult Training Program\, and can join the regularly schedu
 led classes (Indoor 2 classes on the Calendar). \n\nWHAT WE PROVIDE\nWe pro
 vide all archery equipment\, balloons (to shoot at)\, bottled water\, napki
 ns. \nYou can see photos of the interior of our facility on our website or 
 on our Instagram. The white round tables with red/blue/black chairs in the 
 area adjacent to the archery range will seat 10-13 participants comfortably
 . \n\nWHAT YOU COULD BRING\nYou can bring whatever other refreshments and f
 ood you like. Most bring easy-to-eat cupcakes\, doughnuts\, cookies\, cake\
 , soft drinks\, orange juice\, etc.  (There are lots of photos online of ar
 chery-decorated deserts!) Please also remember to bring the cutlery\, plate
 s\, cups\, etc.\, and\, of course\, PRESENTS!\n\nWHEN SHOULD THEY EAT?\nAFT
 ER the shooting and archery photos\, otherwise there are sticky fingers on 
 the equipment\, delays\, etc. (You could set the tables while the archers a
 re shooting.) Most prefer to do the archery part separately\, and go home o
 r to a restaurant for the "cake and presents" part\, as there is often a re
 gularly scheduled archery class starting immediately after the birthday par
 ty archers finish shooting.\n\nPHOTOS\nIn the 2019 Birthday Parties registr
 ation form are some great recommendations on taking photos!\n\nCLEAN UP\nTh
 ere will be trashcans available for your use. Please clean and wipe off the
  tables and pick up any items or food from the range that need to be thrown
  away\, unless the coach instructs otherwise. There may be a class immediat
 ely after your party\, so we appreciate your help cleaning up!\n\nPICK UP\n
 Every archer is to leave the range immediately after the birthday party. Ou
 r instructor(s) may be coaching another class immediately after your party\
 , or turning off the lights and air-conditioning\, locking the range\, and 
 leaving the building\, so the birthday party organizer needs to make sure t
 hat if one or more of your guest junior archers has not been picked up imme
 diately after the party\, you stay with them until they are picked up. Plea
 se have their parents' contact numbers so you can get in touch with them fo
 r instructions\, if necessary.\n\nSAFE SPORTS:\nParents please note we are 
 part of the US Olympic Committee's Safe Sport program\, so we minimally req
 uire one other adult besides the instructor to be present at all times. Ple
 ase plan to stay with your child or take turns with other parents staying w
 henever necessary to fulfill this requirement. THANKS!\n\nQUESTIONS...?\nIf
  you have any questions at any time before your event\, just email us at ar
 cherytrainingcenteraustin.com\, call us at 512 975 1850\, or talk with us a
 t the archery range. \n\nYou're all going to have a great time !!!
LAST-MODIFIED:20260512T052633Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:FULL ! Archery Birthday Party! - Brown
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
