DESCRIPTION:<b>Tuesday\, August 13\, 1:00-4:00 pm</b><br><br><b>WAIVERS:</b
 > Everyone needs to <b>sign the waivers in advance </b>of arriving at the r
 ange\, so we are not delayed in starting. Here's the link: <a href="https:/
 /docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdYr3Yh5msvPHC_-ukFsifcvhYXRrzVRvcdyP4Ybx
 9O5zgUug/viewform" target="_blank"><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u>2024
  Corporate Team Events Waivers Packet</u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></
 u></u></u></a>  <br><br><b>DIRECTIONS:</b> <b>Google Map "Donut Taco Palace
 "</b> to find us quickly - We are right next door in Unit 102. (Some people
  are still being misdirected.) There is a target on the glass door and the 
 unit is facing 290W service road going west on the corner of Industrial Oak
 s Blvd and 290W. <br><br><b>ARRIVAL</b>: For a 1:00 pm start\, please <b>ar
 rive by 12:45 pm</b>\, because we need to start together at 1:00 pm. <br><b
 r><b>CARPOOLING / PARKING:</b> Please meet and carpool earlier from another
  location or from a big box store parking lot across the highway (like Targ
 et or At Home on the corner of Mopac and 290W). It's easy and convenient to
  do. (Parking in front of the range and along Industrial Oaks Blvd may be l
 imited\, depending on the number of participants.)<br><br><b>DRESS RECOMMEN
 DATIONS: </b><br>Flat athletic shoes are best\, as we will be throwing our 
 weight forward a little\, so balance and weight distribution is important. 
 The bowstring can get slowed or entangled in your clothing or hair\, so wea
 ring tightly fitting clothes\, no wide skirts\, shirts without buttons on t
 he front pockets and tying your hair back is preferable. Longer brim baseba
 ll caps often prevent the string from reaching your face\, so shorter brims
  or bucket hats are better. <br>:<br><b>All participants need to complete w
 aivers online before the event.</b><br><b>Here is the direct link to comple
 te: </b><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdYr3Yh5msvPHC_-u
 kFsifcvhYXRrzVRvcdyP4Ybx9O5zgUug/viewform" target="_blank"><u><u><u><u><u><
 u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u>2024 Corporate Team Events Waivers Packet</u></u></u
 ></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></a>  <br><br>Waivers have been re
 ceived from those shown below in <b>bold with (W)</b><br><b>12 people atten
 ded - received 9 scorecards (indicated with -&gt\; Indoor 2)</b><br>Average
 d = score divided by number of arrows shot and recorded x 30 arrows/round <
 br><br>1. <b>Ana M. </b><b>(W) 122 pts </b>(averaged) -. <b>Indoor 2</b><br
 ><b><br></b><br>2. <b>Kathaleen D. (W) 111 pts </b>(averaged) -&gt\; <b>Ind
 oor 2</b><b><br></b><br><p>3. <b>Fred E. <u></u><u></u></b><b> (W) 105 pts 
 </b>(averaged) <b>-&gt\; Indoor 2</b></p>4. <b>Rosa G.(W) 100 pts </b>(aver
 aged) <b>-&gt\; Indoor 2</b><br><b><br></b><br>5. <b>Morgan B. </b><u></u><
 u></u><b> (W)  63 pts </b>(averaged) -&gt\; <b>Indoor 2</b><b><br></b><br><
 b><br></b><br>6. <b>Alexiea F. (W)</b> - <b>50 pts </b>(averaged)<b> -&gt\;
  Indoor 2</b><br><b><br></b><br>7. <b>Claudia M.S.</b><b> (W) -&gt\; Indoor
  2</b><br><br>8. <b>Diana L. (W) -&gt\; Indoor 2</b><br><b><br></b><br>9. <
 b>Elena J. (W) -&gt\; Indoor 2</b><p><u></u></p><p>10. <b>Alyson H. </b><b>
 (W)</b><br></p><p>11. <b>Christian G. (W)</b></p><p>12. <b>Kevin A.</b><b> 
