DESCRIPTION:Registration form: OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m<br><br>REMINDER:  E
 veryone needs to come to at least one Training Class per week to be able to
  attend Open Practice. (All indoor classes are training classes.)<br><br>If
  you are not a coach/instructor\, the fees are:  <br><br>Outdoor Training C
 lass (OTC): $52/class or multi-class pack <br><br>Indoor Training Class (IT
 C): $43/class or multi-class pack or unlimited pack<br><br>Open Practice (O
 P): ($50/mo)  <br><br>If you are a coach/instructor\, you have received an 
 email from Coach Racae outlining your fees.<br><br><br>Coach Racae will coa
 ch the Outdoor 3-9 Training Classes on Saturdays and Sundays\, when at leas
 t 5 archers register by <br>8:00 am on Thursdays (for Saturdays) and <br>8:
 00 am on Fridays (for Sundays) <br>In the case of low or late registrations
  or cancellations\, another coach/instructor\, when available\, will coach 
 the session as a Training Class or oversee it as an Open Practice instead. 
 If this is not possible\, then the class may need to be cancelled.<br>Add y
 our name to the Target Assignment List below.<br>Focus primarily on perfect
 ing your form\, <br>slowly increasing your physical strength and draw weigh
 t\, <br>strengthening your mental program\, <br>determining your average an
 d personal best\, <br>understanding the spread between the two\, and workin
 g on closing it.<br><br>You need your own equipment <br>Competition recurve
  bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-
 bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sl
 ing\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may 
 not be added until you reach a higher level\, but you should order them in 
 advance.) <br><br>Wear your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br>When you score 2
 88 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to th
 e next distance until you reach your competition distance<br>If you trained
  outdoors in the 2024 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you s
 hot.<br><br>Target arrangements may vary each session\, depending on who at
 tends and distances needed.<br>Target 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition d
 istance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent pract
 ice in between classes.<br>Target 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition dista
 nce) <br>Target 3 at 50m<br>Target 4+5 at 40m (U15 competition distance) <b
 r>Target 6+7+8 at 30m (U13 competition distance) <br>Targets 9 at 20m (for 
 those who have shot at 18m indoors or with Coach Racae's approval)<br>Targe
 t 10 at 13.5m (for those who have just graduated from indoors at 9m)<br><br
 >Ideally\, we want to practice with two archers/target to replicate competi
 tion conditions as much as possible.<br><br>Target Assignments:<br>Targets 
 are assigned outdoors in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\,
 <br>so add your name next to your distance below. <br>If you need help or h
 ave questions\, email/text Coach Racae<br>(Dotted lines represent tent pole
 s dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)<br>----------------------------------<br
 >1A. (70m)<br>1B<br><br>2A. (60m)  <b>Joel Y</b>\, adult\, USAA\, ob\, pd <
 b>242 +187 = 429 pts</b><br>2B<br><br>3A. (50m)  <b>Abby Y</b>\, 13\, USAA\
 , ob\, pd <b>271 +258 = 529 pts</b><br>----------------------------------<b
 r>3B<br><br>4A. (40m) <b>Sophia D</b>\, adult\, f - <b>247+248 = 495 pts</b
 ><br>4B. <br>----------------------------------<br>5A. (40m) <b>Colby K</b>
 .!!! Adult!!! USAA!!!  Paid? - <b>262 +289 = 551 pts - CONGRATULATIONS !!! 
 -&gt\; Outdoor 7 @ 50m !!!</b><br>5B. <b>Miles G.</b>\, 13\, USAA\, pd <b>2
 16+193 = 409 pts</b><br><b><br></b>6A. (30m)<b> Ellie Y</b>\, 10\, USAA\, O
 B\,pd <b>215+192 = 407 pts</b><br>----------------------------------<br>6B.
  <br><br>7A. (30m) <b>Emma A</b>.\, 13\, USAA\, OB\, pd <b>173+181 = 354 pt
 s</b><br>7B. <br>---------------------------------- <br>8A. (20m)<br>8B. <b
 r><br>9A. (18m)<br>----------------------------------<br>9B. <br><br>10A. (
 13.5m)<br>10B
