DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><b>UPDATE: With the news that Austin/T
 ravis County is now in Stage 5 of COVID-19 risk-based guidelines\, I have m
 ade the decision to postpone the start of our archery training classes this
  semester until Austin drops back down to Stage 4.&nbsp\;</b><br>I will rev
 iew the situation weekly on Fridays and postpone weekend and Monday classes
 \, if Austin is still in Stage 5.&nbsp\;<b>(See my Friday email to you.)</b
 ><b><br></b><br>I know this is disappointing to most of you - and no one wa
 nts to attend the training classes more than I do. I love to coach you! My 
 main concern\, however\, as always\, is to keep everyone who attends our cl
 asses as safe as possible.&nbsp\;<br><br>Not to worry\, we will start class
 es soon again!<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &
 nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbs
 p\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;
  &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; Coach Racae<br><br>REGISTER NOW !<br>This 
 class is open to adults\, juniors\, and parents who have taken and graduate
 d out of Outdoor 1: First-time Class and are shooting at distances of 9m to
  70m. It is a mixed class of different distances.&nbsp\;<br><br>Sign up any
  time for as many or as few Outdoor 2-9 Classes as you like.<br><br>Registe
 r at one of these links depending on your level:<br><a href="https://docs.g
 oogle.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfhDoxxJ9Ce7AtP_RpCukDqlwQRYE3f0JWOdCeK2UG97HCHX
