 bsp\;</b>NTS Step 9 EXPAND / AIM&nbsp\;<b><br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b
 >30 - MAY 6: MASTER CHALLENGE TOURNAMENT WEEK (Pin Shoot)</b><br><b>MAY</b>
 <br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>7-13&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</b>NTS Step 10 RELE
 ASE + FOLLOW-THROUGH<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>14-20</b>&nbsp\; N
 TS Step 11: FEEDBACK + Putting it all together!<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp
 \;</b><b>21/22 : END OF SEMESTER TOURNAMENT WEEKEND (Pin Shoot)</b><br><br>
 Each week the focus of your lessons will be on particular Steps of Shooting
  of the NTS (National Training System) shot cycle\, to help you focus and i
 mprove your form\, which\, as we all know\, leads to greater precision (tig
 ht groups of arrows) and ultimately greater accuracy (tight groups of arrow
 s dead center).<br><br>Your goal is always to replicate the NTS step(s) min
 dfully and consistently on every shot.<br><br>You do not need to score in e
 very class. In fact\, it would be more beneficial to you if you scored only
  during Master Challenge Tournament Weeks\, which happen the last week of e
 ach month. This is because working on the NTS Steps of Shooting (your form)
  is more easily done without the distraction of the target face or scoring\
 , and you will improve faster.<br><br>As you reach higher levels\, you will
  learn the NTS Steps in progressively greater detail.<br>The NTS Steps are 
 cumulative with each step most successfully completed if the previous steps
  have been completed well.&nbsp\;<br><br>Your ability to learn and understa
 nd the NTS Steps\, and use deep focus on these Steps while shooting outdoor
 s and while using your stretchband/string loop at home to reinforce form po
 isitions will propel you to higher levels fast!<br><br><b>Goals by the end 
 of the semester (May 22):&nbsp\;</b><br>See Coach Racae´s email ¨2022 New Y
 ear´s Goals¨<br></html-blob>
