DESCRIPTION:This class has been cancelled due to low registrations. \n\nREM
 INDER:  Everyone needs to come to at least one Training Class per week to b
 e able to attend Open Practice. (All indoor classes are training classes.)\
 n\nIf you are not a coach/instructor\, the fees are:  \n    * Outdoor Train
 ing Class (OTC): $52/class or multi-class pack \n    * Indoor Training Clas
 s (ITC): $43/class or multi-class pack or unlimited pack\n    * Open Practi
 ce (OP): ($50/mo)  \nIf you are a coach/instructor\, you have received an e
 mail from Coach Racae outlining your fees.\n\nDuring the summer (May 31-Aug
  31)\, at least 5 archers need to register by \n8:00 am on Thursdays (for S
 aturdays) and \n8:00 am on Fridays (for Sundays) \nfor Coach Racae to coach
  the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class. In the case of low or late registrations o
 r cancellations\, another coach/instructor\, when available\, will coach th
 e session as a Training Class or oversee it as an Open Practice instead. If
  this is not possible\, then the class may need to be cancelled.\n\nAdd you
 r name to the Target Assignment List below or submit the above completed fo
 rm.\nFocus primarily on perfecting your form\, \nslowly increasing your phy
 sical strength and draw weight\, \nstrengthening your mental program\, \nde
 termining your average and personal best\, \nunderstanding the spread betwe
 en the two\, and working on closing it.\n\nYou need your own equipment \nCo
 mpetition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arr
 ows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fing
 ertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker a
 nd side rods may not be added until you reach a higher level\, but you shou
 ld order them in advance.) \n\nWear your ATCI shirt to training.\n\nWhen yo
 u score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm target face you'll move b
 ack to the next distance until you reach your competition distance\nIf you 
 trained outdoors in the 2024 season\, you'll return to the farthest distanc
 e you shot.\n\nTarget arrangements may vary each session\, depending on who
  attends and distances needed.\nTarget 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition 
 distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent prac
 tice in between classes.\nTarget 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition distan
 ce) \nTarget 3 at 50m\nTarget 4+5 at 40m (U15 competition distance) \nTarge
 t 6+7+8 at 30m (U13 competition distance) \nTargets 9 at 20m (for those who
  have shot at 18m indoors or with Coach Racae's approval)\nTarget 10 at 13.
 5m (for those who have just graduated from indoors at 9m)\n\nIdeally\, we w
 ant to practice with two archers/target to replicate competition conditions
  as much as possible.\n\nTarget Assignments:\nTargets are assigned outdoors
  in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\,\nso add your name ne
 xt to your distance below. \nIf you need help or have questions\, email/tex
 t Coach Racae\n(Dotted lines represent tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, 
 and 9.)\n----------------------------------\n1A. (70m)\n1B\n\n2A. (60m)  \n
 2B\n\n3A. (50m)  Joseph F\, 14\, pd - reschedule\n-------------------------
 ---------\n3B\n\n4A. (40m) \n4B. \n----------------------------------\n5A. 
 (40m)\n5B. \n\n6A. (30m)\n----------------------------------\n6B. \n\n7A. (
 30m)\n7B. \n---------------------------------- \n8A. (30m)\n8B. \n\n9A. (20
 m)\n----------------------------------\n9B. \n\n10A. (13.5m)\n10B
