DESCRIPTION:For archers in Outdoor 2-9.<br><br><b>Tournament Week</b><br>Fo
 r one week each month during Tournament Week\, you shoot for score and subm
 it your scores to Coach Racae. You can score in your regular classes or com
 e to the tournament on Tournament Saturday.<br><br><b>Tournament Saturday</
 b><br>On the last day of tournament week\, Saturday\, Coach Racae will cond
 uct the Saturday Outdoor 4-9 class as a tournament with timed rounds and sc
 oring and little to no coaching.&nbsp\;<br><br><b>Master Challenge</b><br>W
 hile you´re shooting in the tournament&nbsp\; Coach Racae will look at your
  form and assess how much attention to form you can remember to do while sh
 ooting in a tournament. You can earn Mastered Tags for each step of the for
 m you have consistently done at your level. As you progress through higher 
 levels\, the level of detail required will increase and additional position
 s will be added.<br><br><b>USA Archery Star Pins</b><br>If you are a member
  of USA Archery\, Tournament Saturday is often called a ¨Pin Shoot¨\, when 
 you can earn your USA Archery Star Pins based on the scores you obtain. Loo
 k at the bottom of your scorecard to see how many points you´ll need to rec
 eive a Star Pin.<br><br><b>Winners´ Pot and Fees</b><br>Archers participate
  in Tournament Week by entering one of the following tournaments and paying
  $5.00 towards the Winners´ Pot. Winners will be announced by email and Ins
 tagram following Tournament Saturday.&nbsp\;<br>Archers participating in To
 urnament Saturday or attending any Outdoor 2-9 classes will also pay $30 fo
 r their place on the shooting line\, unless they also take virtual lessons 
 once or twice a week with Coach Racae\, in which case\, their fee is $10.<b
 r><br>Enter one of these tournaments:<br><b>Outdoor 2 + 3 Tournament :&nbsp
 \;</b><br>For beginners at 9m and 13.5m - One or two rounds (depending on y
 our strength) of 10 ends of 3 arrows each for a total of 30 arrows.<br><b>O
 utdoor 4-9 Tournament:&nbsp\;</b><br>For more advanced archers at 20+ m - T
 wo rounds of 6 ends of 6 arrows each for a total of 72 arrows shot on 122-c
 m target faces
LAST-MODIFIED:20260404T082324Z
