DESCRIPTION:For archers in Outdoor 2-9.<br><br><b>Tournament Week</b><br>Fo
 r one week each month during Tournament Week\, you shoot for score and subm
 it your scores to Coach Racae. Score in your regular classes or come to the
  tournament on Tournament Saturday.<br><br><b>Tournament Saturday</b><br>On
  the last day of tournament week\, Saturday\, Coach Racae will conduct the 
 Saturday Outdoor 4-9 class as a tournament with timed rounds and scoring an
 d little to no coaching.&nbsp\;<br><br><b>Master Challenge</b><br>While you
 ´re shooting in the tournament&nbsp\; Coach Racae will look at your form an
 d assess how much attention to form you can remember to do while shooting i
 n a tournament. You can earn Mastered Tags for each step of the form you ha
 ve consistently done at your level. As you progress through higher levels\,
  the level of detail required will increase and additional positions will b
 e added.<br><br><b>USA Archery Star Pins</b><br><b>If you are a member of U
 SA Archery</b>\, Tournament Saturday is often called a ¨Pin Shoot¨\, when y
 ou can earn your USA Archery Star Pins based on the scores you obtain. Look
  at the bottom of your scorecard to see how many points you´ll need to rece
 ive a Star Pin.<br><br><b>Winners´ Pot and Fees</b><br>Archers participate 
 in Tournament Week by entering one of the following tournaments and paying 
 $5.00 towards the Winners´ Pot. Winners will be announced by email and Inst
 agram following Tournament Saturday.&nbsp\;<br>Archers participating in Tou
 rnament Saturday or attending any Outdoor 2-9 classes will also pay $30 for
  their place on the shooting line\, unless they also take virtual lessons o
 nce or twice a week with Coach Racae\, in which case\, their fee is $10.<br
 ><br>Enter one of these tournaments:<br><b>Outdoor 2 + 3 Tournament :&nbsp\
 ;</b><br>For beginners at 9m and 13.5m - One or two rounds (depending on yo
 ur strength) of 10 ends of 3 arrows each for a total of 30 arrows.<br><b>Ou
 tdoor 4-9 Tournament:&nbsp\;</b><br>For more advanced archers at 20m+ - Two
  rounds of 6 ends of 6 arrows each for a total of 72 arrows shot on 122-cm 
 target faces
LAST-MODIFIED:20260404T082343Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:TOURNAMENT + MASTER CHALLENGE WEEK
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
