DESCRIPTION:REMINDER:  Everyone needs to come to at least one Training Clas
 s per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (All indoor classes are trai
 ning classes.)\n\nIf you are not a coach/instructor\, the fees are:  \n    
 * Outdoor Training Class (OTC): $52/class or multi-class pack \n    * Indoo
 r Training Class (ITC): $43/class or multi-class pack or unlimited pack\n  
   * Open Practice (OP): ($50/mo)  \nIf you are a coach/instructor\, you hav
 e received an email from Coach Racae outlining your fees.\n\nDuring the sum
 mer (May 31-Aug 31)\, at least 5 archers need to register by \n8:00 am on T
 hursdays (for Saturdays) and \n8:00 am on Fridays (for Sundays) \nfor Coach
  Racae to coach the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class. \nIn the case of low or lat
 e registrations or cancellations\, another coach/instructor\, when availabl
 e\, will coach the session as a Training Class or oversee it as an Open Pra
 ctice instead. If this is not possible\, then the class may need to be canc
 elled.\n\nAdd your name to the Target Assignment List below or submit the a
 bove completed form.\nFocus primarily on perfecting your form\, \nslowly in
 creasing your physical strength and draw weight\, \nstrengthening your ment
 al program\, \ndetermining your average and personal best\, \nunderstanding
  the spread between the two\, and working on closing it.\n\nYou need your o
 wn equipment \nCompetition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, res
 t\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\
 , armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\
 , etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added until you reach a higher lev
 el\, but you should order them in advance.) \n\nWear your ATCI shirt to tra
 ining.\n\nWhen you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm target f
 ace you'll move back to the next distance until you reach your competition 
 distance\nIf you trained outdoors in the 2024 season\, you'll return to the
  farthest distance you shot.\n\nTarget arrangements may vary each session\,
  depending on who attends and distances needed.\nTarget 1 at 70m (U21 + Sen
 iors competition distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use it for
  independent practice in between classes.\nTarget 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters c
 ompetition distance) \nTarget 3 at 50m\nTarget 4+5 at 40m (U15 competition 
 distance) \nTarget 6+7+8 at 30m (U13 competition distance) \nTargets 9 at 2
 0m (for those who have shot at 18m indoors or with Coach Racae's approval)\
 nTarget 10 at 13.5m (for those who have just graduated from indoors at 9m)\
 n\nIdeally\, we want to practice with two archers/target to replicate compe
 tition conditions as much as possible.\n\nTarget Assignments:\nTargets are 
 assigned outdoors in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\,\nso
  add your name next to your distance below. \nIf you need help or have ques
 tions\, email/text Coach Racae\n(Dotted lines represent tent poles dividing
  Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)\n----------------------------------\n1A. (70m)\n1B
 \n\n2A. (60m)  Joel Y\, adult\, pd\n2B\n\n3A. (50m)  Abby Y\, 13\, pd\n----
 ------------------------------\n3B. Joseph F\, 14\, pd\n\n4A. (40m) Erika O
 G\, adult\, pd\n4B. Javier G\, adult\, pd\n--------------------------------
 --\n5A. (40m) Colby K.!!! Adult\, pd\n5B. Anna P\, adult\,pd\n\n6A. (30m) E
 llie Y\, 10\, pd\n----------------------------------\n6B. \n\n7A. (30m)\n7B
 . \n---------------------------------- \n8A. (30m)\n8B. \n\n9A. (20m)\n----
 ------------------------------\n9B. \n\n10A. (13.5m) Emma A.\, 13\, pd\n10B
LAST-MODIFIED:20260512T052633Z
