UID:7on69dlrtkc98lrh4jcgen44ij@google.com
CREATED:20250403T204202Z
DESCRIPTION:<b>Alex </b>- <i>Shot one round for score. Excellent. Focused o
 n getting to Anchor and holding it for 3 sec.\, testing whether target pani
 c had already set in\, which would show as his inability to actually anchor
 . Needed 10 good anchors\, and started over if one was &lt\; 3 sec. Showed 
 incredible perseverance\, determination\, and grit. Kept going through seve
 ral setbacks to achieve his goal of 10 good anchors. Very impressive! Yay!<
 /i><br><i><br></i><br><b>Alejandro </b>- <i>Excellent discussions on Korean
  vs American NTS form\; looked at video of Rick McKinney. Used camera at fr
 ont view to improve bow arm - raising it to shoulder height to form better 
 alignment and then changing sight position (moving it down) so sight would 
 not dictate form. Adjusting for target height variations should be through 
 bending at waist\, not raising or lowering bow arm or draw elbow. Keeping t
 he "T" and lining up the bones to brace the forces of the bow. Improved.<br
 ></i>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260404T082324Z
LOCATION:5446 W US Hwy 290 Service Rd\, Unit 102\, Austin\, TX 78735\, USA
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY: INTENSIVE PRIVATE CLINIC with Coach Racae - The Alejandros
