 rovided they have also taken an Indoor 1: First-time Class.<br><br>PLEASE C
 OMPLETE ONE REGISTRATION FORM FOR EACH ARCHER. You can register anytime all
  semester\, as long as there are places left in the class. If there are no 
 spaces left\, it will indicate "FULL" for that class on the website calenda
 r.<br><br>CAPACITY: 10 archers per class<br>AGES: 8 - 80? years old&nbsp\;<
 br>DISTANCES: 9m\, 13.5m\, and 18m<br>BOWS: Recurves<br><br>EQUIPMENT:&nbsp
 \;<br>We provide all equipment necessary indefinitely at no extra charge. (
 Recurve bow\, 3 arrows\, armguard\, finger tab\, target)<br>When you are re
 ady to order your own equipment\, we pace and specify what you need and hel
 p you order it\, so you buy the correct equipment for your strength and exp
 erience. Generally\, we do not recommend anyone buys equipment before they 
 have been with us for at least 8 hours.<br><br>CLASS TIMES and COACHES/INST
 RUCTORS:<br>These are the days/times that are available to you. All classes
  are coached by Coach Racae.<br>MIXED Indoor 2/3/4/5+ classes of JOADs\, Pa
 rents\, and Adults at 9m/13.5m/18m.<br>SAT: 3:45-4:45pm<br>SUN: 3:45-4:45pm
 <br>TUES: 6:00-7:00pm&nbsp\;<br>WED: 6:00-7:00pm&nbsp\;<br><br>FEES:&nbsp\;
 <br>$20/hr for any hour above\, and to secure your place in any class befor
 e or after that hour ON THE SAME DAY<br>+ Enrollment fee: $20 (always due o
 nce per semester)&nbsp\;<br>Additional hour(s) ON THE SAME DAY are open to 
 you at the following reduced fees\, provided there are spaces remaining in 
 the class: $20/hr\; $30 for 2 hrs\; $40 for 3 hrs.&nbsp\;<br><br>ENROLLMENT
  IS ON A FIRST-RECEIVED AND PAID BASIS.<br>This enrollment form must be com
 pleted and your payment received in order for you to be enrolled and a plac
 e reserved for you. You can enroll any time during the semester for as many
  or as few classes as you like as long as there are places open.<br>So\, fo
 r example\, you can enroll for the entire semester\, each month\, or sprink
 le the days throughout the semester depending on your schedule. (Please bea
 r in mind\, however\, you'll progress faster with regular attendance.)<br><
 br>DROP INS:<br>Your name will be on the website calendar under the date an
 d time you registered after we receive your fee in advance of the class. Wh
 en classes are not full\, it's okay to just drop in for the class and pay a
 t that time. When you attend\, and the class is near full\, you should pay 
 at least one class in advance to guarantee you have a place next time. You 
 can see the actual attendance (including drop-ins) by looking at past class
 es on the website calendar. If the class is "FULL"\, it will be so indicate
 d on the calendar.<br><br>ATTENDANCE RECOMMENDATIONS (in order to improve o
 ver time). Recreational archers have no attendance requirements.&nbsp\;<br>
 INDOOR 2 at 9m : 2 hrs/wk<br>INDOOR 3A at 13.5m : 3-4 hrs/wk<br>INDOOR 3B a
 t 18m : 4-5 hrs/wk<br>INDOOR 4 at 18m : 6 hrs/wk<br>INDOOR 5 at 18m: 8 hrs/
 wk<br>INDOOR 6 at 18m: 12 hrs/wk<br><br>HOW DOES IT WORK? HOW DO I ADVANCE?
 <br>Please look under Programs at&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.archerytraining
 center.com">www.archerytrainingcenter.com</a>\, and read the information to
  understand how it all works.<br><br>Scores are also listed below\, if you 
 kept score\, which is not required\, except on Master Challenge weeks. You 
 need 230 pts on 40cm target or 240 pts on 60cm target to graduate out of yo
 ur distance into Indoor 3A 13.5m\, and again at 13.5m to get into Indoor 3B
  at 18m (full distance).<br>PB = Personal Best.&nbsp\;<br><br>Registered ar
 chers:<br>1. Richard F.\, adult 18m - to pay<br>2. Ted A.\, adult 9m - paid
  - DNA<br>3. Erwin H.\, Parent\, 18m - paid<br>4. Lea H.\, JOAD\, 13.5m - p
 aid<br>5. Katie G.\, JOAD 18m - paid<br>6. Quinn S.\, JOAD 9m - paid<br>7.&
 nbsp\;<br>8.&nbsp\;<br>9.<br>10.
