CREATED:20190912T183602Z
DESCRIPTION:15-19 people\n\nGeneral information:\n\nWe'd be very happy to h
 ost a Corporate Team Archery Event for your group on a mutually convenient 
 date. \n\nThese sessions are proving to be very popular\, and we appreciate
  the opportunity! \nBook now so you're ready for our indoor corporate arche
 ry tournaments!\n\nA few of the corporations which schedule events with us 
 are:\nFacebook\, Intel\, Dell\, AMD\, Samsung\, Home Away\, National Instru
 ments\, Texas Mutual Insurance\, Electronic Arts\, ERCOT\, Vectra Networks\
 , Austin Children's Advocacy\, Glatfelder Insurance\, Kerbey Lane\, RackSpa
 ce\, Abilitie\, Black Locus\, Boosterthon\, WP Engine\, Camp Gladiator\, Ma
 rriott International\, Zimmer Biomet\, Austin Gastroenterology\, Yeti\, Ret
 ailMeNot\, Tableau Software\, Wikibuy/Capital One\, Managed by Q and others
 . \n\nWe also would like to thank your company for its vital\, indirect sup
 port of USA Archery's Junior Olympic Archery Development (JOAD) program! Su
 pport like yours grows Olympians! \n\nBelow is a typical agenda for a Corpo
 rate Team Event with us\, and some other general info\, which may make thin
 gs run more smoothly. \n\nCAPACITY: 1-20 participants. 10 places on the sho
 oting line. If you'll have over 10 participants\, even numbers are best\, s
 o we can create teams of two.\n\nDAYS CLOSED: \nMONDAYS and THURSDAYS\nJAN 
 1-5: Happy Holidays!\nAPRIL 21: Happy Easter !\nMAY 12: Happy Mother´s Day!
 \nMAY 26-JUNE 7 - Summer Vacation 1\nJUNE 16 - Happy Father´s Day!\nAUG 11 
 - 24th ANNUAL ARCHERS OF THE YEAR POTLUCK BANQUET 5:30-7:30pm - Mark your c
 alendars NOW!\nAUG 12-23 - Summer Vacation 2\nSEPT 27-30 - OLYMPIC TEAM TRI
 ALS at Texas A&M - Ask Coach Racae for details if you´d like to go!\nNOV 25
 -DEC 2 - Happy Thanksgiving!\nDEC 16-JAN 3 - Happy Holidays\n2020 Spring se
 mester starts on Jan. 4\, 2020!\n\nAGENDA (approx.- depends on number and p
 ace of participants)\n\n1:00 Arrival\; waivers (to be signed by participant
 s over 18 years old or adults/parents/guardians)\n1:15 Selecting two-person
  teams\; equipment review and selection (bows\, arrows\, finger tabs\, arm 
 guards\, targets\, etc.)\n1:55 Safety rules\; whistle system\n2:00 Break\n2
 :10 Form (positions) training (stance\, nocking\, hooking/gripping\, set\, 
 mindset\, set-up\, drawing\, anchor\, loading\, aiming\, expanding\, releas
 e)\n2:45 Ranking Round - shooting in teams\; quantity of arrows will depend
  on number and pace of participants\n3:45 Olympic Round: Based on ranking r
 ound\; each team picks a country to represent\; all teams progress in a mat
 ch play to the Gold\, Silver\, and Bronze medal matches\, with other teams 
 cheering them on!\n4:15 Awards Ceremony and podium presentations\, photos!\
 n\nSCHEDULING:\nWe can schedule a corporate team event on T/W/Th/F during t
 he day for a max. of 20 people\, pending your confirmation. If you would pr
 efer another day or time\, please tell us\, and we'll do our best to accomm
 odate you. Sundays 11:00am-2:00pm are also available\, if booked at least t
 wo weeks in advance.\n\nTIME NEEDED:\nIt's best to allow at least 3 hrs. fo
 r a team of up to 10\, and about 3.5-4 hours for more than 10 participants\
 , since we'll need to form two lines of shooting. We may run over by as muc
 h as 30 minutes\, depending on everyone's arrival and ability. If this will
  be a problem\, please let us know\, so we can pace the event carefully.\n\
 nARRIVALS: We'll all start together\, so please have everyone arrive on tim
 e or together. \n\nPARKING: We have limited parking space for about 8-10 ve
 hicles. Some corporations decide to park at a nearby shopping center parkin
 g lot\, and then "carpool" to the archery range.\n\nFEE: There is a minimum
  fee of $250 for 1-10 people\, and then $25/person for 11-20 people. We can
  accommodate 20 people for $500. If your company requires a separate writte
 n receipt for accounting purposes\, please tell us in advance so we can hav
 e one ready for you.\n\nPAYMENT: When you arrive at the range\, you can pay
  for the session individually or by corporate check payable to Archery Trai
 ning Center\, or by credit card (+4%). All fees must be paid before the ses
 sion begins. \n\nREFUNDS: If you pay in advance of arrival\, a refund will 
 be issued only for cancellations or reductions in attendees in writing when
  given notice not less than 24 hours before the session begins.\n\nEQUIPMEN
 T: We provide all equipment necessary during the Corporate Team Event.\n\nD
 RESS RECOMMENDATIONS: Flat shoes are best\, as we stand a lot and throw our
  weight forward a little\, so balance and weight distribution is important.
  The bowstring can get slowed or entangled in your clothing or hair\, so we
 aring tighter fitting clothes\, no wide skirts\, shirts without buttons on 
 the front pockets and tying your hair back is preferable. Longer brim baseb
 all caps often prevent the string from reaching your face\, so shorter brim
 s are better. In the winter on very cold days\, please dress in layers\, as
  it may be chilly in the indoor range.\n\nWAIVERS: There will be waivers fo
 r each archer to fill out and sign when they first come in\, and before ent
 ering the range. All signees must be at least 18 years old. For those under
  18\, a parent/guardian will need to sign for them. \n\nSPECIAL INSTRUCTION
 S: Please let us know if there are any special concepts you would like us t
 o emphasize\, or any other considerations which you would like us to take i
 nto account.\n\nOLYMPIC TARGET ARCHERY LINKS: \nHere are some links\, which
  you and your group may find interesting before you get to the session.\n\n
 http://www.usarchery.org \nhttp://www.olympic.org/archery \nhttp://www.worl
 darchery.org\nhttp://www.youtube.com/archerytv\n\nThe YouTube videos showin
 g the top American male archer\, Brady Ellison\, competing with the top Kor
 ean archer\, KU Bonchan\, in the Rio Olympics Men's Semi Final Match is the
  best we've seen in 20 years! You have to watch every shot.\n\nTHANK YOU fo
 r your interest in and support of Olympic target archery. We know you'll al
 l really enjoy being part of the Olympic Round at the end of your training!
 !\n\nWe look forward to your time with us.\n\nIf you'd like to discuss your
  reservation in more detail\, please call Coach Racae Meyer 512 975 1850 at
  your convenience.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260404T082343Z
LOCATION:10203 Old Manchaca Rd\, Austin\, TX 78748\, USA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Corporate Team Event - Intel - Dale
TRANSP:OPAQUE
