DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u>REGISTER N
 OW !<br><br>Open to adult\, juniors 8+\, and parents! Please read all the i
 nfo below and in the registration and waivers.<br><br>More information\, re
 gistration forms and waivers are available at&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.arc
 herytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrainingcenter.com</a>.<br><br>Register 
 here using ONE of these forms:<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/
 e/1FAIpQLSfcwG419ZK9XmA4-JlXM-zhjhvSPCF8NCwWJlzFP2w-gRliUw/viewform">2022 W
 inter/Spring Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Juniors + Parents</a>&nbsp\; O
 R<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSe-YxPKAMTxiC7kVt6fZ
 uQJeidXENYq_iV4rWj1RaXdLhPoew/viewform">2022 Winter/Spring Outdoor 1: First
 -time Class for Adults</a><br><br>Sign up for just one Outdoor 1 class\, be
 cause most people graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after the first
  lesson.<br><br><b>Your name will be added below and your place reserved on
  a</b>&nbsp\;<b>first registered and paid basis and after we receive 3 thin
 gs</b>:&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br>2022 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM + WAIVERS + FEE<b
 r><br><b>Registered archers&nbsp\;</b>at 9m on 40-cm target face:<br><b>Tar
 get nos:</b><br>1.&nbsp\;<u></u><br><u></u>2.<br>3.<br>4.<br>5.&nbsp\;<br>6
 .<br>7.<br>8.&nbsp\;<br>9.&nbsp\;<br>10.&nbsp\;<br><u></u><br><u></u><b>Jua
 n R</b>.\, dad - pd - canceled - refund or substitution<br><u></u><b>Ela R<
 /b>.\, 9\, on 60-cm target face - pd - canceled - refund or substitution<br
 ><br>Space will be limited to 10-15 archers per session depending on the nu
 mber of family groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC Guidelines.&n
 bsp\;<br>Each person will have a target stand\, except after 10 people have
  registered\, two members from the same family will share one target stand.
 <br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field 
 until further notice or approved by Coach Racae.&nbsp\;<br>Parents of junio
 rs 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator. Parents of juniors
  8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their child for grea
 ter safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into 
 each Outdoor 1: First-time Class.&nbsp\;<br><br>We will accept a limited&nb
 sp\;number of kids under 12 into the program each semester\, depending on t
 he total&nbsp\; number of archers in all the classes. If you join before th
 e limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program a
 nd take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;I
 f you are under 12\, registered and paid after the cut off\, your fee will 
 be returned to you.&nbsp\;<br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or
  three times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You
 ´ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.&nb
 sp\;<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><b
 r>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will
  be needed for Outdoor 2. ($15)<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string l
 oop)\, optional but really needed to practice form\, warm up before classes
  ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be poste
 d. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recogniz
 e your final score\, because it will have been averaged by taking your reco
 rded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot 
 to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full rou
 nd score. After the last class on the weekend\, final scores will also be s
 ent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more information before 
 your next class.<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
