DESCRIPTION:Registration form: OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m\n\n\nREMINDER:  Eve
 ryone needs to come to at least one Training Class per week to be able to a
 ttend Open Practice. (All indoor classes are training classes.)\n\nIf you a
 re not a coach/instructor\, the fees are:  \n\nOutdoor Training Class (OTC)
 : $52/class or multi-class pack \n\nIndoor Training Class (ITC): $43/class 
 or multi-class pack or unlimited pack\n\nOpen Practice (OP): ($50/mo)  \n\n
 \nIf you are a coach/instructor\, you have received an email from Coach Rac
 ae outlining your fees.\n\nDuring the summer (May 31-Aug 31)\, at least 5 a
 rchers need to register by \n8:00 am on Thursdays (for Saturdays) and \n8:0
 0 am on Fridays (for Sundays) \nfor Coach Racae to coach the Outdoor 3-9 Tr
 aining Class. In the case of low or late registrations or cancellations\, a
 nother coach/instructor\, when available\, will coach the session as a Trai
 ning Class or oversee it as an Open Practice instead. If this is not possib
 le\, then the class may need to be cancelled.\n\nAdd your name to the Targe
 t Assignment List below or submit the above completed form.\nFocus primaril
 y on perfecting your form\, \nslowly increasing your physical strength and 
 draw weight\, \nstrengthening your mental program\, \ndetermining your aver
 age and personal best\, \nunderstanding the spread between the two\, and wo
 rking on closing it.\n\nYou need your own equipment \nCompetition recurve b
 ow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-ba
 r assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger slin
 g\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may no
 t be added until you reach a higher level\, but you should order them in ad
 vance.) \n\nWear your ATCI shirt to training.\n\nWhen you score 288 pts in 
 a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the next dis
 tance until you reach your competition distance\nIf you trained outdoors in
  the 2024 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.\n\nTarg
 et arrangements may vary each session\, depending on who attends and distan
 ces needed.\nTarget 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should al
 ways stay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent practice in between cla
 sses.\nTarget 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition distance) \nTarget 3 at 5
 0m\nTarget 4+5 at 40m (U15 competition distance) \nTarget 6+7+8 at 30m (U13
  competition distance) \nTargets 9 at 20m (for those who have shot at 18m i
 ndoors or with Coach Racae's approval)\nTarget 10 at 13.5m (for those who h
 ave just graduated from indoors at 9m)\n\nIdeally\, we want to practice wit
 h two archers/target to replicate competition conditions as much as possibl
 e.\n\nTarget Assignments:\nTargets are assigned outdoors in advance to redu
 ce confusion and delay on the day\,\nso add your name next to your distance
  below. \nIf you need help or have questions\, email/text Coach Racae\n(Dot
 ted lines represent tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)\n----------
 ------------------------\n1A. (70m)\n1B\n\n2A. (60m)  Joel Y\, adult\, USAA
 \,pd\n2B\n\n3A. (50m)  Abby Y\, 13\, USAA\, pd\n---------------------------
 -------\n3B\n\n4A. (40m) Hannah\, USAA\, pd\n4B. \n------------------------
 ----------\n5A. (40m) Colby K!!! Adult!!! USAA!!! Paid?\n5B. \n\n6A. (30m) 
 Ellie Y\, 10\, USAA\, pd\n----------------------------------\n6B. \n\n7A. (
 30m)\n7B. \n---------------------------------- \n8A. (30m). Emma A.\, 13\, 
 USAA\, pd\n8B. \n\n9A. (20m) Chi C.\, adult\, USAA\, pd\n------------------
 ----------------\n9B. \n\n10A. (13.5m) Logan C.\, 8\, USAA\, pd\n10B
