UID:20c179ngcuqimktf7ntmfagc90@google.com
CREATED:20180823T181700Z
DESCRIPTION:When you order arrows they are delivered in pieces: shafts\, fe
 athers\, nocks and points.\nWe teach you how to measure your draw length an
 d cut your arrows\, point\, and fletch them.\n\nYou can schedule an Arrow F
 letching Class with Coach Racae outside of regular class hours\, or you can
  just show up at one of the scheduled classes\, if that's more convenient. 
 Bring your arrows\, points\, feathers\, and nocks.\n\nArchery Training Cent
 er expects you to cut\, point\, and fletch your own arrows after you purcha
 se them - as all competitive archers do. It's part of your training.\n\nIf 
 it is a struggle for you\, we will fletch them for you for $3 each (but you
  should do it yourself to gain experience for when you'll need to do it dur
 ing tournaments).\n\nIf you are 16 years old or older\, you can use the blo
 w torch and table saw\, otherwise one of your parents will need to attend t
 he Arrow Fletching Class with you\, and cut and point your arrows for you u
 ntil you are old enough to use the equipment. \n\nYou must turn off the blo
 w torch and return it to the storage room when you're finished. You also ne
 ed to make sure the table saw is disconnected after you're finished. These 
 are safety precautions! Please also clean up the equipment area.\n\nFee: $1
 5/archer - one-time fee. \n\nTime Needed:\nThe instruction part of the clas
 s will take about 30 min.\, but you will need about 1 hour to 1.5 hours to 
 actually finish fletching/pointing/nocking 6-12 arrows. (Arrows require abo
 ut 30 minutes to dry before shooting them.) Please allow enough time in the
  range. \n\nAfter you complete the arrows and they are drying in the fletch
 ing jigs\, you can leave the range instead of waiting for them to dry\, pro
 vided that you have labeled each of your arrows with tape\, showing your na
 me and the time you put them in the jig\, so others can take them out\, if 
 necessary\, to use the jig later.\n\nIf you have questions\, just ask Coach
  Racae.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260404T082343Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Arrow Fletching Class with Coach Racae: Lauren M.
TRANSP:OPAQUE
