CREATED:20250501T180249Z
DESCRIPTION:Registration form: OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m<br><br>During the s
 ummer (May 31-Aug 31)\, at least <b>5 archers need to register by 8:00 am o
 n Thursdays </b>(for Saturdays) and <b>8:00 am on Fridays </b>(for Sundays)
  <b>for Coach Racae to coach the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class</b> . In the ca
 se of low or late registrations or cancellations\, another coach/instructor
 \, when available\, will coach the session as a Training Class or oversee i
 t as an Open Practice instead. If this is not possible\, then the class may
  need to be cancelled.<br><br>Add your name to the Target Assignment List b
 elow or submit the above completed form.<br>Focus primarily on perfecting y
 our form\, <br>slowly increasing your physical strength and draw weight\, <
 br>strengthening your mental program\, <br>determining your average and per
 sonal best\, <br>understanding the spread between the two\, and working on 
 closing it.<br><br>You need your own equipment <br>Competition recurve bow\
 , sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar a
 ssembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\,
  hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not b
 e added until you reach a higher level\, but you should order them in advan
 ce.) <br><br>Wear your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br>When you score 288 pt
 s in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the nex
 t distance until you reach your competition distance<br>If you trained outd
 oors in the 2024 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.<
 br><br>Target arrangements may vary each session\, depending on who attends
  and distances needed.<br>Target 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distan
 ce) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent practice i
 n between classes.<br>Target 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition distance) 
 <br>Target 3 at 50m<br>Target 4+5 at 40m (U15 competition distance) <br>Tar
 get 6+7+8 at 30m (U13 competition distance) <br>Targets 9 at 20m (for those
  who have shot at 18m indoors or with Coach Racae's approval)<br>Target 10 
 at 13.5m (for those who have just graduated from indoors at 9m)<br><br>Idea
 lly\, we want to practice with two archers/target to replicate competition 
 conditions as much as possible.<br><br>Target Assignments:<br>Targets are a
 ssigned outdoors in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\,<br>s
 o add your name next to your distance below. <br>If you need help or have q
 uestions\, email/text Coach Racae<br>(Dotted lines represent tent poles div
 iding Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)<br>----------------------------------<br>1A. 
 (70m)<br>1B<br><br>2A. (60m)  <br>2B<br><br>3A. (50m)  <br>----------------
 ------------------<br>3B<br><br>4A. (40m) Erika OG\, adult\, pd<br>4B. Javi
 er G\, adult\, pd<br>----------------------------------<br>5A. (40m)<br>5B.
  <br><br>6A. (30m)<br>----------------------------------<br>6B. <br><br>7A.
  (30m)<br>7B. <br>---------------------------------- <br>8A. (30m)<br>8B. <
 br><br>9A. (20m)<br>----------------------------------<br>9B. <br><br>10A. 
 (13.5m)<br>10B
