CREATED:20260412T204358Z
DESCRIPTION:What we worked on today:<br><br><ol><li><b>Bow arm</b><ul><li><
 span>Focused on keeping upper arm up and horizontal during RELEASE / FOLLOW
 -THRU - worked like a charm! Bow arm didn't drop anywhere near as much beca
 use triceps were being used more. Keep working on it to build up more stren
 gth.</span></li><li>Keeping bow elbow as a point in space not as successful
 \, so focus should be on upper arm/triceps</li></ul></li><li><b>Draw elbow<
 /b><ul><li>Raise draw arm almost horizontally<ul><li>Draw elbow should not 
 raise first ahead of forearm or lead the way or tighten up\; it's just part
  of the sides of a platform hinged to the shoulder\, so upper arm\, forearm
 \, and hand all stay together</li><li>Initially\, drop your draw arm alongs
 ide your body\, relax\, then flip your forearm and hand up to in front of y
 our body\, and hook your fingers on the string. That's about the beginning 
 position for the draw arm at SET. Remember the pencil test.</li></ul></li><
 /ul></li><li><b>Draw shoulder</b><ul><li>Set in place before raising bow</l
 i><li>Reduce tension in draw shoulder\; relaxed\, moved up\, down\, and bac
 k into position</li></ul></li><li><b>Make sure to keep the Arrow Line</b> t
 hroughout the above</li></ol><span>BIG IMPROVEMENT in bow arm staying up\, 
 scooping and pushing towards the target. YAY!!</span>\n\nJoin with Google M
 eet: https://meet.google.com/gti-bmxk-xmb\n\nLearn more about Meet at: http
 s://support.google.com/a/users/answer/9282720
LAST-MODIFIED:20260429T004427Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Virtual Private with Coach Racae - Abby
TRANSP:OPAQUE
