UID:2vbufsk2ngg01ig8sv5ii88g4r@google.com
CREATED:20220102T015537Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><br><br><b>Tournaments are held at the end of
  each calendar month at 1:30-3:30pm on Saturdays and Sundays</b>\, weather 
 permitting.&nbsp\;If you are new to our program\, come and try it\, so you 
 will be more comfortable and better prepared next month!<br><br>The only di
 fferences between the regular training sessions and the tournaments are tha
 t we are more closely reproducing tournament conditions\, which include:<br
 ><ul><li>No coaching while you are on the shooting line (but\, as in a real
  tournament\, you can always ask the coach for help in between the ends.) T
 his is your chance to find out how well you can do the form on your own.</l
 i><li>You will shoot more arrows :&nbsp\; Practice arrows + Two rounds -&nb
 sp\;60 arrows at 9m and 13.5m or 72 arrows at 20m-70m</li><li>You will scor
 e every arrow for two rounds.&nbsp\;</li><li>The ends will be timed. You´ll
  have 4 min to shoot 6 arrows.</li><li>Everyone will be shooting at close-t
 o-regular tournament spacing so there will be two archers on each target ab
 out 3 ft apart.</li><li>There will be a maximum of 20 archers on the shooti
 ng line at the same time. Awesome! (Lots of arrow flying towards the target
 s!)</li></ul><br><b>Outside of the tournament weeks</b>\, each week the foc
 us of your lessons will be on particular Steps of Shooting of the NTS (Nati
 onal Training System) shot cycle\, to help you focus and improve your form\
 , which\, as we all know\, leads to greater precision (tighter groups of ar
 rows) and ultimately greater accuracy (tight groups of arrows dead center).
 <br><b><br></b><br><b>FEBRUARY</b><br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>12-1
 8</b>&nbsp\;Welcome Back: Understanding&nbsp\; NTS Concepts&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<b
 r><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>19-25</b>&nbsp\;NTS Steps 1+2: STANCE + 
 NOCK&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>26 - MAR 4: MASTER C
 HALLENGE TOURNAMENT WEEK (Pin Shoot)</b><br><b>MARCH</b><br><b>&nbsp\; &nbs
 p\; &nbsp\;5-11</b>&nbsp\;NTS Step 3: HOOK &amp\; GRIP&nbsp\; &nbsp\;<u></u
 ><br><u></u>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;<b>12-18&nbsp\;</b>NTS Step 4: SET<u></u
 ><br><u></u><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;19-25</b>&nbsp\;<u></u>NTS Step 5: SE
 T-UP&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br><u></u><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>26 - APR 1: M
 ASTER CHALLENGE TOURNAMENT WEEK (Pin Shoot)</b><br><b>APRIL</b><br><b>&nbsp
 \; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;2-8</b>&nbsp\;<u></u>NTS Step 6 DRAW to LOAD&nbsp\; &nbsp
 \; &nbsp\;<br><u></u><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;9-15&nbsp\;</b><u></u>NTS St
 ep 7 ANCHOR&nbsp\; &nbsp\;<br><u></u><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;16-22&nbsp\;
 </b><u></u>NTS Step 8 TRANSFER to HOLD<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;<b>23-29&n
 bsp\;</b>NTS Step 9 EXPAND / AIM<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;30 - MAY 6: M
 ASTER CHALLENGE TOURNAMENT WEEK (Pin Shoot)</b><br><u></u><b>MAY</b><br><b>
 &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>7-13&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</b>NTS Step 10 RELEASE and
  FOLLOW-THROUGH<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>14-20</b>&nbsp\;<u></u>
 NTS Step 11 Feedback and Putting it all together!<br><u></u><b>&nbsp\; &nbs
 p\; &nbsp\;</b><b>21/22 : END OF SEMESTER TOURNAMENT WEEKEND (Pin Shoot)</b
 ><br><br>Your goal is always to replicate the NTS step(s) mindfully and con
 sistently on every shot.<br><br>You do not need to score every class. In fa
 ct\, it would be more beneficial to you if you scored only during Master Ch
 allenge Tournament Weeks\, which happen the last week of each month. This i
 s because working on the NTS Steps of Shooting (your form) is more easily d
 one without the distraction of the target face or scoring\, and you will im
 prove faster.<br><br>As you reach higher levels\, you will learn the NTS St
 eps in progressively greater detail.<br>The NTS Steps are cumulative with e
 ach step most successfully completed if the previous steps have been comple
 ted mindfully.&nbsp\;<br><br>Your ability to learn and understand the NTS S
 teps\, and use deep focus on these Steps while shooting outdoors and while 
 using your stretchband/string loop at home will propel you to higher levels
  fast!<br><br><b>Goals by the end of the semester (May 22):&nbsp\;</b><br>S
 ee Coach Racae´s email ¨2022 New Year´s Goals¨<u></u></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260404T082324Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:ATCI OUTDOOR 2-9 MASTER CHALLENGE TOURNAMENT WEEK (Pin Shoot)
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
