DESCRIPTION:REMINDER:  Everyone needs to come to at least one Training Clas
 s per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (All indoor classes are trai
 ning classes.)<br><br>If you are not a coach/instructor\, the fees are:  <b
 r>Outdoor Training Class (OTC): $52/class or multi-class pack <br>Indoor Tr
 aining Class (ITC): $43/class or multi-class pack or unlimited pack<br>Open
  Practice (OP): ($50/mo)  <br>If you are a coach/instructor\, you have rece
 ived an email from Coach Racae outlining your fees.<br><br>During the summe
 r (May 31-Aug 31)\, at least 5 archers need to register by <br>8:00 am on T
 hursdays (for Saturdays) and <br>8:00 am on Fridays (for Sundays) <br>for C
 oach Racae to coach the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class. In the case of low or l
 ate registrations or cancellations\, another coach/instructor\, when availa
 ble\, will coach the session as a Training Class or oversee it as an Open P
 ractice instead. If this is not possible\, then the class may need to be ca
 ncelled.<br><br>Add your name to the Target Assignment List below or submit
  the above completed form.<br>Focus primarily on perfecting your form\, <br
 >slowly increasing your physical strength and draw weight\, <br>strengtheni
 ng your mental program\, <br>determining your average and personal best\, <
 br>understanding the spread between the two\, and working on closing it.<br
 ><br>You need your own equipment <br>Competition recurve bow\, sight\, stab
 ilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clic
 ker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field 
 quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added until 
 you reach a higher level\, but you should order them in advance.) <br><br>W
 ear your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arro
 w round on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the next distance unt
 il you reach your competition distance<br>If you trained outdoors in the 20
 24 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.<br><br>Target 
 arrangements may vary each session\, depending on who attends and distances
  needed.<br>Target 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should alw
 ays stay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent practice in between clas
 ses.<br>Target 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition distance) <br>Target 3 a
 t 50m<br>Target 4+5 at 40m (U15 competition distance) <br>Target 6+7+8 at 3
 0m (U13 competition distance) <br>Targets 9 at 20m (for those who have shot
  at 18m indoors or with Coach Racae's approval)<br>Target 10 at 13.5m (for 
 those who have just graduated from indoors at 9m)<br><br>Ideally\, we want 
 to practice with two archers/target to replicate competition conditions as 
 much as possible.<br><br>Target Assignments:<br>Targets are assigned outdoo
 rs in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\,<br>so add your nam
 e next to your distance below. <br>If you need help or have questions\, ema
 il/text Coach Racae<br>(Dotted lines represent tent poles dividing Targets 
 3\, 6\, and 9.)<br>----------------------------------<br>1A. (70m)<br>1B<br
 ><br>2A. (60m)  <b>Nick E</b>\, adult\, pd<br>2B<br><br>3A. (50m) <b> Josep
 h F</b>.\, 14\, USAA\, pd<br>----------------------------------<br>3B<br><b
 r>4A. (40m) <b>Colby K</b>.! Adult!  USAA!  Paid!<br>4B. <b>Sophia D</b>\, 
 adults\, USAA\, f<br>----------------------------------<br>5A. (40m) <b>Fin
 n E\,</b> 13\, pd<br>5B. (40m) <b>Adrianne M</b>. adult\, USAA\, pd<br><br>
 6A. (40m) <b>Anna P</b>\, adult\, pd<br>----------------------------------<
 br>6B. <b>Hannah T</b>\, adult\, USAA\, Paid <br><br>7A. (30m)<br>7B. <b>So
 fia W\, </b>13\, pd?<br>---------------------------------- <br>8A. (30m)<br
 >8B. <br><br>9A. (20m) <b>Rhys E</b>\, 10\, pd<br>-------------------------
