DESCRIPTION:Open to members of Archery Training Center\, Inc.<br>There is n
 o minimum age limit\, as long as participant can understand the instruction
 s.<br><br>The CPR class will be given by <a href="https://cprcertificationl
 lc.com/" target="_blank">https://cprcertificationllc.com/</a> and includes 
 a training session with a BLS American Heart accredited instructor. It will
  cover Adult\, Child\, and Infant CPR as well as AED and choking training. 
 Your training will include the hands-on training\, discussion portion\, and
  exam required to get you certified in CPR and AED. Everything will be comp
 leted all in one (2-3) hour class on the same day. <br><br>The First Aid cl
 ass will cover basic wound care\, 1st 2nd &amp\; 3rd degree burn care\, spl
 inting techniques\, and more. They will send us a 1 hour video to be watche
 d before or even after the class. Once done\, they will send you the card. 
 <br><br>Minimum number of participants: 6 <br>(The more register\, the less
  expensive for each person.)<br><br>People    BLS\, CPR\, AED &amp\; First 
 Aid<br>1-6                 $499.95/group<br>7-9                 $79.95/pers
 on<br>10-14             $69.95/person<br>15-19             $ 64.95/person<b
 r><br>To register\, just add your name below\, if you have access\, or emai
 l Coach Racae at <a href="mailto:archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com" tar
 get="_blank">archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a>  .<br><ul><li><p>Coa
 ch Racae will send your email address to the <a href="https://cprcertificat
 ionllc.com/" target="_blank">https://cprcertificationllc.com/</a> in advanc
 e of the class</p></li><li><p><span>The <b>final fee may vary</b>\, as it w
 ill be based on the number of participants on the day\, however\, <b>please
  submit your fee </b><b>to Archery Training Center by May 23 </b></span><b>
 of $64.95/person</b><span> </span><span>by </span><b>Zelle preferred </b><s
 pan>so there is no merchant fee charge - or </span><b>$66.90 if you pay by 
 Venmo or Paypal</b><span>) </span></p></li><li><p><span>Per the American He
 art Association guidelines\, </span><b>each participant must purchase the 2
 020 manual.</b><span> You can get it </span><a href="https://6b689724.strea
 klinks.com/Cajc1JZ-fhd_JbDrmAT8_qg6/https%3A%2F%2Fshopcpr.heart.org%2Fbls-p
 rovider-manual-ebook" target="_blank">here</a><span>. If the link doesn’t w
 ork\, feel free to call 1-888-277-5463 or</span><a href="mailto:shopcpr@ema
 il.shopcpr.heart.org" target="_blank"> emai</a><span>l for assistance.</spa
 n></p></li><li>Please click <a href="https://6b689724.streaklinks.com/Cajc8
 Qwv78B_5zjnyAE8IE_w/https%3A%2F%2Fforms.gle%2FKskhGe3p64qYCFTD9" target="_b
 lank">here</a> to watch the <b>First Aid videos</b> and <b>take the exam</b
 >. We will automatically send your First Aid cards after you complete the t
 raining.</li></ul><ul><li><span>The CPR class will be in-person and require
  hands on\, so the CPR cards will be sent after your training onsite.</span
 ></li></ul><br><b>Participants: (Whoa!)</b><br>    1. Sophia D. - pd<br>   
