DTSTART:20260429T010000Z
DTEND:20260429T013000Z
DTSTAMP:20261004T164458Z
UID:0rg02n3ei3h2n5f7qni7qr8pf0@google.com
X-GOOGLE-CONFERENCE:https://meet.google.com/ngy-cdzx-uoc
CREATED:20260419T193626Z
DESCRIPTION:<b>What we worked on today :</b><br><b><br></b><br><b>SET UP</b
 ><br><ul><li>Bottom of SET UP before DRAW is still a bit too far back\, res
 ulting in\, from the top of SET UP\, a steep diagonal down to almost to LOA
 D position.</li><li>Preferable: Set the height at the bottom of SET UP (mai
 n emphasis is on shoulder alignment with bow arm)\, hand at about shoulder 
 height before DRAW. </li><li>You should be able to see the tips of your dra
 w fingers in your peripheral vision at the bottom of SET UP\, before DRAW t
 o LOAD\, otherwise you're too far back.</li><li>Draw elbow - a bit high at 
 the beginning\, but came down to almost arrow height by end of session\, so
  alignment improved. Back tension is often less with higher elbow.</li><li>
 Bow arm - Over rotation inwards results in overbending\, so seek to have a 
 vertical inner elbow\, so arm is straighter and therefore bones in alignmen
 t</li></ul><br><b>DRAW to LOAD</b><br><ul><li>Bow tilts backwards at DRAW a
 nd then straightens out at LOAD. Should be more vertical throughout.</li><l
 i>Control head</li></ul><br><b>Alignments</b><br><ul><li>Looking better and
  better. Shoulders level\, "T" horizontal\, not angled down at full draw (b
 ow arm\, shoulders\, to draw elbow)</li></ul><br><b>Rhythm - LAT (LOAD\, AN
 CHOR\, TRANSFER)</b><br><ul><li>Learning how to count (1-2-3) to create a c
 onsistent rhythm<ul><li>LOAD - ooonnnneeee (string on chin)</li><li>ANCHOR 
 - two (in as deep as possible and up as high as possible)</li><li>TRANSFER 
 - ttthhrrreeee (remaining tension moves into back)</li></ul></li><li>Make s
 ure that each position is performed and there is a continuous flow</li><li>
 If form goes off because of counting\, go back to practicing form\, and the
 n return to rhythm practice - back and forth</li></ul><br><b>Homework : </b
 ><br><ul><li><b>Read Chapters 11\, 12\, and 13 in <u>Inside the Archer</u><
 /b></li><li>30-60 arrow x 3-4 days/wk working on Rhythm</li></ul>\n\nJoin w
 ith Google Meet: https://meet.google.com/ngy-cdzx-uoc\n\nLearn more about M
 eet at: https://support.google.com/a/users/answer/9282720
LAST-MODIFIED:20260429T015555Z
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Virtual Private Lesson with Coach Racae - Abby
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
