DESCRIPTION:REMINDER:  Everyone needs to come to at least one Training Clas
 s per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (All indoor classes are trai
 ning classes.)\n\nIf you are not a coach/instructor\, the fees are:  \nOutd
 oor Training Class (OTC): $52/class or multi-class pack \nIndoor Training C
 lass (ITC): $43/class or multi-class pack or unlimited pack\nOpen Practice 
 (OP): ($50/mo)  \nIf you are a coach/instructor\, you have received an emai
 l from Coach Racae outlining your fees.\n\nCoach Racae will coach the Outdo
 or 3-9 Training Classes on Saturdays and Sundays\, when at least 5 archers 
 register by \n8:00 am on Thursdays (for Saturdays) and \n8:00 am on Fridays
  (for Sundays) \nIn the case of low or late registrations or cancellations\
 , another coach/instructor\, when available\, will coach the session as a T
 raining Class or oversee it as an Open Practice instead. If this is not pos
 sible\, then the class may need to be cancelled.\nAdd your name to the Targ
 et Assignment List below.\nFocus primarily on perfecting your form\, \nslow
 ly increasing your physical strength and draw weight\, \nstrengthening your
  mental program\, \ndetermining your average and personal best\, \nundersta
 nding the spread between the two\, and working on closing it.\n\nYou need y
 our own equipment \nCompetition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\
 , rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest prote
 ctor\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow pu
 ller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added until you reach a highe
 r level\, but you should order them in advance.) \n\nWear your ATCI shirt t
 o training.\n\nWhen you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm tar
 get face you'll move back to the next distance until you reach your competi
 tion distance\nIf you trained outdoors in the 2024 season\, you'll return t
 o the farthest distance you shot.\n\nTarget arrangements may vary each sess
 ion\, depending on who attends and distances needed.\nTarget 1 at 70m (U21 
 + Seniors competition distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use i
 t for independent practice in between classes.\nTarget 2 at 60m (U18 + Mast
 ers competition distance) \nTarget 3 at 50m\nTarget 4+5 at 40m (U15 competi
 tion distance) \nTarget 6+7+8 at 30m (U13 competition distance) \nTargets 9
  at 20m (for those who have shot at 18m indoors or with Coach Racae's appro
 val)\nTarget 10 at 13.5m (for those who have just graduated from indoors at
  9m)\n\nIdeally\, we want to practice with two archers/target to replicate 
 competition conditions as much as possible.\n\nTarget Assignments:\nTargets
  are assigned outdoors in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\
 ,\nso add your name next to your distance below. \nIf you need help or have
  questions\, email/text Coach Racae\n(Dotted lines represent tent poles div
 iding Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)\n----------------------------------\n1A. (70m
 )\n1B\n\n2A. (60m)  Nick E ad\n2B\n\n3A. (50m)  \n-------------------------
 ---------\n3B\n\n4A. (40m) Luke T\, 16\n4B.  Finn E 13\n-------------------
 ---------------\n5A. (40m)\n5B. \n\n6A. (30m)\n----------------------------
 ------\n6B. \n\n7A. (30m)\n7B. \n---------------------------------- \n8A. (
 30m)\n8B. \n\n9A. (20m) Rhys E\, 11\n----------------------------------\n9B
 . (18m) Miles G\, 13\, pd\n\n10A. (13.5m)\n10B
LAST-MODIFIED:20260512T052633Z
LOCATION:2324 Bliss Spillar Rd\, Manchaca\, TX 78652\, USA
