DESCRIPTION:Let's go indoors to be safe and dry. (If anyone was going to th
 e outdoor competitions\, I'd probably say risk it\, but since no one's goin
 g\, let's just go inside.)<br><br>REMINDER:  Everyone needs to come to at l
 east one Training Class per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (All i
 ndoor classes are training classes.)<br><br>If you are not a coach/instruct
 or\, the fees are:  <br>Outdoor Training Class (OTC): $52/class or multi-cl
 ass pack <br>Indoor Training Class (ITC): $43/class or multi-class pack or 
 unlimited pack<br>Open Practice (OP): ($50/mo)  <br>If you are a coach/inst
 ructor\, you have received an email from Coach Racae outlining your fees.<b
 r><br>During the summer (May 31-Aug 31)\, at least 5 archers need to regist
 er for Coach Racae to coach the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class. They need to do
  it by <br>8:00 am on Thursdays (for Saturdays) and <br>8:00 am on Fridays 
 (for Sundays) <br>In the case of lower or late registrations or cancellatio
 ns\, another coach/instructor\, when available\, will coach the session as 
 a Training Class or oversee it as an Open Practice instead. If this is not 
 possible\, then the class may need to be cancelled.<br><br>Add your name to
  the Target Assignment List below.<br>Focus primarily on perfecting your fo
 rm\, <br>slowly increasing your physical strength and draw weight\, <br>str
 engthening your mental program\, <br>determining your average and personal 
 best\, <br>understanding the spread between the two\, and working on closin
 g it.<br><br>You need your own equipment <br>Competition recurve bow\, sigh
 t\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembl
 y\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip o
 r field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be adde
 d until you reach a higher level\, but you should order them in advance.) <
 br><br>Wear your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br>When you score 288 pts in a
  36-arrow round on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the next dist
 ance until you reach your competition distance<br>If you trained outdoors i
 n the 2024 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.<br><br
 >Target arrangements may vary each session\, depending on who attends and d
 istances needed.<br>Target 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) sh
 ould always stay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent practice in betw
 een classes.<br>Target 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition distance) <br>Ta
 rget 3 at 50m<br>Target 4+5 at 40m (U15 competition distance) <br>Target 6+
 7+8 at 30m (U13 competition distance) <br>Targets 9 at 20m (for those who h
 ave shot at 18m indoors or with Coach Racae's approval)<br>Target 10 at 13.
 5m (for those who have just graduated from indoors at 9m)<br><br>Ideally\, 
 we want to practice with two archers/target to replicate competition condit
 ions as much as possible.<br><br>Target Assignments:<br>Targets are assigne
 d outdoors in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\,<br>so add 
 your name next to your distance below. <br>If you need help or have questio
 ns\, email/text Coach Racae<br>(Dotted lines represent tent poles dividing 
 Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)<br>----------------------------------<br>1A. (70m)<
 br>1B<br><br>2A. (60m)  <b>Nick E</b>\, adult\, pd - 2 hrs<br>2B<br><br>3A.
  (50m)  <b>Joseph F</b>.\,14\, USAA\, pd - 2 hrs<br>-----------------------
 -----------<br>3B<br><br>4A. (40m) <br>4B. <br>----------------------------
 ------<br>5A. (40m)<br>5B. <b>Colby K.</b>\, adult\, pd  USAA - 2 hrs<br><b
 r>6A. (40m) <b>Anna P</b>\, adult\, USAA\, pd - 2 hrs<br>------------------
 ----------------<br>6B.  <b>Finn E</b>\, 13\, pd - 2hrs<br><br>7A. (40m) <b
 >Adrianne M.</b> adult\, USAA\, pd - 2 hrs<br>7B. <br>---------------------
 ------------- <br>8A. (30m)<br>8B. <br><br>9A. (20m) <b>Rhys E\,</b> 10\, p
 d - 2 hrs<br>----------------------------------<br>9B. <b>Lexi E.</b> 16\, 
 pd - 2 hrs<br><br>10A. (13.5m) <b>Anush</b>\,  13\, pd - 2 hrs<br>10B
