DESCRIPTION:REMINDER:  Everyone needs to come to at least one Training Clas
 s per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (All indoor classes are trai
 ning classes.)\n\nIf you are not a coach/instructor\, the fees are:  \nOutd
 oor Training Class (OTC): $52/class or multi-class pack \nIndoor Training C
 lass (ITC): $43/class or multi-class pack or unlimited pack\nOpen Practice 
 (OP): ($50/mo)  \nIf you are a coach/instructor\, you have received an emai
 l from Coach Racae outlining your fees.\n\nDuring the summer (May 31-Aug 31
 )\, at least 5 archers need to register by \n8:00 am on Thursdays (for Satu
 rdays) and \n8:00 am on Fridays (for Sundays) \nfor Coach Racae to coach th
 e Outdoor 3-9 Training Class. In the case of low or late registrations or c
 ancellations\, another coach/instructor\, when available\, will coach the s
 ession as a Training Class or oversee it as an Open Practice instead. If th
 is is not possible\, then the class may need to be cancelled.\n\nAdd your n
 ame to the Target Assignment List below or submit the above completed form.
 \nFocus primarily on perfecting your form\, \nslowly increasing your physic
 al strength and draw weight\, \nstrengthening your mental program\, \ndeter
 mining your average and personal best\, \nunderstanding the spread between 
 the two\, and working on closing it.\n\nYou need your own equipment \nCompe
 tition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows
 \, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingert
 ab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and 
 side rods may not be added until you reach a higher level\, but you should 
 order them in advance.) \n\nWear your ATCI shirt to training.\n\nWhen you s
 core 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm target face you'll move back
  to the next distance until you reach your competition distance\nIf you tra
 ined outdoors in the 2024 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance y
 ou shot.\n\nTarget arrangements may vary each session\, depending on who at
 tends and distances needed.\nTarget 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition dis
 tance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent practic
 e in between classes.\nTarget 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition distance)
  \nTarget 3 at 50m\nTarget 4+5 at 40m (U15 competition distance) \nTarget 6
 +7+8 at 30m (U13 competition distance) \nTargets 9 at 20m (for those who ha
 ve shot at 18m indoors or with Coach Racae's approval)\nTarget 10 at 13.5m 
 (for those who have just graduated from indoors at 9m)\n\nIdeally\, we want
  to practice with two archers/target to replicate competition conditions as
  much as possible.\n\nTarget Assignments:\nTargets are assigned outdoors in
  advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\,\nso add your name next 
 to your distance below. \nIf you need help or have questions\, email/text C
 oach Racae\n(Dotted lines represent tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and
  9.)\n----------------------------------\n1A. (70m)\n1B\n\n2A. (60m)  Ted H
 .\, adult\, DNA\n2B\n\n3A. (50m)  \n----------------------------------\n3B\
 n\n4A. (40m) Luke T\, 16\, pd\n4B. Anna P\, adult\, pd\n-------------------
 ---------------\n5A. (40m) Sophia D\, adult\, f\n5B. \n\n6A. (30m) Sofia W.
 \, 13\n----------------------------------\n6B. \n\n7A. (30m)\n7B. \n-------
 --------------------------- \n8A. (30m)\n8B. \n\n9A. (20m) Lexi E. 16\, pd\
 n----------------------------------\n9B. \n\n10A. (13.5m) Emma A.\, 13\, to
  pay\n10B
