DESCRIPTION:REMINDER:  Everyone needs to come to at least one Training Clas
 s per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (All indoor classes are trai
 ning classes.)\n\nIf you are not a coach/instructor\, the fees are:  \n    
 •Outdoor Training Class (OTC): $52/class or multi-class pack \n    •Indoor 
 Training Class (ITC): $43/class or multi-class pack or unlimited pack\n    
 •Open Practice (OP): ($50/mo)  \n\nIf you are a coach/instructor\, you have
  received an email from Coach Racae outlining your fees.\n\nDuring the summ
 er (May 31-Aug 31)\, at least 5 archers need to register by \n8:00 am on Th
 ursdays (for Saturdays) and \n8:00 am on Fridays (for Sundays) \nfor Coach 
 Racae to coach the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class. \nIn the case of low or late
  registrations or cancellations\, another coach/instructor\, when available
 \, will coach the session as a Training Class or oversee it as an Open Prac
 tice instead. If this is not possible\, then the class may need to be cance
 lled.\n\nAdd your name to the Target Assignment List below or submit the ab
 ove completed form.\nFocus primarily on perfecting your form\, \nslowly inc
 reasing your physical strength and draw weight\, \nstrengthening your menta
 l program\, \ndetermining your average and personal best\, \nunderstanding 
 the spread between the two\, and working on closing it.\n\nYou need your ow
 n equipment \nCompetition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest
 \, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\,
  armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\,
  etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added until you reach a higher leve
 l\, but you should order them in advance.) \n\nWear your ATCI shirt to trai
 ning.\n\nWhen you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm target fa
 ce you'll move back to the next distance until you reach your competition d
 istance\nIf you trained outdoors in the 2024 season\, you'll return to the 
 farthest distance you shot.\n\nTarget arrangements may vary each session\, 
 depending on who attends and distances needed.\nTarget 1 at 70m (U21 + Seni
 ors competition distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use it for 
 independent practice in between classes.\nTarget 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters co
 mpetition distance) \nTarget 3 at 50m\nTarget 4+5 at 40m (U15 competition d
 istance) \nTarget 6+7+8 at 30m (U13 competition distance) \nTargets 9 at 20
 m (for those who have shot at 18m indoors or with Coach Racae's approval)\n
 Target 10 at 13.5m (for those who have just graduated from indoors at 9m)\n
 \nIdeally\, we want to practice with two archers/target to replicate compet
 ition conditions as much as possible.\n\nTarget Assignments:\nTargets are a
 ssigned outdoors in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\,\nso 
 add your name next to your distance below. \nIf you need help or have quest
 ions\, email/text Coach Racae\n(Dotted lines represent tent poles dividing 
 Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)\n----------------------------------\n1A. (70m)\n1B\
 n\n2A. (60m)  \n2B\n\n3A. (50m)  Nick E did not shoot. Coached\n-----------
 -----------------------\n3B\n\n4A. (40m) Luke T. OB\, USAA\, Pd worked on d
 raw and now hand releases. Relaxing hand and following thru\n4B. Colby K.!!
 ! USAA\, pd. Equipment work \n----------------------------------\n5A. (40m)
  Finn E. Worked on coiling\n5B. \n\n6A. (30m) \n---------------------------
 -------\n6B. \n\n7A. (30m)\n7B. \n---------------------------------- \n8A. 
 (30m)\n8B. \n\n9A. (20m) Rhys E worked on anchoring. \n--------------------
 --------------\n9B. \n\n10A. (13.5m)\n10B
LAST-MODIFIED:20260512T052633Z
LOCATION:2324 Bliss Spillar Rd\, Manchaca\, TX 78652\, USA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:OUTDOOR 3-9 (TC) at 13.5m-70m - Coach Nick Erickson
TRANSP:OPAQUE
