DESCRIPTION:Registration form: OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m\n\n\nREMINDER:  Eve
 ryone needs to come to at least one Training Class per week to be able to a
 ttend Open Practice. (All indoor classes are training classes.)\n\nIf you a
 re not a coach/instructor\, the fees are:  \n\nOutdoor Training Class (OTC)
 : $52/class or multi-class pack \n\nIndoor Training Class (ITC): $43/class 
 or multi-class pack or unlimited pack\n\nOpen Practice (OP): ($50/mo)  \n\n
 \nIf you are a coach/instructor\, you have received an email from Coach Rac
 ae outlining your fees.\n\nDuring the summer (May 31-Aug 31)\, at least 5 a
 rchers need to register by \n8:00 am on Thursdays (for Saturdays) and \n8:0
 0 am on Fridays (for Sundays) \nfor Coach Racae to coach the Outdoor 3-9 Tr
 aining Class. In the case of low or late registrations or cancellations\, a
 nother coach/instructor\, when available\, will coach the session as a Trai
 ning Class or oversee it as an Open Practice instead. If this is not possib
 le\, then the class may need to be cancelled.During the summer (May 31-Aug 
 31)\, at least 5 archers need to register by 8:00 am on Thursdays (for Satu
 rdays) and 8:00 am on Fridays (for Sundays) for Coach Racae to coach the Ou
 tdoor 3-9 Training Class . In the case of low or late registrations or canc
 ellations\, another coach/instructor\, when available\, will coach the sess
 ion as a Training Class or oversee it as an Open Practice instead. If this 
 is not possible\, then the class may need to be cancelled.\n\nAdd your name
  to the Target Assignment List below or submit the above completed form.\nF
 ocus primarily on perfecting your form\, \nslowly increasing your physical 
 strength and draw weight\, \nstrengthening your mental program\, \ndetermin
 ing your average and personal best\, \nunderstanding the spread between the
  two\, and working on closing it.\n\nYou need your own equipment \nCompetit
 ion recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, 
 side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\
 , finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and sid
 e rods may not be added until you reach a higher level\, but you should ord
 er them in advance.) \n\nWear your ATCI shirt to training.\n\nWhen you scor
 e 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to
  the next distance until you reach your competition distance\nIf you traine
 d outdoors in the 2024 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you 
 shot.\n\nTarget arrangements may vary each session\, depending on who atten
 ds and distances needed.\nTarget 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distan
 ce) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent practice i
 n between classes.\nTarget 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition distance) \n
 Target 3 at 50m\nTarget 4+5 at 40m (U15 competition distance) \nTarget 6+7+
 8 at 30m (U13 competition distance) \nTargets 9 at 20m (for those who have 
 shot at 18m indoors or with Coach Racae's approval)\nTarget 10 at 13.5m (fo
 r those who have just graduated from indoors at 9m)\n\nIdeally\, we want to
  practice with two archers/target to replicate competition conditions as mu
 ch as possible.\n\nTarget Assignments:\nTargets are assigned outdoors in ad
 vance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\,\nso add your name next to 
 your distance below. \nIf you need help or have questions\, email/text Coac
 h Racae\n(Dotted lines represent tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.
 )\n----------------------------------\n1A. (70m)\n1B\n\n2A. (60m)  \n2B\n\n
 3A. (50m)  \n----------------------------------\n3B\n\n4A. (40m) Hannah T\,
