DESCRIPTION:Registration form: OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m<br><br>Add your nam
 e to Target Assignment List below or send in the above completed form.<br><
 br>Focus primarily on <br>perfecting your form\, <br>slowly increasing your
  physical strength and draw weight\, <br>strengthening your mental program\
 , <br>determining your average and personal best\, <br>understanding the sp
 read between the two\, and working on closing it.<br><br>You need your own 
 equipment <br>Competition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest
 \, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\,
  armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\,
  etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added until you reach a higher leve
 l\, but you should order them in advance.) <br><br>Wear your ATCI shirt to 
 training.<br><br>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm t
 arget face you'll move back to the next distance until you reach your compe
 tition distance<br>If you trained outdoors in the 2024 outdoor season\, you
 'll return to the farthest distance you shot.<br>Target arrangements may va
 ry each session\, depending on who attends and distances needed.<br>Target 
 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should always stay at 70m so 
 Jake can use it for independent practice in between classes.<br>Target 2 at
  60m (U18 + Masters competition distance) <br>Target 3 at 50m<br>Targets 4+
 5 at 40m (U15 competition distance) <br>Targets 6\, 7\, 8 at 30m (U13 compe
 tition distance) <br>Target 9 at 20m (for those who have shot at 18m indoor
 s or with Coach Racae's approval)<br>Targets 10 at 13.5m (for those who hav
 e just graduated from indoors at 9m)<br><br>Ideally\, we want to practice w
 ith two archers/target to replicate competition conditions as often as poss
 ible.<br><br>Target Assignments:<br>Targets are assigned outdoors in advanc
 e to reduce confusion and delay on the day\,<br>so add your name next to yo
 ur distance below. <br>If you need help or have questions\, email/text Coac
 h Racae<br>(Dotted lines represent tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 
 9.)<br>----------------------------------<br>1A. (70m)<br>1B<br><br>2A. (60
 m)  <b>Joel Y</b>\, adult\, USAA\, ob\, pd<br>2B<br><br>3A. (50m)  <br>----
 ------------------------------<br>3B<br><br>4A. (40m) <br>4B<br>-----------
