DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u>This class has been canceled due to the heavy
  rains occurring today.<br>Usually when there has been a heavy rainfall the
  parking area is like a mud rink\, which can be hazardous with cars getting
  stuck or sliding into each other and people falling down.<br>Whether Sunda
 y´s classes will be held will depend on the condition of the area and the t
 emperatures tomorrow. Please re-register for a future class. (There are no 
 classes from Dec 20-Jan 8 inclusively.) Winter/Spring registration forms wi
 ll be up on the website within the next few days.<br><br>REGISTER NOW !<br>
 More information and registration form available on&nbsp\;<a href="http://w
 ww.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrainingcenter.com</a>.<br>Sign up
  for just one Outdoor 1 class\, because most people graduate out of this cl
 ass into Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br><br>Your name will be added b
 elow and your place reserved after we receive 3 things:&nbsp\; REGISTRATION
  + WAIVERS + FEE<br><br><b>Registered archers:</b><br><b>Target nos:</b><br
 >1. <b>Micah G</b>.\, adult - pd - moved to 1/8 - <b>substituted 2/12</b><b
 r>2. <b>Jeremy M</b>.\, adult - pd - moved to 1/8 - - <b>substituted 2/12</
 b><u></u><br><u></u>3.&nbsp\;<b>Jim H</b>. - adult - <b>pd - </b>substitute
 d 2/13<br>4. <b>Taylor T.</b> - adult - pd - <b>substituted 3/19</b><br>5. 
 <b>Jideobinna I.</b>\, adult - pd - <b>substituted 3/19</b><br>6A.&nbsp\;<b
 >Alex B.</b>\, adult - pd - share<br>6B. <b>Margaux B.\, </b>16 - pd - shar
 e<br>7.<br>8<br>9.<br>10.<br><br><br>Space will be limited to 10-15 archers
  per session depending on the number of family groups in attendance or in a
 ccordance with CDC Guidelines.&nbsp\;<br>Each person will have a target sta
 nd\, except after 10 people have registered\, two members from the same fam
 ily will share one target stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectat
 or will be allowed on the field until further notice or approved by Coach R
 acae. Parents can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator.<br><br>As o
 f Sept 15\, we have reached the maximum number of kids under 12 that we acc
 ept into the program this semester. The minimum age to register is now 12 y
 ears old.&nbsp\;<br><br>If you registered by Sept 15\, and are younger than
  12\, you´ll stay in the program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed
  and later join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;<br><br>If you are not yet 12\, and you re
 gistered and paid after Sept 15\, your fee will be returned to you.<br><br>
 Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying to 
 get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score o
 n average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need a minimu
 m score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguar
 d\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($15)<br
 >fp = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but really needed 
 to practice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Ou
 tdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a complete
  round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, because it ha
 s been averaged by taking your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividin
 g by the number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multi
 plying that by 30 to get a full round score. After the last class on the we
 ekend\, final scores will also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an 
 email with more information before your next class.<u></u></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260517T064558Z
