DESCRIPTION:USA Archery Level 3 NTS Coach Racae\n\nAlways check our website
 's calendar just before coming to class in case there are changes or cancel
 lations.\n\nPREREQUISITES: \nIndoor 4 is for JUNIOR archers and their paren
 ts who have \n- taken and qualified in the Indoor 1: First-time Class by sc
 oring 50 pts at 9 m\n- graduated out of Indoor 2 by scoring 240 pts at 9m a
 nd earning Master Tags\,\n- graduated out of Indoor 3A by scoring 240 pts a
 t 13.5m and earning Master Tags\,\n- graduated out of Indoor 3B by scoring 
 200 pts twice at 18m and earning all Master Tags for Indoor 3\n\nPARENTS \n
 can enroll and shoot with their child(ren) in the following classes\, provi
 ded they have completed the above prerequisites..\n\nPLEASE COMPLETE ONE EN
 ROLLMENT FORM FOR EACH ARCHER.\n\nDATES:          January 6 - May 31\, 2015
 \n\nCAPACITY:    10 archers per class\nAGES:            8 - 18 years old \n
 DISTANCES:  18m only\n\nCLASS SCHEDULE:\nSaturdays and Sundays: 4:00-5:30pm
 \n\nDAYS CLOSED:\nMONDAYS and FRIDAYS\nAPRIL 4 and 5: Easter Weekend\nMAY 6
 \, Range closed\nMAY 10\, Mother's Day\n\nENROLLMENT IS ON A FIRST-RECEIVED
  AND PAID BASIS.\nThis enrollment form must be completed and your payment r
 eceived in order for you to be enrolled and a place reserved for you.\nYou 
 can enroll any time during the semester for as many or as few classes as yo
 u like as long as there are places open.\nSo\, for example\, you can enroll
  for the entire semester\, each month\, or sprinkle the days throughout the
  semester depending on your schedule. (Please bear in mind\, however\, you'
 ll progress faster with regular attendance.)\n\nREFUNDS\, CREDITS\, and SUB
 STITUTIONS:\nThere are no refunds or credits for paid days missed January 6
  - May 31\, except in the case of injury\, long-term illness\, unforeseen m
 ove out of the Austin area\, or if we cancel a class. If\, however\, you le
 t us know that you will miss a class\, you can substitute another class as 
 long as there are places left in that class during the Spring 2015 semester
 .\n\nIn the case of physical injury or long-term illness\, we require a doc
 tor's note saying the archer is unable to practice archery\, and then a doc
 tor's note saying the archer is fit to return to archery\, before the arche
 r will be allowed back in class.\n\nATTENDANCE RECOMMENDATIONS in order to 
 improve and advance: \nINDOOR 2 at 9m :        One or two 1.5-hr classes/wk
 .\nINDOOR 3A at 13.5m : Two 1.5-hr classes/wk.\nINDOOR 3B at 18m :    Two o
 r three 1.5-hr classes/wk.\nINDOOR 4 at 18m (200-250 pts) :      \nTwo 1.5-
 hr classes/wk + one 1.5-hr Members Open Practice/wk + one monthly private l
 esson\nINDOOR 5 at 18m (250-270 pts):       \nTwo 1.5-hr classes/wk + two 1
 .5-hr Members Open Practice/wk + one monthly private lesson\nINDOOR 6 at 18
 m (270-280 pts):       \nThree 1.5-hr classes/wk + two 1.5-hr Members Open 
 Practice/wk + one monthly private lesson\nINDOOR 7 at 18m (280-290 pts)   \
 nThree 1.5-hr classes/wk + three 1.5-hr Members Open Practice/wk + one mont
 hly private lesson\nJOAD OLYMPIANS - INDOOR 8 at 18m (290-300 pts):\nThree 
 1.5-hr classes/wk + three 1.5-hr Members Open Practice/wk + one monthly pri
 vate lesson\n\nMINIMUM ENROLLMENT:\nClasses will be held only if there are 
 5 or more archers enrolled in the class. \nIf the class does not make this 
 minimum enrollment requirement\, you will be notified at least one week in 
 advance\, so you can reschedule.\n\nHOW DO I ADVANCE?\nPlease note that mas
 tering NTS positions relevant to each level will be required to advance to 
 the next level\; advancement will no longer be based on scores alone.\n\nYo
 u'll be trained in Indoor 4 at 18m until you score 250 pts and master most 
 NTS* Shot Cycle positions. You'll then be in Indoor 5. At this point you'll
  need to consider whether you want to become a competitive archer or remain
  recreational. \n\nIf you decide to train for competition\, you will be ref
 erred to Coach Alex\, who will conduct an evaluation with you\, expect you 
 to be able to explain to him and shoot the NTS method\, and dedicate at lea
 st 10 hours a week to archery. \n\nIf you are recreational\, you will conti
 nue to work on your NTS form\, mental management\, and strength to eventual
 ly graduate into Indoor 6 by shooting 270 pts at 18m\, into Indoor 7 by sho
 oting 280 pts.\, and then Indoor 8 by shooting 290 pts\, when you will also
  shoot free in the recreational program forever! \n\nYou can also opt to be
 come a USA Archery Level 1 NTS Instructor when you turn 15 years old\, and 
 a Level 2 when you are 18 years old\, which bring additional privileges and
  responsibilities.\n\nFEES:\nAll fees are payable in advance of the class t
 o secure your place in the class.\n$20 / class\, if paid on or before Dec. 
 7\, 2014\n$21 / class\, if paid on or before Dec. 14\, 2014\n$22 / class\, 
 if paid after Dec. 14\, 2014.\n\n+ Enrollment fee: $20 (always due once per
  semester)\n\nPrivate Lessons (recommended at least once a month for Indoor
  4 and above):\n$40/hr: USA Archery Level 3 Coach Racae ($65/hr for 2\, $90
 /hr for 3)\n$30/hr: USA Archery Level 2 Instructor Luke or Dale or Dan\n$20
 /hr  USA Archery Level 1 Instructor Chloe or Tori\n\nMembers Open Practice 
 (times shown on website calendar): \nFree after you have attended two class
 es during the week before\, otherwise it is $10/practice time (1.5 hrs usua
 lly). \nThere is no coaching\; it's time for you to practice what you have 
 learned!\n\nHOW MUCH DO I OWE? \nMultiply the number of classes x the appro
 priate fee above.\nAdd the $20 semester enrollment fee\nAdd the number of p
 rivate one-hour lessons you want to schedule x the private lesson hourly fe
 e\n\nHOW DO I PAY IN ADVANCE?\nPay the total by Paypal using e-mail address
 : racae@aajoad.com.\nWe also accept checks and credit cards in person at th
 e indoor range.\nPlease make your check payable to "Archery Training Center
 \, Inc." and give it to us at JOAD* or mail it to us at:\nArchery Training 
 Center\, Inc.\, PO Box 93216\, Austin\, TX 78709-3216\n\nMEMBERSHIP IN USA 
 ARCHERY:\nMembership in USA Archery is now REQUIRED to participate in JOAD 
 and Adult Training.\nThis is a new USA Archery requirement. If you would li
 ke to see the benefits of a USAA membership:\nhttp://www.teamusa.org/USA-Ar
 chery/Membership/Membership-Benefits\nJOIN USA ARCHERY: https://webpoint.us
 archery.org/wp/Memberships/Join.wp\n(Youths <17yrs: $35\; Adults: $50\; Fam
 ily: $80)\nYou can attend 2 JOAD classes before joining USAA\, but then we'
 ll need to see your membership card!\n\nSAFE SPORTS:\nParents please note w
 e are part of the US Olympic Committee's Safe Sport program\, so we minimal
 ly require one other adult besides the instructor to be present at all time
 s. Please plan to stay with your child or take turns with other parents sta
 ying whenever necessary to fulfill this requirement. THANKS!\n\nWAIVERS:\nP
 lease fill out\, sign\, and return the Membership\, Liability\, Photo\, Med
 ical\, and Supervision Releases available at the range or attached to the e
 -mail you received.\n\nQUESTIONS?\nE-mail us at racae@archerytrainingcenter
 .com or\nCall us at 512 436 8813 or \nText us at 512 925 7794\n\n*NTS = Nat
 ional Training System\n*JOAD = Junior Olympic Archery Development
