DESCRIPTION:Registration form: OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m<br><br>Add your nam
 e to Target Assignment List below or send in the above completed form.<br><
 br>Focus primarily on <br>perfecting your form\, <br>slowly increasing your
  physical strength and draw weight\, <br>strengthening your mental program\
 , <br>determining your average and personal best\, <br>understanding the sp
 read between the two\, and working on closing it.<br>You need your own equi
 pment <br>Competition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 1
 2 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, arm
 guard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc
 . (Clicker and side rods may not be added until you reach a higher level\, 
 but you should order them in advance.) <br><br>Wear your ATCI shirt to trai
 ning.<br><br>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm targe
 t face you'll move back to the next distance until you reach your competiti
 on distance<br>If you trained outdoors in the 2024 season\, you'll return t
 o the farthest distance you shot.<br>Target arrangements may vary each sess
 ion\, depending on who attends and distances needed.<br>Target 1 at 70m (U2
 1 + Seniors competition distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use
  it for independent practice in between classes.<br>Target 2 at 60m (U18 + 
 Masters competition distance) <br>Target 3 at 50m<br>Target 4 at 40m (U15 c
 ompetition distance) <br>Target 5 at 30m (U13 competition distance) <br>Tar
 gets 6+7+8 at 20m (for those who have shot at 18m indoors or with Coach Rac
 ae's approval)<br>Targets 9 + 10 at 13.5m (for those who have just graduate
 d from indoors at 9m)<br><br>Ideally\, we want to practice with two archers
 /target to replicate competition conditions as much as possible.<br><br>Tar
 get Assignments:<br>Targets are assigned outdoors in advance to reduce conf
 usion and delay on the day\,<br>so add your name next to your distance belo
 w. <br>If you need help or have questions\, email/text Coach Racae<br>(Dott
 ed lines represent tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)<br>---------
 -------------------------<br>1A. (70m)<br>1B<br><br>2A. (60m)  <b>Lily R</b
 >.\, 16\, USAA\, OB\, pd<br>2B<br><br>3A. (50m)  <b>Joel Y.</b>\, adult\, U
