 r 2 at 9m and Outdoor 3 at 13.5m</a><br><br>ap = accessories pack purchases
  (this is required for Outdoor 2) $15<br>fp = optional\, but really necessa
 ry to practice form and warm up (stretchband/string loop) $4<br>sef = semes
 ter enrollment fee due once a semester before first Outdoor 2 lesson $20<br
 ><br><b>Registered archers</b>:<br><b>Target nos.</b><br>1. <b>Peggy Jo S</
 b>.\, adult - pd + sef + fp + ap <b>39 pts</b><br>2.&nbsp\;<b>Christopher N
 </b>.\, adult - pd<br>3. <b>Bryson&nbsp\;</b>H.\, adult - pd<br>4&nbsp\;<b>
 Jesse A</b>.\, dad - pd + fp + sef <b>147 pts?</b><br>5. <b>Riley A</b>.\, 
 8 - pd + fp + sef <b>58 pts</b><br>6.&nbsp\;<b>Marissa I.\,&nbsp\;</b>adult
  - pd&nbsp\;<b>&nbsp\;66 pts</b><br>7. <b>Tracy T</b>.\, adult - pd<br>8. <
 b>Kishore P</b>.\, 13 - pd<br>9.&nbsp\;<b>Milo R.\, </b>13 - pd - <b>DNA</b
 ><br>10.<br><br>Space will be limited to a maximum of 10-15 archers per ses
 sion depending on the number of family groups in attendance or in accordanc
 e with CDC Guidelines.&nbsp\;<br>Each person will have a target stand\, exc
 ept after 10 people have registered\, two members from the same family will
  share one target stand.<br><br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator w
 ill be allowed on the field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae
 . Parents can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator.<br><br>As of Se
 pt 15\, we have reached the maximum number of kids under 12 that we accept 
 into the program this semester. The minimum age to register is now 12 years
  old.&nbsp\;<br><br>If you registered by Sept 15\, and are younger than 12\
 , you´ll stay in the program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and
  later join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;<br>More information and other registration fo
