UID:femqkf7loqio45b8msr9nsvp74@google.com
CREATED:20140731T180113Z
DESCRIPTION:USA Archery Level 3 NTS Coach Racae\n\nIf you would like a 2014
  Fall Enrollment Form\, contact racae@archerytrainingcenter.com\n\nAlways c
 heck our website's calendar just before coming to class in case there are c
 hanges or cancellations.\n\nPREREQUISITES: \nIndoor 4 is for JUNIOR archers
  and their parents who have \n- taken and qualified in the Indoor 1: First-
 time Class by scoring 50 pts at 9 m\n- graduated out of Indoor 2 by scoring
  240 pts at 9m\,\n- graduated out of Indoor 3A by scoring 240 pts at 13.5m\
 ,\n- graduated out of Indoor 3B by scoring 200 pts twice at 18m\n\nPARENTS 
 \ncan enroll and shoot with their child(ren) in the following classes\, pro
 vided they have completed the above prerequisites..\n\nPLEASE COMPLETE ONE 
 ENROLLMENT FORM FOR EACH ARCHER.\n\nDATES:          August 23 - December 14
 \, 2014\n\nCAPACITY:    10 archers per class\nAGES:            8 - 18 years
  old \nDISTANCES:  18m only\n\nCLASS SCHEDULE:\nSaturdays and Sundays: 4:00
 -5:30pm\n\nDAYS CLOSED:\nSEPT. 1\, Labor Day\nSEPT. 30\, Range closed\nOCT.
  31\, Halloween\nNOV. 26-30\, Thanksgiving\nDEC. 15 - Jan. 3\, Christmas / 
 New Year's\n\nENROLLMENT IS ON A FIRST-RECEIVED AND PAID BASIS.\nAn enrollm
 ent form must be completed and your payment received in order for you to be
  enrolled and a place reserved for you.\nYou can enroll any time during the
  semester for as many or as few classes as you like as long as there are pl
 aces open.\nSo\, for example\, you can enroll for the entire semester\, eac
 h month\, or sprinkle the days throughout the semester depending on your sc
 hedule. (Please bear in mind\, however\, you'll progress faster with regula
 r attendance.)\n\nREFUNDS\, CREDITS\, and SUBSTITUTIONS:\nThere are no refu
 nds or credits for paid days missed Aug. 23 - Dec. 14\, 2014\, except in th
 e case of injury\, long-term illness\, unforeseen move out of the Austin ar
 ea\, or if we cancel a class. If\, however\, you let us know that you will 
 miss a class\, you can substitute another class as long as there are places
  left in that class during the Fall 2014 semester.\n\nIn the case of physic
 al injury or long-term illness\, we require a doctor's note saying the arch
 er is unable to practice archery\, and then a doctor's note saying the arch
 er is fit to return to archery\, before the archer will be allowed back in 
 class.\n\nATTENDANCE RECOMMENDATIONS in order to improve and advance: \nIND
 OOR 2 at 9m :        One or two 1.5-hr classes/wk.\nINDOOR 3A at 13.5m : Tw
 o 1.5-hr classes/wk.\nINDOOR 3B at 18m :    Two or three 1.5-hr classes/wk.
 \nINDOOR 4 at 18m (200-250 pts) :      \nTwo 1.5-hr classes/wk + one 1.5-hr
  Members Open Practice/wk + one monthly private lesson\nINDOOR 5 at 18m (25
 0-270 pts):       \nTwo 1.5-hr classes/wk + two 1.5-hr Members Open Practic
 e/wk + one monthly private lesson\nINDOOR 6 at 18m (270-280 pts):       \nT
 hree 1.5-hr classes/wk + two 1.5-hr Members Open Practice/wk + one monthly 
 private lesson\nINDOOR 7 at 18m (280-290 pts)   \nThree 1.5-hr classes/wk +
  three 1.5-hr Members Open Practice/wk + one monthly private lesson\nJOAD O
 LYMPIANS - INDOOR 8 at 18m (290-300 pts):\nThree 1.5-hr classes/wk + three 
 1.5-hr Members Open Practice/wk + one monthly private lesson\n\nMINIMUM ENR
 OLLMENT:\nClasses will be held only if there are 5 or more archers enrolled
  in the class. \nIf the class does not make this minimum enrollment require
 ment\, you will be notified at least one week in advance\, so you can resch
 edule.\n\nHOW DO I ADVANCE?\nPlease note that starting in Fall 2014\, maste
 ring NTS positions relevant to each level will be required to advance to th
 e next level\; advancement will no longer be based on scores alone.\n\nYou'
 ll be trained in Indoor 4 at 18m until you score 250 pts and master most NT
 S* Shot Cycle positions. You'll then be in Indoor 5. At this point you'll n
 eed to consider whether you want to become a competitive archer or remain r
 ecreational. \n\nIf you decide to train for competition\, you will be refer
 red to Coach Alex\, who will expect you to be able to explain to him and sh
 oot the NTS method\, and dedicate at least 10 hours a week to archery. \n\n
 If you are recreational\, you will continue to work on your NTS form\, ment
 al management\, and strength to eventually graduate into Indoor 6 by shooti
 ng 270 pts at 18m\, into Indoor 7 by shooting 280 pts.\, and then Indoor 8 
 by shooting 290 pts\, when you will also shoot free in the recreational pro
 gram forever! \n\nYou can also opt to become a USA Archery Level 1 NTS Inst
 ructor when you turn 15 years old\, and a Level 2 when you are 18 years old
 \, which bring additional privileges and responsibilities.\n\nFEES:\nAll fe
 es are payable in advance of the class to secure your place in the class.\n
 $20 / class\, if paid on or before August 3\, 2014 \n$21 / class\, if paid 
 on or before August 24\, 2014 \n$22 / class\, if paid after August 24\, 201
 4.\n\n+ Enrollment fee: $20 (always due once per semester)\n\nPrivate Lesso
 ns (recommended at least once a month for Indoor 4 and above):\n$40/hr: USA
  Archery Level 3 Coach Racae\n$30/hr: USA Archery Level 2 Instructor Luke o
 r Dale\n$20/hr  USA Archery Level 1 Instructor Chloe\n\nMembers Open Practi
 ce (times shown on website calendar): \nFree after you have attended two cl
 asses during the week before\, otherwise it is $10/practice time (1.5 hrs u
 sually). \nThere is no coaching\; it's time for you to practice what you ha
 ve learned!\n\nHOW MUCH DO I OWE? \nMultiply the number of classes x the ap
 propriate fee above.\nAdd the $20 semester enrollment fee\nAdd the number o
 f private one-hour lessons you want to schedule x the private lesson hourly
  fee\n\nHOW DO I PAY IN ADVANCE?\nPay the total by Paypal using e-mail addr
 ess: racae@aajoad.com.\nWe also accept checks and credit cards in person at
  the indoor range.\nPlease make your check payable to "Archery Training Cen
 ter\, Inc." and give it to us at JOAD* or mail it to us at:\nArchery Traini
 ng Center\, Inc.\, PO Box 93216\, Austin\, TX 78709-3216\n\nSAFE SPORTS:\nP
 arents please note we are part of the US Olympic Committee's Safe Sport pro
 gram\, so we minimally require one other adult besides the instructor to be
  present at all times. Please plan to stay with your child or take turns wi
 th other parents staying whenever necessary to fulfill this requirement. TH
 ANKS!\n\nWAIVERS:\nPlease fill out\, sign\, and return the Membership\, Lia
 bility\, Photo\, Medical\, and Supervision Releases attached to the e-mail 
 you received with your enrollment form link..\n\nQUESTIONS?\nE-mail us at r
 acae@archerytrainingcenter.com or\nCall us at 512 436 8813\n\n*NTS = Nation
 al Training System\n*JOAD = Junior Olympic Archery Development
LAST-MODIFIED:20260513T121423Z
LOCATION:10203 Old Manchaca Road\, Austin\, TX\, 78748
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:INDOOR 4/5: Juniors and Parents
TRANSP:OPAQUE
