 ><br>Your name will be added below and your place reserved after we receive
  3 things:&nbsp\; REGISTRATION + WAIVERS + FEE<br><br>Results:<br><b>Adults
 /Parents - (automatic pass into Outdoor 2):</b><br><b>Daniel C</b>.\, <b>70
  pts</b><br><b>Jennifer </b>T.\, <b>39 pts</b><br><b>Jesse&nbsp\;</b>A.\, <
 b>106 pts</b><br><b>Kirk </b>T.\, <b>107 pts</b> <br><b>Valerie T</b>.\, <b
 >10 pts</b><br><br><b>JOAD (Junior Olympic Archery Development) </b><b><br>
 </b><br><i>(Because of the extreme wind conditions\, you only needed 40 pts
  to go to Outdoor 2.)</i><br><b>Khosal R.\,&nbsp\;</b>12 - <b>63 pts</b> -&
 gt\; Outdoor 2<br><br><b>and our youngest ones:</b><br><b>Riley</b>&nbsp\;A
 .\, 8 - <b>45 pts </b>-&gt\; Outdoor 2<br><br>Space will be limited to 10-1
 5 archers per session depending on the number of family groups in attendanc
 e or in accordance with CDC Guidelines.&nbsp\;<br>Each person will have a t
 arget stand\, except after 10 people have registered\, two members from the
  same family will share one target stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of on
 e spectator will be allowed on the field until further notice or approved b
 y Coach Racae. Parents can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator.<br
 ><br>As of Sept 15\, we have reached the maximum number of kids under 12 th
 at we accept into the program this semester. The minimum age to register is
  now 12 years old.&nbsp\;<br><br>If you registered by Sept 15\, and are you
 nger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take other Outdoor 1 classes 
 as needed and later join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;<br><br>If you are not yet 12\, a
 nd you registered and paid after Sept 15\, your fee will be returned to you
 .<br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times before quali
 fying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as yo
 u score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need
  a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet
  (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2.
  ($15)<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but reall
 y needed to practice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end o
 f each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a
  complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, beca
 use it has been averaged by taking your recorded score from your scorecard\
 , dividing by the number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and t
 hen multiplying that by 30 to get a full round score. After the last class 
 on the weekend\, final scores will also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participan
 ts in an email with more information before your next class.
