  - pd DNA - ill<br>10. <b>Linda</b> L.\, adult - pd -&nbsp\;DNA<br><br>Spac
 e will be limited to a maximum of 10-15 archers per session depending on th
 e number of family groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC Guideline
 s.&nbsp\;<br>Each person will have a target stand\, except after 10 people 
 have registered\, two members from the same family will share one target st
 and.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the fi
 eld until further notice or approved by Coach Racae. Parents can sign up as
  an archer or watch as a spectator.<br><br>As of Sept 15\, we have reached 
 the maximum number of kids under 12 that we accept into the program this se
 mester. The minimum age to register is now 12 years old.&nbsp\;<br><br>If y
 ou registered by Sept 15\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the pro
 gram and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2.&n
 bsp\;<br><br>If you are not yet 12\, and you registered and paid after Sept
  15\, your fee will be returned to you.<br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor
  1 two or three times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50
  pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 a
 rrows.&nbsp\;<br><br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Out
 door 2.<br><br>Your name will be added below and your place reserved after 
 we receive your registration form\, waivers\, AND fee.<br><br>ap = purchase
 d accessories packet\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2.<br><br>At the en
 d of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted below. If we did not
  finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final sco
 re\, because it has been averaged by taking your recorded score from your s
 corecard\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot to get an arrow averag
 e\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round score. After the la
 st class on the weekend\, all final scores will additionally be sent to you
  in an email with other information before your next class.
