DESCRIPTION:REGISTER NOW !<br>More information and registration form availa
 ble on&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrai
 ningcenter.com</a>.<br>Sign up for just one Outdoor 1 class\, because most 
 people graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br
 ><br>Your name will be added below and your place reserved after we receive
  3 things:&nbsp\; REGISTRATION + WAIVERS + FEE<br><br><b>Registered archers
 :</b><br><b>Target nos:</b><br>1. <b>Tracy P.\, </b>adult - pd - 62R - <b>3
 9 pts</b> -&gt\; Outdoor 2<br>2. <b>Stefen P</b>.\, 16 - pd - 66R - <b>61 p
 ts </b>-&gt\; Outdoor 2<br>3. <b>Zayne R.\, </b>adult - pd - 68R - <b>89 pt
 s</b> -&gt\; Outdoor 2<br>4. <b>Satya P.\, </b>adult - pd&nbsp\; - <b>119 p
 ts</b> -&gt\; Outdoor 2<br>5. <b>Marin M.\, 15&nbsp\;</b>- pd <b>11 pts</b>
 &nbsp\; -&gt\; Outdoor 1<br>6. <b>Livi F.\, 15 </b>- pd - cash - <b>35 pts<
 /b> -&gt\; Outdoor 1<br>7.<br>8.<br>9.<br>10.<br><br><br>Space will be limi
 ted to 10-15 archers per session depending on the number of family groups i
 n attendance or in accordance with CDC Guidelines.&nbsp\;<br>Each person wi
 ll have a target stand\, except after 10 people have registered\, two membe
 rs from the same family will share one target stand.<br>The archer and a ma
 ximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field until further notice or
  approved by Coach Racae. Parents can sign up as an archer or watch as a sp
 ectator.<br><br>As of Sept 15\, we have reached the maximum number of kids 
 under 12 that we accept into the program this semester. The minimum age to 
 register is now 12 years old.&nbsp\;<br><br>If you registered by Sept 15\, 
 and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take other Outdoor
  1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;<br><br>If you are not
  yet 12\, and you registered and paid after Sept 15\, your fee will be retu
 rned to you.<br><br><b>Juniors </b>may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three 
 times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring <b>50 pts</b>. You
 ´ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.&nb
 sp\;<br><b>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.</b
 ><br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, whi
 ch will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($15)<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and s
 tring loop)\, optional but really needed to practice form\, warm up before 
 classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will b
 e posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not r
 ecognize your final score\, because it has been averaged by taking your rec
 orded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot
  to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full ro
 und score. After the last class on the weekend\, final scores will also be 
 sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more information before
  your next class.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260517T064558Z
SEQUENCE:3
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:OUTDOOR 1 - First-time Class
