DESCRIPTION:<b>Tournaments are held at the end of each calendar month at 9:
 00 am - 11:30 pm on Saturdays and Sundays</b>\, weather permitting.&nbsp\;<
 u></u>If you are new to our program\, come and try it\, so you will be more
  comfortable and better prepared next month!<br><br><u></u>The only differe
 nces between the regular training sessions and the tournaments are that we 
 are more closely reproducing tournament conditions\, which include:<u></u><
 br><ul><li><u></u>No coaching while you are on the shooting line (but\, as 
 in a real tournament\, y<u></u>ou can always ask the coach for help in betw
 een the ends.) This is your chance to find out how well you can do the form
  on your own\, and learn how to go into ¨trusting¨ compared with ¨training¨
  mode.</li><li><u></u>You will shoot more arrows :&nbsp\; 2 practice ends +
  Two rounds -&nbsp\;<u></u>60 arrows at 9m and 13.5m or 72 arrows at 20m-70
 m</li><li><u></u>You will score every arrow for two rounds.&nbsp\;<u></u></
 li><li><u></u>The ends will be timed. You´ll have 4 min to shoot 6 arrows.<
 u></u></li><li>Everyone will be shooting at close-to-regular tournament spa
 cing so there will be two archers on each target about 3 ft apart\, dependi
 ng on the number of registrations</li><li>There will be a maximum of 20 arc
 hers on the shooting line at the same time. Awesome! (Lots of arrow flying 
 towards the targets!)</li></ul><br>Your goal is always to replicate the NTS
  step(s) mindfully and consistently on every shot.<br><u></u><b>Outside of 
 the tournament weeks</b>\, each week the focus of your lessons will be on p
 articular Steps of Shooting of the NTS (National Training System) shot cycl
 e\, to help you focus and improve your form\, which\, as we all know\, lead
 s to greater precision (tighter groups of arrows) and ultimately greater ac
 curacy (tight groups of arrows dead center).<br><u></u><br><b>JUNE</b><br><
 b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>2-5</b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;Welcome Summe
 r!&nbsp\; Understanding&nbsp\; NTS CONCEPTS<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</
 b><b>6-12&nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b>NTS Steps 1+2: STANCE + NOCK&nbsp\;and<b>&nbsp\
 ;</b>NTS Step 3: HOOK &amp\; GRIP<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;<b>13-23&nbsp\;
 </b>NTS Step 4: SET&nbsp\;and&nbsp\;NTS Step 5: SET-UP<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\
 ; &nbsp\;25/</b><b>26 MASTER CHALLENGE and STAR PIN SHOOT&nbsp\;</b>(tourna
 ment)<br><b>JULY</b><br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;2-3</b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &n
 bsp\; NTS Step 6 DRAW to LOAD&nbsp\;and&nbsp\;NTS Step 7 ANCHOR&nbsp\;<br><
 u></u>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;<b>4-10&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</b>&nbsp\; NTS Step 8 TR
 ANSFER to HOLD<br><u></u><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;11-17</b>&nbsp\; NTS Ste
 p 9 EXPAND / AIM<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;<b>18-24&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</b>NTS St
 ep 10 RELEASE and FOLLOW-THROUGH<br><u></u><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b
 >30/31:&nbsp\;</b><b>MASTER CHALLENGE and STAR PIN SHOOT&nbsp\;</b>(tournam
 ent)<br><b>AUGUST</b><br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;1-7</b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &
 nbsp\; &nbsp\;NTS Step 11 FEEDBACK&nbsp\;<br><u></u><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbs
 p\;8-14&nbsp\;</b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; PUTTING IT ALL TOGETHER !!<br>&nbsp\; &nb
 sp\;<i>&nbsp\;<b>&nbsp\;</b></i><b>20&nbsp\;</b>&nbsp\;&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbs
 p\;&nbsp\;<b><i>FALL SEMESTER BEGINS !!</i></b><br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp
 \;27/28:&nbsp\;</b><b>MASTER CHALLENGE and STAR PIN SHOOT&nbsp\;</b>(tourna
 ment)<br><br>You do not need to score every class. In fact\, it would be mo
 re beneficial to you if you scored only during Master Challenge Tournament 
 Weeks\, which happen the last week of each month. This is because working o
 n the NTS Steps of Shooting (your form) is more easily done without the dis
 traction of the target face or scoring\, and you will improve faster.<br><b
 r>As you reach higher levels\, you will learn the NTS Steps in progressivel
 y greater detail.<br>The NTS Steps are cumulative with each step most succe
 ssfully completed if the previous steps have been completed mindfully.&nbsp
 \;<br><br>Your ability to learn and understand the NTS Steps\, and use deep
  focus on these Steps while shooting outdoors and while using your stretchb
 and/string loop at home will propel you to higher levels fast!<br><br><b>Go
 als by the end of the semester:&nbsp\;</b><br>See Coach Racae´s email ¨2022
  New Year´s Goals¨
