DESCRIPTION:REGISTER NOW !<br>More information and registration form availa
 ble on&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrai
 ningcenter.com</a>.<br>Sign up for just one Outdoor 1 class\, because most 
 people graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br
 >Adults automatically go into Outdoor 2 after their first Outdoor 1 class.&
 nbsp\;<br>Juniors need 50 pts at 9m over 30 arrows and other requirements t
 o go into Outdoor 2. (See details in the Outdoor 1 registration form.)<br><
 br>Your name will be added below and your place reserved after we receive 3
  things:&nbsp\; REGISTRATION + WAIVERS + FEE<br><br><b>Registered archers:<
 /b><br><b>Target nos.:<br></b>1. Ana S.\, mom - <b>51 pts.</b><br>2. Nico S
 .\, 8 - <b>14 pts -&gt\; repeat Outdoor 1</b><br>3. Melissa H.\, adult - <b
 >18 pts.</b><br>4. Jan V.\, adult - <b>38 pts</b><br>5. Jenny L.\, adult - 
 <b>64 pts.</b><br>6. Patrick M.\, adult - <b>48 pts</b><br>7. Stephanie L.\
 , adult - <b>18 pts</b><br>8. Yoo-Jin A.\, adult - <b>49 pts</b><br>9. Marc
  E.\, adult - <b>171 pts</b><br>10. Linda L.\, adult - <b>99 pts.</b><br><b
 r>Space will be limited to a maximum of 10-15 archers per session depending
  on the number of family groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC Gui
 delines.&nbsp\;<br>Each person will have a target stand\, except after 10 p
 eople have registered\, two members from the same family will share one tar
 get stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on 
 the field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae. Parents can sign
  up as an archer or watch as a spectator.<br><br>As of Sept 15\, we have re
 ached the maximum number of kids under 12 that we accept into the program t
 his semester. The minimum age to register is now 12 years old.&nbsp\;<br><b
 r>If you registered by Sept 15\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in t
 he program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoo
 r 2.&nbsp\;<br><br>If you are not yet 12\, and you registered and paid afte
 r Sept 15\, your fee will be returned to you.<br>Juniors may need to take O
 utdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scor
 ing 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end 
 of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into O
 utdoor 2.<br><br>Your name will be added below and your place reserved afte
 r we receive your registration form\, waivers\, AND fee.<br><br>ap = access
 ories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, purchased\, which will 
 be needed for Outdoor 2.<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, 
 purchased\, optional but really needed to practice form\, warm up before cl
 asses $4.00<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be
  posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not re
 cognize your final score\, because it has been averaged by taking your reco
 rded score from your scorecard\, dividing it by the number of arrows you sh
 ot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full 
 round score. After the last class on the weekend\, all final scores will al
 so be sent to all Outdoor 1 participates in an email with more information 
 before your next class.
