DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u>REGISTER NOW !<br>More information and regist
 ration form available on&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.co
 m">www.archerytrainingcenter.com</a>.<br>Sign up for just one Outdoor 1 cla
 ss\, because most people graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after th
 e first lesson.<br><br>Your name will be added below and your place reserve
 d after we receive 3 things:&nbsp\; REGISTRATION + WAIVERS + FEE<br><br><b>
 Registered archers </b>at 9m on 40-cm target faces unless otherwise noted:<
 br><b>Target nos:</b><br>1. <b>Alasdair T.\, </b>16 - moved to 1/8<br>2A.&n
 bsp\;<b>Lisa B.</b>\, mom - pd - <b>refunded</b><br>2B.&nbsp\;<b>Paow S.</b
 >\, 12 - pd -<b> refunded</b><br>3A.&nbsp\;<b>Rene S.\,</b>&nbsp\;adult - p
 d - <b>refunded</b><br>3B.&nbsp\;<b>Zuum S.\,</b>&nbsp\;14 - pd - <b>refund
 ed</b><br>4. <b>Margaux B.\,&nbsp\;</b>16<b>&nbsp\;</b>- pd&nbsp\;&nbsp\;- 
 moved from 12/18 - substituted 2/13<br>5. <b>Alex B.\, dad</b>&nbsp\;- pd -
  moved from 12/18 - substituted 2/13<br>6. <b>Carlos B.\, </b>adult - pd&nb
 sp\;<br>7.<br>8.<br>9.<br>10.<br><br><br>Space will be limited to 10-15 arc
 hers per session depending on the number of family groups in attendance or 
 in accordance with CDC Guidelines.&nbsp\;<br>Each person will have a target
  stand\, except after 10 people have registered\, two members from the same
  family will share one target stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spe
 ctator will be allowed on the field until further notice or approved by Coa
 ch Racae. Parents can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator.<br><br>
 As of Sept 15\, we have reached the maximum number of kids under 12 that we
  accept into the program this semester. The minimum age to register is now 
 12 years old.&nbsp\;<br><br>If you registered by Sept 15\, and are younger 
 than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as ne
 eded and later join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;<br><br>If you are not yet 12\, and yo
 u registered and paid after Sept 15\, your fee will be returned to you.<br>
 <br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying
  to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you sco
 re on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need a mi
 nimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (arm
 guard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($15
 )<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but really nee
 ded to practice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of eac
 h Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a comp
 lete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, because i
 t has been averaged by taking your recorded score from your scorecard\, div
 iding by the number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then m
 ultiplying that by 30 to get a full round score. After the last class on th
 e weekend\, final scores will also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in
  an email with more information before your next class.<u></u></html-blob>
