DESCRIPTION:REGISTER NOW !<br>More information and registration form availa
 ble on&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrai
 ningcenter.com</a>.<br>Sign up for just one Outdoor 1 class\, because most 
 people graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br
 ><br>Your name will be added below and your place reserved after we receive
  3 things:&nbsp\; REGISTRATION + WAIVERS + FEE<br><br><b>Registered archers
 :</b><br><b>Target nos:</b><br>1.&nbsp\;<br>2.&nbsp\;<br>3.&nbsp\;<br>4.&nb
 sp\;<br>5.&nbsp\;<br>6.&nbsp\;<br>7.<br>8.<br>9.<br>10.<br><br><br>Space wi
 ll be limited to 10-15 archers per session depending on the number of famil
 y groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC Guidelines.&nbsp\;<br>Each
  person will have a target stand\, except after 10 people have registered\,
  two members from the same family will share one target stand.<br>The arche
 r and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field until further
  notice or approved by Coach Racae. Parents can sign up as an archer or wat
 ch as a spectator.<br><br>As of Sept 15\, we have reached the maximum numbe
 r of kids under 12 that we accept into the program this semester. The minim
 um age to register is now 12 years old.&nbsp\;<br><br>If you registered by 
 Sept 15\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take oth
 er Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;<br><br>If y
 ou are not yet 12\, and you registered and paid after Sept 15\, your fee wi
 ll be returned to you.<br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or thr
 ee times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll 
 make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;
 <br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap
  = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be 
 needed for Outdoor 2. ($15)<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string loop)
 \, optional but really needed to practice form\, warm up before classes ($4
 )<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. I
 f we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize yo
 ur final score\, because it has been averaged by taking your recorded score
  from your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot to get an 
 arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round score. 
 After the last class on the weekend\, final scores will also be sent to all
  Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more information before your next 
 class.
