DESCRIPTION:REGISTER NOW !<br>More information and registration form availa
 ble on&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrai
 ningcenter.com</a>.<br>Sign up for just one Outdoor 1 class\, because most 
 people graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br
 ><br>Your name will be added below and your place reserved after we receive
  3 things:&nbsp\; REGISTRATION + WAIVERS + FEE<br><br>Juniors may need to t
 ake Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by
  scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts
 /end of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate i
 nto Outdoor 2.<br><br><b>Registered archers:</b><br><b>Target nos:</b><br>1
 A. Arik Y.\, parent - <b>87 pts</b><br>1B. Yuval Y.\, 12 -&nbsp\;<b>10 pts 
 -&gt\; Outdoor 1</b><br>2A. Lital Y.\, parent - <b>38 pts</b><br>2B. Shahar
  Y.\, 14 - <b>75 pts -&gt\; Outdoor 2&nbsp\;</b><br>3.&nbsp\; &nbsp\;Dan S.
 \, dad <b>100 pts&nbsp\;</b>&nbsp\;<br>4.&nbsp\; &nbsp\;Lyla S.\, 9 - <b>50
  pts -&gt\; Outdoor 2&nbsp\;</b><br>5.&nbsp\;<br>6.&nbsp\;<br>7.<br>8.<br>9
 .<br>10.<br><br>Space will be limited to 10-15 archers per session dependin
 g on the number of family groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC Gu
 idelines.&nbsp\;<br>Each person will have a target stand\, except after 10 
 people have registered\, two members from the same family will share one ta
 rget stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on
  the field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae. Parents can sig
 n up as an archer or watch as a spectator.<br><br>As of Sept 15\, we have r
 eached the maximum number of kids under 12 that we accept into the program 
 this semester. The minimum age to register is now 12 years old.&nbsp\;<br><
 br>If you registered by Sept 15\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in 
 the program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdo
 or 2.&nbsp\;<br><br>If you are not yet 12\, and you registered and paid aft
 er Sept 15\, your fee will be returned to you.<br><br>ap = accessories pack
 et (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 
 2. ($15)<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but rea
 lly needed to practice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end
  of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we did not finish
  a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, be
 cause it has been averaged by taking your recorded score from your scorecar
 d\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and
  then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round score. After the last clas
 s on the weekend\, final scores will also be sent to all Outdoor 1 particip
 ants in an email with more information before your next class.
