DESCRIPTION:REGISTER NOW !<br>More information and registration form availa
 ble on&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrai
 ningcenter.com</a>.<br>Sign up for just one Outdoor 1 class\, because most 
 people graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br
 ><br>Your name will be added below and your place reserved after we receive
  3 things:&nbsp\; REGISTRATION + WAIVERS + FEE<br>Adults do not need a mini
 mum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br>Juniors need a min. score of 50 pt
 s in one 30-arrow round.<br><br><b>Registered archers: at 9m&nbsp\;</b><br>
 <b>Target nos:</b><br>1A. Olivier G.\, adult - pd - share - R68 - <b>232 pt
 s </b>-&gt\; Outdoor 3 - <b>Wow! Congrats!</b><br>1B. Cristina G.\, adult -
  pd - share - R68 - <b>56 pts</b><br>2. Keri W.\, adult - pd - R66 - <b>56 
 pts</b><br>3A. Arik Y.\, dad - pd - share - R68 - <b>77 pts</b><br>3B. Yuva
 l Y.\, 12 - pd - share - R62 - <b>70 pts</b>&nbsp\;-&gt\; Outdoor 2 - Great
  job!<br>4. Lital Y.\, mom - pd - share - L62 - <b>47 pts</b><br>5. Shahar 
 Y. 14 - pd - share - R62 -&nbsp\;<b>80 pts</b>&nbsp\;-&gt\; Outdoor 2 - Awe
 some!<br>6A. Alok S.\, adult - pd - share - R66 - <b>113 pts</b><br>6B. Cha
 nda S.\, adult - pd - share - R62 - <b>38 pts</b><br>7. Andrew B.\, adult -
  pd - share - R68 - <b>125 pts</b><br>8. Casey D.\, adult - pd - share - L6
 2 - <b>49 pts</b><br>9.&nbsp\;. Audrey B.\, adult - pd - share - R62 - <b>4
 0 pts</b><br>10. Gavin R.\, 12 - pd - share - R54 - <b>78 pts</b>&nbsp\;-&g
 t\; Outdoor 2 - Excellent! - Winner of Unfair Games<br><br>Space will be li
 mited to 10-15 archers per session depending on the number of family groups
  in attendance or in accordance with CDC Guidelines.&nbsp\;<br>Each person 
 will have a target stand\, except after 10 people have registered\, two mem
 bers from the same family will share one target stand.<br>The archer and a 
 maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field until further notice 
 or approved by Coach Racae. Parents can sign up as an archer or watch as a 
 spectator.<br><br>As of Sept 15\, we have reached the maximum number of kid
 s under 12 that we accept into the program this semester. The minimum age t
 o register is now 12 years old.&nbsp\;<br><br>If you registered by Sept 15\
 , and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take other Outdo
 or 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;<br><br>If you are n
 ot yet 12\, and you registered and paid after Sept 15\, your fee will be re
 turned to you.<br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times
  before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it 
 as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adul
 ts don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = acces
 sories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed f
 or Outdoor 2. ($15)<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, optio
 nal but really needed to practice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br
 >At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we did
  not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final
  score\, because it has been averaged by taking your recorded score from yo
 ur scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot to get an arrow av
 erage\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round score. After th
 e last class on the weekend\, final scores will also be sent to all Outdoor
  1 participants in an email with more information before your next class.
