DESCRIPTION:REGISTER NOW !<br>More information and registration form availa
 ble on&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrai
 ningcenter.com</a>.<br>Sign up for just one Outdoor 1 class\, because most 
 people graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br
 ><br>Your name will be added below and your place reserved after we receive
  your registration form\, waivers\, AND fee.<br><br>Juniors may need to tak
 e Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by s
 coring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/e
 nd of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br><br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate
  into Outdoor 2.<br><br>Registered archers:<br><b>Target nos:</b><br>1A. <b
 >Keith</b> M.\, dad - 66 pts -&gt\; Outdoor 2<br>1B. <b>Franklin</b> M.\, 9
  - 104 pts -&gt\; Outdoor 2<br>2A.&nbsp\;<b>Brandi</b> H.\, mom - 38 pts -&
 gt\; Outdoor 2<br>2B. <b>Norah</b> F.\, 8 - 25 pts - repeat Outdoor 1<br>3.
 &nbsp\; &nbsp\;<b>Emma</b> S.\, 8 - 28 pts - repeat Outdoor 1<br>4A. <b>Sta
 cy</b> D.L.\, mom -&gt\; Outdoor 2<br>4B. <b>Len</b>a L.\, 9 - 37 pts - rep
 eat Outdoor 1<br>4.&nbsp\; &nbsp\;Carol S.\, adult - DNA<br>5A. <b>Adam B</
 b>.\, dad - <b>108 pts </b>-&gt\; Outdoor 2<br>5B. <b>Ethan B.</b>\, 8 - re
 peat Outdoor 1<br>6..&nbsp\; <b>Victoria H</b>.\, adult - <b>50 pts&nbsp\;<
 /b>-&gt\; Outdoor 2<br>7.&nbsp\; &nbsp\;<b>John B.</b>\, adult - <b>138 pts
 &nbsp\;</b>-&gt\; Outdoor 2<br>8.&nbsp\; <b>&nbsp\;Kelly V</b>.\, adult - <
 b>24 pts&nbsp\;</b>-&gt\; Outdoor 2<br>9.&nbsp\; &nbsp\;<b>Mariah L</b>.\, 
 adult - <b>14 pts&nbsp\;</b>-&gt\; Outdoor 2<br>10. <b>Bryson</b> H.\, adul
 t - <b>40 pts&nbsp\;</b>-&gt\; Outdoor 2<br><br>Space will be limited to a 
 maximum of 10-15 archers per session depending on the number of family grou
 ps in attendance or in accordance with CDC Guidelines.&nbsp\;<br>Each perso
 n will have a target stand\, except after 10 people have registered\, two m
 embers from the same family will share one target stand.<br>The archer and 
 a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field until further notic
 e or approved by Coach Racae. Parents can sign up as an archer or watch as 
 a spectator.<br><br>As of Sept 15\, we have reached the maximum number of k
 ids under 12 that we accept into the program this semester. The minimum age
  to register is now 12 years old.&nbsp\;<br><br>If you registered by Sept 1
 5\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take other Out
 door 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;<br><br>If you are
  not yet 12\, and you registered and paid after Sept 15\, your fee will be 
 returned to you.<br><br>ap = purchased accessories packet\, which will be n
 eeded for Outdoor 2.<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your score
 s will be posted below. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\,
  you may not recognize your final score\, because it has been averaged by t
 aking your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the number of a
 rrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to
  get a full round score. After the last class on the weekend\, all final sc
 ores will additionally be sent to you in an email with other information be
 fore your next class.
