 trainingcenter.com">www.archerytrainingcenter.com</a>.)<br><br>OPEN to Juni
 ors/Parents/Adults in<br>INDOOR 2 (9m) and<br>INDOOR 3A (13.5m) and<br>INDO
 OR 3B/4/5/6+ (18m)<br><br>Enrollment links at: <a href="http://www.archeryt
 rainingcenter.com/Classes">http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/Classes</a>
 <br><br>Fees: <br>RECREATIONAL: <br>$20/cl for 1 hr\; $30/cl for 2 hrs\; $4
 0/cl for 3 hrs ON THE SAME DAY.<br>There are also reduced Monthly fees when
  you regularly come to more than 3 hrs/week and Progressive fees when you a
 re at 18m and regularly come to more than 5 hrs/week. Ask Coach Racae for m
 ore information.<br>&nbsp\;<br>Your name will be on the list below when we 
 receive your registration form and fee in advance of the class. When you at
 tend\, and the class is near full\, you should pay at least one class in ad
 vance to guarantee you have a place on the shooting line next time. <br><br
 >When classes are not full\, it's okay to just drop in occasionally for the
  class and pay at that time. However it is difficult to tell how many peopl
 e will be dropping in\, so to secure your place\, it is better to register 
 and pay in advance to prevent overcrowding. We can only take 10 people on t
 he shooting line at one time. <br><br>When we have more than 10 archers\, w
 e will form a second line\, as in a tournament\, which will reduce the numb
 er of arrows shot per person within the time. (You can see the actual atten
