DESCRIPTION:<table><tbody><tr><td><br><b><i>18 classes and all entered regi
 strations for Outdoor 3-9 classes were mysteriously cancelled/erased early 
 on Fri 4/25\, so please re-enter your attendance below\, and PLEASE be very
  careful entering data into the calendar so classes and registrations are n
 ot erased!!!</i></b><br><b><br></b><br><b>Registration form: </b><a href="h
 ttps://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfx1RyOwd314Q4zXYiQ9rb_a3oe84E9dIYs
 8CN35Ginmevfpg/viewform?usp=preview" target="_blank">OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-7
 0m</a><br><br><b>Add your name to Target Assignment List below or send in t
 he above completed form.</b><br><br><i>Focus primarily on <br></i><ul><li><
 i>perfecting your form\, </i></li><li><i>slowly increasing your physical st
 rength and draw weight\, </i></li><li><i>strengthening your mental program\
 , </i></li><li><i>determining your average and personal best\, </i></li><li
 ><i>understanding the spread between the two\, and working on closing it.</
 i></li></ul><b>You need your own equipment </b><br>Competition recurve bow\
 , sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar a
 ssembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\,
  hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not b
 e added until you reach a higher level\, but you should order them in advan
 ce.) <br><br>Wear your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br><i>When you score 288
  pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the 
 next distance until you reach your competition distance</i><br><i>If you tr
 ained outdoors in the 2024 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance 
 you shot.</i><br><i>Target arrangements may vary each session\, depending o
 n who attends and distances needed.</i><br><b>Target 1 at 70m (U21 + Senior
 s</b> competition distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use it fo
 r independent practice in between classes.<br><b>Target 2 at 60m (U18 + Mas
 ters</b> competition distance) <br><b>Target 3 at 50m</b><br><b>Target 4+5 
 at 40m</b> (<b>U15</b> competition distance) <br><b>Targets 6+7+8 at 30m</b
 > <span>(</span><b>U13</b><span> </span><span>competition distance) </span>
 <br><b>Target  9 at 20m </b>(for those who have shot at 18m indoors or with
  Coach Racae's approval)<br><b>Targets 10 at 13.5m</b> (for those who have 
 just graduated from indoors at 9m)<br><br>Ideally\, we want to practice wit
 h two archers/target to replicate competition conditions as much as possibl
 e.<br><br><b>Target Assignments:</b><br>Targets are assigned outdoors in ad
 vance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\,<br>so add your name next t
 o your distance below. <br>If you need help or have questions\, email/text 
 Coach Racae<br><i>(Dotted lines represent tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6
 \, and 9.)</i><br>------------------------------<wbr />----<br>1A. (70m)<br
 >1B<br><br>2A. (60m)  <br>2B<br><br>3A. (50m)  <br>------------------------
 ------<wbr />----<br>3B<br><br>4A. (40m) <br>4B<br>------------------------
 ------<wbr />----<br>5A. (40m)<br>5B. <br><br>6A. (30m)<br>----------------
 --------------<wbr />----<br>6B. <br><br>7A. (30m)<br>7B. <br>-------------
 -----------------<wbr />---- <br>8A. (30m)<br>8B. <br><br>9A. (20m)<br>----
 --------------------------<wbr />----<br>9B. <br><br>10A. (13.5m)<br>10B</t
 d></tr><tr><td><time></time><br></td></tr></tbody></table>
