DESCRIPTION:REGISTER NOW !<br>More information and registration form availa
 ble on&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrai
 ningcenter.com</a>.<br>Sign up for just one Outdoor 1 class\, because most 
 people graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br
 ><br>Your name will be added below and your place reserved after we receive
  3 things:&nbsp\; REGISTRATION + WAIVERS + FEE<br><br><b>Registered archers
 :</b><br><b>Target nos:</b><br>1. Lidia G.\, adult - pd <b>55 pts</b><br>2.
  Michael H.\, adult - pd - 66R <b>106 pts</b><br>3. Michelle L.\, adult - p
 d - 62R <b>31 pts</b><br>4A. Benjamin P.\, adult - pd - share - 68R - <b>14
 2 pts</b><br>4B Stephanie P.\, adult - pd - share 62R - <b>75 pts</b><br>5.
  Mac S.\, adult - pd - 66R <b>135 pts</b><br>6. Sarah R.\, adult - pd - 66L
  <b>4 pts</b><br>7. Laxmi P.\, adult - pd <b>64 pts</b><br>8. Karan S.\, ad
 ult - pd - 66R - <b>DNA</b><br>9. Mitchell G.\, adult - pd - 66L <b>63 pts<
 /b><br>10. Jefferson Y.\, adult - pd - 68R <b>134 pts</b><table><colgroup><
 col></colgroup><tbody><tr><td><br><b>Waiting List:</b></td></tr><tr><td><br
 ></td></tr></tbody></table>Space will be limited to 10-15 archers per sessi
 on depending on the number of family groups in attendance or in accordance 
 with CDC Guidelines.&nbsp\;<br>Each person will have a target stand\, excep
 t after 10 people have registered\, two members from the same family will s
 hare one target stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be
  allowed on the field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae. Pare
 nts can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator.<br><br>As of Sept 15\
 , we have reached the maximum number of kids under 12 that we accept into t
 he program this semester. The minimum age to register is now 12 years old.&
 nbsp\;<br><br>If you registered by Sept 15\, and are younger than 12\, you´
 ll stay in the program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later
  join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;<br><br>If you are not yet 12\, and you registered a
 nd paid after Sept 15\, your fee will be returned to you.<br><br>Juniors ma
 y need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying to get into O
 utdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on average 
 about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to
  graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, finger
 tab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($15)<br>fp = form
  pack (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but really needed to practic
 e form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 cl
 ass\, your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30
  arrows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, because it has been ave
 raged by taking your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the n
 umber of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying tha
 t by 30 to get a full round score. After the last class on the weekend\, fi
 nal scores will also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with
  more information before your next class.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260517T064558Z
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:FULL !! OUTDOOR 1 - First-time Class - FULL!!
TRANSP:OPAQUE
