CREATED:20210711T054416Z
DESCRIPTION:REGISTER NOW !<br>More information and registration form availa
 ble on&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrai
 ningcenter.com</a>.<br>Sign up for just one Outdoor 1 class\, because most 
 people graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br
 ><br>Your name will be added below and your place reserved after we receive
  3 things:&nbsp\; REGISTRATION + WAIVERS + FEE<br><br><b>Registered archers
 :</b><br><b>Target nos:</b><br>1. Joe S.\, adult - pd - <b>175 pts - Wow!</
 b><br>2. Kali R.\, adult - pd - <b>37 pts (</b>corrected)<br>3. Jonah L.\, 
 adult - pd - <b>41 pts</b><br>4. Sarah L.\, adult - pd - <b>26 pts</b><br>5
 . Chris S.\, adult - pd - <b>73 pts</b><br>6.&nbsp\;<br>7.<br>8.<br>9.<br>1
 0.<br><br><br>Space will be limited to 10-15 archers per session depending 
 on the number of family groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC Guid
 elines.&nbsp\;<br>Each person will have a target stand\, except after 10 pe
 ople have registered\, two members from the same family will share one targ
 et stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on t
 he field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae. Parents can sign 
 up as an archer or watch as a spectator.<br><br>As of Sept 15\, we have rea
 ched the maximum number of kids under 12 that we accept into the program th
 is semester. The minimum age to register is now 12 years old.&nbsp\;<br><br
 >If you registered by Sept 15\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in th
 e program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor
  2.&nbsp\;<br><br>If you are not yet 12\, and you registered and paid after
  Sept 15\, your fee will be returned to you.<br><br>Juniors may need to tak
 e Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by s
 coring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/e
 nd of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate int
 o Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingers
 ling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($15)<br>fp = form pack (stretc
 hband and string loop)\, optional but really needed to practice form\, warm
  up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your sc
 ores will be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, yo
 u may not recognize your final score\, because it has been averaged by taki
 ng your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arro
 ws you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to ge
 t a full round score. After the last class on the weekend\, final scores wi
 ll also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more informa
 tion before your next class.
