DESCRIPTION:Coach Racae (Recurves only)\n\nPREREQUISITES:\nADULT TRAINING a
 t 9m\nINDOOR 1: First-time Class: Click the Sign Up button at the top of ww
 w.archerytrainingcenter.com\nSaturdays: 11:00am-1:30pm (Fee: $25/cl)\nSunda
 ys: 11:00am-1:30pm (Fee: $25/cl)\n\nENROLLMENT LINKS at:\nhttp://www.archer
 ytrainingcenter.com/news\n\nATTENDEES TONIGHT: (Paid in advance)\n1. Daniel
  H. (18m)\n2. Adrian (18m)\n3. Melissa (18m)\n4. Odin C. (9m)\n5. Steven H.
  (18m)\n6. Lalithya (13.5m)\n7. Dave C. (13.5m)\n8. Christopher C. (13.5m)\
 n9. Suzanne J. (9m)\n10. Michael G.\n\nADULT RECREATIONAL CLASSES at Indoor
  3A-5 and distances (13.5m\, 18m)\n\nPER CLASS FEE: $20/HR \nSundays: 6:00-
 7:00pm \nTuesdays: 7:30-8:30pm \n\nMONTHLY FEES for ADULTS at 18m :\n\nAdul
 t classes ONLY at 18m (Tues 7:30-8:30 + Sun 6:00-7:00):\n(Based on coming 6
  hrs/month. If there are 6 hrs or fewer in the month\, the monthly fees are
  $20/hr.)\nJAN   $ 120 (8 one-hour classes)\nFEB   $ 120  (8 one-hour class
 es)\nMAR  $ 120 (8 one-hour classes)\nAPR   $ 120 (8 one-hour classes)\nMAY
    $ 120 (7 one-hour classes)\n\nAdult classes + Wed. 6:30-8:00 at 18m:\nJA
 N   $ 188 (12.5 hrs available)\nFEB   $ 210 (14 hrs available) \nMAR   $ 23
 3 (15.5 hrs available)\nAPR   $ 210 (14 hrs available)\nMAY   $  210 (14 hr
 s available)\n\nPROGRESSIVE PROGRAM Indoor at 18m\nTraining for those who w
 ant to progress faster towards competitive archery by meeting minimum atten
 dance requirements. (8.5 hrs/week available)\nSaturdays 3:30-5:30pm\nSunday
 s:  3:30-5:30pm \nSundays:  6:00-7:00pm (Adults and Indoor 5 only)\nTuesday
 s: 6:30-7:30pm \nTuesdays: 7:30-8:30pm (Adults and Indoor 5 only) \nWednesd
 ays: 6:30-8:00pm \n\nPROGRESSIVE WEEKLY FEES (after meeting previous week's
  attendance requirement):\nIndoor 3A at 13.5m: $TBD/wk (min. 4 hrs)\nIndoor
  3B at 18m:    $TBD/wk (min. 5 hrs)\nIndoor 4 at 18m:      $TBD/wk (min. 6 
 hrs)\nIndoor 5 at 18m:      $TBD/wk (min. 8 hrs)\n\nUSA Archery's Adult Tra
 ining Program (ATP) follows a similar path to the Junior Olympic Archery De
 velopment (JOAD) program. \n\nYour first step is to take an Indoor 1: First
 -time Class for Adults. Just click the link or the Sign Up button at the to
 p of this website.\n\nEveryone starts out in our Recreational program at 9 
 meters. As you improve you progress to 13.5 meters then on to 18 meters ind
 oors. \n\nWe welcome adult recurve and compound Olympic target archers at a
 ll levels of experience. \nRecurve archers attend any of the group classes 
 above or book private lessons with Coach Racae or Instructor Dale.\nCompoun
 d archers book private lessons with Coach Dan.\n\nWhen you decide that you 
 are interested in competing you'll apply to join USA Archery Level 4 NTS an
 d JDT Coach Alex Meyer's Competitive Archery Program (CAP).\n\nExperienced 
 competitive archers need to be evaluated by Coach Racae for advanced placem
 ent in either the Progressive Program or recommendation to the Competitive 
 Archery Program with Coach Alex.\n\nJoin with Google Hangouts: https://plus
 .google.com/hangouts/_/calendar/M2NkdGhhdDVxNGhmcmcwMGtyYWZ1NGJ0NmtAZ3JvdXA
 uY2FsZW5kYXIuZ29vZ2xlLmNvbQ.r5oo7pf4arjc75j71sh4f2kh4s?hs=121
