DESCRIPTION:Coach Racae (Recurves only)\nADULT RECREATIONAL CLASSES at Indo
 or 3A-5 and distances 13.5m\, 18m\n\nPREREQUISITES:\nADULT TRAINING at 9m\n
 INDOOR 1: First-time Class: Click the Sign Up button at the top of www.arch
 erytrainingcenter.com\nSaturdays: 11:00am-1:30pm (Fee: $25/cl)\nSundays: 11
 :00am-1:30pm (Fee: $25/cl)\n\nENROLLMENT LINKS at:\nhttp://www.archerytrain
 ingcenter.com/news\n\nATTENDEES TONIGHT: (Paid in advance)\n1. Daniel H. (1
 8m)\n2. Adrian (18m)\n3. Melissa (18m)\n4. Michael G. (18m)\n5. Steven H. (
 18m)\n6. Lalithya (13.5m)\n7. Dave C. (13.5m)\n8. Christopher C. (13.5m)\n9
 .\n10.\n\nPER CLASS FEE: $20/HR \nSundays: 6:00-7:00pm \nTuesdays: 7:30-8:3
 0pm \n\nMONTHLY FEES for ADULTS at 18m :\n\nAdult classes ONLY at 18m (Tues
  7:30-8:30 + Sun 6:00-7:00):\n(Based on coming 6 hrs/month. If there are 6 
 hrs or fewer in the month\, the monthly fees are $20/hr.)\nJAN   $ 120 (8 o
 ne-hour classes)\nFEB   $ 120  (8 one-hour classes)\nMAR  $ 120 (8 one-hour
  classes)\nAPR   $ 120 (8 one-hour classes)\nMAY   $ 120 (7 one-hour classe
 s)\n\nAdult classes + Wed. 6:30-8:00 at 18m:\nJAN   $ 188 (12.5 hrs availab
 le)\nFEB   $ 210 (14 hrs available) \nMAR   $ 233 (15.5 hrs available)\nAPR
    $ 210 (14 hrs available)\nMAY   $  210 (14 hrs available)\n\nPROGRESSIVE
  PROGRAM Indoor at 18m\nTraining for those who want to progress faster towa
 rds competitive archery by meeting minimum attendance requirements. (8.5 hr
 s/week available)\nSaturdays 3:30-5:30pm\nSundays:  3:30-5:30pm \nSundays: 
  6:00-7:00pm (Adults and Indoor 5 only)\nTuesdays: 6:30-7:30pm \nTuesdays: 
 7:30-8:30pm (Adults and Indoor 5 only) \nWednesdays: 6:30-8:00pm \n\nPROGRE
 SSIVE WEEKLY FEES (after meeting previous week's attendance requirement):\n
 Indoor 3A at 13.5m: $TBD/wk (min. 4 hrs)\nIndoor 3B at 18m:    $TBD/wk (min
 . 5 hrs)\nIndoor 4 at 18m:      $TBD/wk (min. 6 hrs)\nIndoor 5 at 18m:     
  $TBD/wk (min. 8 hrs)\n\nUSA Archery's Adult Training Program (ATP) follows
  a similar path to the Junior Olympic Archery Development (JOAD) program. \
 n\nYour first step is to take an Indoor 1: First-time Class for Adults. Jus
 t click the link or the Sign Up button at the top of this website.\n\nEvery
 one starts out in our Recreational program at 9 meters. As you improve you 
 progress to 13.5 meters then on to 18 meters indoors. \n\nWe welcome adult 
 recurve and compound Olympic target archers at all levels of experience. \n
 Recurve archers attend any of the group classes above or book private lesso
 ns with Coach Racae or Instructor Dale.\nCompound archers book private less
 ons with Coach Dan.\n\nWhen you decide that you are interested in competing
  you'll apply to join USA Archery Level 4 NTS and JDT Coach Alex Meyer's Co
 mpetitive Archery Program (CAP).\n\nExperienced competitive archers need to
  be evaluated by Coach Racae for advanced placement in either the Progressi
 ve Program or recommendation to the Competitive Archery Program with Coach 
 Alex.\n\nJoin with Google Hangouts: https://plus.google.com/hangouts/_/cale
 ndar/M2NkdGhhdDVxNGhmcmcwMGtyYWZ1NGJ0NmtAZ3JvdXAuY2FsZW5kYXIuZ29vZ2xlLmNvbQ
 .r5oo7pf4arjc75j71sh4f2kh4s?hs=121
