CREATED:20210711T054416Z
DESCRIPTION:REGISTER NOW !<br>More information and registration form availa
 ble on&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrai
 ningcenter.com</a>.<br>Sign up for just one Outdoor 1 class\, because most 
 people graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br
 ><br>Your name will be added below and your place reserved after we receive
  3 things:&nbsp\; REGISTRATION + WAIVERS + FEE<br><br><b>Registered archers
 :</b><br><b>Target nos:</b><br>1. Kris T.\, adult - pd<br>2. Alejandro C.L.
 D.\, adult - <b>31 pts</b><br>3. Devonte\, adult - pd - DNA ill - substitut
 e<br>4. Robert G.\, adult -<b>96 pts</b><br>5. Liz B.\, adult - <b>39 pts</
 b><br>6. Milo R.\, 13 - <b>144 pts </b>(corrected) -&gt\; <b>Outdoor 2</b><
 br>7A. Zach S.\, 13 -&nbsp\; 66¨ bow - <b>36 pts </b>(corrected) -&gt\; <b>
 Outdoor 1</b><br>7B. Matt S.\, dad - 68¨ bow - <b>53 pts</b><br>8.&nbsp\; &
 nbsp\;David L.\, adult - <b>140 pts</b><br>9.<br>10.<br><br><br>Space will 
 be limited to 10-15 archers per session depending on the number of family g
 roups in attendance or in accordance with CDC Guidelines.&nbsp\;<br>Each pe
 rson will have a target stand\, except after 10 people have registered\, tw
 o members from the same family will share one target stand.<br>The archer a
 nd a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field until further no
 tice or approved by Coach Racae. Parents can sign up as an archer or watch 
 as a spectator.<br><br>As of Sept 15\, we have reached the maximum number o
 f kids under 12 that we accept into the program this semester. The minimum 
 age to register is now 12 years old.&nbsp\;<br><br>If you registered by Sep
 t 15\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take other 
 Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;<br><br>If you 
 are not yet 12\, and you registered and paid after Sept 15\, your fee will 
 be returned to you.<br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three 
 times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll mak
 e it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br
 >Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = 
 accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be nee
 ded for Outdoor 2. ($15)<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, 
 optional but really needed to practice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<b
 r><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If w
 e did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your 
 final score\, because it has been averaged by taking your recorded score fr
 om your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot to get an arr
 ow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round score. Aft
 er the last class on the weekend\, final scores will also be sent to all Ou
 tdoor 1 participants in an email with more information before your next cla
 ss.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260517T064558Z
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:OUTDOOR 1 - First-time Class
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
