DESCRIPTION:REGISTER NOW !<br>More information and registration form availa
 ble on&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrai
 ningcenter.com</a>.<br>Sign up for just one Outdoor 1 class\, because most 
 people graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br
 ><br>Your name will be added below and your place reserved after we receive
  3 things:&nbsp\; REGISTRATION + WAIVERS + FEE<br><br>Registered archers:<b
 r><b>Target Nos.:</b><br>1A. Brandon S.\, dad - <b>34 pts</b><br>1B.. Bonha
 m D.\, 9 - pd - <b>40 pts - repeat Outdoor 1</b><br>2. Asra A.\, adult - <b
 >153 pts</b><br>3. Josh H.\, adult - <b>23 pts</b><br>4. Victoria T.\, 19 -
  <b>23 pts</b><br>5. Max D.\, 12 - <b>106 pts</b><br>6.&nbsp\;<br>7.<br>8.<
 br>9.<br>10.<br><br>Space will be limited to a maximum of 10-15 archers per
  session depending on the number of family groups in attendance or in accor
 dance with CDC Guidelines.&nbsp\;<br>Each person will have a target stand\,
  except after 10 people have registered\, two members from the same family 
 will share one target stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator w
 ill be allowed on the field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae
 . Parents can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator.<br><br>As of Se
 pt 15\, we have reached the maximum number of kids under 12 that we accept 
 into the program this semester. The minimum age to register is now 12 years
  old.&nbsp\;<br><br>If you registered by Sept 15\, and are younger than 12\
 , you´ll stay in the program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and
  later join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;<br><br>If you are not yet 12\, and you regist
 ered and paid after Sept 15\, your fee will be returned to you.<br>Juniors 
 may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying to get into
  Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on averag
 e about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score 
 to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fing
 ertab\, fingersling)\, purchased\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2.<br>f
 p = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, purchased\, optional but real
 ly needed to practice form\, warm up before classes $4.00<br><br>At the end
  of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we did not finish
  a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, be
 cause it has been averaged by taking your recorded score from your scorecar
 d\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and
  then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round score. After the last clas
 s on the weekend\, all final scores will also be sent to all Outdoor 1 part
 icipates in an email with more information before your next class.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260517T064558Z
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:OUTDOOR 1 - First-time Class
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
