DESCRIPTION:Coach Racae (Recurves only)\nADULT RECREATIONAL CLASSES at Indo
 or 3A-5 and distances 13.5m\, 18m\n\nPREREQUISITES:\nADULT TRAINING at 9m\n
 INDOOR 1: First-time Class: Click the Sign Up button at the top of www.arch
 erytrainingcenter.com\nSaturdays: 11:00am-1:30pm (Fee: $25/cl)\nSundays: 11
 :00am-1:30pm (Fee: $25/cl)\n\nENROLLMENT LINKS at:\nhttp://www.archerytrain
 ingcenter.com/news\n\nATTENDEES TONIGHT: (Paid in advance)\n1. Daniel H. (1
 8m)\n2. Adrian (18m)\n3. Melissa (18m)\n4. Michael G. (18m)\n5. Steven H. (
 18m)\n6. Lalithya (13.5m)\n7. Dave C. (13.5m)\n8. Christopher C. (13.5m)\n9
 . Odin C.\, 9m\n10. \n\nPER CLASS FEE: $20/HR \nSundays: 6:00-7:00pm \nTues
 days: 7:30-8:30pm \n\nMONTHLY FEES for ADULTS at 18m :\n\nAdult classes ONL
 Y at 18m (Tues 7:30-8:30 + Sun 6:00-7:00):\n(Based on coming 6 hrs/month. I
 f there are 6 hrs or fewer in the month\, the monthly fees are $20/hr.)\nJA
 N   $ 120 (8 one-hour classes)\nFEB   $ 120  (8 one-hour classes)\nMAR  $ 1
 20 (8 one-hour classes)\nAPR   $ 120 (8 one-hour classes)\nMAY   $ 120 (7 o
 ne-hour classes)\n\nAdult classes + Wed. 6:30-8:00 at 18m:\nJAN   $ 188 (12
 .5 hrs available)\nFEB   $ 210 (14 hrs available) \nMAR   $ 233 (15.5 hrs a
 vailable)\nAPR   $ 210 (14 hrs available)\nMAY   $  210 (14 hrs available)\
 n\nPROGRESSIVE PROGRAM Indoor at 18m\nTraining for those who want to progre
 ss faster towards competitive archery by meeting minimum attendance require
 ments. (8.5 hrs/week available)\nSaturdays 3:30-5:30pm\nSundays:  3:30-5:30
 pm \nSundays:  6:00-7:00pm (Adults and Indoor 5 only)\nTuesdays: 6:30-7:30p
 m \nTuesdays: 7:30-8:30pm (Adults and Indoor 5 only) \nWednesdays: 6:30-8:0
 0pm \n\nPROGRESSIVE WEEKLY FEES (after meeting previous week's attendance r
 equirement):\nIndoor 3A at 13.5m: $TBD/wk (min. 4 hrs)\nIndoor 3B at 18m:  
   $TBD/wk (min. 5 hrs)\nIndoor 4 at 18m:      $TBD/wk (min. 6 hrs)\nIndoor 
 5 at 18m:      $TBD/wk (min. 8 hrs)\n\nUSA Archery's Adult Training Program
  (ATP) follows a similar path to the Junior Olympic Archery Development (JO
 AD) program. \n\nYour first step is to take an Indoor 1: First-time Class f
 or Adults. Just click the link or the Sign Up button at the top of this web
 site.\n\nEveryone starts out in our Recreational program at 9 meters. As yo
 u improve you progress to 13.5 meters then on to 18 meters indoors. \n\nWe 
 welcome adult recurve and compound Olympic target archers at all levels of 
 experience. \nRecurve archers attend any of the group classes above or book
  private lessons with Coach Racae or Instructor Dale.\nCompound archers boo
 k private lessons with Coach Dan.\n\nWhen you decide that you are intereste
 d in competing you'll apply to join USA Archery Level 4 NTS and JDT Coach A
 lex Meyer's Competitive Archery Program (CAP).\n\nExperienced competitive a
 rchers need to be evaluated by Coach Racae for advanced placement in either
  the Progressive Program or recommendation to the Competitive Archery Progr
 am with Coach Alex.\n\nJoin with Google Hangouts: https://plus.google.com/h
 angouts/_/calendar/M2NkdGhhdDVxNGhmcmcwMGtyYWZ1NGJ0NmtAZ3JvdXAuY2FsZW5kYXIu
 Z29vZ2xlLmNvbQ.r5oo7pf4arjc75j71sh4f2kh4s?hs=121
LAST-MODIFIED:20260513T121423Z
LOCATION:10203 OLD Manchaca Rd.\, Austin\, TX 78748
