DESCRIPTION:Registration form: 2024 OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m<br><br>Target 
 Assignments:<br><br>Targets 1 and 2 should always stay at 70m or reversed s
 o Jake can shoot.<br>Target 3 at 60m<br>Target 4 at 40m<br>Targets 5+6 at 3
 0m<br>Targets 7-10 will move to18m starting 8/17. Archers at 20m will now s
 hoot at 18m.<br><br>If necessary\, Target #6 can move to 18m when Targets #
 7-10 are full with two archers/target at 18m.<br>When you shoot at 18m to p
 ractice for the Aggie Invitational in Nov\, you'll be on a 40-cm target fac
 e\, set up 4 to a target (even if only one or two archers are on that targe
 t). <br>You should practice one round of 30 arrows at each target face high
 /low/left/right so you are prepared for your target assignment at the indoo
 r competitions<br><br>Ideally\, we want to practice with at least two arche
 rs/target to replicate competition conditions as much as possible.<br>You c
 an decide each week if you want to shoot at your long distance or at 18m an
 d add or move your name on the calendar accordingly. You should alternate d
 istance each day\, so you practice both. <br>Starting Oct 1 to the Nov Aggi
 e Invitational and Jan 1 for the Feb Indoor Nationals\, everyone should be 
 shooting at 18m and scoring to determine their average and their personal b
 ests\, understand the spread between the two\, and working on closing it.<b
