 ule make up<br>9B. <b>Yuval Y.</b>\, 12 - DNA - illness in family - schedul
 e make up<br>10A. <b>Lital Y.</b>\, parent - DNA - illness in family - sche
 dule make up<br>10B. <b>Shahar Y.\,</b> 14 - DNA - illness in family - sche
 dule make up<br><br><br>Space will be limited to 10-15 archers per session 
 depending on the number of family groups in attendance or in accordance wit
 h CDC Guidelines.&nbsp\;<br>Each person will have a target stand\, except a
 fter 10 people have registered\, two members from the same family will shar
 e one target stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be al
 lowed on the field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae. Parents
  can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator.<br><br>As of Sept 15\, w
 e have reached the maximum number of kids under 12 that we accept into the 
 program this semester. The minimum age to register is now 12 years old.&nbs
 p\;<br><br>If you registered by Sept 15\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll 
 stay in the program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later jo
 in Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;<br><br>If you are not yet 12\, and you registered and 
 paid after Sept 15\, your fee will be returned to you.<br><br>Juniors may n
 eed to take Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying to get into Outd
 oor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on average abo
 ut 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to gr
 aduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab
 \, fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($15)<br>fp = form pa
 ck (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but really needed to practice f
 orm\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class
 \, your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 ar
 rows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, because it has been averag
 ed by taking your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the numb
 er of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that b
 y 30 to get a full round score. After the last class on the weekend\, final
  scores will also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with mo
 re information before your next class.
