DESCRIPTION:REGISTER NOW !<br>More information and registration form availa
 ble on&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrai
 ningcenter.com</a>.<br>Sign up for just one Outdoor 1 class\, because most 
 people graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br
 ><br>Your name will be added below and your place reserved after we receive
  3 things:&nbsp\; REGISTRATION + WAIVERS + FEE<br><br><b>Registered archers
  </b>at 9m on 40-cm target face unless otherwise noted<b>:</b><br><b>Target
  nos:</b><br>1. Ashlynn L.\, 12 - pd - on 60-cm target face - <b>73 pts -&g
 t\; Outdoor 2 - Congratulations</b><br>2. Nora L.\, 12 - pd - on 60-cm targ
 et face - <b>40 pts </b>(corrected)<br>3. Gianna G.\, 12 - pd - on 60-cm ta
 rget face - DNP<br>4. Cheyenne E.\, 12 - pd - on 60-cm target face - <b>16 
 pts</b><br>5. Penelope W.\, 12 - pd - on 60-cm target face - <b>16 pts</b><
 br>6. Antonio V.\, adult - pd - <b>41 pts </b>(corrected)<br>7.<br>8.<br>9.
 <br>10.<br><br><br>Space will be limited to 10-15 archers per session depen
 ding on the number of family groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC
  Guidelines.&nbsp\;<br>Each person will have a target stand\, except after 
 10 people have registered\, two members from the same family will share one
  target stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed
  on the field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae. Parents can 
 sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator.<br><br>As of Sept 15\, we hav
 e reached the maximum number of kids under 12 that we accept into the progr
 am this semester. The minimum age to register is now 12 years old.&nbsp\;<b
 r><br>If you registered by Sept 15\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay 
 in the program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Ou
 tdoor 2.&nbsp\;<br><br>If you are not yet 12\, and you registered and paid 
 after Sept 15\, your fee will be returned to you.<br><br>Juniors may need t
 o take Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2
  by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 
 pts/end of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduat
 e into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fi
 ngersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($15)<br>fp = form pack (s
 tretchband and string loop)\, optional but really needed to practice form\,
  warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, yo
 ur scores will be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)
 \, you may not recognize your final score\, because it has been averaged by
  taking your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the number of
  arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 
 to get a full round score. After the last class on the weekend\, final scor
 es will also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more in
 formation before your next class.
