 istration form and fee in advance of the class. When you attend\, and the c
 lass is near full\, you should pay at least one class in advance to guarant
 ee you have a place on the shooting line next time. <br><br>When classes ar
 e not full\, it's okay to just drop in occasionally for the class and pay a
 t that time. However it is difficult to tell how many people will be droppi
 ng in\, so to secure your place\, it is better to register and pay in advan
 ce to prevent overcrowding. We can only take 10 people on the shooting line
  at one time. <br><br>When we have more than 10 archers\, we will form a se
 cond line\, as in a tournament\, which will reduce the number of arrows sho
 t per person within the time. (You can see the actual attendance and class 
 composition by looking at past classes at <a href="http://www.archerytraini
 ngcenter.com/calendar">www.archerytrainingcenter.com/calendar</a>.)<br><br>
 Scores are also listed below\, if you kept score\, which is not required\, 
 except on Master Challenge weeks. You need 230 pts on 40cm target or 240 pt
 s on 60cm target to graduate out of your distance into Indoor 3A 13.5m\, an
