DESCRIPTION:REGISTER NOW !<br>More information and registration form availa
 ble on&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrai
 ningcenter.com</a>.<br>Sign up for just one Outdoor 1 class\, because most 
 people graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br
 ><br>Your name will be added below and your place reserved after we receive
  3 things:&nbsp\; REGISTRATION + WAIVERS + FEE<br><b>Adults</b>&nbsp\;- Do 
 not need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2<br><br><b>Registered ar
 chers:</b><br><b>Target nos:</b><br>1.<b> Kristin T.</b>\, 16 - pd - 62R - 
 <b>115 pts -&gt\; Outdoor 2 !</b><br>2. <b>Tyler T</b>.\, - pd - 54R - <b>3
 1 pts -&gt\; Outdoor 1</b><br>3. <b>Joerg D.</b>\, - dad - pd 68R - <b>90 p
 ts&nbsp\;</b><br>4. <b>Clyde D</b>.\, 14 - pd 66L - <b>24 pts&nbsp\;</b><b>
 -&gt\; Outdoor 1</b><br>5. <b>Steph S</b>. - adult - pd - 62R - <b>?&nbsp\;
 </b><br>6.<b> Jihyun Y</b>.\, adult - pd 62R - <b>28 pts&nbsp\;</b><br>7. <
 b>Ava B</b>.\, adult - pd 54R - <b>90 pts&nbsp\;</b><br>8. <b>Jenna G</b>.\
 , adult - pd 68R - <b>25 pts&nbsp\;</b><br>9.<br>10.<br><br>Space will be l
 imited to 10-15 archers per session depending on the number of family group
 s in attendance or in accordance with CDC Guidelines.&nbsp\;<br>Each person
  will have a target stand\, except after 10 people have registered\, two me
 mbers from the same family will share one target stand.<br>The archer and a
  maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field until further notice
  or approved by Coach Racae. Parents can sign up as an archer or watch as a
  spectator.<br><br>As of Sept 15\, we have reached the maximum number of ki
 ds under 12 that we accept into the program this semester. The minimum age 
 to register is now 12 years old.&nbsp\;<br><br>If you registered by Sept 15
 \, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take other Outd
 oor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;<br><br>If you are 
 not yet 12\, and you registered and paid after Sept 15\, your fee will be r
 eturned to you.<br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three time
 s before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it
  as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adu
 lts don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = acce
 ssories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed 
 for Outdoor 2. ($15)<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, opti
 onal but really needed to practice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><b
 r>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we di
 d not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your fina
 l score\, because it has been averaged by taking your recorded score from y
 our scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot to get an arrow a
 verage\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round score. After t
 he last class on the weekend\, final scores will also be sent to all Outdoo
 r 1 participants in an email with more information before your next class.
