DESCRIPTION:18 classes and all entered registrations for Outdoor 3-9 classe
 s were mysteriously cancelled/erased early on Fri 4/25\, so please re-enter
  your attendance below\, and PLEASE be very careful entering data into the 
 calendar so classes and registrations are not erased!!!<br><br>Registration
  form: OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m<br><br>Add your name to Target Assignment L
 ist below or send in the above completed form.<br><br>Focus primarily on <b
 r>perfecting your form\, <br>slowly increasing your physical strength and d
 raw weight\, <br>strengthening your mental program\, <br>determining your a
 verage and personal best\, <br>understanding the spread between the two\, a
 nd working on closing it.<br><br>You need your own equipment <br>Competitio
 n recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, si
 de rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, 
 finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side 
 rods may not be added until you reach a higher level\, but you should order
  them in advance.) <br><br>Wear your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br>When yo
 u score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm target face you'll move b
 ack to the next distance until you reach your competition distance<br>If yo
 u trained outdoors in the 2024 season\, you'll return to the farthest dista
 nce you shot.<br>Target arrangements may vary each session\, depending on w
 ho attends and distances needed.<br>Target 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competit
 ion distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent 
 practice in between classes.<br>Target 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition 
 distance) <br>Target 3 at 50m<br>Target 4+5 at 40m (U15 competition distanc
 e) <br>Targets 6+7+8 at 30m (U13 competition distance) <br>Target  9 at 20m
  (for those who have shot at 18m indoors or with Coach Racae's approval)<br
 >Targets 10 at 13.5m (for those who have just graduated from indoors at 9m)
 <br><br>Ideally\, we want to practice with two archers/target to replicate 
 competition conditions as much as possible.<br><br>Target Assignments:<br>T
 argets are assigned outdoors in advance to reduce confusion and delay on th
 e day\,<br>so add your name next to your distance below. <br>If you need he
 lp or have questions\, email/text Coach Racae<br>(Dotted lines represent te
 nt poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)<br>------------------------------
