DESCRIPTION:Coach Racae (Recurves only)  PREREQUISITE: INDOOR 1: First-time
  Class: Click the Sign Up button at the top of www.archerytrainingcenter.co
 m Saturdays: 11:00am-1:30pm (Fee: $25/cl) Sundays: 11:00am-1:30pm (Fee: $25
 /cl)  ENROLLMENT LINKS at: http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/news  ADULT
  RECREATIONAL CLASSES at Indoor 2-5 and distances (9m\, 13.5m\, 18m)  PER C
 LASS FEE: $20/HR  Sundays: 6:00-7:00pm  Tuesdays: 7:30-8:30pm   ATTENDEES T
 ONIGHT (paid in advance of class): 1. Adrian (13.5m) 2. Melissa (13.5m) 3. 
 Boston (9m) 4. Christopher C. (13.5m) 5. Daniel H. (18m) 6. Dave C. (13.5m 
 7. Kelly (18m) 8. Michael G. (18m) 9. Steven H. (18m) 10. Deborah P. (9m) 1
 1. Lalithya (9m) 12. Karen M (9m) 13. Ananda (9m)  MONTHLY FEES for ADULTS 
 at 18m :  Adult classes ONLY at 18m (Tues 7:30-8:30 + Sun 6:00-7:00): (Base
 d on coming 6 hrs/month. If there are 6 hrs or fewer in the month\, the mon
 thly fees are $20/hr.) JAN   $ 120 (8 one-hour classes) FEB   $ 120  (8 one
 -hour classes) MAR  $ 120 (8 one-hour classes) APR   $ 120 (8 one-hour clas
 ses) MAY   $ 120 (7 one-hour classes)  Adult classes + Wed. 6:30-8:00 at 18
 m: JAN   $ 188 (12.5 hrs available) FEB   $ 210 (14 hrs available)  MAR   $
  233 (15.5 hrs available) APR   $ 210 (14 hrs available) MAY   $  210 (14 h
 rs available)  PROGRESSIVE PROGRAM Indoor at 18m Training for those who wan
 t to progress faster towards competitive archery by meeting minimum attenda
 nce requirements. (8.5 hrs/week available) Saturdays 3:30-5:30pm Sundays:  
 3:30-5:30pm  Sundays:  6:00-7:00pm (Adults and Indoor 5 only) Tuesdays: 6:3
 0-7:30pm  Tuesdays: 7:30-8:30pm (Adults and Indoor 5 only)  Wednesdays: 6:3
 0-8:00pm   PROGRESSIVE WEEKLY FEES (after meeting previous week's attendanc
 e requirement): Indoor 3A at 13.5m: $TBD/wk (min. 4 hrs) Indoor 3B at 18m: 
    $TBD/wk (min. 5 hrs) Indoor 4 at 18m:      $TBD/wk (min. 6 hrs) Indoor 5
  at 18m:      $TBD/wk (min. 8 hrs)  USA Archery's Adult Training Program (A
 TP) follows a similar path to the Junior Olympic Archery Development (JOAD)
  program.   Your first step is to take an Indoor 1: First-time Class for Ad
 ults. Just click the link or the Sign Up button at the top of this website.
   Everyone starts out in our Recreational program at 9 meters. As you impro
 ve you progress to 13.5 meters then on to 18 meters indoors.   We welcome a
 dult recurve and compound Olympic target archers at all levels of experienc
 e.  Recurve archers attend any of the group classes above or book private l
 essons with Coach Racae or Instructor Dale. Compound archers book private l
 essons with Coach Dan.  When you decide that you are interested in competin
 g you'll apply to join USA Archery Level 4 NTS and JDT Coach Alex Meyer's C
 ompetitive Archery Program (CAP).  Experienced competitive archers need to 
 be evaluated by Coach Racae for advanced placement in either the Progressiv
 e Program or recommendation to the Competitive Archery Program with Coach A
 lex.\n\nJoin with Google Hangouts: https://plus.google.com/hangouts/_/calen
 dar/M2NkdGhhdDVxNGhmcmcwMGtyYWZ1NGJ0NmtAZ3JvdXAuY2FsZW5kYXIuZ29vZ2xlLmNvbQ.
