DESCRIPTION:<html-blob>This class has been canceled due to the heavy rains 
 occurring today.<br>Usually when there has been a heavy rainfall the parkin
 g area is like a mud rink\, which can be hazardous with cars getting stuck 
 or sliding into each other and people falling down.<br>Whether Sunday´s cla
 sses will be held will depend on the condition of the area and the temperat
 ures tomorrow. Please re-register for a future class. (There are no classes
  from Dec 20-Jan 8 inclusively.) Winter/Spring registration forms will be u
 p on the website within the next few days.<br><br>REGISTER NOW !<br>This cl
 ass is open to adults\, juniors\, and parents who have taken and graduated 
 out of Outdoor 1: First-time Class. Sign up any time for as many or as few 
 Outdoor 2 + 3 Classes as you like.<br>Register at this link:&nbsp\;<a href=
 "https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdzkDP5mwDrW_qgrx2YnlLDYipCtg5LRb
 HBqkYVHMJkBolOig/viewform">2021 Outdoor 2 at 9m and Outdoor 3 at 13.5m</a><
 br><br>ap = accessories pack purchases (this is required for Outdoor 2) $15
 <br>fp = optional\, but really necessary to practice form and warm up (stre
 tchband/string loop) $4<br>sef = semester enrollment fee due once a semeste
 r before first Outdoor 2 lesson $20<br><br><b>Registered archers </b>at 9m 
 on 40-cm target faces unless otherwise noted:<br><b>Target nos.</b><br><b><
 br></b>1.&nbsp\;<b>Victor C</b>.\, 9\, @ 9m on 60cm target face&nbsp\;<br>2
 .&nbsp\;<b>Aveesha S</b>.\, adult - pd - substituted 2/12<br>3.&nbsp\;<b>Ch
 ris N.\,&nbsp\;</b>adult - pd - at 13.5m&nbsp\;<br>4.<br>5.<br>6.<br>7.<br>
 8.<br>9.<br>10.<br><br>Space will be limited to a maximum of 10-15 archers 
 per session depending on the number of family groups in attendance or in ac
 cordance with CDC Guidelines.&nbsp\;<br>Each person will have a target stan
 d\, except after 10 people have registered\, two members from the same fami
 ly will share one target stand.<br><br>The archer and a maximum of one spec
 tator will be allowed on the field until further notice or approved by Coac
 h Racae. Parents can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator.<br><br>A
 s of Sept 15\, we have reached the maximum number of kids under 12 that we 
 accept into the program this semester. The minimum age to register is now 1
 2 years old.&nbsp\;<br><br>If you registered by Sept 15\, and are younger t
 han 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as nee
 ded and later join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;<br>More information and other registra
 tion forms are available on&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter
 .com">www.archerytrainingcenter.com</a>.<br><br>To progress to Outdoor 3 at
  13.5m\, you´ll need to shoot 230 pts on the 40-cm target face (14+ y.o.) o
 r 240 pts on the 60-cm target face (&lt\;14 y.o.).</html-blob>
