DESCRIPTION:REGISTER NOW !<br>More information and registration form availa
 ble on&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrai
 ningcenter.com</a>.<br>Sign up for just one Outdoor 1 class\, because most 
 people graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.&nb
 sp\;<br><br>Your name will be added below and your place reserved after we 
 receive 3 things:&nbsp\; REGISTRATION + WAIVERS + FEE<br><br><b>Registered 
 archers:</b><br><b>Target nos:</b><br>1. <b>Carol S</b>.\, adult -pd - DNA<
 br>2. <b>Amanda W.\, </b>adult - pd - <b>32 pts</b><br>3.<b> Anastasia </b>
 I.\, adult - pd 66R - <b>64 pts </b>(averaged)<br>4. <b>Noah K</b>.\, adult
  - pd 66R - DNA<br>5. <b>Alex Y</b>.\, adult - pd 66R - <b>107 pts</b><br>6
 . <b>Vincent L.\, </b>adult - pd 68R <b>30 pts</b><br>7. <b>Thuy N.\, </b>a
 dult\, pd 62R - <b>?</b><br>8. <b>Camden S</b>.\, adult\, pd 66R - <b>57 pt
 s</b><br>9. <b>Carey B.\, </b>adult\, pd 62R - <b>41 pts</b><br>10.<br><br>
 <br>Space will be limited to 10-15 archers per session depending on the num
 ber of family groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC Guidelines.&nb
 sp\;<br>Each person will have a target stand\, except after 10 people have 
 registered\, two members from the same family will share one target stand.<
 br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field u
 ntil further notice or approved by Coach Racae. Parents can sign up as an a
 rcher or watch as a spectator.<br><br>As of Sept 15\, we have reached the m
 aximum number of kids under 12 that we accept into the program this semeste
 r. The minimum age to register is now 12 years old.&nbsp\;<br><br>If you re
 gistered by Sept 15\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program 
 and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;
 <br><br>If you are not yet 12\, and you registered and paid after Sept 15\,
  your fee will be returned to you.<br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 
 1 two or three times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 
 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 ar
 rows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 
 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, wh
 ich will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($15)<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and 
 string loop)\, optional but really needed to practice form\, warm up before
  classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will 
 be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not 
 recognize your final score\, because it has been averaged by taking your re
 corded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrows you sho
 t to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full r
 ound score. After the last class on the weekend\, final scores will also be
  sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more information befor
 e your next class.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260517T064558Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:OUTDOOR 1 - First-time Class - 1 place left on 10/30 at 7:45 pm
TRANSP:OPAQUE
