DESCRIPTION:Coach Racae (Recurves only)\n\nPREREQUISITE:\nINDOOR 1: First-t
 ime Class:\nClick the Sign Up button at the top of www.archerytrainingcente
 r.com\nSaturdays: 11:00am-1:30pm (Fee: $25/cl)\nSundays: 11:00am-1:30pm (Fe
 e: $25/cl)\nINDOOR 2: ADULTS at 9m\n\nENROLLMENT LINKS at:\nhttp://www.arch
 erytrainingcenter.com/news\n\nATTENDEES TONIGHT: (Paid in advance)\n1. Dani
 el H. (18m)\n2. Boston (9m) - dna\n3. Christopher C. (13.5m)\n4. Suzanne J.
  (9m) - dna\n5. Michael G. - dna\n6. Melissa (18m)\n7. Steven H. (18m)\n8. 
 Odin\n9.\n10.\n\nADULT RECREATIONAL CLASSES at Indoor 2-5 and distances (9m
 \, 13.5m\, 18m)\n\nPER CLASS FEE: $20/HR \nSundays: 6:00-7:00pm \nTuesdays:
  7:30-8:30pm \n\nMONTHLY FEES for ADULTS at 18m :\n\nAdult classes ONLY at 
 18m (Tues 7:30-8:30 + Sun 6:00-7:00):\n(Based on coming 6 hrs/month. If the
 re are 6 hrs or fewer in the month\, the monthly fees are $20/hr.)\nJAN   $
  120 (8 one-hour classes)\nFEB   $ 120  (8 one-hour classes)\nMAR  $ 120 (8
  one-hour classes)\nAPR   $ 120 (8 one-hour classes)\nMAY   $ 120 (7 one-ho
 ur classes)\n\nAdult classes + Wed. 6:30-8:00 at 18m:\nJAN   $ 188 (12.5 hr
 s available)\nFEB   $ 210 (14 hrs available) \nMAR   $ 233 (15.5 hrs availa
 ble)\nAPR   $ 210 (14 hrs available)\nMAY   $  210 (14 hrs available)\n\nPR
 OGRESSIVE PROGRAM Indoor at 18m\nTraining for those who want to progress fa
 ster towards competitive archery by meeting minimum attendance requirements
 . (8.5 hrs/week available)\nSaturdays 3:30-5:30pm\nSundays:  3:30-5:30pm \n
 Sundays:  6:00-7:00pm (Adults and Indoor 5 only)\nTuesdays: 6:30-7:30pm \nT
 uesdays: 7:30-8:30pm (Adults and Indoor 5 only) \nWednesdays: 6:30-8:00pm \
 n\nPROGRESSIVE WEEKLY FEES (after meeting previous week's attendance requir
 ement):\nIndoor 3A at 13.5m: $TBD/wk (min. 4 hrs)\nIndoor 3B at 18m:    $TB
 D/wk (min. 5 hrs)\nIndoor 4 at 18m:      $TBD/wk (min. 6 hrs)\nIndoor 5 at 
 18m:      $TBD/wk (min. 8 hrs)\n\nUSA Archery's Adult Training Program (ATP
 ) follows a similar path to the Junior Olympic Archery Development (JOAD) p
 rogram. \n\nYour first step is to take an Indoor 1: First-time Class for Ad
 ults. Just click the link or the Sign Up button at the top of this website.
 \n\nEveryone starts out in our Recreational program at 9 meters. As you imp
 rove you progress to 13.5 meters then on to 18 meters indoors. \n\nWe welco
 me adult recurve and compound Olympic target archers at all levels of exper
 ience. \nRecurve archers attend any of the group classes above or book priv
 ate lessons with Coach Racae or Instructor Dale.\nCompound archers book pri
 vate lessons with Coach Dan.\n\nWhen you decide that you are interested in 
 competing you'll apply to join USA Archery Level 4 NTS and JDT Coach Alex M
 eyer's Competitive Archery Program (CAP).\n\nExperienced competitive archer
 s need to be evaluated by Coach Racae for advanced placement in either the 
 Progressive Program or recommendation to the Competitive Archery Program wi
 th Coach Alex.\n\nJoin with Google Hangouts: https://plus.google.com/hangou
 ts/_/calendar/M2NkdGhhdDVxNGhmcmcwMGtyYWZ1NGJ0NmtAZ3JvdXAuY2FsZW5kYXIuZ29vZ
 2xlLmNvbQ.r5oo7pf4arjc75j71sh4f2kh4s?hs=121
