DESCRIPTION:REGISTER NOW !<br>More information and registration form availa
 ble on&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrai
 ningcenter.com</a>.<br>Sign up for just one Outdoor 1 class\, because most 
 people graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br
 ><br>Your name will be added below and your place reserved after we receive
  3 things:&nbsp\; REGISTRATION + WAIVERS + FEE<br><br><b>Registered archers
 :</b><br><b>Target nos:</b><br>1. Steph S.\, adult - pd - 62R<br>2. Jihyun 
 Y.\, adult - pd<br>3.&nbsp\;<br>4.&nbsp\;<br>5.&nbsp\;<br>6.&nbsp\;<br>7.<b
 r>8.<br>9.<br>10.<br><br><br>Space will be limited to 10-15 archers per ses
 sion depending on the number of family groups in attendance or in accordanc
 e with CDC Guidelines.&nbsp\;<br>Each person will have a target stand\, exc
 ept after 10 people have registered\, two members from the same family will
  share one target stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will 
 be allowed on the field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae. Pa
 rents can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator.<br><br>As of Sept 1
 5\, we have reached the maximum number of kids under 12 that we accept into
  the program this semester. The minimum age to register is now 12 years old
 .&nbsp\;<br><br>If you registered by Sept 15\, and are younger than 12\, yo
 u´ll stay in the program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and lat
 er join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;<br><br>If you are not yet 12\, and you registered
  and paid after Sept 15\, your fee will be returned to you.<br><br>Juniors 
 may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying to get into
  Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on averag
 e about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score 
 to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fing
 ertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($15)<br>fp = fo
 rm pack (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but really needed to pract
 ice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 
 class\, your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (
 30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, because it has been a
 veraged by taking your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the
  number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying t
 hat by 30 to get a full round score. After the last class on the weekend\, 
 final scores will also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email wi
 th more information before your next class.
