DESCRIPTION:<table><tbody><tr><td><br><b><i>18 classes and all entered regi
 strations for Outdoor 3-9 classes were mysteriously cancelled/erased early 
 on Fri 4/25\, so please re-enter your attendance below\, and PLEASE be very
  careful entering data into the calendar so classes and registrations are n
 ot erased!!!</i></b><b><br></b><br><b>Registration form: </b><a href="https
 ://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfx1RyOwd314Q4zXYiQ9rb_a3oe84E9dIYs8CN3
 5Ginmevfpg/viewform?usp=preview" target="_blank">OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m</
 a><br><br><b>Add your name to Target Assignment List below or send in the a
 bove completed form.</b><br><br><i>Focus primarily on <br></i><ul><li><i>pe
 rfecting your form\, </i></li><li><i>slowly increasing your physical streng
 th and draw weight\, </i></li><li><i>strengthening your mental program\, </
 i></li><li><i>determining your average and personal best\, </i></li><li><i>
 understanding the spread between the two\, and working on closing it.</i></
 li></ul><b>You need your own equipment </b><br>Competition recurve bow\, si
 ght\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assem
 bly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip
  or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be ad
 ded until you reach a higher level\, but you should order them in advance.)
  <br><br>Wear your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br><i>When you score 288 pts
  in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the next
  distance until you reach your competition distance</i><br><i>If you traine
 d outdoors in the 2024 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you 
 shot.</i><br><i>Target arrangements may vary each session\, depending on wh
 o attends and distances needed.</i><br><b>Target 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors</b
 > competition distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use it for in
 dependent practice in between classes.<br><b>Target 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters
 </b> competition distance) <br><b>Target 3 at 50m</b><br><b>Target 4+5 at 4
 0m</b> (<b>U15</b> competition distance) <br><b>Targets 6+7+8 at 30m</b> <s
 pan>(</span><b>U13</b><span> </span><span>competition distance) </span><br>
 <b>Target  9 at 20m </b>(for those who have shot at 18m indoors or with Coa
 ch Racae's approval)<br><b>Targets 10 at 13.5m</b> (for those who have just
  graduated from indoors at 9m)<br><br>Ideally\, we want to practice with tw
 o archers/target to replicate competition conditions as much as possible.<b
 r><br><b>Target Assignments:</b><br>Targets are assigned outdoors in advanc
 e to reduce confusion and delay on the day\,<br>so add your name next to yo
 ur distance below. <br>If you need help or have questions\, email/text Coac
 h Racae<br><i>(Dotted lines represent tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, a
 nd 9.)</i><br>------------------------------<u></u>----<br>1A. (70m)<br>1B<
 br><br>2A. (60m)  <br>2B<br><br>3A. (50m)  <br>----------------------------
 --<u></u>----<br>3B<br><br>4A. (40m) <br>4B<br>----------------------------
 --<u></u>----<br>5A. (40m)<br>5B. <br><br>6A. (30m) <b>Adrianne M</b>. ATCI
 \, pd - <b>265 pts</b><br>------------------------------<u></u>----<br>6B. 
 <b>Jacqui  C.</b>-<b> 120 pts</b><br><br>7A. (30m) <b>Anna P - 275 pts</b><
 br>7B.  (30m) <b>Sofia W.</b> - <b>136 pts</b><br>-------------------------
 -----<u></u>---- <br>8A. (30m) <b>Colby</b> - <b>278 pts</b><br>8B. <br><br
 >9A. (20m)<br>------------------------------<u></u>----<br>9B. <br><br>10A.
  (13.5m) <b>Love L-P. - 111 pts</b><br>10B</td></tr><tr><td><u></u><u></u><
