DESCRIPTION:<b>Condiitons: Sunny\, but extremely windy\, heavy gusts (25 mp
 h w/40 mph gusts) - great temperature though - 67-72 degF. Blew the tents a
 part! Only erect in winds &lt\;25 mph.</b><br><br>Registration form: OUTDOO
 R 3-9 at 13.5m-70m (<a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfx1R
 yOwd314Q4zXYiQ9rb_a3oe84E9dIYs8CN35Ginmevfpg/viewform?usp=preview" target="
 _blank">https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfx1RyOwd314Q4zXYiQ9rb_a3o
 e84E9dIYs8CN35Ginmevfpg/viewform?usp=preview</a>)<br><br>Add your name to T
 arget Assignment List below or send in the above completed form.<br><br>Foc
 us primarily on <br>    * perfecting your form\, <br>    * slowly increasin
 g your physical strength and draw weight\, <br>    * strengthening your men
 tal program\, <br>    * determining your average and personal best\, <br>  
   * understanding the spread between the two\, and working on closing it.<b
 r>You need your own equipment <br>Competition recurve bow\, sight\, stabili
 zer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker
 \, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field qui
 ver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added until you
  reach a higher level\, but you should order them in advance.) <br><br>Wear
  your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow r
 ound on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the next distance until 
 you reach your competition distance<br>If you trained outdoors in the 2024 
 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.<br>Target arrange
 ments may vary each session\, depending on who attends and distances needed
 .<br>Target 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should always sta
 y at 70m so Jake can use it for independent practice in between classes.<br
 >Target 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition distance) <br>Target 3 at 50m<b
