UID:j5689siu5vlkdp0llsa2g0rf8m_R20211030T140000@google.com
CREATED:20210711T054416Z
DESCRIPTION:REGISTER NOW !<br>More information and registration form availa
 ble on&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrai
 ningcenter.com</a>.<br>Sign up for just one Outdoor 1 class\, because most 
 people graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br
 ><br>Your name will be added below and your place reserved after we receive
  3 things:&nbsp\; REGISTRATION + WAIVERS + FEE<br><br><b>Registered archers
 :</b><br><b>Target nos:</b><br>1.&nbsp\;<br>2.&nbsp\;<br>3.&nbsp\;<br>4.&nb
 sp\;<br>5.&nbsp\;<br>6.&nbsp\;<br>7.<br>8.<br>9.<br>10.<br><br>Space will b
 e limited to a maximum of 10-15 archers per session depending on the number
  of family groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC Guidelines.&nbsp\
 ;<br>Each person will have a target stand\, except after 10 people have reg
 istered\, two members from the same family will share one target stand.<br>
 The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field unti
 l further notice or approved by Coach Racae. Parents can sign up as an arch
 er or watch as a spectator.<br><br>As of Sept 15\, we have reached the maxi
 mum number of kids under 12 that we accept into the program this semester. 
 The minimum age to register is now 12 years old.&nbsp\;<br><br>If you regis
 tered by Sept 15\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and
  take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;<br
 ><br>If you are not yet 12\, and you registered and paid after Sept 15\, yo
 ur fee will be returned to you.<br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two o
 r three times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. Yo
 u´ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.&n
 bsp\;<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><
 br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, purchased
 \, which will be needed for Outdoor 2.<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and s
 tring loop)\, purchased\, optional but really needed to practice form\, war
 m up before classes $4.00<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your 
 scores will be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, 
 you may not recognize your final score\, because it has been averaged by ta
 king your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the number of ar
 rows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to 
 get a full round score. After the last class on the weekend\, all final sco
 res will also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participates in an email with more i
 nformation before your next class.
