DESCRIPTION:<b>Step #9 - Expand and Aim </b>(see email for details)<br><b><
 br></b><br><br><b>Expansion</b><br><ul><li>Definition</li><li><b>Directiona
 l intensity control</b></li><li>Maintain: <ul><li><b>tension and direction<
 /b> </li><li><b>50/50 balance</b></li><li><b>Alignments</b></li></ul></li><
 li>Small movement is enough to move the arrow 2mm through the clicker</li><
 li><b>The arrow always hits where it is pointed!</b><ul><li>Release and Fol
 low-through are reactions to the force and direction of expansion</li></ul>
 </li></ul><br><b>Aiming</b><br><ul><li>Begins after Expansion begins<ul><li
 >Aim only after achieving Holding and starting Expansion </li><li>Conscious
  to subconscious </li></ul></li><li><b>Timing &lt\; 3 secs after aperture i
 s on aiming point.</b></li><li><b>Mental focus</b></li><li><b>Eye focus</b>
  </li><li>Physically:<ul><li><b>Aiming point</b></li><li><b>String alignmen
 t</b></li><li><b>Target in focus</b></li></ul></li></ul><br><b>What is more
  important than aiming?</b><br><b>Where does consistency </b><span>come fro
 m?<br></span>\n\nJoin with Google Meet: https://meet.google.com/zqe-efhd-ia
 d\n\nLearn more about Meet at: https://support.google.com/a/users/answer/92
 82720
