DESCRIPTION:Registration form: 2024 OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m<br><br>Those w
 ho have already qualified for TAMU's Aggie Invitational by scoring 210 pts 
 at 18m on 40-cm target face :<br>Coach Joel\, Coach Nike\, Instructor Lily\
 , Christine\, Finn\, Javier\, Ted<br><br>Those who scored 110 pts/round by 
 Oct 6 stay at 18m:  <br>Abby\, Ananya\, Christine\, Daisy\, Erika\, Finn\, 
 Gianna\, Jacqui\, Javier\, Coach Joel\, Joseph\, Kishore\, Instructor Lily\
 , Coach Nick\, Pranav\, Rhys\, Yugan<br><br>OtherJOAD archers and new outdo
 or JOAD arrivals will be shooting at 13.5m on 60-cm target face until your 
 form and groups tighten up\, and you shoot 240 pts to move back to 18m.<br>
 <br>Field work: This weekend:<br>    •Spectators start painting outside wal
 ls of the enclosure fence. (Wear your paint clothes!)<br>    •Clean up insi
 de enclosure area - weed whack in prep for painting<br>    •Flatten/Distrib
 ute lumps of earth along new wood/concrete fence<br>    •Plant cacti\, etc.
  in planters (Clarissa (Miles´s mom) and Finn)<br>    •Clean up around POD<
 br>    •Create plan and materials list for repairing/stabilizing leaning pa
 rt of enclosure fence <br><br>Target Assignments:<br><br>Targets 1 should a
 lways stay at 70m so Jake can shoot.<br>Target 2 at 60m<br>Target 3 at 40m<
 br>Target 4 at 30m - can move to 18m when needed<br>Targets 5-8 at 18m <br>
 Target 9 can move back and forth between 13.5m and 18m when needed<br>Targe
 t 10 at 13.5m<br>See notes below list.<br><br><br><b>Two timed and scored r
 ounds or 30 arrows during this class.</b><br><br>--------------------------
 --------<br>1A. (70m)<br>1B<br><br>2A. (60m)  <br>2B<br><br>3A. (40m)  <br>
 ----------------------------------<br>3B<br><br><b>18m 40-cm:</b><br><br>4A
  <b>Lily R.</b>\, 15\, USAA\, OB - 199 + 185 = <b>384 pts</b><br>4B <b>Jacq
