 ><br>9A. <b>Pranav C</b>\, 16\, USAA\, OB\, pd  - 153 + 89 (corrected) = <b
 >242 pts</b><br>----------------------------------<br>9B  <b>Yugan 12</b>\,
  USAA Pd (5/12) 77 + 134 (corrected) = <b>211 pts</b><br><br><b>13.5m 40-cm
 :</b><br><br>10A. <b>Riley M</b>.\, 13\, USAA\, OB\, pd - 218 (corrected) +
 218 (corrected) = <b>436 pts</b><br>10B<br><br>When you shoot at 18m to pra
 ctice for the Aggie Invitational in Nov\, you'll be on a 40-cm target face\
 , set up 4 to a target (even if only one or two archers are on that target)
 . <br>You should practice one round of 30 arrows at each target face high/l
 ow/left/right so you are prepared for your target assignment at the indoor 
 competitions<br><br>Ideally\, we want to practice with at least two archers
 /target to replicate competition conditions as much as possible.<br>You can
  decide each week if you want to shoot at your long distance or at 18m and 
 add or move your name on the calendar accordingly. You should alternate dis
 tance each day\, so you practice both. Starting Oct 1 to the Nov Aggie Invi
 tational and Jan 1 for the Feb Indoor Nationals\, everyone should be shooti
 ng at 18m and scoring to determine their average and their personal bests\,
  understand the spread between the two\, and work on closing it.
