 <b>211 pts</b> (corrected)<br>10B<br><br>When you shoot at 18m to practice 
 for the Aggie Invitational in Nov\, you'll be on a 40-cm target face\, set 
 up 4 to a target (even if only one or two archers are on that target). <br>
 You should practice one round of 30 arrows at each target face high/low/lef
 t/right so you are prepared for your target assignment at the indoor compet
 itions<br><br>Ideally\, we want to practice with at least two archers/targe
 t to replicate competition conditions as much as possible.<br>You can decid
 e each week if you want to shoot at your long distance or at 18m and add or
  move your name on the calendar accordingly. You should alternate distance 
 each day\, so you practice both. Starting Oct 1 to the Nov Aggie Invitation
 al and Jan 1 for the Feb Indoor Nationals\, everyone should be shooting at 
 18m and scoring to determine their average and their personal bests\, under
 stand the spread between the two\, and work on closing it.
