  full with two archers/target at 18m.</i><br><i>When you shoot at 18m to pr
 actice for the Aggie Invitational in Nov\, you'll be on a 60-cm or 40-cm ta
 rget face. 60-cm target faces should be centered side-by-side\, and 40-cm t
 arget faces should be set up 4 to a target (even if only one or two archers
  are on that target). </i><br><i>You should practice one round of 30 arrows
  at each target face high/low/left/right so you are prepared for your targe
 t assignment at the indoor competitions</i><i><br></i><br><i>Ideally\, we w
 ant to practice with at least two archers/target to replicate competition c
 onditions as much as possible.</i><br><i>You can decide each week if you wa
 nt to shoot at your long distance or at 18m and add or move your name on th
 e calendar accordingly. You should alternate distance each day\, so you pra
 ctice both. S</i><br><i>tarting Oct 1 to the Nov Aggie Invitational and Jan
  1 for the Feb Indoor Nationals\, everyone should be shooting at 18m and sc
 oring to determine their average and their personal bests\, understand the 
 spread between the two\, and work on closing it.</i>
