 7A. <b>Abby Y.</b>\, 12\, USAA\, OB\, pd - <b>101 pts</b><br>7B. <b>Rhys E<
 /b>\, 10\, USAA OB\, pd - <b>74 pts</b><br>--------------------------------
 -- <br>8A. <br>8B. <br><br><b>13.5m 60-cm:</b><br><br>9A. <b>Riley M.</b>\,
  13\, USAA\, OB\, pd - <b>200 pts</b><br>----------------------------------
 <br>9B. <b>Miles G.</b>\, 12\, USAA\, OB\, pd - <b>222 pts</b><br><br>10A.<
 br>10B<br><br><b>Jacqui C</b>.\, 10\, USAA\, OB\, pd - DNA - fee forfeited<
 br><br>When you shoot at 18m to practice for the Aggie Invitational in Nov\
 , you'll be on a 40-cm target face\, set up 4 to a target (even if only one
  or two archers are on that target). <br>You should practice one round of 3
 0 arrows at each target face high/low/left/right so you are prepared for yo
 ur target assignment at the indoor competitions<br><br>Ideally\, we want to
  practice with at least two archers/target to replicate competition conditi
 ons as much as possible.<br>You can decide each week if you want to shoot a
 t your long distance or at 18m and add or move your name on the calendar ac
 cordingly. You should alternate distance each day\, so you practice both. S
 tarting Oct 1 to the Nov Aggie Invitational and Jan 1 for the Feb Indoor Na
 tionals\, everyone should be shooting at 18m and scoring to determine their
  average and their personal bests\, understand the spread between the two\,
  and work on closing it.
