 irst-time class is for juniors age 8+\, optionally their parents\, and othe
 r adults who would like to try archery for the first time and join in futur
 e Junior Olympic Archery Development (JOAD) and Adult Training classes.   \
 nThis class is a prerequisite for all classes. \n \nIf you have more than o
 ne year's experience\, contact us for a placement evaluation ($45) instead 
 of attending the Indoor 1 Class.  \n(You will be on the waiting list after 
 10 people register - see below.)  \n\nRegistered archers: \n1.  Christopher
