DESCRIPTION:Registered Archers:<br>1. Lily R. 20m - to pay<br>2. Yuhan X.\,
  9m on 60-cm target face - paid<br>3.<br>4..<br>5.<br>6.<br>7.<br>8.<br>9.<
 br>10.<br><br>OVERVIEW:<br>These Outdoor Target Archery recreational classe
 s prepare you to shoot at longer and longer distances until you reach your 
 USA Archery tournament distance (see below)\, while learning the National T
 raining System\, which is the most highly researched biomechanical method o
 f shooting taught out at the Olympic Training Center. You will be shooting 
 with other archers in group sessions\, so you can all learn together and fr
 om each other. <br><br>PREREQUISITE: <br>Some archery experience and your o
 wn recurve archery equipment is required.<br><br>OPEN TO ADULTS / JUNIORS /
  PARENTS (with experience and own recurve archery equipment)<br>The archer 
 and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field until further n
 otice or approved by Coach Racae.<br>Space will be limited to a maximum of 
 10 archers per session or in accordance with CDC Guidelines.<br><br>NO DROP
  INS:<br>You cannot just drop in\, because the number of archers on the sho
 oting line is very limited and we are observing CDC guidelines with social 
 distancing.<br><br>DATES:    Start Dates: MAY 15 (Adults) or JUNE 12 (Junio
 rs 10+) <br>&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;
 &nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;Ending Date:  AUGUST 14  <br><br>ADDRESS
 ES:<br>OUTDOOR FIELD SOUTH:    2310 Bliss Spillar Road\, Manchaca\, TX 7865
 2<br>MAILING:  Archery Training Center\, Inc.\, PO Box 93216\, Austin\, TX 
 78709<br><br>E-MAIL: <a href="mailto:archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com"
 >archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a><br><br>PHONE/TEXT:  512 975 1850
 <br><br>CAPACITY:    10 archers per class or in accordance with CDC guideli
 nes<br>AGES:             10 - 80+ years old (See start dates above)<br>DIST
 ANCES:  9m\, 13.5m\, 18m\, 20m-70m<br>BOWS:           Recurves  <br>(If you
  are not a recurve archer\, but would like to learn to shoot a recurve bow\
 , please stay tuned to our Instagram for announcements of the re-opening of
  our in-person First-time Classes\, or register online for a few Virtual NT
 S Form classes with Coach Racae.)<br><br>EQUIPMENT: <br>These classes are f
 or archers who have their own equipment\, consisting of at least a recurve 
 bow\, 12 aluminum or carbon arrows\, armguard\, finger tab\, hip or field q
 uiver.  (If you need to change your equipment or order your own\, please co
 ntact Coach Racae at <a href="mailto:archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com"
 >archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a>. She will specify what you´ll ne
 ed and help you order it\, so you buy the correct equipment for your streng
 th and experience.)<br><br>INSTRUCTOR / COACH:<br>USA Archery Level 2 Instr
 uctor Ted Aanstoos  <br><br>CLASS TIMES:<br>These are the days/times that a
 re available to you. (Additional sessions will be added in future.)<br><br>
 SAT:     9:00-10:30pm <br>WED:    9:00-10:30pm <br>Please check <a href="ht
 tp://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/calendar">www.archerytrainingcenter.com/
 calendar</a> before registering!<br><br>DAYS CLOSED: <br>The outdoor range 
 is closed\, gates locked\, and targets stored away except during the above 
 class times.<br><br>ENROLLMENT IS ON A FIRST-RECEIVED AND PAID BASIS.<br>Co
 mplete the Outdoor Target Archery Registration Form under Adults or Juniors
  at <a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrainingcente
 r.com</a><br><br>ATTENDANCE RECOMMENDATIONS: <br>Recreational archers have 
 no attendance requirements\, but we would recommend attending at least twic
 e a week to improve faster. <br><br>FEES: <br>All fees are payable in advan
 ce of the class to secure your place in the class. <br>$30/archer for each 
 1.5-hr training session  OR <br>$115/mo (for 1 training session/week) OR <b
 r>$213/mo (for 2 training sessions/week)<br>+ Enrollment fee: $20 (always d
 ue once per semester) <br><br>WEATHER:<br>Archers need to practice in all w
 eather\, except when there is lightning. <br><br>REFUNDS\, CREDITS\, and SU
 BSTITUTIONS:<br>Substitutions or credits will be applied if we cancel a cla
 ss due to weather conditions or instructor illness or if the 24-hr notice i
 s met.<br>There are no refunds for paid classes missed during the summer\, 
 except in the case of injury\, long-term illness\, unforeseen move out of t
 he Austin area\, or being expelled for a safety violation. <br><br>24-HR NO
 TICE: <br>If you let us know within 24 hours of the class that you will mis
 s the class\, you can substitute another class and use your fee as long as 
 there are places left in that class during the semester. If you notify us l
 ess than 24 hours in advance of the class that you will need to cancel (exc
 ept for sudden illness)\, or you do a "no-show"\, you'll forfeit your fee.<
 br><br>ILLNESS or INJURY: In the case of physical injury or long-term illne
 ss\, we require a doctor's note saying that you are unable to practice arch
 ery\, and then a doctor's note saying that you are again fit to return to a
 rchery\, before you will be allowed back in class or a refund/credit issued
 .<br><br>MEMBERSHIP IN USA ARCHERY:<br>Membership in USA Archery is now REQ
 UIRED to participate in JOAD and Adult Training.<br>You can attend 2 sessio
 ns before joining USAA\, but then we'll need to see your membership card BE
 FORE WE CAN HAND OUT ANY USA ARCHERY STAR PINS to you during Master Challen
 ge Weeks! <br>If you would like to see the benefits of USAA membership: <a 
 href="http://www.teamusa.org/USA-Archery/Membership/Membership-Benefits">ht
 tp://www.teamusa.org/USA-Archery/Membership/Membership-Benefits</a><br>JOIN
  USA ARCHERY: <a href="https://www.usarchery.org/memberships/become-a-membe
 r">https://www.usarchery.org/memberships/become-a-member</a><br><br>SAFE SP
 ORTS:<br>PARENTS PLEASE NOTE: We are part of the US Olympic Committee's Saf
 e Sport program\, so we minimally require one other adult besides the instr
 uctor to be present at all times. Please plan to stay with your child or ta
 ke turns with other parents staying whenever necessary to fulfill this requ
 irement. THANKS!<br><br>SIGN AND RETURN THESE OUTDOOR WAIVERS:<br>The follo
 wing documents and waivers will be part of your Registration and Waiver Pac
 ket. You will need to sign these  documents before we add your name to thos
 e shooting in the class:<br>o Membership Form<br>o Safety Rules <br>o Relea
 se of Liability Waiver<br>o Supervision Policy (Under 18)<br>o Medical Rele
 ase  <br>o Photo/Video Release<br>o COVID-19 Guidelines<br>o Outdoor Field 
 Rules of Participation <br><br>VACCINATIONS:<br>We do not at this time requ
 ire archers to be vaccinated\, but we would like to know if you have been\,
  so we can take it into consideration when deciding on issues such as masks
  and social distancing and abiding by the CDC Guidelines. All our instructo
 rs have been fully vaccinated of their own accord.<br><br>QUESTIONS?<br>E-m
 ail us at <a href="mailto:archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com">archerytra
 iningcenteraustin@gmail.com</a> or<br>Call/Text us at 512 975 1850 <br><br>
 *NTS = National Training System (which is used for training the USA Olympic
  team!)<br>*JDT = Junior Dream Team (top 20 Junior archers in the USA!)<br>
 *JOAD = Junior Olympic Archery Development
