DESCRIPTION:Registration form: 2024 OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m<br><br>Those w
 ho have already qualified for TAMU's Aggie Invitational :<br>Coach Joel\, C
 oach Nike\, Instructor Lily\, Christine\, Erika\, Finn\, Javier\, Ted<br><b
 r>You will be shooting at 13.5m on 60-cm target face until your form and gr
 oups tighten up\, and you shoot 240 pts to move back to 18m again unless yo
 u have already scored 110 pts on the 40-cm target face at 18m.<br><br>Those
  who scored 110 pts/round by Oct 6 stay at 18m:  <br>Abby\, Ananya\, Christ
 ine\, Daisy\, Erika\, Finn\, Gianna\, Jacqui\, Javier\, Coach Joel\, Joseph
 \, Kishore\, Instructor Lily\, Coach Nick\, Pranav\, Rhys\, Yugan<br><br>Fi
 eld work: This weekend\, .<br><br>Target Assignments:<br><br>Targets 1 shou
 ld always stay at 70m so Jake can shoot.<br>Target 2 at 60m<br>Target 3 at 
 40m<br>Targets 4-9 at 18m <br>Targets 10 at 13.5m<br>See notes below list.<
 br><br>----------------------------------<br>1A. (70m)<br>1B<br><br>2A. (60
 m)  <br>2B<br><br>3A. (40m)  <br>----------------------------------<br>3B<b
 r><br><b>18m 40-cm:</b><br>4A. <br>4B. <b>Jacqui C.\, </b>10\, USAA\, OB\, 
 pd - <b>68 pts = 2.27 pts arrow avg.</b><br>-------------------------------
 ---<br><br>5A. <b>Joseph F</b>.\,14\, USAA\, OB\, pd = 190 +185 = <b>375 pt
 s/60 arrows = 6.25 pt arrow avg.</b><br>5B. <b>Abby Y</b>.\, 12\, USAA\, OB
 \, pd - 206+187 = <b>393 pts/60 arrows = 6.55 pt arrow avg.</b><br><br>6A. 
 <b>Joel Y</b>.\, adult\, USAA\, OB\, pd - 174 + 149 = <b>323 pts/60 arrows 
 = 5.38 pt arrow avg.</b><br>----------------------------------<br>6B <b>Yug
 an\,</b> 12\, USAA\, pd (9/12) - 156 +107 = <b>263 pts/60 arrows = 4.38 pt 
 arrow avg</b><br><br>7A.   <br>7B<br><br>----------------------------------
  <br>8A. <br>8B. <br><br>9A. <br>----------------------------------<br>9B.<
 br><br><b>13.5m 40-cm:</b><br><b><br></b>10A.<br>10B<br><br>When you shoot 
 at 18m to practice for the Aggie Invitational in Nov\, you'll be on a 40-cm
  target face\, set up 4 to a target (even if only one or two archers are on
  that target). <br>You should practice one round of 30 arrows at each targe
 t face high/low/left/right so you are prepared for your target assignment a
 t the indoor competitions<br><br>Ideally\, we want to practice with at leas
 t two archers/target to replicate competition conditions as much as possibl
 e.<br>You can decide each week if you want to shoot at your long distance o
 r at 18m and add or move your name on the calendar accordingly. You should 
 alternate distance each day\, so you practice both. Starting Oct 1 to the N
 ov Aggie Invitational and Jan 1 for the Feb Indoor Nationals\, everyone sho
 uld be shooting at 18m and scoring to determine their average and their per
 sonal bests\, understand the spread between the two\, and work on closing i
 t.
