DESCRIPTION:Training classes at this location are reserved for competitive 
 and advanced archers.\n\nIf you participated in the 2024 or 2025 Aggie Invi
 tationals\, you are in! You should receive an email with info and instructi
 ons before your first session at this location.\n\nIf you haven't yet made 
 the 2026 Indoor Competition Team\, but have your own equipment\, and have s
 cored 240 on the 60-cm target face or 230 on the 40-cm target face in a 30-
 arrow indoor round at 9m\, contact Coach Racae.\n\nSpace is limited\, so si
 gn up soon and pay the class and facility fees in advance to secure your pl
 ace! We have 3 target stands\, so 6 archers per line. Ideally\, it would be
  best to keep it to 12 archers each session. There are about 21 archers int
 erested. We may need to create a additional class on one of the two weekend
  days\, but we'll see how it goes.\n\nMove-in: Nov 15\nClass fee: $52/class
 /archer for 3 hours !\nFacility fee: $205/mo due on Nov 15\, Dec. 15\, and 
 Jan. 15\nMove-out will be after the Indoor Nationals about Feb 15.\nPlease 
 add your name below to register:\n    1. Vivian C.\, 12\, (1st Place U13 at
  Aggie Invite) Yay! - visiting from Houston\n    2. Charles C.\, 9\, barebo
 w on 60-cm target face\n    3. Kelvin C\, adult\, barebow\n    4. Yang C.\,
  adult\n    5. Sara T.\, 14\, 40 or 60cm? 217\n    6. Sofia W. 40 or 60 cm?
  179\n    7. Abby Y\, 13\, 40cm 238 \n    8. Ellie Y\, 11\, on 60-cm target
  face\, 213\n    9. Joel Y\, adult 239\n    10. .\n    11. .\n    12. .
