DESCRIPTION:Registration form: 2024 OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m<br><br><br>Tho
 se who have already qualified for TAMU's Aggie Invitational by scoring <br>
 at 18m: <br>210 on 40-cm target faces or <br>220 on 60-cm target faces or <
 br>at 9m:<br>270 on 40-cm target faces or <br>280 on 60-cm target faces or<
 br>200 on reduced target face <br>Coach Joel\, Coach Nike\, Instructor Lily
 \, Abby\, Christine\, Finn\, Ted<br><br>Those who have advanced from Outdoo
 r 3 at 13.5m to Outdoor 4 at 18m by scoring: <br>at 9m:<br>250 on 40-cm or 
 <br>260 on 60-cm target faces or<br>at 13.5m <br>240 on 60-cm target face a
 t 13.5m advance to Outdoor 4 at 18m: <br>Miles<br><br>Those who scored 110 
 pts/round by Oct 6 stay at 18m:  <br>Abby\, Ananya\, Christine\, Daisy\, Er
 ika\, Finn\, Gianna\, Jacqui\, Javier\, Coach Joel\, Joseph\, Kishore\, Ins
 tructor Lily\, Coach Nick\, Pranav\, Rhys\, Yugan<br><br>Field work this we
 ekend: Many thanks to Randy (Riley's dad) for stabilizing the long run of e
 nclosure fencing!!!  Spectators paint long run of fence on the outside\, we
 ed whack at base of fence\, remove tarp and chairs in enclosure to prepare 
 for painting inside walls of enclosure\, Clarissa (Miles's mom) and Finn wi
 ll do planters after fence is painted<br><br>Target Assignments:<br><br>Tar
 gets 1 should always stay at 70m so Jake can shoot.<br>Target 2 at 60m<br>T
 arget 3 at 40m<br>Targets 4-9 at 18m <br>Targets 10 at 13.5m<br>See notes b
 elow list.<br><br>If you do not find a space at the distance you shoot\, ju
 st enter your name and distance somewhere on the list and Coach Racae will 
 adjust the assignments.<br><br>----------------------------------<br>1A. (7
 0m)<br>1B<br><br>2A. (60m)  <br>2B<br><br>3A. (40m)  <br>------------------
 ----------------<br>3B<br><br>18m 40-cm:<br><br>4A. <b>Joseph F.</b>\, 14\,
  USAA\, OB\, pd - <b>189 pts </b>(corrected)<br>4B. <b>Yugan.C\,</b> 12\, U
 SAA\, OB\, pd (8/12) - <b>75 pts</b><br>----------------------------------<
 br><br>5A. <b>Pranav C.\, </b>16\, USAA\, OB\, pd - <b>136 pts</b><br>5B. <
 b>Kishore C.\, </b>16\, USAA\, OB\, pd - <b>192 pts</b><br><br>6A. <b>Anany
 a C.\, </b>13\, USAA\, OB\, pd - <b>133 pts</b><br>------------------------
 ----------<br>6B.<b> Luke T.</b> 15\, USAA\, OB\, pd - <b>147 pts </b>(corr
 ected)<br><br>7A.   <br>7B<br><br>---------------------------------- <br>8A
 . <br>8B. <br><br><br>9A. <br>----------------------------------<br>9B. <br
 ><br>13.5m 40-cm:<br><br>10A. <b>Lexi E.</b> 15\, USAA\, OB\, pd - <b>113 p
 ts</b><br>10B. <b>Colby K.\, </b>adult\, USAA\, OB\, pd - <b>DNS</b><br><br
 >When you shoot at 18m to practice for the Aggie Invitational in Nov\, you'
 ll be on a 40-cm target face\, set up 4 to a target (even if only one or tw
 o archers are on that target). <br>You should practice one round of 30 arro
 ws at each target face high/low/left/right so you are prepared for your tar
 get assignment at the indoor competitions<br><br>Ideally\, we want to pract
 ice with at least two archers/target to replicate competition conditions as
  much as possible.<br>You can decide each week if you want to shoot at your
  long distance or at 18m and add or move your name on the calendar accordin
 gly. You should alternate distance each day\, so you practice both. Startin
 g Oct 1 to the Nov Aggie Invitational and Jan 1 for the Feb Indoor National
 s\, everyone should be shooting at 18m and scoring to determine their avera
 ge and their personal bests\, understand the spread between the two\, and w
 ork on closing it.
