DESCRIPTION:<b>What we worked on:</b><br>Shooting outdoors at 50m in the wi
 nd<br>Metallic sound in riser\, so limb bolt mechanism lose<br>Check that n
 ew limbs are in correct position (upper in top position\, etc.)<br><b>What 
 we learned:</b><br>Bring everything out to the field when shooting: stringe
 r\, allen key set\, etc.\, in case equipment repair or maintenance is requi
 red<br><b>Homework:</b><br>Find cause for and correct metallic sound by com
 paring top and bottom limb bolt interiors \; send video of solution and how
  the bow sounds after correction<br>Holding SPTs: 20 sec/ 40 sec rest\; up 
 to 80% endurance\; all or nothing (don´t reduce duration - 20 sec. or stop)
 <br>Also\, check brace height\, center shot (whether string is in lined up 
 with center of the limbs and tip of arrow is behind the string or slightly 
 to the left of it when viewed from behind the string as if shooting).
