DESCRIPTION:USA Archery Level 3 NTS Coach Racae\nIf you would like a 2014 F
 all Enrollment Form\, contact racae@archerytrainingcenter.com\n\nAlways che
 ck our website's calendar just before coming to class in case there are cha
 nges or cancellations.\n\nPREREQUISITES: \nIndoor 4 is for JUNIOR archers a
 nd their parents who have \n- taken and qualified in the Indoor 1: First-ti
 me Class by scoring 50 pts at 9 m\n- graduated out of Indoor 2 by scoring 2
 40 pts at 9m\,\n- graduated out of Indoor 3A by scoring 240 pts at 13.5m\,\
 n- graduated out of Indoor 3B by scoring 200 pts twice at 18m\n\nPARENTS \n
 can enroll and shoot with their child(ren) in the following classes\, provi
 ded they have completed the above prerequisites..\n\nPLEASE COMPLETE ONE EN
 ROLLMENT FORM FOR EACH ARCHER.\n\nDATES:          August 23 - December 14\,
  2014\n\nCAPACITY:    10 archers per class\nAGES:            8 - 18 years o
 ld \nDISTANCES:  18m only\n\nCLASS SCHEDULE:\nSaturdays and Sundays: 4:00-5
 :30pm\n\nDAYS CLOSED:\nSEPT. 1\, Labor Day\nSEPT. 30\, Range closed\nOCT. 3
 1\, Halloween\nNOV. 26-30\, Thanksgiving\nDEC. 15 - Jan. 3\, Christmas / Ne
 w Year's\n\nENROLLMENT IS ON A FIRST-RECEIVED AND PAID BASIS.\nAn enrollmen
 t form must be completed and your payment received in order for you to be e
 nrolled and a place reserved for you.\nYou can enroll any time during the s
 emester for as many or as few classes as you like as long as there are plac
 es open.\nSo\, for example\, you can enroll for the entire semester\, each 
 month\, or sprinkle the days throughout the semester depending on your sche
 dule. (Please bear in mind\, however\, you'll progress faster with regular 
 attendance.)\n\nREFUNDS\, CREDITS\, and SUBSTITUTIONS:\nThere are no refund
 s or credits for paid days missed Aug. 23 - Dec. 14\, 2014\, except in the 
 case of injury\, long-term illness\, unforeseen move out of the Austin area
 \, or if we cancel a class. If\, however\, you let us know that you will mi
 ss a class\, you can substitute another class as long as there are places l
 eft in that class during the Fall 2014 semester.\n\nIn the case of physical
  injury or long-term illness\, we require a doctor's note saying the archer
  is unable to practice archery\, and then a doctor's note saying the archer
  is fit to return to archery\, before the archer will be allowed back in cl
 ass.\n\nATTENDANCE RECOMMENDATIONS in order to improve and advance: \nINDOO
 R 2 at 9m :        One or two 1.5-hr classes/wk.\nINDOOR 3A at 13.5m : Two 
 1.5-hr classes/wk.\nINDOOR 3B at 18m :    Two or three 1.5-hr classes/wk.\n
 INDOOR 4 at 18m (200-250 pts) :      \nTwo 1.5-hr classes/wk + one 1.5-hr M
 embers Open Practice/wk + one monthly private lesson\nINDOOR 5 at 18m (250-
 270 pts):       \nTwo 1.5-hr classes/wk + two 1.5-hr Members Open Practice/
 wk + one monthly private lesson\nINDOOR 6 at 18m (270-280 pts):       \nThr
 ee 1.5-hr classes/wk + two 1.5-hr Members Open Practice/wk + one monthly pr
 ivate lesson\nINDOOR 7 at 18m (280-290 pts)   \nThree 1.5-hr classes/wk + t
 hree 1.5-hr Members Open Practice/wk + one monthly private lesson\nJOAD OLY
 MPIANS - INDOOR 8 at 18m (290-300 pts):\nThree 1.5-hr classes/wk + three 1.
 5-hr Members Open Practice/wk + one monthly private lesson\n\nMINIMUM ENROL
 LMENT:\nClasses will be held only if there are 5 or more archers enrolled i
 n the class. \nIf the class does not make this minimum enrollment requireme
 nt\, you will be notified at least one week in advance\, so you can resched
 ule.\n\nHOW DO I ADVANCE?\nPlease note that starting in Fall 2014\, masteri
 ng NTS positions relevant to each level will be required to advance to the 
 next level\; advancement will no longer be based on scores alone.\n\nYou'll
  be trained in Indoor 4 at 18m until you score 250 pts and master most NTS*
  Shot Cycle positions. You'll then be in Indoor 5. At this point you'll nee
 d to consider whether you want to become a competitive archer or remain rec
 reational. \n\nIf you decide to train for competition\, you will be referre
 d to Coach Alex\, who will expect you to be able to explain to him and shoo
 t the NTS method\, and dedicate at least 10 hours a week to archery. \n\nIf
  you are recreational\, you will continue to work on your NTS form\, mental
  management\, and strength to eventually graduate into Indoor 6 by shooting
  270 pts at 18m\, into Indoor 7 by shooting 280 pts.\, and then Indoor 8 by
  shooting 290 pts\, when you will also shoot free in the recreational progr
 am forever! \n\nYou can also opt to become a USA Archery Level 1 NTS Instru
 ctor when you turn 15 years old\, and a Level 2 when you are 18 years old\,
  which bring additional privileges and responsibilities.\n\nFEES:\nAll fees
  are payable in advance of the class to secure your place in the class.\n$2
 0 / class\, if paid on or before August 3\, 2014 \n$21 / class\, if paid on
  or before August 24\, 2014 \n$22 / class\, if paid after August 24\, 2014.
 \n\n+ Enrollment fee: $20 (always due once per semester)\n\nPrivate Lessons
  (recommended at least once a month for Indoor 4 and above):\n$40/hr: USA A
 rchery Level 3 Coach Racae\n$30/hr: USA Archery Level 2 Instructor Luke or 
 Dale\n$20/hr  USA Archery Level 1 Instructor Chloe\n\nMembers Open Practice
  (times shown on website calendar): \nFree after you have attended two clas
 ses during the week before\, otherwise it is $10/practice time (1.5 hrs usu
 ally). \nThere is no coaching\; it's time for you to practice what you have
  learned!\n\nHOW MUCH DO I OWE? \nMultiply the number of classes x the appr
 opriate fee above.\nAdd the $20 semester enrollment fee\nAdd the number of 
 private one-hour lessons you want to schedule x the private lesson hourly f
 ee\n\nHOW DO I PAY IN ADVANCE?\nPay the total by Paypal using e-mail addres
 s: racae@aajoad.com.\nWe also accept checks and credit cards in person at t
 he indoor range.\nPlease make your check payable to "Archery Training Cente
 r\, Inc." and give it to us at JOAD* or mail it to us at:\nArchery Training
  Center\, Inc.\, PO Box 93216\, Austin\, TX 78709-3216\n\nSAFE SPORTS:\nPar
 ents please note we are part of the US Olympic Committee's Safe Sport progr
 am\, so we minimally require one other adult besides the instructor to be p
 resent at all times. Please plan to stay with your child or take turns with
  other parents staying whenever necessary to fulfill this requirement. THAN
 KS!\n\nWAIVERS:\nPlease fill out\, sign\, and return the Membership\, Liabi
 lity\, Photo\, Medical\, and Supervision Releases attached to the e-mail yo
 u received with your enrollment form link..\n\nQUESTIONS?\nE-mail us at rac
 ae@archerytrainingcenter.com or\nCall us at 512 436 8813\n\n*NTS = National
  Training System\n*JOAD = Junior Olympic Archery Development
