UID:cb6gr4b1gds930labopmhurjs8@google.com
CREATED:20160520T191906Z
DESCRIPTION:Coach Racae (Recurves only)\n\nClick the Sign Up button at the 
 top of ATCI website to Register for Indoor 1: First-time Classes for Adults
 . This is a requirement to join regular adult training classes.\nSaturdays:
  11:00am-1:30pm (Fee: $25/cl)\nSundays: 11:00am-1:30pm (Fee: $25/cl)\n\nEnr
 ollment links at:\nhttp://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/news\n\nADULT TRAIN
 ING CLASSES at Indoor 2-5 and distances (9m\, 13.5m\, 18m) \nSundays: 6:00-
 7:00pm (Fee: $20/cl) \nTuesdays: 7:30-8:30pm (Fee: $20/cl) \n\nPROGRESSIVE 
 PROGRAM Indoor 2-5\nJOAD and ADULT TRAINING for those who want to progress 
 faster toward competitive archery by meeting minimum attendance requirement
 s.\nSaturdays 3:30-5:30pm \nSundays:  3:30-5:30pm \nSundays:  6:00-7:00pm (
 Adults and Indoor 5 only)\nTuesdays: 6:30-7:30pm \nTuesdays: 7:30-8:30pm (A
 dults and Indoor 5 only) \nWednesdays: 6:30-8:00pm \n\nProgressive weekly f
 ees (after meeting previous week's attendance requirement):\nIndoor 3A at 1
 3.5m: $48/wk (min. 4 hrs)\nIndoor 3B at 18m:    $55/wk (min. 5 hrs)\nIndoor
  4 at 18m:      $60/wk (min. 6 hrs)\nIndoor 5 at 18m:      $72/wk (min. 8 h
 rs)\n\nUSA Archery's Adult Training Program (ATP) follows a similar path to
  the Junior Olympic Archery Development (JOAD) program. \n\nYour first step
  is to take an Indoor 1: First-time Class for Adults. Just click the link o
 r the Sign Up button at the top of this website.\n\nEveryone starts out in 
 our Recreational program at 9 meters. As you improve you progress to 13.5 m
 eters then on to 18 meters indoors. \n\nWe welcome adult recurve and compou
 nd Olympic target archers at all levels of experience. \nRecurve archers at
 tend any of the group classes above or book private lessons with Coach Raca
 e or Instructor Dale.\nCompound archers book private lessons with Coach Dan
  or Instructor Bailey.\n\nExperienced competitive archers need to be evalua
 ted by Coach Racae for advanced placement in either the Progressive Program
  or recommendation to the Competitive Archery Program with Coach Alex.\n\nW
 hen you decide that you are interested in competing you'll apply to join US
 A Archery Level 4 NTS and JDT Coach Alex Meyer's Competitive Archery Progra
 m (CAP).
LAST-MODIFIED:20260517T065947Z
LOCATION:10203 OLD Manchaca Rd.\, Austin\, TX 78748
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:ADULT Training
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
