UID:6hhqjafimpee9nsudavu07m3u9@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;VALUE=DATE:20220625
CREATED:20220524T151816Z
DESCRIPTION:<b>Tournaments are held at the end of each calendar month at 10
 :30 am - 12:30 pm on Saturdays and Sundays</b>\, weather permitting.&nbsp\;
 <u></u>If you are new to our program\, come and try it\, so you will be mor
 e comfortable and better prepared next month!<br><br><u></u>The only differ
 ences between the regular training sessions and the tournaments are that we
  are more closely reproducing tournament conditions\, which include:<u></u>
 <br><ul><li><u></u>No coaching while you are on the shooting line (but\, as
  in a real tournament\, y<u></u>ou can always ask the coach for help in bet
 ween the ends.) This is your chance to find out how well you can do the for
 m on your own\, and learn how to go into ¨trusting¨ compared with ¨training
 ¨ mode.</li><li><u></u>You will shoot more arrows :&nbsp\; 2 practice ends 
 + Two rounds -&nbsp\;<u></u>60 arrows at 9m and 13.5m or 72 arrows at 20m-7
 0m</li><li><u></u>You will score every arrow for two rounds.&nbsp\;<u></u><
 /li><li><u></u>The ends will be timed. You´ll have 4 min to shoot 6 arrows.
 <u></u></li><li>Everyone will be shooting at close-to-regular tournament sp
 acing so there will be two archers on each target about 3 ft apart\, depend
 ing on the number of registrations</li><li>There will be a maximum of 20 ar
 chers on the shooting line at the same time. Awesome! (Lots of arrow flying
  towards the targets!)</li></ul><br>Your goal is always to replicate the NT
 S step(s) mindfully and consistently on every shot.<br><u></u><b>Outside of
  the tournament weeks</b>\, each week the focus of your lessons will be on 
 particular Steps of Shooting of the NTS (National Training System) shot cyc
 le\, to help you focus and improve your form\, which\, as we all know\, lea
 ds to greater precision (tighter groups of arrows) and ultimately greater a
 ccuracy (tight groups of arrows dead center).<br><u></u><br><b>JUNE</b><br>
 <b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>2-5</b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;Welcome Summ
 er!&nbsp\; Understanding&nbsp\; NTS CONCEPTS<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;<
 /b><b>6-12&nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b>NTS Steps 1+2: STANCE + NOCK and<b> </b>NTS St
 ep 3: HOOK &amp\; GRIP<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;<b>13-23&nbsp\;</b>NTS Ste
 p 4: SET and NTS Step 5: SET-UP<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;25/</b><b>26 M
 ASTER CHALLENGE and STAR PIN SHOOT </b>(tournament)<br><b>JULY</b><br><b>&n
 bsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;2-3</b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; NTS Step 6 DRAW to LOAD
  and NTS Step 7 ANCHOR&nbsp\;<br><u></u>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;<b>4-10&nbsp
 \;&nbsp\;</b>&nbsp\; NTS Step 8 TRANSFER to HOLD<br><u></u><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp
 \; &nbsp\;11-17</b>&nbsp\; NTS Step 9 EXPAND / AIM<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp
 \;<b>18-24&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</b>NTS Step 10 RELEASE and FOLLOW-THROUGH<br><u></
 u><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>30/31:&nbsp\;</b><b>MASTER CHALLENGE and
  STAR PIN SHOOT&nbsp\;</b>(tournament)<br><b>AUGUST</b><br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp
 \; &nbsp\;1-7</b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;NTS Step 11 FEEDBACK&nbsp\;
 <br><u></u><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;8-14&nbsp\;</b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; PUTTING
  IT ALL TOGETHER !!<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\;<i>&nbsp\;<b> </b></i><b>20&nbsp\;</b
 > &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; <b style="font-style: italic\;">FALL SEMESTER BEG
 INS !!</b><br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;27/28:&nbsp\;</b><b>MASTER CHALLENG
 E and STAR PIN SHOOT&nbsp\;</b>(tournament)<br><br>You do not need to score
  every class. In fact\, it would be more beneficial to you if you scored on
 ly during Master Challenge Tournament Weeks\, which happen the last week of
  each month. This is because working on the NTS Steps of Shooting (your for
 m) is more easily done without the distraction of the target face or scorin
 g\, and you will improve faster.<br><br>As you reach higher levels\, you wi
 ll learn the NTS Steps in progressively greater detail.<br>The NTS Steps ar
 e cumulative with each step most successfully completed if the previous ste
 ps have been completed mindfully.&nbsp\;<br><br>Your ability to learn and u
 nderstand the NTS Steps\, and use deep focus on these Steps while shooting 
 outdoors and while using your stretchband/string loop at home will propel y
 ou to higher levels fast!<br><br><b>Goals by the end of the semester:&nbsp\
 ;</b><br>See Coach Racae´s email ¨2022 New Year´s Goals¨
LAST-MODIFIED:20260517T073156Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:10:30 am Outdoor 2-9 ATCI MASTER CHALLENGE and STAR PIN SHOOT
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
