DESCRIPTION:<h1>2025 TSAA State Indoors</h1><p>Here is the registration Lin
 k.</p><p><a href="https://eyesonscore.com/archer-registration-form/NG4zaE0y
 U29JbFBPOVcraUZqU1Zndz09" target="_blank"><u>https://eyesonscore.com/archer
 -registration-form/NG4zaE0yU29JbFBPOVcraUZqU1Zndz09</u></a></p><p><b>ATCI R
 egistered Archers:</b></p><p></p><ol><li><b>Coach Joel </b>SMR </li><li><b>
 Javier </b>SMR</li><li><b>Erika </b>SFR</li><li><b>Hannah </b>SFR</li><li><
 b>Lily</b> U18</li><li><b>Joseph </b>U18</li><li><b>Kishore </b>U18</li><li
 ><b>Finn </b>U15</li><li><b>Miles</b> U15</li><li><b>Riley </b>U15</li><li>
 <b>Abby </b>U15</li><li><b>Sofia</b> U15</li><li><b>Rhys</b> U13</li></ol><
 p></p><p>The 2025 Texas State Indoor Championships are set for January 11 a
 nd 12\, 2025 with a new location now available!</p><p>Fort Grard Guns &amp\
 ; Archery 3800 Mineral Wells Hwy\, Weatherford\, Texas 76088 for our North 
 Location\;</p><p><b>Kealing Middle School 1607 Pennsylvania Ave\, Austin\, 
 TX 78702 for our central location\;</b></p><p> <span>And Texas Archery Lear
 ning Center - 5833 Treaschwig Rd. Spring\, TX 77373 for our southeast locat
 ion.</span></p><p>Participants must be a member of USA Archery or the NFAA 
 with a temporary membership. International Guests (non U.S. citizens) - Ple
 ase go to <a href="http://www.usarchery.org" target="_blank">www.usarchery.
 org</a> to purchase a Temporary Membership for Foreign Nationals.</p><p>Arc
 hers will register to shoot a single 60 arrow World Archery indoor round on
  a 3-spot or single spot target on either Saturday or Sunday. Awards will b
 e mailed out for the divisions.</p><p>Divisions in the State Championship a
 re available for U13\, U15\, U18\, U21\, Senior\, 50+\, 60+ and 70+\, in Re
 curve\, Compound\, Barebow\, Fixed Pins\, Longbow\, and Para. </p><p>U13 an
 d U15 have the option to shoot a 60 cm face.</p><p>Line times are:</p><p>Sa
 turday 10:00 am and 2:00 pm</p><p>Sunday 10:00 am. We will open another lin
 e if we get all lines full before the shoot.</p><p>Registration is $60 for 
 U21\, Seniors\, 50+\, 60+\, and 70+ and $45 for Youth (U13\, U15\, and U18)
 \, plus a $1.99 service fee and any PayPal fees.</p><p>Registration is set 
 to check for age of participants based on the 2025 calendar year.</p><p>All
  divisions follow World Archery Rules except for Fixed Pins\, which follows
  the rules set by USA Archery.</p><p><b>Deadline for registration January 9
 th</b>.</p><p>For inquiries about registration please contact the event org
 anizer at: <a href="mailto:president@texasarchery.org" target="_blank">pres
 ident@texasarchery.org</a></p><p>Please Note: As a registered participant i
 n a USA Archery sanctioned event\, you are required to adhere to the Minor 
 Athlete Abuse Prevention Policies for the duration of the event.</p><p><br>
 </p>
