  field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae.&nbsp\;<br>Parents o
 f juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator.&nbsp\;<br>P
 arents of juniors 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with the
 ir child for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) 
 is accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-time Class.&nbsp\;<br><br>We will ac
 cept a limited&nbsp\;number of kids under 12 into the program each semester
 \, depending on the total&nbsp\; number of archers in all the classes. If y
 ou join before the limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay
  in the program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join O
 utdoor 2.&nbsp\;If you are under 12\, registered and paid after the cut off
 \, your fee will be returned to you.&nbsp\;<br><br>Juniors may need to take
  Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by sc
 oring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/en
 d of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into
  Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersl
 ing)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($18) Please pay for this at the
  field\, as our stock fluctuates because of dealer supply fluctuations<br>f
 p = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but really needed to
  practice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outd
 oor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a complete r
 ound (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, because it will
  have been averaged by taking your recorded score from your scorecard\, div
 iding by the number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then m
 ultiplying that by 30 to get a full round score. After the last class on th
 e weekend\, final scores will also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in
  an email with more information before your next class.<u></u></html-blob>
