  is to get to the next distance (+10m) by shooting 320 pts at your present 
 distance on a 122-cm target in one round of 36 arrows until you reach your 
 tournament distance as listed here:<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbs
 p\; &nbsp\; Masters: (50+) 60m&nbsp\;<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &n
 bsp\; &nbsp\; Seniors (21-50+) 70m\;<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nb
 sp\; &nbsp\; Juniors (18-20) 70m&nbsp\;<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; 
 &nbsp\; &nbsp\; Cadets (15-17) 60m&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;
  &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; Cubs (13-14) 50m&nbsp\;<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;
  &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; Bowman (10-12) 30m.<br><br>1. Lindsay L. 30m<br>2.
  Lily R. 20m<br>3. Kevin B.\, 20m (45 min make up for 1/2 of June 5)<br>4. 
 Yuhan\, 9m<br>5.<br>6.<br>7.<br>8.<br>9.<br>10.<br><br>OVERVIEW:<br>These O
 utdoor Target Archery recreational classes prepare you to shoot at longer a
 nd longer distances until you reach your USA Archery tournament distance (s
 ee below)\, while learning the National Training System\, which is the most
  highly researched biomechanical method of shooting taught out at the Olymp
 ic Training Center. You will be shooting with other archers in group sessio
 ns\, so you can all learn together and from each other. <br><br>PREREQUISIT
 E: <br>Some archery experience and your own recurve archery equipment is re
 quired.<br><br>OPEN TO ADULTS / JUNIORS / PARENTS (with experience and own 
 recurve archery equipment)<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator wil
 l be allowed on the field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae.<
 br>Space will be limited to a maximum of 10 archers per session or in accor
 dance with CDC Guidelines.<br><br>NO DROP INS:<br>You cannot just drop in\,
  because the number of archers on the shooting line is very limited and we 
 are observing CDC guidelines with social distancing.<br><br>DATES:    Start
  Dates: MAY 15 (Adults) or JUNE 12 (Juniors 10+) <br>&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&
 nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\
 ;Ending Date:  AUGUST 14  <br><br>ADDRESSES:<br>OUTDOOR FIELD SOUTH:    231
 0 Bliss Spillar Road\, Manchaca\, TX 78652<br>MAILING:  Archery Training Ce
 nter\, Inc.\, PO Box 93216\, Austin\, TX 78709<br><br>E-MAIL: <a href="mail
 to:archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com">archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail
 .com</a><br><br>PHONE/TEXT:  512 975 1850<br><br>CAPACITY:    10 archers pe
 r class or in accordance with CDC guidelines<br>AGES:             10 - 80+ 
 years old (See start dates above)<br>DISTANCES:  9m\, 13.5m\, 18m\, 20m-70m
 <br>BOWS:           Recurves  <br>(If you are not a recurve archer\, but wo
 uld like to learn to shoot a recurve bow\, please stay tuned to our Instagr
 am for announcements of the re-opening of our in-person First-time Classes\
 , or register online for a few Virtual NTS Form classes with Coach Racae.)<
 br><br>EQUIPMENT: <br>These classes are for archers who have their own equi
 pment\, consisting of at least a recurve bow\, 12 aluminum or carbon arrows
 \, armguard\, finger tab\, hip or field quiver.  (If you need to change you
 r equipment or order your own\, please contact Coach Racae at <a href="mail
 to:archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com">archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail
 .com</a>. She will specify what you´ll need and help you order it\, so you 
 buy the correct equipment for your strength and experience.)<br><br>INSTRUC
 TOR / COACH:<br>USA Archery Level 2 Instructor Ted Aanstoos  <br><br>CLASS 
 TIMES:<br>These are the days/times that are available to you. (Additional s
 essions will be added in future.)<br><br>SAT:     9:00-10:30pm <br>WED:    
 9:00-10:30pm <br>Please check <a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com
 /calendar">www.archerytrainingcenter.com/calendar</a> before registering!<b
 r><br>DAYS CLOSED: <br>The outdoor range is closed\, gates locked\, and tar
 gets stored away except during the above class times.<br><br>ENROLLMENT IS 
 ON A FIRST-RECEIVED AND PAID BASIS.<br>Complete the Outdoor Target Archery 
 Registration Form under Adults or Juniors at <a href="http://www.archerytra
 iningcenter.com">www.archerytrainingcenter.com</a><br><br>ATTENDANCE RECOMM
 ENDATIONS: <br>Recreational archers have no attendance requirements\, but w
 e would recommend attending at least twice a week to improve faster. <br><b
 r>FEES: <br>All fees are payable in advance of the class to secure your pla
 ce in the class. <br>$30/archer for each 1.5-hr training session  OR <br>$1
 15/mo (for 1 training session/week) OR <br>$213/mo (for 2 training sessions
 /week)<br>+ Enrollment fee: $20 (always due once per semester) <br><br>WEAT
 HER:<br>Archers need to practice in all weather\, except when there is ligh
 tning. <br><br>REFUNDS\, CREDITS\, and SUBSTITUTIONS:<br>Substitutions or c
 redits will be applied if we cancel a class due to weather conditions or in
 structor illness or if the 24-hr notice is met.<br>There are no refunds for
  paid classes missed during the summer\, except in the case of injury\, lon
 g-term illness\, unforeseen move out of the Austin area\, or being expelled
  for a safety violation. <br><br>24-HR NOTICE: <br>If you let us know withi
 n 24 hours of the class that you will miss the class\, you can substitute a
 nother class and use your fee as long as there are places left in that clas
 s during the semester. If you notify us less than 24 hours in advance of th
 e class that you will need to cancel (except for sudden illness)\, or you d
 o a "no-show"\, you'll forfeit your fee.<br><br>ILLNESS or INJURY: In the c
 ase of physical injury or long-term illness\, we require a doctor's note sa
 ying that you are unable to practice archery\, and then a doctor's note say
 ing that you are again fit to return to archery\, before you will be allowe
 d back in class or a refund/credit issued.<br><br>MEMBERSHIP IN USA ARCHERY
 :<br>Membership in USA Archery is now REQUIRED to participate in JOAD and A
 dult Training.<br>You can attend 2 sessions before joining USAA\, but then 
 we'll need to see your membership card BEFORE WE CAN HAND OUT ANY USA ARCHE
 RY STAR PINS to you during Master Challenge Weeks! <br>If you would like to
  see the benefits of USAA membership: <a href="http://www.teamusa.org/USA-A
 rchery/Membership/Membership-Benefits">http://www.teamusa.org/USA-Archery/M
 embership/Membership-Benefits</a><br>JOIN USA ARCHERY: <a href="https://www
 .usarchery.org/memberships/become-a-member">https://www.usarchery.org/membe
 rships/become-a-member</a><br><br>SAFE SPORTS:<br>PARENTS PLEASE NOTE: We a
 re part of the US Olympic Committee's Safe Sport program\, so we minimally 
 require one other adult besides the instructor to be present at all times. 
 Please plan to stay with your child or take turns with other parents stayin
 g whenever necessary to fulfill this requirement. THANKS!<br><br>SIGN AND R
 ETURN THESE OUTDOOR WAIVERS:<br>The following documents and waivers will be
  part of your Registration and Waiver Packet. You will need to sign these  
 documents before we add your name to those shooting in the class:<br>o Memb
 ership Form<br>o Safety Rules <br>o Release of Liability Waiver<br>o Superv
 ision Policy (Under 18)<br>o Medical Release  <br>o Photo/Video Release<br>
 o COVID-19 Guidelines<br>o Outdoor Field Rules of Participation <br><br>VAC
 CINATIONS:<br>We do not at this time require archers to be vaccinated\, but
  we would like to know if you have been\, so we can take it into considerat
 ion when deciding on issues such as masks and social distancing and abiding
  by the CDC Guidelines. All our instructors have been fully vaccinated of t
 heir own accord.<br><br>QUESTIONS?<br>E-mail us at <a href="mailto:archeryt
 rainingcenteraustin@gmail.com">archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a> or
 <br>Call/Text us at 512 975 1850 <br><br>*NTS = National Training System (w
 hich is used for training the USA Olympic team!)<br>*JDT = Junior Dream Tea
 m (top 20 Junior archers in the USA!)<br>*JOAD = Junior Olympic Archery Dev
 elopment
