  a year.)<u></u><br><br><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u>REGISTER NOW !<b
 r><br>Open to adult\, juniors 8+\, and parents! Please read all the info be
 low and in the registration and waivers.<br><br>More information\, registra
 tion forms and waivers are available at&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.archerytr
 ainingcenter.com"><u><u>www.archerytrainingcenter.com</u></u></a>.<br><br>R
 egister here using ONE of these forms:<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/
 forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfcwG419ZK9XmA4-JlXM-zhjhvSPCF8NCwWJlzFP2w-gRliUw/viewform
 "><u><u>2022 Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Juniors + Parents</u></u></a>&
 nbsp\; OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSe-YxPKAMTxi
 C7kVt6fZuQJeidXENYq_iV4rWj1RaXdLhPoew/viewform"><u><u>2022 Outdoor 1: First
 -time Class for Adults</u></u></a><br><br>Sign up for just ONE Outdoor 1 cl
 ass\, because most people graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after t
 he first lesson.<br><br>Your name will be added below and your place reserv
 ed on a&nbsp\;first registered and paid basis and after we receive 3 things
 :&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br><b>2022 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM&nbsp\; &nbsp\;+&nbsp
 \; MEMBERSHIP AND WAIVERS PACKET +&nbsp\; &nbsp\;FEE</b><b><br></b><u></u><
 br><br><b>If your name is PENDING\,&nbsp\;</b>it means we have not received
  one of the above three things in advance of the class. Your name will be r
 emoved\, if your space is needed by another person before we receive the ab
 ove. You will then need to reschedule.&nbsp\;<b><br></b><br><b>Registered a
 rchers&nbsp\;</b>at 9m on 40-cm target face unless otherwise noted below:<b
 r><br><b>Target Assignments:</b><br>1. (70m target)&nbsp\;<br>2. (40m targe
 t)<br>3. (30m target)<br>4. (20m target)<u></u><br><u></u><br>5A.&nbsp\;<u>
 </u><br><u></u>5B.<br>.<u></u><br><u></u><br>6A.<u></u><br><u></u>6B.<u></u
 ><br><u></u><br>7A.<u></u><br><u></u>7B.<u></u><br><u></u><br>8A.<u></u><br
 ><u></u>8B.<u></u><br><u></u>&nbsp\;<u></u><br><u></u>9A.<u></u><br><u></u>
 9B.<u></u><br><u></u><br>10A.<u></u><br><u></u>10B.<br>Space will be limite
 d to 10-15 archers per session depending on the number of family groups in 
 attendance or in accordance with CDC Guidelines.&nbsp\;<br>Each person will
  have a target stand\, except after 10 people have registered\, two members
  from the same family will share one target stand.<br>The archer and a maxi
 mum of one spectator will be allowed on the field until further notice or a
 pproved by Coach Racae.&nbsp\;<br>Parents of juniors 10+ can sign up as an 
 archer or watch as a spectator.&nbsp\;<br>Parents of juniors 8-9 years old 
 need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their child for greater safety.<br>
 <br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into each Outdoor 1:
  First-time Class.&nbsp\;<br><br>We will accept a limited&nbsp\;number of k
 ids under 12 into the program each semester\, depending on the total&nbsp\;
  number of archers in all the classes. If you join before the limit is reac
 hed\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take other O
 utdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;If you are under
  12\, registered and paid after the cut off\, your fee will be returned to 
 you.&nbsp\;<br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times be
 fore qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as 
 soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults 
 don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessor
 ies packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for 
 Outdoor 2. ($18) Please pay for this at the field\, as our stock fluctuates
  because of dealer supply fluctuations<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and s
 tring loop)\, optional but really needed to practice form\, warm up before 
 classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will b
 e posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not r
 ecognize your final score\, because it will have been averaged by taking yo
 ur recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrows yo
 u shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a f
 ull round score. After the last class on the weekend\, final scores will al
 so be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more information 
 before your next class.<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
