 evel 2 Instructor Ted Aanstoos  <br><br>CLASS TIMES:<br>These are the days/
 times that are available to you. (Additional sessions will be added in futu
 re.)<br><br>SAT:     9:00-10:30pm <br>WED:    9:00-10:30pm <br>Please check
  <a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/calendar">www.archerytrainin
 gcenter.com/calendar</a> before registering!<br><br>DAYS CLOSED: <br>The ou
 tdoor range is closed\, gates locked\, and targets stored away except durin
 g the above class times.<br><br>ENROLLMENT IS ON A FIRST-RECEIVED AND PAID 
 BASIS.<br>Complete the Outdoor Target Archery Registration Form under Adult
 s or Juniors at <a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.archeryt
 rainingcenter.com</a><br><br>ATTENDANCE RECOMMENDATIONS: <br>Recreational a
 rchers have no attendance requirements\, but we would recommend attending a
 t least twice a week to improve faster. <br><br>FEES: <br>All fees are paya
 ble in advance of the class to secure your place in the class. <br>$30/arch
 er for each 1.5-hr training session  OR <br>$115/mo (for 1 training session
 /week) OR <br>$213/mo (for 2 training sessions/week)<br>+ Enrollment fee: $
 20 (always due once per semester) <br><br>WEATHER:<br>Archers need to pract
 ice in all weather\, except when there is lightning. <br><br>REFUNDS\, CRED
 ITS\, and SUBSTITUTIONS:<br>Substitutions or credits will be applied if we 
 cancel a class due to weather conditions or instructor illness or if the 24
 -hr notice is met.<br>There are no refunds for paid classes missed during t
 he summer\, except in the case of injury\, long-term illness\, unforeseen m
 ove out of the Austin area\, or being expelled for a safety violation. <br>
 <br>24-HR NOTICE: <br>If you let us know within 24 hours of the class that 
 you will miss the class\, you can substitute another class and use your fee
  as long as there are places left in that class during the semester. If you
  notify us less than 24 hours in advance of the class that you will need to
  cancel (except for sudden illness)\, or you do a "no-show"\, you'll forfei
 t your fee.<br><br>ILLNESS or INJURY: In the case of physical injury or lon
 g-term illness\, we require a doctor's note saying that you are unable to p
 ractice archery\, and then a doctor's note saying that you are again fit to
  return to archery\, before you will be allowed back in class or a refund/c
 redit issued.<br><br>MEMBERSHIP IN USA ARCHERY:<br>Membership in USA Archer
 y is now REQUIRED to participate in JOAD and Adult Training.<br>You can att
 end 2 sessions before joining USAA\, but then we'll need to see your member
 ship card BEFORE WE CAN HAND OUT ANY USA ARCHERY STAR PINS to you during Ma
 ster Challenge Weeks! <br>If you would like to see the benefits of USAA mem
 bership: <a href="http://www.teamusa.org/USA-Archery/Membership/Membership-
 Benefits">http://www.teamusa.org/USA-Archery/Membership/Membership-Benefits
 </a><br>JOIN USA ARCHERY: <a href="https://www.usarchery.org/memberships/be
 come-a-member">https://www.usarchery.org/memberships/become-a-member</a><br
 ><br>SAFE SPORTS:<br>PARENTS PLEASE NOTE: We are part of the US Olympic Com
 mittee's Safe Sport program\, so we minimally require one other adult besid
 es the instructor to be present at all times. Please plan to stay with your
  child or take turns with other parents staying whenever necessary to fulfi
 ll this requirement. THANKS!<br><br>SIGN AND RETURN THESE OUTDOOR WAIVERS:<
 br>The following documents and waivers will be part of your Registration an
 d Waiver Packet. You will need to sign these  documents before we add your 
 name to those shooting in the class:<br>o Membership Form<br>o Safety Rules
  <br>o Release of Liability Waiver<br>o Supervision Policy (Under 18)<br>o 
 Medical Release  <br>o Photo/Video Release<br>o COVID-19 Guidelines<br>o Ou
 tdoor Field Rules of Participation <br><br>VACCINATIONS:<br>We do not at th
 is time require archers to be vaccinated\, but we would like to know if you
  have been\, so we can take it into consideration when deciding on issues s
 uch as masks and social distancing and abiding by the CDC Guidelines. All o
 ur instructors have been fully vaccinated of their own accord.<br><br>QUEST
 IONS?<br>E-mail us at <a href="mailto:archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com
 ">archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a> or<br>Call/Text us at 512 975 1
 850 <br><br>*NTS = National Training System (which is used for training the
  USA Olympic team!)<br>*JDT = Junior Dream Team (top 20 Junior archers in t
 he USA!)<br>*JOAD = Junior Olympic Archery Development
