DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u>REG
 ISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to adult\, juniors 8+\, and parents! Please read al
 l the info below and in the registration and waivers.<br><br>More informati
 on\, registration forms and waivers are available at&nbsp\;<a href="http://
 www.archerytrainingcenter.com"><u><u>www.archerytrainingcenter.com</u></u><
 /a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE of these forms:<br><a href="https://doc
 s.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfcwG419ZK9XmA4-JlXM-zhjhvSPCF8NCwWJlzFP2w-gR
 liUw/viewform"><u><u>2022 Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Juniors + Parents
 </u></u></a>&nbsp\; OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQ
 LSe-YxPKAMTxiC7kVt6fZuQJeidXENYq_iV4rWj1RaXdLhPoew/viewform"><u><u>2022 Out
 door 1: First-time Class for Adults</u></u></a><br><br>Sign up for just ONE
  Outdoor 1 class\, because most people graduate out of this class into Outd
 oor 2 after the first lesson.<br><br>Your name will be added below and your
  place reserved on a&nbsp\;first registered and paid basis and after we rec
 eive 3 things:&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br><b>2022 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM&nbsp\; 
 &nbsp\;+&nbsp\; MEMBERSHIP AND WAIVERS PACKET +&nbsp\; &nbsp\;FEE</b><br><b
 r><br><b>If your name is PENDING\,&nbsp\;</b>it means we have not received 
 one of the above three things in advance of the class. Your name will be re
 moved\, if your space is needed by another person before we receive the abo
 ve. You will then need to reschedule.&nbsp\;<b><br></b><br><b>Registered ar
 chers&nbsp\;</b>at 9m on 40-cm target face unless otherwise noted below:<br
 ><b>Target Assignments:</b><br>1. (70m target)&nbsp\;<br>2. (40m target)<br
 >3. (30m target)<br>4. (20m target)<br><br>5A.&nbsp\;<b>Paul M.\,&nbsp\;</b
 >adult - pd - substituted for 9/11 - <b>106 pts (averaged) -&gt\; Outdoor 2
 </b><br>5B.&nbsp\;<b>Lauren F.\,&nbsp\;</b>adult - pd - substituted for 9/1
 1 - <b>85 pts (averaged) -&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br><br>6A. <b>Angela B.\, </b
 >adult - check - -&gt\; <b>Outdoor 2</b><br>6B.<br><br>7A. <b>Dave L.\, </b
 >adult - pd - <b>124 pts (averaged)-&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br>7B.&nbsp\;<b>Eva
 n J</b>.\, adult - pd - <b>93 pts (averaged) -&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br><br>8A
 . <b>Alex F.</b>\, 15 - pd - <b>173 pts (averaged) -&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br>
 8B.<br>&nbsp\;<u></u><br><u></u>9A. <b>Eben P.\, </b>adult - pd - <b>79 pts
  (averaged) -&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br>9B.&nbsp\;<br><br>10A.&nbsp\;<b>Love La
 lla P</b>.\, 9\, pd - on 60-cm target face - <b>34 pts (averaged)-&gt\; Out
 door 1</b><br>10B.<u></u><br><u></u><br>Space will be limited to 10-15 arch
 ers per session depending on the number of family groups in attendance or i
 n accordance with CDC Guidelines.&nbsp\;<br>The archer and a maximum of one
  spectator will be allowed on the field until further notice or approved by
  Coach Racae.&nbsp\;<br>Parents of juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or 
 watch as a spectator.&nbsp\;<br>Parents of juniors 8-9 years old need to re
 gister\, pay\, and shoot with their child for greater safety.<br><br>A maxi
 mum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-tim
 e Class.&nbsp\;<br><br>We will accept a limited&nbsp\;number of kids under 
 12 into the program each semester\, depending on the total&nbsp\; number of
  archers in all the classes. If you join before the limit is reached\, and 
 are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take other Outdoor 1 c
 lasses as needed and later join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;If you are under 12\, regi
 stered and paid after the cut off\, your fee will be returned to you.&nbsp\
 ;<br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times before quali
 fying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as yo
 u score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need
  a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet
  (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2.
  ($18) Please pay for this at the field\, as our stock fluctuates because o
 f dealer supply fluctuations<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string loop
 )\, optional but really needed to practice form\, warm up before classes ($
 4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. 
 If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize y
 our final score\, because it will have been averaged by taking your recorde
 d score from your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot to 
 get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round 
 score. After the last class on the weekend\, final scores will also be sent
  to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more information before you
 r next class.<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
