DESCRIPTION:Registered Archers:<br>Once you are shooting at 20m\, your goal
  is to get to the next distance (+10m) by shooting 320 pts at your present 
 distance on a 122-cm target in one round of 36 arrows until you reach your 
 tournament distance as listed here:<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbs
 p\; &nbsp\; Masters: (50+) 60m&nbsp\;<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &n
 bsp\; &nbsp\; Seniors (21-50+) 70m<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp
 \; &nbsp\; Juniors (18-20) 70m&nbsp\;<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &n
 bsp\; &nbsp\; Cadets (15-17) 60m&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &
 nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; Cubs (13-14) 50m&nbsp\;<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &
 nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; Bowman (10-12) 30m.<br><br>1. Nate H.\, 20m on 122-c
 m target face - DNA&nbsp\;<br>2. Cyrenna V. 13.5m on 40-cm target face (45 
 min make up for 1/2 of June 5)<br>3. Yuhan X.\, 9m on 60-cm target face (JO
 AD target)<br>4..Kevin B.\, 20m on 122-cm target face<br>5.<br>6.<br>7.<br>
 8.<br>9.<br>10.<br><br>OVERVIEW:<br>These Outdoor Target Archery recreation
 al classes prepare you to shoot at longer and longer distances until you re
 ach your USA Archery tournament distance (see below)\, while learning the N
 ational Training System\, which is the most highly researched biomechanical
  method of shooting taught out at the Olympic Training Center. You will be 
 shooting with other archers in group sessions\, so you can all learn togeth
 er and from each other. <br><br>PREREQUISITE: <br>Some archery experience a
 nd your own recurve archery equipment is required.<br><br>OPEN TO ADULTS / 
 JUNIORS / PARENTS (with experience and own recurve archery equipment)<br>Th
 e archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field until 
 further notice or approved by Coach Racae.<br>Space will be limited to a ma
 ximum of 10 archers per session or in accordance with CDC Guidelines.<br><b
 r>NO DROP INS:<br>You cannot just drop in\, because the number of archers o
 n the shooting line is very limited and we are observing CDC guidelines wit
 h social distancing.<br><br>DATES:    Start Dates: MAY 15 (Adults) or JUNE 
 12 (Juniors 10+) <br>&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp
 \;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;Ending Date:  AUGUST 14  <br><b
 r>ADDRESSES:<br>OUTDOOR FIELD SOUTH:    2310 Bliss Spillar Road\, Manchaca\
 , TX 78652<br>MAILING:  Archery Training Center\, Inc.\, PO Box 93216\, Aus
 tin\, TX 78709<br><br>E-MAIL: <a href="mailto:archerytrainingcenteraustin@g
 mail.com">archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a><br><br>PHONE/TEXT:  512
  975 1850<br><br>CAPACITY:    10 archers per class or in accordance with CD
 C guidelines<br>AGES:             10 - 80+ years old (See start dates above
 )<br>DISTANCES:  9m\, 13.5m\, 18m\, 20m-70m<br>BOWS:           Recurves  <b
 r>(If you are not a recurve archer\, but would like to learn to shoot a rec
 urve bow\, please stay tuned to our Instagram for announcements of the re-o
 pening of our in-person First-time Classes\, or register online for a few V
 irtual NTS Form classes with Coach Racae.)<br><br>EQUIPMENT: <br>These clas
 ses are for archers who have their own equipment\, consisting of at least a
  recurve bow\, 12 aluminum or carbon arrows\, armguard\, finger tab\, hip o
 r field quiver.  (If you need to change your equipment or order your own\, 
 please contact Coach Racae at <a href="mailto:archerytrainingcenteraustin@g
 mail.com">archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a>. She will specify what 
 you´ll need and help you order it\, so you buy the correct equipment for yo
 ur strength and experience.)<br><br>INSTRUCTOR / COACH:<br>USA Archery Leve
 l 2 Instructor Ted Aanstoos  <br><br>CLASS TIMES:<br>These are the days/tim
 es that are available to you. (Additional sessions will be added in future.
 )<br><br>SAT:     9:00-10:30pm <br>WED:    9:00-10:30pm <br>Please check <a
  href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/calendar">www.archerytrainingce
 nter.com/calendar</a> before registering!<br><br>DAYS CLOSED: <br>The outdo
 or range is closed\, gates locked\, and targets stored away except during t
 he above class times.<br><br>ENROLLMENT IS ON A FIRST-RECEIVED AND PAID BAS
 IS.<br>Complete the Outdoor Target Archery Registration Form under Adults o
 r Juniors at <a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrai
 ningcenter.com</a><br><br>ATTENDANCE RECOMMENDATIONS: <br>Recreational arch
 ers have no attendance requirements\, but we would recommend attending at l
 east twice a week to improve faster. <br><br>FEES: <br>All fees are payable
  in advance of the class to secure your place in the class. <br>$30/archer 
 for each 1.5-hr training session  OR <br>$115/mo (for 1 training session/we
 ek) OR <br>$213/mo (for 2 training sessions/week)<br>+ Enrollment fee: $20 
 (always due once per semester) <br><br>WEATHER:<br>Archers need to practice
  in all weather\, except when there is lightning. <br><br>REFUNDS\, CREDITS
 \, and SUBSTITUTIONS:<br>Substitutions or credits will be applied if we can
 cel a class due to weather conditions or instructor illness or if the 24-hr
  notice is met.<br>There are no refunds for paid classes missed during the 
 summer\, except in the case of injury\, long-term illness\, unforeseen move
  out of the Austin area\, or being expelled for a safety violation. <br><br
 >24-HR NOTICE: <br>If you let us know within 24 hours of the class that you
  will miss the class\, you can substitute another class and use your fee as
  long as there are places left in that class during the semester. If you no
 tify us less than 24 hours in advance of the class that you will need to ca
 ncel (except for sudden illness)\, or you do a "no-show"\, you'll forfeit y
 our fee.<br><br>ILLNESS or INJURY: In the case of physical injury or long-t
 erm illness\, we require a doctor's note saying that you are unable to prac
 tice archery\, and then a doctor's note saying that you are again fit to re
 turn to archery\, before you will be allowed back in class or a refund/cred
 it issued.<br><br>MEMBERSHIP IN USA ARCHERY:<br>Membership in USA Archery i
 s now REQUIRED to participate in JOAD and Adult Training.<br>You can attend
  2 sessions before joining USAA\, but then we'll need to see your membershi
 p card BEFORE WE CAN HAND OUT ANY USA ARCHERY STAR PINS to you during Maste
 r Challenge Weeks! <br>If you would like to see the benefits of USAA member
 ship: <a href="http://www.teamusa.org/USA-Archery/Membership/Membership-Ben
 efits">http://www.teamusa.org/USA-Archery/Membership/Membership-Benefits</a
 ><br>JOIN USA ARCHERY: <a href="https://www.usarchery.org/memberships/becom
 e-a-member">https://www.usarchery.org/memberships/become-a-member</a><br><b
 r>SAFE SPORTS:<br>PARENTS PLEASE NOTE: We are part of the US Olympic Commit
 tee's Safe Sport program\, so we minimally require one other adult besides 
 the instructor to be present at all times. Please plan to stay with your ch
 ild or take turns with other parents staying whenever necessary to fulfill 
 this requirement. THANKS!<br><br>SIGN AND RETURN THESE OUTDOOR WAIVERS:<br>
 The following documents and waivers will be part of your Registration and W
 aiver Packet. You will need to sign these  documents before we add your nam
 e to those shooting in the class:<br>o Membership Form<br>o Safety Rules <b
 r>o Release of Liability Waiver<br>o Supervision Policy (Under 18)<br>o Med
 ical Release  <br>o Photo/Video Release<br>o COVID-19 Guidelines<br>o Outdo
 or Field Rules of Participation <br><br>VACCINATIONS:<br>We do not at this 
 time require archers to be vaccinated\, but we would like to know if you ha
 ve been\, so we can take it into consideration when deciding on issues such
  as masks and social distancing and abiding by the CDC Guidelines. All our 
 instructors have been fully vaccinated of their own accord.<br><br>QUESTION
 S?<br>E-mail us at <a href="mailto:archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com">a
 rcherytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a> or<br>Call/Text us at 512 975 1850
  <br><br>*NTS = National Training System (which is used for training the US
 A Olympic team!)<br>*JDT = Junior Dream Team (top 20 Junior archers in the 
 USA!)<br>*JOAD = Junior Olympic Archery Development
