DESCRIPTION:Coach Racae will be on the field<br>Registered Archers:<br>1. L
 ily R. 30m - paid<br>2. Yuhan X.\, 9m on 60-cm target face - paid<br>3. Lin
 dsay L. 30m on 122-cm target<br>4..<br>5.<br>6.<br>7.<br>8.<br>9.<br>10.<br
 ><br>OVERVIEW:<br>These Outdoor Target Archery recreational classes prepare
  you to shoot at longer and longer distances until you reach your USA Arche
 ry tournament distance (see below)\, while learning the National Training S
 ystem\, which is the most highly researched biomechanical method of shootin
 g taught out at the Olympic Training Center. You will be shooting with othe
 r archers in group sessions\, so you can all learn together and from each o
 ther. <br><br>PREREQUISITE: <br>Some archery experience and your own recurv
 e archery equipment is required.<br><br>OPEN TO ADULTS / JUNIORS / PARENTS 
 (with experience and own recurve archery equipment)<br>The archer and a max
 imum of one spectator will be allowed on the field until further notice or 
 approved by Coach Racae.<br>Space will be limited to a maximum of 10 archer
 s per session or in accordance with CDC Guidelines.<br><br>NO DROP INS:<br>
 You cannot just drop in\, because the number of archers on the shooting lin
 e is very limited and we are observing CDC guidelines with social distancin
 g.<br><br>DATES:    Start Dates: MAY 15 (Adults) or JUNE 12 (Juniors 10+) <
 br>&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&n
 bsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;Ending Date:  AUGUST 14  <br><br>ADDRESSES:<br>OU
 TDOOR FIELD SOUTH:    2310 Bliss Spillar Road\, Manchaca\, TX 78652<br>MAIL
 ING:  Archery Training Center\, Inc.\, PO Box 93216\, Austin\, TX 78709<br>
 <br>E-MAIL: <a href="mailto:archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com">archeryt
 rainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a><br><br>PHONE/TEXT:  512 975 1850<br><br>C
 APACITY:    10 archers per class or in accordance with CDC guidelines<br>AG
 ES:             10 - 80+ years old (See start dates above)<br>DISTANCES:  9
 m\, 13.5m\, 18m\, 20m-70m<br>BOWS:           Recurves  <br>(If you are not 
 a recurve archer\, but would like to learn to shoot a recurve bow\, please 
 stay tuned to our Instagram for announcements of the re-opening of our in-p
 erson First-time Classes\, or register online for a few Virtual NTS Form cl
 asses with Coach Racae.)<br><br>EQUIPMENT: <br>These classes are for archer
 s who have their own equipment\, consisting of at least a recurve bow\, 12 
 aluminum or carbon arrows\, armguard\, finger tab\, hip or field quiver.  (
 If you need to change your equipment or order your own\, please contact Coa
 ch Racae at <a href="mailto:archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com">archeryt
 rainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a>. She will specify what you´ll need and he
 lp you order it\, so you buy the correct equipment for your strength and ex
 perience.)<br><br>INSTRUCTOR / COACH:<br>USA Archery Level 2 Instructor Ted
  Aanstoos  <br><br>CLASS TIMES:<br>These are the days/times that are availa
 ble to you. (Additional sessions will be added in future.)<br><br>SAT:     
 9:00-10:30pm <br>WED:    9:00-10:30pm <br>Please check <a href="http://www.
 archerytrainingcenter.com/calendar">www.archerytrainingcenter.com/calendar<
 /a> before registering!<br><br>DAYS CLOSED: <br>The outdoor range is closed
 \, gates locked\, and targets stored away except during the above class tim
 es.<br><br>ENROLLMENT IS ON A FIRST-RECEIVED AND PAID BASIS.<br>Complete th
 e Outdoor Target Archery Registration Form under Adults or Juniors at <a hr
 ef="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrainingcenter.com</a>
 <br><br>ATTENDANCE RECOMMENDATIONS: <br>Recreational archers have no attend
 ance requirements\, but we would recommend attending at least twice a week 
 to improve faster. <br><br>FEES: <br>All fees are payable in advance of the
  class to secure your place in the class. <br>$30/archer for each 1.5-hr tr
 aining session  OR <br>$115/mo (for 1 training session/week) OR <br>$213/mo
  (for 2 training sessions/week)<br>+ Enrollment fee: $20 (always due once p
 er semester) <br><br>WEATHER:<br>Archers need to practice in all weather\, 
 except when there is lightning. <br><br>REFUNDS\, CREDITS\, and SUBSTITUTIO
 NS:<br>Substitutions or credits will be applied if we cancel a class due to
  weather conditions or instructor illness or if the 24-hr notice is met.<br
 >There are no refunds for paid classes missed during the summer\, except in
  the case of injury\, long-term illness\, unforeseen move out of the Austin
  area\, or being expelled for a safety violation. <br><br>24-HR NOTICE: <br
 >If you let us know within 24 hours of the class that you will miss the cla
 ss\, you can substitute another class and use your fee as long as there are
  places left in that class during the semester. If you notify us less than 
 24 hours in advance of the class that you will need to cancel (except for s
 udden illness)\, or you do a "no-show"\, you'll forfeit your fee.<br><br>IL
 LNESS or INJURY: In the case of physical injury or long-term illness\, we r
 equire a doctor's note saying that you are unable to practice archery\, and
  then a doctor's note saying that you are again fit to return to archery\, 
 before you will be allowed back in class or a refund/credit issued.<br><br>
 MEMBERSHIP IN USA ARCHERY:<br>Membership in USA Archery is now REQUIRED to 
 participate in JOAD and Adult Training.<br>You can attend 2 sessions before
  joining USAA\, but then we'll need to see your membership card BEFORE WE C
 AN HAND OUT ANY USA ARCHERY STAR PINS to you during Master Challenge Weeks!
  <br>If you would like to see the benefits of USAA membership: <a href="htt
 p://www.teamusa.org/USA-Archery/Membership/Membership-Benefits">http://www.
 teamusa.org/USA-Archery/Membership/Membership-Benefits</a><br>JOIN USA ARCH
 ERY: <a href="https://www.usarchery.org/memberships/become-a-member">https:
 //www.usarchery.org/memberships/become-a-member</a><br><br>SAFE SPORTS:<br>
 PARENTS PLEASE NOTE: We are part of the US Olympic Committee's Safe Sport p
 rogram\, so we minimally require one other adult besides the instructor to 
 be present at all times. Please plan to stay with your child or take turns 
 with other parents staying whenever necessary to fulfill this requirement. 
 THANKS!<br><br>SIGN AND RETURN THESE OUTDOOR WAIVERS:<br>The following docu
 ments and waivers will be part of your Registration and Waiver Packet. You 
 will need to sign these  documents before we add your name to those shootin
 g in the class:<br>o Membership Form<br>o Safety Rules <br>o Release of Lia
 bility Waiver<br>o Supervision Policy (Under 18)<br>o Medical Release  <br>
 o Photo/Video Release<br>o COVID-19 Guidelines<br>o Outdoor Field Rules of 
 Participation <br><br>VACCINATIONS:<br>We do not at this time require arche
 rs to be vaccinated\, but we would like to know if you have been\, so we ca
 n take it into consideration when deciding on issues such as masks and soci
 al distancing and abiding by the CDC Guidelines. All our instructors have b
 een fully vaccinated of their own accord.<br><br>QUESTIONS?<br>E-mail us at
  <a href="mailto:archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com">archerytrainingcent
 eraustin@gmail.com</a> or<br>Call/Text us at 512 975 1850 <br><br>*NTS = Na
 tional Training System (which is used for training the USA Olympic team!)<b
 r>*JDT = Junior Dream Team (top 20 Junior archers in the USA!)<br>*JOAD = J
 unior Olympic Archery Development
