 ers. <b>Get ready for the Winter/Spring Classes\, which start on Sat.\, Jan
 . 7\, 2023.</b><br /><br />More information\, registration forms and waiver
 s are available at <a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com"><u><u>www
 .archerytrainingcenter.com</u></u></a>.<br /><br />Register here using ONE 
 of these forms:<br /><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfcw
 G419ZK9XmA4-JlXM-zhjhvSPCF8NCwWJlzFP2w-gRliUw/viewform"><u><u>2022 Outdoor 
 1: First-time Class for Juniors + Parents</u></u></a>  OR<br /><a href="htt
 ps://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSe-YxPKAMTxiC7kVt6fZuQJeidXENYq_iV4rW
 j1RaXdLhPoew/viewform"><u><u>2022 Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Adults</u
 ></u></a><br /><br />Sign up for just ONE Outdoor 1 class\, because most pe
 ople graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br /
 ><br />Your name will be added below and your place reserved on a first reg
 istered and paid basis and after we receive 3 things:  <br /><b>2022 OUTDOO
 R 1 REGISTRATION FORM   +  MEMBERSHIP AND WAIVERS PACKET +   FEE</b><b><br 
 /></b><br /><b>USA Archery Level 4 NTS Coach Racae Meyer</b><br /><b>USA Ar
 chery Level 3 NTS Coach Lindsay Rerecich<br /></b><br /><b>Registered arche
 rs </b>at 9m on 40-cm target face unless otherwise noted below.<br /><br />
 <b>Target Assignments:</b><br />1. (70m target)<br />2. (40m target)<br />3
 . (30m target)<br />4. (20m target)<br /><br />5A. <b>Steven A.</b>\, adult
 \, pd  - <b>183 pts</b><br /><span>5B.</span><br /><br />6A. <b>Alan A.</b>
 \, adult\, pd - <b>154 pts</b><br />6B. <br /><br />7A. <b>Janet R.</b>\, a
 dult\, pd - <b>60 pts</b><br />7B.<br /><br />8A. <b>Christine N.\, </b>adu
 lt\, pd - <b>45 pts</b><br />8B.<br /><br />9A. <b>Munira A-K.\, </b>adult\
 , pd - <b>53 pts</b><br />9B.<br /><br />10A. <b>Samantha A.\,</b> 12\, on 
 60-cm target facde - pd - <b>88 pts -&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br />10B. <br /><b
 r /><b>Lauren H</b>.\, adult\, pd - changed to 1/7\, and then to 1/14<br />
 <br />Space will be limited to 10-15 archers per session depending on the n
 umber of family groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC Guidelines. 
 <br />Each person will have a target stand\, except after 10 people have re
 gistered\, two members from the same family will share one target stand.<br
  />The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field u
 ntil further notice or approved by Coach Racae. <br />Parents of juniors 10
 + can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator. <br />Parents of junior
 s 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their child for gre
 ater safety.<br /><br />A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted 
 into each Outdoor 1: First-time Class. <br /><br />We will accept a limited
  number of kids under 12 into the program each semester\, depending on the 
 total  number of archers in all the classes. If you join before the limit i
 s reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take o
 ther Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2. If you are under
  12\, registered and paid after the cut off\, your fee will be returned to 
 you. <br /><br />Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times befo
 re qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as so
 on as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows. <br />Adults don´t 
 need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br /><br />ap = accessorie
 s packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for Ou
 tdoor 2. ($18) Please pay for this at the field\, as our stock fluctuates b
 ecause of dealer supply fluctuations<br />fp = form pack (stretchband and s
 tring loop)\, optional but really needed to practice form\, warm up before 
 classes ($4)<br /><br />At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores wi
 ll be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may n
 ot recognize your final score\, because it will have been averaged by takin
 g your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrow
 s you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get
  a full round score. After the last class on the weekend\, final scores wil
 l also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more informat
 ion before your next class.<u></u>
