DESCRIPTION:At least 5 archers need to be in attendance for Coach Racae to 
 coach the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class alone. In the case of low registration
 s\, another coach/instructor may be coaching the class.\n\nRegistration for
 m: OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m\n\nAdd your name to Target Assignment List belo
 w or submit the above completed form.\nFocus primarily on perfecting your f
 orm\, \nslowly increasing your physical strength and draw weight\, \nstreng
 thening your mental program\, \ndetermining your average and personal best\
 , \nunderstanding the spread between the two\, and working on closing it.\n
 \nYou need your own equipment \nCompetition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilize
 r\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\,
  chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quive
 r\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added until you r
 each a higher level\, but you should order them in advance.) \n\nWear your 
 ATCI shirt to training.\n\nWhen you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on th
 e 122-cm target face you'll move back to the next distance until you reach 
 your competition distance\nIf you trained outdoors in the 2024 season\, you
 'll return to the farthest distance you shot.\n\nTarget arrangements may va
 ry each session\, depending on who attends and distances needed.\nTarget 1 
 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should always stay at 70m so Ja
 ke can use it for independent practice in between classes.\nTarget 2 at 60m
  (U18 + Masters competition distance) \nTarget 3 at 50m\nTarget 4 at 40m (U
 15 competition distance) \nTarget 5 at 30m (U13 competition distance) \nTar
 gets 6+7+8 at 20m (for those who have shot at 18m indoors or with Coach Rac
 ae's approval)\nTargets 9 + 10 at 13.5m (for those who have just graduated 
 from indoors at 9m)\n\nIdeally\, we want to practice with two archers/targe
 t to replicate competition conditions as much as possible.\n\nTarget Assign
 ments:\nTargets are assigned outdoors in advance to reduce confusion and de
 lay on the day\,\nso add your name next to your distance below. \nIf you ne
 ed help or have questions\, email/text Coach Racae\n(Dotted lines represent
  tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)\n-----------------------------
 -----\n1A. (70m)\n1B\n\n2A. (60m)  Joel Y\, adult\, USAA\, pd\n2B\n\n3A. (5
 0m)  Abby Y\, 13\, USAA\, pd\n----------------------------------\n3B\n\n4A.
  (40m) \n4B. Luke T\, 16\, USAA\, pd\n----------------------------------\n5
 A. (40m)\n5B. \n\n6A. (30m) Ellie Y\, 10\, pd\n----------------------------
