DESCRIPTION:Registered Archers:<br>1. Kevin B.\, 20m on 122cm target face<b
 r>2. Yuhan X.\, 9m on 60-cm target face - paid<br>3. Andrew M.\, at 30m on 
 122-cm target face - paid - substitute for canceled 7/10?)<br>4..<br>5.&nbs
 p\; Cyrenna V. at 20m on 122-cm target face<br>6.<br>7.<br>8.<br>9.<br>10.<
 br><br>OVERVIEW:<br>These Outdoor Target Archery recreational classes prepa
 re you to shoot at longer and longer distances until you reach your USA Arc
 hery tournament distance (see below)\, while learning the National Training
  System\, which is the most highly researched biomechanical method of shoot
 ing taught out at the Olympic Training Center. You will be shooting with ot
 her archers in group sessions\, so you can all learn together and from each
  other. <br><br>PREREQUISITE: <br>Some archery experience and your own recu
 rve archery equipment is required.<br><br>OPEN TO ADULTS / JUNIORS / PARENT
 S (with experience and own recurve archery equipment)<br>The archer and a m
 aximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field until further notice o
 r approved by Coach Racae.<br>Space will be limited to a maximum of 10 arch
 ers per session or in accordance with CDC Guidelines.<br><br>NO DROP INS:<b
 r>You cannot just drop in\, because the number of archers on the shooting l
 ine is very limited and we are observing CDC guidelines with social distanc
 ing.<br><br>DATES:    Start Dates: MAY 15 (Adults) or JUNE 12 (Juniors 10+)
  <br>&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;
 &nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;Ending Date:  AUGUST 14  <br><br>ADDRESSES:<br>
 OUTDOOR FIELD SOUTH:    2310 Bliss Spillar Road\, Manchaca\, TX 78652<br>MA
 ILING:  Archery Training Center\, Inc.\, PO Box 93216\, Austin\, TX 78709<b
 r><br>E-MAIL: <a href="mailto:archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com">archer
 ytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a><br><br>PHONE/TEXT:  512 975 1850<br><br
 >CAPACITY:    10 archers per class or in accordance with CDC guidelines<br>
 AGES:             10 - 80+ years old (See start dates above)<br>DISTANCES: 
  9m\, 13.5m\, 18m\, 20m-70m<br>BOWS:           Recurves  <br>(If you are no
 t a recurve archer\, but would like to learn to shoot a recurve bow\, pleas
 e stay tuned to our Instagram for announcements of the re-opening of our in
 -person First-time Classes\, or register online for a few Virtual NTS Form 
 classes with Coach Racae.)<br><br>EQUIPMENT: <br>These classes are for arch
 ers who have their own equipment\, consisting of at least a recurve bow\, 1
 2 aluminum or carbon arrows\, armguard\, finger tab\, hip or field quiver. 
  (If you need to change your equipment or order your own\, please contact C
 oach Racae at <a href="mailto:archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com">archer
 ytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a>. She will specify what you´ll need and 
 help you order it\, so you buy the correct equipment for your strength and 
 experience.)<br><br>INSTRUCTOR / COACH:<br>USA Archery Level 2 Instructor T
 ed Aanstoos  <br><br>CLASS TIMES:<br>These are the days/times that are avai
 lable to you. (Additional sessions will be added in future.)<br><br>SAT:   
   9:00-10:30pm <br>WED:    9:00-10:30pm <br>Please check <a href="http://ww
 w.archerytrainingcenter.com/calendar">www.archerytrainingcenter.com/calenda
 r</a> before registering!<br><br>DAYS CLOSED: <br>The outdoor range is clos
 ed\, gates locked\, and targets stored away except during the above class t
 imes.<br><br>ENROLLMENT IS ON A FIRST-RECEIVED AND PAID BASIS.<br>Complete 
 the Outdoor Target Archery Registration Form under Adults or Juniors at <a 
 href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrainingcenter.com</
 a><br><br>ATTENDANCE RECOMMENDATIONS: <br>Recreational archers have no atte
 ndance requirements\, but we would recommend attending at least twice a wee
 k to improve faster. <br><br>FEES: <br>All fees are payable in advance of t
 he class to secure your place in the class. <br>$30/archer for each 1.5-hr 
 training session  OR <br>$115/mo (for 1 training session/week) OR <br>$213/
 mo (for 2 training sessions/week)<br>+ Enrollment fee: $20 (always due once
  per semester) <br><br>WEATHER:<br>Archers need to practice in all weather\
 , except when there is lightning. <br><br>REFUNDS\, CREDITS\, and SUBSTITUT
 IONS:<br>Substitutions or credits will be applied if we cancel a class due 
 to weather conditions or instructor illness or if the 24-hr notice is met.<
 br>There are no refunds for paid classes missed during the summer\, except 
 in the case of injury\, long-term illness\, unforeseen move out of the Aust
 in area\, or being expelled for a safety violation. <br><br>24-HR NOTICE: <
 br>If you let us know within 24 hours of the class that you will miss the c
 lass\, you can substitute another class and use your fee as long as there a
 re places left in that class during the semester. If you notify us less tha
 n 24 hours in advance of the class that you will need to cancel (except for
  sudden illness)\, or you do a "no-show"\, you'll forfeit your fee.<br><br>
 ILLNESS or INJURY: In the case of physical injury or long-term illness\, we
  require a doctor's note saying that you are unable to practice archery\, a
 nd then a doctor's note saying that you are again fit to return to archery\
 , before you will be allowed back in class or a refund/credit issued.<br><b
 r>MEMBERSHIP IN USA ARCHERY:<br>Membership in USA Archery is now REQUIRED t
 o participate in JOAD and Adult Training.<br>You can attend 2 sessions befo
 re joining USAA\, but then we'll need to see your membership card BEFORE WE
  CAN HAND OUT ANY USA ARCHERY STAR PINS to you during Master Challenge Week
 s! <br>If you would like to see the benefits of USAA membership: <a href="h
 ttp://www.teamusa.org/USA-Archery/Membership/Membership-Benefits">http://ww
 w.teamusa.org/USA-Archery/Membership/Membership-Benefits</a><br>JOIN USA AR
 CHERY: <a href="https://www.usarchery.org/memberships/become-a-member">http
 s://www.usarchery.org/memberships/become-a-member</a><br><br>SAFE SPORTS:<b
 r>PARENTS PLEASE NOTE: We are part of the US Olympic Committee's Safe Sport
  program\, so we minimally require one other adult besides the instructor t
 o be present at all times. Please plan to stay with your child or take turn
 s with other parents staying whenever necessary to fulfill this requirement
 . THANKS!<br><br>SIGN AND RETURN THESE OUTDOOR WAIVERS:<br>The following do
 cuments and waivers will be part of your Registration and Waiver Packet. Yo
 u will need to sign these  documents before we add your name to those shoot
 ing in the class:<br>o Membership Form<br>o Safety Rules <br>o Release of L
 iability Waiver<br>o Supervision Policy (Under 18)<br>o Medical Release  <b
 r>o Photo/Video Release<br>o COVID-19 Guidelines<br>o Outdoor Field Rules o
 f Participation <br><br>VACCINATIONS:<br>We do not at this time require arc
 hers to be vaccinated\, but we would like to know if you have been\, so we 
 can take it into consideration when deciding on issues such as masks and so
 cial distancing and abiding by the CDC Guidelines. All our instructors have
  been fully vaccinated of their own accord.<br><br>QUESTIONS?<br>E-mail us 
 at <a href="mailto:archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com">archerytrainingce
 nteraustin@gmail.com</a> or<br>Call/Text us at 512 975 1850 <br><br>*NTS = 
 National Training System (which is used for training the USA Olympic team!)
 <br>*JDT = Junior Dream Team (top 20 Junior archers in the USA!)<br>*JOAD =
  Junior Olympic Archery Development
