DESCRIPTION:Registered Archers:<br>1. Kevin B.\, 18m on 40cm target face<br
 >2. Nate H.\, Distance TBD<br>3.<br>4..<br>5.<br>6.<br>7.<br>8.<br>9.<br>10
 .<br><br>OVERVIEW:<br>These Outdoor Target Archery recreational classes pre
 pare you to shoot at longer and longer distances until you reach your USA A
 rchery tournament distance (see below)\, while learning the National Traini
 ng System\, which is the most highly researched biomechanical method of sho
 oting taught out at the Olympic Training Center. You will be shooting with 
 other archers in group sessions\, so you can all learn together and from ea
 ch other. <br><br>PREREQUISITE: <br>Some archery experience and your own re
 curve archery equipment is required.<br><br>OPEN TO ADULTS / JUNIORS / PARE
 NTS (with experience and own recurve archery equipment)<br>The archer and a
  maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field until further notice
  or approved by Coach Racae.<br>Space will be limited to a maximum of 10 ar
 chers per session or in accordance with CDC Guidelines.<br><br>NO DROP INS:
 <br>You cannot just drop in\, because the number of archers on the shooting
  line is very limited and we are observing CDC guidelines with social dista
 ncing.<br><br>DATES:    Start Dates: MAY 15 (Adults) or JUNE 12 (Juniors 10
 +) <br>&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp
 \;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;Ending Date:  AUGUST 14  <br><br>ADDRESSES:<b
 r>OUTDOOR FIELD SOUTH:    2310 Bliss Spillar Road\, Manchaca\, TX 78652<br>
 MAILING:  Archery Training Center\, Inc.\, PO Box 93216\, Austin\, TX 78709
 <br><br>E-MAIL: <a href="mailto:archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com">arch
 erytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a><br><br>PHONE/TEXT:  512 975 1850<br><
 br>CAPACITY:    10 archers per class or in accordance with CDC guidelines<b
 r>AGES:             10 - 80+ years old (See start dates above)<br>DISTANCES
 :  9m\, 13.5m\, 18m\, 20m-70m<br>BOWS:           Recurves  <br>(If you are 
 not a recurve archer\, but would like to learn to shoot a recurve bow\, ple
 ase stay tuned to our Instagram for announcements of the re-opening of our 
 in-person First-time Classes\, or register online for a few Virtual NTS For
 m classes with Coach Racae.)<br><br>EQUIPMENT: <br>These classes are for ar
 chers who have their own equipment\, consisting of at least a recurve bow\,
  12 aluminum or carbon arrows\, armguard\, finger tab\, hip or field quiver
 .  (If you need to change your equipment or order your own\, please contact
  Coach Racae at <a href="mailto:archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com">arch
 erytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a>. She will specify what you´ll need an
 d help you order it\, so you buy the correct equipment for your strength an
 d experience.)<br><br>INSTRUCTOR / COACH:<br>USA Archery Level 2 Instructor
  Ted Aanstoos  <br><br>CLASS TIMES:<br>These are the days/times that are av
 ailable to you. (Additional sessions will be added in future.)<br><br>SAT: 
     9:00-10:30pm <br>WED:    9:00-10:30pm <br>Please check <a href="http://
 www.archerytrainingcenter.com/calendar">www.archerytrainingcenter.com/calen
 dar</a> before registering!<br><br>DAYS CLOSED: <br>The outdoor range is cl
 osed\, gates locked\, and targets stored away except during the above class
  times.<br><br>ENROLLMENT IS ON A FIRST-RECEIVED AND PAID BASIS.<br>Complet
 e the Outdoor Target Archery Registration Form under Adults or Juniors at <
 a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrainingcenter.com
 </a><br><br>ATTENDANCE RECOMMENDATIONS: <br>Recreational archers have no at
 tendance requirements\, but we would recommend attending at least twice a w
 eek to improve faster. <br><br>FEES: <br>All fees are payable in advance of
  the class to secure your place in the class. <br>$30/archer for each 1.5-h
 r training session  OR <br>$115/mo (for 1 training session/week) OR <br>$21
 3/mo (for 2 training sessions/week)<br>+ Enrollment fee: $20 (always due on
 ce per semester) <br><br>WEATHER:<br>Archers need to practice in all weathe
 r\, except when there is lightning. <br><br>REFUNDS\, CREDITS\, and SUBSTIT
 UTIONS:<br>Substitutions or credits will be applied if we cancel a class du
 e to weather conditions or instructor illness or if the 24-hr notice is met
 .<br>There are no refunds for paid classes missed during the summer\, excep
 t in the case of injury\, long-term illness\, unforeseen move out of the Au
 stin area\, or being expelled for a safety violation. <br><br>24-HR NOTICE:
  <br>If you let us know within 24 hours of the class that you will miss the
  class\, you can substitute another class and use your fee as long as there
  are places left in that class during the semester. If you notify us less t
 han 24 hours in advance of the class that you will need to cancel (except f
 or sudden illness)\, or you do a "no-show"\, you'll forfeit your fee.<br><b
 r>ILLNESS or INJURY: In the case of physical injury or long-term illness\, 
 we require a doctor's note saying that you are unable to practice archery\,
  and then a doctor's note saying that you are again fit to return to archer
 y\, before you will be allowed back in class or a refund/credit issued.<br>
 <br>MEMBERSHIP IN USA ARCHERY:<br>Membership in USA Archery is now REQUIRED
  to participate in JOAD and Adult Training.<br>You can attend 2 sessions be
 fore joining USAA\, but then we'll need to see your membership card BEFORE 
 WE CAN HAND OUT ANY USA ARCHERY STAR PINS to you during Master Challenge We
 eks! <br>If you would like to see the benefits of USAA membership: <a href=
 "http://www.teamusa.org/USA-Archery/Membership/Membership-Benefits">http://
 www.teamusa.org/USA-Archery/Membership/Membership-Benefits</a><br>JOIN USA 
 ARCHERY: <a href="https://www.usarchery.org/memberships/become-a-member">ht
 tps://www.usarchery.org/memberships/become-a-member</a><br><br>SAFE SPORTS:
 <br>PARENTS PLEASE NOTE: We are part of the US Olympic Committee's Safe Spo
 rt program\, so we minimally require one other adult besides the instructor
  to be present at all times. Please plan to stay with your child or take tu
 rns with other parents staying whenever necessary to fulfill this requireme
 nt. THANKS!<br><br>SIGN AND RETURN THESE OUTDOOR WAIVERS:<br>The following 
 documents and waivers will be part of your Registration and Waiver Packet. 
 You will need to sign these  documents before we add your name to those sho
 oting in the class:<br>o Membership Form<br>o Safety Rules <br>o Release of
  Liability Waiver<br>o Supervision Policy (Under 18)<br>o Medical Release  
 <br>o Photo/Video Release<br>o COVID-19 Guidelines<br>o Outdoor Field Rules
  of Participation <br><br>VACCINATIONS:<br>We do not at this time require a
 rchers to be vaccinated\, but we would like to know if you have been\, so w
 e can take it into consideration when deciding on issues such as masks and 
 social distancing and abiding by the CDC Guidelines. All our instructors ha
 ve been fully vaccinated of their own accord.<br><br>QUESTIONS?<br>E-mail u
 s at <a href="mailto:archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com">archerytraining
 centeraustin@gmail.com</a> or<br>Call/Text us at 512 975 1850 <br><br>*NTS 
 = National Training System (which is used for training the USA Olympic team
 !)<br>*JDT = Junior Dream Team (top 20 Junior archers in the USA!)<br>*JOAD
  = Junior Olympic Archery Development
