DESCRIPTION:Registered Archers:<br>1. Nate H.\, at 20m on 122cm target face
 : Goal: 320 pts in 1 round of 36 arrows (outdoor scorecard)<br>2. Kevin B.\
 , at 20m on 122cm target face: Goal: 320 pts in 1 round of 36 arrows (outdo
 or scorecard)<br>3. Cyrenna V. at 9m on 40cm target face: Goal 230 pts in 1
  round of 30 arrows (indoor scorecard)<br>4..<br>5.<br>6.<br>7.<br>8.<br>9.
 <br>10.<br><br>OVERVIEW:<br>These Outdoor Target Archery recreational class
 es prepare you to shoot at longer and longer distances until you reach your
  USA Archery tournament distance (see below)\, while learning the National 
 Training System\, which is the most highly researched biomechanical method 
 of shooting taught out at the Olympic Training Center. You will be shooting
  with other archers in group sessions\, so you can all learn together and f
 rom each other. <br><br>PREREQUISITE: <br>Some archery experience and your 
 own recurve archery equipment is required.<br><br>OPEN TO ADULTS / JUNIORS 
 / PARENTS (with experience and own recurve archery equipment)<br>The archer
  and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field until further 
 notice or approved by Coach Racae.<br>Space will be limited to a maximum of
  10 archers per session or in accordance with CDC Guidelines.<br><br>NO DRO
 P INS:<br>You cannot just drop in\, because the number of archers on the sh
 ooting line is very limited and we are observing CDC guidelines with social
  distancing.<br><br>DATES:    Start Dates: MAY 15 (Adults) or JUNE 12 (Juni
 ors 10+) <br>&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\
 ;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;Ending Date:  AUGUST 14  <br><br>ADDRES
 SES:<br>OUTDOOR FIELD SOUTH:    2310 Bliss Spillar Road\, Manchaca\, TX 786
 52<br>MAILING:  Archery Training Center\, Inc.\, PO Box 93216\, Austin\, TX
  78709<br><br>E-MAIL: <a href="mailto:archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com
 ">archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a><br><br>PHONE/TEXT:  512 975 185
 0<br><br>CAPACITY:    10 archers per class or in accordance with CDC guidel
 ines<br>AGES:             10 - 80+ years old (See start dates above)<br>DIS
 TANCES:  9m\, 13.5m\, 18m\, 20m-70m<br>BOWS:           Recurves  <br>(If yo
 u are not a recurve archer\, but would like to learn to shoot a recurve bow
 \, please stay tuned to our Instagram for announcements of the re-opening o
 f our in-person First-time Classes\, or register online for a few Virtual N
 TS Form classes with Coach Racae.)<br><br>EQUIPMENT: <br>These classes are 
 for archers who have their own equipment\, consisting of at least a recurve
  bow\, 12 aluminum or carbon arrows\, armguard\, finger tab\, hip or field 
 quiver.  (If you need to change your equipment or order your own\, please c
 ontact Coach Racae at <a href="mailto:archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com
 ">archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a>. She will specify what you´ll n
 eed and help you order it\, so you buy the correct equipment for your stren
 gth and experience.)<br><br>INSTRUCTOR / COACH:<br>USA Archery Level 2 Inst
 ructor Ted Aanstoos  <br><br>CLASS TIMES:<br>These are the days/times that 
 are available to you. (Additional sessions will be added in future.)<br><br
 >SAT:     9:00-10:30pm <br>WED:    9:00-10:30pm <br>Please check <a href="h
 ttp://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/calendar">www.archerytrainingcenter.com
 /calendar</a> before registering!<br><br>DAYS CLOSED: <br>The outdoor range
  is closed\, gates locked\, and targets stored away except during the above
  class times.<br><br>ENROLLMENT IS ON A FIRST-RECEIVED AND PAID BASIS.<br>C
 omplete the Outdoor Target Archery Registration Form under Adults or Junior
 s at <a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrainingcent
 er.com</a><br><br>ATTENDANCE RECOMMENDATIONS: <br>Recreational archers have
  no attendance requirements\, but we would recommend attending at least twi
 ce a week to improve faster. <br><br>FEES: <br>All fees are payable in adva
 nce of the class to secure your place in the class. <br>$30/archer for each
  1.5-hr training session  OR <br>$115/mo (for 1 training session/week) OR <
 br>$213/mo (for 2 training sessions/week)<br>+ Enrollment fee: $20 (always 
 due once per semester) <br><br>WEATHER:<br>Archers need to practice in all 
 weather\, except when there is lightning. <br><br>REFUNDS\, CREDITS\, and S
 UBSTITUTIONS:<br>Substitutions or credits will be applied if we cancel a cl
 ass due to weather conditions or instructor illness or if the 24-hr notice 
 is met.<br>There are no refunds for paid classes missed during the summer\,
  except in the case of injury\, long-term illness\, unforeseen move out of 
 the Austin area\, or being expelled for a safety violation. <br><br>24-HR N
 OTICE: <br>If you let us know within 24 hours of the class that you will mi
 ss the class\, you can substitute another class and use your fee as long as
  there are places left in that class during the semester. If you notify us 
 less than 24 hours in advance of the class that you will need to cancel (ex
 cept for sudden illness)\, or you do a "no-show"\, you'll forfeit your fee.
 <br><br>ILLNESS or INJURY: In the case of physical injury or long-term illn
 ess\, we require a doctor's note saying that you are unable to practice arc
 hery\, and then a doctor's note saying that you are again fit to return to 
 archery\, before you will be allowed back in class or a refund/credit issue
 d.<br><br>MEMBERSHIP IN USA ARCHERY:<br>Membership in USA Archery is now RE
 QUIRED to participate in JOAD and Adult Training.<br>You can attend 2 sessi
 ons before joining USAA\, but then we'll need to see your membership card B
 EFORE WE CAN HAND OUT ANY USA ARCHERY STAR PINS to you during Master Challe
 nge Weeks! <br>If you would like to see the benefits of USAA membership: <a
  href="http://www.teamusa.org/USA-Archery/Membership/Membership-Benefits">h
 ttp://www.teamusa.org/USA-Archery/Membership/Membership-Benefits</a><br>JOI
 N USA ARCHERY: <a href="https://www.usarchery.org/memberships/become-a-memb
 er">https://www.usarchery.org/memberships/become-a-member</a><br><br>SAFE S
 PORTS:<br>PARENTS PLEASE NOTE: We are part of the US Olympic Committee's Sa
 fe Sport program\, so we minimally require one other adult besides the inst
 ructor to be present at all times. Please plan to stay with your child or t
 ake turns with other parents staying whenever necessary to fulfill this req
 uirement. THANKS!<br><br>SIGN AND RETURN THESE OUTDOOR WAIVERS:<br>The foll
 owing documents and waivers will be part of your Registration and Waiver Pa
 cket. You will need to sign these  documents before we add your name to tho
 se shooting in the class:<br>o Membership Form<br>o Safety Rules <br>o Rele
 ase of Liability Waiver<br>o Supervision Policy (Under 18)<br>o Medical Rel
 ease  <br>o Photo/Video Release<br>o COVID-19 Guidelines<br>o Outdoor Field
  Rules of Participation <br><br>VACCINATIONS:<br>We do not at this time req
 uire archers to be vaccinated\, but we would like to know if you have been\
 , so we can take it into consideration when deciding on issues such as mask
 s and social distancing and abiding by the CDC Guidelines. All our instruct
 ors have been fully vaccinated of their own accord.<br><br>QUESTIONS?<br>E-
 mail us at <a href="mailto:archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com">archerytr
 ainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a> or<br>Call/Text us at 512 975 1850 <br><br
 >*NTS = National Training System (which is used for training the USA Olympi
 c team!)<br>*JDT = Junior Dream Team (top 20 Junior archers in the USA!)<br
 >*JOAD = Junior Olympic Archery Development
