DESCRIPTION:<b>2022 Summer Schedule and Goals for Outdoor 2-9 (9m to 70m)</
 b><b><br></b><br><b>Goals by the end of the summer semester (Aug 14):&nbsp\
 ;</b><br>Make a list of what you want to accomplish<b><br></b>&nbsp\;<br><b
 >JUNE</b><br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>2-5</b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\
 ; Welcome Back: Understanding&nbsp\; NTS Concepts \; Mental Program<br><b>&
 nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>9-12</b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; NTS Steps 1+2: STANCE 
 + NOCK&nbsp\;<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\;&nbsp\;<b>16-19&nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b>NTS Step 
 3: HOOK &amp\; GRIP&nbsp\;<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; 25/</b><b>26&nbsp\; JUNE A
 TCI MASTER CHALLENGE TOURNAMENT (Pin Shoot)&nbsp\;</b><b>10:30am-12:30pm&nb
 sp\;</b><br><b>JULY</b><br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;6/30-7/3&nbsp\;</b>NTS
  Step 4: SET\; NTS Step 5: SET-UP&nbsp\;<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;7-10<
 /b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; NTS Step 6 DRAW to LOAD&nbsp\;<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\
 ;<b>14-17&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</b>NTS Step 7 ANCHOR&nbsp\;<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &
 nbsp\;</b><b>21-24&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</b>NTS Step 8 TRANSFER to HOLD<br><b>&nbsp
 \; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;30/31&nbsp\; JULY ATCI MASTER CHALLENGE TOURNAMENT (Pin S
 hoot)</b><br><b>AUGUST</b><br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;4-7</b>&nbsp\; &nbs
 p\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;NTS Step 9 EXPAND / AIM&nbsp\;<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nb
 sp\;11-14</b>&nbsp\; NTS Step 10 RELEASE + FOLLOW-THROUGH<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\
 ; &nbsp\;<b>18-21</b>&nbsp\;<b>&nbsp\;</b>NTS Step 11: FEEDBACK + Putting i
 t all together!<b><br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>27/28&nbsp\; AUGUST ATC
 I MASTER CHALLENGE TOURNAMENT (Pin Shoot)</b><br><br>Each week the focus of
  your lessons will be on particular Steps of Shooting of the NTS (National 
 Training System) shot cycle\, to help you focus and improve your form\, whi
 ch\, as we all know\, leads to greater and consistent precision (tight grou
 ps of arrows) and ultimately greater accuracy (tight groups of arrows dead 
 center).<br><br>Your goal is always to replicate the NTS step(s) mindfully 
 and consistently on every shot. If you stay in the present just doing what 
 you need to do as you need to it\, your conscious mind will be occupied\, i
 nstead of random thoughts entering your head or you being distracted by emo
 tional or environmental elements. You´ll need to build up your mental progr
 am alongside your form knowledge\, so when your body is trained to shoot ex
 cellent shots\, your self image and subsonscious support you\, instead of u
 ndermining you. Confidence and consistency in form and mind are major goals
 .<br><br>You do not need to score in every class. In fact\, it would be mor
 e beneficial to you if you scored only during Master Challenge Tournament W
 eeks\, which happen the last week of each month. This is because working on
  the NTS Steps of Shooting (your form) is more easily done without the dist
 raction of the target face or scoring\, and you will improve faster.<br><br
 >As you reach higher levels\, you will learn the NTS Steps in progressively
  greater detail.<br>The NTS Steps are cumulative with each step most succes
 sfully completed if the previous steps have been completed well.&nbsp\;<br>
 <br>Your ability to learn and understand the NTS Steps\, and use deep focus
  on these Steps while shooting outdoors and while using your stretchband/st
 ring loop at home to reinforce form poisitions will propel you to higher le
 vels fast!
