  spectator.&nbsp\;<br>Parents of juniors 8-9 years old need to register\, p
 ay\, and shoot with their child for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one
  8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-time Class.&n
 bsp\;<br><br>We will accept a limited&nbsp\;number of kids under 12 into th
 e program each semester\, depending on the total&nbsp\; number of archers i
 n all the classes. If you join before the limit is reached\, and are younge
 r than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as 
 needed and later join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;If you are under 12\, registered and
  paid after the cut off\, your fee will be returned to you.&nbsp\;<br><br>J
 uniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying to g
 et into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on
  average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need a minimum
  score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard
 \, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($18) Ple
 ase pay for this at the field\, as our stock fluctuates because of dealer s
 upply fluctuations<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, option
 al but really needed to practice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>
 At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we did 
 not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final 
 score\, because it will have been averaged by taking your recorded score fr
 om your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot to get an arr
 ow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round score. Aft
 er the last class on the weekend\, final scores will also be sent to all Ou
 tdoor 1 participants in an email with more information before your next cla
 ss.<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u
 ></u><u></u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
