 u>8B.&nbsp\;<br><u></u><br><u></u>9A. <b>Paul B.</b>\, adult - pd - <b>DNA<
 /b><br><u></u>9B. <b>Wesley B..\,</b> 10\,&nbsp\;on 60cm target face&nbsp\;
 - pd - <b>DNA</b><br><br><u></u>10A. <b>Alexander O.\,</b> 10\,&nbsp\;on 60
 cm target face&nbsp\;- pd - <b>139 pts </b>(corrected)<b> -&gt\; Outdoor 2 
 !</b><br><u></u>10B.<br><br><b>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or th
 ree times&nbsp\;</b>before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 p
 ts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arr
 ows.&nbsp\;<br><b>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoo
 r 2.</b><br><br>Space will be limited to 10-15 archers per session dependin
 g on the number of family groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC Gu
 idelines.&nbsp\;<br>Each person will have a target stand\, except after 10 
 people have registered\, two members from the same family will share one ta
 rget stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on
  the field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae.&nbsp\;<br>Paren
 ts of juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator.&nbsp\;<
 br>Parents of juniors 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with
  their child for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ pare
 nt) is accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-time Class.&nbsp\;<br><br>We wil
 l accept a limited&nbsp\;number of kids under 12 into the program each seme
 ster\, depending on the total&nbsp\; number of archers in all the classes. 
 If you join before the limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll 
 stay in the program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later jo
 in Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;If you are under 12\, registered and paid after the cut
  off\, your fee will be returned to you.&nbsp\;<br><br>ap = accessories pac
 ket (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor
  2. ($18) Please pay for this at the field\, as our stock fluctuates becaus
 e of dealer supply fluctuations<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string l
 oop)\, optional but really needed to practice form\, warm up before classes
  ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be poste
 d. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recogniz
 e your final score\, because it will have been averaged by taking your reco
 rded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot 
 to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full rou
 nd score. After the last class on the weekend\, final scores will also be s
 ent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more information before 
 your next class.<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u>
