DESCRIPTION:Instructor/Coach: Level 4 NTS Coach Racae Meyer<br><br>Register
 ed Archers:<br>1. Natalie H.\, 60m on 122 cm target face<br>2.<br>3.<br>4..
 <br>5.<br>6.<br>7.<br>8.<br>9.<br>10.<br><br>OVERVIEW:<br>These Outdoor Tar
 get Archery recreational classes prepare you to shoot at longer and longer 
 distances until you reach your USA Archery tournament distance (see below)\
 , while learning the National Training System\, which is the most highly re
 searched biomechanical method of shooting taught out at the Olympic Trainin
 g Center. You will be shooting with other archers in group sessions\, so yo
 u can all learn together and from each other. <br><br>PREREQUISITE: <br>Som
 e archery experience and your own recurve archery equipment is required.<br
 ><br>OPEN TO ADULTS / JUNIORS / PARENTS (with experience and own recurve ar
 chery equipment)<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allow
 ed on the field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae.<br>Space w
 ill be limited to a maximum of 10 archers per session or in accordance with
  CDC Guidelines.<br><br>NO DROP INS:<br>You cannot just drop in\, because t
 he number of archers on the shooting line is very limited and we are observ
 ing CDC guidelines with social distancing.<br><br>DATES:    Start Dates: MA
 Y 15 (Adults) or JUNE 12 (Juniors 10+) <br>&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbs
 p\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;Ending Da
 te:  AUGUST 14  <br><br>ADDRESSES:<br>OUTDOOR FIELD SOUTH:    2310 Bliss Sp
 illar Road\, Manchaca\, TX 78652<br>MAILING:  Archery Training Center\, Inc
 .\, PO Box 93216\, Austin\, TX 78709<br><br>E-MAIL: <a href="mailto:archery
 trainingcenteraustin@gmail.com">archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a><b
 r><br>PHONE/TEXT:  512 975 1850<br><br>CAPACITY:    10 archers per class or
  in accordance with CDC guidelines<br>AGES:             10 - 80+ years old 
 (See start dates above)<br>DISTANCES:  9m\, 13.5m\, 18m\, 20m-70m<br>BOWS: 
           Recurves  <br>(If you are not a recurve archer\, but would like t
 o learn to shoot a recurve bow\, please stay tuned to our Instagram for ann
 ouncements of the re-opening of our in-person First-time Classes\, or regis
 ter online for a few Virtual NTS Form classes with Coach Racae.)<br><br>EQU
 IPMENT: <br>These classes are for archers who have their own equipment\, co
 nsisting of at least a recurve bow\, 12 aluminum or carbon arrows\, armguar
 d\, finger tab\, hip or field quiver.  (If you need to change your equipmen
 t or order your own\, please contact Coach Racae at <a href="mailto:archery
 trainingcenteraustin@gmail.com">archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a>. 
 She will specify what you´ll need and help you order it\, so you buy the co
 rrect equipment for your strength and experience.)<br><br>INSTRUCTOR / COAC
 H:<br>USA Archery Level 2 Instructor Ted Aanstoos  <br><br>CLASS TIMES:<br>
 These are the days/times that are available to you. (Additional sessions wi
 ll be added in future.)<br><br>SAT:     9:00-10:30pm <br>WED:    9:00-10:30
 pm <br>Please check <a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/calendar"
 >www.archerytrainingcenter.com/calendar</a> before registering!<br><br>DAYS
  CLOSED: <br>The outdoor range is closed\, gates locked\, and targets store
 d away except during the above class times.<br><br>ENROLLMENT IS ON A FIRST
 -RECEIVED AND PAID BASIS.<br>Complete the Outdoor Target Archery Registrati
 on Form under Adults or Juniors at <a href="http://www.archerytrainingcente
 r.com">www.archerytrainingcenter.com</a><br><br>ATTENDANCE RECOMMENDATIONS:
  <br>Recreational archers have no attendance requirements\, but we would re
 commend attending at least twice a week to improve faster. <br><br>FEES: <b
 r>All fees are payable in advance of the class to secure your place in the 
 class. <br>$30/archer for each 1.5-hr training session  OR <br>$115/mo (for
  1 training session/week) OR <br>$213/mo (for 2 training sessions/week)<br>
 + Enrollment fee: $20 (always due once per semester) <br><br>WEATHER:<br>Ar
 chers need to practice in all weather\, except when there is lightning. <br
 ><br>REFUNDS\, CREDITS\, and SUBSTITUTIONS:<br>Substitutions or credits wil
 l be applied if we cancel a class due to weather conditions or instructor i
 llness or if the 24-hr notice is met.<br>There are no refunds for paid clas
 ses missed during the summer\, except in the case of injury\, long-term ill
 ness\, unforeseen move out of the Austin area\, or being expelled for a saf
 ety violation. <br><br>24-HR NOTICE: <br>If you let us know within 24 hours
  of the class that you will miss the class\, you can substitute another cla
 ss and use your fee as long as there are places left in that class during t
 he semester. If you notify us less than 24 hours in advance of the class th
 at you will need to cancel (except for sudden illness)\, or you do a "no-sh
 ow"\, you'll forfeit your fee.<br><br>ILLNESS or INJURY: In the case of phy
 sical injury or long-term illness\, we require a doctor's note saying that 
 you are unable to practice archery\, and then a doctor's note saying that y
 ou are again fit to return to archery\, before you will be allowed back in 
 class or a refund/credit issued.<br><br>MEMBERSHIP IN USA ARCHERY:<br>Membe
 rship in USA Archery is now REQUIRED to participate in JOAD and Adult Train
 ing.<br>You can attend 2 sessions before joining USAA\, but then we'll need
  to see your membership card BEFORE WE CAN HAND OUT ANY USA ARCHERY STAR PI
 NS to you during Master Challenge Weeks! <br>If you would like to see the b
 enefits of USAA membership: <a href="http://www.teamusa.org/USA-Archery/Mem
 bership/Membership-Benefits">http://www.teamusa.org/USA-Archery/Membership/
 Membership-Benefits</a><br>JOIN USA ARCHERY: <a href="https://www.usarchery
 .org/memberships/become-a-member">https://www.usarchery.org/memberships/bec
 ome-a-member</a><br><br>SAFE SPORTS:<br>PARENTS PLEASE NOTE: We are part of
  the US Olympic Committee's Safe Sport program\, so we minimally require on
 e other adult besides the instructor to be present at all times. Please pla
 n to stay with your child or take turns with other parents staying whenever
  necessary to fulfill this requirement. THANKS!<br><br>SIGN AND RETURN THES
 E OUTDOOR WAIVERS:<br>The following documents and waivers will be part of y
 our Registration and Waiver Packet. You will need to sign these  documents 
 before we add your name to those shooting in the class:<br>o Membership For
 m<br>o Safety Rules <br>o Release of Liability Waiver<br>o Supervision Poli
 cy (Under 18)<br>o Medical Release  <br>o Photo/Video Release<br>o COVID-19
  Guidelines<br>o Outdoor Field Rules of Participation <br><br>VACCINATIONS:
 <br>We do not at this time require archers to be vaccinated\, but we would 
 like to know if you have been\, so we can take it into consideration when d
 eciding on issues such as masks and social distancing and abiding by the CD
 C Guidelines. All our instructors have been fully vaccinated of their own a
 ccord.<br><br>QUESTIONS?<br>E-mail us at <a href="mailto:archerytrainingcen
 teraustin@gmail.com">archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a> or<br>Call/T
 ext us at 512 975 1850 <br><br>*NTS = National Training System (which is us
 ed for training the USA Olympic team!)<br>*JDT = Junior Dream Team (top 20 
 Junior archers in the USA!)<br>*JOAD = Junior Olympic Archery Development
