DESCRIPTION:Registration form: OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m<br><br>At least 5 a
 rchers need to be in attendance for Coach Racae to coach the Outdoor 3-9 Tr
 aining Class alone. In the case of low registrations\, another coach/instru
 ctor may be coaching the class.<br><br>Add your name to Target Assignment L
 ist below or submit the above completed form.<br>Focus primarily on perfect
 ing your form\, <br>slowly increasing your physical strength and draw weigh
 t\, <br>strengthening your mental program\, <br>determining your average an
 d personal best\, <br>understanding the spread between the two\, and workin
 g on closing it.<br><br>You need your own equipment <br>Competition recurve
  bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-
 bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sl
 ing\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may 
 not be added until you reach a higher level\, but you should order them in 
 advance.) <br><br>Wear your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br>When you score 2
 88 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to th
 e next distance until you reach your competition distance<br>If you trained
  outdoors in the 2024 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you s
 hot.<br><br>Target arrangements may vary each session\, depending on who at
 tends and distances needed.<br>Target 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition d
 istance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent pract
 ice in between classes.<br>Target 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition dista
 nce) <br>Target 3 at 50m<br>Target 4 at 40m (U15 competition distance) <br>
 Target 5 at 30m (U13 competition distance) <br>Targets 6+7+8 at 20m (for th
 ose who have shot at 18m indoors or with Coach Racae's approval)<br>Targets
  9 + 10 at 13.5m (for those who have just graduated from indoors at 9m)<br>
 <br>Ideally\, we want to practice with two archers/target to replicate comp
 etition conditions as much as possible.<br><br>Target Assignments:<br>Targe
 ts are assigned outdoors in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the da
 y\,<br>so add your name next to your distance below. <br>If you need help o
 r have questions\, email/text Coach Racae<br>(Dotted lines represent tent p
 oles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)<br>----------------------------------
 <br>1A. (70m)<br>1B<br><br>2A. (60m)  <b>Joel Y\,</b> USAA\, pd - <b>162 pt
 s</b><br>2B<br><br>3A. (50m)  <b>Abby Y\,</b> 13\, USAA\, pd - <b>208 / 207
  (averaged) pts</b><br>----------------------------------<br>3B<br><br>4A. 
 (40m) <b>Hannah T\,</b> USAA\, pd DNS?<br>4B. <br>-------------------------
