 ors 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their child for g
 reater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted in
 to each Outdoor 1: First-time Class.&nbsp\;<br><br>We will accept a limited
 &nbsp\;number of kids under 12 into the program each semester\, depending o
 n the total&nbsp\; number of archers in all the classes. If you join before
  the limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the progra
 m and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2.&nbsp
 \;If you are under 12\, registered and paid after the cut off\, your fee wi
 ll be returned to you.&nbsp\;<br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two
  or three times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. 
 You´ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.
 &nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br
 ><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which w
 ill be needed for Outdoor 2. ($18) Please pay for this at the field\, as ou
 r stock fluctuates because of dealer supply fluctuations<br>fp = form pack 
 (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but really needed to practice form
 \, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, 
 your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrow
 s)\, you may not recognize your final score\, because it will have been ave
 raged by taking your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the n
 umber of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying tha
 t by 30 to get a full round score. After the last class on the weekend\, fi
 nal scores will also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with
  more information before your next class.<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u
 ><u></u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
