DESCRIPTION:Registered Archers:<br>Once you are shooting at 20m\, your goal
  is to get to the next distance (+10m) by shooting 320 pts at your present 
 distance on a 122-cm target in one round of 36 arrows until you reach your 
 tournament distance as listed here:<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbs
 p\; &nbsp\; Masters: (50+) 60m&nbsp\;<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &n
 bsp\; &nbsp\; Seniors (21-50+) 70m<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp
 \; &nbsp\; Juniors (18-20) 70m&nbsp\;<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &n
 bsp\; &nbsp\; Cadets (15-17) 60m&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &
 nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; Cubs (13-14) 50m&nbsp\;<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &
 nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; Bowman (10-12) 30m.<br><br>1. Kevin B.\, 20m (45 min
  make up for 1/2 of Jun 5)<br>2. Nate H.\, 20m (45 min make up for 1/2 Jun 
 5)<br>3. Lily R. 20m on 122cm target face (will not attend due to hand burn
 )<br>4. Cyrenna V. 13.5m (45 min make up for 1/2 of June 5)<br>5. Yuhan X.\
 , 9m on 60-cm target face (JOAD target)<br>6. Andrew M.\, 20m on 122-cm tar
 get face<br>7.<br>8.<br>9.<br>10.<br><br>OVERVIEW:<br>These Outdoor Target 
 Archery recreational classes prepare you to shoot at longer and longer dist
 ances until you reach your USA Archery tournament distance (see below)\, wh
 ile learning the National Training System\, which is the most highly resear
 ched biomechanical method of shooting taught out at the Olympic Training Ce
 nter. You will be shooting with other archers in group sessions\, so you ca
 n all learn together and from each other. <br><br>PREREQUISITE: <br>Some ar
 chery experience and your own recurve archery equipment is required.<br><br
 >OPEN TO ADULTS / JUNIORS / PARENTS (with experience and own recurve archer
 y equipment)<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed o
 n the field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae.<br>Space will 
 be limited to a maximum of 10 archers per session or in accordance with CDC
  Guidelines.<br><br>NO DROP INS:<br>You cannot just drop in\, because the n
 umber of archers on the shooting line is very limited and we are observing 
 CDC guidelines with social distancing.<br><br>DATES:    Start Dates: MAY 15
  (Adults) or JUNE 12 (Juniors 10+) <br>&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&
 nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;Ending Date: 
  AUGUST 14  <br><br>ADDRESSES:<br>OUTDOOR FIELD SOUTH:    2310 Bliss Spilla
 r Road\, Manchaca\, TX 78652<br>MAILING:  Archery Training Center\, Inc.\, 
 PO Box 93216\, Austin\, TX 78709<br><br>E-MAIL: <a href="mailto:archerytrai
 ningcenteraustin@gmail.com">archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a><br><b
 r>PHONE/TEXT:  512 975 1850<br><br>CAPACITY:    10 archers per class or in 
 accordance with CDC guidelines<br>AGES:             10 - 80+ years old (See
  start dates above)<br>DISTANCES:  9m\, 13.5m\, 18m\, 20m-70m<br>BOWS:     
       Recurves - Olympic target recurves\, rather than tradiitional or hunt
 ing recurves<br>(If you are not a recurve archer\, but would like to learn 
 to shoot a recurve bow\, please stay tuned to our Instagram for announcemen
 ts of the re-opening of our in-person First-time Classes\, or register onli
 ne for a few Virtual NTS Form classes with Coach Racae.)<br><br>EQUIPMENT: 
 <br>These classes are for archers who have their own equipment\, consisting
  of at least a recurve bow\, 12 aluminum or carbon arrows\, armguard\, fing
 er tab\, hip or field quiver.  (If you need to change your equipment or ord
 er your own\, please contact Coach Racae at <a href="mailto:archerytraining
 centeraustin@gmail.com">archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a>. She will
  specify what you´ll need and help you order it\, so you buy the correct eq
 uipment for your strength and experience.)<br><br>INSTRUCTOR / COACH:<br>US
 A Archery Level 2 Instructor Ted Aanstoos  <br><br>CLASS TIMES:<br>These ar
 e the days/times that are available to you. (Additional sessions will be ad
 ded in future.)<br><br>SAT:     9:00-10:30pm <br>WED:    9:00-10:30pm <br>P
 lease check <a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/calendar">www.arc
 herytrainingcenter.com/calendar</a> before registering!<br><br>DAYS CLOSED:
  <br>The outdoor range is closed\, gates locked\, and targets stored away e
 xcept during the above class times.<br><br>ENROLLMENT IS ON A FIRST-RECEIVE
 D AND PAID BASIS.<br>Complete the Outdoor Target Archery Registration Form 
 under Adults or Juniors at <a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com">w
 ww.archerytrainingcenter.com</a><br><br>ATTENDANCE RECOMMENDATIONS: <br>Rec
 reational archers have no attendance requirements\, but we would recommend 
 attending at least twice a week to improve faster. <br><br>FEES: <br>All fe
 es are payable in advance of the class to secure your place in the class. <
 br>$30/archer for each 1.5-hr training session  OR <br>$115/mo (for 1 train
 ing session/week) OR <br>$213/mo (for 2 training sessions/week)<br>+ Enroll
 ment fee: $20 (always due once per semester) <br><br>WEATHER:<br>Archers ne
 ed to practice in all weather\, except when there is lightning. <br><br>REF
 UNDS\, CREDITS\, and SUBSTITUTIONS:<br>Substitutions or credits will be app
 lied if we cancel a class due to weather conditions or instructor illness o
 r if the 24-hr notice is met.<br>There are no refunds for paid classes miss
 ed during the summer\, except in the case of injury\, long-term illness\, u
 nforeseen move out of the Austin area\, or being expelled for a safety viol
 ation. <br><br>24-HR NOTICE: <br>If you let us know within 24 hours of the 
 class that you will miss the class\, you can substitute another class and u
 se your fee as long as there are places left in that class during the semes
 ter. If you notify us less than 24 hours in advance of the class that you w
 ill need to cancel (except for sudden illness)\, or you do a "no-show"\, yo
 u'll forfeit your fee.<br><br>ILLNESS or INJURY: In the case of physical in
 jury or long-term illness\, we require a doctor's note saying that you are 
 unable to practice archery\, and then a doctor's note saying that you are a
 gain fit to return to archery\, before you will be allowed back in class or
  a refund/credit issued.<br><br>MEMBERSHIP IN USA ARCHERY:<br>Membership in
  USA Archery is now REQUIRED to participate in JOAD and Adult Training.<br>
 You can attend 2 sessions before joining USAA\, but then we'll need to see 
 your membership card BEFORE WE CAN HAND OUT ANY USA ARCHERY STAR PINS to yo
 u during Master Challenge Weeks! <br>If you would like to see the benefits 
 of USAA membership: <a href="http://www.teamusa.org/USA-Archery/Membership/
 Membership-Benefits">http://www.teamusa.org/USA-Archery/Membership/Membersh
 ip-Benefits</a><br>JOIN USA ARCHERY: <a href="https://www.usarchery.org/mem
 berships/become-a-member">https://www.usarchery.org/memberships/become-a-me
 mber</a><br><br>SAFE SPORTS:<br>PARENTS PLEASE NOTE: We are part of the US 
 Olympic Committee's Safe Sport program\, so we minimally require one other 
 adult besides the instructor to be present at all times. Please plan to sta
 y with your child or take turns with other parents staying whenever necessa
 ry to fulfill this requirement. THANKS!<br><br>SIGN AND RETURN THESE OUTDOO
 R WAIVERS:<br>The following documents and waivers will be part of your Regi
 stration and Waiver Packet. You will need to sign these  documents before w
 e add your name to those shooting in the class:<br>o Membership Form<br>o S
 afety Rules <br>o Release of Liability Waiver<br>o Supervision Policy (Unde
 r 18)<br>o Medical Release  <br>o Photo/Video Release<br>o COVID-19 Guideli
 nes<br>o Outdoor Field Rules of Participation <br><br>VACCINATIONS:<br>We d
 o not at this time require archers to be vaccinated\, but we would like to 
 know if you have been\, so we can take it into consideration when deciding 
 on issues such as masks and social distancing and abiding by the CDC Guidel
 ines. All our instructors have been fully vaccinated of their own accord.<b
 r><br>QUESTIONS?<br>E-mail us at <a href="mailto:archerytrainingcenterausti
 n@gmail.com">archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a> or<br>Call/Text us a
 t 512 975 1850 <br><br>*NTS = National Training System (which is used for t
 raining the USA Olympic team!)<br>*JDT = Junior Dream Team (top 20 Junior a
 rchers in the USA!)<br>*JOAD = Junior Olympic Archery Development
