DESCRIPTION:Registered Archers:<br>1. Scott M. at 20m on 122-cm target face
 <br>2.<br>3.<br>4..<br>5.<br>6.<br>7.<br>8.<br>9.<br>10.<br><br>OVERVIEW:<b
 r>These Outdoor Target Archery recreational classes prepare you to shoot at
  longer and longer distances until you reach your USA Archery tournament di
 stance (see below)\, while learning the National Training System\, which is
  the most highly researched biomechanical method of shooting taught out at 
 the Olympic Training Center. You will be shooting with other archers in gro
 up sessions\, so you can all learn together and from each other. <br><br>PR
 EREQUISITE: <br>Some archery experience and your own recurve archery equipm
 ent is required.<br><br>OPEN TO ADULTS / JUNIORS / PARENTS (with experience
  and own recurve archery equipment)<br>The archer and a maximum of one spec
 tator will be allowed on the field until further notice or approved by Coac
 h Racae.<br>Space will be limited to a maximum of 10 archers per session or
  in accordance with CDC Guidelines.<br><br>NO DROP INS:<br>You cannot just 
 drop in\, because the number of archers on the shooting line is very limite
 d and we are observing CDC guidelines with social distancing.<br><br>DATES:
     Start Dates: MAY 15 (Adults) or JUNE 12 (Juniors 10+) <br>&nbsp\;&nbsp\
 ;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbs
 p\;&nbsp\;Ending Date:  AUGUST 14  <br><br>ADDRESSES:<br>OUTDOOR FIELD SOUT
 H:    2310 Bliss Spillar Road\, Manchaca\, TX 78652<br>MAILING:  Archery Tr
 aining Center\, Inc.\, PO Box 93216\, Austin\, TX 78709<br><br>E-MAIL: <a h
 ref="mailto:archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com">archerytrainingcenteraus
 tin@gmail.com</a><br><br>PHONE/TEXT:  512 975 1850<br><br>CAPACITY:    10 a
 rchers per class or in accordance with CDC guidelines<br>AGES:             
 10 - 80+ years old (See start dates above)<br>DISTANCES:  9m\, 13.5m\, 18m\
 , 20m-70m<br>BOWS:           Recurves  <br>(If you are not a recurve archer
 \, but would like to learn to shoot a recurve bow\, please stay tuned to ou
 r Instagram for announcements of the re-opening of our in-person First-time
  Classes\, or register online for a few Virtual NTS Form classes with Coach
  Racae.)<br><br>EQUIPMENT: <br>These classes are for archers who have their
  own equipment\, consisting of at least a recurve bow\, 12 aluminum or carb
 on arrows\, armguard\, finger tab\, hip or field quiver.  (If you need to c
 hange your equipment or order your own\, please contact Coach Racae at <a h
 ref="mailto:archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com">archerytrainingcenteraus
 tin@gmail.com</a>. She will specify what you´ll need and help you order it\
 , so you buy the correct equipment for your strength and experience.)<br><b
 r>INSTRUCTOR / COACH:<br>USA Archery Level 2 Instructor Ted Aanstoos  <br><
 br>CLASS TIMES:<br>These are the days/times that are available to you. (Add
 itional sessions will be added in future.)<br><br>SAT:     9:00-10:30pm <br
 >WED:    9:00-10:30pm <br>Please check <a href="http://www.archerytrainingc
 enter.com/calendar">www.archerytrainingcenter.com/calendar</a> before regis
 tering!<br><br>DAYS CLOSED: <br>The outdoor range is closed\, gates locked\
 , and targets stored away except during the above class times.<br><br>ENROL
 LMENT IS ON A FIRST-RECEIVED AND PAID BASIS.<br>Complete the Outdoor Target
  Archery Registration Form under Adults or Juniors at <a href="http://www.a
 rcherytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrainingcenter.com</a><br><br>ATTENDAN
 CE RECOMMENDATIONS: <br>Recreational archers have no attendance requirement
 s\, but we would recommend attending at least twice a week to improve faste
 r. <br><br>FEES: <br>All fees are payable in advance of the class to secure
  your place in the class. <br>$30/archer for each 1.5-hr training session  
 OR <br>$115/mo (for 1 training session/week) OR <br>$213/mo (for 2 training
  sessions/week)<br>+ Enrollment fee: $20 (always due once per semester) <br
 ><br>WEATHER:<br>Archers need to practice in all weather\, except when ther
 e is lightning. <br><br>REFUNDS\, CREDITS\, and SUBSTITUTIONS:<br>Substitut
 ions or credits will be applied if we cancel a class due to weather conditi
 ons or instructor illness or if the 24-hr notice is met.<br>There are no re
 funds for paid classes missed during the summer\, except in the case of inj
 ury\, long-term illness\, unforeseen move out of the Austin area\, or being
  expelled for a safety violation. <br><br>24-HR NOTICE: <br>If you let us k
 now within 24 hours of the class that you will miss the class\, you can sub
 stitute another class and use your fee as long as there are places left in 
 that class during the semester. If you notify us less than 24 hours in adva
 nce of the class that you will need to cancel (except for sudden illness)\,
  or you do a "no-show"\, you'll forfeit your fee.<br><br>ILLNESS or INJURY:
  In the case of physical injury or long-term illness\, we require a doctor'
 s note saying that you are unable to practice archery\, and then a doctor's
  note saying that you are again fit to return to archery\, before you will 
 be allowed back in class or a refund/credit issued.<br><br>MEMBERSHIP IN US
 A ARCHERY:<br>Membership in USA Archery is now REQUIRED to participate in J
 OAD and Adult Training.<br>You can attend 2 sessions before joining USAA\, 
 but then we'll need to see your membership card BEFORE WE CAN HAND OUT ANY 
 USA ARCHERY STAR PINS to you during Master Challenge Weeks! <br>If you woul
 d like to see the benefits of USAA membership: <a href="http://www.teamusa.
 org/USA-Archery/Membership/Membership-Benefits">http://www.teamusa.org/USA-
 Archery/Membership/Membership-Benefits</a><br>JOIN USA ARCHERY: <a href="ht
 tps://www.usarchery.org/memberships/become-a-member">https://www.usarchery.
 org/memberships/become-a-member</a><br><br>SAFE SPORTS:<br>PARENTS PLEASE N
 OTE: We are part of the US Olympic Committee's Safe Sport program\, so we m
 inimally require one other adult besides the instructor to be present at al
 l times. Please plan to stay with your child or take turns with other paren
 ts staying whenever necessary to fulfill this requirement. THANKS!<br><br>S
 IGN AND RETURN THESE OUTDOOR WAIVERS:<br>The following documents and waiver
 s will be part of your Registration and Waiver Packet. You will need to sig
 n these  documents before we add your name to those shooting in the class:<
 br>o Membership Form<br>o Safety Rules <br>o Release of Liability Waiver<br
 >o Supervision Policy (Under 18)<br>o Medical Release  <br>o Photo/Video Re
 lease<br>o COVID-19 Guidelines<br>o Outdoor Field Rules of Participation <b
 r><br>VACCINATIONS:<br>We do not at this time require archers to be vaccina
 ted\, but we would like to know if you have been\, so we can take it into c
 onsideration when deciding on issues such as masks and social distancing an
 d abiding by the CDC Guidelines. All our instructors have been fully vaccin
 ated of their own accord.<br><br>QUESTIONS?<br>E-mail us at <a href="mailto
 :archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com">archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.c
 om</a> or<br>Call/Text us at 512 975 1850 <br><br>*NTS = National Training 
 System (which is used for training the USA Olympic team!)<br>*JDT = Junior 
 Dream Team (top 20 Junior archers in the USA!)<br>*JOAD = Junior Olympic Ar
 chery Development
