 nally for the class and pay at that time. However it is difficult to tell h
 ow many people will be dropping in\, so to secure your place\, it is better
  to register and pay in advance to prevent overcrowding. We can only take 1
 0 people on the shooting line at one time. <br><br>When we have more than 1
 0 archers\, we will form a second line\, as in a tournament\, which will re
 duce the number of arrows shot per person within the time. (You can see the
  actual attendance and class composition by looking at past classes at <a h
 ref="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/calendar">www.archerytrainingcent
 er.com/calendar</a>.)<br><br>Scores are also listed below\, if you kept sco
 re\, which is not required\, except on Master Challenge weeks. You need 230
  pts on 40cm target or 240 pts on 60cm target to graduate out of your dista
 nce into Indoor 3A 13.5m\, and again at 13.5m to get into Indoor 3B at 18m 
 (full distance). To be competitive\, you´ll need 230 pts to compete in the 
 indoor tournaments\; 250 pts to graduate into the Outdoor Advanced Archery 
 Program (OAAP) and 250 pts x 5 rounds to apply to join Olympic Path Trainin
 g (OPT) with Coach Racae as your Personal Coach\, private lessons and targe
 ted individualized training.<br><br>PB = Personal Best. <br><br>Registered 
