DESCRIPTION:REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to adult\, juniors 8+\, and parents!
  Please read all the info below and in the registration and waivers.<br><br
 >More information\, registration forms and waivers are available at&nbsp\;<
 a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com"><u><u>www.archerytrainingcent
 er.com</u></u></a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE of these forms:<br><a hr
 ef="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfcwG419ZK9XmA4-JlXM-zhjhvSPCF
 8NCwWJlzFP2w-gRliUw/viewform"><u><u>2022 Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Ju
 niors + Parents</u></u></a>&nbsp\; OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/f
 orms/d/e/1FAIpQLSe-YxPKAMTxiC7kVt6fZuQJeidXENYq_iV4rWj1RaXdLhPoew/viewform"
 ><u><u>2022 Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Adults</u></u></a><br><br>Sign 
 up for just ONE Outdoor 1 class\, because most people graduate out of this 
 class into Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br><br>Your name will be added
  below and your place reserved on a&nbsp\;first registered and paid basis a
 nd after we receive 3 things:&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br><b>2022 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATI
 ON FORM&nbsp\; &nbsp\;+&nbsp\; MEMBERSHIP AND WAIVERS PACKET +&nbsp\; &nbsp
 \;FEE</b><br><br><b>Registered archers&nbsp\;</b>at 9m on 40-cm target face
 :<br><b>Target Assignments:</b><br>1.&nbsp\;<br>2.&nbsp\;<br>3.&nbsp\;<br>4
 .&nbsp\;<br>5.<br>6.<br>7.<br>8.&nbsp\;<br>9.&nbsp\;<br>10.<br><br>Space wi
 ll be limited to 10-15 archers per session depending on the number of famil
 y groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC Guidelines.&nbsp\;<br>Each
  person will have a target stand\, except after 10 people have registered\,
  two members from the same family will share one target stand.<br>The arche
 r and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field until further
  notice or approved by Coach Racae.&nbsp\;<br>Parents of juniors 10+ can si
 gn up as an archer or watch as a spectator.&nbsp\;<br>Parents of juniors 8-
 9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their child for greater
  safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into eac
 h Outdoor 1: First-time Class.&nbsp\;<br><br>We will accept a limited&nbsp\
 ;number of kids under 12 into the program each semester\, depending on the 
 total&nbsp\; number of archers in all the classes. If you join before the l
 imit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and 
 take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;If y
 ou are under 12\, registered and paid after the cut off\, your fee will be 
 returned to you.&nbsp\;<br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or th
 ree times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll
  make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.&nbsp\
 ;<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>a
 p = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be
  needed for Outdoor 2. ($18) Please pay for this at the field\, as our stoc
 k fluctuates because of dealer supply fluctuations<br>fp = form pack (stret
 chband and string loop)\, optional but really needed to practice form\, war
 m up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your s
 cores will be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, y
 ou may not recognize your final score\, because it will have been averaged 
 by taking your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the number 
 of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 3
 0 to get a full round score. After the last class on the weekend\, final sc
 ores will also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more 
 information before your next class.
