DESCRIPTION:REGISTRATIONS NOW OPEN at<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/f
 orms/d/e/1FAIpQLSf_mqxKATQHP9e6XLYCejMhC4_uQX4h4Wj2MzDfEqWVaIku5A/viewform"
 >2021 Summer JOAD Archery Camps</a><br><br>More information and registratio
 n form will also&nbsp\; be available soon on&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.arch
 erytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrainingcenter.com</a>.<br>Coach: USA Arc
 hery Level 4 NTS Coach Racae Meyer<br><br>Registered Archers:<br>1. Avi B\,
 . 13 at 9m -&nbsp\;<br>2. Ashrit B.\, 10 at 9m&nbsp\;<br>3. Skye A.\, 14\,&
 nbsp\; 9m\, graduated to 13.5m with 245 at 9m&nbsp\;<br>4. Sharon A. L3 coa
 ch in training @ 9m<br>5. Sierra H.\, 14 @ 9m&nbsp\;<br>6. Sam M.\, 12 @ 9m
 <br>7. Victor C.\, 9 @ 9m<br>8.&nbsp\;<br>9.<br>10.<br><br><b>What we worke
 d on today:</b><br>The hands: the only part of your body that touches the b
 ow.<br>&nbsp\;<b># 3: Hook and Grip</b> -&nbsp\;<br>- Hook:<br>- - Place th
 e string in front of the 1st joint of 1st and 3rd fingers\; behind the midd
 le finger<br>- - Little finger and thumb behind palm of hand\;&nbsp\; &nbsp
 \;goes under jaw\, not on side of face<br>- Grip:&nbsp\;<br>- - Meaty part 
 of thumb pushes on grip towards target\; nothing past the lifeline<br>- - R
 elax fingers under or just down - but off the bow to the side<br>- - Thumb 
 pointing to target<br>- - Index finger pointing down<br>How to put on and u
 se a <b>fingersling</b><br>How to <b>score a JOAD target\; scoring on round
 </b>&nbsp\;on indoor scorecard<br>Trying to create <b>groups of arrows</b> 
 by consistency of form<br><b>#4: Set - Posture</b><br>- - Keep core tight\,
  chest down\; set hips under rib cage<br><b>#5: Set Up </b>- Raising the bo
 w<br>- - Keep shoulders level\, down and back<br>Keeping the <b>bow arm up<
 /b> after release until you hear the arrow hit the paper<br><b>Distraction 
 exercise: </b>Shooting for fun at balloons
