DESCRIPTION:This weekly practice time is being offered on a trial basis thi
 s Spring to see how popular the evening would be. It´s intended to give eve
 ryone more time to practice in the range\, but not as a substitute for the 
 regularly scheduled and coached classes.&nbsp\;<br><br>Details:<br><ul><li>
 One fee: <b>$25 for the evening</b> payable upon arrival.<br></li><li>You c
 an <b>sign up at the range in advance </b>to reserve your place on the shoo
 ting line\,<b> or just show up</b>\, if it´s not nearing full.<br></li><li>
 <b>No coaching</b> - just focused practice!<br></li><li>Open to recurve arc
 hers who have taken the <b>Indoor 1: First-time Class</b> and regularly att
 end at least <b>two (2) hours/month</b> in scheduled group coached classes&
 nbsp\;<br></li><li>Also open to <b>experienced recurve archers</b>\, who ha
 ve previously met with Coach Racae.<br></li><li><b>Olympic recurve bows onl
 y</b> (not compounds\, traditional bows\, cross bows)<br></li><li>If junior
  archers are present\, there must be <b>at least two adults</b> in the rang
 e at all times (parents\, adult archers).<br></li><li>Max. draw weight:<b> 
 45 lbs.</b><br></li><li>This same time can also be booked in advance for <b
 >one-hour private lessons</b> with Coach Racae ($50/hr)<br></li><li>All <b>
 safety rules</b> will be enforced and obeyed.</li></ul>Any questions: Conta
 ct Coach Racae 512 975 1850<br><br>See you soon!
