DESCRIPTION:Registration form: OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m<br><br>Add your nam
 e to Target Assignment List below or submit the above completed form.<br>Fo
 cus primarily on perfecting your form\, <br>slowly increasing your physical
  strength and draw weight\, <br>strengthening your mental program\, <br>det
 ermining your average and personal best\, <br>understanding the spread betw
 een the two\, and working on closing it.<br><br>You need your own equipment
  <br>Competition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 car
 bon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard
 \, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Cl
 icker and side rods may not be added until you reach a higher level\, but y
 ou should order them in advance.) <br><br>Wear your ATCI shirt to training.
 <br><br>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm target fac
 e you'll move back to the next distance until you reach your competition di
 stance<br>If you trained outdoors in the 2024 season\, you'll return to the
  farthest distance you shot.<br><br>Target arrangements may vary each sessi
 on\, depending on who attends and distances needed.<br>Target 1 at 70m (U21
  + Seniors competition distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use 
 it for independent practice in between classes.<br>Target 2 at 60m (U18 + M
 asters competition distance) <br>Target 3 at 50m<br>Target 4 at 40m (U15 co
 mpetition distance) <br>Target 5 at 30m (U13 competition distance) <br>Targ
 ets 6+7+8 at 20m (for those who have shot at 18m indoors or with Coach Raca
 e's approval)<br>Targets 9 + 10 at 13.5m (for those who have just graduated
  from indoors at 9m)<br><br>Ideally\, we want to practice with two archers/
 target to replicate competition conditions as much as possible.<br><br>Targ
 et Assignments:<br>Targets are assigned outdoors in advance to reduce confu
 sion and delay on the day\,<br>so add your name next to your distance below
 . <br>If you need help or have questions\, email/text Coach Racae<br>(Dotte
 d lines represent tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)<br>----------
 ------------------------<br>1A. (70m) <b>Jake L.\, </b>USAA<br>1B<br><br>2A
 . (60m)  <br>2B<br><br>3A. (50m)  <b>Nick E.\, </b>adult\, USAA\, pd<br>---
 -------------------------------<br>3B<br><br>4A. (40m) <b>Finn E.\, </b>13\
 , USAA\, pd<br>4B <b>Erika OG</b>\, adult\, USAA\, pd<br>------------------
 ----------------<br>5A. (40m)<b>Sophia D</b>\, adult\, USAA\, f<br>5B. <br>
 <br>6A. (30m) <b>Anna P</b>\, adult\,USAA\,  pd<br>------------------------
 ----------<br>6B. 30m<b> Adrianne M\,</b> USAA\, pd  <b>286 pts.<br></b><br
 >7A. (30m) <b>Riley M.\,</b>USAA\,13\,pd<br>7B. <br>-----------------------
