DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u>REGISTER N
 OW !<br><br>Open to adult\, juniors 8+\, and parents! Please read all the i
 nfo below and in the registration and waivers.<br><br>More information\, re
 gistration forms and waivers are available at&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.arc
 herytrainingcenter.com"><u><u>www.archerytrainingcenter.com</u></u></a>.<br
 ><br>Register here using ONE of these forms:<br><a href="https://docs.googl
 e.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfcwG419ZK9XmA4-JlXM-zhjhvSPCF8NCwWJlzFP2w-gRliUw/vi
 ewform"><u><u>2022 Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Juniors + Parents</u></u
 ></a>&nbsp\; OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSe-YxP
 KAMTxiC7kVt6fZuQJeidXENYq_iV4rWj1RaXdLhPoew/viewform"><u><u>2022 Outdoor 1:
  First-time Class for Adults</u></u></a><br><br>Sign up for just ONE Outdoo
 r 1 class\, because most people graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 a
 fter the first lesson.<br><br>Your name will be added below and your place 
 reserved on a&nbsp\;first registered and paid basis and after we receive 3 
 things:&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br><b>2022 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM&nbsp\; &nbsp\;
 +&nbsp\; MEMBERSHIP AND WAIVERS PACKET +&nbsp\; &nbsp\;FEE</b><br><br><br><
 b>If your name is PENDING\,&nbsp\;</b>it means we have not received one of 
 the above three things in advance of the class. Your name will be removed\,
  if your space is needed by another person before we receive the above. You
  will then need to reschedule.&nbsp\;<b><br></b><br><b>Registered archers&n
 bsp\;</b>at 9m on 40-cm target face unless otherwise noted below:<br><b>Tar
 get Assignments:</b><br>1. (70m target)&nbsp\;<br>2. (40m target)<br>3. (30
 m target)<br>4. (20m target)<br><br>5A.&nbsp\;<b>Jennie B</b>.\, adult - pd
  - <b>42 pts -&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br>5B.<br><br>6A. <b>Caleb R.\, </b>adult
  - pd - <b>71 pts -&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br>6B.<br><br>7A. <b>Joel H.\, </b>a
 dult - pd - <b>58 pts -&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br>7B.<br><br>8A.&nbsp\;<b>Aiyla
  M.\,&nbsp\;</b>&nbsp\;11\, on 60-cm target face - pd - <b>73 pts -&gt\; Ou
 tdoor 2</b><br>8B.<br>&nbsp\;<u></u><br><u></u>9A. <b>Eddie A.\, </b>adult\
 , pd - <b>77 pts -&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br>9B.<br><br>10A.<br>10B.<u></u><br>
 <u></u><br>Space will be limited to 10-15 archers per session depending on 
 the number of family groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC Guideli
 nes.&nbsp\;<br>Each person will have a target stand\, except after 10 peopl
 e have registered\, two members from the same family will share one target 
 stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the 
 field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae.&nbsp\;<br>Parents of
  juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator.&nbsp\;<br>Pa
 rents of juniors 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with thei
 r child for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) i
 s accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-time Class.&nbsp\;<br><br>We will acc
 ept a limited&nbsp\;number of kids under 12 into the program each semester\
 , depending on the total&nbsp\; number of archers in all the classes. If yo
 u join before the limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay 
 in the program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Ou
 tdoor 2.&nbsp\;If you are under 12\, registered and paid after the cut off\
 , your fee will be returned to you.&nbsp\;<br><br>Juniors may need to take 
 Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by sco
 ring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end
  of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into 
 Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersli
 ng)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($18) Please pay for this at the 
 field\, as our stock fluctuates because of dealer supply fluctuations<br>fp
  = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but really needed to 
 practice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdo
 or 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a complete ro
 und (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, because it will 
 have been averaged by taking your recorded score from your scorecard\, divi
 ding by the number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then mu
 ltiplying that by 30 to get a full round score. After the last class on the
  weekend\, final scores will also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in 
 an email with more information before your next class.<u></u><u></u><u></u>
 <u></u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
