 sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator.&nbsp\;<br>Parents of juniors 
 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their child for great
 er safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into e
 ach Outdoor 1: First-time Class.&nbsp\;<br><br>We will accept a limited&nbs
 p\;number of kids under 12 into the program each semester\, depending on th
 e total&nbsp\; number of archers in all the classes. If you join before the
  limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program an
 d take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;If
  you are under 12\, registered and paid after the cut off\, your fee will b
 e returned to you.&nbsp\;<br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or 
 three times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´
 ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.&nbs
 p\;<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br
 >ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will 
 be needed for Outdoor 2. ($18) Please pay for this at the field\, as our st
 ock fluctuates because of dealer supply fluctuations<br>fp = form pack (str
 etchband and string loop)\, optional but really needed to practice form\, w
 arm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your
  scores will be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\,
  you may not recognize your final score\, because it will have been average
 d by taking your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the numbe
 r of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by
  30 to get a full round score. After the last class on the weekend\, final 
 scores will also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with mor
 e information before your next class.<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u>
