 . You´ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrow
 s.&nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<
 br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which
  will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($18) Please pay for this at the field\, as 
 our stock fluctuates because of dealer supply fluctuations.<br>fp = form pa
 ck (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but really needed to practice f
 orm\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class
 \, your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 ar
 rows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, because it will have been 
 averaged by taking your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by th
 e number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying 
 that by 30 to get a full round score. After the last class on the weekend\,
  final scores will usually be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an emai
 l with more information before your next class.<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u>
 <u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></
 u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
