DESCRIPTION:Registered Archers:<br>1.&nbsp\;<br>2.<br>3.<br>4..<br>5.<br>6.
 <br>7.<br>8.<br>9.<br>10.<br><br>OVERVIEW:<br>These Outdoor Target Archery 
 recreational classes prepare you to shoot at longer and longer distances un
 til you reach your USA Archery tournament distance (see below)\, while lear
 ning the National Training System\, which is the most highly researched bio
 mechanical method of shooting taught out at the Olympic Training Center. Yo
 u will be shooting with other archers in group sessions\, so you can all le
 arn together and from each other. <br><br>PREREQUISITE: <br>Some archery ex
 perience and your own recurve archery equipment is required.<br><br>OPEN TO
  ADULTS / JUNIORS / PARENTS (with experience and own recurve archery equipm
 ent)<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the fi
 eld until further notice or approved by Coach Racae.<br>Space will be limit
 ed to a maximum of 10 archers per session or in accordance with CDC Guideli
 nes.<br><br>NO DROP INS:<br>You cannot just drop in\, because the number of
  archers on the shooting line is very limited and we are observing CDC guid
 elines with social distancing.<br><br>DATES:    Start Dates: MAY 15 (Adults
 ) or JUNE 12 (Juniors 10+) <br>&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&n
 bsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;Ending Date:  AUGUST 
 14  <br><br>ADDRESSES:<br>OUTDOOR FIELD SOUTH:    2310 Bliss Spillar Road\,
  Manchaca\, TX 78652<br>MAILING:  Archery Training Center\, Inc.\, PO Box 9
 3216\, Austin\, TX 78709<br><br>E-MAIL: <a href="mailto:archerytrainingcent
 eraustin@gmail.com">archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a><br><br>PHONE/
 TEXT:  512 975 1850<br><br>CAPACITY:    10 archers per class or in accordan
 ce with CDC guidelines<br>AGES:             10 - 80+ years old (See start d
 ates above)<br>DISTANCES:  9m\, 13.5m\, 18m\, 20m-70m<br>BOWS:           Re
 curves  <br>(If you are not a recurve archer\, but would like to learn to s
 hoot a recurve bow\, please stay tuned to our Instagram for announcements o
 f the re-opening of our in-person First-time Classes\, or register online f
 or a few Virtual NTS Form classes with Coach Racae.)<br><br>EQUIPMENT: <br>
 These classes are for archers who have their own equipment\, consisting of 
 at least a recurve bow\, 12 aluminum or carbon arrows\, armguard\, finger t
 ab\, hip or field quiver.  (If you need to change your equipment or order y
 our own\, please contact Coach Racae at <a href="mailto:archerytrainingcent
 eraustin@gmail.com">archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a>. She will spe
 cify what you´ll need and help you order it\, so you buy the correct equipm
 ent for your strength and experience.)<br><br>INSTRUCTOR / COACH:<br>USA Ar
 chery Level 2 Instructor Ted Aanstoos  <br><br>CLASS TIMES:<br>These are th
 e days/times that are available to you. (Additional sessions will be added 
 in future.)<br><br>SAT:     9:00-10:30pm <br>WED:    9:00-10:30pm <br>Pleas
 e check <a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/calendar">www.archery
 trainingcenter.com/calendar</a> before registering!<br><br>DAYS CLOSED: <br
 >The outdoor range is closed\, gates locked\, and targets stored away excep
 t during the above class times.<br><br>ENROLLMENT IS ON A FIRST-RECEIVED AN
 D PAID BASIS.<br>Complete the Outdoor Target Archery Registration Form unde
 r Adults or Juniors at <a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.a
 rcherytrainingcenter.com</a><br><br>ATTENDANCE RECOMMENDATIONS: <br>Recreat
 ional archers have no attendance requirements\, but we would recommend atte
 nding at least twice a week to improve faster. <br><br>FEES: <br>All fees a
 re payable in advance of the class to secure your place in the class. <br>$
 30/archer for each 1.5-hr training session  OR <br>$115/mo (for 1 training 
 session/week) OR <br>$213/mo (for 2 training sessions/week)<br>+ Enrollment
  fee: $20 (always due once per semester) <br><br>WEATHER:<br>Archers need t
 o practice in all weather\, except when there is lightning. <br><br>REFUNDS
 \, CREDITS\, and SUBSTITUTIONS:<br>Substitutions or credits will be applied
  if we cancel a class due to weather conditions or instructor illness or if
  the 24-hr notice is met.<br>There are no refunds for paid classes missed d
 uring the summer\, except in the case of injury\, long-term illness\, unfor
 eseen move out of the Austin area\, or being expelled for a safety violatio
 n. <br><br>24-HR NOTICE: <br>If you let us know within 24 hours of the clas
 s that you will miss the class\, you can substitute another class and use y
 our fee as long as there are places left in that class during the semester.
  If you notify us less than 24 hours in advance of the class that you will 
 need to cancel (except for sudden illness)\, or you do a "no-show"\, you'll
  forfeit your fee.<br><br>ILLNESS or INJURY: In the case of physical injury
  or long-term illness\, we require a doctor's note saying that you are unab
 le to practice archery\, and then a doctor's note saying that you are again
  fit to return to archery\, before you will be allowed back in class or a r
 efund/credit issued.<br><br>MEMBERSHIP IN USA ARCHERY:<br>Membership in USA
  Archery is now REQUIRED to participate in JOAD and Adult Training.<br>You 
 can attend 2 sessions before joining USAA\, but then we'll need to see your
  membership card BEFORE WE CAN HAND OUT ANY USA ARCHERY STAR PINS to you du
 ring Master Challenge Weeks! <br>If you would like to see the benefits of U
 SAA membership: <a href="http://www.teamusa.org/USA-Archery/Membership/Memb
 ership-Benefits">http://www.teamusa.org/USA-Archery/Membership/Membership-B
 enefits</a><br>JOIN USA ARCHERY: <a href="https://www.usarchery.org/members
 hips/become-a-member">https://www.usarchery.org/memberships/become-a-member
 </a><br><br>SAFE SPORTS:<br>PARENTS PLEASE NOTE: We are part of the US Olym
 pic Committee's Safe Sport program\, so we minimally require one other adul
 t besides the instructor to be present at all times. Please plan to stay wi
 th your child or take turns with other parents staying whenever necessary t
 o fulfill this requirement. THANKS!<br><br>SIGN AND RETURN THESE OUTDOOR WA
 IVERS:<br>The following documents and waivers will be part of your Registra
 tion and Waiver Packet. You will need to sign these  documents before we ad
 d your name to those shooting in the class:<br>o Membership Form<br>o Safet
 y Rules <br>o Release of Liability Waiver<br>o Supervision Policy (Under 18
 )<br>o Medical Release  <br>o Photo/Video Release<br>o COVID-19 Guidelines<
 br>o Outdoor Field Rules of Participation <br><br>VACCINATIONS:<br>We do no
 t at this time require archers to be vaccinated\, but we would like to know
  if you have been\, so we can take it into consideration when deciding on i
 ssues such as masks and social distancing and abiding by the CDC Guidelines
 . All our instructors have been fully vaccinated of their own accord.<br><b
 r>QUESTIONS?<br>E-mail us at <a href="mailto:archerytrainingcenteraustin@gm
 ail.com">archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a> or<br>Call/Text us at 51
 2 975 1850 <br><br>*NTS = National Training System (which is used for train
 ing the USA Olympic team!)<br>*JDT = Junior Dream Team (top 20 Junior arche
 rs in the USA!)<br>*JOAD = Junior Olympic Archery Development
