DESCRIPTION:<h4><b>November 7-9\, 2025 in the Physical Education Activity B
 uilding at Texas A&amp\;M University</b></h4><br>The response to the Aggie 
 Invitational registration opening on 9/8 at 7:00am has been overwhelming al
 ready\, so....<b><br></b><br><b>Sign up NOW</b><br>Do not wait to see if yo
 u qualify to go or you won't get a place:<br><a href="https://www.usarchery
 .org/events/event-information/48257" target="_blank">https://www.usarchery.
 org/events/event-information/48257</a><br><br><b>Our team shooting times ar
 e:</b><br><b>8:00 am </b><br><b>1:00 pm </b>(already full)<br><b>6:00 pm </
 b><br>but sign up for any time available or convenient.<br>Other times are 
 listed in the registration link above.<br><br><b>Sign up for </b><b>one sho
 oting time of 60 arrows (2 rounds of 30 arrows) on </b><b>a 40-cm target fa
 ce.</b><br><b><br>Target face: </b>Choose single NOT triangular 3-spot unle
 ss you have practiced on and really like a 3-spot.<b> </b><br><br><b>Scroll
  down for a list of our members and their shooting times.</b><br><br><b>Let
  Coach Racae know your shooting time</b>\, if it is not listed below.  <br>
 If you do not intend to register\, let her know that\, too\, please.<br><br
 >We will be practicing outdoors from now on at 18m<b>.</b> Alternate some d
 ays with shooting at your outdoor distance\, so you practice for both indoo
 r and outdoor competitions. <br><br>If you're thinking of participating or 
 competing\, and want to try out for the new <b>2026 ATCI Competition Team</
 b>\, let Coach Racae know. <br><br><b>To make the team\, you'll need to sho
 ot an MQS (minimum qualifying score):</b> The <b>Arrow Average (AA) is 7 pt
 s in one round of 30 arrows (indoors) or 36 arrows (outdoors) at 18m</b>:<u
 l><li>The <b>MQS for 2026 ATCI Indoor Competition Team</b> is <b>210 pts </
 b>at 18m on either 60cm target face (U13 and U15) or 40cm target face (U18\
 , U21\,Seniors (21-49)\, Masters (50+). </li><li>The <b>MQS for</b> <b>2026
  ATCI Outdoor Competition Team</b> will be <b>250 pts</b> on 122cm target f
 ace at competition distance for age. </li></ul><br>Even if you don't quite 
 make the MQS (arrow avg of 6 pts)\, you can still register for competitions
  and participate for the experience\, to be better prepared for the followi
 ng seasons with a view of trying for one of the 2027 ATCI Competition Teams
 .<br><br>If your arrow average is less than 6 pts in time to register for t
 he competition\, go to observe as a spectator instead\, so you'll be more p
 repared for the competitions the following year.<br><br><b>ATCI archers and
  their shooting times </b><br>These are also on the calendar under the shoo
 ting times on the day.<br>SMR = Senior Male Recurve\; SFR = Senior Female R
 ecurve<br><b>Sat 8 am</b><ol><li>Joel Y - SMR</li><li>Nick E - SMR</li><li>
 Javier G - SMR</li><li>Erika G - SFR</li><li>Hannah T - SFR</li></ol><b>Sat
  1 pm</b><br><ol><li>Finn E. U15 M</li><li>Miles G. U15 M</li><li>Abby Y. U
 15 F</li><li>Sara T. U15 F</li><li>Rhys E. U13 M</li><li>Ellie Y. U13 F</li
 ></ol><br><b>Sat 6 pm</b><br><ol><li>Colby K. SMR</li><li>Adrianne M. SFR</
 li><li>Alexandra (Lexi) E. U18 F</li><li>Matt L. U15 M</li><li>Luke T. U15 
 M<br></li><li>Anush  U15 M</li><li>Emma T. U15 F</li></ol>
