DESCRIPTION:Due to the HUGE amount of rain over this last week\, we anticip
 ate the parking will be deep mud and slippery\, so we´ll cancel today´s cla
 ss\, and add an extra 45 min onto June 12 and 19.<br>Let us know if you wou
 ld prefer another solution.<br><br>Registered :<br>Once you are shooting at
  20m\, your goal is to get to the next distance (+10m) by shooting 320 pts 
 at your present distance on a 122-cm target in one round of 36 arrows until
  you reach your tournament distance as listed here:<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbs
 p\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; Masters: (50+) 60m&nbsp\;<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &n
 bsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; Seniors (21-50+) 70m\;<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nb
 sp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; Juniors (18-20) 70m&nbsp\;<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; 
 &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; Cadets (15-17) 60m&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br>&nbsp\;
  &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; Cubs (13-14) 50m&nbsp\;<br>&nbsp\;
  &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; Bowman (10-12) 30m<br><br>1. Kevin
  B.\, 20m (to make up)<br>2. Cyrenna V.\, 9m on 40cm target face\; Goal 230
  pts to move to 13.5m (to make up)<br>3. Nate H.\, 20m (add 45 min to June 
 12 + 19)<br>4..<br>5.<br>6.<br>7.<br>8.<br>9.<br>10.<br><br>OVERVIEW:<br>Th
 ese Outdoor Target Archery recreational classes prepare you to shoot at lon
 ger and longer distances until you reach your USA Archery tournament distan
 ce (see below)\, while learning the National Training System\, which is the
  most highly researched biomechanical method of shooting taught out at the 
 Olympic Training Center. You will be shooting with other archers in group s
 essions\, so you can all learn together and from each other. <br><br>PREREQ
 UISITE: <br>Some archery experience and your own recurve archery equipment 
 is required.<br><br>OPEN TO ADULTS / JUNIORS / PARENTS (with experience and
  own recurve archery equipment)<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectato
 r will be allowed on the field until further notice or approved by Coach Ra
 cae.<br>Space will be limited to a maximum of 10 archers per session or in 
 accordance with CDC Guidelines.<br><br>NO DROP INS:<br>You cannot just drop
  in\, because the number of archers on the shooting line is very limited an
 d we are observing CDC guidelines with social distancing.<br><br>DATES:    
 Start Dates: MAY 15 (Adults) or JUNE 12 (Juniors 10+) <br>&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nb
 sp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&
 nbsp\;Ending Date:  AUGUST 14  <br><br>ADDRESSES:<br>OUTDOOR FIELD SOUTH:  
   2310 Bliss Spillar Road\, Manchaca\, TX 78652<br>MAILING:  Archery Traini
 ng Center\, Inc.\, PO Box 93216\, Austin\, TX 78709<br><br>E-MAIL: <a href=
 "mailto:archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com">archerytrainingcenteraustin@
 gmail.com</a><br><br>PHONE/TEXT:  512 975 1850<br><br>CAPACITY:    10 arche
 rs per class or in accordance with CDC guidelines<br>AGES:             10 -
  80+ years old (See start dates above)<br>DISTANCES:  9m\, 13.5m\, 18m\, 20
 m-70m<br>BOWS:           Recurves  <br>(If you are not a recurve archer\, b
 ut would like to learn to shoot a recurve bow\, please stay tuned to our In
 stagram for announcements of the re-opening of our in-person First-time Cla
 sses\, or register online for a few Virtual NTS Form classes with Coach Rac
 ae.)<br><br>EQUIPMENT: <br>These classes are for archers who have their own
  equipment\, consisting of at least a recurve bow\, 12 aluminum or carbon a
 rrows\, armguard\, finger tab\, hip or field quiver.  (If you need to chang
 e your equipment or order your own\, please contact Coach Racae at <a href=
 "mailto:archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com">archerytrainingcenteraustin@
 gmail.com</a>. She will specify what you´ll need and help you order it\, so
  you buy the correct equipment for your strength and experience.)<br><br>IN
 STRUCTOR / COACH:<br>USA Archery Level 2 Instructor Ted Aanstoos  <br><br>C
 LASS TIMES:<br>These are the days/times that are available to you. (Additio
 nal sessions will be added in future.)<br><br>SAT:     9:00-10:30pm <br>WED
 :    9:00-10:30pm <br>Please check <a href="http://www.archerytrainingcente
 r.com/calendar">www.archerytrainingcenter.com/calendar</a> before registeri
 ng!<br><br>DAYS CLOSED: <br>The outdoor range is closed\, gates locked\, an
 d targets stored away except during the above class times.<br><br>ENROLLMEN
 T IS ON A FIRST-RECEIVED AND PAID BASIS.<br>Complete the Outdoor Target Arc
 hery Registration Form under Adults or Juniors at <a href="http://www.arche
 rytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrainingcenter.com</a><br><br>ATTENDANCE R
 ECOMMENDATIONS: <br>Recreational archers have no attendance requirements\, 
 but we would recommend attending at least twice a week to improve faster. <
 br><br>FEES: <br>All fees are payable in advance of the class to secure you
 r place in the class. <br>$30/archer for each 1.5-hr training session  OR <
 br>$115/mo (for 1 training session/week) OR <br>$213/mo (for 2 training ses
 sions/week)<br>+ Enrollment fee: $20 (always due once per semester) <br><br
 >WEATHER:<br>Archers need to practice in all weather\, except when there is
  lightning. <br><br>REFUNDS\, CREDITS\, and SUBSTITUTIONS:<br>Substitutions
  or credits will be applied if we cancel a class due to weather conditions 
 or instructor illness or if the 24-hr notice is met.<br>There are no refund
 s for paid classes missed during the summer\, except in the case of injury\
 , long-term illness\, unforeseen move out of the Austin area\, or being exp
 elled for a safety violation. <br><br>24-HR NOTICE: <br>If you let us know 
 within 24 hours of the class that you will miss the class\, you can substit
 ute another class and use your fee as long as there are places left in that
  class during the semester. If you notify us less than 24 hours in advance 
 of the class that you will need to cancel (except for sudden illness)\, or 
 you do a "no-show"\, you'll forfeit your fee.<br><br>ILLNESS or INJURY: In 
 the case of physical injury or long-term illness\, we require a doctor's no
 te saying that you are unable to practice archery\, and then a doctor's not
 e saying that you are again fit to return to archery\, before you will be a
 llowed back in class or a refund/credit issued.<br><br>MEMBERSHIP IN USA AR
 CHERY:<br>Membership in USA Archery is now REQUIRED to participate in JOAD 
 and Adult Training.<br>You can attend 2 sessions before joining USAA\, but 
 then we'll need to see your membership card BEFORE WE CAN HAND OUT ANY USA 
 ARCHERY STAR PINS to you during Master Challenge Weeks! <br>If you would li
 ke to see the benefits of USAA membership: <a href="http://www.teamusa.org/
 USA-Archery/Membership/Membership-Benefits">http://www.teamusa.org/USA-Arch
 ery/Membership/Membership-Benefits</a><br>JOIN USA ARCHERY: <a href="https:
 //www.usarchery.org/memberships/become-a-member">https://www.usarchery.org/
 memberships/become-a-member</a><br><br>SAFE SPORTS:<br>PARENTS PLEASE NOTE:
  We are part of the US Olympic Committee's Safe Sport program\, so we minim
 ally require one other adult besides the instructor to be present at all ti
 mes. Please plan to stay with your child or take turns with other parents s
 taying whenever necessary to fulfill this requirement. THANKS!<br><br>SIGN 
 AND RETURN THESE OUTDOOR WAIVERS:<br>The following documents and waivers wi
 ll be part of your Registration and Waiver Packet. You will need to sign th
 ese  documents before we add your name to those shooting in the class:<br>o
  Membership Form<br>o Safety Rules <br>o Release of Liability Waiver<br>o S
 upervision Policy (Under 18)<br>o Medical Release  <br>o Photo/Video Releas
 e<br>o COVID-19 Guidelines<br>o Outdoor Field Rules of Participation <br><b
 r>VACCINATIONS:<br>We do not at this time require archers to be vaccinated\
 , but we would like to know if you have been\, so we can take it into consi
 deration when deciding on issues such as masks and social distancing and ab
 iding by the CDC Guidelines. All our instructors have been fully vaccinated
  of their own accord.<br><br>QUESTIONS?<br>E-mail us at <a href="mailto:arc
 herytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com">archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</
 a> or<br>Call/Text us at 512 975 1850 <br><br>*NTS = National Training Syst
 em (which is used for training the USA Olympic team!)<br>*JDT = Junior Drea
 m Team (top 20 Junior archers in the USA!)<br>*JOAD = Junior Olympic Archer
 y Development
