DESCRIPTION:Registration form: OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m\n\nAdd your name to
  Target Assignment List below or submit the above completed form.\nFocus pr
 imarily on perfecting your form\, \nslowly increasing your physical strengt
 h and draw weight\, \nstrengthening your mental program\, \ndetermining you
 r average and personal best\, \nunderstanding the spread between the two\, 
 and working on closing it.\n\nYou need your own equipment \nCompetition rec
 urve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side ro
 d/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finge
 r sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods 
 may not be added until you reach a higher level\, but you should order them
  in advance.) \n\nWear your ATCI shirt to training.\n\nWhen you score 288 p
 ts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the ne
 xt distance until you reach your competition distance\nIf you trained outdo
 ors in the 2024 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.\n
 \nTarget arrangements may vary each session\, depending on who attends and 
 distances needed.\nTarget 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) sho
 uld always stay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent practice in betwe
 en classes.\nTarget 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition distance) \nTarget 
 3 at 50m\nTarget 4 at 40m (U15 competition distance) \nTarget 5 at 30m (U13
  competition distance) \nTargets 6+7+8 at 20m (for those who have shot at 1
 8m indoors or with Coach Racae's approval)\nTargets 9 + 10 at 13.5m (for th
 ose who have just graduated from indoors at 9m)\n\nIdeally\, we want to pra
 ctice with two archers/target to replicate competition conditions as much a
 s possible.\n\nTarget Assignments:\nTargets are assigned outdoors in advanc
 e to reduce confusion and delay on the day\,\nso add your name next to your
  distance below. \nIf you need help or have questions\, email/text Coach Ra
 cae\n(Dotted lines represent tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)\n-
 ---------------------------------\n1A. (70m)\n1B\n\n2A. (60m)  \n2B\n\n3A. 
 (50m)  \n----------------------------------\n3B\n\n4A. (40m) \n4B\n--------
 --------------------------\n5A. (40m)\n5B. \n\n6A. (30m)\n-----------------
 -----------------\n6B. \n\n7A. (30m)\n7B. \n-------------------------------
 --- \n8A. (30m)\n8B. \n\n9A. (20m)\n----------------------------------\n9B.
  \n\n10A. (13.5m)\n10B
