 b>Miles G.</b>\, 12\, USAA\, OB\, pd = 91 + 82 = <b>173/2 = 87 avg</b><br>1
 0B. <b>Rhys E\, </b>10\, USAA\, OB\, pd =  33 + 54 = <b>87/2 = 44 avg</b><b
 r><br> <b>Yugan C</b>.\, 12\, USAA\, OB pd (3/12)  - injured deltoid - rest
  until Wed.<br><br>When you shoot at 18m to practice for the Aggie Invitati
 onal in Nov\, you'll be on a 40-cm target face set up 4 to a target (even i
 f only one or two archers are on that target). <br>You should practice one 
 round of 30 arrows at each target face high/low/left/right so you are prepa
 red for your target assignment at the indoor competitions<br><br>Ideally\, 
 we want to practice with at least two archers/target to replicate competiti
 on conditions as much as possible.<br>You can decide each week if you want 
 to shoot at your long distance or at 18m and add or move your name on the c
 alendar accordingly. You should alternate distance each day\, so you practi
 ce both. <br><br>Starting Oct 1 to the Nov Aggie Invitational and Jan 1 for
  the Feb Indoor Nationals\, everyone should be shooting at 18m and scoring 
 to determine their average and their personal bests\, understand the spread
  between the two\, and work on closing it.
