DESCRIPTION:Registered Archers:<br>1. Cyrenna V. 13.5m on 40-cm target face
  (45 min make up for 1/2 of June 5) - paid<br>2.&nbsp\;<br>3. Andrew M. - 3
 0m on 122-cm target face - paid<br>4..Nate H. - 20m on 122-cm target face -
  paid<br>5.<br>6.<br>7.<br>8.<br>9.<br>10.<br><br>OVERVIEW:<br>These Outdoo
 r Target Archery recreational classes prepare you to shoot at longer and lo
 nger distances until you reach your USA Archery tournament distance (see be
 low)\, while learning the National Training System\, which is the most high
 ly researched biomechanical method of shooting taught out at the Olympic Tr
 aining Center. You will be shooting with other archers in group sessions\, 
 so you can all learn together and from each other. <br><br>PREREQUISITE: <b
 r>Some archery experience and your own recurve archery equipment is require
 d.<br><br>OPEN TO ADULTS / JUNIORS / PARENTS (with experience and own recur
 ve archery equipment)<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be 
 allowed on the field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae.<br>Sp
 ace will be limited to a maximum of 10 archers per session or in accordance
  with CDC Guidelines.<br><br>NO DROP INS:<br>You cannot just drop in\, beca
 use the number of archers on the shooting line is very limited and we are o
 bserving CDC guidelines with social distancing.<br><br>DATES:    Start Date
 s: MAY 15 (Adults) or JUNE 12 (Juniors 10+) <br>&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\
 ;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;Endi
 ng Date:  AUGUST 14  <br><br>ADDRESSES:<br>OUTDOOR FIELD SOUTH:    2310 Bli
 ss Spillar Road\, Manchaca\, TX 78652<br>MAILING:  Archery Training Center\
 , Inc.\, PO Box 93216\, Austin\, TX 78709<br><br>E-MAIL: <a href="mailto:ar
 cherytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com">archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com<
 /a><br><br>PHONE/TEXT:  512 975 1850<br><br>CAPACITY:    10 archers per cla
 ss or in accordance with CDC guidelines<br>AGES:             10 - 80+ years
  old (See start dates above)<br>DISTANCES:  9m\, 13.5m\, 18m\, 20m-70m<br>B
 OWS:           Recurves  <br>(If you are not a recurve archer\, but would l
 ike to learn to shoot a recurve bow\, please stay tuned to our Instagram fo
 r announcements of the re-opening of our in-person First-time Classes\, or 
 register online for a few Virtual NTS Form classes with Coach Racae.)<br><b
 r>EQUIPMENT: <br>These classes are for archers who have their own equipment
 \, consisting of at least a recurve bow\, 12 aluminum or carbon arrows\, ar
 mguard\, finger tab\, hip or field quiver.  (If you need to change your equ
 ipment or order your own\, please contact Coach Racae at <a href="mailto:ar
 cherytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com">archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com<
 /a>. She will specify what you´ll need and help you order it\, so you buy t
 he correct equipment for your strength and experience.)<br><br>INSTRUCTOR /
  COACH:<br>USA Archery Level 2 Instructor Ted Aanstoos  <br><br>CLASS TIMES
 :<br>These are the days/times that are available to you. (Additional sessio
 ns will be added in future.)<br><br>SAT:     9:00-10:30pm <br>WED:    9:00-
 10:30pm <br>Please check <a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/cale
 ndar">www.archerytrainingcenter.com/calendar</a> before registering!<br><br
 >DAYS CLOSED: <br>The outdoor range is closed\, gates locked\, and targets 
 stored away except during the above class times.<br><br>ENROLLMENT IS ON A 
 FIRST-RECEIVED AND PAID BASIS.<br>Complete the Outdoor Target Archery Regis
 tration Form under Adults or Juniors at <a href="http://www.archerytraining
 center.com">www.archerytrainingcenter.com</a><br><br>ATTENDANCE RECOMMENDAT
 IONS: <br>Recreational archers have no attendance requirements\, but we wou
 ld recommend attending at least twice a week to improve faster. <br><br>FEE
 S: <br>All fees are payable in advance of the class to secure your place in
  the class. <br>$30/archer for each 1.5-hr training session  OR <br>$115/mo
  (for 1 training session/week) OR <br>$213/mo (for 2 training sessions/week
 )<br>+ Enrollment fee: $20 (always due once per semester) <br><br>WEATHER:<
 br>Archers need to practice in all weather\, except when there is lightning
 . <br><br>REFUNDS\, CREDITS\, and SUBSTITUTIONS:<br>Substitutions or credit
 s will be applied if we cancel a class due to weather conditions or instruc
 tor illness or if the 24-hr notice is met.<br>There are no refunds for paid
  classes missed during the summer\, except in the case of injury\, long-ter
 m illness\, unforeseen move out of the Austin area\, or being expelled for 
 a safety violation. <br><br>24-HR NOTICE: <br>If you let us know within 24 
 hours of the class that you will miss the class\, you can substitute anothe
 r class and use your fee as long as there are places left in that class dur
 ing the semester. If you notify us less than 24 hours in advance of the cla
 ss that you will need to cancel (except for sudden illness)\, or you do a "
 no-show"\, you'll forfeit your fee.<br><br>ILLNESS or INJURY: In the case o
 f physical injury or long-term illness\, we require a doctor's note saying 
 that you are unable to practice archery\, and then a doctor's note saying t
 hat you are again fit to return to archery\, before you will be allowed bac
 k in class or a refund/credit issued.<br><br>MEMBERSHIP IN USA ARCHERY:<br>
 Membership in USA Archery is now REQUIRED to participate in JOAD and Adult 
 Training.<br>You can attend 2 sessions before joining USAA\, but then we'll
  need to see your membership card BEFORE WE CAN HAND OUT ANY USA ARCHERY ST
 AR PINS to you during Master Challenge Weeks! <br>If you would like to see 
 the benefits of USAA membership: <a href="http://www.teamusa.org/USA-Archer
 y/Membership/Membership-Benefits">http://www.teamusa.org/USA-Archery/Member
 ship/Membership-Benefits</a><br>JOIN USA ARCHERY: <a href="https://www.usar
 chery.org/memberships/become-a-member">https://www.usarchery.org/membership
 s/become-a-member</a><br><br>SAFE SPORTS:<br>PARENTS PLEASE NOTE: We are pa
 rt of the US Olympic Committee's Safe Sport program\, so we minimally requi
 re one other adult besides the instructor to be present at all times. Pleas
 e plan to stay with your child or take turns with other parents staying whe
 never necessary to fulfill this requirement. THANKS!<br><br>SIGN AND RETURN
  THESE OUTDOOR WAIVERS:<br>The following documents and waivers will be part
  of your Registration and Waiver Packet. You will need to sign these  docum
 ents before we add your name to those shooting in the class:<br>o Membershi
 p Form<br>o Safety Rules <br>o Release of Liability Waiver<br>o Supervision
  Policy (Under 18)<br>o Medical Release  <br>o Photo/Video Release<br>o COV
 ID-19 Guidelines<br>o Outdoor Field Rules of Participation <br><br>VACCINAT
 IONS:<br>We do not at this time require archers to be vaccinated\, but we w
 ould like to know if you have been\, so we can take it into consideration w
 hen deciding on issues such as masks and social distancing and abiding by t
 he CDC Guidelines. All our instructors have been fully vaccinated of their 
 own accord.<br><br>QUESTIONS?<br>E-mail us at <a href="mailto:archerytraini
 ngcenteraustin@gmail.com">archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a> or<br>C
 all/Text us at 512 975 1850 <br><br>*NTS = National Training System (which 
 is used for training the USA Olympic team!)<br>*JDT = Junior Dream Team (to
 p 20 Junior archers in the USA!)<br>*JOAD = Junior Olympic Archery Developm
 ent
