DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><br><b>Tournaments are held at the end of eac
 h calendar month at 8:30 am - 12:00 pm on Saturdays and Sundays</b>\, weath
 er permitting.&nbsp\;<u></u>If you are new to our program\, come and try it
 \, so you will be more comfortable and better prepared next month!<br><br><
 u></u>The only differences between the regular training sessions and the to
 urnaments are that we are more closely reproducing tournament conditions\, 
 which include:<u></u><br><ul><li><u></u>No coaching while you are on the sh
 ooting line (but\, as in a real tournament\, y<u></u>ou can always ask the 
 coach for help in between the ends.) This is your chance to find out how we
 ll you can do the form on your own\, and learn how to go into ¨trusting¨ co
 mpared with ¨training¨ mode.</li><li><u></u>You will shoot more arrows :&nb
 sp\; 3 practice ends + two rounds -&nbsp\;<u></u>60 arrows at 9m and 13.5m 
 or 72 arrows at 20m-70m</li><li><u></u>You will score every arrow for two r
 ounds.&nbsp\;<u></u></li><li><u></u>The ends will be timed. You´ll have 4 m
 in to shoot 6 arrows.<u></u></li><li>Everyone will be shooting at close to 
 tournament spacing so there will be two archers on each target about 3 ft a
 part\, depending on the number of registrations</li><li>There will be a max
 imum of 20 archers on the shooting line at the same time. Awesome! (Lots of
  arrow flying towards the targets!)</li></ul>Your goal is always to replica
 te the NTS step(s) mindfully and consistently on every shot.<br><u></u><b>O
 utside of the tournament weeks</b>\, each week the focus of your lessons wi
 ll be on particular Steps of Shooting of the NTS (National Training System)
  shot cycle\, to help you focus and improve your form\, which\, as we all k
 now\, leads to greater precision (tighter groups of arrows) and ultimately 
 greater accuracy (tight groups of arrows dead center).<br><u></u><br><b>JUN
 E</b><br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>2-5</b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;Wel
 come Summer!&nbsp\; Understanding&nbsp\; NTS CONCEPTS<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\;
  &nbsp\;</b><b>6-12&nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b>NTS Steps 1+2: STANCE + NOCK&nbsp\;an
 d<b>&nbsp\;</b>NTS Step 3: HOOK &amp\; GRIP<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;<b>13
 -23&nbsp\;</b>NTS Step 4: SET&nbsp\;and&nbsp\;NTS Step 5: SET-UP<br><b>&nbs
 p\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;25/</b><b>26 MASTER CHALLENGE and STAR PIN SHOOT&nbsp\;<
 /b>(tournament)<br><b>JULY</b><br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;2-3</b>&nbsp\; 
 &nbsp\; &nbsp\; NTS Step 6 DRAW to LOAD&nbsp\;and&nbsp\;NTS Step 7 ANCHOR&n
 bsp\;<br><u></u>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;<b>4-10&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</b>&nbsp\; NTS
  Step 8 TRANSFER to HOLD<br><u></u><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;11-17</b>&nbsp
 \; NTS Step 9 EXPAND / AIM<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;<b>18-24&nbsp\;&nbsp\;
 </b>NTS Step 10 RELEASE and FOLLOW-THROUGH<br><u></u><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nb
 sp\;</b><b>30/31:&nbsp\;</b><b>MASTER CHALLENGE and STAR PIN SHOOT&nbsp\;</
 b>(tournament)<br><b>AUGUST</b><br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;1-7</b>&nbsp\;
  &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;NTS Step 11 FEEDBACK&nbsp\;<br><u></u><b>&nbsp\; &n
 bsp\; &nbsp\;8-14&nbsp\;</b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; PUTTING IT ALL TOGETHER !!<br>&
 nbsp\; &nbsp\;<i>&nbsp\;<b>&nbsp\;</b></i><b>20&nbsp\;</b>&nbsp\;&nbsp\; &n
 bsp\; &nbsp\;&nbsp\;<b><i>FALL SEMESTER BEGINS !!</i></b><br><b>&nbsp\; &nb
 sp\; &nbsp\;27/28:&nbsp\;</b><b>MASTER CHALLENGE and STAR PIN SHOOT&nbsp\;<
 /b>(tournament)<br><br>You do not need to score every class. In fact\, it w
 ould be more beneficial to you if you scored only during Master Challenge T
 ournament Weeks\, which happen the last week of each month. This is because
  working on the NTS Steps of Shooting (your form) is more easily done witho
 ut the distraction of the target face or scoring\, and you will improve fas
 ter.<br><br>As you reach higher levels\, you will learn the NTS Steps in pr
 ogressively greater detail.<br>The NTS Steps are cumulative with each step 
 most successfully completed if the previous steps have been completed mindf
 ully.&nbsp\;<br><br>Your ability to learn and understand the NTS Steps\, an
 d use deep focus on these Steps while shooting outdoors and while using you
 r stretchband/string loop at home will propel you to higher levels fast!<br
 ><br><b>Goals by the end of the semester:&nbsp\;</b><br>See Coach Racae´s e
 mail ¨2022 New Year´s Goals¨<u></u></html-blob>
