 blank"><u><u><u><u><u><u><u>2024 OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m</u></u></u></u></
 u></u></u></a><br><br><i>See target notes below assignments.</i><br><br><b>
 Target Assignments:</b><br><br><br>1. (70m)<br>3. (70m)  reversed direction
 <br><br>2. (60m)  <br><br>4A. (40m) <b>Joseph F</b>.\, 13\, USAA\, OB\, pd<
 br>4B.             <b>Nick E.\, </b>adult\, USAA\, OB\, pd<br><b><br></b>5A
 . (30m) <br>5B<br><br>6A. (30m)  <br>6B<br><br>7A. (18m) <b>Abby Y.\, </b>U
 SAA\, OB\, pd<br>7B.             <b>Joel Y.\, </b>USAA\, OB\, pd<br><br>8A.
  (18m) <b>Christine S.</b>\, USAA\, OB\, pd<br>8B.            <br><br>9A. (
 18m) <b>Finn E.\, </b>12\, USAA\, OB\, pd<br>9B.             <b>Rhys E.\, <
 /b>10\, USAA&lt\; OB\, pd<br><br>10A. (18m)<br>10B.<br><br><i>Targets 1 and
  2 should always stay at 70m or reversed so Jake can shoot.</i><br><i>Targe
 t 3 at 60m</i><br><i>Target 4 at 40m</i><br><i>Targets 5+6 at 30m</i><br><i
 >Targets 7-10 will move to18m starting 8/17. </i><i>Archers at 20m will now
  shoot at 18m.</i><i><br></i><br><i>If necessary\, Target #6 can move to 18
 m when Targets #7-10 are full with two archers/target at 18m.</i><br><i>Whe
 n you shoot at 18m to practice for the Aggie Invitational in Nov\, you'll b
 e on a 60-cm or 40-cm target face. 60-cm target faces should be centered si
 de-by-side\, and 40-cm target faces should be set up 4 to a target (even if
  only one or two archers are on that target). </i><br><i>You should practic
 e one round of 30 arrows at each target face high/low/left/right so you are
  prepared for your target assignment at the indoor competitions</i><i><br><
 /i><i>Ideally\, we want to practice with at least two archers/target to rep
 licate competition conditions as much as possible.</i><br><i><br>You can de
 cide each week if you want to shoot at your long distance or at 18m and add
  or move your name on the calendar accordingly. You should alternate distan
 ce each day\, so you practice both. </i><br><i><br></i><br><i>S</i><i>tarti
 ng Oct 1 to the Nov Aggie Invitational and Jan 1 for the Feb Indoor Nationa
 ls\, everyone should be shooting at 18m and scoring to determine their aver
 age and their personal bests\, understand the spread between the two\, and 
 work on closing it.</i>
