DESCRIPTION:Registration form: 2024 OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m\n\nSat.\, 11/3
 0\, you'll have the option of going outdoors and shooting at 18m with Coach
  Joel (9:00-12:00) or coming indoors and working hard on form (10:00-12:00)
  with me - or you could even do a bit of both. \n\nThought we'd give you th
 e option since the weather has turned a bit chillier. (We usually don't hol
 d classes outdoors if the temperature or windchill is less than 55F\, but C
 oach Joel said he'd try it with the sun and hand warmers.)  Coach Racae\nTh
 ose who have already qualified for Indoor Nationals at TAMU in February:\nC
 oach Joel\, Coach Nick\, Instructor Lily\, Ted\, Christine\, Javier\, Erika
 \n\nAll archers going to the Indoor Nationals wll be shooting at 18m unless
  you need to build up your strength and tighten your form to group out that
  far. In that case\, you will be shooting at 13.5m on 60-cm target face if 
 JOAD until your form and groups tighten up\, and you shoot  an arrow averag
 e of 6.0 pts.\nU15 and U13 JOAD archers shoot on 60-cm target face to get r
 eady for JOAD Indoor Nationals\; use 40-cm target face if you are going to 
 Indoor Nationals (any age)\n\nField work this weekend: Finish cleaning up a
 nd painting fenced enclosure.\n \nCoach Joel Yu\, Coach Nick Erickson\n\nTa
 rget Assignments:\n\nTargets 1 should always stay at 70m so Jake can shoot.
 \nTarget 2 at 60m\nTarget 3 at 40m\nTargets 4-9 at 18m \nTargets 10 at 13.5
 m\nSee notes below list.\n\n----------------------------------\n1A. (70m)\n
 1B\n\n2A. (60m)  \n2B\n\n3A. (40m)  Nick E\, AD\, USAA\, OB\n--------------
 --------------------\n3B\n\n18m 40-cm:\n\n4A. (30m)  Joel Y\, adult\, USAA\
 , OB\, pd\n4B  (30m) Finn E\, 12\, usaa\, OB\n-----------------------------
 -----\n5A. Abby Y\, 12\, USAA\, OB\, pd\n5B  Joseph F.\, 14\, USAA\, OB\, p
 d\n\n6A. Sophia D\, adult \, USAA\, f\n----------------------------------\n
 6B. Riley M. 13\, USAA\, OB\, pd\n\n7A.  Jacqui C\, USAA\, OB\, pd\n7B. Mil
 es G.\, 12\, USAA\, OB\, pd\n---------------------------------- \n8A. \n8B.
  \n\n9A. \n----------------------------------\n9B\n\n13.5m 40-cm:\n10A. \n1
 0B\n\nIdeally\, we want to practice with at least two archers/target to rep
 licate competition conditions as much as possible.\nYou can decide each wee
 k if you want to shoot at your long distance or at 18m and add or move your
  name on the calendar accordingly. You should alternate distance each day\,
  so you practice both. Everyone should be shooting at 18m and scoring to de
 termine their average and their personal bests\, understand the spread betw
 een the two\, and work on closing it.
