DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><br><b>Tournaments are held at the end of eac
 h calendar month at 9:00 am - 11:30 pm on Saturdays and Sundays</b>\, weath
 er permitting.&nbsp\;<u></u>If you are new to our program\, come and try it
 \, so you will be more comfortable and better prepared next month!<br><br><
 u></u>The only differences between the regular training sessions and the to
 urnaments are that we are more closely reproducing tournament conditions\, 
 which include:<u></u><br><ul><li><u></u>No coaching while you are on the sh
 ooting line (but\, as in a real tournament\, y<u></u>ou can always ask the 
 coach for help in between the ends.) This is your chance to find out how we
 ll you can do the form on your own\, and learn how to go into ¨trusting¨ co
 mpared with ¨training¨ mode.</li><li><u></u>You will shoot more arrows :&nb
 sp\; 2 practice ends + Two rounds -&nbsp\;<u></u>60 arrows at 9m and 13.5m 
 or 72 arrows at 20m-70m</li><li><u></u>You will score every arrow for two r
 ounds.&nbsp\;<u></u></li><li><u></u>The ends will be timed. You´ll have 4 m
 in to shoot 6 arrows.<u></u></li><li>Everyone will be shooting at close-to-
 regular tournament spacing so there will be two archers on each target abou
 t 3 ft apart\, depending on the number of registrations</li><li>There will 
 be a maximum of 20 archers on the shooting line at the same time. Awesome! 
 (Lots of arrow flying towards the targets!)</li></ul><br>Your goal is alway
 s to replicate the NTS step(s) mindfully and consistently on every shot.<br
 ><u></u><b>Outside of the tournament weeks</b>\, each week the focus of you
 r lessons will be on particular Steps of Shooting of the NTS (National Trai
 ning System) shot cycle\, to help you focus and improve your form\, which\,
  as we all know\, leads to greater precision (tighter groups of arrows) and
  ultimately greater accuracy (tight groups of arrows dead center).<br><u></
 u><br><b>JUNE</b><br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>2-5</b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\
 ; &nbsp\;Welcome Summer!&nbsp\; Understanding&nbsp\; NTS CONCEPTS<br><b>&nb
 sp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>6-12&nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b>NTS Steps 1+2: STANCE + N
 OCK&nbsp\;and<b>&nbsp\;</b>NTS Step 3: HOOK &amp\; GRIP<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; 
 &nbsp\;<b>13-23&nbsp\;</b>NTS Step 4: SET&nbsp\;and&nbsp\;NTS Step 5: SET-U
 P<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;25/</b><b>26 MASTER CHALLENGE and STAR PIN S
 HOOT&nbsp\;</b>(tournament)<br><b>JULY</b><br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;2-3
 </b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; NTS Step 6 DRAW to LOAD&nbsp\;and&nbsp\;NTS Ste
 p 7 ANCHOR&nbsp\;<br><u></u>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;<b>4-10&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</b
 >&nbsp\; NTS Step 8 TRANSFER to HOLD<br><u></u><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;11
 -17</b>&nbsp\; NTS Step 9 EXPAND / AIM<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;<b>18-24&n
 bsp\;&nbsp\;</b>NTS Step 10 RELEASE and FOLLOW-THROUGH<br><u></u><b>&nbsp\;
  &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>30/31:&nbsp\;</b><b>MASTER CHALLENGE and STAR PIN SH
 OOT&nbsp\;</b>(tournament)<br><b>AUGUST</b><br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;1-
 7</b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;NTS Step 11 FEEDBACK&nbsp\;<br><u></u><
 b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;8-14&nbsp\;</b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; PUTTING IT ALL TOGE
 THER !!<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\;<i>&nbsp\;<b>&nbsp\;</b></i><b>20&nbsp\;</b>&nbsp
 \;&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;&nbsp\;<b><i>FALL SEMESTER BEGINS !!</i></b><br><b
 >&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;27/28:&nbsp\;</b><b>MASTER CHALLENGE and STAR PIN S
 HOOT&nbsp\;</b>(tournament)<br><br>You do not need to score every class. In
  fact\, it would be more beneficial to you if you scored only during Master
  Challenge Tournament Weeks\, which happen the last week of each month. Thi
 s is because working on the NTS Steps of Shooting (your form) is more easil
 y done without the distraction of the target face or scoring\, and you will
  improve faster.<br><br>As you reach higher levels\, you will learn the NTS
  Steps in progressively greater detail.<br>The NTS Steps are cumulative wit
 h each step most successfully completed if the previous steps have been com
 pleted mindfully.&nbsp\;<br><br>Your ability to learn and understand the NT
 S Steps\, and use deep focus on these Steps while shooting outdoors and whi
 le using your stretchband/string loop at home will propel you to higher lev
 els fast!<br><br><b>Goals by the end of the semester:&nbsp\;</b><br>See Coa
 ch Racae´s email ¨2022 New Year´s Goals¨<u></u></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260517T074246Z
