 n a 60-cm or 40-cm target face. 60-cm target faces should be centered side-
 by-side\, and 40-cm target faces should be set up 4 to a target (even if on
 ly one or two archers are on that target). </i><br><i>You should practice o
 ne round of 30 arrows at each target face high/low/left/right so you are pr
 epared for your target assignment at the indoor competitions</i><i><br></i>
 <br><i>Ideally\, we want to practice with at least two archers/target to re
 plicate competition conditions as much as possible.</i><br><i>You can decid
 e each week if you want to shoot at your long distance or at 18m and add or
  move your name on the calendar accordingly. You should alternate distance 
 each day\, so you practice both. S</i><br><i>tarting Oct 1 to the Nov Aggie
  Invitational and Jan 1 for the Feb Indoor Nationals\, everyone should be s
 hooting at 18m and scoring to determine their average and their personal be
 sts\, understand the spread between the two\, and work on closing it.</i><b
