  targets\, etc.\, below<br><br><b>Target Assignments:</b><br><br>1. (70m)<b
 r>2. (70m)  reversed direction<br><br>3. (60m)  <br><br>4A. (40m)  <b>Josep
 h F</b>.\,13\,  <b>USAA\, OB\,</b> pd  266 + 278 = <b>544 pts</b><br>4B<br>
 <b><br></b>5A. (30m) <b>Gianna L.</b>\, 11\, <b>USAA\, OB\,</b> pd  239 + 2
 44 = <b>483 pts</b><br>5B<br><br>6A. (30m)  <b>Nick E.\, </b>adult\, <b>USA
 A\, OB\, </b>pd 313 + 325 = <b>638 pts  - CONGRATULATIONS -&gt\; 40m (Outdo
 or 6)</b><br>6B<br><br>7A. (18m)  <b>Kishore P.\, </b>16\, <b>USAA\, OB\, p
 d </b>148 + 174 =<b> 322 pts</b><br>7B               <br><br>8A. (18m) <b>D
 aisy D.\, </b>9\,  <b>USAA\, OB\, pd </b>162 +209 = <b>371 pts</b><br>8B <b
 r>             <br>9A. (18m) <br>9B<br><br>10A. (18m)<br>10B<br><br><i>Targ
 ets 1 and 2 should always stay at 70m or reversed so Jake can shoot.</i><br
 ><i>Target 3 at 60m</i><br><i>Target 4 at 40m</i><br><i>Targets 5+6 at 30m<
 /i><br><i>Targets 7-10 will move to18m starting 8/17. </i><i>Archers at 20m
  will now shoot at 18m.</i><i><br></i><br><i>If necessary\, Target #6 can m
 ove to 18m when Targets #7-10 are full with two archers/target at 18m.</i><
 br><i>When you shoot at 18m to practice for the Aggie Invitational in Nov\,
  you'll be on a 60-cm or 40-cm target face. 60-cm target faces should be ce
 ntered side-by-side\, and 40-cm target faces should be set up 4 to a target
  (even if only one or two archers are on that target). </i><br><i>You shoul
 d practice one round of 30 arrows at each target face high/low/left/right s
 o you are prepared for your target assignment at the indoor competitions</i
 ><i><br></i><br><i>Ideally\, we want to practice with at least <b>two arche
 rs/target</b> to replicate competition conditions as much as possible.</i><
 br><i>You can decide each week if you want to shoot at your long distance o
 r at 18m and add or move your name on the calendar accordingly. You should 
 alternate distance each day\, so you practice both. </i><br><i><br></i><br>
 <i>S</i><i>tarting Oct 1 to the Nov Aggie Invitational and Jan 1 for the Fe
 b Indoor Nationals\, everyone should be shooting at 18m and scoring to dete
 rmine their average and their personal bests\, understand the spread betwee
 n the two\, and work on closing it.</i>
