DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u>REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to a
 dult\, juniors 8+\, and parents! Please read all the info below and in the 
 registration and waivers.<br><br>More information\, registration forms and 
 waivers are available at&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.co
 m"><u>www.archerytrainingcenter.com</u></a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE
  of these forms:<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfcwG
 419ZK9XmA4-JlXM-zhjhvSPCF8NCwWJlzFP2w-gRliUw/viewform"><u>2022 Outdoor 1: F
 irst-time Class for Juniors + Parents</u></a>&nbsp\; OR<br><a href="https:/
 /docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSe-YxPKAMTxiC7kVt6fZuQJeidXENYq_iV4rWj1Ra
 XdLhPoew/viewform"><u>2022 Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Adults</u></a><b
 r><br>Sign up for just ONE Outdoor 1 class\, because most people graduate o
 ut of this class into Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br><br>Your name wi
 ll be added below and your place reserved on a&nbsp\;first registered and p
 aid basis and after we receive 3 things:&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br><b>2022 OUTDOOR 1
  REGISTRATION FORM&nbsp\; &nbsp\;+&nbsp\; MEMBERSHIP AND WAIVERS PACKET +&n
 bsp\; &nbsp\;FEE</b><br><br><b>Registered archers&nbsp\;</b>at 9m on 40-cm 
 target face:<br><b>Target Assignments:</b><br>1.&nbsp\;<br>2.<br>3.&nbsp\;<
 br>4.&nbsp\;<b>Kartik P.\,&nbsp\;</b>adult - pd - substituted for 6/4&nbsp\
 ; - <b>105 pts</b><br>5.&nbsp\;<b>Karen S</b>.\, adult - pd - substituted f
 or 6/4&nbsp\;<u></u>-&nbsp\;<b>31 pts</b><br><u></u>6.&nbsp\;<b>Neiladri R-
 S.\,&nbsp\;</b>10\, on 60-cm target face - pd - substituted for 6/4 <b>54 p
 ts -&gt\; Outdoor 2 !</b><br>7.<br>8.&nbsp\;<br>9.<br>10.<br><br>Space will
  be limited to 10-15 archers per session depending on the number of family 
 groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC Guidelines.&nbsp\;<br>Each p
 erson will have a target stand\, except after 10 people have registered\, t
 wo members from the same family will share one target stand.<br>The archer 
 and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field until further n
 otice or approved by Coach Racae.&nbsp\;<br>Parents of juniors 10+ can sign
  up as an archer or watch as a spectator. Parents of juniors 8-9 years old 
 need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their child for greater safety.<br>
 <br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into each Outdoor 1:
  First-time Class.&nbsp\;<br><br>We will accept a limited&nbsp\;number of k
 ids under 12 into the program each semester\, depending on the total&nbsp\;
  number of archers in all the classes. If you join before the limit is reac
 hed\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take other O
 utdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;If you are under
  12\, registered and paid after the cut off\, your fee will be returned to 
 you.&nbsp\;<br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times be
 fore qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as 
 soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults 
 don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessor
 ies packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for 
 Outdoor 2. ($18)<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, optional
  but really needed to practice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At
  the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we did no
 t finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final sc
 ore\, because it will have been averaged by taking your recorded score from
  your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot to get an arrow
  average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round score. After
  the last class on the weekend\, final scores will also be sent to all Outd
 oor 1 participants in an email with more information before your next class
 .<u></u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
