DESCRIPTION:Registration form: OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m<br><br>Add your nam
 e to Target Assignment List below or send in the above completed form.<br><
 br>Focus primarily on: <br>perfecting your form\, <br>slowly increasing you
 r physical strength and draw weight\, <br>strengthening your mental program
 \, <br>determining your average and personal best\, <br>understanding the s
 pread between the two\, and working on closing it.<br><br>You need your own
  equipment <br>Competition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, res
 t\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\
 , armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\
 , etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added until you reach a higher lev
 el\, but you should order them in advance.) <br><br>Wear your ATCI shirt to
  training.<br><br>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm 
 target face you'll move back to the next distance until you reach your comp
 etition distance<br>If you trained outdoors in the 2024 season\, you'll ret
 urn to the farthest distance you shot.<br>Target arrangements may vary each
  session\, depending on who attends and distances needed.<br>Target 1 at 70
 m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake ca
 n use it for independent practice in between classes.<br>Target 2 at 60m (U
 18 + Masters competition distance) <br>Target 3 at 50m<br>Targets 4+5 at 40
 m (U15 competition distance) <br>Targets 6\, 7\, 8 at 30m (U13 competition 
 distance) <br>Target 9 at 20m (for those who have shot at 18m indoors or wi
 th Coach Racae's approval)<br>Targets 10 at 13.5m (for those who have just 
 graduated from indoors at 9m)<br><br>Ideally\, we want to practice with two
  archers/target to replicate competition conditions as much as possible.<br
 ><br>Target Assignments:<br>Targets are assigned outdoors in advance to red
 uce confusion and delay on the day\,<br>so add your name next to your dista
 nce below. <br>If you need help or have questions\, email/text Coach Racae<
 br>(Dotted lines represent tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)<br>-
 ---------------------------------<br>1A. (70m) <b>Jake L.\, </b>adult\, 2 h
 rs<br>1B<br><br>2A. (60m)  <br>2B<br><br>3A. (50m)  <br>-------------------
 ---------------<br>3B<br><br>4A. (40m) <br>4B<br>--------------------------
