DESCRIPTION:<u></u><u></u>REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to adult\, juniors 8+\
 , and parents! Please read all the info below and in the registration and w
 aivers.<br><br>More information\, registration forms and waivers are availa
 ble at <a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com"><u>www.archerytrainin
 gcenter.com</u></a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE of these forms:<br><a h
 ref="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfcwG419ZK9XmA4-JlXM-zhjhvSPC
 F8NCwWJlzFP2w-gRliUw/viewform"><u>2022 Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Juni
 ors + Parents</u></a>  OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FA
 IpQLSe-YxPKAMTxiC7kVt6fZuQJeidXENYq_iV4rWj1RaXdLhPoew/viewform"><u>2022 Out
 door 1: First-time Class for Adults</u></a><br><br>Sign up for just ONE Out
 door 1 class\, because most people graduate out of this class into Outdoor 
 2 after the first lesson.<br><br>Your name will be added below and your pla
 ce reserved on a first registered and paid basis and after we receive 3 thi
 ngs:  <br><b>2022 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM   +  MEMBERSHIP AND WAIVERS P
 ACKET +   FEE</b><br><br><b>Registered archers </b>at 9m on 40-cm target fa
 ce:<br><b>Target Assignments:</b><br>1. <br>2. <b>Chris W.</b>\, adult - pd
  - substituted 4/15/23<br>3. <b>Andrew W.</b>\, adult - pd - substituted 4/
 15/23<br>4. <b>Dean W.</b>\, adult - pd - substituted 4/15/23<br>5.<br>6.<b
 r>7.<br>8.<br>9.<br>10.<br><br>Space will be limited to 10-15 archers per s
 ession depending on the number of family groups in attendance or in accorda
 nce with CDC Guidelines. <br>Each person will have a target stand\, except 
 after 10 people have registered\, two members from the same family will sha
 re one target stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be a
 llowed on the field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae. <br>Pa
 rents of juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator. Pare
 nts of juniors 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their 
 child for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is 
 accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-time Class. <br><br>We will accept a li
 mited number of kids under 12 into the program each semester\, depending on
  the total  number of archers in all the classes. If you join before the li
 mit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and t
 ake other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2. If you are 
 under 12\, registered and paid after the cut off\, your fee will be returne
 d to you. <br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times bef
 ore qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as s
 oon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows. <br>Adults don´t n
 eed a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories pac
 ket (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor
  2. ($18)<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but re
 ally needed to practice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the en
 d of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we did not finis
 h a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, b
 ecause it will have been averaged by taking your recorded score from your s
 corecard\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot to get an arrow averag
 e\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round score. After the la
 st class on the weekend\, final scores will also be sent to all Outdoor 1 p
 articipants in an email with more information before your next class.<u></u
 ><u></u>
