 s/d/e/1FAIpQLSfx1RyOwd314Q4zXYiQ9rb_a3oe84E9dIYs8CN35Ginmevfpg/viewform?usp
 =preview" target="_blank">OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m</a><br><br><b>Add your n
 ame to Target Assignment List below or send in the above completed form.</b
 ><br><br><i>Focus primarily on <br></i><ul><li><i>perfecting your form\, </
 i></li><li><i>slowly increasing your physical strength and draw weight\, </
 i></li><li><i>strengthening your mental program\, </i></li><li><i>determini
 ng your average and personal best\, </i></li><li><i>understanding the sprea
 d between the two\, and working on closing it.</i></li></ul><b>You need you
 r own equipment </b><br>Competition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plun
 ger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest p
 rotector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arro
 w puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added until you reach a h
 igher level\, but you should order them in advance.) <br><br>Wear your ATCI
  shirt to training.<br><br><i>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on
  the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the next distance until you rea
 ch your competition distance</i><br><i>If you trained outdoors in the 2024 
 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.</i><br><i>Target 
 arrangements may vary each session\, depending on who attends and distances
  needed.</i><br><b>Target 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors</b> competition distance)
  should always stay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent practice in b
 etween classes.<br><b>Target 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters</b> competition distan
 ce) <br><b>Target 3 at 50m</b><br><b>Target 4 at 40m</b> (U15 competition d
 istance) <br><b>Target 5 at 30m</b> (U13 competition distance) <br><b>Targe
 ts 6+7+8 at 20m</b> (for those who have shot at 18m indoors or with Coach R
 acae's approval)<br><b>Targets 9 + 10 at 13.5m</b> (for those who have just
  graduated from indoors at 9m)<br><br>Ideally\, we want to practice with tw
 o archers/target to replicate competition conditions as much as possible.<b
 r><br><b>Target Assignments:</b><br>Targets are assigned outdoors in advanc
 e to reduce confusion and delay on the day\,<br>so a<span>dd your name next
  to your distance below. </span><br><span>If you need help or have question
