DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u>REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to a
 dult\, juniors 8+\, and parents! Please read all the info below and in the 
 registration and waivers.<br><br>More information\, registration forms and 
 waivers are available at&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.co
 m"><u>www.archerytrainingcenter.com</u></a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE
  of these forms:<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfcwG
 419ZK9XmA4-JlXM-zhjhvSPCF8NCwWJlzFP2w-gRliUw/viewform"><u>2022 Outdoor 1: F
 irst-time Class for Juniors + Parents</u></a>&nbsp\; OR<br><a href="https:/
 /docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSe-YxPKAMTxiC7kVt6fZuQJeidXENYq_iV4rWj1Ra
 XdLhPoew/viewform"><u>2022 Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Adults</u></a><b
 r><br>Sign up for just ONE Outdoor 1 class\, because most people graduate o
 ut of this class into Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br><br>Your name wi
 ll be added below and your place reserved on a&nbsp\;first registered and p
 aid basis and after we receive 3 things:&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br><b>2022 OUTDOOR 1
  REGISTRATION FORM&nbsp\; &nbsp\;+&nbsp\; MEMBERSHIP AND WAIVERS PACKET +&n
 bsp\; &nbsp\;FEE</b><br><br><b>Registered archers&nbsp\;</b>at 9m on 40-cm 
 target face:<br><b>Target Assignments:</b><br>1.&nbsp\;<br>2. <b>Melek S.\,
  </b>adult - pd - substituted 9/3<br>3. <b>Nancy Y</b>.\, adult - pd<br>4.&
 nbsp\;<br>5.<br>6.<br>7.<br>8. <b>Steve K.\, </b>dad\, - pd<br>9. <b>Fox K.
 </b>\, 9\, on 60-cm target face - pf<br>10.<br><br>Space will be limited to
  10-15 archers per session depending on the number of family groups in atte
 ndance or in accordance with CDC Guidelines.&nbsp\;<br>Each person will hav
 e a target stand\, except after 10 people have registered\, two members fro
 m the same family will share one target stand.<br>The archer and a maximum 
 of one spectator will be allowed on the field until further notice or appro
 ved by Coach Racae.&nbsp\;<br>Parents of juniors 10+ can sign up as an arch
 er or watch as a spectator. Parents of juniors 8-9 years old need to regist
 er\, pay\, and shoot with their child for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum 
 of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-time Cl
 ass.&nbsp\;<br><br>We will accept a limited&nbsp\;number of kids under 12 i
 nto the program each semester\, depending on the total&nbsp\; number of arc
 hers in all the classes. If you join before the limit is reached\, and are 
 younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take other Outdoor 1 class
 es as needed and later join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;If you are under 12\, register
 ed and paid after the cut off\, your fee will be returned to you.&nbsp\;<br
 ><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifyin
 g to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you sc
 ore on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need a m
 inimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (ar
 mguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($1
 8)<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but really ne
 eded to practice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of ea
 ch Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a com
 plete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, because 
 it will have been averaged by taking your recorded score from your scorecar
 d\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and
  then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round score. After the last clas
 s on the weekend\, final scores will also be sent to all Outdoor 1 particip
 ants in an email with more information before your next class.<u></u><u></u
 ><u></u></html-blob>
