 r 2 at 9m and Outdoor 3 at 13.5m</a><br><br>Your total score for all arrows
  shot was divided by the number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\
 , noted in parentheses. The arrow average was multiplied by 30 arrows to ge
 t an average round score. If your actual first round score was higher than 
 your averaged round score\, that is used instead for both your round total 
 and your arrow average.<br><br>To progress to Outdoor 3 at 13.5m\, you´ll n
 eed to shoot <b>230 pts</b> on the 40-cm target face (14+ y.o.)\, or <b>240
  pts\,</b> on the 60-cm target face (&lt\;14 y.o.).in a 30-arrow round. You
  need to do the same again to progress to Outdoor 4 at 20m. These scores ar
 e about 24 pts each end of 3 arrows or an <b>8 arrow average</b>.&nbsp\;<br
 ><b>Please note: Scoring is optonal except on Tournament Saturdays and Sund
 ays once a month\, when it is required. If you´re scoring\, every arrow sho
 t must be scored\, including M´s!</b><br><br><b>Registered archers:</b><br>
