DESCRIPTION:<u></u><br><b>ATCI monthly competitions are held at the end of 
 each calendar month on Saturdays and Sundays</b>\, weather permitting. <u><
 /u>If you are new to our program\, come and try it\, so you will be more co
 mfortable and better prepared next month!<br><br><u></u>The only difference
 s between the regular training sessions and the tournaments are that we are
  more closely reproducing official competition conditions\, which include:<
 u></u><br><ul><li><u></u>No coaching while you are on the shooting line (bu
 t\, as in a real tournament\, y<u></u>ou can always ask the coach for help 
 in between the ends.) </li><li>This is your chance to find out how well you
  can do the form on your own\, and learn how to go into ¨trusting¨ compared
  with ¨training¨ mode.</li><li><u></u>You will shoot more arrows :  2 pract
 ice ends + two rounds (<u></u>60 arrows at 9m and 13.5m or 72 arrows at 20m
 -70m)</li><li><u></u>You will score every arrow for two rounds. <u></u></li
 ><li><u></u>The ends will be timed. You´ll have 4 min to shoot 6 arrows.<u>
 </u></li><li>Everyone will be shooting at close-to-official competition spa
 cing\, so there will be two archers on each target about 3 ft apart\, depen
 ding on the number of registrations</li><li>There will be a maximum of 20 a
 rchers on the shooting line at the same time. Awesome! (Lots of arrow flyin
 g towards the targets!)</li></ul>Your goal is always to replicate the NTS s
 tep(s) mindfully and consistently on every shot.<br><u></u><b>Outside of th
 e competition weekends</b>\, the focus of your regular lessons will be on o
 ne or two of the Steps of Shooting of the NTS (National Training System) sh
 ot cycle\, to help you focus and improve your form\, which\, as we all know
 \, leads to greater precision (tighter groups of arrows) and ultimately gre
 ater accuracy (tight groups of arrows dead center).<br><b><br></b>You do no
 t need to score every class. In fact\, it would be more beneficial to you i
 f you scored only during the ATCI Monthly Competition and Star Pin Shoot\, 
 which happen the last week of each month. This is because working on the NT
 S Steps of Shooting (your form) is more easily done without the distraction
  of the target face or scoring\, and you will improve faster.<br><br>As you
  reach higher levels\, you will learn the NTS Steps in progressively greate
 r detail.<br>The NTS Steps are cumulative with each step most successfully 
 completed if the previous steps have been completed mindfully. <br><br>Your
  ability to learn and understand the NTS Steps\, and use deep focus on thes
 e Steps while shooting outdoors and while using your stretchband/string loo
 p at home will propel you to higher levels fast!<br><br><b>Goals by the end
  of the semester: </b><br>See Coach Racae´s email ¨2023 New Year´s Goals¨<u
 ></u>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260517T074246Z
