DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u>
 </u>REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to adult\, juniors 8+\, and parents! Please 
 read all the info below and in the registration and waivers.<br><br>More in
 formation\, registration forms and waivers are available at&nbsp\;<a href="
 http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com"><u>www.archerytrainingcenter.com</u><
 /a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE of these forms:<br><a href="https://doc
 s.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfcwG419ZK9XmA4-JlXM-zhjhvSPCF8NCwWJlzFP2w-gR
 liUw/viewform"><u>2022 Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Juniors + Parents</u
 ></a>&nbsp\; OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSe-YxP
 KAMTxiC7kVt6fZuQJeidXENYq_iV4rWj1RaXdLhPoew/viewform"><u>2022 Outdoor 1: Fi
 rst-time Class for Adults</u></a><br><br>Sign up for just ONE Outdoor 1 cla
 ss\, because most people graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after th
 e first lesson.<br><br>Your name will be added below and your place reserve
 d on a&nbsp\;first registered and paid basis and after we receive 3 things:
 &nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br><b>2022 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM&nbsp\; &nbsp\;+&nbsp\
 ; MEMBERSHIP AND WAIVERS PACKET +&nbsp\; &nbsp\;FEE</b><br><br><b>Registere
 d archers&nbsp\;</b>at 9m on 40-cm target face unless otherwise noted:<br><
 b>Target Assignments:</b><br>1.&nbsp\;<b>Stephen B</b>.\, adult - pd - subs
 tituted for 5/22 - <b>153 pts</b><br>2.&nbsp\;<b>Rachel D</b>.\, adult - pd
  - substituted for 5/22 - <b>77 pts</b><br>3. <b>Karen S.</b>\, adult - pd 
 - <b>?</b><br>4. <b>Gracie E.\, </b>adult - pd - <b>157 pts</b><br>5. <b>Ga
 ry H.\, </b>adult - pd - <b>140 pts</b><br>6. <b>Michael D.\, </b>15 - pd -
  <b>39 pts -&gt\; Outdoor 2 (with wind handicap)</b><br>7.&nbsp\;<b>Valerie
  W.\,&nbsp\;</b>11\, on 60-cm target face - pd - <b>138 pts -&gt\; Outdoor 
 2</b><br>8.<br>9.<br>10.<br><br>Space will be limited to 10-15 archers per 
 session depending on the number of family groups in attendance or in accord
 ance with CDC Guidelines.&nbsp\;<br>Each person will have a target stand\, 
 except after 10 people have registered\, two members from the same family w
 ill share one target stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator wi
 ll be allowed on the field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae.
 &nbsp\;<br>Parents of juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a sp
 ectator. Parents of juniors 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoo
 t with their child for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (
 + parent) is accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-time Class.&nbsp\;<br><br>
 We will accept a limited&nbsp\;number of kids under 12 into the program eac
 h semester\, depending on the total&nbsp\; number of archers in all the cla
 sses. If you join before the limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, y
 ou´ll stay in the program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and la
 ter join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;If you are under 12\, registered and paid after t
 he cut off\, your fee will be returned to you.&nbsp\;<br><br>Juniors may ne
 ed to take Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying to get into Outdo
 or 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on average abou
 t 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to gra
 duate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\
 , fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($18)<br>fp = form pac
 k (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but really needed to practice fo
 rm\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\
 , your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arr
 ows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, because it will have been a
 veraged by taking your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the
  number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying t
 hat by 30 to get a full round score. After the last class on the weekend\, 
 final scores will also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email wi
 th more information before your next class.<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u><
 /u><u></u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
