 e will accept a limited&nbsp\;number of kids under 12 into the program each
  semester\, depending on the total&nbsp\; number of archers in all the clas
 ses. If you join before the limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, yo
 u´ll stay in the program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and lat
 er join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;If you are under 12\, registered and paid after th
 e cut off\, your fee will be returned to you.&nbsp\;<br><br>Juniors may nee
 d to take Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying to get into Outdoo
 r 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on average about
  5 pts/end of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to grad
 uate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\,
  fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($18)<br>fp = form pack
  (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but really needed to practice for
 m\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\,
  your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arro
 ws)\, you may not recognize your final score\, because it will have been av
 eraged by taking your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the 
 number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying th
 at by 30 to get a full round score. After the last class on the weekend\, f
 inal scores will also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email wit
 h more information before your next class.<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></
 u><u></u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260517T074326Z
SEQUENCE:4
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:OUTDOOR 1: First-time Class
TRANSP:OPAQUE
