UID:j9214jkr0c2cnjrf7u1g10u0d9@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;VALUE=DATE:20221029
CREATED:20220524T151816Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><br><b>Tournaments are held at the end of each calen
 dar month at 9:00 am - 11:30 pm on Saturdays and Sundays</b>\, weather perm
 itting.&nbsp\;<u></u>If you are new to our program\, come and try it\, so y
 ou will be more comfortable and better prepared next month!<br><br><u></u>T
 he only differences between the regular training sessions and the tournamen
 ts are that we are more closely reproducing tournament conditions\, which i
 nclude:<u></u><br><ul><li><u></u>No coaching while you are on the shooting 
 line (but\, as in a real tournament\, y<u></u>ou can always ask the coach f
 or help in between the ends.) This is your chance to find out how well you 
 can do the form on your own\, and learn how to go into ¨trusting¨ compared 
 with ¨training¨ mode.</li><li><u></u>You will shoot more arrows :&nbsp\; 2 
 practice ends + Two rounds -&nbsp\;<u></u>60 arrows at 9m and 13.5m or 72 a
 rrows at 20m-70m</li><li><u></u>You will score every arrow for two rounds.&
 nbsp\;<u></u></li><li><u></u>The ends will be timed. You´ll have 4 min to s
 hoot 6 arrows.<u></u></li><li>Everyone will be shooting at close-to-regular
  tournament spacing so there will be two archers on each target about 3 ft 
 apart\, depending on the number of registrations</li><li>There will be a ma
 ximum of 20 archers on the shooting line at the same time. Awesome! (Lots o
 f arrow flying towards the targets!)</li></ul><br>Your goal is always to re
 plicate the NTS step(s) mindfully and consistently on every shot.<br><u></u
 ><b>Outside of the tournament weeks</b>\, each week the focus of your lesso
 ns will be on particular Steps of Shooting of the NTS (National Training Sy
 stem) shot cycle\, to help you focus and improve your form\, which\, as we 
 all know\, leads to greater precision (tighter groups of arrows) and ultima
 tely greater accuracy (tight groups of arrows dead center).<br><u></u><br><
 b>JUNE</b><br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>2-5</b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp
 \;Welcome Summer!&nbsp\; Understanding&nbsp\; NTS CONCEPTS<br><b>&nbsp\; &n
 bsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>6-12&nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b>NTS Steps 1+2: STANCE + NOCK&nbs
 p\;and<b>&nbsp\;</b>NTS Step 3: HOOK &amp\; GRIP<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;
 <b>13-23&nbsp\;</b>NTS Step 4: SET&nbsp\;and&nbsp\;NTS Step 5: SET-UP<br><b
 >&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;25/</b><b>26 MASTER CHALLENGE and STAR PIN SHOOT&nb
 sp\;</b>(tournament)<br><b>JULY</b><br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;2-3</b>&nb
 sp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; NTS Step 6 DRAW to LOAD&nbsp\;and&nbsp\;NTS Step 7 ANC
 HOR&nbsp\;<br><u></u>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;<b>4-10&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</b>&nbsp\
 ; NTS Step 8 TRANSFER to HOLD<br><u></u><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;11-17</b>
 &nbsp\; NTS Step 9 EXPAND / AIM<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;<b>18-24&nbsp\;&n
 bsp\;</b>NTS Step 10 RELEASE and FOLLOW-THROUGH<br><u></u><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\
 ; &nbsp\;</b><b>30/31:&nbsp\;</b><b>MASTER CHALLENGE and STAR PIN SHOOT&nbs
 p\;</b>(tournament)<br><b>AUGUST</b><br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;1-7</b>&n
 bsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;NTS Step 11 FEEDBACK&nbsp\;<br><u></u><b>&nbsp
 \; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;8-14&nbsp\;</b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; PUTTING IT ALL TOGETHER !!
 <br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\;<i>&nbsp\;<b>&nbsp\;</b></i><b>20&nbsp\;</b>&nbsp\;&nbsp
 \; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;&nbsp\;<b><i>FALL SEMESTER BEGINS !!</i></b><br><b>&nbsp\
 ; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;27/28:&nbsp\;</b><b>MASTER CHALLENGE and STAR PIN SHOOT&nb
 sp\;</b>(tournament)<br><br>You do not need to score every class. In fact\,
  it would be more beneficial to you if you scored only during Master Challe
 nge Tournament Weeks\, which happen the last week of each month. This is be
 cause working on the NTS Steps of Shooting (your form) is more easily done 
 without the distraction of the target face or scoring\, and you will improv
 e faster.<br><br>As you reach higher levels\, you will learn the NTS Steps 
 in progressively greater detail.<br>The NTS Steps are cumulative with each 
 step most successfully completed if the previous steps have been completed 
 mindfully.&nbsp\;<br><br>Your ability to learn and understand the NTS Steps
 \, and use deep focus on these Steps while shooting outdoors and while usin
 g your stretchband/string loop at home will propel you to higher levels fas
 t!<br><br><b>Goals by the end of the semester:&nbsp\;</b><br>See Coach Raca
 e´s email ¨2022 New Year´s Goals¨</html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260517T074246Z
