DESCRIPTION:Registration form: 2024 OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m<br><br><b>This
  weekend is fence erection weekend! Please come to help!</b><br><b>It's als
 o scoring weekend.<br></b><br><i>See notes about targets below.</i><br><br>
 <b>Target Assignments:</b><br><br>1. (70m)<br>2. (70m)  reversed direction<
 br><br>3. (60m)  <br><br>4. (40m)  <b>Yugan.C</b>\, 12\, USAA\, OB\, pd - n
 o scorecard<br><br>5A (30m)<b> </b><br>5B.            <br><br>6A.(30m)<br>6
 B <br><br>7A. (18m) <b>Abby Y.\,</b> 12\, USAA\, OB\, pd - 230 + 232 + 185 
 = <b>647 pts</b><br>7B.<br><br>8A. (18m)<b> Rhys E\,</b> 10\, USAA\, OB\, p
 d <b>131 pts </b>(averaged)<br>8B.            <b> Finn E\, </b>12\, USAA\, 
 OB\, pd  <b>209 pts</b><br><br>9A. (18m) <br>9B              <br><br>10A. (
 18m)<br>10B<br><br><b>Nick E</b>\, Adult\, USAA\, OB\, pd - Didnt shoot\, w
 orked on fence<br><br>Targets 1 and 2 should always stay at 70m or reversed
  so Jake can shoot.<br>Target 3 at 60m<br>Target 4 at 40m<br>Targets 5+6 at
  30m<br>Targets 7-10 will move to18m starting 8/17. Archers at 20m will now
  shoot at 18m.<br><br>If necessary\, Target #6 can move to 18m when Targets
  #7-10 are full with two archers/target at 18m.<br><br>When you shoot at 18
 m to practice for the Aggie Invitational in Nov\, you'll be on a 60-cm or 4
 0-cm target face. 60-cm target faces should be centered side-by-side\, and 
 40-cm target faces should be set up 4 to a target (even if only one or two 
 archers are on that target). <br>You should practice one round of 30 arrows
  at each target face high/low/left/right so you are prepared for your targe
 t assignment at the indoor competitions<br>Ideally\, we want to practice wi
 th at least two archers/target to replicate competition conditions as much 
 as possible.<br><br>You can decide each week if you want to shoot at your l
 ong distance or at 18m and add or move your name on the calendar accordingl
 y. You should alternate distance each day\, so you practice both. <br>Start
 ing Oct 1 to the Nov Aggie Invitational and Jan 1 for the Feb Indoor Nation
 als\, everyone should be shooting at 18m and scoring to determine their ave
 rage and their personal bests\, understand the spread between the two\, and
  work on closing it.
