DESCRIPTION:Registration form: 2024 OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m<br><br>Target 
 Assignments:<br><br>Targets 1 and 2 should always stay at 70m or reversed s
 o Jake can shoot.<br>Target 3 at 60m<br>Target 4 at 40m<br>Targets 5+6 at 3
 0m<br>Targets 7-10 will move to18m starting 8/17. Archers at 20m will now s
 hoot at 18m.<br><br>If necessary\, Target #6 can move to 18m when Targets #
 7-10 are full with two archers/target at 18m.<br>When you shoot at 18m to p
 ractice for the Aggie Invitational in Nov\, you'll be on a 60-cm or 40-cm t
 arget face. 60-cm target faces should be centered side-by-side\, and 40-cm 
 target faces should be set up 4 to a target (even if only one or two archer
 s are on that target). <br>You should practice one round of 30 arrows at ea
 ch target face high/low/left/right so you are prepared for your target assi
 gnment at the indoor competitions<br><br>Ideally\, we want to practice with
  at least two archers/target to replicate competition conditions as much as
  possible.<br>You can decide each week if you want to shoot at your long di
 stance or at 18m and add or move your name on the calendar accordingly. You
  should alternate distance each day\, so you practice both. S<br>tarting Oc
 t 1 to the Nov Aggie Invitational and Jan 1 for the Feb Indoor Nationals\, 
 everyone should be shooting at 18m and scoring to determine their average a
 nd their personal bests\, understand the spread between the two\, and work 
 on closing it.<br><br><b>JOADs U15 or U13</b>\, you will be shooting at eit
 her a 60cm target face in the JOAD portion of the indoor competitions or a 
 60-cm target face in the FITA portion of the indoor competition. <br><b>JOA
 Ds U18 and U21 and Adults</b> always shoot 40-cm target faces at any indoor
