 ns!<br><br>USA Archery Level 4 NTS Coach Racae Meyer unless otherwise noted
  above.<br><br>The level of each attending archer is noted next to their na
 me below\, to help you decide which classes to join. (Example: Indoor 2 or 
 more advanced are Outdoor 3+ (O4 @20m\, etc.)<br><br>2025 INDOOR 2-6 at 9m<
 br><br><b>Registered archers:</b><br>1. Drew S.\, adult\, pd - please resch
 edule or come at 6:30 pm<br>2\, <br>3. <br>4.<br>5.<br>6.<br>7.<br>8.<br>9.
 <br>10.<br>11.<br>12.<br><br><b>SINGLE Class Fees per archer for one Indoor
  2-6 class:</b><br>$31 for 1 hr (arrive 30 min after class starts or leave 
 30 min before class ends)<br>$43 for 1.5 hrs<br><br><b>MULTI-Class Discount
  Packets</b><br>  9 hours : $250 (six 1.5-hr classes)<br> 12 hours : $320 (
 eight 1.5-hr classes)<br> 18 hours : $460 (twelve 1.5-hr classes) <br><br>T
 here are 8 places on the shooting line\, and we sometimes have double lines
  depending on attendance.<br><br>Sign in/out upon arrival/departure<br>For 
 single classes\, book and pay in advance.<br>For multi-class discount packs
 \, pay in advance and book when you are sure of the dates.<br>Coaching and 
 whistle commands at all times.<br>Instruction in the National Training Syst
 em.<br>Unfair games depending on attendance.<br><br>Please note: Youths &lt
 \;12 y.o. should not shoot more than 100 arrows/day!<br><br>Prerequisites f
 or Indoor 2: <br>Adults: No min. score in Indoor 1 <br>Juniors: 50 pts in I
 ndoor 1<br>Scores needed at 9m to advance to Indoor 3-6 and Outdoor 3-6:<br
 ><br>                 On 40-cm                  On 60-cm<br>               
 target face                 target face<br>Indoor 3:          230 pts      
