 ill share one target stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator wi
 ll be allowed on the field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae.
 &nbsp\;<br>Parents of juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a sp
 ectator. Parents of juniors 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoo
 t with their child for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (
 + parent) is accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-time Class.&nbsp\;<br><br>
 We will accept a limited&nbsp\;number of kids under 12 into the program eac
 h semester\, depending on the total&nbsp\; number of archers in all the cla
 sses. If you join before the limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, y
 ou´ll stay in the program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and la
 ter join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;If you are under 12\, registered and paid after t
 he cut off\, your fee will be returned to you.&nbsp\;<br><br>Juniors may ne
 ed to take Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying to get into Outdo
 or 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on average abou
 t 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to gra
 duate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\
 , fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($18)<br>fp = form pac
 k (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but really needed to practice fo
 rm\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\
 , your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arr
 ows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, because it will have been a
 veraged by taking your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the
  number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying t
 hat by 30 to get a full round score. After the last class on the weekend\, 
 final scores will also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email wi
 th more information before your next class.<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u><
 /u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
