 n\nCLASS SCHEDULE and COACHES / INSTRUCTORS:\n(Read enrollment info below)\
 nSaturdays: 12:00-1:30 and 2:00-3:30 USA Archery Level 1 Instructor TBD\nSu
 ndays: 12:00-1:30 and 2:00-3:30 USA Archery Level 1 Instructor Chloe / Tori
 \nTues: 5:30-7:00: USA Archery Level 2 Instructor Dan\nWed: 5:30-7:00: USA 
 Archery Level 2 Instructor Dale\nThurs: 5:30-7:00: USA Archery Level 3 NTS 
 Coach Racae\n\nDAYS CLOSED:  \nMONDAYS and FRIDAYS\nAPRIL 4 and 5\, Easter 
 Weekend\nMAY 6\, Range closed\nMAY 10\, Mother's Day\n\nENROLLMENT IS ON A 
 FIRST-RECEIVED AND PAID BASIS.\nAn enrollment form must be completed and yo
 ur payment received in order for you to be enrolled and a place reserved fo
 r you.\nYou can enroll any time during the semester for as many or as few c
 lasses as you like as long as there are places open.\nSo\, for example\, yo
 u can enroll for the entire semester\, each month\, or sprinkle the days th
 roughout the semester depending on your schedule. (Please bear in mind\, ho
 wever\, you'll progress faster with regular attendance.)\n\nREFUNDS\, CREDI
 TS\, and SUBSTITUTIONS:\nThere are no refunds or credits for paid days miss
 ed Jan. 6 - May 31\, except in the case of injury\, long-term illness\, unf
 oreseen move out of the Austin area\, or if we cancel a class. If\, however
 \, you let us know before a class that you will miss that class\, you can s
 ubstitute another class as long as there are places left in that class duri
 ng the Spring 2015 semester. If you fail to let us know before a class that
  you will miss that class and want to substitute another class\, there is n
 o substitution or refund. Substitutions do not carry forward to the next se
 mester.\n\nIn the case of physical injury or long-term illness\, we require
  a doctor's note saying the archer is unable to practice archery\, and then
  a doctor's note saying the archer is fit to return to archery\, before the
  archer will be allowed back in class.\n\nATTENDANCE RECOMMENDATIONS in ord
 er to improve: \nINDOOR 2 at 9m :        One or two 1.5-hr classes per week
 .\nINDOOR 3A at 13.5m : Two 1.5-hr classes per week.\nINDOOR 3B at 18m :   
  Two or three 1.5-hr classes per week.\n\nMINIMUM ENROLLMENT:\nClasses will
  be held only if there are 5 or more archers enrolled in the class. \nIf th
 e class does not make this minimum enrollment requirement\, you will be not
 ified at least one week in advance\, so you can reschedule.\n\nHOW DO I ADV
 ANCE?\nYou'll be trained in Indoor 2 at 9m until you score 240 pts and mast
 er certain NTS* Shot Cycle positions\, then you'll move back to 13.5m in In
 door 3A until you score 240 pts and master more NTS Shot Cycle positions\, 
 and then to 18m in Indoor 3B until you score 200 pts. twice and master more
  NTS Shot Cycle positions. After that you'll be in Indoor 4: Advanced Recre
 ational with Coach Racae!\n\nFEES:\nAll fees are payable in advance of the 
 class to secure your place in the class.\n$21 / class\, if paid on or befor
 e Nov. 30\, 2014 \n$22 / class\, if paid on or before Dec. 14\, 2014 \n$23 
 / class\, if paid after Dec. 14\, 2014.\n\n+ Enrollment fee: $20 (always du
 e once per semester)\n\nHOW MUCH DO I OWE? \nMultiply the number of classes
  x the appropriate fee above.\nAdd the $20 semester enrollment fee\n\nHOW D
 O I PAY IN ADVANCE (after I submit the enrollment form)?\nPay the total by 
 Paypal using e-mail address: racae@aajoad.com.\nWe also accept checks and c
 redit cards in person at the indoor range.\nPlease make your check payable 
 to "Archery Training Center\, Inc." and give it to us at JOAD* or mail it t
 o us at:\nArchery Training Center\, Inc.\, PO Box 93216\, Austin\, TX 78709
 -3216\n\nSAFE SPORTS:\nParents please note we are part of the US Olympic Co
 mmittee's Safe Sport program\, so we minimally require one other adult besi
 des the instructor to be present at all times. Please plan to stay with you
 r child or take turns with other parents staying whenever necessary to fulf
 ill this requirement. THANKS!\n\nINDOOR 2/3 WAIVERS:\nPlease fill out\, sig
 n\, and return the Photo\, Medical\, and Supervision Releases attached to t
 he e-mail you received with the enrollment form link..\n\nQUESTIONS?\nE-mai
 l us at racae@archerytrainingcenter.com or\nCall us at 512 436 8813\n\n*NTS
  = National Training System\n*JOAD = Junior Olympic Archery Development
