DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u>
 </u>REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to adult\, juniors 8+\, and parents! Please 
 read all the info below and in the registration and waivers.<br><br>More in
 formation\, registration forms and waivers are available at&nbsp\;<a href="
 http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com"><u>www.archerytrainingcenter.com</u><
 /a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE of these forms:<br><a href="https://doc
 s.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfcwG419ZK9XmA4-JlXM-zhjhvSPCF8NCwWJlzFP2w-gR
 liUw/viewform"><u>2022 Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Juniors + Parents</u
 ></a>&nbsp\; OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSe-YxP
 KAMTxiC7kVt6fZuQJeidXENYq_iV4rWj1RaXdLhPoew/viewform"><u>2022 Outdoor 1: Fi
 rst-time Class for Adults</u></a><br><br>Sign up for just ONE Outdoor 1 cla
 ss\, because most people graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after th
 e first lesson.<br><br>Your name will be added below and your place reserve
 d on a&nbsp\;first registered and paid basis and after we receive 3 things:
 &nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br><b>2022 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM&nbsp\; &nbsp\;+&nbsp\
 ; MEMBERSHIP AND WAIVERS PACKET +&nbsp\; &nbsp\;FEE</b><br><br><b>Registere
 d archers&nbsp\;</b>at 9m on 40-cm target face:<br><b>Target Assignments:</
 b><br>1.&nbsp\;<br>2.&nbsp\;<br>3.&nbsp\;<br>4.&nbsp\;<b>Liza G</b>.\, adul
 t - pd - substituted for 6/4 - canceled - rescheduled to 7/9<u></u><br><u><
 /u>5.&nbsp\;<b>Ryan K</b>.\, adult - pd - substituted for 6/4 - canceled - 
 rescheduled to 7/9<br>6.&nbsp\;<b>Natalie O</b>.\, adult - pd - refund<br>7
 . <b>Erica R.\, </b>adult - pd - rescheduled to 6/26<br>8.<br>9.<br>10.<br>
 <br>Space will be limited to 10-15 archers per session depending on the num
 ber of family groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC Guidelines.&nb
 sp\;<br>Each person will have a target stand\, except after 10 people have 
 registered\, two members from the same family will share one target stand.<
 br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field u
 ntil further notice or approved by Coach Racae.&nbsp\;<br>Parents of junior
 s 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator. Parents of juniors 
 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their child for great
 er safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into e
 ach Outdoor 1: First-time Class.&nbsp\;<br><br>We will accept a limited&nbs
 p\;number of kids under 12 into the program each semester\, depending on th
 e total&nbsp\; number of archers in all the classes. If you join before the
  limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program an
 d take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;If
  you are under 12\, registered and paid after the cut off\, your fee will b
 e returned to you.&nbsp\;<br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or 
 three times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´
 ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.&nbs
 p\;<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br
 >ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will 
 be needed for Outdoor 2. ($18)<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string lo
 op)\, optional but really needed to practice form\, warm up before classes 
 ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted
 . If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize
  your final score\, because it will have been averaged by taking your recor
 ded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot t
 o get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full roun
 d score. After the last class on the weekend\, final scores will also be se
 nt to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more information before y
 our next class.<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u></ht
 ml-blob>
