DESCRIPTION:To register for this class\, you will have already completed an
 d graduated out of Outdoor 1: First-time Class\, Outdoor 2 at 9m\, and Outd
 oor 3 at 13.5m\, and your distance will be at least 20m. Register here:&nbs
 p\;<a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfF-EGKsMPSlfPLuLe3aLk
 qThTFZs0qqb8zleJ_0W3B6Xn7mA/viewform">2021 Outdoor 4-9 at 20m-70m</a><br><b
 r><b>Registered Archers</b> - all on 122cm target face:<br><br>1.&nbsp\;<br
 >2.&nbsp\;<br>3.&nbsp\;<br>4..Kevin B.\, @ 30m&nbsp\;<br>5. Lily R.\, @ 30m
 <br>6. Emma W.\, @ 20m&nbsp\;<br>7. John B.\, @ 20m<br>8.<br>9.<br>10.<br><
 br><b>Tournament Week</b><br>For one week each month during Tournament Week
 \, you shoot for score and submit your scores to Coach Racae. Score in your
  regular classes or come to the tournament on Tournament Saturday.<br><br><
 b>Tournament Saturday</b><br>On the last day of tournament week\, Saturday\
 , Coach Racae will conduct the Saturday Outdoor 4-9 class as a tournament w
 ith timed rounds and scoring and little to no coaching.&nbsp\;<br><br><b>Ma
 ster Challenge</b><br>While you´re shooting in the tournament&nbsp\; Coach 
 Racae will look at your form and assess how much attention to form you can 
 remember to do while shooting in a tournament. You can earn Mastered Tags f
 or each step of the form you have consistently done at your level. As you p
 rogress through higher levels\, the level of detail required will increase 
 and additional positions will be added.<br><br><b>USA Archery Star Pins</b>
 <br><b>If you are a member of USA Archery</b>\, Tournament Saturday is ofte
 n called a ¨Pin Shoot¨\, when you can earn your USA Archery Star Pins based
  on the scores you obtain. Look at the bottom of your scorecard to see how 
 many points you´ll need to receive a Star Pin.<br><br><b>Winners´ Pot and F
 ees</b><br>Archers participate in Tournament Week by entering one of the fo
 llowing tournaments and paying $5.00 towards the Winners´ Pot. Winners will
  be announced by email and Instagram following Tournament Saturday.&nbsp\;<
 br>Archers participating in Tournament Saturday or attending any Outdoor 2-
 9 classes will also pay $30 for their place on the shooting line\, unless t
 hey also take virtual lessons once or twice a week with Coach Racae\, in wh
 ich case\, their fee is $10.<br><br>Enter one of these tournaments:<br><b>O
 utdoor 2 + 3 Tournament :&nbsp\;</b><br>For beginners at 9m and 13.5m - One
  or two rounds (depending on your strength) of 10 ends of 3 arrows each for
  a total of 30 arrows.<br><b>Outdoor 4-9 Tournament:&nbsp\;</b><br>For more
  advanced archers at 20m+ - Two rounds of 6 ends of 6 arrows each for a tot
 al of 72 arrows shot on 122-cm target faces.<br><br>More information and re
 gistration links at&nbsp\;<a>www.archerytrainingcenter.com</a>
