DESCRIPTION:<b>What we worked on:</b><br>Anchor/Transfer/Hold -&nbsp\;<br>K
 eeping draw elbow at or slightly above height of shoulder.<br>If you´re not
  sure where your bow arm should be and how it should fee\, which muscles sh
 ould be used\, just lift both arms up until they are in line with your shou
 lders (from in front and above) - that is the postion we´re trying to get t
 o.<br>Back tension should be slowly increased starting at Set until you are
  bracing the bow at Transfer/Hold:<br>Set : 40%<br>Set-Up: 60%<br>Draw to L
 oad: 80%<br>Anchor: 90%<br>Transfer to Hold: 95%<br>Expand/Aim -<br>Keep si
 ght aperture above yellow (like in the black at 10-12 o´clock) until Expand
  and then drop it into yellow at Aim. There is no Aiming before the Aim pos
 ition. In other words\, you finish your getting your positions in place (yo
 ur form) before you aim.<br>Focus -&nbsp\;<br>Keeping mental focus on form 
 positions - one at a time - even while physically aiming<br>Keep expanding 
 internally by opening chest\; you´ll feel your back compressing&nbsp\;<br><
 b>What to practice:</b><br>Anchor / Transfer / Hold / Expand / Aim&nbsp\;<b
 r>Try to determine the movement and direction of your draw elbow (what musc
 les move it up and when)<br>It should move very slightly up at Anchor and t
 hen horizontally &lt\;1 inch at Transfer as you build up back tension<br>De
 termine when you lose focus:<br>o by backtracking into previous position(s)
  or distractions - break down\, start over<br>o by focusing on target inste
 ad of form - break down\, start over<br>Take down target to help with focus
 ing on form instead\, but periodically put it back up to see if you can sti
 ll keep your focus.<br><b>Equipment:</b><br>Move target face around on targ
 et bale so you don´t shoot out one spot and cause richochets.<br><b>Distanc
 e:</b><br>Move back 5 ft at a time\, making sure to keep the arrow groups t
 ight as a reflection of improving form\, before you move back 5 ft more.<br
 ><b>Homework:</b><br>Watch video links sent you&nbsp\;<br>Read Transfer -&g
 t\; Aim inclusively<br><b>Goals:</b><br><b>Process leads to Performance</b>
 <br>I´ll send you some goal-setting sheets soon.<br>In the meantime\, think
  about what you would like to achieve in archery over the next month and ye
 ar. Write them down. Think about what you think it would take to get there\
 , and how you would measure your success. They can be form and mental\, pro
 cess goals\, and scoring and strength performance&nbsp\; goals.
