DESCRIPTION:To register for this class\, you will have already completed an
 d graduated out of Outdoor 1: First-time Class\, Outdoor 2 at 9m\, and Outd
 oor 3 at 13.5m\, and your distance will be at least 20m. Register here:&nbs
 p\;<a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfF-EGKsMPSlfPLuLe3aLk
 qThTFZs0qqb8zleJ_0W3B6Xn7mA/viewform">2021 Outdoor 4-9 at 20m-70m</a><br><b
 r><b>Registered Archers </b>(all on 122cm target face):<br><br>1.&nbsp\;<br
 >2.&nbsp\;<br>3. Sarah X.\, @ 50m&nbsp\;<br>4. Kevin B.\, @ 30m&nbsp\;<br>5
 .<br>6. Emma W.\, @ 20m&nbsp\;<br>7.<br>8.<br>9.<br>10.<br><br><b>Tournamen
 t Week</b><br>For one week each month during Tournament Week\, you shoot fo
 r score and submit your scores to Coach Racae. Score in your regular classe
 s or come to the tournament on Tournament Saturday.<br><br><b>Tournament Sa
 turday</b><br>On the last day of tournament week\, Saturday\, Coach Racae w
 ill conduct the Saturday Outdoor 4-9 class as a tournament with timed round
 s and scoring and little to no coaching.&nbsp\;<br><br><b>Master Challenge<
 /b><br>While you´re shooting in the tournament&nbsp\; Coach Racae will look
  at your form and assess how much attention to form you can remember to do 
 while shooting in a tournament. You can earn Mastered Tags for each step of
  the form you have consistently done at your level. As you progress through
  higher levels\, the level of detail required will increase and additional 
 positions will be added.<br><br><b>USA Archery Star Pins</b><br><b>If you a
 re a member of USA Archery</b>\, Tournament Saturday is often called a ¨Pin
  Shoot¨\, when you can earn your USA Archery Star Pins based on the scores 
 you obtain. Look at the bottom of your scorecard to see how many points you
 ´ll need to receive a Star Pin.<br><br><b>Winners´ Pot and Fees</b><br>Arch
 ers participate in Tournament Week by entering one of the following tournam
 ents and paying $5.00 towards the Winners´ Pot. Winners will be announced b
 y email and Instagram following Tournament Saturday.&nbsp\;<br>Archers part
 icipating in Tournament Saturday or attending any Outdoor 2-9 classes will 
 also pay $30 for their place on the shooting line\, unless they also take v
 irtual lessons once or twice a week with Coach Racae\, in which case\, thei
 r fee is $10.<br><br>Enter one of these tournaments:<br><b>Outdoor 2 + 3 To
 urnament :&nbsp\;</b><br>For beginners at 9m and 13.5m - One or two rounds 
 (depending on your strength) of 10 ends of 3 arrows each for a total of 30 
 arrows.<br><b>Outdoor 4-9 Tournament:&nbsp\;</b><br>For more advanced arche
 rs at 20m+ - Two rounds of 6 ends of 6 arrows each for a total of 72 arrows
  shot on 122-cm target faces.<br><br>More information and registration link
 s at&nbsp\;<a>www.archerytrainingcenter.com</a>
