DESCRIPTION:Registration form: OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m<br><br>REMINDER:  E
 veryone needs to come to at least one Training Class per week to be able to
  attend Open Practice. (All indoor classes are training classes.)<br><br>If
  you are not a coach/instructor\, the fees are:  <br><br>Outdoor Training C
 lass (OTC): $52/class or multi-class pack <br><br>Indoor Training Class (IT
 C): $43/class or multi-class pack or unlimited pack<br><br>Open Practice (O
 P): ($50/mo)  <br><br>If you are a coach/instructor\, you have received an 
 email from Coach Racae outlining your fees.<br><br>During the fall (Aug 31-
 Dec 18)\, for Coach Racae to coach the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class\, at leas
 t 5 archers need to register by <br>8:00 am on Thursdays (for Saturdays) an
 d <br>8:00 am on Fridays (for Sundays) <br>In the case of low or late regis
 trations or cancellations\, another coach/instructor\, when available\, wil
 l coach the session as a Training Class or oversee it as an Open Practice i
 nstead. If this is not possible\, then the class may need to be cancelled.<
 br><br>Add your name to the Target Assignment List below or submit the abov
 e completed form.<br>Focus primarily on perfecting your form\, <br>slowly i
 ncreasing your physical strength and draw weight\, <br>strengthening your m
 ental program\, <br>determining your average and personal best\, <br>unders
 tanding the spread between the two\, and working on closing it.<br><br>You 
 need your own equipment <br>Competition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, 
 plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, che
 st protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, 
 arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added until you reach
  a higher level\, but you should order them in advance.) <br><br>Wear your 
 ATCI shirt to training.<br><br>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round o
 n the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the next distance until you re
 ach your competition distance<br>If you trained outdoors in the 2024 season
 \, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.<br><br>Target arrangeme
 nts may vary each session\, depending on who attends and distances needed.<
 br>Target 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should always stay 
 at 70m so Jake can use it for independent practice in between classes.<br>T
 arget 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition distance) <br>Target 3 at 50m<br>
 Target 4+5 at 40m (U15 competition distance) <br>Target 6 at 30m (U13 compe
 tition distance) <br><br>Targets 7-10 at 18m (for those wanting to qualify 
 to shoot competitively at 18m indoors or with Coach Racae's approval)<br><b
 r>Ideally\, we want to practice with two archers/target to replicate outdoo
 r competition conditions.<br>Alternate daily: Outdoor distance and 18m dist
 ance. <br>For 18m distance\, put up four 40-cm target faces on one target\,
  even if fewer people are shooting the target\, so you practice high/low/le
 ft/right. <br>For 18m JOAD\, put up two 60cm target faces on one target sid
 e-by-side for max two people shooting on each target bale.<br>Target Assign
 ments:<br>Targets are assigned outdoors in advance to reduce confusion and 
 delay on the day\,<br>so add your name next to your distance below. <br>If 
 you need help or have questions\, email/text Coach Racae<br>(Dotted lines r
 epresent tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)<br><br><b>ATCIICT = 20
 26 ATCI Indoor Competition Team : </b><br><b>MQS 210 pts or 420 pts (2 roun
 ds)</b><br>----------------------------------<br>1A. (70m)<br>1B<br><br>2A.
  (60m)  <br>2B<br><br>3A. (50m)  <b>Adrianne M</b>\, adult\, USAA\, pd - <b
 >ATCIICT - </b>DNS<br>----------------------------------<br>3B<br><br>4A. (
 40m) <b>Sophia D</b>\, adult\, USAA\, f - DNS<br>4B. <br>------------------
 ----------------<br>5A. (40m)<br>5B. <br><br>6A. (30m)<br>-----------------
 -----------------<br>6B. <br><br>7A. (18m)<br>7B. (18m) <b>Anush M\, 13 </b
 > - 164 + 117 = <b>281 pts</b><br>---------------------------------- <br>8A
 . (18m) <b>Matt L</b>\, 13\, pd - <b>100 pts</b><br>8B. <br><br>9A. (18m) <
 b>Finn E</b> 13  - 183 + 193 = <b>376 pts</b><br>--------------------------
 --------<br>9B.  <b>Nick E</b> adult\, 261 + 249 = <b>510 pts - CONGRATULAT
 IONS !!! - You made the 2026 ATCI Indoor Competition Team (ATCIICT)</b><br>
