CREATED:20220603T213527Z
DESCRIPTION:<b>2022 Summer Schedule and Goals for Outdoor 2-9 (9m to 70m)</
 b><br><b><br></b><br><b>Goals by the end of the summer semester (Aug 14):&n
 bsp\;</b><br>Make a list of what you want to accomplish<b><br></b>&nbsp\;<b
 r><b>JUNE</b><br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>2-5</b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &n
 bsp\; Welcome Back: Understanding&nbsp\; NTS Concepts \; Mental Program<br>
 <b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>9-12</b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; NTS Steps 1+2: STA
 NCE + NOCK&nbsp\;<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\;&nbsp\;<b>16-19&nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b>NTS S
 tep 3: HOOK &amp\; GRIP&nbsp\;<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; 25/</b><b>26&nbsp\; JU
 NE ATCI MASTER CHALLENGE TOURNAMENT (Pin Shoot)</b><br><b>JULY</b><br><b>&n
 bsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;6/30-7/3&nbsp\;</b>NTS Step 4: SET\; NTS Step 5: SET-U
 P&nbsp\;<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;7-10</b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;NTS St
 ep 6 DRAW to LOAD&nbsp\;<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;<b>14-17&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</
 b>NTS Step 7 ANCHOR&nbsp\;<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>21-24&nbsp\;
 &nbsp\;</b>NTS Step 8 TRANSFER to HOLD<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;30/31&n
 bsp\; JULY ATCI MASTER CHALLENGE TOURNAMENT (Pin Shoot)</b><br><b>AUGUST</b
 ><br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;4-7</b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;NTS St
 ep 9 EXPAND / AIM&nbsp\;<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;11-14</b>&nbsp\; NTS 
 Step 10 RELEASE + FOLLOW-THROUGH<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;<b>18-21</b>&nbs
 p\;<b>&nbsp\;</b>NTS Step 11: FEEDBACK + Putting it all together!<b><br>&nb
 sp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>27/28&nbsp\; AUGUST ATCI MASTER CHALLENGE TOURNA
 MENT (Pin Shoot)</b><br><br>Each week the focus of your lessons will be on 
 particular Steps of Shooting of the NTS (National Training System) shot cyc
 le\, to help you focus and improve your form\, which\, as we all know\, lea
 ds to greater and consistent precision (tight groups of arrows) and ultimat
 ely greater accuracy (tight groups of arrows dead center).<br><br>Your goal
  is always to replicate the NTS step(s) mindfully and consistently on every
  shot. If you stay in the present just doing what you need to do as you nee
 d to it\, your conscious mind will be occupied\, instead of random thoughts
  entering your head or you being distracted by emotional or environmental e
 lements. You´ll need to build up your mental program alongside your form kn
 owledge\, so when your body is trained to shoot excellent shots\, your self
  image and subsonscious support you\, instead of undermining you. Confidenc
 e and consistency in form and mind are major goals.<br><br>You do not need 
 to score in every class. In fact\, it would be more beneficial to you if yo
 u scored only during Master Challenge Tournament Weeks\, which happen the l
 ast week of each month. This is because working on the NTS Steps of Shootin
 g (your form) is more easily done without the distraction of the target fac
 e or scoring\, and you will improve faster.<br><br>As you reach higher leve
 ls\, you will learn the NTS Steps in progressively greater detail.<br>The N
 TS Steps are cumulative with each step most successfully completed if the p
 revious steps have been completed well.&nbsp\;<br><br>Your ability to learn
  and understand the NTS Steps\, and use deep focus on these Steps while sho
 oting outdoors and while using your stretchband/string loop at home to rein
 force form poisitions will propel you to higher levels fast!
LAST-MODIFIED:20260517T080536Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:FORM FOCUS: NTS Step 3: HOOK & GRIP
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
