DESCRIPTION:<i>Practice 18m at the outdoor range today.</i><br><i>TODAY is 
 move day into the 18m range located at 110 Wild Basin Rd.\, Suite 210\, Wes
 tlake (just off 360).  It should be ready by Sunday 11/16\, but we'll confi
 rm on the calendar. </i><br><i>The outdoor range will be open for practice/
 training throughout the winter with instructor/coach supervision.</i><br><b
 r><b>REMINDER</b>:  Everyone needs to come to at least one Training Class p
 er week to be able to attend Open Practice. (All indoor classes are trainin
 g classes.)<br><br>If you are not a coach/instructor\, the fees are:  <ul><
 li><b>Outdoor Training Class (OTC)</b>: $52/class or multi-class pack </li>
 <li><b>Indoor Training Class (ITC)</b>: $43/class or multi-class pack or un
 limited pack</li><li><b>Open Practice (OP)</b>: ($50/mo)  </li></ul><br>If 
 you are a coach/instructor\, you have received an email from Coach Racae ou
 tlining your fees.<br><br>During the fall (Aug 31-Dec 18)\, for Coach Racae
  to coach the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class\, at least 5 archers need to regis
 ter by <br>8:00 am on Thursdays (for Saturdays) and <br>8:00 am on Fridays 
 (for Sundays) <br>In the case of low or late registrations or cancellations
 \, another coach/instructor\, when available\, will coach the session as a 
 Training Class or oversee it as an Open Practice instead. If this is not po
 ssible\, then the class may need to be cancelled.<br><br>Add your name to t
 he Target Assignment List below or submit the above completed form.<br>Focu
 s primarily on perfecting your form\, <br>slowly increasing your physical s
 trength and draw weight\, <br>strengthening your mental program\, <br>deter
 mining your average and personal best\, <br>understanding the spread betwee
 n the two\, and working on closing it.<br><br>You need your own equipment <
 br>Competition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbo
 n arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\,
  fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clic
 ker and side rods may not be added until you reach a higher level\, but you
  should order them in advance.) <br><br>Wear your ATCI shirt to training.<b
 r><br>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm target face 
 you'll move back to the next distance until you reach your competition dist
 ance<br>If you trained outdoors in the 2024 season\, you'll return to the f
 arthest distance you shot.<br><br>Target arrangements may vary each session
 \, depending on who attends and distances needed.<br>Target 1 at 70m (U21 +
  Seniors competition distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use it
  for independent practice in between classes.<br>Target 2 at 60m (U18 + Mas
 ters competition distance) <br>Target 3 at 50m<br>Target 4+5 at 40m (U15 co
 mpetition distance) <br>Target 6 at 30m (U13 competition distance) <br><br>
 Targets 7-10 at 18m (for those wanting to qualify to shoot competitively at
  18m indoors or with Coach Racae's approval)<br><br>Ideally\, we want to pr
 actice with two archers/target to replicate outdoor competition conditions.
 <br><b>Alternate daily</b>: Outdoor distance and 18m distance. <br>For <b>1
 8m distance</b>\, put up <b>four 40-cm target faces on one target</b>\, eve
 n if fewer people are shooting the target\, so you practice high/low/left/r
 ight. <br>For <b>18m JOAD</b>\, put up <b>two 60cm target faces on one targ
 et side-by-side</b> for max two people shooting on each target bale.<br>Tar
 get Assignments:<br>Targets are assigned outdoors in advance to reduce conf
 usion and delay on the day\,<br>so add your name next to your distance belo
 w. <br>If you need help or have questions\, email/text Coach Racae<br>(Dott
 ed lines represent tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)<br><br><br><
 b>2026 ATCI Indoor Competition Team = </b><b>ATCIICT </b><br><b>MQS at 18m\
 , 30-arrow rounds: 210 pts or 420 pts (2 rounds)</b><br>Abby <br>Instr. Adr
 ianne <br>Instr. Anna <br>Instr. Colby <br>Emma <br>Instr. Erika<br>Finn <b
 r>Instr. Javier<br>Coach Joel <br>Luke <br>Coach Nick <br>Sara  <br>Instr. 
 Sophia<br><b>REGISTERED ARCHERS TODAY:</b><br>-----------------------------
 -----<br>1A. (70m)<br>1B<br><br>2A. (60m)  Joel Y\, adult\, usaa\, pd<br>2B
 <br><br>3A. (50m)  Abby Y\, 13\, usaa\, pd<br>-----------------------------
 -----<br>3B<br><br>4A. (40m) Sophia D\, adult\, USAA\, f<br>4B. <br>-------
 ---------------------------<br>5A. (40m)<br>5B. <br><br>6A. (30m) Ellie Y\,
  11\, usaa\, pd<br>----------------------------------<br>6B. <br><br>7A. (1
 8m)<br>7B. <br>---------------------------------- <br>8A. (18m)<br>8B. <br>
 <br>9A. (18m)<br>----------------------------------<br>9B. <br><br>10A. (18
