DESCRIPTION:To register for this class usually\, you will have already comp
 leted and graduated out of Outdoor 1: First-time Class\, Outdoor 2 at 9m\, 
 and Outdoor 3 at 13.5m\, and your distance will be at least 20m. Register h
 ere:&nbsp\;<a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfF-EGKsMPSlfP
 LuLe3aLkqThTFZs0qqb8zleJ_0W3B6Xn7mA/viewform">2021 Outdoor 4-9 at 20m-70m</
 a><br><br>Registered Archers:<br>1. Kevin B.\, @ 30m on 122cm target face -
  pd<br>2. Lily R.\, @ 30m on 122cm target face - pd<br>3. Elizabeth M.\, 12
  @9m on 60cm target face - DNA late cancellation - pd<br>4..Kishore P.\, 13
  @ 13.5m - to pay - <b>218 pts</b><br>5. Victor C.\, 9 @ 9m - pd<br>6.<br>7
 .<br>8.<br>9.<br>10.<br><br><b>Tournament Week</b><br>For one week each mon
 th during Tournament Week\, you shoot for score and submit your scores to C
 oach Racae. Score in your regular classes or come to the tournament on Tour
 nament Saturday.<br><br><b>Tournament Saturday</b><br>On the last day of to
 urnament week\, Saturday\, Coach Racae will conduct the Saturday Outdoor 4-
 9 class as a tournament with timed rounds and scoring and little to no coac
 hing.&nbsp\;<br><br><b>Master Challenge</b><br>While you´re shooting in the
  tournament&nbsp\; Coach Racae will look at your form and assess how much a
 ttention to form you can remember to do while shooting in a tournament. You
  can earn Mastered Tags for each step of the form you have consistently don
 e at your level. As you progress through higher levels\, the level of detai
 l required will increase and additional positions will be added.<br><br><b>
 USA Archery Star Pins</b><br><b>If you are a member of USA Archery</b>\, To
 urnament Saturday is often called a ¨Pin Shoot¨\, when you can earn your US
 A Archery Star Pins based on the scores you obtain. Look at the bottom of y
 our scorecard to see how many points you´ll need to receive a Star Pin.<br>
 <br><b>Winners´ Pot and Fees</b><br>Archers participate in Tournament Week 
 by entering one of the following tournaments and paying $5.00 towards the W
 inners´ Pot. Winners will be announced by email and Instagram following Tou
 rnament Saturday.&nbsp\;<br>Archers participating in Tournament Saturday or
  attending any Outdoor 2-9 classes will also pay $30 for their place on the
  shooting line\, unless they also take virtual lessons once or twice a week
  with Coach Racae\, in which case\, their fee is $10.<br><br>Enter one of t
 hese tournaments:<br><b>Outdoor 2 + 3 Tournament :&nbsp\;</b><br>For beginn
 ers at 9m and 13.5m - One or two rounds (depending on your strength) of 10 
 ends of 3 arrows each for a total of 30 arrows.<br><b>Outdoor 4-9 Tournamen
 t:&nbsp\;</b><br>For more advanced archers at 20m+ - Two rounds of 6 ends o
 f 6 arrows each for a total of 72 arrows shot on 122-cm target faces.<br><b
 r>More information and registration links at&nbsp\;<a>www.archerytrainingce
 nter.com</a>
