DESCRIPTION:To register for this class\, you will have already completed an
 d graduated out of Outdoor 1: First-time Class\, Outdoor 2 at 9m\, and Outd
 oor 3 at 13.5m\, and your distance will be at least 20m. Register here:&nbs
 p\;<a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfF-EGKsMPSlfPLuLe3aLk
 qThTFZs0qqb8zleJ_0W3B6Xn7mA/viewform">2021 Outdoor 4-9 at 20m-70m</a><br><b
 r><b>Registered Archers </b>on 122-cm target face unless otherwise noted:<b
 r>1. <b>Kevin B</b>.\, @ 40m&nbsp\;<br>2.&nbsp\;<b>Lily R.</b>\, 12\, at 30
 m&nbsp\;<br>3.&nbsp\;<br>4..<br>5.<br>6.<br>7.<br>8.<br>9.<br>10.<br><br><b
 >Cyrenna V.&nbsp\;</b>@ 13.5m to reschedule<br><br><b>Tournament Week</b><b
 r>For one week each month during Tournament Week\, you shoot for score and 
 submit your scores to Coach Racae. Score in your regular classes or come to
  the tournament on Tournament Saturday.<br><br><b>Tournament Saturday</b><b
 r>On the last day of tournament week\, Saturday\, Coach Racae will conduct 
 the Saturday Outdoor 4-9 class as a tournament with timed rounds and scorin
 g and little to no coaching.&nbsp\;<br><br><b>Master Challenge</b><br>While
  you´re shooting in the tournament&nbsp\; Coach Racae will look at your for
 m and assess how much attention to form you can remember to do while shooti
 ng in a tournament. You can earn Mastered Tags for each step of the form yo
 u have consistently done at your level. As you progress through higher leve
 ls\, the level of detail required will increase and additional positions wi
 ll be added.<br><br><b>USA Archery Star Pins</b><br><b>If you are a member 
 of USA Archery</b>\, Tournament Saturday is often called a ¨Pin Shoot¨\, wh
 en you can earn your USA Archery Star Pins based on the scores you obtain. 
 Look at the bottom of your scorecard to see how many points you´ll need to 
 receive a Star Pin.<br><br><b>Winners´ Pot and Fees</b><br>Archers particip
 ate in Tournament Week by entering one of the following tournaments and pay
 ing $5.00 towards the Winners´ Pot. Winners will be announced by email and 
 Instagram following Tournament Saturday.&nbsp\;<br>Archers participating in
  Tournament Saturday or attending any Outdoor 2-9 classes will also pay $30
  for their place on the shooting line\, unless they also take virtual lesso
 ns once or twice a week with Coach Racae\, in which case\, their fee is $10
 .<br><br>Enter one of these tournaments:<br><b>Outdoor 2 + 3 Tournament :&n
 bsp\;</b><br>For beginners at 9m and 13.5m - One or two rounds (depending o
 n your strength) of 10 ends of 3 arrows each for a total of 30 arrows.<br><
 b>Outdoor 4-9 Tournament:&nbsp\;</b><br>For more advanced archers at 20m+ -
  Two rounds of 6 ends of 6 arrows each for a total of 72 arrows shot on 122
 -cm target faces.<br><br>More information and registration links at&nbsp\;<
 a>www.archerytrainingcenter.com</a>
