DESCRIPTION:Registration form: OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m<br><br><b>REMINDER<
 /b>:  Everyone needs to come to at least one Training Class per week to be 
 able to attend Open Practice. (All indoor classes are training classes.)<br
 ><br>If you are not a coach/instructor\, the fees are:  <br><ul><li><b>Outd
 oor Training Class (OTC)</b>: $52/class or multi-class pack </li><li><b>Ind
 oor Training Class (ITC)</b>: $43/class or multi-class pack or unlimited pa
 ck</li><li><b>Open Practice (OP)</b>: ($50/mo)  </li></ul>If you are a coac
 h/instructor\, you have received an email from Coach Racae outlining your f
 ees.<br><br>During the fall (Aug 31-Dec 18)\, for Coach Racae to coach the 
 Outdoor 3-9 Training Class\, at least 5 archers need to register by <br>8:0
 0 am on Thursdays (for Saturdays) and <br>8:00 am on Fridays (for Sundays) 
 <br>In the case of low or late registrations or cancellations\, another coa
 ch/instructor\, when available\, will coach the session as a Training Class
  or oversee it as an Open Practice instead. If this is not possible\, then 
 the class may need to be cancelled.<br><br>Add your name to the Target Assi
 gnment List below or submit the above completed form.<br>Focus primarily on
  perfecting your form\, <br>slowly increasing your physical strength and dr
 aw weight\, <br>strengthening your mental program\, <br>determining your av
 erage and personal best\, <br>understanding the spread between the two\, an
 d working on closing it.<br><br>You need your own equipment <br>Competition
  recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, sid
 e rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, f
 inger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side r
 ods may not be added until you reach a higher level\, but you should order 
 them in advance.) <br><br>Wear your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br>When you
  score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm target face you'll move ba
 ck to the next distance until you reach your competition distance<br>If you
  trained outdoors in the 2024 season\, you'll return to the farthest distan
 ce you shot.<br><br>Target arrangements may vary each session\, depending o
 n who attends and distances needed.<br>Target 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors compe
 tition distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use it for independe
 nt practice in between classes.<br>Target 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competiti
 on distance) <br>Target 3 at 50m<br>Target 4+5 at 40m (U15 competition dist
 ance) <br>Target 6 at 30m (U13 competition distance) <br><br>Targets 7-10 a
 t 18m (for those wanting to qualify to shoot competitively at 18m indoors o
 r with Coach Racae's approval)<br><br>Ideally\, we want to practice with tw
 o archers/target to replicate outdoor competition conditions.<br><b>Alterna
 te daily</b>: Outdoor distance and 18m distance. <br>For <b>18m distance</b
 >\, put up <b>four 40-cm target faces on one target</b>\, even if fewer peo
