DESCRIPTION:Once a month until October 18\,&nbsp\; Outdoor 2+3 can register
  for Tournament Saturday at&nbsp\;<a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/
 e/1FAIpQLSeXKGqxUPCkcYHxJgXLxz62jkCFDOFvJswqN_cthIWgsBps7g/viewform">ATCI V
 irtual Monthly Tournament</a><br><br>To register for this class usually\, y
 ou will have already completed and graduated out of Outdoor 1: First-time C
 lass\, Outdoor 2 at 9m\, and Outdoor 3 at 13.5m\, and your distance will be
  at least 20m. Register here:&nbsp\;<a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/
 d/e/1FAIpQLSfF-EGKsMPSlfPLuLe3aLkqThTFZs0qqb8zleJ_0W3B6Xn7mA/viewform">2021
  Outdoor 4-9 at 20m-70m</a><br><br>Registered Archers:<br>1. <b>Kevin B</b>
 .\, @ 30m on 122cm target face<br>2. <b>Victor C</b>.\, 9\, @9m on 60cm tar
 get face - admitted until 10/16<br>3. <b>Sarah X.</b>\, 14 - @50m on 122cm 
 target face<br>4. <b>Emma W.? </b>14<b> -&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</b>@20m on 122cm ta
 rget face<br>5. <b>Elizabeth M</b>.\, 12 - @9m on 60cm target face - admitt
 ed until 10/16<br>6.&nbsp\;<b>Mila M.\,&nbsp\;</b>13 - @9m on 60cm target f
 ace - admitted until 10/16<br>7. <b>Cyrenna V.</b>\, adult @ 13.5m on 40cm 
 target face<br>8.<br>9.<br>10.<br><br><b>Tournament Week</b><br>For one wee
 k each month during Tournament Week\, you shoot for score and submit your s
 cores to Coach Racae. Score in your regular classes or come to the tourname
 nt on Tournament Saturday.<br><br><b>Tournament Saturday</b><br>On the last
  day of tournament week\, Saturday\, Coach Racae will conduct the Saturday 
 Outdoor 4-9 class as a tournament with timed rounds and scoring and little 
 to no coaching.&nbsp\;<br><br><b>Master Challenge</b><br>While you´re shoot
 ing in the tournament&nbsp\; Coach Racae will look at your form and assess 
 how much attention to form you can remember to do while shooting in a tourn
 ament. You can earn Mastered Tags for each step of the form you have consis
 tently done at your level. As you progress through higher levels\, the leve
 l of detail required will increase and additional positions will be added.<
 br><br><b>USA Archery Star Pins</b><br><b>If you are a member of USA Archer
 y</b>\, Tournament Saturday is often called a ¨Pin Shoot¨\, when you can ea
 rn your USA Archery Star Pins based on the scores you obtain. Look at the b
 ottom of your scorecard to see how many points you´ll need to receive a Sta
 r Pin.<br><br><b>Winners´ Pot and Fees</b><br>Archers participate in Tourna
 ment Week by entering one of the following tournaments and paying $5.00 tow
 ards the Winners´ Pot. Winners will be announced by email and Instagram fol
 lowing Tournament Saturday.&nbsp\;<br>Archers participating in Tournament S
 aturday or attending any Outdoor 2-9 classes will also pay $30 for their pl
 ace on the shooting line\, unless they also take virtual lessons once or tw
 ice a week with Coach Racae\, in which case\, their fee is $10.<br><br>Ente
 r one of these tournaments:<br><b>Outdoor 2 + 3 Tournament :&nbsp\;</b><br>
 For beginners at 9m and 13.5m - One or two rounds (depending on your streng
 th) of 10 ends of 3 arrows each for a total of 30 arrows.<br><b>Outdoor 4-9
  Tournament:&nbsp\;</b><br>For more advanced archers at 20m+ - Two rounds o
 f 6 ends of 6 arrows each for a total of 72 arrows shot on 122-cm target fa
 ces.<br><br>More information and registration links at&nbsp\;<a>www.archery
 trainingcenter.com</a>
