CREATED:20250808T205345Z
DESCRIPTION:The Outdoor Range will be open all winter to those who have qua
 lified (see below) and want to practice the longer distances. All classes n
 eed to be supervised by a USA Archery certified Level 2-4 Instructor or Coa
 ch. \n\n\nCoach Racae will be coaching Indoor 4-9 in the Indoor 18m range i
 n Westlake as indicated on the calendar\, until after the Indoor Nationals 
 in early February. She will also be coaching Indoor 2-6 in the 9m indoor ra
 nge as indicated on the calendar. \n\nRegistration form: OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.
 5m-70m\n\nREMINDER:  Everyone needs to come to at least one Training Class 
 per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (All indoor classes are traini
 ng classes.)\n\nIf you are not a coach/instructor\, the fees are:  \n    * 
 Outdoor Training Class (OTC): $52/class or multi-class pack \n    * Indoor 
 Training Class (ITC): $43/class or multi-class pack or unlimited pack\n    
 * Open Practice (OP): ($50/mo)  \n\nIf you are a coach/instructor\, you hav
 e received an email from Coach Racae outlining your fees.\n\nDuring the fal
 l (Aug 31-Dec 18)\, for Coach Racae to coach the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class
 \, at least 5 archers need to register by \n8:00 am on Thursdays (for Satur
 days) and \n8:00 am on Fridays (for Sundays) \nIn the case of low or late r
 egistrations or cancellations\, another coach/instructor\, when available\,
  will coach the session as a Training Class or oversee it as an Open Practi
 ce instead. If this is not possible\, then the class may need to be cancell
 ed.\n\nAdd your name to the Target Assignment List below or submit the abov
 e completed form.\nFocus primarily on perfecting your form\, \nslowly incre
 asing your physical strength and draw weight\, \nstrengthening your mental 
 program\, \ndetermining your average and personal best\, \nunderstanding th
 e spread between the two\, and working on closing it.\n\nYou need your own 
 equipment \nCompetition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\,
  12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, a
 rmguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, e
 tc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added until you reach a higher level\
 , but you should order them in advance.) \n\nWear your ATCI shirt to traini
 ng.\n\nWhen you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm target face
  you'll move back to the next distance until you reach your competition dis
 tance\nIf you trained outdoors in the 2024 season\, you'll return to the fa
 rthest distance you shot.\n\nTarget arrangements may vary each session\, de
 pending on who attends and distances needed.\nTarget 1 at 70m (U21 + Senior
 s competition distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use it for in
 dependent practice in between classes.\nTarget 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters comp
 etition distance) \nTarget 3 at 50m\nTarget 4+5 at 40m (U15 competition dis
 tance) \nTarget 6 at 30m (U13 competition distance) \n\nTargets 7-10 at 18m
  (for those wanting to qualify to shoot competitively at 18m indoors or wit
 h Coach Racae's approval)\n\nIdeally\, we want to practice with two archers
 /target to replicate outdoor competition conditions.\nAlternate daily: Outd
 oor distance and 18m distance. \nFor 18m distance\, put up four 40-cm targe
 t faces on one target\, even if fewer people are shooting the target\, so y
 ou practice high/low/left/right. \nFor 18m JOAD\, put up two 60cm target fa
 ces on one target side-by-side for max two people shooting on each target b
 ale.\nTarget Assignments:\nTargets are assigned outdoors in advance to redu
 ce confusion and delay on the day\,\nso add your name next to your distance
  below. \nIf you need help or have questions\, email/text Coach Racae\n(Dot
 ted lines represent tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)\n\n\nATCIIC
 T = 2026 ATCI Indoor Competition Team : \nMQS at 18m\, 30-arrow rounds: 210
  pts or 420 pts (2 rounds)----------------------------------\n1A. (70m)\n1B
