DESCRIPTION:If you have been with us for a while\, and have been given acce
 ss to the ATCI Calendar via an email from Coach Racae\, just add the archer
 ´s name under Registered Archers below.<br>For newer archers\, register usi
 ng the 2025 INDOOR 2-6 at 9m Registration form<br><br>SCHEDULE :<br>​Regist
 er for ​​as many as your schedule and budget allows to progress faster:<br>
 Sat/Sun 4:00-5:30 pm - <br>T/W/Th  5:00-6:30 pm  and  <br>T/W/Th   6:30-8\;
 :00 pm<br>​Weekdays: Juniors usually come to the 5:00 pm class\, and adults
  to the 6:30 class\, but all classes are open to both adults and juniors.<b
 r><br>Always check this calendar just before driving to class in case there
  are last-minutes changes or cancellations!<br><br>USA Archery Level 3 NTS 
 Coach Nicholas Erickson<br><br>After you graduate out of Indoor 1\, sign up
  for 2025 INDOOR 2-6 at 9m<br><br>Registered archers:<br><ol><li><b>Keane G
 .</b>\, 11\, pd - 1.5 hrs</li><li><b>Sophie B</b>.\, 11\, pd - $2 credit to
  her - 1.5 hrs</li><li><b>Colby K</b>.!!! adult USAA - to pay - 1.5 hrs</li
 ><li><b>Milvia A</b>.\, adult\, pd - 1.5 hrs</li><li><b>Trenton T</b>.\, ad
 ult\, pd - 1.5 hrs</li><li><b>Kelsey T</b>.\, adult\, ps - 1.5 hrs</li></ol
 ><i>Worked on expansion and aim with all.  For newer archers keane and Soph
 ie worked on aim point and adjusting it.  Worked a bit on “expansion” and h
 ow it feeds into follow thru.  Hand behind draw elbow. <br><br>Kelsey and M
 ilvia it was about how to adjust sight and setting eye dominance for aiming
 .  Also hand behind elbow on follow thru as a feedback for a strong expansi
 on. <br><br>Colby and Trenton creating a strong expansion to create a stron
 g shot.  Helps flatten out arrow flight. But being careful that you aren’t 
 expanding to exhaustion. <br></i><br>SINGLE Class Fees per archer for one I
 ndoor 2-6 class:<br>$31 for 1 hr (arrive 30 min after class starts or leave
  30 min before class ends)<br>$43 for 1.5 hrs<br><br>MULTI-Class Discount P
 ackets<br>  9 hours : $250 (six 1.5-hr classes)<br> 12 hours : $320 (eight 
 1.5-hr classes)<br> 18 hours : $460 (twelve 1.5-hr classes) <br><br>There a
 re 8 places on the shooting line\, and we sometimes have double lines depen
 ding on attendance.<br><br>Sign in/out upon arrival/departure<br>For single
  classes\, book and pay in advance.<br>For multi-class discount packs\, pay
  in advance and book when you are sure of the dates.<br>Coaching and whistl
 e commands at all times.<br>Instruction in the National Training System.<br
 >Unfair games depending on attendance.<br><br>Please note: Youths &lt\;12 y
 .o. should not shoot more than 100 arrows/day!<br><br>Prerequisites for Ind
 oor 2: <br>Adults: No min. score in Indoor 1 <br>Juniors: 50 pts in Indoor 
 1<br>Scores needed at 9m to advance to Indoor 3-6 and Outdoor 3-6:<br><br> 
                 On 40-cm                  On 60-cm<br>               target
  face                 target face<br>Indoor 3:          230 pts            
     240 pts           -&gt\; Outdoor 3 at 13.5m<br>Indoor 4:          250 p
 ts                260 pts           -&gt\; Outdoor 4 at 18m/20m<br>Indoor 5
 :          270 pts                280 pts           -&gt\; Outdoor 5 at 30m
 <br>Indoor 6:          290 pts                300 pts          -&gt\;  Outd
 oor 6 at 40m
