CREATED:20260129T073448Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><b>WINTER TRAINING PROGRAM - 11 weeks (Jan 3 - Mar 22)</b> <
 /p><p>We will go through the <b>National Training System (NTS) 11 Steps of 
 Shooting</b> and <b>Building Your Mental Program</b> step-by-step during th
 e regular training classes\, covering each one in sequence during the follo
 wing weeks.. </p><p>Learning\, understanding and doing the NTS and building
  a strong mental program are ongoing quests that all archers are continuous
 ly trying to achieve - even at the highest levels !</p><p><b><i>What if you
  miss some of the weeks?</i></b><i>  </i>We'll do our best to catch you up 
 during your next sessions. </p><p><b><i>Also see more important notes below
 \, under the schedule.</i></b></p><p><b>JANUARY</b></p><ul><li><p><b>  Sat 
 Jan 3 - F 9</b>       <b>WELCOME </b>!  Understanding  <b>NTS CONCEPTS</b> 
 especially TRANSFER + <span>NTS Step 1</span><b> STANCE</b></p></li><li><p>
 <b>  Sat 10- F 16  </b><span>NTS Step 2</span><span> </span><b> NOCK +  </b
 ><span>NTS Step 3</span><span> </span><b>HOOK &amp\; GRIP </b><span>+ Build
 ing Your Mental Program</span></p></li><li><p>  <b>Sat 17 - F 23</b>  NTS S
 tep 4<b> SET + </b>Building Your Mental Program</p></li><li><p><b>  Sat 24 
 - F 30 </b><span>NTS Step 5 </span><b>SET-UP +</b><span> Building Your Ment
 al Program</span></p></li></ul><p><b>FEBRUARY</b></p><ul><li><p><b>  Sat 31
  - F 6 </b><span>NTS Step 6 </span><b>DRAW</b><span> to </span><b>LOAD </b>
 <span>+ Building Your Mental Program</span></p></li><li><p>  <b>Sat 7 - F 1
 3  </b><span>NTS Step 7 </span><b>ANCHOR </b><span>+ Building Your Mental P
 rogram</span></p></li><li><p><b>  Sat 4 - F 20</b>  <span>NTS Step 8</span>
 <b> </b><b> TRANSFER to HOLD </b><span>+ Building Your Mental Program</span
 ></p></li><li><p>  <b>Sat 21 - F 27  </b>N<span>TS Step 9</span><b> </b><b>
 EXPAND / AIM + </b><span>Building Your Mental Program</span></p></li></ul><
 p><b>MARCH</b></p><ul><li><p><b>Sat 28 - F 6  </b><span>NTS Step 10 </span>
 <b>RELEASE / FOLLOW-THROUGH </b><b>+</b><span> Building Your Mental Program
 </span></p></li><li><p><b>Sat 7 - F 13  </b><span>NTS Step 11 </span><b>FEE
 DBACK +</b><span> Building Your Mental Program</span></p></li><li><p><b>Sat
  14 - F 20 </b> <b>Putting it All Together</b></p></li><li><p><b>Sat 21 + S
 un 22  </b><b>SCORING WEEKEND - </b><b>ATCI MONTHLY COMPETITION and STAR PI
 N SHOOT</b></p></li></ul><p><b>INTRO</b></p><p><i>Each week the focus of yo
 ur lessons will be on one or two particular </i><b><i>Steps of Shooting of 
 the NTS (National Training System) </i></b><i>shot cycle\, to help you focu
 s and improve your form\, which\, as we all know\, leads to greater and mor
 e consistent precision (tight groups of arrows) and ultimately greater accu
 racy (tight groups of arrows dead center)</i>. <i>Concurrently you will be 
 learning how to build a </i><b><i>strong mental program</i></b><i>\, which 
 will improve your focus\, awareness and confidence for competitions later.<
 /i></p><p><i>The NTS is the </i><b><i>most biomechanically efficient and le
 ast injurious method of shooting</i></b><i>\, and is highly and continuousl
 y researched out at the Elite Athletes Center in Chula Vista\, CA. It is wh
 at the Olympians do!</i></p><p><i>The 11 NTS Steps are cumulative with each
  step most successfully completed if the previous steps have been completed
  well. As you reach higher levels\, you will learn the NTS Steps in progres
 sively greater detail.</i></p><p><b>Goals by the end of the winter semester
  (March 22)</b></p><p>Make a list of what you want to accomplish by the end
  of the semester. Email it to Coach Racae\, so you can discuss it together.
  </p><p>Confidence and consistency in form and mind are your two main goals
 . Replicate the NTS step(s) mindfully and consistently on every shot\, and 
 build a strong mental program that is consistent on every shot. </p><p>Your
  conscious mind commands your subconscious mind to put your body into posit
 ion\, after you train your body to be in those positions. When you stay in 
 the present\, just doing what you need to do as you need to do it\, your co
 nscious mind will be occupied\, instead of random thoughts entering your he
 ad or you being distracted by emotional or environmental elements. </p><p>Y
 ou´ll need to build up your mental program alongside your form knowledge\, 
 so when your body is trained to shoot excellent shots\, your self image and
  subconscious support you\, instead of undermining you. </p><p><i>Improving
  your training\, practicing\, and competition components\, process\, and sk
 ills is a perpetual lifetime quest\, which you´ll slowly learn to love. You
 ´ll  realize what is under your control\, and you'll become your own best c
 oach! Those who find all this fun and enjoy the journey are the ones who wi
 n - the champions!</i></p><p><i>I know you can do it -  I'm your biggest fa
 n!</i></p><p><i>​I'm also really looking forward to seeing you improve\, su
 cceed\, and thrive !​</i></p><p><b><i>                                     
               Coach Racae<br></i></b></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260517T082125Z
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:FORM FOCUS for INDOOR 2-6
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
