CREATED:20250808T205345Z
DESCRIPTION:Registration form: OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m<br><br>REMINDER:  E
 veryone needs to come to at least one Training Class per week to be able to
  attend Open Practice. (All indoor classes are training classes.)<br><br>If
  you are not a coach/instructor\, the fees are:  <br>    * Outdoor Training
  Class (OTC): $52/class or multi-class pack <br>    * Indoor Training Class
  (ITC): $43/class or multi-class pack or unlimited pack<br>    * Open Pract
 ice (OP): ($50/mo)  <br><br>If you are a coach/instructor\, you have receiv
 ed an email from Coach Racae outlining your fees.<br><br>During the fall (A
 ug 31-Dec 18)\, for Coach Racae to coach the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class\, a
 t least 5 archers need to register by <br>8:00 am on Thursdays (for Saturda
 ys) and <br>8:00 am on Fridays (for Sundays) <br>In the case of low or late
  registrations or cancellations\, another coach/instructor\, when available
 \, will coach the session as a Training Class or oversee it as an Open Prac
 tice instead. If this is not possible\, then the class may need to be cance
 lled.<br><br>Add your name to the Target Assignment List below or submit th
 e above completed form.<br>Focus primarily on perfecting your form\, <br>sl
 owly increasing your physical strength and draw weight\, <br>strengthening 
 your mental program\, <br>determining your average and personal best\, <br>
 understanding the spread between the two\, and working on closing it.<br><b
 r>You need your own equipment <br>Competition recurve bow\, sight\, stabili
 zer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker
 \, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field qui
 ver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added until you
  reach a higher level\, but you should order them in advance.) <br><br>Wear
  your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow r
 ound on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the next distance until 
 you reach your competition distance<br>If you trained outdoors in the 2024 
 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.<br><br>Target arr
 angements may vary each session\, depending on who attends and distances ne
 eded.<br>Target 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should always
  stay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent practice in between classes
 .<br>Target 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition distance) <br>Target 3 at 5
 0m<br>Target 4+5 at 40m (U15 competition distance) <br>Target 6 at 30m (U13
  competition distance) <br>Targets 7-10 at 18m (for those wanting to qualif
 y to shoot competitively at 18m indoors or with Coach Racae's approval)<br>
 <br>Ideally\, we want to practice with two archers/target to replicate outd
 oor competition conditions.<br>Alternate daily: Outdoor distance and 18m di
 stance. <br>For 18m distance\, put up four 40-cm target faces on one target
 \, even if fewer people are shooting the target\, so you practice high/low/
 left/right. <br>For 18m JOAD\, put up two 60cm target faces on one target s
 ide-by-side for max two people shooting on each target bale.<br>Target Assi
 gnments:<br>Targets are assigned outdoors in advance to reduce confusion an
 d delay on the day\, so add your name next to your distance below. <br>    
 * The MQS for 2026 ATCI Indoor Competition Team is 210 pts at 18m on either
  60cm target face (U13 and U15) or 40cm target face (U18\, U21\,Seniors (21
