DESCRIPTION:<br><i>The Outdoor Range will be open all winter to those who h
 ave qualified (see below) and want to practice the longer distances. All cl
 asses need to be supervised by a USA Archery certified Level 2-4 Instructor
  or Coach. </i><br><i><br></i><br><i>Coach Racae will be coaching Indoor 4-
 9 in the Indoor 18m range in Westlake as indicated on the calendar\, until 
 after the Indoor Nationals in early February. She will also be coaching Ind
 oor 2-6 in the 9m indoor range as indicated on the calendar. </i><br><br>Re
 gistration form: OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m<br><br><b>REMINDER</b>:  Everyone
  needs to come to at least one Training Class per week to be able to attend
  Open Practice. (All indoor classes are training classes.)<br><br>If you ar
 e not a coach/instructor\, the fees are:  <ul><li><b>Outdoor Training Class
  (OTC)</b>: $52/class or multi-class pack </li><li><b>Indoor Training Class
  (ITC)</b>: $43/class or multi-class pack or unlimited pack</li><li><b>Open
  Practice (OP)</b>: ($50/mo)  </li></ul><br>If you are a coach/instructor\,
  you have received an email from Coach Racae outlining your fees.<br><br>Du
 ring the fall (Aug 31-Dec 18)\, for Coach Racae to coach the Outdoor 3-9 Tr
 aining Class\, at least 5 archers need to register by <br>8:00 am on Thursd
 ays (for Saturdays) and <br>8:00 am on Fridays (for Sundays) <br>In the cas
 e of low or late registrations or cancellations\, another coach/instructor\
 , when available\, will coach the session as a Training Class or oversee it
  as an Open Practice instead. If this is not possible\, then the class may 
 need to be cancelled.<br><br>Add your name to the Target Assignment List be
 low or submit the above completed form.<br>Focus primarily on perfecting yo
 ur form\, <br>slowly increasing your physical strength and draw weight\, <b
 r>strengthening your mental program\, <br>determining your average and pers
 onal best\, <br>understanding the spread between the two\, and working on c
 losing it.<br><br>You need your own equipment <br>Competition recurve bow\,
  sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar as
 sembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, 
 hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be
  added until you reach a higher level\, but you should order them in advanc
 e.) <br><br>Wear your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br>When you score 288 pts
  in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the next
  distance until you reach your competition distance<br>If you trained outdo
 ors in the 2024 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.<b
 r><br>Target arrangements may vary each session\, depending on who attends 
 and distances needed.<br>Target 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distanc
 e) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent practice in
  between classes.<br>Target 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition distance) <
 br>Target 3 at 50m<br>Target 4+5 at 40m (U15 competition distance) <br>Targ
 et 6 at 30m (U13 competition distance) <br><br>Targets 7-10 at 18m (for tho
 se wanting to qualify to shoot competitively at 18m indoors or with Coach R
 acae's approval)<br><br>Ideally\, we want to practice with two archers/targ
 et to replicate outdoor competition conditions.<br><b>Alternate daily</b>: 
 Outdoor distance and 18m distance. <br>For <b>18m distance</b>\, put up <b>
 four 40-cm target faces on one target</b>\, even if fewer people are shooti
 ng the target\, so you practice high/low/left/right. <br>For <b>18m JOAD</b
 >\, put up <b>two 60cm target faces on one target side-by-side</b> for max 
 two people shooting on each target bale.<br>Target Assignments:<br>Targets 
 are assigned outdoors in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\,
 <br>so add your name next to your distance below. <br>If you need help or h
 ave questions\, email/text Coach Racae<br>(Dotted lines represent tent pole
 s dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)<br><br><br><b>ATCIICT = 2026 ATCI Indoor
  Competition Team : </b><br><b>MQS at 18m\, 30-arrow rounds: 210 pts or 420
  pts (2 rounds)</b>----------------------------------<br>1A. (70m)<br>1B<br
 ><br>2A. (60m)  <br>2B<br><br>3A. (50m)  <br>------------------------------
 ----<br>3B<br><br>4A. (40m) <br>4B. <br>----------------------------------<
 br>5A. (40m)<br>5B. <br><br>6A. (30m)<br>----------------------------------
 <br>6B. <br><br>7A. (18m)<br>7B. <br>---------------------------------- <br
 >8A. (18m)<br>8B. <br><br>9A. (18m)<br>----------------------------------<b
 r>9B. <br><br>10A. (18m)<br>10B
