DESCRIPTION:<b>Registration form: </b><a href="https://docs.google.com/form
 s/d/e/1FAIpQLSfx1RyOwd314Q4zXYiQ9rb_a3oe84E9dIYs8CN35Ginmevfpg/viewform?usp
 =preview" target="_blank"><u>OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m</u></a><br><br><b>Add
  your name to Target Assignment List below or send in the above completed f
 orm.</b><br><br><i>Focus primarily on <br></i><ul><li><i>perfecting your fo
 rm\, </i></li><li><i>slowly increasing your physical strength and draw weig
 ht\, </i></li><li><i>strengthening your mental program\, </i></li><li><i>de
 termining your average and personal best\, </i></li><li><i>understanding th
 e spread between the two\, and working on closing it.</i></li></ul><b>You n
 eed your own equipment </b><br>Competition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer
 \, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, 
 chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver
 \, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added until you re
 ach a higher level\, but you should order them in advance.) <br><br>Wear yo
 ur ATCI shirt to training.<br><br><i>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow r
 ound on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the next distance until 
 you reach your competition distance</i><br><i>If you trained outdoors in th
 e 2024 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.</i><br><i>
 Target arrangements may vary each session\, depending on who attends and di
 stances needed.</i><br><b>Target 1 at 70m</b> (U21 + Seniors competition di
 stance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent practi
 ce in between classes.<br><b>Target 2 at 60m</b> (U18 + Masters competition
  distance) <br><b>Target 3 at 50m</b><br><b>Targets 4+5 at 40m </b>(U15 com
 petition distance) <br><b>Targets 6\, 7\, 8 at 30m</b> (U13 competition dis
 tance) <br><b>Target 9 at 20m</b> (for those who have shot at 18m indoors o
 r with Coach Racae's approval)<br><b>Targets 10 at 13.5m</b> (for those who
  have just graduated from indoors at 9m)<br><br>Ideally\, we want to practi
 ce with two archers/target to replicate competition conditions as much as p
 ossible.<br><br><b>Target Assignments:</b><br>Targets are assigned outdoors
  in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\,<br>so add your name 
 next to your distance below. <br>If you need help or have questions\, email
