DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20251018T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20251018T113000
DTSTAMP:20261004T164459Z
UID:7h7d0rp4steh1al545m919e8et_R20250921T140000@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Chicago:20251018T090000
CREATED:20250808T205345Z
DESCRIPTION:Registration form: OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m<br><br>REMINDER:  E
 veryone needs to come to at least one Training Class per week to be able to
  attend Open Practice. (All indoor classes are training classes.)<br><br>If
  you are not a coach/instructor\, the fees are:  <br>    * Outdoor Training
  Class (OTC): $52/class or multi-class pack <br>    * Indoor Training Class
  (ITC): $43/class or multi-class pack or unlimited pack<br>    * Open Pract
 ice (OP): ($50/mo)  <br><br><br>If you are a coach/instructor\, you have re
 ceived an email from Coach Racae outlining your fees.<br><br>During the fal
 l (Aug 31-Dec 18)\, for Coach Racae to coach the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class
 \, at least 5 archers need to register by <br>8:00 am on Thursdays (for Sat
 urdays) and <br>8:00 am on Fridays (for Sundays) <br>In the case of low or 
 late registrations or cancellations\, another coach/instructor\, when avail
 able\, will coach the session as a Training Class or oversee it as an Open 
 Practice instead. If this is not possible\, then the class may need to be c
 ancelled.<br><br>Add your name to the Target Assignment List below or submi
 t the above completed form.<br>Focus primarily on perfecting your form\, <b
 r>slowly increasing your physical strength and draw weight\, <br>strengthen
 ing your mental program\, <br>determining your average and personal best\, 
 <br>understanding the spread between the two\, and working on closing it.<b
 r><br>You need your own equipment <br>Competition recurve bow\, sight\, sta
 bilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, cli
 cker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field
  quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added until
  you reach a higher level\, but you should order them in advance.) <br><br>
 Wear your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arr
 ow round on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the next distance un
 til you reach your competition distance<br>If you trained outdoors in the 2
 024 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.<br><br>Target
  arrangements may vary each session\, depending on who attends and distance
 s needed.<br>Target 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should al
 ways stay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent practice in between cla
 sses.<br>Target 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition distance) <br>Target 3 
 at 50m<br>Target 4+5 at 40m (U15 competition distance) <br>Target 6 at 30m 
 (U13 competition distance) <br><br>Targets 7-10 at 18m (for those wanting t
 o qualify to shoot competitively at 18m indoors or with Coach Racae's appro
 val)<br><br>Ideally\, we want to practice with two archers/target to replic
 ate outdoor competition conditions.<br>Alternate daily: Outdoor distance an
 d 18m distance. <br>For 18m distance\, put up four 40-cm target faces on on
 e target\, even if fewer people are shooting the target\, so you practice h
 igh/low/left/right. <br>For 18m JOAD\, put up two 60cm target faces on one 
 target side-by-side for max two people shooting on each target bale.<br>Tar
 get Assignments:<br>Targets are assigned outdoors in advance to reduce conf
 usion and delay on the day\,<br>so add your name next to your distance belo
