  Racae. Score in your regular classes or come to the tournament on Tourname
 nt Saturday.<br><br><b>Tournament Saturday</b><br>On the last day of tourna
 ment week\, Saturday\, Coach Racae will conduct the Saturday Outdoor 4-9 cl
 ass as a tournament with timed rounds and scoring and little to no coaching
 .&nbsp\;<br><br><b>Master Challenge</b><br>While you´re shooting in the tou
 rnament&nbsp\; Coach Racae will look at your form and assess how much atten
 tion to form you can remember to do while shooting in a tournament. You can
  earn Mastered Tags for each step of the form you have consistently done at
  your level. As you progress through higher levels\, the level of detail re
 quired will increase and additional positions will be added.<br><br><b>USA 
 Archery Star Pins</b><br><b>If you are a member of USA Archery</b>\, Tourna
 ment Saturday is often called a ¨Pin Shoot¨\, when you can earn your USA Ar
 chery Star Pins based on the scores you obtain. Look at the bottom of your 
 scorecard to see how many points you´ll need to receive a Star Pin.<br><br>
 <b>Winners´ Pot and Fees</b><br>Archers participate in Tournament Week by e
 ntering one of the following tournaments and paying $5.00 towards the Winne
 rs´ Pot. Winners will be announced by email and Instagram following Tournam
 ent Saturday.&nbsp\;<br>Archers participating in Tournament Saturday or att
 ending any Outdoor 2-9 classes will also pay $30 for their place on the sho
 oting line\, unless they also take virtual lessons once or twice a week wit
 h Coach Racae\, in which case\, their fee is $10.<br><br>Enter one of these
  tournaments:<br><b>Outdoor 2 + 3 Tournament :&nbsp\;</b><br>For beginners 
 at 9m and 13.5m - One or two rounds (depending on your strength) of 10 ends
  of 3 arrows each for a total of 30 arrows.<br><b>Outdoor 4-9 Tournament:&n
 bsp\;</b><br>For more advanced archers at 20m+ - Two rounds of 6 ends of 6 
 arrows each for a total of 72 arrows shot on 122-cm target faces.<br><br>Mo
 re information and registration links at&nbsp\;<a>www.archerytrainingcenter
 .com</a>
