DESCRIPTION:This class has been moved to the indoor range due to rainy weat
 her and the field being soggy muddy. We'll shoot two rounds of 30 arrows at
  3 arrows/end getting ready for the Aggie Invite!<br><br>REMINDER:  Everyon
 e needs to come to at least one Training Class per week to be able to atten
 d Open Practice. (All indoor classes are training classes.)<br><br>If you a
 re not a coach/instructor\, the fees are:  <br>Outdoor Training Class (OTC)
 : $52/class or multi-class pack <br>Indoor Training Class (ITC): $43/class 
 or multi-class pack or unlimited pack<br>Open Practice (OP): ($50/mo)  <br>
 If you are a coach/instructor\, you have received an email from Coach Racae
  outlining your fees.<br><br>During the fall (Aug 31-Dec 18)\, for Coach Ra
 cae to coach the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class\, at least 5 archers need to re
 gister by <br>8:00 am on Thursdays (for Saturdays) and <br>8:00 am on Frida
 ys (for Sundays) <br>In the case of low or late registrations or cancellati
 ons\, another coach/instructor\, when available\, will coach the session as
  a Training Class or oversee it as an Open Practice instead. If this is not
  possible\, then the class may need to be cancelled.<br><br>Add your name t
 o the Target Assignment List below or submit the above completed form.<br>F
 ocus primarily on perfecting your form\, <br>slowly increasing your physica
 l strength and draw weight\, <br>strengthening your mental program\, <br>de
 termining your average and personal best\, <br>understanding the spread bet
 ween the two\, and working on closing it.<br><br>You need your own equipmen
 t <br>Competition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 ca
 rbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguar
 d\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (C
 licker and side rods may not be added until you reach a higher level\, but 
 you should order them in advance.) <br><br>Wear your ATCI shirt to training
 .<br><br>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm target fa
 ce you'll move back to the next distance until you reach your competition d
 istance<br>If you trained outdoors in the 2024 season\, you'll return to th
 e farthest distance you shot.<br><br>Target arrangements may vary each sess
 ion\, depending on who attends and distances needed.<br>Target 1 at 70m (U2
 1 + Seniors competition distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use
  it for independent practice in between classes.<br>Target 2 at 60m (U18 + 
 Masters competition distance) <br>Target 3 at 50m<br>Target 4+5 at 40m (U15
  competition distance) <br>Target 6 at 30m (U13 competition distance) <br><
 br>Targets 7-10 at 18m (for those wanting to qualify to shoot competitively
  at 18m indoors or with Coach Racae's approval)<br><br>Ideally\, we want to
  practice with two archers/target to replicate outdoor competition conditio
 ns.<br>Alternate daily: Outdoor distance and 18m distance. <br>For 18m dist
 ance\, put up four 40-cm target faces on one target\, even if fewer people 
 are shooting the target\, so you practice high/low/left/right. <br>For 18m 
 JOAD\, put up two 60cm target faces on one target side-by-side for max two 
 people shooting on each target bale.<br>Target Assignments:<br>Targets are 
 assigned outdoors in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\,<br>
 so add your name next to your distance below. <br>If you need help or have 
 questions\, email/text Coach Racae<br>(Dotted lines represent tent poles di
 viding Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)<br><br>ATCIICT = 2026 ATCI Indoor Competitio
 n Team : <br>MQS at 18m\, 30-arrow rounds: 210 pts or 420 pts (2 rounds)<br
 >Abby<br>Instr. Adrianne<br>Instr. Anna<br>Instr. Colby<br>Emma<br>Finn<br>
 Coach Joel<br>Luke<br>Coach Nick<br>Sara <br>Instr. Sophia<br>-------------
 ---------------------<br>1A. (70m)<br>1B<br><br>2A. (60m)  <br>2B<br><br>3A
 . (50m)  <br>----------------------------------<br>3B<br><br>4A. (40m) <br>
 4B. <br>----------------------------------<br>5A. (40m)<br>5B. <br><br>6A. 
 (18m)<br>----------------------------------<br>6B. <br><br>7A. (18m)<b> Col
 by K.</b>(sick) <b>DNA</b><br>7B. <b>Adrianne M</b>. : 40cm @9m  278+276 = 
 <b>554 pts </b>- 3 hrs<br>---------------------------------- <br>8A. (18m) 
 <b>Emma A</b>.\, 13\, USAA\, pd 40cm @9m  =264+273 = <b>537 pts </b>- 3 hrs
 <br>8B. <br><br>9A. (18m) <b>Matt L</b>\, 13\, USAA\, pd = 266+270 = <b>536
  pts - </b>3 hrs<br>----------------------------------<br>9B. <b>Finn E</b>
 \, 13\, USAA\, = 40cm @9m = 254 (corrected)+263 = <b>517 pts </b>3 hrs<br><
 br>10A. (18m) <b>Nick E </b>40cm @9m : 281+291 = <b>572 pts</b> - 3 hrs<br>
 10B <b>Rhys E</b> DNS - 3 hrs
