DESCRIPTION:Registered Archers:<br>1.&nbsp\;<br>2.&nbsp\;<br>3.<br>4..<br>5
 .<br>6.<br>7.<br>8.<br>9.<br>10.<br><br>OVERVIEW:<br>These Outdoor Target A
 rchery recreational classes prepare you to shoot at longer and longer dista
 nces until you reach your USA Archery tournament distance (see below)\, whi
 le learning the National Training System\, which is the most highly researc
 hed biomechanical method of shooting taught out at the Olympic Training Cen
 ter. You will be shooting with other archers in group sessions\, so you can
  all learn together and from each other. <br><br>PREREQUISITE: <br>Some arc
 hery experience and your own recurve archery equipment is required.<br><br>
 OPEN TO ADULTS / JUNIORS / PARENTS (with experience and own recurve archery
  equipment)<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on
  the field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae.<br>Space will b
 e limited to a maximum of 10 archers per session or in accordance with CDC 
 Guidelines.<br><br>NO DROP INS:<br>You cannot just drop in\, because the nu
 mber of archers on the shooting line is very limited and we are observing C
 DC guidelines with social distancing.<br><br>DATES:    Start Dates: MAY 15 
 (Adults) or JUNE 12 (Juniors 10+) <br>&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&n
 bsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;Ending Date:  
 AUGUST 14  <br><br>ADDRESSES:<br>OUTDOOR FIELD SOUTH:    2310 Bliss Spillar
  Road\, Manchaca\, TX 78652<br>MAILING:  Archery Training Center\, Inc.\, P
 O Box 93216\, Austin\, TX 78709<br><br>E-MAIL: <a href="mailto:archerytrain
 ingcenteraustin@gmail.com">archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a><br><br
 >PHONE/TEXT:  512 975 1850<br><br>CAPACITY:    10 archers per class or in a
 ccordance with CDC guidelines<br>AGES:             10 - 80+ years old (See 
 start dates above)<br>DISTANCES:  9m\, 13.5m\, 18m\, 20m-70m<br>BOWS:      
      Recurves  <br>(If you are not a recurve archer\, but would like to lea
 rn to shoot a recurve bow\, please stay tuned to our Instagram for announce
 ments of the re-opening of our in-person First-time Classes\, or register o
 nline for a few Virtual NTS Form classes with Coach Racae.)<br><br>EQUIPMEN
 T: <br>These classes are for archers who have their own equipment\, consist
 ing of at least a recurve bow\, 12 aluminum or carbon arrows\, armguard\, f
 inger tab\, hip or field quiver.  (If you need to change your equipment or 
 order your own\, please contact Coach Racae at <a href="mailto:archerytrain
 ingcenteraustin@gmail.com">archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a>. She w
 ill specify what you´ll need and help you order it\, so you buy the correct
  equipment for your strength and experience.)<br><br>INSTRUCTOR / COACH:<br
 >USA Archery Level 2 Instructor Ted Aanstoos  <br><br>CLASS TIMES:<br>These
  are the days/times that are available to you. (Additional sessions will be
  added in future.)<br><br>SAT:     9:00-10:30pm <br>WED:    9:00-10:30pm <b
 r>Please check <a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/calendar">www.
 archerytrainingcenter.com/calendar</a> before registering!<br><br>DAYS CLOS
 ED: <br>The outdoor range is closed\, gates locked\, and targets stored awa
 y except during the above class times.<br><br>ENROLLMENT IS ON A FIRST-RECE
 IVED AND PAID BASIS.<br>Complete the Outdoor Target Archery Registration Fo
 rm under Adults or Juniors at <a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com
 ">www.archerytrainingcenter.com</a><br><br>ATTENDANCE RECOMMENDATIONS: <br>
 Recreational archers have no attendance requirements\, but we would recomme
 nd attending at least twice a week to improve faster. <br><br>FEES: <br>All
  fees are payable in advance of the class to secure your place in the class
 . <br>$30/archer for each 1.5-hr training session  OR <br>$115/mo (for 1 tr
 aining session/week) OR <br>$213/mo (for 2 training sessions/week)<br>+ Enr
 ollment fee: $20 (always due once per semester) <br><br>WEATHER:<br>Archers
  need to practice in all weather\, except when there is lightning. <br><br>
 REFUNDS\, CREDITS\, and SUBSTITUTIONS:<br>Substitutions or credits will be 
 applied if we cancel a class due to weather conditions or instructor illnes
 s or if the 24-hr notice is met.<br>There are no refunds for paid classes m
 issed during the summer\, except in the case of injury\, long-term illness\
 , unforeseen move out of the Austin area\, or being expelled for a safety v
 iolation. <br><br>24-HR NOTICE: <br>If you let us know within 24 hours of t
 he class that you will miss the class\, you can substitute another class an
 d use your fee as long as there are places left in that class during the se
 mester. If you notify us less than 24 hours in advance of the class that yo
 u will need to cancel (except for sudden illness)\, or you do a "no-show"\,
  you'll forfeit your fee.<br><br>ILLNESS or INJURY: In the case of physical
  injury or long-term illness\, we require a doctor's note saying that you a
 re unable to practice archery\, and then a doctor's note saying that you ar
 e again fit to return to archery\, before you will be allowed back in class
  or a refund/credit issued.<br><br>MEMBERSHIP IN USA ARCHERY:<br>Membership
  in USA Archery is now REQUIRED to participate in JOAD and Adult Training.<
 br>You can attend 2 sessions before joining USAA\, but then we'll need to s
 ee your membership card BEFORE WE CAN HAND OUT ANY USA ARCHERY STAR PINS to
  you during Master Challenge Weeks! <br>If you would like to see the benefi
 ts of USAA membership: <a href="http://www.teamusa.org/USA-Archery/Membersh
 ip/Membership-Benefits">http://www.teamusa.org/USA-Archery/Membership/Membe
 rship-Benefits</a><br>JOIN USA ARCHERY: <a href="https://www.usarchery.org/
 memberships/become-a-member">https://www.usarchery.org/memberships/become-a
 -member</a><br><br>SAFE SPORTS:<br>PARENTS PLEASE NOTE: We are part of the 
 US Olympic Committee's Safe Sport program\, so we minimally require one oth
 er adult besides the instructor to be present at all times. Please plan to 
 stay with your child or take turns with other parents staying whenever nece
 ssary to fulfill this requirement. THANKS!<br><br>SIGN AND RETURN THESE OUT
 DOOR WAIVERS:<br>The following documents and waivers will be part of your R
 egistration and Waiver Packet. You will need to sign these  documents befor
 e we add your name to those shooting in the class:<br>o Membership Form<br>
 o Safety Rules <br>o Release of Liability Waiver<br>o Supervision Policy (U
 nder 18)<br>o Medical Release  <br>o Photo/Video Release<br>o COVID-19 Guid
 elines<br>o Outdoor Field Rules of Participation <br><br>VACCINATIONS:<br>W
 e do not at this time require archers to be vaccinated\, but we would like 
 to know if you have been\, so we can take it into consideration when decidi
 ng on issues such as masks and social distancing and abiding by the CDC Gui
 delines. All our instructors have been fully vaccinated of their own accord
 .<br><br>QUESTIONS?<br>E-mail us at <a href="mailto:archerytrainingcenterau
 stin@gmail.com">archerytrainingcenteraustin@gmail.com</a> or<br>Call/Text u
 s at 512 975 1850 <br><br>*NTS = National Training System (which is used fo
 r training the USA Olympic team!)<br>*JDT = Junior Dream Team (top 20 Junio
 r archers in the USA!)<br>*JOAD = Junior Olympic Archery Development
