DESCRIPTION:Once a month until October 18\,&nbsp\; Outdoor 2+3 can register
  for Tournament Saturday at&nbsp\;<a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/
 e/1FAIpQLSeXKGqxUPCkcYHxJgXLxz62jkCFDOFvJswqN_cthIWgsBps7g/viewform">ATCI V
 irtual Monthly Tournament</a><br><br>To register for this class usually\, y
 ou will have already completed and graduated out of Outdoor 1: First-time C
 lass\, Outdoor 2 at 9m\, and Outdoor 3 at 13.5m\, and your distance will be
  at least 20m. Register here:&nbsp\;<a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/
 d/e/1FAIpQLSfF-EGKsMPSlfPLuLe3aLkqThTFZs0qqb8zleJ_0W3B6Xn7mA/viewform">2021
  Outdoor 4-9 at 20m-70m</a><br><br>Registered Archers:<br>Target Nos:<br>1.
  Richard F.\, adult @70m on 122cm target face<br>2. Sarah X.\, 14\, @50m on
  122cm target face<br>3. Kevin B.\, @ 30m on 122cm target face&nbsp\;<br>4.
  Lily R.\, @ 30m on 60cm target face&nbsp\;<br>5. Emma W.\, 14 @ 20m on 122
 cm target fact<br>6. Cyrenna V.\, adult @ 13.5m on 122cm target face<br>7. 
 Elizabeth M.\,13\, @9m on 60cm target face - admitted until 10/16<br>8. Mil
 a M.\, 13\, @9m on 60cm target face - admitted until 10/16&nbsp\;<br>9. Kis
 hore P.\, 13\, @9m on 60cm target face - admitted until 10/16<br>10. Victor
  C.\, 9\, @9m on 60cm target face - admitted until 10/16<br><br><b>Tourname
 nt Week</b><br>For one week each month during Tournament Week\, you shoot f
 or score and submit your scores to Coach Racae. Score in your regular class
 es or come to the tournament on Tournament Saturday.<br><br><b>Tournament S
 aturday</b><br>On the last day of tournament week\, Saturday\, Coach Racae 
 will conduct the Saturday Outdoor 4-9 class as a tournament with timed roun
 ds and scoring and little to no coaching.&nbsp\;<br><br><b>Master Challenge
 </b><br>While you´re shooting in the tournament&nbsp\; Coach Racae will loo
 k at your form and assess how much attention to form you can remember to do
  while shooting in a tournament. You can earn Mastered Tags for each step o
 f the form you have consistently done at your level. As you progress throug
 h higher levels\, the level of detail required will increase and additional
  positions will be added.<br><br><b>USA Archery Star Pins</b><br><b>If you 
 are a member of USA Archery</b>\, Tournament Saturday is often called a ¨Pi
 n Shoot¨\, when you can earn your USA Archery Star Pins based on the scores
  you obtain. Look at the bottom of your scorecard to see how many points yo
 u´ll need to receive a Star Pin.<br><br><b>Winners´ Pot and Fees</b><br>Arc
 hers participate in Tournament Week by entering one of the following tourna
 ments and paying $5.00 towards the Winners´ Pot. Winners will be announced 
 by email and Instagram following Tournament Saturday.&nbsp\;<br>Archers par
 ticipating in Tournament Saturday or attending any Outdoor 2-9 classes will
  also pay $30 for their place on the shooting line\, unless they also take 
 virtual lessons once or twice a week with Coach Racae\, in which case\, the
 ir fee is $10.<br><br>Enter one of these tournaments:<br><b>Outdoor 2 + 3 T
 ournament :&nbsp\;</b><br>For beginners at 9m and 13.5m - One or two rounds
  (depending on your strength) of 10 ends of 3 arrows each for a total of 30
  arrows.<br><b>Outdoor 4-9 Tournament:&nbsp\;</b><br>For more advanced arch
 ers at 20m+ - Two rounds of 6 ends of 6 arrows each for a total of 72 arrow
 s shot on 122-cm target faces.<br><br>More information and registration lin
 ks at&nbsp\;<a>www.archerytrainingcenter.com</a>
