BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20250413T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20250413T150000
DTSTAMP:20261004T164459Z
UID:i0ipq2ivunp1mhm90ei7ik96aa@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Chicago:20250413T130000
CREATED:20250211T001646Z
DESCRIPTION:Registration form: OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m<br><br>Add your nam
 e to Target Assignment List below or send in the above completed form.<br><
 br>Focus primarily on <br>    •perfecting your form\, <br>    •slowly incre
 asing your physical strength and draw weight\, <br>    •strengthening your 
 mental program\, <br>    •determining your average and personal best\, <br>
     •understanding the spread between the two\, and working on closing it.<
 br>You need your own equipment <br>Competition recurve bow\, sight\, stabil
 izer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicke
 r\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field qu
 iver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added until yo
 u reach a higher level\, but you should order them in advance.) <br><br>Wea
 r your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow 
 round on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the next distance until
  you reach your competition distance<br>If you trained outdoors in the 2024
  season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.<br>Target arrang
 ements may vary each session\, depending on who attends and distances neede
 d.<br>Target 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should always st
 ay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent practice in between classes.<b
 r>Target 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition distance) <br>Target 3 at 50m<
 br>Targets 4+5 at 40m (U15 competition distance) <br>Targets 6\, 7\, 8 at 3
 0m (U13 competition distance) <br>Target 9 at 20m (for those who have shot 
 at 18m indoors or with Coach Racae's approval)<br>Targets 10 at 13.5m (for 
 those who have just graduated from indoors at 9m)<br><br>Ideally\, we want 
