DESCRIPTION:<i>The Outdoor Range will be open all winter to those who have 
 qualified (see below) and want to practice the longer distances. All classe
 s need to be supervised by a USA Archery certified Level 2-4 Instructor or 
 Coach. </i><br><i><br></i><br><i>Coach Racae will be coaching Indoor 4-9 in
  the Indoor 18m range in Westlake as indicated on the calendar\, until afte
 r the Indoor Nationals in early February. She will also be coaching Indoor 
 2-6 in the 9m indoor range as indicated on the calendar. </i><br><br>Regist
 ration form: OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m<br><br><b>REMINDER</b>:  Everyone nee
 ds to come to at least one Training Class per week to be able to attend Ope
 n Practice. (All indoor classes are training classes.)<br><br>If you are no
 t a coach/instructor\, the fees are:  <ul><li><b>Outdoor Training Class (OT
 C)</b>: $52/class or multi-class pack </li><li><b>Indoor Training Class (IT
 C)</b>: $43/class or multi-class pack or unlimited pack</li><li><b>Open Pra
 ctice (OP)</b>: ($50/mo)  </li></ul><br>If you are a coach/instructor\, you
  have received an email from Coach Racae outlining your fees.<br><br>During
  the fall (Aug 31-Dec 18)\, for Coach Racae to coach the Outdoor 3-9 Traini
 ng Class\, at least 5 archers need to register by <br>8:00 am on Thursdays 
 (for Saturdays) and <br>8:00 am on Fridays (for Sundays) <br>In the case of
  low or late registrations or cancellations\, another coach/instructor\, wh
 en available\, will coach the session as a Training Class or oversee it as 
 an Open Practice instead. If this is not possible\, then the class may need
  to be cancelled.<br><br>Add your name to the Target Assignment List below 
 or submit the above completed form.<br>Focus primarily on perfecting your f
 orm\, <br>slowly increasing your physical strength and draw weight\, <br>st
 rengthening your mental program\, <br>determining your average and personal
  best\, <br>understanding the spread between the two\, and working on closi
 ng it.<br><br>You need your own equipment <br>Competition recurve bow\, sig
 ht\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assemb
 ly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip 
 or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be add
 ed until you reach a higher level\, but you should order them in advance.) 
 <br><br>Wear your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br>When you score 288 pts in 
 a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the next dis
 tance until you reach your competition distance<br>If you trained outdoors 
 in the 2024 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.<br><b
 r>Target arrangements may vary each session\, depending on who attends and 
 distances needed.<br>Target 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) s
 hould always stay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent practice in bet
 ween classes.<br>Target 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition distance) <br>T
 arget 3 at 50m<br>Target 4+5 at 40m (U15 competition distance) <br>Target 6
  at 30m (U13 competition distance) <br><br>Targets 7-10 at 18m (for those w
 anting to qualify to shoot competitively at 18m indoors or with Coach Racae
 's approval)<br><br>Ideally\, we want to practice with two archers/target t
 o replicate outdoor competition conditions.<br><b>Alternate daily</b>: Outd
 oor distance and 18m distance. <br>For <b>18m distance</b>\, put up <b>four
  40-cm target faces on one target</b>\, even if fewer people are shooting t
 he target\, so you practice high/low/left/right. <br>For <b>18m JOAD</b>\, 
 put up <b>two 60cm target faces on one target side-by-side</b> for max two 
 people shooting on each target bale.<br>Target Assignments:<br>Targets are 
 assigned outdoors in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\,<br>
 so add your name next to your distance below. <br>If you need help or have 
 questions\, email/text Coach Racae<br>(Dotted lines represent tent poles di
 viding Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)<br><br><br><b>ATCIICT = 2026 ATCI Indoor Com
 petition Team : </b><br><b>MQS at 18m\, 30-arrow rounds: 210 pts or 420 pts
  (2 rounds)</b>----------------------------------<br>1A. (70m)<br>1B<br><br
 >2A. (60m)  <br>2B<br><br>3A. (50m)  <br>----------------------------------
 <br>3B<br><br>4A. (40m) <br>4B. <br>----------------------------------<br>5
 A. (40m)<br>5B. <br><br>6A. (30m)<br>----------------------------------<br>
 6B. <br><br>7A. (18m)<br>7B. <br>---------------------------------- <br>8A.
  (18m)<br>8B. <br><br>9A. (18m)<br>----------------------------------<br>9B
 . <br><br>10A. (18m)<br>10B
