UID:7h7d0rp4steh1al545m919e8et@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Chicago:20250906T090000
CREATED:20250808T205345Z
DESCRIPTION:Registration form: OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m\n\nREMINDER:  Every
 one needs to come to at least one Training Class per week to be able to att
 end Open Practice. (All indoor classes are training classes.)\n\nIf you are
  not a coach/instructor\, the fees are:  \n\nOutdoor Training Class (OTC): 
 $52/class or multi-class pack \n\nIndoor Training Class (ITC): $43/class or
  multi-class pack or unlimited pack\n\nOpen Practice (OP): ($50/mo)  \n\nIf
  you are a coach/instructor\, you have received an email from Coach Racae o
 utlining your fees.\n\nDuring the fall (Aug 31-Dec 18)\, for Coach Racae to
  coach the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class\, at least 5 archers need to register
  by \n8:00 am on Thursdays (for Saturdays) and \n8:00 am on Fridays (for Su
 ndays) \nIn the case of low or late registrations or cancellations\, anothe
 r coach/instructor\, when available\, will coach the session as a Training 
 Class or oversee it as an Open Practice instead. If this is not possible\, 
 then the class may need to be cancelled.\n\nAdd your name to the Target Ass
 ignment List below or submit the above completed form.\nFocus primarily on 
 perfecting your form\, \nslowly increasing your physical strength and draw 
 weight\, \nstrengthening your mental program\, \ndetermining your average a
 nd personal best\, \nunderstanding the spread between the two\, and working
  on closing it.\n\nYou need your own equipment \nCompetition recurve bow\, 
 sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar ass
 embly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, h
 ip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be 
 added until you reach a higher level\, but you should order them in advance
 .) \n\nWear your ATCI shirt to training.\n\nWhen you score 288 pts in a 36-
 arrow round on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the next distance
  until you reach your competition distance\nIf you trained outdoors in the 
 2024 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.\n\nTarget ar
 rangements may vary each session\, depending on who attends and distances n
 eeded.\nTarget 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should always 
 stay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent practice in between classes.
 \nTarget 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition distance) \nTarget 3 at 50m\nT
 arget 4+5 at 40m (U15 competition distance) \nTarget 6 at 30m (U13 competit
 ion distance) \nTargets 7-10 at 18m (for those wanting to qualify to shoot 
 competitively at 18m indoors or with Coach Racae's approval)\n\nIdeally\, w
 e want to practice with two archers/target to replicate outdoor competition
  conditions.\nAlternate daily: Outdoor distance and 18m distance. \nFor 18m
  distance\, put up four 40-cm target faces on one target\, even if fewer pe
 ople are shooting the target\, so you practice high/low/left/right. \nFor 1
 8m JOAD\, put up two 60cm target faces on one target side-by-side for max t
 wo people shooting on each target bale.\nTarget Assignments:\nTargets are a
 ssigned outdoors in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\,  so 
 add your name next to your distance below. \n\nThe MQS for 2026 ATCI Indoor
  Competition Team is 210 pts at 18m on either 60cm target face (U13 and U15
 ) or 40cm target face (U18\, U21\,Seniors (21-49)\, Masters (50+). \n\nThe 
 MQS for 2026 ATCI Outdoor Competition Team will be 250 pts on 122cm target 
 face at competition distance for age. \n\n\nIf you need help or have questi
 ons\, email/text Coach Racae\n(Dotted lines represent tent poles dividing T
 argets 3\, 6\, and 9.)\n----------------------------------\n1A. (70m)\n1B\n
 \n2A. (60m)  \n2B\n\n3A. (50m)  Abby Y\, 13\, USAA\, ob\, pd - 2 hrs\n-----
 -----------------------------\n3B\n\n4A. \n4B. \n--------------------------
