CREATED:20210505T051536Z
DESCRIPTION:To register for this class\, you will have already completed an
 d graduated out of Outdoor 1: First-time Class\, Outdoor 2 at 9m\, and Outd
 oor 3 at 13.5m\, and your distance will be at least 20m. Register here:&nbs
 p\;<a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfF-EGKsMPSlfPLuLe3aLk
 qThTFZs0qqb8zleJ_0W3B6Xn7mA/viewform">2021 Outdoor 4-9 at 20m-70m</a><br><b
 r>Registered Archers on 122-cm target face unless otherwise noted:<br>1.&nb
 sp\;<br>2. <b>Chris C.\, </b>@ 60m?<br>3.&nbsp\;<b>Lily R.</b>\, @ 30m - <b
 >209 pts </b>- You´re back!!<br>4.<b> Kevin B</b>.\, @ 40m<br>5.&nbsp\;<b>C
 yrenna V</b>. @ 13.5m on 40-cm target face - <b>191 pts</b> - Great!<br>6.<
 br>7.<br>8.<br>9.<br>10.<br><br><b>Tournament Week</b><br>For one week each
  month during Tournament Week\, you shoot for score and submit your scores 
 to Coach Racae. Score in your regular classes or come to the tournament on 
 Tournament Saturday.<br><br><b>Tournament Saturday</b><br>On the last day o
 f tournament week\, Saturday\, Coach Racae will conduct the Saturday Outdoo
 r 4-9 class as a tournament with timed rounds and scoring and little to no 
 coaching.&nbsp\;<br><br><b>Master Challenge</b><br>While you´re shooting in
  the tournament&nbsp\; Coach Racae will look at your form and assess how mu
 ch attention to form you can remember to do while shooting in a tournament.
  You can earn Mastered Tags for each step of the form you have consistently
  done at your level. As you progress through higher levels\, the level of d
 etail required will increase and additional positions will be added.<br><br
 ><b>USA Archery Star Pins</b><br><b>If you are a member of USA Archery</b>\
 , Tournament Saturday is often called a ¨Pin Shoot¨\, when you can earn you
 r USA Archery Star Pins based on the scores you obtain. Look at the bottom 
 of your scorecard to see how many points you´ll need to receive a Star Pin.
 <br><br><b>Winners´ Pot and Fees</b><br>Archers participate in Tournament W
 eek by entering one of the following tournaments and paying $5.00 towards t
 he Winners´ Pot. Winners will be announced by email and Instagram following
  Tournament Saturday.&nbsp\;<br>Archers participating in Tournament Saturda
 y or attending any Outdoor 2-9 classes will also pay $30 for their place on
  the shooting line\, unless they also take virtual lessons once or twice a 
 week with Coach Racae\, in which case\, their fee is $10.<br><br>Enter one 
 of these tournaments:<br><b>Outdoor 2 + 3 Tournament :&nbsp\;</b><br>For be
 ginners at 9m and 13.5m - One or two rounds (depending on your strength) of
  10 ends of 3 arrows each for a total of 30 arrows.<br><b>Outdoor 4-9 Tourn
 ament:&nbsp\;</b><br>For more advanced archers at 20m+ - Two rounds of 6 en
 ds of 6 arrows each for a total of 72 arrows shot on 122-cm target faces.<b
 r><br>More information and registration links at&nbsp\;<a>www.archerytraini
 ngcenter.com</a>
