CREATED:20250808T205345Z
DESCRIPTION:This class has been moved indoors due to coming storm. See you 
 at the Indoor range! <br><br>Registration form: OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m<br
 ><br>REMINDER:  Everyone needs to come to at least one Training Class per w
 eek to be able to attend Open Practice. (All indoor classes are training cl
 asses.)<br><br>If you are not a coach/instructor\, the fees are:  <br><br>O
 utdoor Training Class (OTC): $52/class or multi-class pack <br><br>Indoor T
 raining Class (ITC): $43/class or multi-class pack or unlimited pack<br><br
 >Open Practice (OP): ($50/mo)  <br><br>If you are a coach/instructor\, you 
 have received an email from Coach Racae outlining your fees.<br><br>During 
 the fall (Aug 31-Dec 18)\, for Coach Racae to coach the Outdoor 3-9 Trainin
 g Class\, at least 5 archers need to register by <br>8:00 am on Thursdays (
 for Saturdays) and <br>8:00 am on Fridays (for Sundays) <br>In the case of 
 low or late registrations or cancellations\, another coach/instructor\, whe
 n available\, will coach the session as a Training Class or oversee it as a
 n Open Practice instead. If this is not possible\, then the class may need 
 to be cancelled.<br><br>Add your name to the Target Assignment List below o
 r submit the above completed form.<br>Focus primarily on perfecting your fo
 rm\, <br>slowly increasing your physical strength and draw weight\, <br>str
 engthening your mental program\, <br>determining your average and personal 
 best\, <br>understanding the spread between the two\, and working on closin
 g it.<br><br>You need your own equipment <br>Competition recurve bow\, sigh
 t\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembl
 y\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip o
 r field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be adde
 d until you reach a higher level\, but you should order them in advance.) <
 br><br>Wear your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br>When you score 288 pts in a
  36-arrow round on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the next dist
 ance until you reach your competition distance<br>If you trained outdoors i
 n the 2024 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.<br><br
 >Target arrangements may vary each session\, depending on who attends and d
 istances needed.<br>Target 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) sh
 ould always stay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent practice in betw
 een classes.<br>Target 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition distance) <br>Ta
 rget 3 at 50m<br>Target 4+5 at 40m (U15 competition distance) <br>Target 6 
 at 30m (U13 competition distance) <br>Targets 7-10 at 18m (for those wantin
 g to qualify to shoot competitively at 18m indoors or with Coach Racae's ap
 proval)<br><br>Ideally\, we want to practice with two archers/target to rep
 licate outdoor competition conditions.<br>Alternate daily: Outdoor distance
  and 18m distance. <br>For 18m distance\, put up four 40-cm target faces on
  one target\, even if fewer people are shooting the target\, so you practic
 e high/low/left/right. <br>For 18m JOAD\, put up two 60cm target faces on o
 ne target side-by-side for max two people shooting on each target bale.<br>
 <br>Target Assignments:<br>Targets are assigned outdoors in advance to redu
 ce confusion and delay on the day\,<br>so add your name next to your distan
 ce below. <br>The MQS for 2026 ATCI Indoor Competition Team is 210 pts at 1
 8m on either 60cm target face (U13 and U15) or 40cm target face (U18\, U21\
 ,Seniors (21-49)\, Masters (50+). <br>The MQS for 2026 ATCI Outdoor Competi
 tion Team will be 250 pts on 122cm target face at competition distance for 
 age. <br>If you need help or have questions\, email/text Coach Racae<br>(Do
 tted lines represent tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)<br>-------
 ---------------------------<br><b>Nick E</b>\, adult\, USAA\, ob\, pd - 2 h
 rs<br><b>Adrianne M</b>. USAA\, ob\, pd - 2 hrs<br><b>Colby K</b>.\,adult\,
  USAA\, ob\, pd? - 2 hrs<br><b>Finn E</b>\, 13\, USAA\, ob\, pd - 2 hrs<br>
 <b>Emma A</b>.\, 13\, USAA\, ob\,\, pd - 2 hrs<br><b>Anush K\, </b>12?\, US
 AA\, ob\, pd - 2 hrs<br><b>Miles G\,</b> 13\, USAA\, ob\, pd - 2 hrs<br><b>
 Rhys E.\, </b><span>11\, USAA\, ob\, pd </span><span>- 2 hrs</span><br><br>
 <b>Hannah</b>\, USAA\, ob\, pd -<b> DNA</b>
