DESCRIPTION:Once a month until October 18\,&nbsp\; Outdoor 2+3 can register
  for Tournament Saturday at&nbsp\;<a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/
 e/1FAIpQLSeXKGqxUPCkcYHxJgXLxz62jkCFDOFvJswqN_cthIWgsBps7g/viewform">ATCI V
 irtual Monthly Tournament</a><br><br>To register for this class usually\, y
 ou will have already completed and graduated out of Outdoor 1: First-time C
 lass\, Outdoor 2 at 9m\, and Outdoor 3 at 13.5m\, and your distance will be
  at least 20m. Register here:&nbsp\;<a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/
 d/e/1FAIpQLSfF-EGKsMPSlfPLuLe3aLkqThTFZs0qqb8zleJ_0W3B6Xn7mA/viewform">2021
  Outdoor 4-9 at 20m-70m</a><br><br>Registered Archers:<br>1. Kevin B.\, @ 3
 0m on 122cm target face - 268 / 226 = <b>544</b><br>2. Victor C.\, @9m on 6
 0m target face - admitted until 10/18 - DNA - ill<br>3. Sarah X.\, @50m on 
 122cm target face - 268 /281 = <b>549</b><br>4. Ted H.\, @9m on 40cm target
  face - admitted until 10/18 - 117 / 135 = <b>252</b><br>5. Emma W.\, @ 20m
  on 122cm target face - 277 / 199 = <b>476</b><br>6. Lily R.\, @ 30m on 60c
 m target face - 135 / 190 = <b>325</b><br>7. Richard F. @ 70m on 122cm targ
 et face -&nbsp\;<br>8.<br>9.<br>10.<br><br><b>Tournament Week</b><br>For on
 e week each month during Tournament Week\, you shoot for score and submit y
 our scores to Coach Racae. Score in your regular classes or come to the tou
 rnament on Tournament Saturday.<br><br><b>Tournament Saturday</b><br>On the
  last day of tournament week\, Saturday\, Coach Racae will conduct the Satu
 rday Outdoor 4-9 class as a tournament with timed rounds and scoring and li
 ttle to no coaching.&nbsp\;<br><br><b>Master Challenge</b><br>While you´re 
 shooting in the tournament&nbsp\; Coach Racae will look at your form and as
 sess how much attention to form you can remember to do while shooting in a 
 tournament. You can earn Mastered Tags for each step of the form you have c
 onsistently done at your level. As you progress through higher levels\, the
  level of detail required will increase and additional positions will be ad
 ded.<br><br><b>USA Archery Star Pins</b><br><b>If you are a member of USA A
 rchery</b>\, Tournament Saturday is often called a ¨Pin Shoot¨\, when you c
 an earn your USA Archery Star Pins based on the scores you obtain. Look at 
 the bottom of your scorecard to see how many points you´ll need to receive 
 a Star Pin.<br><br><b>Winners´ Pot and Fees</b><br>Archers participate in T
 ournament Week by entering one of the following tournaments and paying $5.0
 0 towards the Winners´ Pot. Winners will be announced by email and Instagra
 m following Tournament Saturday.&nbsp\;<br>Archers participating in Tournam
 ent Saturday or attending any Outdoor 2-9 classes will also pay $30 for the
 ir place on the shooting line\, unless they also take virtual lessons once 
 or twice a week with Coach Racae\, in which case\, their fee is $10.<br><br
 >Enter one of these tournaments:<br><b>Outdoor 2 + 3 Tournament :&nbsp\;</b
 ><br>For beginners at 9m and 13.5m - One or two rounds (depending on your s
 trength) of 10 ends of 3 arrows each for a total of 30 arrows.<br><b>Outdoo
 r 4-9 Tournament:&nbsp\;</b><br>For more advanced archers at 20m+ - Two rou
 nds of 6 ends of 6 arrows each for a total of 72 arrows shot on 122-cm targ
 et faces.<br><br>More information and registration links at&nbsp\;<a>www.ar
 cherytrainingcenter.com</a>
