DESCRIPTION:The Outdoor Range will be open all winter to those who have qua
 lified (see below) and want to practice the longer distances. All classes n
 eed to be supervised by a USA Archery certified Level 2-4 Instructor or Coa
 ch. \n\nCoach Racae will be coaching Indoor 4-9 in the Indoor 18m range in 
 Westlake as indicated on the calendar\, until after the Indoor Nationals in
  early February. She will also be coaching Indoor 2-6 in the 9m indoor rang
 e as indicated on the calendar. \n\nRegistration form: OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m
 -70m\n\nREMINDER:  Everyone needs to come to at least one Training Class pe
 r week to be able to attend Open Practice. (All indoor classes are training
  classes.)\n\nIf you are not a coach/instructor\, the fees are:  \n    * Ou
 tdoor Training Class (OTC): $52/class or multi-class pack \n    * Indoor Tr
 aining Class (ITC): $43/class or multi-class pack or unlimited pack\n    * 
 Open Practice (OP): ($50/mo)  \n\nIf you are a coach/instructor\, you have 
 received an email from Coach Racae outlining your fees.\n\nDuring the fall 
 (Aug 31-Dec 18)\, for Coach Racae to coach the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class\,
  at least 5 archers need to register by \n8:00 am on Thursdays (for Saturda
 ys) and \n8:00 am on Fridays (for Sundays) \nIn the case of low or late reg
 istrations or cancellations\, another coach/instructor\, when available\, w
 ill coach the session as a Training Class or oversee it as an Open Practice
  instead. If this is not possible\, then the class may need to be cancelled
 .\n\nAdd your name to the Target Assignment List below or submit the above 
 completed form.\nFocus primarily on perfecting your form\, \nslowly increas
 ing your physical strength and draw weight\, \nstrengthening your mental pr
 ogram\, \ndetermining your average and personal best\, \nunderstanding the 
 spread between the two\, and working on closing it.\n\nYou need your own eq
 uipment \nCompetition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 1
 2 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, arm
 guard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc
 . (Clicker and side rods may not be added until you reach a higher level\, 
 but you should order them in advance.) \n\nWear your ATCI shirt to training
 .\n\nWhen you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm target face y
 ou'll move back to the next distance until you reach your competition dista
 nce\nIf you trained outdoors in the 2024 season\, you'll return to the fart
 hest distance you shot.\n\nTarget arrangements may vary each session\, depe
 nding on who attends and distances needed.\nTarget 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors 
 competition distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use it for inde
 pendent practice in between classes.\nTarget 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters compet
 ition distance) \nTarget 3 at 50m\nTarget 4+5 at 40m (U15 competition dista
 nce) \nTarget 6 at 30m (U13 competition distance) \n\nTargets 7-10 at 18m (
 for those wanting to qualify to shoot competitively at 18m indoors or with 
 Coach Racae's approval)\n\nIdeally\, we want to practice with two archers/t
 arget to replicate outdoor competition conditions.\nAlternate daily: Outdoo
 r distance and 18m distance. \nFor 18m distance\, put up four 40-cm target 
 faces on one target\, even if fewer people are shooting the target\, so you
  practice high/low/left/right. \nFor 18m JOAD\, put up two 60cm target face
 s on one target side-by-side for max two people shooting on each target bal
 e.\nTarget Assignments:\nTargets are assigned outdoors in advance to reduce
  confusion and delay on the day\,\nso add your name next to your distance b
 elow. \nIf you need help or have questions\, email/text Coach Racae\n(Dotte
 d lines represent tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)\n\n\nATCIICT 
 = 2026 ATCI Indoor Competition Team : \nMQS at 18m\, 30-arrow rounds: 210 p
 ts or 420 pts (2 rounds)----------------------------------\n1A. (70m)\n1B\n
 \n2A. (60m)  \n2B\n\n3A. (50m)  \n----------------------------------\n3B\n\
 n4A. (40m) \n4B. \n----------------------------------\n5A. (40m)\n5B. \n\n6
 A. (30m)\n----------------------------------\n6B. \n\n7A. (18m)\n7B. \n----
 ------------------------------ \n8A. (18m)\n8B. \n\n9A. (18m)\n------------
 ----------------------\n9B. \n\n10A. (18m)\n10B
LAST-MODIFIED:20260517T080916Z
