DESCRIPTION:TODAY - Because of the weather forecast\, we are moving to the 
 Indoor Range\, will still practice scoring for Aggie Invite - but only on r
 educed (smaller than 40-cm) target faces.<br>Just for fun. See who wins eac
 h round. Two rounds. Good luck!<br><br>REMINDER:  Everyone needs to come to
  at least one Training Class per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (
 All indoor classes are training classes.)<br><br>If you are not a coach/ins
 tructor\, the fees are:  <br>    * Outdoor Training Class (OTC): $52/class 
 or multi-class pack <br>    * Indoor Training Class (ITC): $43/class or mul
 ti-class pack or unlimited pack<br>    * Open Practice (OP): ($50/mo)  <br>
 <br>If you are a coach/instructor\, you have received an email from Coach R
 acae outlining your fees.<br><br>During the fall (Aug 31-Dec 18)\, for Coac
 h Racae to coach the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class\, at least 5 archers need t
 o register by <br>8:00 am on Thursdays (for Saturdays) and <br>8:00 am on F
 ridays (for Sundays) <br>In the case of low or late registrations or cancel
 lations\, another coach/instructor\, when available\, will coach the sessio
 n as a Training Class or oversee it as an Open Practice instead. If this is
  not possible\, then the class may need to be cancelled.<br><br>Add your na
 me to the Target Assignment List below or submit the above completed form.<
 br>Focus primarily on perfecting your form\, <br>slowly increasing your phy
 sical strength and draw weight\, <br>strengthening your mental program\, <b
 r>determining your average and personal best\, <br>understanding the spread
  between the two\, and working on closing it.<br><br>You need your own equi
 pment <br>Competition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 1
 2 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, arm
 guard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc
 . (Clicker and side rods may not be added until you reach a higher level\, 
 but you should order them in advance.) <br><br>Wear your ATCI shirt to trai
 ning.<br><br>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm targe
 t face you'll move back to the next distance until you reach your competiti
 on distance<br>If you trained outdoors in the 2024 season\, you'll return t
 o the farthest distance you shot.<br><br>Target arrangements may vary each 
 session\, depending on who attends and distances needed.<br>Target 1 at 70m
  (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can
  use it for independent practice in between classes.<br>Target 2 at 60m (U1
 8 + Masters competition distance) <br>Target 3 at 50m<br>Target 4+5 at 40m 
 (U15 competition distance) <br>Target 6 at 30m (U13 competition distance) <
 br><br>Targets 7-10 at 18m (for those wanting to qualify to shoot competiti
 vely at 18m indoors or with Coach Racae's approval)<br><br>Ideally\, we wan
 t to practice with two archers/target to replicate outdoor competition cond
 itions.<br>Alternate daily: Outdoor distance and 18m distance. <br>For 18m 
 distance\, put up four 40-cm target faces on one target\, even if fewer peo
 ple are shooting the target\, so you practice high/low/left/right. <br>For 
 18m JOAD\, put up two 60cm target faces on one target side-by-side for max 
 two people shooting on each target bale.<br>Target Assignments:<br>Targets 
 are assigned outdoors in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\,
 <br>so add your name next to your distance below. <br>If you need help or h
 ave questions\, email/text Coach Racae<br><br><b>ATCIICT = 2026 ATCI Indoor
  Competition Team </b>: <br>MQS at 18m\, 30-arrow rounds: 210 pts or 420 pt
 s (2 rounds)<br><ol><li>Abby</li><li>Adrianne</li><li>Anna</li><li>Colby</l
 i><li>Emma</li><li>Finn</li><li>Luke</li><li>Coach Nick</li><li>Sara </li><
 li>Sophia</li></ol><b>RESULTS from FUN INDOOR COMP AT 9m:</b><br>All shot a
 t triangular 3-spot\, except Ellie shot 40-cm<ol><li><b>Joel Y</b>\, adult\
 , USAA 286 + 267 = <b>553 pts</b></li><li><b>Luke T</b>\, 16 USAA - 279 + 2
 64 = <b>543 pts</b></li><li><b>Abby Y\,</b> 13\, USAA - 269 + 268 = <b>537 
 pts</b></li><li><b>Sara T</b>.\, 14\, USAA - 246 + 241 = <b>487 pts</b></li
 ><li><b>Miles G</b>\, 13\, USAA - 233+252 = <b>485 pts</b></li><li><b>Ellie
  Y</b>\, 11\, USAA - 251 +237 = <b>488 pts on 40-cm</b></li></ol>
