DESCRIPTION:<b>Today's class has been canceled so that Outdoor 2-9 can move
  to an earlier time due to extreme heat conditions. All first-time Classes 
 will move indoors starting Sept 2.</b><br><br>REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to
  adult\, juniors 8+\, and parents! Please read all the info below and in th
 e registration and waivers.<br><br>More information\, registration forms an
 d waivers are available at <a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com"><
 u><u><u><u>www.archerytrainingcenter.com</u></u></u></u></a>.<br><br>Regist
 er here using ONE of these forms:<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms
 /d/e/1FAIpQLSeciOgkyuKTLZ5_ZaWCEyQKYSX1fWGpP5qakhT6OuAc6jJ_FQ/viewform"><u>
 2023 Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Adults</u></a>  OR<br><a href="https:/
 /docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSc_bYEFoE4oXkcm0T6fZK99fu_q6lL8wZGClXyfa1
 GZbahh-g/viewform"><u>2023 Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Juniors and Pare
 nts</u></a><br><br>Sign up for just ONE Outdoor 1 class\, because most peop
 le graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br><br
 >Your name will be added below and your place reserved on a first registere
 d and paid basis and after we receive 3 things:  <br><b>2023 OUTDOOR 1 REGI
 STRATION FORM   +  MEMBERSHIP AND WAIVERS PACKET +   FEE</b><b><br></b><u><
 /u><br><b>USA Archery Level 4 NTS Coach Racae Meyer and other instructors/c
 oaches.</b><br><b>See </b><a href="https://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/wh
 o-we-are"><u><u>https://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/who-we-are</u></u></a
 ><b><br></b><br><b>Registered archers </b>at 9m on 40-cm target face unless
  otherwise noted:<u></u><br><u></u><br><b>Target Assignments:</b><br><u></u
 ><b><br></b>5A. <b>Allen J</b>.\, 10\, on 60-cm target face\, pd - substitu
 ted 9/30<br>5B.<br><br>6A. <b>Owen H</b>.\, age? - need waivers\, pd - subs
 tituted 9/30<br>6B.<br><br>7A.<br>7B.<br><br>8A.<br>8B.<br><br>9A.<br>9B.<b
 r><br>10A.<br>10B.<br><br>Space will be limited to 10-15 archers per sessio
 n depending on the number of family groups in attendance or in accordance w
 ith CDC Guidelines. <br>Each person will have a target stand\, except after
  10 people have registered\, members may be assigned to share a target stan
 d.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the fiel
 d until further notice or approved by Coach Racae. <br>Parents of juniors 1
 0+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator. <br>Parents of juniors
  8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their child for grea
 ter safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into 
 each Outdoor 1: First-time Class. <br><br>We will accept a limited number o
 f kids under 12 into the program each semester\, depending on the total  nu
 mber of archers in all the classes. If you join before the limit is reached
 \, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take other Outd
 oor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2. If you are under 12\, reg
 istered and paid after the cut off\, your fee will be returned to you. <br>
 <br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying
  to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you sco
 re on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows. <br>Adults don´t need a minimum 
 score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\
 , fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($18) Plea
 se pay for this at the field\, as our stock fluctuates because of dealer su
 pply fluctuations<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, optiona
 l but really needed to practice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>A
 t the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we did n
 ot finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final s
 core\, because it will have been averaged by taking your recorded score fro
 m your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot to get an arro
 w average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round score. Afte
 r the last first-time class each weekend\, final scores may also be sent to
  all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more information before your n
 ext class.
