RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Chicago:20251213T090000
CREATED:20250808T205345Z
DESCRIPTION:The Outdoor Range will be open all winter to those who have qua
 lified (see below) and want to practice the longer distances. All classes n
 eed to be supervised by a USA Archery certified Level 2-4 Instructor or Coa
 ch. \n\n\nCoach Racae will be coaching Indoor 4-9 in the Indoor 18m range i
 n Westlake as indicated on the calendar\, until after the Indoor Nationals 
 in early February. She will also be coaching Indoor 2-6 in the 9m indoor ra
 nge as indicated on the calendar. \n\nRegistration form: OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.
 5m-70m\n\nREMINDER:  Everyone needs to come to at least one Training Class 
 per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (All indoor classes are traini
 ng classes.)\n\nIf you are not a coach/instructor\, the fees are:  \n\nOutd
 oor Training Class (OTC): $52/class or multi-class pack \n\nIndoor Training
  Class (ITC): $43/class or multi-class pack or unlimited pack\n\nOpen Pract
 ice (OP): ($50/mo)  \n\n\nIf you are a coach/instructor\, you have received
  an email from Coach Racae outlining your fees.\n\nDuring the fall (Aug 31-
 Dec 18)\, for Coach Racae to coach the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class\, at leas
 t 5 archers need to register by \n8:00 am on Thursdays (for Saturdays) and 
 \n8:00 am on Fridays (for Sundays) \nIn the case of low or late registratio
 ns or cancellations\, another coach/instructor\, when available\, will coac
 h the session as a Training Class or oversee it as an Open Practice instead
 . If this is not possible\, then the class may need to be cancelled.\n\nAdd
  your name to the Target Assignment List below or submit the above complete
 d form.\nFocus primarily on perfecting your form\, \nslowly increasing your
  physical strength and draw weight\, \nstrengthening your mental program\, 
 \ndetermining your average and personal best\, \nunderstanding the spread b
 etween the two\, and working on closing it.\n\nYou need your own equipment 
 \nCompetition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon
  arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, 
 fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Click
 er and side rods may not be added until you reach a higher level\, but you 
 should order them in advance.) \n\nWear your ATCI shirt to training.\n\nWhe
 n you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm target face you'll mo
 ve back to the next distance until you reach your competition distance\nIf 
 you trained outdoors in the 2024 season\, you'll return to the farthest dis
 tance you shot.\n\nTarget arrangements may vary each session\, depending on
  who attends and distances needed.\nTarget 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competit
 ion distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent 
 practice in between classes.\nTarget 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition di
 stance) \nTarget 3 at 50m\nTarget 4+5 at 40m (U15 competition distance) \nT
 arget 6 at 30m (U13 competition distance) \n\nTargets 7-10 at 18m (for thos
 e wanting to qualify to shoot competitively at 18m indoors or with Coach Ra
 cae's approval)\n\nIdeally\, we want to practice with two archers/target to
  replicate outdoor competition conditions.\nAlternate daily: Outdoor distan
 ce and 18m distance. \nFor 18m distance\, put up four 40-cm target faces on
  one target\, even if fewer people are shooting the target\, so you practic
 e high/low/left/right. \nFor 18m JOAD\, put up two 60cm target faces on one
  target side-by-side for max two people shooting on each target bale.\nTarg
 et Assignments:\nTargets are assigned outdoors in advance to reduce confusi
 on and delay on the day\,\nso add your name next to your distance below. \n
 If you need help or have questions\, email/text Coach Racae\n(Dotted lines 
 represent tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)\n\n\nATCIICT = 2026 A
 TCI Indoor Competition Team : \nMQS at 18m\, 30-arrow rounds: 210 pts or 42
 0 pts (2 rounds)----------------------------------\n1A. (70m)\n1B\n\n2A. (6
 0m)  \n2B\n\n3A. (50m)  \n----------------------------------\n3B\n\n4A. (40
 m) \n4B. \n----------------------------------\n5A. (40m)\n5B. \n\n6A. (30m)
 \n----------------------------------\n6B. \n\n7A. (18m)\n7B. \n------------
 ---------------------- \n8A. (18m)\n8B. \n\n9A. (18m)\n--------------------
 --------------\n9B. \n\n10A. (18m)\n10B
LAST-MODIFIED:20260517T080916Z
LOCATION:2324 Bliss Spillar Rd\, Manchaca\, TX 78652\, USA
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
