DESCRIPTION:Registration form: OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m\n\nREMINDER:  Every
 one needs to come to at least one Training Class per week to be able to att
 end Open Practice. (All indoor classes are training classes.)\n\nIf you are
  not a coach/instructor\, the fees are:  \n    * Outdoor Training Class (OT
 C): $52/class or multi-class pack \n    * Indoor Training Class (ITC): $43/
 class or multi-class pack or unlimited pack\n    * Open Practice (OP): ($50
 /mo)  \nIf you are a coach/instructor\, you have received an email from Coa
 ch Racae outlining your fees.\n\nDuring the fall (Aug 31-Dec 18)\, for Coac
 h Racae to coach the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class\, at least 5 archers need t
 o register by \n8:00 am on Thursdays (for Saturdays) and \n8:00 am on Frida
 ys (for Sundays) \nIn the case of low or late registrations or cancellation
 s\, another coach/instructor\, when available\, will coach the session as a
  Training Class or oversee it as an Open Practice instead. If this is not p
 ossible\, then the class may need to be cancelled.\n\nAdd your name to the 
 Target Assignment List below.\nFocus primarily on perfecting your form\, \n
 slowly increasing your physical strength and draw weight\, \nstrengthening 
 your mental program\, \ndetermining your average and personal best\, \nunde
 rstanding the spread between the two\, and working on closing it.\n\nYou ne
 ed your own equipment: \nCompetition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plu
 nger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest 
 protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arr
 ow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added until you reach a 
 higher level\, but you should order them in advance.) \n\nWear your ATCI sh
 irt to training.\n\nWhen you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-c
 m target face you'll move back to the next distance until you reach your co
 mpetition distance\nIf you trained outdoors in the 2024 season\, you'll ret
 urn to the farthest distance you shot.\n\nTarget arrangements may vary each
  session\, depending on who attends and distances needed.\nTarget 1 at 70m 
 (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can 
 use it for independent practice in between classes.\nTarget 2 at 60m (U18 +
  Masters competition distance) \nTarget 3 at 50m\nTarget 4+5 at 40m (U15 co
 mpetition distance) \nTarget 6 at 30m (U13 competition distance) \n\nTarget
 s 7-10 at 18m (for those wanting to qualify to shoot competitively at 18m i
 ndoors or with Coach Racae's approval)\n\nIdeally\, we want to practice wit
 h two archers/target to replicate outdoor competition conditions.\nAlternat
 e daily: Outdoor distance and 18m distance. \nFor 18m distance\, put up fou
 r 40-cm target faces on one target\, even if fewer people are shooting the 
 target\, so you practice high/low/left/right. \nFor 18m JOAD\, put up two 6
 0cm target faces on one target side-by-side for max two people shooting on 
 each target bale.\nTarget Assignments:\nTargets are assigned outdoors in ad
 vance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\,\nso add your name next to 
 your distance below. \nIf you need help or have questions\, email/text Coac
 h Racae\n(Dotted lines represent tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.
 )\n\nATCIICT = 2026 ATCI Indoor Competition Team : \nMQS at 18m\, 30-arrow 
 rounds: 210 pts or 420 pts (2 rounds)\n    1. Abby\n    2. Adrianne\n    3.
  Anna\n    4. Colby\n    5. Emma\n    6. Finn\n    7. Coach Joel\n    8. Lu
 ke\n    9. Coach Nick\n    10. Sara \n    11. Sophia\n---------------------
 -------------\n1A. (70m)\n1B\n\n2A. (60m)  \n2B\n\n3A. (50m)  \n-----------
 -----------------------\n3B\n\n4A. (40m) \n4B. \n--------------------------
 --------\n5A. (40m)\n5B. \n\n6A. (18m) Abby Y\, 13\, USAA\, pd 227+212=439\
 n----------------------------------\n6B. Joel Y\, adult\, USAA\, pd 242\n\n
 7A. (18m) Ellie\, Y\, 11\, USAA\, pd 108+140=248\n7B. \n-------------------
 --------------- \n8A. (18m) \n8B. \n\n9A. (18m) Luke T\, 16\, USAA\, pd 204
 +211=415\n----------------------------------\n9B. Sara T\, 185+196=381\n\n1
 0A. (18m)\n10B
LAST-MODIFIED:20260517T080916Z
