DESCRIPTION:To register for this class\, you will have already completed an
 d graduated out of Outdoor 1: First-time Class\, Outdoor 2 at 9m\, and Outd
 oor 3 at 13.5m\, and your distance will be at least 20m. Register here:&nbs
 p\;<a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfF-EGKsMPSlfPLuLe3aLk
 qThTFZs0qqb8zleJ_0W3B6Xn7mA/viewform">2021 Outdoor 4-9 at 20m-70m</a><br><b
 r><b>Registered Archers</b>&nbsp\;<br>1.&nbsp\;<br>2. &nbsp\;<br>3. <b>Kevi
 n</b> B.\, @ 30m - <b>296 / 298 pts = 594 pts</b><br>4..<b>Lily R</b>.\, @ 
 30m <b>197 / 222 pts = 419 pts</b><br>5.&nbsp\;<b>John B</b>.\, @ 20m - <b>
 326 / 312 pts = 638 pts -&gt\; Outdoor 5 at 30m - CONGRATULATIONS !</b><br>
 6. <b>Cyrenna V. </b>@ 13.5m -&nbsp\;<b>163 / 179 pts = 342 pts </b>(correc
 ted)<br>7.<br>8.<br>9.<br>10.<br><br><b>Tournament Week</b><br>For one week
  each month during Tournament Week\, you shoot for score and submit your sc
 ores to Coach Racae. Score in your regular classes or come to the tournamen
 t on Tournament Saturday.<br><br><b>Tournament Saturday</b><br>On the last 
 day of tournament week\, Saturday\, Coach Racae will conduct the Saturday O
 utdoor 4-9 class as a tournament with timed rounds and scoring and little t
 o no coaching.&nbsp\;<br><br><b>Master Challenge</b><br>While you´re shooti
 ng in the tournament&nbsp\; Coach Racae will look at your form and assess h
 ow much attention to form you can remember to do while shooting in a tourna
 ment. You can earn Mastered Tags for each step of the form you have consist
 ently done at your level. As you progress through higher levels\, the level
  of detail required will increase and additional positions will be added.<b
 r><br><b>USA Archery Star Pins</b><br><b>If you are a member of USA Archery
 </b>\, Tournament Saturday is often called a ¨Pin Shoot¨\, when you can ear
 n your USA Archery Star Pins based on the scores you obtain. Look at the bo
 ttom of your scorecard to see how many points you´ll need to receive a Star
  Pin.<br><br><b>Winners´ Pot and Fees</b><br>Archers participate in Tournam
 ent Week by entering one of the following tournaments and paying $5.00 towa
 rds the Winners´ Pot. Winners will be announced by email and Instagram foll
 owing Tournament Saturday.&nbsp\;<br>Archers participating in Tournament Sa
 turday or attending any Outdoor 2-9 classes will also pay $30 for their pla
 ce on the shooting line\, unless they also take virtual lessons once or twi
 ce a week with Coach Racae\, in which case\, their fee is $10.<br><br>Enter
  one of these tournaments:<br><b>Outdoor 2 + 3 Tournament :&nbsp\;</b><br>F
 or beginners at 9m and 13.5m - One or two rounds (depending on your strengt
 h) of 10 ends of 3 arrows each for a total of 30 arrows.<br><b>Outdoor 4-9 
 Tournament:&nbsp\;</b><br>For more advanced archers at 20m+ - Two rounds of
  6 ends of 6 arrows each for a total of 72 arrows shot on 122-cm target fac
 es.<br><br>More information and registration links at&nbsp\;<a>www.archeryt
 rainingcenter.com</a>
