DESCRIPTION:Registration form: OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m\n\nREMINDER:  Every
 one needs to come to at least one Training Class per week to be able to att
 end Open Practice. (All indoor classes are training classes.)\n\nIf you are
  not a coach/instructor\, the fees are:  \nOutdoor Training Class (OTC): $5
 2/class or multi-class pack \nIndoor Training Class (ITC): $43/class or mul
 ti-class pack or unlimited pack\nOpen Practice (OP): ($50/mo)  \n\nIf you a
 re a coach/instructor\, you have received an email from Coach Racae outlini
 ng your fees.\n\nDuring the fall (Aug 31-Dec 18)\, for Coach Racae to coach
  the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class\, at least 5 archers need to register by \n
 8:00 am on Thursdays (for Saturdays) and \n8:00 am on Fridays (for Sundays)
  \nIn the case of low or late registrations or cancellations\, another coac
 h/instructor\, when available\, will coach the session as a Training Class 
 or oversee it as an Open Practice instead. If this is not possible\, then t
 he class may need to be cancelled.\n\nAdd your name to the Target Assignmen
 t List below or submit the above completed form.\nFocus primarily on perfec
 ting your form\, \nslowly increasing your physical strength and draw weight
 \, \nstrengthening your mental program\, \ndetermining your average and per
 sonal best\, \nunderstanding the spread between the two\, and working on cl
 osing it.\n\nYou need your own equipment \nCompetition recurve bow\, sight\
 , stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\
 , clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or 
 field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added 
 until you reach a higher level\, but you should order them in advance.) \n\
 nWear your ATCI shirt to training.\n\nWhen you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow 
 round on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the next distance until
  you reach your competition distance\nIf you trained outdoors in the 2024 s
 eason\, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.\n\nTarget arrangem
 ents may vary each session\, depending on who attends and distances needed.
 \nTarget 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should always stay a
 t 70m so Jake can use it for independent practice in between classes.\nTarg
 et 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition distance) \nTarget 3 at 50m\nTarget 
 4+5 at 40m (U15 competition distance) \nTarget 6 at 30m (U13 competition di
 stance) \n\nTargets 7-10 at 18m (for those wanting to qualify to shoot comp
 etitively at 18m indoors or with Coach Racae's approval)\n\nIdeally\, we wa
 nt to practice with two archers/target to replicate outdoor competition con
 ditions.\nAlternate daily: Outdoor distance and 18m distance. \nFor 18m dis
 tance\, put up four 40-cm target faces on one target\, even if fewer people
  are shooting the target\, so you practice high/low/left/right. \nFor 18m J
 OAD\, put up two 60cm target faces on one target side-by-side for max two p
 eople shooting on each target bale.\nTarget Assignments:\nTargets are assig
 ned outdoors in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\, so add y
 our name next to your distance below. \nThe MQS for 2026 ATCI Indoor Compet
 ition Team is 210 pts at 18m on either 60cm target face (U13 and U15) or 40
 cm target face (U18\, U21\,Seniors (21-49)\, Masters (50+). \nThe MQS for 2
 026 ATCI Outdoor Competition Team will be 250 pts on 122cm target face at c
 ompetition distance for age. \nIf you need help or have questions\, email/t
 ext Coach Racae\n(Dotted lines represent tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\
 , and 9.)\n----------------------------------\n1A. (70m)\n1B\n\n2A. (60m)  
 Joel Y\, adult\, USAA\, ob\, pd\n2B Nick E\n\n3A. (50m)  \n----------------
 ------------------\n3B  Adrianne M\, adult USAA\, pd\n\n4A. (40m)  Hannah T
 \, USAA\, pd\n4B. \n----------------------------------\n5A. (40m) Anna P\, 
 USAA\, pd\n5B. \n\n6A. (30m) Ellie Y\, 10\, USAA\, ob\, pd\n---------------
 -------------------\n6B. \n\n7A. (18m) Emma A.\, 13\, USAA\, pd\n7B. \n----
 ------------------------------ \n8A. (18m) Finn E.\, 13\, USAA\, pd\n8B. (1
 8m) Sara T.\, 14\, USAA\, pd\n\n9A. (18m) Rhys E.\, 11\, USAA\, pd\n-------
 ---------------------------\n9B. Anush K (18m)\n\n10A. (18m) Chi C.\, Adult
 \, USAA\, pd\n10B Logan C.\, 8\, USAA\, pd
