DESCRIPTION:<b>WAIVERS:</b> Everyone needs to <b>sign the waivers in advanc
 e </b>of arriving at the range\, so we are not delayed in starting. Here's 
 the link: <a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdYr3Yh5msvPHC_
 -ukFsifcvhYXRrzVRvcdyP4Ybx9O5zgUug/viewform"><u><u><u><u><u><u>2024 Corpora
 te Team Events Waivers Packet</u></u></u></u></u></u></a>  <br><br><b>DIREC
 TIONS:</b> <b>Google Map "Donut Taco Palace"</b> to find us quickly - We ar
 e right next door in Unit 102. (Some people are still being misdirected.) T
 here is a target on the glass door and the unit is facing 290W service road
  going west on the corner of Industrial Oaks Blvd and 290W. <br><br><b>ARRI
 VAL</b>: For a 2:00 pm start\, please <b>arrive by 1:45 pm</b>\, because we
  will all be starting together at 2:00 pm. <br><br><b>CARPOOLING / PARKING:
 </b> Please meet and carpool earlier from another location or from a big bo
 x store parking lot across the highway (like Target or At Home on the corne
 r of Mopac and 290W). It's easy and convenient to do. (Parking in front of 
 the range and along Industrial Oaks Blvd may be limited\, depending on the 
 number of participants.)<br><br><b>DRESS RECOMMENDATIONS: </b><br>Flat athl
 etic shoes are best\, as we will be throwing our weight forward a little\, 
 so balance and weight distribution is important. The bowstring can get slow
 ed or entangled in your clothing or hair\, so wearing tightly fitting cloth
 es\, no wide skirts\, shirts without buttons on the front pockets and tying
  your hair back is preferable. Longer brim baseball caps often prevent the 
 string from reaching your face\, so shorter brims or bucket hats are better
 . <br>:<br><b>All participants need to complete waivers online before the e
 vent.</b><br><b>Here is the direct link to complete: </b><a href="https://d
 ocs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdYr3Yh5msvPHC_-ukFsifcvhYXRrzVRvcdyP4Ybx9O
 5zgUug/viewform"><u><u><u><u><u><u><u>2024 Corporate Team Events Waivers Pa
 cket</u></u></u></u></u></u></u></a>  <br><br>Waivers have been received fr
 om those shown below in <b>bold with (W)</b><b><br></b><br><u>Tuesday\, Feb
 ruary 13th</u><br><u><br>Olympic Round - Eliminations</u><br><b>1st Place -
  Germany - </b>Ben F.<br><b>2nd Place - Brazil  </b>- Zach G.<br><b>3rd Pla
 ce - Jamaica </b>- Tyler B.<br><br><b><u>Ranking Round</u></b><br>1. <b>Ben
  F. (W) </b>(Germany) <b>163 pts -&gt\; Indoor 2</b><br>2. <b>Zach G. (W)  
 (</b>Brazil) <b>160 pts -&gt\; Indoor 2</b><br>3. <b>Tyler B. (W) </b>(Jama
 ica) <b>108 pts -&gt\; Indoor 2</b><br><span>4.</span><span> </span><b>Gabr
 iela J. (W) </b><span>(Mexico) </span><b>90 pts -&gt\; Indoor 2</b><br>5. <
 b>Alyssa M. (W) </b>(S. Korea) <b>89 pts -&gt\; Indoor 2</b><br><span>6.</s
 pan><span> </span><b>Lauren T. (W) </b><span>(Canada)</span><b> 47 pts -&gt
 \; Indoor 2</b><br>7. <b>Mackenzie W. (W) </b>(Italy) <b>28 pts -&gt\; Indo
 or 2</b><br><b><br></b>Alison D. DNA<br><b>Foster F. (W) </b>DNA
