DESCRIPTION:<p><b>WINTER TRAINING PROGRAM - 12 weeks (Jan 4 - Mar 27)</b> <
 /p><p>We will go through the <b>National Training System (NTS) 11 Steps of 
 Shooting</b> and <b>Building Your Mental Program</b> step-by-step during th
 e regular training classes\, covering each one in sequence during the follo
 wing weeks.. </p><p>Learning\, understanding and doing the NTS and building
  a strong mental program are ongoing quests that all archers are continuous
 ly trying to achieve - even at the highest levels !</p><p><b><i>What if you
  miss some of the weeks?</i></b><i>  </i>We'll do our best to catch you up 
 during your next sessions. </p><p><b><i>Also see more important notes below
 \, under the schedule.</i></b></p><p><b>JANUARY</b></p><ul><li><p><b>  Sat 
 Jan 4 - Th 9</b>       <b>WELCOME </b>!  Understanding  <b>NTS CONCEPTS</b>
  especially TRANSFER + NTS Step 1<b> STANCE</b></p></li><li><p><b>  Sat 11 
 - Th 16    </b>NTS Step 2 <b> NOCK +  </b>NTS Step 3 <b>HOOK &amp\; GRIP </
 b>+ Building Your Mental Program</p></li><li><p>  <b>Sat 18 - Th 23</b>   N
 TS Step 4<b> SET + </b>Building Your Mental Program</p></li><li><p><b>  Sat
  25 - F 31  SCORING WEEK - </b><b>ATCI MONTHLY COMPETITION and STAR PIN SHO
 OT </b><b>   </b></p></li></ul><p><b>FEBRUARY</b></p><ul><li><p><b>  Sat 1 
 - Th 6    </b>NTS Step 5 <b>SET-UP +</b> Building Your Mental Program</p></
 li><li><p>  <b>Sat 8 - Th 13  </b>  NTS Step 6 <b>DRAW</b> to <b>LOAD </b>+
  Building Your Mental Program</p></li><li><p><b>  Sat 15 - Th 20</b>  NTS S
 tep 7 <b>ANCHOR </b>+ Building Your Mental Program</p></li><li><p>  <b>Sat 
 22 - Th 27  </b><b>SCORING WEEK - </b><b>ATCI MONTHLY COMPETITION and STAR 
 PIN SHOOT </b><b>     </b></p></li></ul><p><b>MARCH</b></p><ul><li><p><b>Sa
 t 1 - Th 6  </b>NTS Step 8<b> </b><b> TRANSFER to HOLD </b>+ Building Your 
 Mental Program</p></li><li><p><b>Sat 8 - Th 13  </b>NTS Step 9<b> </b><b>EX
 PAND / AIM + </b>Building Your Mental Program</p></li><li><p><b>Sat 15 - Th
  20 </b> <b>NTS Step 10</b> <b>RELEASE / FOLLOW-THROUGH</b> + NTS Step 11 <
 b>FEEDBACK +</b> Building Your Mental Program</p></li><li><p><b>Sat 22 - Th
  27  </b><b>SCORING WEEK - </b><b>ATCI MONTHLY COMPETITION and STAR PIN SHO
 OT</b></p></li></ul><p><b>INTRO</b></p><p><i>Each week the focus of your le
 ssons will be on one or two particular </i><b><i>Steps of Shooting of the N
 TS (National Training System) </i></b><i>shot cycle\, to help you focus and
  improve your form\, which\, as we all know\, leads to greater and more con
 sistent precision (tight groups of arrows) and ultimately greater accuracy 
 (tight groups of arrows dead center)</i>. <i>Concurrently you will be learn
 ing how to build a </i><b><i>strong mental program</i></b><i>\, which will 
 improve your focus\, awareness and confidence for competitions later\, and 
 also learning about and experimenting with archery equipment</i></p><p><i>T
 he NTS is the </i><b><i>most biomechanically efficient and least injurious 
 method of shooting</i></b><i>\, and is highly and continuously researched o
 ut at the Elite Athletes Center in Chula Vista\, CA. It is what the Olympia
 ns do!</i></p><p><i>The 11 NTS Steps are cumulative with each step most suc
 cessfully completed if the previous steps have been completed well. As you 
 reach higher levels\, you will learn the NTS Steps in progressively greater
  detail.</i></p><p><b>Goals by the end of the winter semester (March 27)</b
 ></p><p>Make a list of what you want to accomplish by the end of the semest
 er. Email it to Coach Racae\, so you can discuss it together. </p><p>Confid
 ence and consistency in form and mind are your two main goals. Replicate th
 e NTS step(s) mindfully and consistently on every shot\, and build a strong
  mental program that is consistent on every shot. </p><p>Your conscious min
 d commands your subconscious mind to put your body into position\, after yo
 u train your body to be in those positions. When you stay in the present\, 
 just doing what you need to do as you need to do it\, your conscious mind w
 ill be occupied\, instead of random thoughts entering your head or you bein
 g distracted by emotional or environmental elements. </p><p>You´ll need to 
 build up your mental program alongside your form knowledge\, so when your b
 ody is trained to shoot excellent shots\, your self image and subconscious 
 support you\, instead of undermining you. </p><p><i>Improving your training
 \, practicing\, and competition components\, process\, and skills is a perp
 etual lifetime quest\, which you´ll slowly learn to love. You´ll  realize w
 hat is under your control\, and you'll become your own best coach! Those wh
 o find all this fun and enjoy the journey are the ones who win - the champi
 ons!</i></p><p><i>I know you can do it -  I'm your biggest fan!</i></p><p><
 i>​I'm also really looking forward to seeing you improve\, succeed\, and th
 rive !​</i></p><p><b><i>                                                   
 Coach Racae</i></b></p>
