 ournament Week\, you shoot for score and submit your scores to Coach Racae.
  Score in your regular classes or come to the tournament on Tournament Satu
 rday.<br><br><b>Tournament Saturday</b><br>On the last day of tournament we
 ek\, Saturday\, Coach Racae will conduct the Saturday Outdoor 4-9 class as 
 a tournament with timed rounds and scoring and little to no coaching.&nbsp\
 ;<br><br><b>Master Challenge</b><br>While you´re shooting in the tournament
 &nbsp\; Coach Racae will look at your form and assess how much attention to
  form you can remember to do while shooting in a tournament. You can earn M
 astered Tags for each step of the form you have consistently done at your l
 evel. As you progress through higher levels\, the level of detail required 
 will increase and additional positions will be added.<br><br><b>USA Archery
  Star Pins</b><br><b>If you are a member of USA Archery</b>\, Tournament Sa
 turday is often called a ¨Pin Shoot¨\, when you can earn your USA Archery S
 tar Pins based on the scores you obtain. Look at the bottom of your scoreca
 rd to see how many points you´ll need to receive a Star Pin.<br><br><b>Winn
 ers´ Pot and Fees</b><br>Archers participate in Tournament Week by entering
  one of the following tournaments and paying $5.00 towards the Winners´ Pot
 . Winners will be announced by email and Instagram following Tournament Sat
 urday.&nbsp\;<br>Archers participating in Tournament Saturday or attending 
 any Outdoor 2-9 classes will also pay $30 for their place on the shooting l
 ine\, unless they also take virtual lessons once or twice a week with Coach
  Racae\, in which case\, their fee is $10.<br><br>Enter one of these tourna
 ments:<br><b>Outdoor 2 + 3 Tournament :&nbsp\;</b><br>For beginners at 9m a
 nd 13.5m - One or two rounds (depending on your strength) of 10 ends of 3 a
 rrows each for a total of 30 arrows.<br><b>Outdoor 4-9 Tournament:&nbsp\;</
 b><br>For more advanced archers at 20m+ - Two rounds of 6 ends of 6 arrows 
 each for a total of 72 arrows shot on 122-cm target faces.<br><br>More info
 rmation and registration links at&nbsp\;<a>www.archerytrainingcenter.com</a
 >
