DESCRIPTION:Registration form: OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m<br><br>REMINDER:  E
 veryone needs to come to at least one Training Class per week to be able to
  attend Open Practice. (All indoor classes are training classes.)<br><br>If
  you are not a coach/instructor\, the fees are:  <br>Outdoor Training Class
  (OTC): $52/class or multi-class pack <br>Indoor Training Class (ITC): $43/
 class or multi-class pack or unlimited pack<br>Open Practice (OP): ($50/mo)
   <br><br>If you are a coach/instructor\, you have received an email from C
 oach Racae outlining your fees.<br><br>During the fall (Aug 31-Dec 18)\, fo
 r Coach Racae to coach the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class\, at least 5 archers 
 need to register by <br>8:00 am on Thursdays (for Saturdays) and <br>8:00 a
 m on Fridays (for Sundays) <br>In the case of low or late registrations or 
 cancellations\, another coach/instructor\, when available\, will coach the 
 session as a Training Class or oversee it as an Open Practice instead. If t
 his is not possible\, then the class may need to be cancelled.<br><br>Add y
 our name to the Target Assignment List below or submit the above completed 
 form.<br>Focus primarily on perfecting your form\, <br>slowly increasing yo
 ur physical strength and draw weight\, <br>strengthening your mental progra
 m\, <br>determining your average and personal best\, <br>understanding the 
 spread between the two\, and working on closing it.<br><br>You need your ow
 n equipment <br>Competition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, re
 st\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector
 \, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller
 \, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added until you reach a higher le
 vel\, but you should order them in advance.) <br><br>Wear your ATCI shirt t
 o training.<br><br>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm
  target face you'll move back to the next distance until you reach your com
 petition distance<br>If you trained outdoors in the 2024 season\, you'll re
 turn to the farthest distance you shot.<br><br>Target arrangements may vary
  each session\, depending on who attends and distances needed.<br>Target 1 
 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should always stay at 70m so Ja
 ke can use it for independent practice in between classes.<br>Target 2 at 6
 0m (U18 + Masters competition distance) <br>Target 3 at 50m<br>Target 4+5 a
 t 40m (U15 competition distance) <br>Target 6 at 30m (U13 competition dista
 nce) <br><br>Targets 7-10 at 18m (for those wanting to qualify to shoot com
 petitively at 18m indoors or with Coach Racae's approval)<br><br>Ideally\, 
 we want to practice with two archers/target to replicate outdoor competitio
 n conditions.<br>Alternate daily: Outdoor distance and 18m distance. <br>Fo
 r 18m distance\, put up four 40-cm target faces on one target\, even if few
 er people are shooting the target\, so you practice high/low/left/right. <b
 r>For 18m JOAD\, put up two 60cm target faces on one target side-by-side fo
 r max two people shooting on each target bale.<br>Target Assignments:<br>Ta
 rgets are assigned outdoors in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the
  day\,<br>so add your name next to your distance below. <br>If you need hel
 p or have questions\, email/text Coach Racae<br>(Dotted lines represent ten
 t poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)<br><br><b>Weather : At least 20mph
  winds\, so 20 pts handicap added where noted.</b><br><b>ATCIICT = 2026 ATC
 I Indoor Competition Team (so far) : </b><br>MQS at 18m\, 30-arrow rounds: 
 210 pts or 420 pts (2 rounds)<br><ol><li>Abby</li><li>Adrianne</li><li>Anna
 </li><li>Colby</li><li>Emma</li><li>Finn</li><li>Luke</li><li>Coach Nick</l
 i><li>Sara </li><li>Sophia</li></ol><br>----------------------------------<
 br>1A. (70m)<br>1B<br><br>2A. (60m)  <br>2B<br><br>3A. (50m) <br>----------
 ------------------------<br>3B<br><br>4A. (40m) <br>4B. <br>---------------
 -------------------<br>5A. (40m)<br>5B. <br><br>6A. (30m)<br>--------------
 --------------------<br>6B.<b> Sophia D</b>\, adult\, USAA\, f (18m) - <b>2
 18 pts - CONGRATULATIONs! You're on the 2026 Indoor Competition Team !</b><
 br><br>7A. (18m) <b>Colby K</b>.\, USAA\, adult\, need to pay - 188 + 20 = 
 <b>208 pts</b><br>7B. <b>Finn E\,</b> 13\, <b>169 + 20 = 189 pts</b><br>---
 ------------------------------- <br>8A. (18m) <b>Matt L\,</b> 13\, USAA\, p
 d 80+20 = <b>100 pts</b><br>8B. <b>Rhys E</b> \, 11 \, 47 + 20 = <b>67 pts<
 /b><br><br>9A. (18m) <b>Nick E</b>\, adult = <b>231 pts</b><br>------------
