 nd above (18m)<br><br>Registration links at: <a href="http://www.archerytra
 iningcenter.com/register">www.archerytrainingcenter.com/register</a><br><br
 >Fees:&nbsp\;<br>RECREATIONAL:&nbsp\;<br>$20/cl for 1 hr\; $30/cl for 2 hrs
 \; $40/cl for 3 hrs ON THE SAME DAY.<br>There are also reduced monthly fees
  when you regularly come to more than 3 hrs/week and Progressive fees when 
 you are at 18m and regularly come to more than 5 hrs/week. Ask Coach Racae 
 for more information.<br><br>Your name will be on the list below when we re
 ceive your registration form and fee in advance of the class. When you atte
 nd\, and the class is near full\, you should pay at least one class in adva
 nce to guarantee you have a place on the shooting line next time.&nbsp\;<br
 ><br>When classes are not full\, it's okay to just drop in occasionally for
  the class and pay at that time. However it is difficult to tell how many p
 eople will be dropping in\, so to secure your place\, it is better to regis
 ter and pay in advance to prevent overcrowding. We can only take 10 people 
 on the shooting line at one time.&nbsp\;<br><br>When we have more than 10 a
 rchers\, we will form a second line\, as in a tournament\, which will reduc
 e the number of arrows shot per person within the time. (You can see the ac
 tual attendance and class composition by looking at past classes at&nbsp\;<
 a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/calendar">www.archerytrainingc
 enter.com/calendar</a>.)<br><br>Scores are also listed below\, if you kept 
 score\, which is not required\, except on Master Challenge weeks. You need 
 230 pts on 40cm target or 240 pts on 60cm target to graduate out of your di
 stance into Indoor 3A 13.5m\, and again at 13.5m to get into Indoor 3B at 1
 8m (full distance).<br>PB = Personal Best.&nbsp\;<br><br>Registered archers
 :<br>1. Zoë C.\, JOAD 13.5m - paid<br>2. Lily R.\, JOAD 13.5m - paid<br>3. 
