DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u><b>JAN 26 UPDATE: Classes will 
 resume on Feb 12. Register for new class dates or substitute dates to make 
 up for previously postponed classes for which you´ve already paid.</b><b><b
 r></b><u></u><br><u></u><u></u><b>JAN 7 UPDATE: </b>With the news that Aust
 in/Travis County is now in Stage 5 of COVID-19 risk-based guidelines\, I ha
 ve made the decision to postpone the start of our archery training classes 
 this semester possibly until Austin drops back down to Stage 4.&nbsp\;<br>I
  will review the situation weekly on Fridays and postpone classes on the we
 ekend if Austin is still in Stage 5.&nbsp\;<br><br>I know this is disappoin
 ting to most of you - and no one wants to attend the training classes more 
 than I do. I love to coach you! My main concern\, however\, as always\, is 
 to keep everyone who attends our classes as safe as possible.&nbsp\;<br><br
 >Not to worry\, we will start classes soon again!<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\
 ; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &
 nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbs
 p\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; Coach R
 acae<u></u><br><u></u><br><u></u><br><u></u>REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to a
 dult\, juniors 8+\, and parents! Please read all the info below and in the 
 registration and waivers.<br><br>More information\, registration forms and 
 waivers are available at&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.co
 m">www.archerytrainingcenter.com</a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE of the
 se forms:<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfcwG419ZK9X
 mA4-JlXM-zhjhvSPCF8NCwWJlzFP2w-gRliUw/viewform">2022 Winter/Spring Outdoor 
 1: First-time Class for Juniors + Parents</a>&nbsp\; OR<br><a href="https:/
 /docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSe-YxPKAMTxiC7kVt6fZuQJeidXENYq_iV4rWj1Ra
 XdLhPoew/viewform">2022 Winter/Spring Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Adult
 s</a><br><br>Sign up for just one Outdoor 1 class\, because most people gra
 duate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br><br><b>Yo
 ur name will be added below and your place reserved on a</b> <b>first regis
 tered and paid basis and after we receive 3 things</b>:&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br>20
 22 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM + WAIVERS + FEE<br><br><b>Registered archers
 &nbsp\;</b>at 9m on 40-cm target face:<br><b>Target nos:</b><br>1. <b>Marle
 y S.\,</b> 10\, pd - <b>refunded</b><br>2.<br>3.<br>4.<br>5.<br>6.<br>7.<br
 >8.<br>9.<br>10.<br><br>Space will be limited to 10-15 archers per session 
 depending on the number of family groups in attendance or in accordance wit
 h CDC Guidelines.&nbsp\;<br>Each person will have a target stand\, except a
 fter 10 people have registered\, two members from the same family will shar
 e one target stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be al
 lowed on the field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae.&nbsp\;<
 br>Parents of juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator.
  Parents of juniors 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with t
 heir child for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent
 ) is accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-time Class.&nbsp\;<br><br>We will 
 accept a limited&nbsp\;number of kids under 12 into the program each semest
 er\, depending on the total&nbsp\; number of archers in all the classes. If
  you join before the limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll st
 ay in the program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join
  Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;If you are under 12\, registered and paid after the cut o
 ff\, your fee will be returned to you.&nbsp\;<br><br>Juniors may need to ta
 ke Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by 
 scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/
 end of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate in
 to Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, finger
 sling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($15)<br>fp = form pack (stret
 chband and string loop)\, optional but really needed to practice form\, war
 m up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your s
 cores will be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, y
 ou may not recognize your final score\, because it will have been averaged 
 by taking your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the number 
 of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 3
 0 to get a full round score. After the last class on the weekend\, final sc
 ores will also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more 
 information before your next class.<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
