 ed form.</b><br><br><i>Focus primarily on <br></i><ul><li><i>perfecting you
 r form\, </i></li><li><i>slowly increasing your physical strength and draw 
 weight\, </i></li><li><i>strengthening your mental program\, </i></li><li><
 i>determining your average and personal best\, </i></li><li><i>understandin
 g the spread between the two\, and working on closing it.</i></li></ul><b>Y
 ou need your own equipment </b><br>Competition recurve bow\, sight\, stabil
 izer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicke
 r\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field qu
 iver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added until yo
 u reach a higher level\, but you should order them in advance.) <br><br>Wea
 r your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br><i>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arr
 ow round on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the next distance un
 til you reach your competition distance</i><br><i>If you trained outdoors i
 n the 2024 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.</i><br
 ><i>Target arrangements may vary each session\, depending on who attends an
 d distances needed.</i><br><b>Target 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors</b> competitio
 n distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent pr
 actice in between classes.<br><b>Target 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters</b> competi
 tion distance) <br><b>Target 3 at 50m</b><br><b>Target 4 at 40m</b> (U15 co
 mpetition distance) <br><b>Target 5 at 30m</b> (U13 competition distance) <
 br><b>Targets 6+7+8 at 20m</b> (for those who have shot at 18m indoors or w
 ith Coach Racae's approval)<br><b>Targets 9 + 10 at 13.5m</b> (for those wh
 o have just graduated from indoors at 9m)<br><br>Ideally\, we want to pract
 ice with two archers/target to replicate competition conditions as much as 
 possible.<br><br><b>Target Assignments:</b><br>Targets are assigned outdoor
 s in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\,<br>so add your name
  next to your distance below. <br>If you need help or have questions\, emai
 l/text Coach Racae<br><i>(Dotted lines represent tent poles dividing Target
 s 3\, 6\, and 9.)</i><br>----------------------------------<br>1A. (70m)<br
 >1B<br><br>2A. (60m)  <br>2B<br><br>3A. (50m)  <br>------------------------
 ----------<br>3B<br><br>4A. (40m) <br>4B<br>-------------------------------
 ---<br>5A. (30m)<br>5B. <br><br>6A. (20m)<br>------------------------------
 ----<br>6B. <br><br>7A. (20m)<br>7B. <br>----------------------------------
  <br>8A. (20m)<br>8B. <br><br>9A. (13.5m)<br>------------------------------
 ----<br>9B. <br><br>10A. (13.5m)<br>10B
