DESCRIPTION:Training classes at this location are reserved for competitive 
 and advanced archers..<br><br><b>REMINDER</b>:  Everyone needs to come to a
 t least one Training Class per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (Al
 l Indoor 2-6 at 9m classes are training classes.)<br><br>Coach Racae will c
 oach the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class whenever there are at least 5 archers r
 egistered by Fri 12:00 pm (for Sat) and Sat 12:00 pm (for Sun).   <br><br><
 b>TRAINING CLASS (TC)</b>: <b>$57/archer/3-hr class</b><br>(1x/wk required 
 to attend Open Practice)<br><b>FACILITY FEE (FF) </b>(required each month):
  <b>$75/month/archer</b> due on 1st of the month. (USAA Level 3 Coaches do 
 not pay facility fee.)<br><b>OPEN PRACTICE (OP) </b>Included in facility fe
 e (1-2x/wk recommended)<br><b>PRIVATE LESSON (PL)</b>: $125/hr/archer (1x/m
 o recommended)<br><br><b>Please add your name to the target list below to r
 egister</b><br>Focus primarily on perfecting your form\, <br>slowly increas
 ing your physical strength and draw weight\, <br>strengthening your mental 
 program\, <br>determining your average and personal best\, <br>understandin
 g the spread between the two\, and working on closing it.<br><br><b>EQUIPME
 NT:</b><br>You need your own equipment: <br>Competition recurve bow\, sight
 \, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly
 \, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or
  field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added
  until you reach a higher level\, but you should order them in advance.) <b
 r><br>Wear your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br><b>WEATHER / DAYLIGHT</b><br
 ><br>Session times may vary depending on temperature/daylight conditions.<b
 r>During inclement weather (&lt\;52F or 100F&gt\;\, 20 mph winds\, heavy ra
 in\, lightning) class will move to the Indoor 9m range to practice form and
  be noted on the calendar shortly before the scheduled session.<br><b>TARGE
 T ARRANGEMENTS</b><br>May vary each session\, depending on who attends and 
 distances needed.<br>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-
 cm target face you'll move back to the next distance until you reach your c
 ompetition distance (see below)<br>If you trained outdoors in the 2025 seas
 on\, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.<br><br>Target 1 at 70
 m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake ca
 n use it for independent practice in between classes.<br>Target 2 at 60m (U
 18 + Masters competition distance) <br>Targets 3+4 at 50m<br>Target 5+6 at 
 40m (U15 competition distance) <br>Target 7+8 at 30m (U13 competition dista
 nce) <br>Targets 9 at 20m (for adults who have just graduated out of Indoor
  2)<br>Target 10 at 13.5m (for juniors who have just graduated out of Indoo
 r 2)<br><br>Ideally\, we want to practice with two archers/target to replic
 ate outdoor competition conditions.<br><br><b>TARGET ASSIGNMENTS</b><br>Tar
 gets are assigned outdoors in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the 
 day\, so <b>add your name next to your distance below</b>. <br>If you need 
 help or have questions\, email/text Coach Racae<br>(Dotted lines represent 
 tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)<br><br><b>ATCIOCT</b> = 2026 AT
 CI Outdoor Competition Team  <br><b>MQS </b>at your tournament distance\, 3
 6-arrow rounds on 122-cm target face: <br><b>260 pts</b> or <b>520 pts</b> 
 (2 rounds)<br>----------------------------------<br>1A. (70m)<br>1B<br><br>
 2A. (60m)  <br>2B<br><br>3A. (50m)  <br>----------------------------------<
 br>3B<br><br>4A. (50m) <br>4B. <br>----------------------------------<br>5A
 . (40m)<br>5B. <br><br>6A. (40m) <br>----------------------------------<br>
 6B. <br><br>7A. (30m) <b>Ethan N</b> (3/12)<br>7B. <br>--------------------
 -------------- <br>8A. (30m) <br>8B.<br><br>9A. (20m) <br>-----------------
 -----------------<br>9B. <br><br>10A. (13.5m)<br>10B
LAST-MODIFIED:20260517T084025Z
LOCATION:2324 Bliss Spillar Rd\, Manchaca\, TX 78652\, USA
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5-70m with Coach Racae
TRANSP:OPAQUE
