DESCRIPTION:<i>This class has been cancelled due to low registrations and o
 ther factors.</i><br><i>Looks like everyone's studying this weekend! </i><b
 r><br>Training classes at this location are reserved for competitive and ad
 vanced archers..<br><br>REMINDER:  Everyone needs to come to at least one T
 raining Class per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (All Indoor 2-6 
 at 9m classes are training classes.)<br><br>Coach Racae will coach the Outd
 oor 3-9 Training Class whenever there are at least 5 archers registered by 
 Thursday 12:00 pm (for Sat) and Friday 9:00 am (for Sun)\, except on federa
 l holidays\, because Medicare's GUIDE program does not pay for caregivers o
 n federal holidays!!! Sorry to disappoint!  <br><br>TRAINING CLASS (TC): $5
 7/archer/3-hr class<br>(1x/wk required to attend Open Practice)<br>FACILITY
  FEE (FF) (required each month): $75/month/archer due on 1st of the month. 
 (USAA Level 3 Coaches do not pay facility fee.)<br>OPEN PRACTICE (OP) Inclu
 ded in facility fee (1-2x/wk recommended)<br>PRIVATE LESSON (PL): $125/hr/a
 rcher (1x/mo recommended)<br><br>Please add your name to the target list be
 low to register<br>Focus primarily on perfecting your form\, <br>slowly inc
 reasing your physical strength and draw weight\, <br>strengthening your men
 tal program\, <br>determining your average and personal best\, <br>understa
 nding the spread between the two\, and working on closing it.<br><br>EQUIPM
 ENT:<br>You need your own equipment: <br>Competition recurve bow\, sight\, 
 stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, 
 clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or fi
 eld quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added un
 til you reach a higher level\, but you should order them in advance.) <br><
 br>Wear your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br>WEATHER / DAYLIGHT<br><br>Sessi
 on times may vary depending on temperature/daylight conditions.<br>During i
 nclement weather (&lt\;52F or 100F&gt\;\, 20 mph winds\, heavy rain\, light
 ning) class will move to the Indoor 9m range to practice form and be noted 
 on the calendar shortly before the scheduled session.<br>TARGET ARRANGEMENT
 S<br>May vary each session\, depending on who attends and distances needed.
 <br>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm target face yo
 u'll move back to the next distance until you reach your competition distan
 ce (see below)<br>If you trained outdoors in the 2025 season\, you'll retur
 n to the farthest distance you shot.<br><br>Target 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors 
 competition distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use it for inde
 pendent practice in between classes.<br>Target 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters comp
 etition distance) <br>Targets 3+4 at 50m<br>Target 5+6 at 40m (U15 competit
 ion distance) <br>Target 7+8 at 30m (U13 competition distance) <br>Targets 
 9 at 20m (for adults who have just graduated out of Indoor 2)<br>Target 10 
 at 13.5m (for juniors who have just graduated out of Indoor 2)<br><br>Ideal
 ly\, we want to practice with two archers/target to replicate outdoor compe
 tition conditions.<br><br>TARGET ASSIGNMENTS<br>Targets are assigned outdoo
 rs in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\, so add your name n
 ext to your distance below. <br>If you need help or have questions\, email/
 text Coach Racae<br>(Dotted lines represent tent poles dividing Targets 3\,
  6\, and 9.)<br><br>ATCIOCT = 2026 ATCI Outdoor Competition Team  <br>MQS a
 t your tournament distance\, 36-arrow rounds on 122-cm target face: <br>260
  pts or 520 pts (2 rounds)<br>----------------------------------<br>1A. (70
 m)<br>1B<br><br>2A. (60m)  <br>2B<br><br>3A. (50m)  <br>-------------------
 ---------------<br>3B<br><br>4A. (50m) <br>4B. <br>------------------------
 ----------<br>5A. (40m) Abby Y\, 14<br>5B. <br><br>6A. (40m) <br>----------
 ------------------------<br>6B. <br><br>7A. (30m) Ellie Y\, 11<br>7B.  Sara
  T. (O6 @ 40m)<br>---------------------------------- <br>8A. (30m) <br>8B.<
 br><br>9A. (20m) <br>----------------------------------<br>9B. <br><br>10A.
  (13.5m)<br>10B
