DESCRIPTION:Coach Racae (Recurves only)  Click the Sign Up button at the to
 p of ATCI website to Register for Spring 2016 Indoor 1: First-time Classes 
 for Adults if you are at least 18 years old. This is a requirement to join 
 regular adult training classes. Saturdays: 11:30am-1:30pm (Fee: $25/cl) Sun
 days: 11:30am-1:30pm (Fee: $25/cl)  Enrollment link: https://docs.google.co
 m/forms/d/1sPp_1NRpCtLb-SHXJR1dgEn7LVMV6BFgnCKW6-67GYM/viewform  RECREATION
 AL ADULT CLASSES at Indoor 2-5 and distances (9m\, 13.5m\, 18m)  Sundays: 6
 :00-7:00pm (Fee: $20/cl) (Recurves) Tuesdays: 7:30-8:30pm (Fee: $20/cl) (Co
 mpounds and Recurves)  PROGRESSIVE PROGRAM Indoor 2-5 JOAD and ADULT TRAINI
 NG for those who want to progress faster toward competitive archery by meet
 ing minimum attendance requirements. Saturdays 3:30-5:30pm (Recurves) Sunda
 ys:  3:30-5:30pm (Recurves) Sundays:  6:00-7:00pm (Adults and Indoor 5 only
 ) (Recurves) Tuesdays: 6:30-7:30pm (Compounds and Recurves) Tuesdays: 7:30-
 8:30pm (Adults and Indoor 5 only) (Compounds and Recurves) Wednesdays: 6:30
 -8:00pm (Recurves)  Progressive weekly fees (after meeting previous week's 
 attendance requirement): Indoor 3A at 13.5m: $48/wk (min. 4 hrs) Indoor 3B 
 at 18m:    $55/wk (min. 5 hrs) Indoor 4 at 18m:      $60/wk (min. 6 hrs) In
 door 5 at 18m:      $72/wk (min. 8 hrs)  USA Archery's Adult Training Progr
 am (ATP) follows a similar path to the Junior Olympic Archery Development (
 JOAD) program.   Your first step is to take an Indoor 1: First-time Class f
 or Adults. Just click the link or the Sign Up button at the top of this web
 site.  Everyone starts out in our Recreational program at 9 meters. As you 
 improve you progress to 13.5 meters then on to 18 meters indoors.   We welc
 ome adult recurve and compound Olympic target archers at all levels of expe
 rience.  Recurve archers can attend any of the group classes above or book 
 private lessons with Coach Racae or Instructor Dale. Compound archers can a
 ttend the group class on Tues. evenings or book private lessons with Coach 
 Dan or Instructor Bailey.  Experienced competitive archers need to be evalu
 ated by Coach Racae for advanced placement in either the Progressive Progra
 m or recommendation to the Competitive Archery Program with Coach Alex.  Wh
 en you decide that you are interested in competing you'll apply to join USA
  Archery Level 4 NTS and JDT Coach Alex Meyer's Competitive Archery Program
  (CAP).
