DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u>
 </u><u></u>REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to adult\, juniors 8+\, and parents! 
 Please read all the info below and in the registration and waivers.<br><br>
 More information\, registration forms and waivers are available at&nbsp\;<a
  href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrainingcenter.com<
 /a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE of these forms:<br><a href="https://doc
 s.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfcwG419ZK9XmA4-JlXM-zhjhvSPCF8NCwWJlzFP2w-gR
 liUw/viewform">2022 Winter/Spring Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Juniors +
  Parents</a>&nbsp\; OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQ
 LSe-YxPKAMTxiC7kVt6fZuQJeidXENYq_iV4rWj1RaXdLhPoew/viewform">2022 Winter/Sp
 ring Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Adults</a><br><br>Sign up for just one
  Outdoor 1 class\, because most juniors 11+ and all adults graduate out of 
 this class into Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<u></u><br><br><u></u><b>W
 eather conditions today:</b> 51F-60F\, wind chill 47F-57F\, 10 mph winds\, 
 cloudy then sunny and bright! Felt a little cold and windy!<br><br><b>Your 
 name will be added below and your place reserved on a</b> <b>first register
 ed and paid basis and after we receive 3 things</b>:&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br>2022 
 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM + WAIVERS + FEE<br><br><u></u><b>Registered arc
 hers&nbsp\;</b>at 9m on 40-cm target face unless otherwise noted below:<u><
 /u><br><u></u>:<br><b>Target Assignments:</b><br>1.<u></u><br><u></u>2.<u><
 /u><br><u></u>3.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<b>Evie P.\,</b> 14\, on 60-cm target face - 
 pd - <b>68 pts </b>-&gt\; <b>Outdoor 2</b><br>4.&nbsp\; <b>Callie D.</b>\, 
 14\, on 60-cm target face - pd - <b>20 pts</b> -&gt\; <b>Outdoor 1</b><br>5
 .&nbsp\; <b>Ariel V</b>.\, dad\, pd - <b>12 pts</b><br>6.&nbsp\; <b>Gabe V.
 </b>\, 14 - pd - <b>39 pts</b> -&gt\; <b>Outdoor 2</b><br>7.&nbsp\; <b>Chri
 stian V.\,</b> 10 on 60-cm target face - pd&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<b>?&nbsp\;</b>-&g
 t\;&nbsp\;<b>Outdoor 1</b><br>8.&nbsp\; <b>Emily V. </b>mom - pd<u></u>&nbs
 p\;- <b>70 pts</b><br>9.<br>10.<br><br>Space will be limited to 10-15 arche
 rs per session depending on the number of family groups in attendance or in
  accordance with CDC Guidelines.&nbsp\;<br>Each person will have a target s
 tand\, except after 10 people have registered\, two members from the same f
 amily will share one target stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spect
 ator will be allowed on the field until further notice or approved by Coach
  Racae.&nbsp\;<br>Parents of juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch 
 as a spectator. Parents of juniors 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, a
 nd shoot with their child for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-yea
 r-old (+ parent) is accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-time Class.&nbsp\;<
 br><br>We will accept a limited&nbsp\;number of kids under 12 into the prog
 ram each semester\, depending on the total&nbsp\; number of archers in all 
 the classes. If you join before the limit is reached\, and are younger than
  12\, you´ll stay in the program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed
  and later join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;If you are under 12\, registered and paid 
 after the cut off\, your fee will be returned to you.&nbsp\;<br><br>Juniors
  may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying to get int
 o Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on avera
 ge about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score
  to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fin
 gertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($15)<br>fp = f
 orm pack (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but really needed to prac
 tice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1
  class\, your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a complete round 
 (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, because it will have
  been averaged by taking your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing
  by the number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multip
 lying that by 30 to get a full round score. After the last class on the wee
 kend\, final scores will also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an e
 mail with more information before your next class.<u></u><u></u><u></u><u><
 /u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
