 t a limited&nbsp\;number of kids under 12 into the program each semester\, 
 depending on the total&nbsp\; number of archers in all the classes. If you 
 join before the limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in
  the program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outd
 oor 2.&nbsp\;If you are under 12\, registered and paid after the cut off\, 
 your fee will be returned to you.&nbsp\;<br><br>Juniors may need to take Ou
 tdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scori
 ng 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end o
 f 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Ou
 tdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling
 )\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($15)<br>fp = form pack (stretchban
 d and string loop)\, optional but really needed to practice form\, warm up 
 before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores
  will be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you ma
 y not recognize your final score\, because it will have been averaged by ta
 king your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the number of ar
 rows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to 
 get a full round score. After the last class on the weekend\, final scores 
 will also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more infor
 mation before your next class.<u></u><u></u></html-blob>
