DESCRIPTION:REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to adult\, juniors 8+\, and parents!
  Please read all the info below and in the registration and waivers.<br><br
 >More information\, registration forms and waivers are available at <a href
 ="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com"><u><u><u><u>www.archerytrainingcent
 er.com</u></u></u></u></a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE of these forms:<
 br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeciOgkyuKTLZ5_ZaWCEyQ
 KYSX1fWGpP5qakhT6OuAc6jJ_FQ/viewform"><u>2023 Outdoor 1: First-time Class f
 or Adults</u></a>  OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQL
 Sc_bYEFoE4oXkcm0T6fZK99fu_q6lL8wZGClXyfa1GZbahh-g/viewform"><u>2023 Outdoor
  1: First-time Class for Juniors and Parents</u></a><br><br>Sign up for jus
 t ONE Outdoor 1 class\, because most people graduate out of this class into
  Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br><br>Your name will be added below and
  your place reserved on a first registered and paid basis and after we rece
 ive 3 things:  <br><b>2023 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM   +  MEMBERSHIP AND 
 WAIVERS PACKET +   FEE</b><b><br></b><u></u><br><b>USA Archery Level 4 NTS 
 Coach Racae Meyer and other instructors/coaches.</b><br><b>See </b><a href=
 "https://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/who-we-are"><u><u>https://www.archer
 ytrainingcenter.com/who-we-are</u></u></a><b><br></b><br><b>Registered arch
 ers </b>at 9m on 40-cm target face unless otherwise noted:<u></u><br><u></u
 ><br><b>Target Assignments:</b>  <br><br>6. <b>Emily J.\, </b>adult\, pd - 
 <b>65 pts -&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br><br>7.  <b>Kenny J.\, </b>adult\, pd - <b
 >136 pts -&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br><br>8.  <b>Amelia R.\, </b><span>10\, on 6
 0-cm target face - pd - <b>45+ pts -&gt\; Outdoor 2</b></span><br><br>9.   
 <b>Ke D.\, </b>adult\, awaiting check - <b>113 pts  </b><b>-&gt\; Outdoor 2
 </b><br><br>10. <b>Daisy D.\, </b>8\, on 60-cm target face - awaiting check
  - <b>182 pts -&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br>.<br><br><b>Colleen H.\, </b>adult\, 
 DNA - awaiting check - need substitute date<br><b>Weston H.\, </b>11\, on 6
 0-cm target face - DNA - awaiting check - need substitute date<br><br>Space
  will be limited to 10-15 archers per session depending on the number of fa
 mily groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC Guidelines. <br>Each pe
 rson will have a target stand\, except after 10 people have registered\, me
 mbers may be assigned to share a target stand.<br>The archer and a maximum 
 of one spectator will be allowed on the field until further notice or appro
 ved by Coach Racae. <br>Parents of juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or 
 watch as a spectator. <br>Parents of juniors 8-9 years old need to register
 \, pay\, and shoot with their child for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of
  one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-time Clas
 s. <br><br>We will accept a limited number of kids under 12 into the progra
 m each semester\, depending on the total  number of archers in all the clas
 ses. If you join before the limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, yo
 u´ll stay in the program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and lat
 er join Outdoor 2. If you are under 12\, registered and paid after the cut 
 off\, your fee will be returned to you. <br><br>Juniors may need to take Ou
 tdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scori
 ng 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end o
 f 3 arrows. <br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 
 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, wh
 ich will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($18) Please pay for this at the field\, 
 as our stock fluctuates because of dealer supply fluctuations<br>fp = form 
 pack (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but really needed to practice
  form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 cla
 ss\, your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 
 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, because it will have bee
 n averaged by taking your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by 
 the number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplyin
 g that by 30 to get a full round score. After the last first-time class eac
 h weekend\, final scores may also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in 
 an email with more information before your next class.
