DESCRIPTION:<i>This class has been moved to the indoor 9m range  due to hea
 vy rain and difficult field conditions. Let's work hard on form and have so
 me fun!</i><br><br>Training classes at this location are reserved for compe
 titive and advanced archers..<br><br>REMINDER:  Everyone needs to come to a
 t least one Training Class per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (Al
 l Indoor 2-6 at 9m classes are training classes.)<br><br>Coach Racae will c
 oach the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class whenever there are at least 5 archers r
 egistered by Thursday 12:00 pm (for Sat) and Friday 9:00 am (for Sun)\, exc
 ept on federal holidays\, because Medicare's GUIDE program does not pay for
  caregivers on federal holidays!!! Sorry to disappoint!  <br><br>TRAINING C
 LASS (TC): $57/archer/3-hr class<br>(1x/wk required to attend Open Practice
 )<br>FACILITY FEE (FF) (required each month): $75/month/archer due on 1st o
 f the month. (USAA Level 3 Coaches do not pay facility fee.)<br>OPEN PRACTI
 CE (OP) Included in facility fee (1-2x/wk recommended)<br>PRIVATE LESSON (P
 L): $125/hr/archer (1x/mo recommended)<br><br>Please add your name to the t
 arget list below to register<br>Focus primarily on perfecting your form\, <
 br>slowly increasing your physical strength and draw weight\, <br>strengthe
 ning your mental program\, <br>determining your average and personal best\,
  <br>understanding the spread between the two\, and working on closing it.<
 br><br>EQUIPMENT:<br>You need your own equipment: <br>Competition recurve b
 ow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-ba
 r assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger slin
 g\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may no
 t be added until you reach a higher level\, but you should order them in ad
 vance.) <br><br>Wear your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br>WEATHER / DAYLIGHT
 <br><br>Session times may vary depending on temperature/daylight conditions
 .<br>During inclement weather (&lt\;52F or 100F&gt\;\, 20 mph winds\, heavy
  rain\, lightning) class will move to the Indoor 9m range to practice form 
 and be noted on the calendar shortly before the scheduled session.<br>TARGE
 T ARRANGEMENTS<br>May vary each session\, depending on who attends and dist
 ances needed.<br>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm t
 arget face you'll move back to the next distance until you reach your compe
 tition distance (see below)<br>If you trained outdoors in the 2025 season\,
  you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.<br><br>Target 1 at 70m (U
 21 + Seniors competition distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can us
 e it for independent practice in between classes.<br>Target 2 at 60m (U18 +
  Masters competition distance) <br>Targets 3+4 at 50m<br>Target 5+6 at 40m 
 (U15 competition distance) <br>Target 7+8 at 30m (U13 competition distance)
  <br>Targets 9 at 20m (for adults who have just graduated out of Indoor 2)<
 br>Target 10 at 13.5m (for juniors who have just graduated out of Indoor 2)
 <br><br>Ideally\, we want to practice with two archers/target to replicate 
 outdoor competition conditions.<br><br>TARGET ASSIGNMENTS<br>Targets are as
 signed outdoors in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\, so ad
 d your name next to your distance below. <br>If you need help or have quest
 ions\, email/text Coach Racae<br>(Dotted lines represent tent poles dividin
 g Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)<br><br>ATCIOCT = 2026 ATCI Outdoor Competition Te
 am  <br>MQS at your tournament distance\, 36-arrow rounds on 122-cm target 
 face: <br>260 pts or 520 pts (2 rounds)<br>--------------------------------
 --<br>1A. (70m)<br>1B<br><br>2A. (60m)  <br>2B<br><br>3A. (50m)  Colby K.\,
  adult USAA<br>----------------------------------<br>3B. Adrianne M.\, adul
 t\, USAA pd.<br><br>4A. (50m) <br>4B. <br>---------------------------------
 -<br>5A. (40m) Luke T\, 17\, USAA pd.<br>5B. <br><br>6A. (40m) <br>--------
