 p - 75 pts</b><br><u></u>4. <b>Jim H.</b>\, adult - pd - <b>substituted for
  12/18 - 27 pts</b><br>5. <b>Carol S.</b>\, adult - pd<br>6. <b>Joseph H</b
 >.\, adult - pd - <b>43 pts</b><br>7. <b>Linda T.\,</b> adult - pd - <b>42 
 pts</b><br>8. <b>Nate L.\,</b> adult - pd - <b>125 pts</b><br><u></u>9A. <b
 >Alex B.</b>\, dad - pd - <b>substituted for 12/19 </b>- <b>77 pts</b><u></
 u><br><u></u>9B. <b>Margaux B</b>.\, 14 - pd - <b>substituted for 12/19 - 3
 8 pts -&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br>10A. <b>Juan R.</b>\, dad - pd - <b>substitut
 ed for 1/9 -&nbsp\;</b><b>95 pts</b><br>10B.<b> Ela R.</b>\, 9\, on 60-cm t
 arget face - pd - <b>substituted for 1/9&nbsp\; </b>- stays in Outdoor 1<br
 ><br>Space will be limited to 10-15 archers per session depending on the nu
 mber of family groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC Guidelines.&n
 bsp\;<br>Each person will have a target stand\, except after 10 people have
  registered\, two members from the same family will share one target stand.
 <br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field 
 until further notice or approved by Coach Racae.&nbsp\;<br>Parents of junio
 rs 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator. Parents of juniors
  8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their child for grea
 ter safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into 
 each Outdoor 1: First-time Class.&nbsp\;<br><br>We will accept a limited&nb
 sp\;number of kids under 12 into the program each semester\, depending on t
 he total&nbsp\; number of archers in all the classes. If you join before th
 e limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program a
 nd take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;I
 f you are under 12\, registered and paid after the cut off\, your fee will 
 be returned to you.&nbsp\;<br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or
  three times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. If 
 you are 12+ and did not quite finish an entire round of 30 arrows due to ti
 me limits\, but improved over the arrows you did shoot\, you may move into 
 Outdoor 2\, if you have at least 35 points. You´ll make it as soon as you s
 core on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need a 
 minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (a
 rmguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($
 15)<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but really n
 eeded to practice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of e
 ach Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a co
 mplete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, because
  it will have been averaged by taking your recorded score from your scoreca
 rd\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, an
 d then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round score. After the last cla
 ss on the weekend\, final scores will also be sent to all Outdoor 1 partici
 pants in an email with more information before your next class.<u></u><u></
 u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u>
