CREATED:20211220T034437Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u>REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to adult\, 
 juniors 8+\, and parents! Please read all the info below and in the registr
 ation and waivers.<br><br>More information\, registration forms and waivers
  are available at&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.
 archerytrainingcenter.com</a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE of these form
 s:<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfcwG419ZK9XmA4-JlX
 M-zhjhvSPCF8NCwWJlzFP2w-gRliUw/viewform">2022 Winter/Spring Outdoor 1: Firs
 t-time Class for Juniors + Parents</a>&nbsp\; OR<br><a href="https://docs.g
 oogle.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSe-YxPKAMTxiC7kVt6fZuQJeidXENYq_iV4rWj1RaXdLhPoe
 w/viewform">2022 Winter/Spring Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Adults</a><b
 r><br>Sign up for just one Outdoor 1 class\, because most juniors 11+ and a
 ll adults graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.
 <u></u><br><br><b>Your name will be added below and your place reserved on 
 a</b> <b>first registered and paid basis and after we receive 3 things</b>:
 &nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br>2022 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM + WAIVERS + FEE<br><br><
 b>Registered archers&nbsp\;</b>at 9m on 40-cm target face:<br><b>Target nos
 :</b><br>1.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br>2. Bryson F.\, 13<br>3. Aidan W.\, 14<br>4. Na
 than S.\, waiver needed<br>5.<br>6.<br>7.<br>8.<br>9.<br>10.<br><br>Space w
 ill be limited to 10-15 archers per session depending on the number of fami
 ly groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC Guidelines.&nbsp\;<br>Eac
 h person will have a target stand\, except after 10 people have registered\
 , two members from the same family will share one target stand.<br>The arch
 er and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field until furthe
 r notice or approved by Coach Racae.&nbsp\;<br>Parents of juniors 10+ can s
 ign up as an archer or watch as a spectator. Parents of juniors 8-9 years o
 ld need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their child for greater safety.<
 br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into each Outdoor
  1: First-time Class.&nbsp\;<br><br>We will accept a limited&nbsp\;number o
 f kids under 12 into the program each semester\, depending on the total&nbs
 p\; number of archers in all the classes. If you join before the limit is r
 eached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take othe
 r Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;If you are un
 der 12\, registered and paid after the cut off\, your fee will be returned 
 to you.&nbsp\;<br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times
  before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it 
 as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adul
 ts don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = acces
 sories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed f
 or Outdoor 2. ($15)<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, optio
 nal but really needed to practice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br
 >At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we did
  not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final
  score\, because it will have been averaged by taking your recorded score f
 rom your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot to get an ar
 row average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round score. Af
 ter the last class on the weekend\, final scores will also be sent to all O
 utdoor 1 participants in an email with more information before your next cl
 ass.<u></u><u></u></html-blob>
