CREATED:20220102T020915Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u><br><b>Tournaments are held at 
 the end of each calendar month at 10:30 am - 12:30 pm on Saturdays and Sund
 ays</b>\, weather permitting.&nbsp\;<u></u>If you are new to our program\, 
 come and try it\, so you will be more comfortable and better prepared next 
 month!<br><br><u></u>The only differences between the regular training sess
 ions and the tournaments are that we are more closely reproducing tournamen
 t conditions\, which include:<u></u><br><ul><li><u></u>No coaching while yo
 u are on the shooting line (but\, as in a real tournament\, y<u></u>ou can 
 always ask the coach for help in between the ends.) This is your chance to 
 find out how well you can do the form on your own.</li><li><u></u>You will 
 shoot more arrows :&nbsp\; 2 practice ends + Two rounds -&nbsp\;<u></u>60 a
 rrows at 9m and 13.5m or 72 arrows at 20m-70m</li><li><u></u>You will score
  every arrow for two rounds.&nbsp\;<u></u></li><li><u></u>The ends will be 
 timed. You´ll have 4 min to shoot 6 arrows.<u></u></li><li>Everyone will be
  shooting at close-to-regular tournament spacing so there will be two arche
 rs on each target about 3 ft apart\, depending on the number of registratio
 ns</li><li>There will be a maximum of 20 archers on the shooting line at th
 e same time. Awesome! (Lots of arrow flying towards the targets!)</li></ul>
 <u></u><b>Outside of the tournament weeks</b>\, each week the focus of your
  lessons will be on particular Steps of Shooting of the NTS (National Train
 ing System) shot cycle\, to help you focus and improve your form\, which\, 
 as we all know\, leads to greater precision (tighter groups of arrows) and 
 ultimately greater accuracy (tight groups of arrows dead center).<u></u><br
 ><br><u></u><b>FEBRUARY</b><br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>12-18</b>&n
 bsp\;Welcome Back: Understanding&nbsp\; NTS Concepts&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br><b>&n
 bsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>19-25</b>&nbsp\;NTS Steps 1+2: STANCE + NOCK&nb
 sp\;&nbsp\;<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>26 - MAR 4: MASTER CHALLENG
 E TOURNAMENT WEEK (Pin Shoot)</b><br><b>MARCH</b><br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nb
 sp\;5-11</b>&nbsp\;NTS Step 3: HOOK &amp\; GRIP&nbsp\; &nbsp\;<u></u><br><u
 ></u>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;<b>12-18&nbsp\;</b>NTS Step 4: SET<u></u><br><u
 ></u><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;19-25</b>&nbsp\;<u></u>NTS Step 5: SET-UP&nb
 sp\;&nbsp\;<br><u></u><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>26 - APR 1: MASTER C
 HALLENGE TOURNAMENT WEEKEND (Pin Shoot)</b><br><b>APRIL</b><br><b>&nbsp\; &
 nbsp\; &nbsp\;2-8</b>&nbsp\;<u></u>NTS Step 6 DRAW to LOAD&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &
 nbsp\;<br><u></u><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;9-15&nbsp\;</b><u></u>NTS Step 7
  ANCHOR&nbsp\; &nbsp\;<br><u></u><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;16-22&nbsp\;</b>
 <u></u>NTS Step 8 TRANSFER to HOLD<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;<b>23-29&nbsp\
 ;</b>NTS Step 9 EXPAND / AIM<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;30 - MAY 6: MASTE
 R CHALLENGE TOURNAMENT WEEKEND (Pin Shoot)</b><br><u></u><b>MAY</b><br><b>&
 nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>7-13&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</b>NTS Step 10 RELEASE and 
 FOLLOW-THROUGH<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>14-20</b>&nbsp\;<u></u>N
 TS Step 11 FEEDBACK&nbsp\;</html-blob><br><html-blob>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\
 ;<b>21-27 </b>Putting it all together!<br><u></u><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;
 </b><b>28-29 : END OF SEMESTER MASTER CHALLENGE TOURNAMENT WEEKEND (Pin Sho
 ot)</b><br><br>Your goal is always to replicate the NTS step(s) mindfully a
 nd consistently on every shot.<br><br>You do not need to score every class.
  In fact\, it would be more beneficial to you if you scored only during Mas
 ter Challenge Tournament Weeks\, which happen the last week of each month. 
 This is because working on the NTS Steps of Shooting (your form) is more ea
 sily done without the distraction of the target face or scoring\, and you w
 ill improve faster.<br><br>As you reach higher levels\, you will learn the 
 NTS Steps in progressively greater detail.<br>The NTS Steps are cumulative 
 with each step most successfully completed if the previous steps have been 
 completed mindfully.&nbsp\;<br><br>Your ability to learn and understand the
  NTS Steps\, and use deep focus on these Steps while shooting outdoors and 
 while using your stretchband/string loop at home will propel you to higher 
 levels fast!<br><br><b>Goals by the end of the semester:&nbsp\;</b><br>See 
 Coach Racae´s email ¨2022 New Year´s Goals¨<br><u></u><u></u><u></u></html-
 blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260517T083255Z
SEQUENCE:3
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:ATCI OUTDOOR 2-9 END-OF-SEMESTER TOURNAMENT  (Pin Shoot)
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
