CREATED:20251111T213821Z
DESCRIPTION:Training classes at this location are reserved for competitive 
 and advanced archers..\n\nREMINDER:  Everyone needs to come to at least one
  Training Class per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (All Indoor 2-
 6 at 9m classes are training classes.)\n\nCoach Racae will coach the Outdoo
 r 3-9 Training Class whenever there are at least 5 archers registered by Th
 ursday 12:00 pm (for Sat) and Friday 9:00 am (for Sun)\, except on federal 
 holidays\, because Medicare's GUIDE program does not pay for caregivers on 
 federal holidays!!! Sorry to disappoint!  \n\nTRAINING CLASS (TC): $57/arch
 er/3-hr class\n(1x/wk required to attend Open Practice)\nFACILITY FEE (FF) 
 (required each month): $75/month/archer due on 1st of the month. (USAA Leve
 l 3 Coaches do not pay facility fee.)\nOPEN PRACTICE (OP) Included in facil
 ity fee (1-2x/wk recommended)\nPRIVATE LESSON (PL): $125/hr/archer (1x/mo r
 ecommended)\n\nPlease add your name to the target list below to register\nF
 ocus primarily on perfecting your form\, \nslowly increasing your physical 
 strength and draw weight\, \nstrengthening your mental program\, \ndetermin
 ing your average and personal best\, \nunderstanding the spread between the
  two\, and working on closing it.\n\nEQUIPMENT:\nYou need your own equipmen
 t: \nCompetition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 car
 bon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard
 \, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Cl
 icker and side rods may not be added until you reach a higher level\, but y
 ou should order them in advance.) \n\nWear your ATCI shirt to training.\n\n
 WEATHER / DAYLIGHT\n\nSession times may vary depending on temperature/dayli
 ght conditions.\nDuring inclement weather (<52F or 100F>\, 20 mph winds\, h
 eavy rain\, lightning) class will move to the Indoor 9m range to practice f
 orm and be noted on the calendar shortly before the scheduled session.\nTAR
 GET ARRANGEMENTS\nMay vary each session\, depending on who attends and dist
 ances needed.\nWhen you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm tar
 get face you'll move back to the next distance until you reach your competi
 tion distance (see below)\nIf you trained outdoors in the 2025 season\, you
 'll return to the farthest distance you shot.\n\nTarget 1 at 70m (U21 + Sen
 iors competition distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use it for
  independent practice in between classes.\nTarget 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters c
 ompetition distance) \nTargets 3+4 at 50m\nTarget 5+6 at 40m (U15 competiti
 on distance) \nTarget 7+8 at 30m (U13 competition distance) \nTargets 9 at 
 20m (for adults who have just graduated out of Indoor 2)\nTarget 10 at 13.5
 m (for juniors who have just graduated out of Indoor 2)\n\nIdeally\, we wan
 t to practice with two archers/target to replicate outdoor competition cond
 itions.\n\nTARGET ASSIGNMENTS\nTargets are assigned outdoors in advance to 
 reduce confusion and delay on the day\, so add your name next to your dista
 nce below. \nIf you need help or have questions\, email/text Coach Racae\n(
 Dotted lines represent tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)\n\nATCIO
 CT = 2026 ATCI Outdoor Competition Team  \nMQS at your tournament distance\
 , 36-arrow rounds on 122-cm target face: \n260 pts or 520 pts (2 rounds)\n-
 ---------------------------------\n1A. (70m)\n1B\n\n2A. (60m)  \n2B\n\n3A. 
 (50m)  \n----------------------------------\n3B\n\n4A. (50m) \n4B. \n------
 ----------------------------\n5A. (40m) \n5B. \n\n6A. (40m) \n-------------
 ---------------------\n6B. \n\n7A. (30m) \n7B.  Sara T. (O6 @ 40m)\n-------
 --------------------------- \n8A. (30m) \n8B.\n\n9A. (20m) \n--------------
 --------------------\n9B. \n\n10A. (13.5m)\n10B
