DESCRIPTION:Today's class has been moved indoors to the 9m range due to hea
 vy rain and lightning during the time of the class. Great time to work on f
 orm with the monitors and cameras\, especially on the back end of the shot 
 - Transfer to Hold\, Expand/Aim\, Release/Follow-thrpugh. Looking forward t
 o seeing you all there.<br><br>Training classes at this location are reserv
 ed for competitive and advanced archers..<br><br>REMINDER:  Everyone needs 
 to come to at least one Training Class per week to be able to attend Open P
 ractice. (All Indoor 2-6 at 9m classes are training classes.)<br><br>Coach 
 Racae will coach the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class whenever there are at least
  5 archers registered by Fri 12:00 pm (for Sat) and Sat 12:00 pm (for Sun).
    <br><br>TRAINING CLASS (TC): $57/archer/3-hr class<br>(1x/wk required to
  attend Open Practice)<br>FACILITY FEE (FF) (required each month): $75/mont
 h/archer due on 1st of the month. (USAA Level 3 Coaches do not pay facility
  fee.)<br>OPEN PRACTICE (OP) Included in facility fee (1-2x/wk recommended)
 <br>PRIVATE LESSON (PL): $125/hr/archer (1x/mo recommended)<br><br>Please a
 dd your name to the target list below to register<br>Focus primarily on per
 fecting your form\, <br>slowly increasing your physical strength and draw w
 eight\, <br>strengthening your mental program\, <br>determining your averag
 e and personal best\, <br>understanding the spread between the two\, and wo
 rking on closing it.<br><br>EQUIPMENT:<br>You need your own equipment: <br>
 Competition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon a
 rrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fi
 ngertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker
  and side rods may not be added until you reach a higher level\, but you sh
 ould order them in advance.) <br><br>Wear your ATCI shirt to training.<br><
 br>WEATHER / DAYLIGHT<br><br>Session times may vary depending on temperatur
 e/daylight conditions.<br>During inclement weather (&lt\;52F or 100F&gt\;\,
  20 mph winds\, heavy rain\, lightning) class will move to the Indoor 9m ra
 nge to practice form and be noted on the calendar shortly before the schedu
 led session.<br>TARGET ARRANGEMENTS<br>May vary each session\, depending on
  who attends and distances needed.<br>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow 
 round on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the next distance until
  you reach your competition distance (see below)<br>If you trained outdoors
  in the 2025 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.<br><
 br>Target 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should always stay 
 at 70m so Jake can use it for independent practice in between classes.<br>T
 arget 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition distance) <br>Targets 3+4 at 50m<
 br>Target 5+6 at 40m (U15 competition distance) <br>Target 7+8 at 30m (U13 
 competition distance) <br>Targets 9 at 20m (for adults who have just gradua
 ted out of Indoor 2)<br>Target 10 at 13.5m (for juniors who have just gradu
 ated out of Indoor 2)<br><br>Ideally\, we want to practice with two archers
 /target to replicate outdoor competition conditions.<br><br>TARGET ASSIGNME
 NTS<br>Targets are assigned outdoors in advance to reduce confusion and del
 ay on the day\, so add your name next to your distance below. <br>If you ne
 ed help or have questions\, email/text Coach Racae<br>(Dotted lines represe
 nt tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)<br><br>ATCIOCT = 2026 ATCI O
 utdoor Competition Team  <br>MQS at your tournament distance\, 36-arrow rou
 nds on 122-cm target face: <br>260 pts or 520 pts (2 rounds)<br>-----------
 -----------------------<br><ol><li><b>Adrianne M</b>. USAA\, adult pd - 3 h
 rs</li><li><b>Abby Y\,</b> USAA\, 13\, pd - 3 hrs</li><li><b>Emma A.</b>\, 
 14\, USAA\, pd - 3 hrs</li><li><b>Ellie Y\,</b> USAA 11\, pd - 3 hrs</li><l
 i><b>Drew S.</b>\, USAA\, OB\, pd - 3 hrs</li><li><b>Chi C</b>. USAA\, adul
 t\, pd (11/12) - 3 hrs</li><li><b>Logan C</b>. 9\, USAA\, 9 (12/12) - 3 hrs
 </li><li><b>Sara T.</b>\, 15?\, USAA\, \, pd - 3 hrs</li></ol>
