DESCRIPTION:REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to adult\, juniors 8+\, and parents!
  Please read all the info below and in the registration and waivers.<br><br
 >More information\, registration forms and waivers are available at&nbsp\;<
 a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrainingcenter.com
 </a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE of these forms:<br><a href="https://do
 cs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfcwG419ZK9XmA4-JlXM-zhjhvSPCF8NCwWJlzFP2w-g
 RliUw/viewform" id="ow3654" __is_owner="true">2022 Winter/Spring Outdoor 1:
  First-time Class for Juniors + Parents</a>&nbsp\; OR<br><a href="https://d
 ocs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSe-YxPKAMTxiC7kVt6fZuQJeidXENYq_iV4rWj1RaXd
 LhPoew/viewform" id="ow3665" __is_owner="true">2022 Winter/Spring Outdoor 1
 : First-time Class for Adults</a><br><br>Sign up for just one Outdoor 1 cla
 ss\, because most people graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after th
 e first lesson.<br><br><b>Your name will be added below and your place rese
 rved on a</b> <b>first registered and paid basis and after we receive 3 thi
 ngs</b>:&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br>2022 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM + WAIVERS + FEE<
 br><br><b>Registered archers&nbsp\;</b>at 9m on 40-cm target face:<br><b>Ta
 rget nos:</b><br>1.&nbsp\;<br>2.<br>3.<br>4.<br>5.<br>6.<br>7.<br>8.<br>9.<
 br>10.<br><br>Space will be limited to 10-15 archers per session depending 
 on the number of family groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC Guid
 elines.&nbsp\;<br>Each person will have a target stand\, except after 10 pe
 ople have registered\, two members from the same family will share one targ
 et stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on t
 he field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae.&nbsp\;<br>Parents
  of juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator. Parents o
 f juniors 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their child
  for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accep
 ted into each Outdoor 1: First-time Class.&nbsp\;<br><br>We will accept a l
 imited&nbsp\;number of kids under 12 into the program each semester\, depen
 ding on the total&nbsp\; number of archers in all the classes. If you join 
 before the limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the 
 program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2
 .&nbsp\;If you are under 12\, registered and paid after the cut off\, your 
 fee will be returned to you.&nbsp\;<br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor
  1 two or three times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50
  pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 a
 rrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor
  2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, w
 hich will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($15)<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and
  string loop)\, optional but really needed to practice form\, warm up befor
 e classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will
  be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not
  recognize your final score\, because it will have been averaged by taking 
 your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrows 
 you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a
  full round score. After the last class on the weekend\, final scores will 
 also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more informatio
 n before your next class.
