DESCRIPTION:Training classes at this location are reserved for competitive 
 and advanced archers..<br><br>REMINDER:  Everyone needs to come to at least
  one Training Class per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (All Indoo
 r 2-6 at 9m classes are training classes.)<br><br>Coach Racae will coach th
 e Outdoor 3-9 Training Class whenever there are at least 5 archers register
 ed by Fri 12:00 pm (for Sat) and Sat 12:00 pm (for Sun).   <br><br>TRAINING
  CLASS (TC): $57/archer/3-hr class outdoors (1x/wk required to attend Open 
 Practice)<br>FACILITY FEE (FF) (required each month): $75/month/archer due 
 on 1st of the month. (USAA Level 3 Coaches do not pay facility fee.)<br>OPE
 N PRACTICE (OP) Included in facility fee (1-2x/wk recommended)<br>PRIVATE L
 ESSON (PL): $125/hr/archer (1x/mo recommended)<br><br>Please add your name 
 to the target list below to register<br>Focus primarily on perfecting your 
 form\, <br>slowly increasing your physical strength and draw weight\, <br>s
 trengthening your mental program\, <br>determining your average and persona
 l best\, <br>understanding the spread between the two\, and working on clos
 ing it.<br><br>EQUIPMENT:<br>You need your own equipment: <br>Competition r
 ecurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side 
 rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, fin
 ger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rod
 s may not be added until you reach a higher level\, but you should order th
 em in advance.) <br><br>Wear your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br>WEATHER / 
 DAYLIGHT<br><br>Session times may vary depending on temperature/daylight co
 nditions.<br>During inclement weather (&lt\;52F or 100F&gt\;\, 20 mph winds
 \, heavy rain\, lightning) class will move to the Indoor 9m range to practi
 ce form and be noted on the calendar shortly before the scheduled session.<
 br>TARGET ARRANGEMENTS<br>May vary each session\, depending on who attends 
 and distances needed.<br>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 
 122-cm target face you'll move back to the next distance until you reach yo
 ur competition distance (see below)<br>If you trained outdoors in the 2025 
 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.<br><br>Target 1 a
 t 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should always stay at 70m so Jak
 e can use it for independent practice in between classes.<br>Target 2 at 60
 m (U18 + Masters competition distance) <br>Targets 3+4 at 50m<br>Target 5+6
  at 40m (U15 competition distance) <br>Target 7+8 at 30m (U13 competition d
 istance) <br>Targets 9 at 20m (for adults who have just graduated out of In
 door 2)<br>Target 10 at 13.5m (for juniors who have just graduated out of I
 ndoor 2)<br><br>Ideally\, we want to practice with two archers/target to re
 plicate outdoor competition conditions.<br><br>TARGET ASSIGNMENTS<br>Target
 s are assigned outdoors in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day
 \, so add your name next to your distance below. <br>If you need help or ha
 ve questions\, email/text Coach Racae<br>(Dotted lines represent tent poles
  dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)<br><br>ATCIOCT = <b>2026 ATCI Outdoor Com
 petition Team</b>  <br><b>MQS at your tournament distance</b>\, 36-arrow ro
 unds on 122-cm target face: <br><b>260 pts or 520 pts</b> (2 rounds)<br>---
 -------------------------------<br>1A. (70m)<br>1B<br><br>2A. (60m)   <br>2
 B <br><br>3A. (50m)  <br>----------------------------------<br>3B<br><br>4A
 . (50m) <br>4B. <br>----------------------------------<br>5A. (40m). <b>Fin
 n E</b> 14 <b>U15 </b>223 + 261 = <b>484 pts </b><br>5B.  <b>Nick E\,</b> a
 dult\, (new 70" bow - one round - back hurt)<br><br>6A. (40m) <b>Luke T.</b
 >\, 17 <b>U18 </b>162 + 241 = <b>403 pts</b><br>---------------------------
 -------<br>6B. <br><br>7A. (30m) <b>Emma A</b>.\, 14 <b>U15 </b>228 + 233 =
  <b>461 pts</b><br>7B.  <b>Ethan N.\, </b>adult\, <b>273 pts </b>(Round 2) 
 <br>---------------------------------- <br>8A. (20m) <b>Ethan N.</b>\, adul
 t\,  <b>345 pts </b>(Round 1) &gt\;<b> CONGRATULATIONS!! -&gt\; 30 m</b><br
 >8B.<br><br>9A. (20m) <b>Rhys E</b>.\, 11 <b>U13 </b>86 + 114 = <b>200 pts<
