DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u>
 </u>REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to adult\, juniors 8+\, and parents! Please 
 read all the info below and in the registration and waivers.<br><br>More in
 formation\, registration forms and waivers are available at&nbsp\;<a href="
 http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrainingcenter.com</a>.<br
 ><br>Register here using ONE of these forms:<br><a href="https://docs.googl
 e.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfcwG419ZK9XmA4-JlXM-zhjhvSPCF8NCwWJlzFP2w-gRliUw/vi
 ewform">2022 Winter/Spring Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Juniors + Parent
 s</a>&nbsp\; OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSe-YxP
 KAMTxiC7kVt6fZuQJeidXENYq_iV4rWj1RaXdLhPoew/viewform">2022 Winter/Spring Ou
 tdoor 1: First-time Class for Adults</a><br><br>Sign up for just one Outdoo
 r 1 class\, because most people graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 a
 fter the first lesson.<br><br><b>Your name will be added below and your pla
 ce reserved on a</b> <b>first registered and paid basis and after we receiv
 e 3 things</b>:&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br>2022 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM + WAIVERS
  + FEE<br><br><b>Registered archers&nbsp\;</b>at 9m on 40-cm target face un
 less otherwise noted:<br><b>Target Assignments:</b><br>1. <b>Stephen B</b>.
 \, adult - pd - substituted 5/29<br>2. <b>Rachel D</b>.\, adult - pd - subs
 tituted 5/29<br>3.&nbsp\;<b>Bri F.\, </b>adult - pd - refunded<u></u><br><u
 ></u>4.<u></u><br><u></u>5.<br>6.<br>7.<br>8.<br>9.<br>10.<br><br>Space wil
 l be limited to 10-15 archers per session depending on the number of family
  groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC Guidelines.&nbsp\;<br>Each 
 person will have a target stand\, except after 10 people have registered\, 
 two members from the same family will share one target stand.<br>The archer
  and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field until further 
 notice or approved by Coach Racae.&nbsp\;<br>Parents of juniors 10+ can sig
 n up as an archer or watch as a spectator. Parents of juniors 8-9 years old
  need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their child for greater safety.<br
 ><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into each Outdoor 1
 : First-time Class.&nbsp\;<br><br>We will accept a limited&nbsp\;number of 
 kids under 12 into the program each semester\, depending on the total&nbsp\
 ; number of archers in all the classes. If you join before the limit is rea
 ched\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take other 
 Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;If you are unde
 r 12\, registered and paid after the cut off\, your fee will be returned to
  you.&nbsp\;<br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times b
 efore qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as
  soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults
  don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accesso
 ries packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for
  Outdoor 2. ($15)<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, optiona
 l but really needed to practice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>A
 t the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we did n
 ot finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final s
 core\, because it will have been averaged by taking your recorded score fro
 m your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot to get an arro
 w average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round score. Afte
 r the last class on the weekend\, final scores will also be sent to all Out
 door 1 participants in an email with more information before your next clas
 s.<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
