 stand.<br />The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on th
 e field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae. <br />Parents of j
 uniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator. Parents of jun
 iors 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their child for 
 greater safety.<br /><br />A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accept
 ed into each Outdoor 1: First-time Class. <br /><br />We will accept a limi
 ted number of kids under 12 into the program each semester\, depending on t
 he total  number of archers in all the classes. If you join before the limi
 t is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and tak
 e other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2. If you are un
 der 12\, registered and paid after the cut off\, your fee will be returned 
 to you. <br /><br />Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times b
 efore qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as
  soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows. <br />Adults don
 ´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br /><br />ap = accesso
 ries packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for
  Outdoor 2. ($15)<br />fp = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, optio
 nal but really needed to practice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br /><
 br />At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we
  did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your f
 inal score\, because it will have been averaged by taking your recorded sco
 re from your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot to get a
 n arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round score
 . After the last class on the weekend\, final scores will also be sent to a
 ll Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more information before your nex
 t class.<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u></span>
