DESCRIPTION:​Looks like it's going to pour on Sat. 2/14\, so I've moved thi
 s Training Class into the 9m range for some form work instead\, review of t
 he Nationals\, and celebrating the end of the Indoor season!. <br>If you're
  coming\, just reply to this email or add your name on the calendar\, so I 
 know to hire a caregiver in time. <br><br>Training classes at this location
  are reserved for competitive and advanced archers..<br><br>REMINDER:  Ever
 yone needs to come to at least one Training Class per week to be able to at
 tend Open Practice. (All Indoor 2-6 at 9m classes are training classes.)<br
 ><br>Coach Racae will coach the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class whenever there a
 re at least 5 archers registered by Fri 12:00 pm (for Sat) and Sat 12:00 pm
  (for Sun).   <br><br>TRAINING CLASS (TC): $57/archer/3-hr class<br>(1x/wk 
 required to attend Open Practice)<br>FACILITY FEE (FF) (required each month
 ): $75/month/archer due on 1st of the month. (USAA Level 3 Coaches do not p
 ay facility fee.)<br>OPEN PRACTICE (OP) Included in facility fee (1-2x/wk r
 ecommended)<br>PRIVATE LESSON (PL): $125/hr/archer (1x/mo recommended)<br><
 br>Please add your name to the target list below to register<br>Focus prima
 rily on perfecting your form\, <br>slowly increasing your physical strength
  and draw weight\, <br>strengthening your mental program\, <br>determining 
 your average and personal best\, <br>understanding the spread between the t
 wo\, and working on closing it.<br><br>EQUIPMENT:<br>You need your own equi
 pment: <br>Competition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 
 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, ar
 mguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, et
 c. (Clicker and side rods may not be added until you reach a higher level\,
  but you should order them in advance.) <br><br>Wear your ATCI shirt to tra
 ining.<br><br>WEATHER / DAYLIGHT<br><br>Session times may vary depending on
  temperature/daylight conditions.<br>During inclement weather (&lt\;52F or 
 100F&gt\;\, 20 mph winds\, heavy rain\, lightning) class will move to the I
 ndoor 9m range to practice form and be noted on the calendar shortly before
  the scheduled session.<br>TARGET ARRANGEMENTS<br>May vary each session\, d
 epending on who attends and distances needed.<br>When you score 288 pts in 
 a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the next dis
 tance until you reach your competition distance (see below)<br>If you train
 ed outdoors in the 2025 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you
  shot.<br><br>Target 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should a
 lways stay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent practice in between cl
 asses.<br>Target 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition distance) <br>Targets 
 3+4 at 50m<br>Target 5+6 at 40m (U15 competition distance) <br>Target 7+8 a
 t 30m (U13 competition distance) <br>Targets 9 at 20m (for adults who have 
 just graduated out of Indoor 2)<br>Target 10 at 13.5m (for juniors who have
  just graduated out of Indoor 2)<br><br>Ideally\, we want to practice with 
 two archers/target to replicate outdoor competition conditions.<br><br>TARG
 ET ASSIGNMENTS<br>Targets are assigned outdoors in advance to reduce confus
 ion and delay on the day\, so add your name next to your distance below. <b
 r>If you need help or have questions\, email/text Coach Racae<br>(Dotted li
 nes represent tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)<br><br>ATCIOCT = 
 2026 ATCI Outdoor Competition Team  <br>MQS at your tournament distance\, 3
 6-arrow rounds on 122-cm target face: <br>260 pts or 520 pts (2 rounds)  (7
 .2 arrow average)<br>----------------------------------<br>1A. (70m)<br>1B<
 br><br>2A. (60m)  Joel y<br>2B<br><br>3A. (50m)  Adrianne M. <br>----------
 ------------------------<br>3B<br><br>4A. (50m) Abby y<br>4B. <br>---------
 -------------------------<br>5A. (40m)<br>5B. <br><br>6A. (40m) <br>-------
 ---------------------------<br>6B. <br><br>7A. (30m) Emma A (will be a few 
 minutes late)<br>7B. <br>---------------------------------- <br>8A. (30m) <
 br>8B.<br><br>9A. (20m) Ellie y<br>----------------------------------<br>9B
 . <br><br>10A. (13.5m)<br>10B
