DESCRIPTION:<p><a href="https://usarchery.sport80.com/public/wizard/e/44941
 /home">https://usarchery.sport80.com/public/wizard/e/44941/home</a><b><br><
 /b></p><p><b>2024 USA Archery Texas State Outdoor Championship </b><br></p>
 <p>Arrow Minded Outdoors\, 5835 FM 1863\, Bulverde\, Texas</p><p>This is a 
 <b>World Archery sanctioned tournament\, USA Archery rules and distances.</
 b></p><p>All archers will shoot two rounds of 72 arrows each (144 arrows to
 tal)\, with one round being on Saturday\, August 10th and the other Sunday\
 , August 11th.  Final rankings based on total accumulated score from both d
 ays. </p><ul><li>First place in all divisions will determine Texas State Ch
 ampion.  TSAA medals will be awarded to all 1st\, 2nd and 3rd place in all 
 divisions. <br></li><li>We will have two separate shooting sessions/flights
 .  You must shoot with your age class and division at the set time.</li><li
 >Entry is on a first come first serve basis as space is limited. Registrati
 on closes on Tuesday\, August 6th at midnight.<br></li><li>We will have two
  official practice ends prior to first official arrow for each flight on ea
 ch day.</li><li>More on age classes\, divisions\, and distances can be foun
 d in the <a href="https://www.usarchery.org/resource-center/events/event-re
 ference-guidebook"></a><a href="https://online.fliphtml5.com/ufvzu/xvbn/">U
 SA Archery Event Reference Guidebook.</a></li></ul><p>Notes about Arrow Min
 ded Outdoors Archery Club:</p><ul><li>Please bring your own chairs and pop-
 up tents. You may setup on day one and leave your tents overnight if you de
 sire\, but you must be willing to share with the other flight time. We are 
 not responsible for lost or stolen items left overnight. We do have some sh
 ade in the spectator area if you do not wish to bring a tent/canopy. </li><
 li>We are working on contracting with a food truck\, but archers are encour
 aged to bring their own snacks and refreshments. </li><li>Please do NOT wea
 r open-toed shoes. Briars are abundant in the area. The grass will be cut s
 hort\, so low-top sockless shoes (such as Hey Dudes) are acceptable.</li><l
 i>We encourage everyone to bring bug spray and sunscreen. </li></ul><p><b>O
 perating Schedule:</b></p><p><b>Saturday\, August 10</b></p><ul><li>7:30 am
  - Gates open for setup</li><li>8:00 am - Check in and registration\, equip
 ment inspection for A Flight</li><li>9:00 am - Two ends official practice f
 ollowed by 72 arrow round for A Flight</li><li>1:00 pm - Check in and regis
 tration\, equipment inspection for B Flight</li><li>2:00 pm - Two ends offi
 cial practice followed by 72 arrow round for B Flight</li></ul><p><b>Sunday
 \, August 11</b></p><ul><li>7:30 am - Gates open</li><li>9:00 am - Two ends
  official practice followed by 72 arrow round for B Flight<br></li><li>Noon
  or after conclusion of morning session - Awards for B Flight</li><li>2:00 
 pm - Two ends official practice followed by 72 arrow round for A Flight<br>
 </li><li>5:30 pm or after conclusion of afternoon session - Awards for A Fl
 ight</li></ul><p><b>Notes about the A and B Flights</b>:</p><ul><li>ALL PAR
 A DIVISIONS AND 70+ MASTER CLASSES WILL SHOOT ON THE MORNING FLIGHT ON BOTH
  DAYS.</li><li>A Flight will shoot Saturday\, 9:00 am and Sunday\, 2:00 pm.
 </li><li>B Flight will shoot Saturday\, 2:00 pm and Sunday\, 9:00 am. </li>
 <li>If registration numbers permit\, we will consolidate down to a single f
 light shooting at 9:00 am on both days.</li><li>Age class/equipment divisio
 ns in each flight are as follows:</li></ul><table><colgroup><col /><col /><
 col /><col /></colgroup><tbody><tr><td><b>A Flight</b></td><td><b></b></td>
