CREATED:20151230T001753Z
DESCRIPTION:Coach Racae (Recurves and Compounds)  Click the Sign Up button 
 at the top of ATCI website to Register for Spring 2016 Indoor 1: First-time
  Classes for Adults if you are at least 18 years old. This is a requirement
  to join regular adult training classes. Saturdays: 11:30am-1:30pm (Fee: $2
 5/cl) Sundays: 11:30am-1:30pm (Fee: $25/cl)  Enrollment link: https://docs.
 google.com/forms/d/1sPp_1NRpCtLb-SHXJR1dgEn7LVMV6BFgnCKW6-67GYM/viewform  R
 ECREATIONAL ADULT CLASSES at Indoor 2-5 and distances (9m\, 13.5m\, 18m)  S
 undays: 6:00-7:00pm (Fee: $20/cl) (Recurves) Tuesdays: 7:30-8:30pm (Fee: $2
 0/cl) (Compounds and Recurves)  PROGRESSIVE PROGRAM Indoor 2-5 JOAD and ADU
 LT TRAINING for those who want to progress faster toward competitive archer
 y by meeting minimum attendance requirements. Saturdays 3:30-5:30pm (Recurv
 es) Sundays:  3:30-5:30pm (Recurves) Sundays:  6:00-7:00pm (Adults and Indo
 or 5 only) (Recurves) Tuesdays: 6:30-7:30pm (Compounds and Recurves) Tuesda
 ys: 7:30-8:30pm (Adults and Indoor 5 only) (Compounds and Recurves) Wednesd
 ays: 6:30-8:00pm (Recurves)  Progressive weekly fees (after meeting previou
 s week's attendance requirement): Indoor 3A at 13.5m: $48/wk (min. 4 hrs) I
 ndoor 3B at 18m:    $55/wk (min. 5 hrs) Indoor 4 at 18m:      $60/wk (min. 
 6 hrs) Indoor 5 at 18m:      $72/wk (min. 8 hrs)  USA Archery's Adult Train
 ing Program (ATP) follows a similar path to the Junior Olympic Archery Deve
 lopment (JOAD) program.   Your first step is to take an Indoor 1: First-tim
 e Class for Adults. Just click the link or the Sign Up button at the top of
  this website.  Everyone starts out in our Recreational program at 9 meters
 . As you improve you progress to 13.5 meters then on to 18 meters indoors. 
   We welcome adult recurve and compound Olympic target archers at all level
 s of experience.  Recurve archers can attend any of the group classes above
  or book private lessons with Coach Racae or Instructor Dale. Compound arch
 ers can attend the group class on Tues. evenings or book private lessons wi
 th Coach Dan or Instructor Bailey.  Experienced competitive archers need to
  be evaluated by Coach Racae for advanced placement in either the Progressi
 ve Program or recommendation to the Competitive Archery Program with Coach 
 Alex.  When you decide that you are interested in competing you'll apply to
  join USA Archery Level 4 NTS and JDT Coach Alex Meyer's Competitive Archer
 y Program (CAP). 
