 u>6.&nbsp\;<b>Katy W</b>.\, mom - pd - <b>19 pts&nbsp\;</b><br><u></u>7.&nb
 sp\;<b>Evan W</b>.\, 15 - pd - <b>15 pts -&gt\; Outdoor 1</b><br>8.&nbsp\;<
 b>Everett Z.</b>\, 9\, on 60-cm target face - pd - <b>19 pts </b>-&gt\; <b>
 Outdoor 1</b><br>9. <b>Deborah G</b>.\, mom - pd - <b>73 pts</b><br><u></u>
 10. <b>Eleanor G</b>.\, 8\, on 60-cm target face - pd -&gt\; <b>Outdoor 1</
 b><br><br>Space will be limited to 10-15 archers per session depending on t
 he number of family groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC Guidelin
 es.&nbsp\;<br>Each person will have a target stand\, except after 10 people
  have registered\, two members from the same family will share one target s
 tand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the f
 ield until further notice or approved by Coach Racae.&nbsp\;<br>Parents of 
 juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator. Parents of ju
 niors 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their child for
  greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted 
 into each Outdoor 1: First-time Class.&nbsp\;<br><br>We will accept a limit
 ed&nbsp\;number of kids under 12 into the program each semester\, depending
  on the total&nbsp\; number of archers in all the classes. If you join befo
 re the limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the prog
 ram and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2.&nb
 sp\;If you are under 12\, registered and paid after the cut off\, your fee 
 will be returned to you.&nbsp\;<br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 t
 wo or three times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts
 . You´ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrow
 s.&nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<
 br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which
  will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($15)<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and str
 ing loop)\, optional but really needed to practice form\, warm up before cl
 asses ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be 
 posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not rec
 ognize your final score\, because it will have been averaged by taking your
  recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrows you 
 shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a ful
 l round score. After the last class on the weekend\, final scores will also
  be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more information be
 fore your next class.<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></
 u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u>
 </u><u></u></html-blob>
