DESCRIPTION:<i>This class has been cancelled due to field conditions after 
 heavy rains on Friday. We are not transferring indoors because the indoor r
 ange will be occupied by the Yale Club event with Instructor Colby.</i><br>
 <br>Training classes at this location are reserved for competitive and adva
 nced archers..<br><br><b>REMINDER</b>:  Everyone needs to come to at least 
 one Training Class per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (All Indoor
  2-6 at 9m classes are training classes.)<br><br>Coach Racae will coach the
  Outdoor 3-9 Training Class whenever there are at least 5 archers registere
 d by Thursday 12:00 pm (for Sat) and Friday 9:00 am (for Sun)\, except on f
 ederal holidays\, because Medicare's GUIDE program does not pay for caregiv
 ers on federal holidays!!! Sorry to disappoint!   <br><br><b>TRAINING CLASS
  (TC)</b>: <b>$57/archer/3-hr class</b><br>(1x/wk required to attend Open P
 ractice)<br><b>FACILITY FEE (FF) </b>(required each month): <b>$75/month/ar
 cher</b> due on 1st of the month. (USAA Level 3 Coaches do not pay facility
  fee.)<br><b>OPEN PRACTICE (OP) </b>Included in facility fee (1-2x/wk recom
 mended)<br><b>PRIVATE LESSON (PL)</b>: $125/hr/archer (1x/mo recommended)<b
 r><br><b>Please add your name to the target list below to register</b><br>F
 ocus primarily on perfecting your form\, <br>slowly increasing your physica
 l strength and draw weight\, <br>strengthening your mental program\, <br>de
 termining your average and personal best\, <br>understanding the spread bet
 ween the two\, and working on closing it.<br><br><b>EQUIPMENT:</b><br>You n
 eed your own equipment: <br>Competition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, 
 plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, che
 st protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, 
 arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added until you reach
  a higher level\, but you should order them in advance.) <br><br>Wear your 
 ATCI shirt to training.<br><br><b>WEATHER / DAYLIGHT</b><br><br>Session tim
 es may vary depending on temperature/daylight conditions.<br>During incleme
 nt weather (&lt\;52F or 100F&gt\;\, 20 mph winds\, heavy rain\, lightning) 
 class will move to the Indoor 9m range to practice form and be noted on the
  calendar shortly before the scheduled session.<br><b>TARGET ARRANGEMENTS</
 b><br>May vary each session\, depending on who attends and distances needed
 .<br>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm target face y
 ou'll move back to the next distance until you reach your competition dista
 nce (see below)<br>If you trained outdoors in the 2025 season\, you'll retu
 rn to the farthest distance you shot.<br><br>Target 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors
  competition distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use it for ind
 ependent practice in between classes.<br>Target 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters com
 petition distance) <br>Targets 3+4 at 50m<br>Target 5+6 at 40m (U15 competi
 tion distance) <br>Target 7+8 at 30m (U13 competition distance) <br>Targets
  9 at 20m (for adults who have just graduated out of Indoor 2)<br>Target 10
  at 13.5m (for juniors who have just graduated out of Indoor 2)<br><br>Idea
 lly\, we want to practice with two archers/target to replicate outdoor comp
 etition conditions.<br><br><b>TARGET ASSIGNMENTS</b><br>Targets are assigne
 d outdoors in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\, so <b>add 
 your name next to your distance below</b>. <br>If you need help or have que
 stions\, email/text Coach Racae<br>(Dotted lines represent tent poles divid
 ing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)<br><br><b>ATCIOCT</b> = 2026 ATCI Outdoor Compe
 tition Team  <br><b>MQS </b>at your tournament distance\, 36-arrow rounds o
 n 122-cm target face: <br><b>260 pts</b> or <b>520 pts</b> (2 rounds)<br>--
 --------------------------------<br>1A. (70m)<br>1B<br><br>2A. (60m)  <br>2
 B<br><br>3A. (50m)  <br>----------------------------------<br>3B<br><br>4A.
  (50m) <br>4B. <br>----------------------------------<br>5A. (40m)<br>5B. <
 br><br>6A. (40m) <br>----------------------------------<br>6B. <br><br>7A. 
 (30m) <br>7B. <br>---------------------------------- <br>8A. (30m) <br>8B.<
 br><br>9A. (20m) <br>----------------------------------<br>9B. <br><br>10A.
  (13.5m)<br>10B
