  the cut off\, your fee will be returned to you.&nbsp\;<br><br>Juniors may 
 need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying to get into Out
 door 2 by scoring 50 pts. If you are 12+ and did not quite finish an entire
  round of 30 arrows due to time limits\, but improved over the arrows you d
 id shoot\, you may move into Outdoor 2\, if you have at least 35 points. Ge
 nerally\, you´ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of
  3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Out
 door 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)
 \, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($15)<br>fp = form pack (stretchband
  and string loop)\, optional but really needed to practice form\, warm up b
 efore classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores 
 will be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may
  not recognize your final score\, because it will have been averaged by tak
 ing your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arr
 ows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to g
 et a full round score. After the last class on the weekend\, final scores w
 ill also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more inform
 ation before your next class.<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u><
