DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u>This class has been canceled by ATCI because 
 it did not meet the minimum registration of 4 archers. It happens perhaps o
 nce or twice a year. Please reschedule your time with us.<u></u><br><u></u>
 <br><u></u><br><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u>REGISTER NOW !<br>
 <br>Open to adult\, juniors 8+\, and parents! Please read all the info belo
 w and in the registration and waivers.<br><br>More information\, registrati
 on forms and waivers are available at&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.archerytrai
 ningcenter.com">www.archerytrainingcenter.com</a>.<br><br>Register here usi
 ng ONE of these forms:<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQ
 LSfcwG419ZK9XmA4-JlXM-zhjhvSPCF8NCwWJlzFP2w-gRliUw/viewform">2022 Winter/Sp
 ring Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Juniors + Parents</a>&nbsp\; OR<br><a 
 href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSe-YxPKAMTxiC7kVt6fZuQJeidXE
 NYq_iV4rWj1RaXdLhPoew/viewform">2022 Winter/Spring Outdoor 1: First-time Cl
 ass for Adults</a><br><br>Sign up for just one Outdoor 1 class\, because mo
 st juniors 11+ and all adults graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 aft
 er the first lesson.<u></u><br><br><b>Your name will be added below and you
 r place reserved on a</b> <b>first registered and paid basis and after we r
 eceive 3 things</b>:&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br>2022 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM + WA
 IVERS + FEE<br><br><b>Registered archers&nbsp\;</b>at 9m on 40-cm target fa
 ce:<br><b>Target nos:</b><br>1.&nbsp\;<b>Han L.\,&nbsp\;</b>dad - pd - resc
 heduled to 4/17<br>2.&nbsp\;<b>Gianna L.\,&nbsp\;</b>8 - pd - rescheduled t
 o 4/17<br>3.<br>4.<br>5.<br>6.<br>7.<br>8.<br>9.<u></u><br><u></u>10.&nbsp\
 ;&nbsp\;<br><br>Space will be limited to 10-15 archers per session dependin
 g on the number of family groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC Gu
 idelines.&nbsp\;<br>Each person will have a target stand\, except after 10 
 people have registered\, two members from the same family will share one ta
 rget stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on
  the field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae.&nbsp\;<br>Paren
 ts of juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator. Parents
  of juniors 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their chi
 ld for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is acc
 epted into each Outdoor 1: First-time Class.&nbsp\;<br><br>We will accept a
  limited&nbsp\;number of kids under 12 into the program each semester\, dep
 ending on the total&nbsp\; number of archers in all the classes. If you joi
 n before the limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in th
 e program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor
  2.&nbsp\;If you are under 12\, registered and paid after the cut off\, you
 r fee will be returned to you.&nbsp\;<br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdo
 or 1 two or three times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 
 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3
  arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdo
 or 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\,
  which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($15)<br>fp = form pack (stretchband a
 nd string loop)\, optional but really needed to practice form\, warm up bef
 ore classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores wi
 ll be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may n
 ot recognize your final score\, because it will have been averaged by takin
 g your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrow
 s you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get
  a full round score. After the last class on the weekend\, final scores wil
 l also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more informat
 ion before your next class.<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u></html
 -blob>
