DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><b>
 UPDATE: With the news that Austin/Travis County is now in Stage 5 of COVID-
 19 risk-based guidelines\, I have made the decision to postpone the start o
 f our archery training classes this semester possibly until Austin drops ba
 ck down to Stage 4.&nbsp\;</b><br>I will review the situation weekly on Fri
 days and postpone weekend and Monday classes\, if Austin is still in Stage 
 5.&nbsp\;<b>(See my Friday email to you.)</b><b><br></b><br>I know this is 
 disappointing to most of you - and no one wants to attend the training clas
 ses more than I do. I love to coach you! My main concern\, however\, as alw
 ays\, is to keep everyone who attends our classes as safe as possible.&nbsp
 \;<br><br>Not to worry\, we will start classes soon again!<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp
 \; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; 
 &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nb
 sp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\
 ; Coach Racae<br>REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to adult\, juniors 8+\, and par
 ents! Please read all the info below and in the registration and waivers.<b
 r><br>More information\, registration forms and waivers are available at&nb
 sp\;<a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrainingcente
 r.com</a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE of these forms:<br><a href="https
 ://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfcwG419ZK9XmA4-JlXM-zhjhvSPCF8NCwWJlzF
 P2w-gRliUw/viewform">2022 Winter/Spring Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Jun
 iors + Parents</a>&nbsp\; OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/
 1FAIpQLSe-YxPKAMTxiC7kVt6fZuQJeidXENYq_iV4rWj1RaXdLhPoew/viewform">2022 Win
 ter/Spring Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Adults</a><br><br>Sign up for ju
 st one Outdoor 1 class\, because most people graduate out of this class int
 o Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br><br><b>Your name will be added below
  and your place reserved on a</b> <b>first registered and paid basis and af
 ter we receive 3 things</b>:&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br>2022 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION F
 ORM + WAIVERS + FEE<br><br><b>Registered archers&nbsp\;</b>at 9m on 40-cm t
 arget face unless noted otherwise:<br><b>Target nos:</b><br>1A. Charles W.\
 , adult - pd - substituted 3/5<br>1B. Cristian W.\, adult - pd - substitute
 d 3/5<br>2. Dave S.\, dad - pd - substituted 2/12<br>3. Max S.\, 16 - pd - 
 substituted 2/12<br>4. Gael C.\, 9 - pd at 9m on 60-cm target face - substi
 tuted 2/12<br>5.<br>6.<br>7.<br>8.<br>9.<br>10.<br><br>Space will be limite
 d to 10-15 archers per session depending on the number of family groups in 
 attendance or in accordance with CDC Guidelines.&nbsp\;<br>Each person will
  have a target stand\, except after 10 people have registered\, two members
  from the same family will share one target stand.<br>The archer and a maxi
 mum of one spectator will be allowed on the field until further notice or a
 pproved by Coach Racae.&nbsp\;<br>Parents of juniors 10+ can sign up as an 
 archer or watch as a spectator. Parents of juniors 8-9 years old need to re
 gister\, pay\, and shoot with their child for greater safety.<br><br>A maxi
 mum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-tim
 e Class.&nbsp\;<br><br>We will accept a limited&nbsp\;number of kids under 
 12 into the program each semester\, depending on the total&nbsp\; number of
  archers in all the classes. If you join before the limit is reached\, and 
 are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take other Outdoor 1 c
 lasses as needed and later join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;If you are under 12\, regi
 stered and paid after the cut off\, your fee will be returned to you.&nbsp\
 ;<br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times before quali
 fying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as yo
 u score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need
  a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet
  (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2.
  ($15)<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but reall
 y needed to practice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end o
 f each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a
  complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, beca
 use it will have been averaged by taking your recorded score from your scor
 ecard\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\,
  and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round score. After the last 
 class on the weekend\, final scores will also be sent to all Outdoor 1 part
 icipants in an email with more information before your next class.<u></u><u
 ></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
