DESCRIPTION:<i>This class has been cancelled due to field conditions and hi
 gh winds.</i><br><i>Come to the Indoor 2-6 at 9m class at 4:30-6:00 to prac
 tice form.</i><br><br>Training classes at this location are reserved for co
 mpetitive and advanced archers..<br><br>REMINDER:  Everyone needs to come t
 o at least one Training Class per week to be able to attend Open Practice. 
 (All Indoor 2-6 at 9m classes are training classes.)<br><br>Coach Racae wil
 l coach the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class whenever there are at least 5 archer
 s registered by Fri 12:00 pm (for Sat) and Sat 12:00 pm (for Sun).   <br><b
 r>TRAINING CLASS (TC): $57/archer/3-hr class<br>(1x/wk required to attend O
 pen Practice)<br>FACILITY FEE (FF) (required each month): $75/month/archer 
 due on 1st of the month. (USAA Level 3 Coaches do not pay facility fee.)<br
 >OPEN PRACTICE (OP) Included in facility fee (1-2x/wk recommended)<br>PRIVA
 TE LESSON (PL): $125/hr/archer (1x/mo recommended)<br><br>Please add your n
 ame to the target list below to register<br>Focus primarily on perfecting y
 our form\, <br>slowly increasing your physical strength and draw weight\, <
 br>strengthening your mental program\, <br>determining your average and per
 sonal best\, <br>understanding the spread between the two\, and working on 
 closing it.<br><br>EQUIPMENT:<br>You need your own equipment: <br>Competiti
 on recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, s
 ide rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\,
  finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side
  rods may not be added until you reach a higher level\, but you should orde
