DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u>
 </u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u>REGISTER NOW !<br><br>GIRL SCOUT TRO
 OPS: <br>If you would like to book a training session for your Girl Scout T
 roop\, use the Outdoor 1: First-time Class registration form for Juniors + 
 Parents below . The minimum fee is $350 \, and then $35/girl starting with 
 the 11th partcipant. The training class is usualy two hours. Parents can al
 so join in the fun optionally by paying for a place on the shooting line. .
 <br><br>GENERAL PUBLIC:<u></u><br><u></u>More information\, registration fo
 rms and waivers are available at&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.archerytrainingc
 enter.com">www.archerytrainingcenter.com</a>.<br><br>Register here using ON
 E of these forms:<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfcw
 G419ZK9XmA4-JlXM-zhjhvSPCF8NCwWJlzFP2w-gRliUw/viewform">2022 Winter/Spring 
 Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Juniors + Parents</a>&nbsp\; OR<br><a href=
 "https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSe-YxPKAMTxiC7kVt6fZuQJeidXENYq_i
 V4rWj1RaXdLhPoew/viewform">2022 Winter/Spring Outdoor 1: First-time Class f
 or Adults</a><br><br>Sign up for just one Outdoor 1 class\, because most ju
 niors 11+ and all adults graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after th
 e first lesson.<u></u><br><br><b>Your name will be added below and your pla
 ce reserved on a</b> <b>first registered and paid basis and after we receiv
 e 3 things</b>:&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br>2022 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM + WAIVERS
  + FEE<br><br><b>Registered archers&nbsp\;</b>at 9m on 60-cm target face:<b
 r><b>Target Assignments:</b><br>1A. <b>Annika W.A</b>.\, 13 - <b>30 pts</b>
  (corrected)<br><u></u>1B.&nbsp\;<u></u><b>Blaine B.\,</b> 14 - <b>17 pts.<
 /b><br>2. <b>Cate P.\, </b>13 - <b>10 pts</b><br>3. <b>Elenora M.</b>\, 13 
 - <b>95 pts -&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br>4. <b>Elise C.R.\,</b> 13 - scorecard?<
 br>5. <b>Flora C.\,</b> 14 - <b>68 pts </b>(corrected) <b>-&gt\; Outdoor 2<
 /b><br>6. <b>Lena J.\,</b> 13 - <b>25 pts</b><br>7. <b>Lexi&nbsp\; F.\, </b
 >14 - <b>43 pts -&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br><u></u>8. <b>Vivian<u></u>&nbsp\;M.
 \,</b> 14 - <b>74 pts</b> (corrected) <b>-&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br><u></u>9. 
 <b>Margret C.</b>\, 14 - <b>158 pts </b>(corrected) <b>-&gt\; Outdoor 2</b>
 <br><u></u>10A. <b>Lynda B-R\, </b>14 - <b>86 pts -&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br><
 u></u>10B. <b>Valentina<u></u>&nbsp\;B-R\,</b> 10 - <b>44? -&gt\; Outdoor 2
 </b><br><br><u></u>Space will be limited to 10-15 archers per session depen
 ding on the number of family groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC
  Guidelines.&nbsp\;<br>Each person will have a target stand\, except after 
 10 people have registered\, two members from the same family will share one
  target stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed
  on the field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae.&nbsp\;<br>Pa
 rents of juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator. Pare
 nts of juniors 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their 
 child for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is 
 accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-time Class.&nbsp\;<br><br>We will accep
 t a limited&nbsp\;number of kids under 12 into the program each semester\, 
 depending on the total&nbsp\; number of archers in all the classes. If you 
 join before the limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in
  the program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outd
 oor 2.&nbsp\;If you are under 12\, registered and paid after the cut off\, 
 your fee will be returned to you.&nbsp\;<br><br>Juniors may need to take Ou
 tdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scori
 ng 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end o
 f 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Ou
 tdoor 2.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab
 \, fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($15)<br>fp = form pa
 ck (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but really needed to practice f
 orm\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class
 \, your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 ar
 rows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, because it will have been 
 averaged by taking your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by th
 e number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying 
 that by 30 to get a full round score.&nbsp\; When necessary we also correct
  your scores\, if there was an arithmetical error. If you are 13+ and score
  at least 35 pts\, if you improved over time\, then you will graduate to Ou
 tdoor 2. After the last class on the weekend\, final scores will also be se
 nt to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more information before y
 our next class.<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u><
 /u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
