DESCRIPTION:Training classes at this location are reserved for competitive 
 and advanced archers..\n\nREMINDER:  Everyone needs to come to at least one
  Training Class per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (All Indoor 2-
 6 at 9m classes are training classes.)\n\nCoach Racae will coach the Outdoo
 r 3-9 Training Class whenever there are at least 5 archers registered by Th
 ursday 12:00 pm (for Sat) and Friday 9:00 am (for Sun)\, except on federal 
 holidays\, because Medicare's GUIDE program does not pay for caregivers on 
 federal holidays!!! Sorry to disappoint!   \n\nTRAINING CLASS (TC): $57/arc
 her/3-hr class\n(1x/wk required to attend Open Practice)\nFACILITY FEE (FF)
  (required each month): $75/month/archer due on 1st of the month. (USAA Lev
 el 3 Coaches do not pay facility fee.)\nOPEN PRACTICE (OP) Included in faci
 lity fee (1-2x/wk recommended)\nPRIVATE LESSON (PL): $125/hr/archer (1x/mo 
 recommended)\n\nPlease add your name to the target list below to register\n
 Focus primarily on perfecting your form\, \nslowly increasing your physical
  strength and draw weight\, \nstrengthening your mental program\, \ndetermi
 ning your average and personal best\, \nunderstanding the spread between th
 e two\, and working on closing it.\n\nEQUIPMENT:\nYou need your own equipme
 nt: \nCompetition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 ca
 rbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguar
 d\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (C
 licker and side rods may not be added until you reach a higher level\, but 
 you should order them in advance.) \n\nWear your ATCI shirt to training.\n\
 nWEATHER / DAYLIGHT\n\nSession times may vary depending on temperature/dayl
 ight conditions.\nDuring inclement weather (<52F or 100F>\, 20 mph winds\, 
 heavy rain\, lightning) class will move to the Indoor 9m range to practice 
 form and be noted on the calendar shortly before the scheduled session.\nTA
 RGET ARRANGEMENTS\nMay vary each session\, depending on who attends and dis
 tances needed.\nWhen you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm ta
 rget face you'll move back to the next distance until you reach your compet
 ition distance (see below)\nIf you trained outdoors in the 2025 season\, yo
 u'll return to the farthest distance you shot.\n\nTarget 1 at 70m (U21 + Se
 niors competition distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use it fo
 r independent practice in between classes.\nTarget 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters 
 competition distance) \nTargets 3+4 at 50m\nTarget 5+6 at 40m (U15 competit
 ion distance) \nTarget 7+8 at 30m (U13 competition distance) \nTargets 9 at
  20m (for adults who have just graduated out of Indoor 2)\nTarget 10 at 13.
 5m (for juniors who have just graduated out of Indoor 2)\n\nIdeally\, we wa
 nt to practice with two archers/target to replicate outdoor competition con
 ditions.\n\nTARGET ASSIGNMENTS\nTargets are assigned outdoors in advance to
  reduce confusion and delay on the day\, so add your name next to your dist
 ance below. \nIf you need help or have questions\, email/text Coach Racae\n
 (Dotted lines represent tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)\n\nATCI
 OCT = 2026 ATCI Outdoor Competition Team  \nMQS at your tournament distance
 \, 36-arrow rounds on 122-cm target face: \n260 pts or 520 pts (2 rounds)\n
 ----------------------------------\n1A. (70m)\n1B\n\n2A. (60m)  Joel Y\, ad
 ult\, pd\n2B\n\n3A. (50m)  \n----------------------------------\n3B\n\n4A. 
 (50m) \n4B. \n----------------------------------\n5A. (40m) Abby Y\, 14\, p
 d\n5B. \n\n6A. (40m) \n----------------------------------\n6B. \n\n7A. (30m
 ) Ellie Y\, 13\, pd\n7B. \n---------------------------------- \n8A. (30m) \
 n8B.\n\n9A. (20m) Everett Z \, 13\n----------------------------------\n9B. 
 \n\n10A. (13.5m)\n10B
