 ld conditions after heavy rain yesterday. Great time to work on form with t
 he monitors and cameras\, especially on the back end of the shot - Transfer
  to Hold\, Expand/Aim\, Release/Follow-through. <br>Looking forward to seei
 ng you all there<br><br>The classes at this location are reserved for compe
 titive and advanced archers..<br><br>REMINDER:  Everyone needs to come to a
 t least one Training Class per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (Al
 l Indoor 2-6 at 9m classes are training classes.)<br><br>Coach Racae will c
 oach the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class whenever there are at least 5 archers r
 egistered by Fri 12:00 pm (for Sat) and Sat 12:00 pm (for Sun).   <br><br>T
 RAINING CLASS (TC): $57/archer/3-hr class<br>(1x/wk required to attend Open
  Practice)<br>FACILITY FEE (FF) (required each month): $75/month/archer due
  on 1st of the month. (USAA Level 3 Coaches do not pay facility fee.)<br>OP
 EN PRACTICE (OP) Included in facility fee (1-2x/wk recommended)<br>PRIVATE 
 LESSON (PL): $125/hr/archer (1x/mo recommended)<br><br>Please add your name
  to the target list below to register<br>Focus primarily on perfecting your
  form\, <br>slowly increasing your physical strength and draw weight\, <br>
 strengthening your mental program\, <br>determining your average and person
 al best\, <br>understanding the spread between the two\, and working on clo
 sing it.<br><br>EQUIPMENT:<br>You need your own equipment: <br>Competition 
 recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side
  rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, fi
 nger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side ro
 ds may not be added until you reach a higher level\, but you should order t
 hem in advance.) <br><br>Wear your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br>WEATHER /
  DAYLIGHT<br><br>Session times may vary depending on temperature/daylight c
 onditions.<br>During inclement weather (&lt\;52F or 100F&gt\;\, 20 mph wind
 s\, heavy rain\, lightning) class will move to the Indoor 9m range to pract
 ice form and be noted on the calendar shortly before the scheduled session.
 <br>TARGET ARRANGEMENTS<br>May vary each session\, depending on who attends
  and distances needed.<br>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the
  122-cm target face you'll move back to the next distance until you reach y
 our competition distance (see below)<br>If you trained outdoors in the 2025
  season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.<br><br>Target 1 
 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should always stay at 70m so Ja
 ke can use it for independent practice in between classes.<br>Target 2 at 6
 0m (U18 + Masters competition distance) <br>Targets 3+4 at 50m<br>Target 5+
 6 at 40m (U15 competition distance) <br>Target 7+8 at 30m (U13 competition 
