DESCRIPTION:REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to adult\, juniors 8+\, and parents!
  Please read all the info below and in the registration and waivers.<br><br
 >More information\, registration forms and waivers are available at <a href
 ="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com"><u><u><u><u>www.archerytrainingcent
 er.com</u></u></u></u></a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE of these forms:<
 br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeciOgkyuKTLZ5_ZaWCEyQ
 KYSX1fWGpP5qakhT6OuAc6jJ_FQ/viewform"><u>2023 Outdoor 1: First-time Class f
 or Adults</u></a>  OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQL
 Sc_bYEFoE4oXkcm0T6fZK99fu_q6lL8wZGClXyfa1GZbahh-g/viewform"><u>2023 Outdoor
  1: First-time Class for Juniors and Parents</u></a><br><br>Sign up for jus
 t ONE Outdoor 1 class\, because most people graduate out of this class into
  Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br><br>Your name will be added below and
  your place reserved on a first registered and paid basis and after we rece
 ive 3 things:  <br><b>2023 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM   +  MEMBERSHIP AND 
 WAIVERS PACKET +   FEE</b><b><br></b><u></u><br><b>USA Archery Level 4 NTS 
 Coach Racae Meyer and other instructors/coaches.</b><br><b>See </b><a href=
 "https://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/who-we-are"><u><u>https://www.archer
 ytrainingcenter.com/who-we-are</u></u></a><b><br></b><br><b>Registered arch
 ers </b>at 9m on 40-cm target face unless otherwise noted:<u></u><br><u></u
 ><br><b>Target Assignments:</b><u></u><br>5A.<br>5B.<br><br>6A. <b>Rudy S.\
 , </b>adult\, pd - 111 pts (average for 30 arrows)-&gt\; Outdoor 2<br>6B.<b
 r><br>7A. <b>Laura P.</b>\, adult\, pd - 86 pts (average for 30 arrows) -&g
 t\; Outdoor 2<br>7B. <br><br>8A. <b>Matt Y</b>.\, adult\, pd - 109 pts (ave
 rage for 30 arrows) -&gt\; Outdoor 2<br>8B.<br><br>9A.<br>9B.<br><br>10A.<b
 r>10B.<br><br>Space will be limited to 10-15 archers per session depending 
 on the number of family groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC Guid
 elines. <br>Each person will have a target stand\, except after 10 people h
 ave registered\, members may be assigned to share a target stand.<br>The ar
 cher and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field until furt
 her notice or approved by Coach Racae. <br>Parents of juniors 10+ can sign 
 up as an archer or watch as a spectator. <br>Parents of juniors 8-9 years o
 ld need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their child for greater safety.<
 br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into each Outdoor
  1: First-time Class. <br><br>We will accept a limited number of kids under
  12 into the program each semester\, depending on the total  number of arch
 ers in all the classes. If you join before the limit is reached\, and are y
 ounger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take other Outdoor 1 classe
 s as needed and later join Outdoor 2. If you are under 12\, registered and 
 paid after the cut off\, your fee will be returned to you. <br><br>Juniors 
 may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying to get into
  Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on averag
 e about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows. <br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to gra
 duate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\
 , fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($18) Please pay for t
 his at the field\, as our stock fluctuates because of dealer supply fluctua
 tions<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but really
  needed to practice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of
  each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a 
 complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, becau
 se it will have been averaged by taking your recorded score from your score
 card\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, 
 and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round score. After the last f
 irst-time class each weekend\, final scores may also be sent to all Outdoor
  1 participants in an email with more information before your next class.
