 w and in the registration and waivers.<br><br>More information\, registrati
 on forms and waivers are available at&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.archerytrai
 ningcenter.com">www.archerytrainingcenter.com</a>.<br><br>Register here usi
 ng ONE of these forms:<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQ
 LSfcwG419ZK9XmA4-JlXM-zhjhvSPCF8NCwWJlzFP2w-gRliUw/viewform">2022 Winter/Sp
 ring Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Juniors + Parents</a>&nbsp\; OR<br><a 
 href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSe-YxPKAMTxiC7kVt6fZuQJeidXE
 NYq_iV4rWj1RaXdLhPoew/viewform">2022 Winter/Spring Outdoor 1: First-time Cl
 ass for Adults</a><br><br>Sign up for just one Outdoor 1 class\, because mo
 st people graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.
 <br><br><b>Your name will be added below and your place reserved on a</b> <
 b>first registered and paid basis and after we receive 3 things</b>:&nbsp\;
 &nbsp\;<br>2022 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM + WAIVERS + FEE</span><br><span
 ><br></span><br><span><b>Adults do not need a minimum score to advance to O
 utdoor 2.</b></span><br><span><b>Juniors need 50 pts min.\, except as noted
  below\, to advance to Outdoor 2.<br></b><br><b>Registered archers&nbsp\;</
 b>at 9m on 40-cm target face unless otherwise noted:<u></u><br><u></u><br><
 b>Target Assignments:</b><br>1.<u></u><br><u></u>2. <b>Khang L.\, </b>adult
  - pd - <b>12 pts</b><br>3. <b>Heather O´K G</b>\, adult - pd - <b>29 pts</
 b><br>4. <b>Campbell G</b>.\, 15 - pd - substituted for 4/24 - fee transfer
 red -&nbsp\;<b>&nbsp\;60 pts</b> (corrected) -&gt\; <b>Outdoor 2</b><br>5.&
 nbsp\;<b>Joseph V</b>.\, adult - pd - <b>81 pts </b>(corrected)<br>6.&nbsp\
 ;<b>Christiana A</b>.\,&nbsp\;15&nbsp\;- pd - <b>36 pts </b>-&gt\; <b>Outdo
 or 1</b><br>7.<b> Gabriel K.T.\, </b>9 - on 60-cm target face - pd - <b>65 
 pts </b>(corrected) -&gt\; <b>Outdoor 2</b><br>8.<br>9.<br>10.<br><br>Space
  will be limited to 10-15 archers per session depending on the number of fa
 mily groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC Guidelines.&nbsp\;<br>E
 ach person will have a target stand\, except after 10 people have registere
 d\, two members from the same family will share one target stand.<br>The ar
 cher and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field until furt
 her notice or approved by Coach Racae.&nbsp\;<br>Parents of juniors 10+ can
  sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator. Parents of juniors 8-9 years
  old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their child for greater safety
 .<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into each Outdo
 or 1: First-time Class.&nbsp\;<br><br>We will accept a limited&nbsp\;number
  of kids under 12 into the program each semester\, depending on the total&n
 bsp\; number of archers in all the classes. If you join before the limit is
  reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take ot
 her Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;If you are 
 under 12\, registered and paid after the cut off\, your fee will be returne
 d to you.&nbsp\;<br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three tim
 es before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make i
 t as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Ad
 ults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = acc
 essories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed
  for Outdoor 2. ($18)<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, opt
 ional but really needed to practice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><
 br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we d
 id not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your fin
 al score\, because it will have been averaged by taking your recorded score
  from your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot to get an 
 arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round score. 
 After the last class on the weekend\, final scores will also be sent to all
  Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more information before your next 
 class.<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u></span></html-blob>
