DESCRIPTION:Registration form: OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m<br><br>Add your nam
 e to Target Assignment List below or send in the above completed form.<br><
 br>Focus primarily on <br>    •perfecting your form\, <br>    •slowly incre
 asing your physical strength and draw weight\, <br>    •strengthening your 
 mental program\, <br>    •determining your average and personal best\, <br>
     •understanding the spread between the two\, and working on closing it.<
 br>You need your own equipment <br>Competition recurve bow\, sight\, stabil
 izer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicke
 r\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field qu
 iver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added until yo
 u reach a higher level\, but you should order them in advance.) <br><br>Wea
 r your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br><b>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arr
 ow round on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the next distance un
 til you reach your competition distance</b><br>If you trained outdoors in t
 he 2024 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.<br>Target
  arrangements may vary each session\, depending on who attends and distance
 s needed.<br>Target 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should al
 ways stay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent practice in between cla
 sses.<br>Target 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition distance) <br>Target 3 
 at 50m<br>Target 4 at 40m (U15 competition distance) <br>Target 5 at 30m (U
 13 competition distance) <br>Targets 6+7+8 at 20m (for those who have shot 
 at 18m indoors or with Coach Racae's approval)<br>Targets 9 + 10 at 13.5m (
 for those who have just graduated from indoors at 9m)<br><br>Ideally\, we w
 ant to practice with two archers/target to replicate competition conditions
  as much as possible.<br><br>Target Assignments:<br>Targets are assigned ou
 tdoors in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\,<br>so add your
  name next to your distance below. <br>If you need help or have questions\,
