DESCRIPTION:REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to adult\, juniors 8+\, and parents!
  Please read all the info below and in the registration and waivers.<br><br
 >More information\, registration forms and waivers are available at <a href
 ="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com"><u><u><u><u>www.archerytrainingcent
 er.com</u></u></u></u></a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE of these forms:<
 br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeciOgkyuKTLZ5_ZaWCEyQ
 KYSX1fWGpP5qakhT6OuAc6jJ_FQ/viewform"><u>2023 Outdoor 1: First-time Class f
 or Adults</u></a>  OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQL
 Sc_bYEFoE4oXkcm0T6fZK99fu_q6lL8wZGClXyfa1GZbahh-g/viewform"><u>2023 Outdoor
  1: First-time Class for Juniors and Parents</u></a><br><br>Sign up for jus
 t ONE Outdoor 1 class\, because most people graduate out of this class into
  Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br><br>Your name will be added below and
  your place reserved on a first registered and paid basis and after we rece
 ive 3 things:  <br><b>2023 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM   +  MEMBERSHIP AND 
 WAIVERS PACKET +   FEE</b><b><br></b><u></u><br><b>USA Archery Level 4 NTS 
 Coach Racae Meyer and other instructors/coaches.</b><br><b>See </b><a href=
 "https://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/who-we-are"><u><u>https://www.archer
 ytrainingcenter.com/who-we-are</u></u></a><b><br></b><br><b>Registered arch
 ers </b>at 9m on 40-cm target face unless otherwise noted:<u></u><br><u></u
 ><br><b>Target Assignments:</b><br><u></u><b><br></b>5A. <b>Teri DeS.</b>\,
  adult\, pd - substituted for 4/8 - <b>64 pts</b> averaged -&gt\; Outdoor 2
 <br>5B. <b>Madeline K.\, </b>adult\, pd - substituted for 4/8 - <b>19 pts</
 b> averaged -&gt\; Outdoor 2<br><br>6.  <b>Lisa H</b>.\, adult\, pd - <b>63
  pts</b> averaged -&gt\; Outdoor 2<br><br>7A. <b>John DeW\,</b> adult - pd 
 - <b>63 pts</b> averaged -&gt\; Outdoor 2<br>7B. <b>John P.\,</b> 9\, on 60
 -cm target face - pd - <b>63 pts </b>averaged -&gt\; Outdoor 2<br><br>8A. <
 b>Yue D.\,</b> adult  - pd - <b>68 pts</b> averaged -&gt\; Outdoor 2<br><br
 >9A. <b>Blake Z.</b>\, 18 - pd - <b>94 pts</b> averaged -&gt\; Outdoor 2 <b
 r>9B. <b>Brian Z.\,</b> 18 - pd - <b>116 pts</b> averaged -&gt\; Outdoor 2<
 br><br>10A.<br>10B.<br><br><b>Jocelin E.\, </b>adult\, pd - canceled 5/30 -
  emergency - fee refunded<br><b>Kerry E.\, </b>adult\, pd - canceled 5/30 -
  emergency - fee refunded<br><br>Space will be limited to 10-15 archers per
  session depending on the number of family groups in attendance or in accor
 dance with CDC Guidelines. <br>Each person will have a target stand\, excep
 t after 10 people have registered\, members may be assigned to share a targ
 et stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on t
 he field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae. <br>Parents of ju
 niors 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator. <br>Parents of 
 juniors 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their child f
 or greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepte
 d into each Outdoor 1: First-time Class. <br><br>We will accept a limited n
 umber of kids under 12 into the program each semester\, depending on the to
 tal  number of archers in all the classes. If you join before the limit is 
 reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take oth
 er Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2. If you are under 1
 2\, registered and paid after the cut off\, your fee will be returned to yo
 u. <br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times before qua
 lifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as 
 you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows. <br>Adults don´t need a m
 inimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (ar
 mguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($1
 8) Please pay for this at the field\, as our stock fluctuates because of de
 aler supply fluctuations<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, 
 optional but really needed to practice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<b
 r><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If w
 e did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your 
 final score\, because it will have been averaged by taking your recorded sc
 ore from your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot to get 
 an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round scor
 e. After the last first-time class each weekend\, final scores may also be 
 sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more information before
  your next class.
