DESCRIPTION:REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to adult\, juniors 8+\, and parents!
  Please read all the info below and in the registration and waivers.<br><br
 >More information\, registration forms and waivers are available at <a href
 ="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com"><u><u><u><u>www.archerytrainingcent
 er.com</u></u></u></u></a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE of these forms:<
 br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeciOgkyuKTLZ5_ZaWCEyQ
 KYSX1fWGpP5qakhT6OuAc6jJ_FQ/viewform"><u>2023 Outdoor 1: First-time Class f
 or Adults</u></a>  OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQL
 Sc_bYEFoE4oXkcm0T6fZK99fu_q6lL8wZGClXyfa1GZbahh-g/viewform"><u>2023 Outdoor
  1: First-time Class for Juniors and Parents</u></a><br><br>Sign up for jus
 t ONE Outdoor 1 class\, because most people graduate out of this class into
  Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<br><br>Your name will be added below and
  your place reserved on a first registered and paid basis and after we rece
 ive 3 things:  <br><b>2023 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM   +  MEMBERSHIP AND 
 WAIVERS PACKET +   FEE</b><b><br></b><u></u><br><b>USA Archery Level 4 NTS 
 Coach Racae Meyer and other instructors/coaches.</b><br><b>See </b><a href=
 "https://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/who-we-are"><u><u>https://www.archer
 ytrainingcenter.com/who-we-are</u></u></a><b><br></b><br><b>Registered arch
 ers </b>at 9m on 40-cm target face unless otherwise noted:<u></u><br><u></u
 ><br><b>Target Assignments:</b><br><b><br></b><br>4A.<br>4B.<br><u></u><b><
 br></b>5. <b>Brennan F.\, </b>20\, pd - <b>-&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br><br>6A. 
 <b>Perrin S.\, </b>adult\, pd - <b>131 pts</b>( avg´d)<b>-&gt\; </b><b>Outd
 oor 2</b><br>6B. <b>Marguerite S.\, </b>16\, pd -&gt\; <b>Outdoor 2</b><br>
 <br>7. <b>Rachel J.\, </b>adult\, pd -&gt\; <b>Outdoor 2<br></b><br>8A. <b>
 Colleen H.\, </b>adult\, pd - <b>103 pts </b>(avg´d)<b>-&gt\; Outdoor 2</b>
 <br>8B. <b>Weston H.</b>\, 11.\, on 60-cm target face\, substituted for 6/1
 8\, pd - <b>156 pts </b>(avg´d)<b>-&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br><br>9. <b>Zac M.\
 , </b>11.\, on 60-cm target face\, pd. - <b>204 pts </b>(avg´d) <b>-&gt\; O
 utdoor 2</b><br><br>10A.<br>10B.<br><br>Space will be limited to 10-15 arch
 ers per session depending on the number of family groups in attendance or i
 n accordance with CDC Guidelines. <br>Each person will have a target stand\
 , except after 10 people have registered\, members may be assigned to share
  a target stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allow
 ed on the field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae. <br>Parent
 s of juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator. <br>Pare
 nts of juniors 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their 
 child for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is 
 accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-time Class. <br><br>We will accept a li
 mited number of kids under 12 into the program each semester\, depending on
  the total  number of archers in all the classes. If you join before the li
 mit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and t
 ake other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later join Outdoor 2. If you are 
 under 12\, registered and paid after the cut off\, your fee will be returne
 d to you. <br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times bef
 ore qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as s
 oon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows. <br>Adults don´t n
 eed a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories pac
 ket (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor
  2. ($18) Please pay for this at the field\, as our stock fluctuates becaus
 e of dealer supply fluctuations<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string l
 oop)\, optional but really needed to practice form\, warm up before classes
  ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be poste
 d. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recogniz
 e your final score\, because it will have been averaged by taking your reco
 rded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the number of arrows you shot 
 to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full rou
 nd score. After the last first-time class each weekend\, final scores may a
 lso be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an email with more information
  before your next class.
