DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u>
 </u>REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to adult\, juniors 8+\, and parents! Please 
 read all the info below and in the registration and waivers.<br><br>More in
 formation\, registration forms and waivers are available at&nbsp\;<a href="
 http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrainingcenter.com</a>.<br
 ><br>Register here using ONE of these forms:<br><a href="https://docs.googl
 e.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfcwG419ZK9XmA4-JlXM-zhjhvSPCF8NCwWJlzFP2w-gRliUw/vi
 ewform">2022 Winter/Spring Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Juniors + Parent
 s</a>&nbsp\; OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSe-YxP
 KAMTxiC7kVt6fZuQJeidXENYq_iV4rWj1RaXdLhPoew/viewform">2022 Winter/Spring Ou
 tdoor 1: First-time Class for Adults</a><br><br>Sign up for just one Outdoo
 r 1 class\, because most juniors 11+ and all adults graduate out of this cl
 ass into Outdoor 2 after the first lesson.<u></u><br><br><b>Your name will 
 be added below and your place reserved on a</b> <b>first registered and pai
 d basis and after we receive 3 things</b>:&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br>2022 OUTDOOR 1 
 REGISTRATION FORM + WAIVERS + FEE<u></u><br><u></u><br><b>Adults do not nee
 d a minimum score to move to Outdoor 2!</b><u></u><br><u></u><b><br></b><u>
 </u><b>Registered archers&nbsp\;</b>at 9m on 40-cm target face unless other
 wise noted:<br><b>Target Assignments:</b><br>1.&nbsp\;<br>2.<br>3.&nbsp\;<b
 >Betsy S</b>.\, adult - pd <b>93 pts</b><br>4.&nbsp\;<b>Cara B</b>.\, adult
  - pd - <b>48 pts</b><br>5.&nbsp\;<b>Victor G</b>.\, adult - pd - <b>31 pts
 </b><br>6. <b>Tyler W.\, </b>dad - pd <b>-?</b><br>7. <b>River T.\, </b>14 
 - <b>163 pts -&gt\;Outdoor 2</b><br>8. <b>Ryan M</b>.\, dad - pd - <b>95 pt
 s</b><br>9. <b>Reed M.</b>\, 11\, on 60-cm target face - pd - <b>94 pts </b
 >- averaged <b>-&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br>10.<br><br>Space will be limited to 
 10-15 archers per session depending on the number of family groups in atten
 dance or in accordance with CDC Guidelines.&nbsp\;<br>Each person will have
  a target stand\, except after 10 people have registered\, two members from
  the same family will share one target stand.<br>The archer and a maximum o
 f one spectator will be allowed on the field until further notice or approv
 ed by Coach Racae.&nbsp\;<br>Parents of juniors 10+ can sign up as an arche
 r or watch as a spectator. Parents of juniors 8-9 years old need to registe
 r\, pay\, and shoot with their child for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum o
 f one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-time Cla
 ss.&nbsp\;<br><br>We will accept a limited&nbsp\;number of kids under 12 in
 to the program each semester\, depending on the total&nbsp\; number of arch
 ers in all the classes. If you join before the limit is reached\, and are y
 ounger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take other Outdoor 1 classe
 s as needed and later join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;If you are under 12\, registere
 d and paid after the cut off\, your fee will be returned to you.&nbsp\;<br>
 <br>Juniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying
  to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you sco
 re on average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need a mi
 nimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (arm
 guard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($15
 )<br>fp = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but really nee
 ded to practice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of eac
 h Outdoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a comp
 lete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, because i
 t will have been averaged by taking your recorded score from your scorecard
 \, dividing by the number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and 
 then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round score. After the last class
  on the weekend\, final scores will also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participa
 nts in an email with more information before your next class.<u></u><u></u>
 <u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
