RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Chicago:20220528T103000
CREATED:20220102T020915Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><br><b>Tournament
 s are held at the end of each calendar month at 10:30 am - 12:30 pm on Satu
 rdays and Sundays</b>\, weather permitting.&nbsp\;<u></u>If you are new to 
 our program\, come and try it\, so you will be more comfortable and better 
 prepared next month!<br><br><u></u>The only differences between the regular
  training sessions and the tournaments are that we are more closely reprodu
 cing tournament conditions\, which include:<u></u><br><ul><li><u></u>No coa
 ching while you are on the shooting line (but\, as in a real tournament\, y
 <u></u>ou can always ask the coach for help in between the ends.) This is y
 our chance to find out how well you can do the form on your own\, and learn
  how to go into ¨trusting¨ compared with ¨training¨ mode.</li><li><u></u>Yo
 u will shoot more arrows :&nbsp\; 2 practice ends + Two rounds -&nbsp\;<u><
 /u>60 arrows at 9m and 13.5m or 72 arrows at 20m-70m</li><li><u></u>You wil
 l score every arrow for two rounds.&nbsp\;<u></u></li><li><u></u>The ends w
 ill be timed. You´ll have 4 min to shoot 6 arrows.<u></u></li><li>Everyone 
 will be shooting at close-to-regular tournament spacing so there will be tw
 o archers on each target about 3 ft apart\, depending on the number of regi
 strations</li><li>There will be a maximum of 20 archers on the shooting lin
 e at the same time. Awesome! (Lots of arrow flying towards the targets!)</l
 i></ul><u></u><b>Outside of the tournament weeks</b>\, each week the focus 
 of your lessons will be on particular Steps of Shooting of the NTS (Nationa
 l Training System) shot cycle\, to help you focus and improve your form\, w
 hich\, as we all know\, leads to greater precision (tighter groups of arrow
 s) and ultimately greater accuracy (tight groups of arrows dead center).<u>
 </u><br><br><u></u><b>FEBRUARY</b><br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>12-1
 8</b>&nbsp\;Welcome Back: Understanding&nbsp\; NTS Concepts&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<b
 r><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>19-25</b>&nbsp\;NTS Steps 1+2: STANCE + 
 NOCK&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>26 - MAR 4: MASTER C
 HALLENGE TOURNAMENT WEEK (Pin Shoot)</b><br><b>MARCH</b><br><b>&nbsp\; &nbs
 p\; &nbsp\;5-11</b>&nbsp\;NTS Step 3: HOOK &amp\; GRIP&nbsp\; &nbsp\;<u></u
 ><br><u></u>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;<b>12-18&nbsp\;</b>NTS Step 4: SET<u></u
 ><br><u></u><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;19-25</b>&nbsp\;<u></u>NTS Step 5: SE
 T-UP&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br><u></u><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>26 - APR 1: M
 ASTER CHALLENGE TOURNAMENT WEEKEND (Pin Shoot)</b><br><b>APRIL</b><br><b>&n
 bsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;2-8</b>&nbsp\;<u></u>NTS Step 6 DRAW to LOAD&nbsp\; &n
 bsp\; &nbsp\;<br><u></u><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;9-15&nbsp\;</b><u></u>NTS
  Step 7 ANCHOR&nbsp\; &nbsp\;<br><u></u><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;16-22&nbs
 p\;</b><u></u>NTS Step 8 TRANSFER to HOLD<br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;<b>23-2
 9&nbsp\;</b>NTS Step 9 EXPAND / AIM<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;30 - MAY 6
 : MASTER CHALLENGE TOURNAMENT WEEKEND (Pin Shoot)</b><br><u></u><b>MAY</b><
 br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>7-13&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</b>NTS Step 10 RELEA
 SE and FOLLOW-THROUGH<br><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</b><b>14-20</b>&nbsp\;<
 u></u>NTS Step 11 FEEDBACK&nbsp\;<u></u><br><u></u>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;<
 b>21-27 </b>Putting it all together!<br><u></u><b>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\;</
 b><b>28-29 : END OF SEMESTER MASTER CHALLENGE TOURNAMENT WEEKEND (Pin Shoot
 )</b><br><br>Your goal is always to replicate the NTS step(s) mindfully and
  consistently on every shot.<br><br>You do not need to score every class. I
 n fact\, it would be more beneficial to you if you scored only during Maste
 r Challenge Tournament Weeks\, which happen the last week of each month. Th
 is is because working on the NTS Steps of Shooting (your form) is more easi
 ly done without the distraction of the target face or scoring\, and you wil
 l improve faster.<br><br>As you reach higher levels\, you will learn the NT
 S Steps in progressively greater detail.<br>The NTS Steps are cumulative wi
 th each step most successfully completed if the previous steps have been co
 mpleted mindfully.&nbsp\;<br><br>Your ability to learn and understand the N
 TS Steps\, and use deep focus on these Steps while shooting outdoors and wh
 ile using your stretchband/string loop at home will propel you to higher le
 vels fast!<br><br><b>Goals by the end of the semester:&nbsp\;</b><br>See Co
 ach Racae´s email ¨2022 New Year´s Goals¨<br><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u
 ></u></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260517T083255Z
SEQUENCE:3
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:ATCI OUTDOOR 2-9 END-OF-SEMESTER TOURNAMENT  (Pin Shoot)
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
