DESCRIPTION:Training classes at this location are reserved for competitive 
 and advanced archers..\n\nREMINDER:  Everyone needs to come to at least one
  Training Class per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (All Indoor 2-
 6 at 9m classes are training classes.)\n\nCoach Racae will coach the Outdoo
 r 3-9 Training Class whenever there are at least 5 archers registered by Th
 ursday 12:00 pm (for Sat) and Friday 12:00 pm (for Sun)\, except on federal
  holidays (like Easter)\, because Medicare's GUIDE program does not pay for
  caregivers on federal holidays!!! Sorry to disappoint!  \n\nTRAINING CLASS
  (TC): $57/archer/3-hr class\n(1x/wk required to attend Open Practice)\nFAC
 ILITY FEE (FF) (required each month): $75/month/archer due on 1st of the mo
 nth. (USAA Level 3 Coaches do not pay facility fee.)\nOPEN PRACTICE (OP) In
 cluded in facility fee (1-2x/wk recommended)\nPRIVATE LESSON (PL): $125/hr/
 archer (1x/mo recommended)\n\nPlease add your name to the target list below
  to register\nFocus primarily on perfecting your form\, \nslowly increasing
  your physical strength and draw weight\, \nstrengthening your mental progr
 am\, \ndetermining your average and personal best\, \nunderstanding the spr
 ead between the two\, and working on closing it.\n\nEQUIPMENT:\nYou need yo
 ur own equipment: \nCompetition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\
 , rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest prote
 ctor\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow pu
 ller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added until you reach a highe
 r level\, but you should order them in advance.) \n\nWear your ATCI shirt t
 o training.\n\nWEATHER / DAYLIGHT\n\nSession times may vary depending on te
 mperature/daylight conditions.\nDuring inclement weather (<52F or 100F>\, 2
 0 mph winds\, heavy rain\, lightning) class will move to the Indoor 9m rang
 e to practice form and be noted on the calendar shortly before the schedule
 d session.\nTARGET ARRANGEMENTS\nMay vary each session\, depending on who a
 ttends and distances needed.\nWhen you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on
  the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the next distance until you rea
 ch your competition distance (see below)\nIf you trained outdoors in the 20
 25 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.\n\nTarget 1 at
  70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake
  can use it for independent practice in between classes.\nTarget 2 at 60m (
 U18 + Masters competition distance) \nTargets 3+4 at 50m\nTarget 5+6 at 40m
  (U15 competition distance) \nTarget 7+8 at 30m (U13 competition distance) 
 \nTargets 9 at 20m (for adults who have just graduated out of Indoor 2)\nTa
 rget 10 at 13.5m (for juniors who have just graduated out of Indoor 2)\n\nI
 deally\, we want to practice with two archers/target to replicate outdoor c
 ompetition conditions.\n\nTARGET ASSIGNMENTS\nTargets are assigned outdoors
  in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\, so add your name nex
 t to your distance below. \nIf you need help or have questions\, email/text
  Coach Racae\n(Dotted lines represent tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, a
 nd 9.)\n\nATCIOCT = 2026 ATCI Outdoor Competition Team  \nMQS at your tourn
 ament distance\, 36-arrow rounds on 122-cm target face: \n260 pts or 520 pt
 s (2 rounds)\n----------------------------------\n1A. (70m)\n1B\n\n2A. (60m
 )  \n2B\n\n3A. (50m)  \n----------------------------------\n3B Adrianne M. 
 \n\n4A. (50m) Nick E\n4B. Colby K.\n----------------------------------\n5A.
  (40m) Finn E\n5B.  Ethan N (5/12)\n \n6A. (40m) Sara T\n------------------
 ----------------\n6B. Luke T\n\n7A. (30m) Emma A.\n7B. \n------------------
 ---------------- \n8A. (30m) \n8B.\n\n9A. (20m) Rhys E\n-------------------
 ---------------\n9B. Matt L\n\n10A. (13.5m) Akhil C\n10B
