 1fWGpP5qakhT6OuAc6jJ_FQ/viewform"><u>2023 Outdoor 1: First-time Class for A
 dults</u></a>  OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSc_b
 YEFoE4oXkcm0T6fZK99fu_q6lL8wZGClXyfa1GZbahh-g/viewform"><u>2023 Outdoor 1: 
 First-time Class for Juniors and Parents</u></a><br><br>Sign up for just ON
 E Outdoor 1 class\, because most people graduate out of this class into Out
 door 2 after the first lesson.<br>Your name will be added below and your pl
 ace reserved on a first registered and paid basis and after we receive 3 th
 ings:  <br><b>2023 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM   +  MEMBERSHIP AND WAIVERS 
 PACKET +   FEE</b><b><br></b><u></u><br><b>USA Archery Level 4 NTS Coach Ra
 cae Meyer and other instructors/coaches.</b><br><b>See </b><a href="https:/
 /www.archerytrainingcenter.com/who-we-are"><u><u>https://www.archerytrainin
 gcenter.com/who-we-are</u></u></a><b><br></b><br><b>Registered archers </b>
 at 9m on 40-cm target face unless otherwise noted:<u></u><br><u></u><br><b>
 Target Assignments:</b><br><br>4A. <br>4B. <br><u></u><b><br></b>5A. <b>Kru
 thika R</b>.\, adult\, pd - <b>38 pts (avg´d) -&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br>5B. <
 b>Adithya V.R</b>.\, adult\, pd - <b>64 pts (avg´d) -&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br
 ><br>6A. <br>6B. <br><br>7.. <b>Whitney R</b>.\, adult\, pd - <b>55 pts (av
 g´d) -&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br><br>8A. <b>Jill Y.\, </b>adult\, pd - <b>44 pt
 s (avg´d) -&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br>8B. <b>Nolan Y.\, 8 \, </b>pd  - <b>53 pt
 s (avg´d) -&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br><br>9.<br><br>10A. <b>Chris C.\, </b>adul
 t\, pd - <b>115 pts (avg´d) -&gt\; Outdoor 2</b><br>10B. <b>Mack C.\, </b>8
 \, pd - <b>30 pts (avg´d) -&gt\; Outdoor 1<br></b><br> <b>James S.\, </b>ad
 ult\, pd - need waivers - <b>DNA </b>- <b>fee forfeited</b><br><br>Space wi
 ll be limited to 10-15 archers per session depending on the number of famil
 y groups in attendance or in accordance with CDC Guidelines. <br>Each perso
 n will have a target stand\, except after 10 people have registered\, membe
 rs may be assigned to share a target stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of 
 one spectator will be allowed on the field until further notice or approved
  by Coach Racae. <br>Parents of juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or wat
 ch as a spectator. <br>Parents of juniors 8-9 years old need to register\, 
 pay\, and shoot with their child for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of on
 e 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-time Class. 
 <br><br>We will accept a limited number of kids under 12 into the program e
 ach semester\, depending on the total  number of archers in all the classes
 . If you join before the limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´l
 l stay in the program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as needed and later 
 join Outdoor 2. If you are under 12\, registered and paid after the cut off
 \, your fee will be returned to you. <br><br>Juniors may need to take Outdo
 or 1 two or three times before qualifying to get into Outdoor 2 by scoring 
 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on average about 5 pts/end of 3
  arrows. <br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<
 br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard\, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which
  will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($18) Please pay for this at the field\, as 
 our stock fluctuates because of dealer supply fluctuations<br>fp = form pac
 k (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but really needed to practice fo
 rm\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Outdoor 1 class\
 , your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arr
 ows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, because it will have been a
 veraged by taking your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing by the
  number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying t
 hat by 30 to get a full round score. After the last first-time class each w
 eekend\, final scores may also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants in an 
 email with more information before your next class.
