 rcherytrainingcenter.com/news\n\n1. Daniel H.\n2. Evan L. JOAD\n3. Ty H.\n4
 . \n5. \n6.\n7.\n8.\n9.\n10.\n\n\nTime / Attendance Requirements: \nRECREAT
 IONAL: None \nPROGRESSIVE: Must continuously meet the time/attendance requi
 rements to remain in the Progressive Program. Those who fall short of the w
 eekly time/attendance requirements will automatically be considered Recreat
 ional\, and Recreational class fees will apply.  These classes are designed
  to prepared archers for CAP (Competitive Archery Program).\n\nFees:  \nREC
 REATIONAL FEES: \nAll fees are payable in advance of the Indoor at 18m clas
 s to secure your place in the class: \nTues 6:30-7:30pm: 1-hr class - $20\n
 Wed  6:30-8:00pm: 1.5-hr class - $30\nSat   3:30-5:30pm:  2-hr class - $40\
 nSun  3:30-5:30pm:  2-hr class - $40\n+ Enrollment fee: $20 (always due onc
 e per semester) \n\nPROGRESSIVE (min. attendance required):  \nIndoor 3B:  
      $TBD/wk (min. 5 hrs)  \nIndoor 4:         $TBD/wk (min. 6 hrs) \nIndoo
 r 5:         $TBD/wk (min. 8 hrs)  \n\nMONTHLY FEES for ADULTS at 18m:\n\nA
 dult classes only (Tues 7:30-8:30 + Sun 6:00-7:00):\nJAN   $ 120    \nFEB  
  $ 120 \nMAR   $ 120     \nAPR   $ 120      \nMAY   $ 120    \n\nAdult clas
 ses + Wed. 6:30-8:00:\nJAN   $ 188    \nFEB   $ 210 \nMAR   $ 233    \nAPR 
   $ 210      \nMAY   $ 210   \n\nMONTHLY FEES for JUNIORS at 18m:\nRecreati
 onal hourly fees apply. At this level archers should be in the range at lea
 st 5 hrs/wk to improve over time. If your schedule allows for this\, you ar
 e a Progressive archer\; if not\, you are a Recreational archer.
