DESCRIPTION:Training classes at this location are reserved for competitive 
 and advanced archers..<br><br>REMINDER:  Everyone needs to come to at least
  one Training Class per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (All Indoo
 r 2-6 at 9m classes are training classes.)<br><br>Coach Racae will coach th
 e Outdoor 3-9 Training Class whenever there are at least 5 archers register
 ed by Thursday 12:00 pm (for Sat) and Friday 9:00 am (for Sun)\, except on 
 federal holidays\, because Medicare's GUIDE program does not pay for caregi
 vers on federal holidays!!! Sorry to disappoint!   <br><br>TRAINING CLASS (
 TC): $57/archer/3-hr class<br>(1x/wk required to attend Open Practice)<br>F
 ACILITY FEE (FF) (required each month): $75/month/archer due on 1st of the 
 month. (USAA Level 3 Coaches do not pay facility fee.)<br>OPEN PRACTICE (OP
 ) Included in facility fee (1-2x/wk recommended)<br>PRIVATE LESSON (PL): $1
 25/hr/archer (1x/mo recommended)<br><br>Please add your name to the target 
 list below to register<br>Focus primarily on perfecting your form\, <br>slo
 wly increasing your physical strength and draw weight\, <br>strengthening y
 our mental program\, <br>determining your average and personal best\, <br>u
 nderstanding the spread between the two\, and working on closing it.<br><br
 >EQUIPMENT:<br>You need your own equipment: <br>Competition recurve bow\, s
 ight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar asse
 mbly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hi
 p or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be a
 dded until you reach a higher level\, but you should order them in advance.
 ) <br><br>Wear your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br>WEATHER / DAYLIGHT<br><b
 r>Session times may vary depending on temperature/daylight conditions.<br>D
 uring inclement weather (&lt\;52F or 100F&gt\;\, 20 mph winds\, heavy rain\
 , lightning) class will move to the Indoor 9m range to practice form and be
  noted on the calendar shortly before the scheduled session.<br>TARGET ARRA
 NGEMENTS<br>May vary each session\, depending on who attends and distances 
 needed.<br>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm target 
 face you'll move back to the next distance until you reach your competition
  distance (see below)<br>If you trained outdoors in the 2025 season\, you'l
 l return to the farthest distance you shot.<br><br>Target 1 at 70m (U21 + S
 eniors competition distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use it f
 or independent practice in between classes.<br>Target 2 at 60m (U18 + Maste
 rs competition distance) <br>Targets 3+4 at 50m<br>Target 5+6 at 40m (U15 c
 ompetition distance) <br>Target 7+8 at 30m (U13 competition distance) <br>T
 argets 9 at 20m (for adults who have just graduated out of Indoor 2)<br>Tar
 get 10 at 13.5m (for juniors who have just graduated out of Indoor 2)<br><b
 r>Ideally\, we want to practice with two archers/target to replicate outdoo
 r competition conditions.<br><br>TARGET ASSIGNMENTS<br>Targets are assigned
  outdoors in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\, so add your
  name next to your distance below. <br>If you need help or have questions\,
  email/text Coach Racae<br>(Dotted lines represent tent poles dividing Targ
 ets 3\, 6\, and 9.)<br><br>ATCIOCT = 2026 ATCI Outdoor Competition Team  <b
