DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u>
 </u>REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to adult\, juniors 8+\, and parents! Please 
 read all the info below and in the registration and waivers.<br><br>More in
 formation\, registration forms and waivers are available at&nbsp\;<a href="
 http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com">www.archerytrainingcenter.com</a>.<br
 ><br>Register here using ONE of these forms:<br><a href="https://docs.googl
 e.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfcwG419ZK9XmA4-JlXM-zhjhvSPCF8NCwWJlzFP2w-gRliUw/vi
 ewform">2022 Winter/Spring Outdoor 1: First-time Class for Juniors + Parent
 s</a>&nbsp\; OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSe-YxP
 KAMTxiC7kVt6fZuQJeidXENYq_iV4rWj1RaXdLhPoew/viewform">2022 Winter/Spring Ou
 tdoor 1: First-time Class for Adults</a><br><br>Sign up for just one Outdoo
 r 1 class\, because most people graduate out of this class into Outdoor 2 a
 fter the first lesson.<br><br><b>Your name will be added below and your pla
 ce reserved on a</b> <b>first registered and paid basis and after we receiv
 e 3 things</b>:&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br>2022 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM + WAIVERS
  + FEE<u></u><br><br><b>Registered archers&nbsp\;</b>at 9m on 40-cm target 
 face unless otherwise noted:<br><b>Target assignments:</b><br>1.&nbsp\;<br>
 2.<br>3. Adam McM.\, adult - pd - <b>107 pts</b><br>4. Jit K.\, adult - pd 
 - <b>99 pts</b><br>5. Kundana A.\, 12 - on 60-cm target face - pd -&nbsp\;<
 b>96 pts -&gt\; Outdoor 2 - CONGRATS!</b><br>6. Porter K.\, 11 - on 60-cm t
 arget face - pd - <b>59 pts </b>(corrected) <b>-&gt\; Outdoor 2 - CONGRATS!
 !</b><br>7.&nbsp\;<br>8.<br>9.<br>10.<br><br>Space will be limited to 10-15
  archers per session depending on the number of family groups in attendance
  or in accordance with CDC Guidelines.&nbsp\;<br>Each person will have a ta
 rget stand\, except after 10 people have registered\, two members from the 
 same family will share one target stand.<br>The archer and a maximum of one
  spectator will be allowed on the field until further notice or approved by
  Coach Racae.&nbsp\;<br>Parents of juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or 
 watch as a spectator. Parents of juniors 8-9 years old need to register\, p
 ay\, and shoot with their child for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one
  8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into each Outdoor 1: First-time Class.&n
 bsp\;<br><br>We will accept a limited&nbsp\;number of kids under 12 into th
 e program each semester\, depending on the total&nbsp\; number of archers i
 n all the classes. If you join before the limit is reached\, and are younge
 r than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take other Outdoor 1 classes as 
 needed and later join Outdoor 2.&nbsp\;If you are under 12\, registered and
  paid after the cut off\, your fee will be returned to you.&nbsp\;<br><br>J
 uniors may need to take Outdoor 1 two or three times before qualifying to g
 et into Outdoor 2 by scoring 50 pts. You´ll make it as soon as you score on
  average about 5 pts/end of 3 arrows.&nbsp\;<br>Adults don´t need a minimum
  score to graduate into Outdoor 2.<br><br>ap = accessories packet (armguard
 \, fingertab\, fingersling)\, which will be needed for Outdoor 2. ($15)<br>
 fp = form pack (stretchband and string loop)\, optional but really needed t
 o practice form\, warm up before classes ($4)<br><br>At the end of each Out
 door 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a complete 
 round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, because it wil
 l have been averaged by taking your recorded score from your scorecard\, di
 viding by the number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then 
 multiplying that by 30 to get a full round score. After the last class on t
 he weekend\, final scores will also be sent to all Outdoor 1 participants i
 n an email with more information before your next class.<u></u><u></u><u></
 u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
