 W !<br><br>Open to adults\, juniors 8+\, and parents! Please read all the i
 nfo below and in the registration and waivers. <br><br>The composition of t
 he classes are by skill level\, not age.. There is usually about an even sp
 lit between adults and juniors in each class.<br><br>More information\, reg
 istration forms and waivers are available at <a href="http://www.archerytra
 iningcenter.com"><u><u><u><u><u>www.archerytrainingcenter.com</u></u></u></
 u></u></a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE of these forms:<br><a href="http
 s://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeciOgkyuKTLZ5_ZaWCEyQKYSX1fWGpP5qakhT
 6OuAc6jJ_FQ/viewform"><u><u>2023 Indoor 1: First-time Class for Adults</u><
 /u></a>  OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSc_bYEFoE4
 oXkcm0T6fZK99fu_q6lL8wZGClXyfa1GZbahh-g/viewform"><u><u>2023 Indoor 1: Firs
 t-time Class for Juniors and Parents</u></u></a><br><br>Sign up for just ON
 E Indoor 1 class\, because most people graduate out of this class into Indo
 or 2 after the first lesson.<br><br>Your name will be added below and your 
 place reserved on a first registered and paid basis and after we receive 3 
 things:  <br><b>2023 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM   +  MEMBERSHIP AND WAIVER
 S PACKET +   FEE</b><b><br></b><u></u><br><b>USA Archery Level 4 NTS Coach 
 Racae Meyer and other instructors/coaches.</b><br><b>See </b><a href="https
 ://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/who-we-are"><u><u><u>https://www.archerytr
 ainingcenter.com/who-we-are</u></u></u></a><b><br></b><br><b>Registered arc
 hers </b>at 9m on 40-cm target face unless otherwise noted:<br><u></u><b><b
 r></b>1. <b>Garrett W.</b>\, adult\, pd - <b>116 pts -&gt\; Indoor 2</b><br
 ><br>2. <b>Caleb W.</b>\, 11\, on 60-cm target face\, pd - <b>123 pts -&gt\
 ; Indoor 2</b><br><br>3. <b>Gabriel W</b>.\, 8\, on 60-cm target face\, pd 
 - <b> 41 pts -&gt\; Indoor 1</b><br><br>4. <b>Clay W</b>.\, adult\, pd - <b
 >92 pts -&gt\; Indoor 2</b><br><br>5. <b>Rachel K.\, </b>adult\, pd - <b>66
  pts -&gt\; Indoor 2</b><br><br>6. <b>Johnny L.\, </b>adult\, pd - <b>89 pt
 s -&gt\; Indoor 2</b><br><br>7. <b>Tatum F.\, </b>11\, on 60-cm target face
 \, pd - <b>46 pts -&gt\; Indoor 2</b><br><br>8.<br><br>Space will be limite
 d to 16 archers per session or in accordance with CDC Guidelines. <br><br>T
 here will be two lines of 8 archers when the number of participants exceeds
  8 archers.<br>Not more than 8 archers will be on the shooting line at the 
 same time.<br>A = Line A<br>B = Line B<br><br>The archer and a maximum of o
 ne spectator will be allowed on the field until further notice or approved 
 by Coach Racae. <br><br>Parents of juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or 
 watch as a spectator. <br>Parents of juniors 8-9 years old need to register
 \, pay\, and shoot with their child for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of
  one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into each Indoor 1: First-time Class
 . <br><br>We will accept a limited number of juniors under 12 into the prog
 ram each semester\, depending on the total  number of archers in all the cl
 asses. If you join before the limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, 
 you´ll stay in the program and take other Indoor 1 classes as needed and la
 ter join Indoor 2. If you are under 12\, and have registered and paid after
  the cut off\, your fee will be returned to you. <br><br>Juniors may need t
 o take Indoor 1 two or three times before qualifying for Indoor 2 by scorin
 g 50 pts over 30 arrows.<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate i
 nto Indoor 2.<br><br>At the end of each Indoor 1 class\, your scores will b
 e posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not r
 ecognize your final score\, because it will have been averaged by taking yo
 ur recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing it by the number of arrows
  you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get 
 a full round score.
