 8.<br><br>Space will be limited to 16 archers per session or in accordance 
 with CDC Guidelines. <br>Each person will have a target no. assigned as abo
 ve. <br><br>There will be two lines of 8 archers when the number of partici
 pants exceeds 8 archers.<br>Not more than 8 archers will be on the shooting
  line at the same time.<br>A = Line A<br>B = Line B<br><br>The archer and a
  maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field until further notice
  or approved by Coach Racae. <br><br>Parents of juniors 10+ can sign up as 
 an archer or watch as a spectator. <br>Parents of juniors 8-9 years old nee
 d to register\, pay\, and shoot with their child for greater safety.<br><br
 >A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into each Indoor 1: Fir
 st-time Class. <br><br>We will accept a limited number of juniors under 12 
 into the program each semester\, depending on the total  number of archers 
 in all the classes. If you join before the limit is reached\, and are young
 er than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take other Indoor 1 classes as 
 needed and later join Indoor 2. If you are under 12\, and have registered a
 nd paid after the cut off\, your fee will be returned to you. <br><br>Junio
 rs may need to take Indoor 1 two or three times before qualifying for Indoo
 r 2 by scoring 50 pts over 30 arrows.<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score 
 to graduate into Indoor 2.<br><br>At the end of each Indoor 1 class\, your 
 scores will be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, 
 you may not recognize your final score\, because it will have been averaged
  by taking your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing it by the num
 ber of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying that 
 by 30 to get a full round score.
