DESCRIPTION:Training classes at this location are reserved for competitive 
 and advanced archers..\n\nREMINDER:  Everyone needs to come to at least one
  Training Class per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (All Indoor 2-
 6 at 9m classes are training classes.)\n\nCoach Racae will coach the Outdoo
 r 3-9 Training Class whenever there are at least 5 archers registered by Fr
 i 12:00 pm (for Sat) and Sat 12:00 pm (for Sun).   \n\nTRAINING CLASS (TC):
  $57/archer/3-hr class\n(1x/wk required to attend Open Practice)\nFACILITY 
 FEE (FF) (required each month): $75/month/archer due on 1st of the month. (
 USAA Level 3 Coaches do not pay facility fee.)\nOPEN PRACTICE (OP) Included
  in facility fee (1-2x/wk recommended)\nPRIVATE LESSON (PL): $125/hr/archer
  (1x/mo recommended)\n\nPlease add your name to the target list below to re
 gister\nFocus primarily on perfecting your form\, \nslowly increasing your 
 physical strength and draw weight\, \nstrengthening your mental program\, \
 ndetermining your average and personal best\, \nunderstanding the spread be
 tween the two\, and working on closing it.\n\nEQUIPMENT:\nYou need your own
  equipment: \nCompetition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest
 \, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\,
  armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\,
  etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added until you reach a higher leve
 l\, but you should order them in advance.) \n\nWear your ATCI shirt to trai
 ning.\n\nWEATHER / DAYLIGHT\n\nSession times may vary depending on temperat
 ure/daylight conditions.\nDuring inclement weather (<52F or 100F>\, 20 mph 
 winds\, heavy rain\, lightning) class will move to the Indoor 9m range to p
 ractice form and be noted on the calendar shortly before the scheduled sess
 ion.\nTARGET ARRANGEMENTS\nMay vary each session\, depending on who attends
  and distances needed.\nWhen you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 1
 22-cm target face you'll move back to the next distance until you reach you
 r competition distance (see below)\nIf you trained outdoors in the 2025 sea
 son\, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.\n\nTarget 1 at 70m (
 U21 + Seniors competition distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can u
 se it for independent practice in between classes.\nTarget 2 at 60m (U18 + 
 Masters competition distance) \nTargets 3+4 at 50m\nTarget 5+6 at 40m (U15 
 competition distance) \nTarget 7+8 at 30m (U13 competition distance) \nTarg
 ets 9 at 20m (for adults who have just graduated out of Indoor 2)\nTarget 1
 0 at 13.5m (for juniors who have just graduated out of Indoor 2)\n\nIdeally
 \, we want to practice with two archers/target to replicate outdoor competi
 tion conditions.\n\nTARGET ASSIGNMENTS\nTargets are assigned outdoors in ad
 vance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\, so add your name next to y
 our distance below. \nIf you need help or have questions\, email/text Coach
  Racae\n(Dotted lines represent tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)
 \n\nATCIOCT = 2026 ATCI Outdoor Competition Team  \nMQS at your tournament 
 distance\, 36-arrow rounds on 122-cm target face: \n260 pts or 520 pts (2 r
 ounds)\n----------------------------------\n1A. (70m)\n1B\n\n2A. (60m)  \n2
 B\n\n3A. (50m)  \n----------------------------------\n3B\n\n4A. (50m) ABBY 
 y\, 14. 256+253\n4B. \n----------------------------------\n5A. (40m)\n5B.  
 Sara T. (O6 @ 40m) DNS\n\n6A. (40m) \n----------------------------------\n6
 B. \n\n7A. (30m) Akhil C. 13\, 174 + 245\n7B.  Emma A.\, 14 210 + 205\n----
 ------------------------------ \n8A. (30m)  Ellie Y\, 11 DNS\n8B.\n\n9A. (2
 0m) \n----------------------------------\n9B. \n\n10A. (13.5m)  \n10B
