DESCRIPTION:<b>What we worked on:</b><br>Staying consistent and confident.<
 br>Vacation: June 21-27<br>About 3 weeks of practice left before JTN<span> 
 </span><br><br>There is not enough time or arrows left before JTN to change
  or improve the "default" positions\, so concentrate on being consistent an
 d keeping your confidence.<br>"Just shoot your shot." The same shot you sho
 ot in practice. This will give you the best chance of shooting consistent a
 nd tighter groups at JTN.<br><br>There will be time to work more on SET UP 
 / DRAW to LOAD / TRANSFER to HOLD after JTN.<br><br>So reinforce the positi
 ons you are doing well\, and feel the shot\, especially when the positions 
 are not consistent\, and then break down whenever they aren't the same. Tak
 e a deep breath and start your shot again.<br><br>Focus on:<br>Increasing a
 rrow count in the weeks left before JTN.<br>Breaking down.<br>Does it feel 
 the same?<br>Solidifying your alignments by the end of SET UP and certainly
  before RELEASE<br>Keeping your bow arm up.<br><br>Your strong points are m
 any - most of the shot cycle and particularly<br>POSTURE<br>SHOULDERS Level
 <br>HEAD still<br>RELEASE / FOLLOW-THROUGH<br><br>You've done very well thi
 s year\, so go with confidence and make yourself proud!<br>I'll see you whe
 n you get back from Mexico! Have a great time!\n\nJoin with Google Meet: ht
 tps://meet.google.com/srb-htjf-kxk\n\nLearn more about Meet at: https://sup
 port.google.com/a/users/answer/9282720
