 , but you should order them in advance.) \n\nWear your ATCI shirt to traini
 ng.\n\nWEATHER / DAYLIGHT\nSession times may vary depending on temperature/
 daylight conditions.\nDuring inclement weather (<52F or 100F>\, 20 mph wind
 s\, heavy rain\, lightning) class will move to the Indoor 9m range to pract
 ice form and be noted on the calendar shortly before the scheduled session.
 \n\nTARGET ARRANGEMENTS\nMay vary each session\, depending on who attends a
 nd distances needed.\nWhen you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122
 -cm target face you'll move back to the next distance until you reach your 
 competition distance (see below)\nIf you trained outdoors in the 2025 seaso
 n\, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.\n\nTarget 1 at 70m (U2
 1 + Seniors competition distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use
  it for independent practice in between classes.\nTarget 2 at 60m (U18 + Ma
 sters competition distance) \nTargets 3+4 at 50m\nTarget 5+6 at 40m (U15 co
 mpetition distance) \nTarget 7+8 at 30m (U13 competition distance) \nTarget
 s 9 at 20m (for adults who have just graduated out of Indoor 2)\nTarget 10 
 at 13.5m (for juniors who have just graduated out of Indoor 2)\n\nIdeally\,
  we want to practice with two archers/target to replicate outdoor competiti
 on conditions.\n\nTARGET ASSIGNMENTS\nTargets are assigned outdoors in adva
 nce to reduce confusion and delay on the day\, so add your name next to you
 r distance below. \nIf you need help or have questions\, email/text Coach R
