DESCRIPTION:<b>Tournament Prep:</b><br><b>Some of the things we covered tod
 ay:</b><br><b><br></b><br><span><b>10 weeks to JOAD Target Nationals</b></s
 pan><br><ul><li><span><b>Homework: Come up with your own training program\,
  based on what's possible/doable in the time</b></span></li><li><span>I'll 
 also come up with a training program</span></li><li><span>Let's discuss and
  analyze in next session</span></li></ul><br><span>Believe in yourself.</sp
 an><br><span>Have a big-sky goal - something to drive and motivate you!</sp
 an><br><ul><li><span>Remember: Motivation comes through action (not the oth
 er way around) So if you want to achieve something\, you need to act accord
 ingly. </span></li><li>What are the champions doing? How close can you get 
 to that?</li></ul><br><span>Set achievable\, realistic goals based on resou
 rces</span><br><ul><li>Time - what can you accomplish in 8.5-10 hrs/wk?</li
 ><li>Parental support - excellent</li><li>Financial support - excellent</li
 ></ul><br>How do you see yourself? <br><br><b>Confidence --&gt\; Consistenc
 y --&gt\; Confidence in</b><br><ul><li><b>Physical:</b><ul><li><b>Form </b>
 - Consistency\, esp. BOW ARM and clean\, strong RELEASE</li><li><b>Strength
  </b><span>- Holding SPTs at least </span></li><li><span><b>Endurance </b>-
  Goal: Form and strength endures thru 150 arrows</span></li><li><b>Training
  - </b>arrow count\, hours practicing\, exercises<ul><li>Present schedule:<
 ul><li>Sun O</li><li>Mon 2 hrs</li><li>Tues 30 min virtual</li><li>Wed 1.5-
 2.0 hrs in indoor range or on field</li><li>Thurs 0</li><li>Fri 1.5-2.0 hrs
  on field</li><li>Sat 3 hrs on field in training class</li></ul></li></ul><
 /li></ul></li><li><b>Mental:</b><ul><li><b>Strength</b><ul><li><b>Deep focu
 s </b>until it becomes a habit on every shot</li><li><b>Trusting mode: </b>
 Trust your training</li></ul></li><li><b>Strategy in difficult situations</
 b><ul><li>What could happen? What is the solution?</li><li>What do you say 
 to yourself? "Ooops\, keep going"</li></ul></li><li><b>Recognize what is in
  and out of your control</b><ul><li>Out - Who shows up\, the weather\, othe
 r people's comments\, rankings\, etc.</li><li>In <ul><li>How you react \; w
 hat you say to yourself - </li><li>Have a backup strategy <ul><li>What do y
 ou replace the anxiety with? (Something in your control)</li></ul></li></ul
 ></li></ul></li></ul></li><li><b>Emotion</b><ul><li><b>Strength</b><ul><li>
 What do you do/think when you get emotional?</li></ul></li></ul></li><li><b
 >Equipment</b><ul><li>Know your equipment and how to fix everything</li><li
 >Check it yourself before the competition so you know it's okay</li><li>Hav
 e back up everything\, esp. tab\, string\, rest\, arrows\, etc.</li><li>Bui
 ld your confidence in your equipment through knowledge and use</li></ul></l
 i><li><b>Scores</b><ul><li><b>Average Score</b></li><li><b>Personal Best</b
 ></li><li><b>Close the gap between average score and PB</b></li><li><b>Rank
 ing - </b>Goal: in top half of division: Look up what last year's U15 score
 s were in top half</li></ul></li><li><b>Social / Atmosphere</b><ul><li>Supp
 ortive archers</li><li>Fun</li></ul></li></ul>\n\nJoin with Google Meet: ht
 tps://meet.google.com/uxu-zjrg-dym\n\nLearn more about Meet at: https://sup
 port.google.com/a/users/answer/9282720
