 oXkcm0T6fZK99fu_q6lL8wZGClXyfa1GZbahh-g/viewform"><u><u>2023 Indoor 1: Firs
 t-time Class for Juniors and Parents</u></u></a><br><br>Sign up for just ON
 E Indoor 1 class\, because most people graduate out of this class into Indo
 or 2 after the first lesson.<br><br>Your name will be added below and your 
 place reserved on a first registered and paid basis and after we receive 3 
 things:  <br><b>2023 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM   +  MEMBERSHIP AND WAIVER
 S PACKET +   FEE</b><b><br></b><u></u><br><b>USA Archery Level 4 NTS Coach 
 Racae Meyer and other instructors/coaches.</b><br><b>See </b><a href="https
 ://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/who-we-are"><u><u><u>https://www.archerytr
 ainingcenter.com/who-we-are</u></u></u></a><b><br></b><br><b>Registered arc
 hers </b>at 9m on 40-cm target face unless otherwise noted:<u></u><br><u></
 u><br><b>Target Assignments:</b><br><u></u><b><br></b>1. <br><br>2. <b>Kai 
 M.\, age? </b> pd - need waivers - <b>108 pts -&gt\; Indoor 2</b><br><br>3.
  <b>Virgil M.\, </b>adult\, pd - need waivers - <b>143 pts -&gt\; Indoor 2<
 /b><br><br>4<br><br>5<br><br>6<br><br>7<br><br>8.<br><br><b>Myron K</b>.\, 
 adult\, pd - to be rescheduled w/doctor's note<br><b>Melonie M. </b>age?\, 
 pd - need waivers - DNA - need substituted date<br><br>Space will be limite
 d to 16 archers per session or in accordance with CDC Guidelines. <br>Each 
 person will have a target no. assigned as above. <br><br>There will be two 
 lines of 8 archers when the number of participants exceeds 8 archers.<br>No
 t more than 8 archers will be on the shooting line at the same time.<br>A =
  Line A<br>B = Line B<br><br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will
  be allowed on the field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae. <
 br><br>Parents of juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a specta
 tor. <br>Parents of juniors 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoo
 t with their child for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (
 + parent) is accepted into each Indoor 1: First-time Class. <br><br>We will
  accept a limited number of juniors under 12 into the program each semester
 \, depending on the total  number of archers in all the classes. If you joi
 n before the limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in th
 e program and take other Indoor 1 classes as needed and later join Indoor 2
 . If you are under 12\, and have registered and paid after the cut off\, yo
 ur fee will be returned to you. <br><br>Juniors may need to take Indoor 1 t
 wo or three times before qualifying for Indoor 2 by scoring 50 pts over 30 
 arrows.<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Indoor 2.<br>
 <br>At the end of each Indoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we d
 id not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your fin
 al score\, because it will have been averaged by taking your recorded score
  from your scorecard\, dividing it by the number of arrows you shot to get 
 an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round scor
 e.
