DESCRIPTION:What we worked on today -<br><br>Head:  Keep head in position a
 s far to the left as possible to reach a reproducible stopping point<br><ul
 ><li>Head does not turn\, lift\, or tilt from Set\, especially not when dra
 wing or anchoring</li><li>String moves towards head\, not head to string</l
 i><li>Profile should be the same throughout the shot\; from front view\; if
  left eye becomes more visible\, head is turning</li><li>Keep left ear abov
 e left shoulder</li><li>Plumb line dropped from right front edge of chin sh
 ould not touch anything on your body</li><li>Tighten core so chest is down\
 , but head is turned and up\; </li><li>Ideally\, jaw parallel to ground\, s
 o head is up</li></ul><br>Draw elbow: At arrow height\, never lower than sh
 oulder\n\nJoin with Google Meet: https://meet.google.com/oso-fmfi-ygx\n\nLe
 arn more about Meet at: https://support.google.com/a/users/answer/9282720
