DESCRIPTION:Training classes at this location are reserved for competitive 
 and advanced archers..<br><br>REMINDER:  Everyone needs to come to at least
  one Training Class per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (All Indoo
 r 2-6 at 9m classes are training classes.)<br><br>Coach Racae will coach th
 e Outdoor 3-9 Training Class whenever there are at least 5 archers register
 ed by Fri 12:00 pm (for Sat) and Sat 12:00 pm (for Sun).   <br><br>TRAINING
  CLASS (TC): $57/archer/3-hr class<br>(1x/wk required to attend Open Practi
 ce)<br>FACILITY FEE (FF) (required each month): $75/month/archer due on 1st
  of the month. (USAA Level 3 Coaches do not pay facility fee.)<br>OPEN PRAC
 TICE (OP) Included in facility fee (1-2x/wk recommended)<br>PRIVATE LESSON 
 (PL): $125/hr/archer (1x/mo recommended)<br><br>Please add your name to the
  target list below to register<br>Focus primarily on perfecting your form\,
  <br>slowly increasing your physical strength and draw weight\, <br>strengt
 hening your mental program\, <br>determining your average and personal best
 \, <br>understanding the spread between the two\, and working on closing it
 .<br><br>EQUIPMENT:<br>You need your own equipment: <br>Competition recurve
  bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-
 bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sl
 ing\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may 
 not be added until you reach a higher level\, but you should order them in 
 advance.) <br><br>Wear your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br>WEATHER / DAYLIG
 HT<br><br>Session times may vary depending on temperature/daylight conditio
 ns.<br>During inclement weather (&lt\;52F or 100F&gt\;\, 20 mph winds\, hea
 vy rain\, lightning) class will move to the Indoor 9m range to practice for
 m and be noted on the calendar shortly before the scheduled session.<br>TAR
 GET ARRANGEMENTS<br>May vary each session\, depending on who attends and di
 stances needed.<br>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm
  target face you'll move back to the next distance until you reach your com
 petition distance (see below)<br>If you trained outdoors in the 2025 season
 \, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.<br><br>Target 1 at 70m 
 (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can 
 use it for independent practice in between classes.<br>Target 2 at 60m (U18
  + Masters competition distance) <br>Targets 3+4 at 50m<br>Target 5+6 at 40
 m (U15 competition distance) <br>Target 7+8 at 30m (U13 competition distanc
 e) <br>Targets 9 at 20m (for adults who have just graduated out of Indoor 2
 )<br>Target 10 at 13.5m (for juniors who have just graduated out of Indoor 
 2)<br><br>Ideally\, we want to practice with two archers/target to replicat
 e outdoor competition conditions.<br><br>TARGET ASSIGNMENTS<br>Targets are 
 assigned outdoors in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\, so 
 add your name next to your distance below. <br>If you need help or have que
 stions\, email/text Coach Racae<br>(Dotted lines represent tent poles divid
 ing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)<br><br>ATCIOCT = 2026 ATCI Outdoor Competition 
 Team  <br>MQS at your tournament distance\, 36-arrow rounds on 122-cm targe
 t face: <br>260 pts or 520 pts (2 rounds)<br>------------------------------
 ----<br>1A. (70m)<br>1B<br><br>2A. (60m)  <br>2B<br><br>3A. (50m)  <br>----
 ------------------------------<br>3B<br><br>4A. (50m) <br>4B.<b> Adrianne M
 .</b><br>----------------------------------<br>5A. (40m) <b>Ethan N </b>(8/
 12)<br>5B.  <b>Sara T.</b> (O6 @ 40m)<br><br>6A. (40m) <b>Finn E</b><br>---
 -------------------------------<br>6B. <br><br>7A. (30m) <b>Emma A.</b>\, 1
 4<br>7B. <br>---------------------------------- <br>8A. (30m) <br>8B.<br><b
 r>9A. (20m) <b>Rhys E</b><br>----------------------------------<br>9B. <br>
 <br>10A. (13.5m) <b>Akhil C.</b><br>10B
