 ed to 16 archers per session or in accordance with CDC Guidelines. <br>Each
  person will have a target no. assigned as above. <br><br>There will be two
  lines of 8 archers when the number of participants exceeds 8 archers.<br>N
 ot more than 8 archers will be on the shooting line at the same time.<br>A 
 = Line A<br>B = Line B<br><br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator wil
 l be allowed on the field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae. 
 <br><br>Parents of juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a spect
 ator. <br>Parents of juniors 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and sho
 ot with their child for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old 
 (+ parent) is accepted into each Indoor 1: First-time Class. <br><br>We wil
 l accept a limited number of juniors under 12 into the program each semeste
 r\, depending on the total  number of archers in all the classes. If you jo
 in before the limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in t
 he program and take other Indoor 1 classes as needed and later join Indoor 
 2. If you are under 12\, and have registered and paid after the cut off\, y
 our fee will be returned to you. <br><br>Juniors may need to take Indoor 1 
 two or three times before qualifying for Indoor 2 by scoring 50 pts over 30
  arrows.<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Indoor 2.<br
 ><br>At the end of each Indoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we 
 did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your fi
 nal score\, because it will have been averaged by taking your recorded scor
 e from your scorecard\, dividing it by the number of arrows you shot to get
  an arrow average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round sco
 re.
