DESCRIPTION:<b>Google Maps</b>: We're next to <b>Donut Taco Palace</b> in A
 ustin Business Park in East Oak Hill in Southwest Austin\, 78735 near the i
 ntersection of Mopac (Loop 1) and 290W.<br><br>COME JOIN US AND REGISTER NO
 W !<br><br>Open to adults\, juniors 8+\, and parents! Please read all the i
 nfo below and in the registration and waivers. <br><br>The composition of t
 he classes are by skill level\, not age.. There is usually about an even sp
 lit between adults and juniors in each class.<br><br>More information\, reg
 istration forms and waivers are available at <a href="http://www.archerytra
 iningcenter.com"><u><u><u><u><u>www.archerytrainingcenter.com</u></u></u></
 u></u></a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE of these forms:<br><a href="http
 s://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeciOgkyuKTLZ5_ZaWCEyQKYSX1fWGpP5qakhT
 6OuAc6jJ_FQ/viewform"><u><u>2023 Indoor 1: First-time Class for Adults</u><
 /u></a>  OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSc_bYEFoE4
 oXkcm0T6fZK99fu_q6lL8wZGClXyfa1GZbahh-g/viewform"><u><u>2023 Indoor 1: Firs
 t-time Class for Juniors and Parents</u></u></a><br><br>Sign up for just ON
 E Indoor 1 class\, because most people graduate out of this class into Indo
 or 2 after the first lesson.<br><br>Your name will be added below and your 
 place reserved on a first registered and paid basis and after we receive 3 
 things:  <br><b>2023 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM   +  MEMBERSHIP AND WAIVER
 S PACKET +   FEE</b><b><br></b><u></u><br><b>USA Archery Level 4 NTS Coach 
 Racae Meyer and other instructors/coaches.</b><br><b>See </b><a href="https
 ://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/who-we-are"><u><u><u>https://www.archerytr
 ainingcenter.com/who-we-are</u></u></u></a><b><br></b><br><b>Registered arc
 hers </b>at 9m on 40-cm target face unless otherwise noted:<u></u><br><u></
 u><br><b>Target Assignments:</b><br><u></u><b><br></b>1. <b>Michel G.\, </b
 >adult\, pd -&gt\; <b>Indoor 2</b><br><br>2<br><br>3<br><br>4.<br><br>5<br>
 <br>6.<br><br>7<br><br>8<br><br>Space will be limited to 16 archers per ses
 sion or in accordance with CDC Guidelines. <br>Each person will have a targ
 et no. assigned as above. <br><br>There will be two lines of 8 archers when
  the number of participants exceeds 8 archers.<br>Not more than 8 archers w
 ill be on the shooting line at the same time.<br>A = Line A<br>B = Line B<b
 r><br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the fiel
 d until further notice or approved by Coach Racae. <br><br>Parents of junio
 rs 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator. <br>Parents of jun
 iors 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their child for 
 greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted i
 nto each Indoor 1: First-time Class. <br><br>We will accept a limited numbe
 r of juniors under 12 into the program each semester\, depending on the tot
 al  number of archers in all the classes. If you join before the limit is r
 eached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take othe
 r Indoor 1 classes as needed and later join Indoor 2. If you are under 12\,
  and have registered and paid after the cut off\, your fee will be returned
  to you. <br><br>Juniors may need to take Indoor 1 two or three times befor
 e qualifying for Indoor 2 by scoring 50 pts over 30 arrows.<br>Adults don´t
  need a minimum score to graduate into Indoor 2.<br><br>At the end of each 
 Indoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a complet
 e round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, because it w
 ill have been averaged by taking your recorded score from your scorecard\, 
 dividing it by the number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and 
 then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round score.
