DESCRIPTION:Training classes at this location are reserved for competitive 
 and advanced archers..<br><br><b>REMINDER</b>:  Everyone needs to come to a
 t least one Training Class per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (Al
 l Indoor 2-6 at 9m classes are training classes.)<br><br>Coach Racae will c
 oach the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class whenever there are at least 5 archers r
 egistered by Fri 9:00 am (for Sat) and Sat 9:00 am (for Sun).   <br><br><b>
 TRAINING CLASS (TC)</b>: <b>$57/archer/3-hr class</b><br>(1x/wk required to
  attend Open Practice)<br><b>FACILITY FEE (FF) </b>(required each month): <
 b>$75/month/archer</b> due on 1st of the month. (USAA Level 3 Coaches do no
 t pay facility fee.)<br><b>OPEN PRACTICE (OP) </b>Included in facility fee 
 (1-2x/wk recommended)<br><b>PRIVATE LESSON (PL)</b>: $125/hr/archer (1x/mo 
 recommended)<br><br><b>Please add your name to the target list below to reg
 ister</b><br>Focus primarily on perfecting your form\, <br>slowly increasin
 g your physical strength and draw weight\, <br>strengthening your mental pr
 ogram\, <br>determining your average and personal best\, <br>understanding 
 the spread between the two\, and working on closing it.<br><br><b>EQUIPMENT
 :</b><br>You need your own equipment: <br>Competition recurve bow\, sight\,
  stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\,
  clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or f
 ield quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added u
 ntil you reach a higher level\, but you should order them in advance.) <br>
 <br>Wear your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br><b>WEATHER / DAYLIGHT</b><br>S
 ession times may vary depending on temperature/daylight conditions.<br>Duri
 ng inclement weather (&lt\;52F or 100F&gt\;\, 20 mph winds\, heavy rain\, l
 ightning) class will move to the Indoor 9m range to practice form and be no
 ted on the calendar shortly before the scheduled session.<br><br><b>TARGET 
 ARRANGEMENTS</b><br><b>The target arrangements have changed as of 8/22\, </
 b>because it's the beginning of the indoor season\, so everyone needs to sh
 oot 18m to attend the indoor competitions at Texas A&amp\;M in Nov and Feb.
  Ideally\, you want to alternate between 18m and your outdoor distance each
  time you come\, so you continue to improve at the longer distance over the
  fall and winter. <br><br><b>If there is not space at the distance you want
  to shoot</b>\, shoot at 18m. <br>Alternatively\, Targets 6 and 7 can be mo
 ved to 30m or 18m and Target 10 to 18m when necessary. <br><br><b>YOUR SCOR
 ING GOALS:</b><br><ol><li><span>Meet the<b> MQS  to move back 10m </b>until
  you reach your competition distance (see below) </span></li><li><span>Meet
  the <b>MQS </b>to get on the</span><b> ATCI Indoor and Outdoor Competition
  Teams </b><span>each year</span><br></li></ol><b>MQS (Minimum Qualifying S
 cores):</b><br><b><br></b><br><b>To move back 10 m </b><span>until you reac
 h your competition distance (see below)</span><b>: </b><br><b>2026: 288 pts
  </b><span> in a 36-arrow </span><span>round on the 122-cm target face </sp
 an><br><b>2027 297 pts </b><span> in a 36-arrow </span><span>round on the 1
 22-cm target face </span><br><span><br></span><br><b>ATCI Indoor Competitio
 n Team (ATCIICT): </b><br><b>2026:  210 pts </b>or <b>410 pts</b> (2 rounds
 ) <b>at 18m</b> <b> </b>on 60cm target face (U13/U15) or 40cm target face (
 U18\, U21\, Seniors 21-49\, Masters 50+) in 30-arrow indoor round (arrow av
 g: 7.0 pts)<br><b>2027:  225 pts or 450 pts </b><span>(2 rounds) </span><sp
 an><b>at</b> <b>18m </b></span><span>on 60cm target face (U13/U15) or 40cm 
 target face (U18\, U21\, Seniors 21-49\, Masters 50+) in 30-arrow indoor ro
 und (arrow avg: 7.5 pts)</span><br><span><br></span><br><b>ATCI Outdoor Com
 petition Team  (</b><b>ATCIOCT)</b><br><b>2026 </b><b>: </b><b>260 pts</b><
 span> or </span><b>520 pts</b><span> (2 rounds) </span><span>At your tourna
 ment distance\, 36-arrow round on 122-cm target face (arrow avg: 7.22 pts)<
 /span><br><b>2027 :</b><b> </b><b>270 pts</b> or <b>540 pts</b> (2 rounds)<
 br>At your tournament distance\, 36-arrow round on 122-cm target face (arro
 w avg: 7.5 pts)<br><br><span>Target distances vary with each session\, depe
 nding on who attends and distances needed.</span><br>When you score <b>288 
