DESCRIPTION:<i>This class has been cancelled due to the coach being unavail
 able. Register for Saturday instead.</i><br><br>Training classes at this lo
 cation are reserved for competitive and advanced archers..<br><br><b>REMIND
 ER</b>:  Everyone needs to come to at least one Training Class per week to 
 be able to attend Open Practice. (All Indoor 2-6 at 9m classes are training
  classes.)<br><br>Coach Racae will coach the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class whe
 never there are at least 5 archers registered by Fri 9:00 am (for Sat) and 
 Sat 9:00 am (for Sun).   <br><br><b>TRAINING CLASS (TC)</b>: <b>$57/archer/
 3-hr class</b><br>(1x/wk required to attend Open Practice)<br><b>FACILITY F
 EE (FF) </b>(required each month): <b>$75/month/archer</b> due on 1st of th
 e month. (USAA Level 3 Coaches do not pay facility fee.)<br><b>OPEN PRACTIC
 E (OP) </b>Included in facility fee (1-2x/wk recommended)<br><b>PRIVATE LES
 SON (PL)</b>: $125/hr/archer (1x/mo recommended)<br><br><b>Please add your 
 name to the target list below to register</b><br>Focus primarily on perfect
 ing your form\, <br>slowly increasing your physical strength and draw weigh
 t\, <br>strengthening your mental program\, <br>determining your average an
 d personal best\, <br>understanding the spread between the two\, and workin
 g on closing it.<br><br><b>EQUIPMENT:</b><br>You need your own equipment: <
 br>Competition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbo
 n arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\,
  fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clic
 ker and side rods may not be added until you reach a higher level\, but you
  should order them in advance.) <br><br>Wear your ATCI shirt to training.<b
 r><br><b>WEATHER / DAYLIGHT</b><br>Session times may vary depending on temp
 erature/daylight conditions.<br>During inclement weather (&lt\;52F or 100F&
 gt\;\, 20 mph winds\, heavy rain\, lightning) class will move to the Indoor
  9m range to practice form and be noted on the calendar shortly before the 
 scheduled session.<br><br><b>TARGET ARRANGEMENTS</b><br><b>The target arran
 gements have changed as of 8/22\, </b>because it's the beginning of the ind
 oor season\, so everyone needs to shoot 18m to attend the indoor competitio
 ns at Texas A&amp\;M in Nov and Feb. Ideally\, you want to alternate betwee
 n 18m and your outdoor distance each time you come\, so you continue to imp
 rove at the longer distance over the fall and winter. <br><br><b>If there i
 s not space at the distance you want to shoot</b>\, shoot at 18m. <br>Alter
 natively\, Targets 6 and 7 can be moved to 30m or 18m and Target 10 to 18m 
 when necessary. <br><br><b>YOUR SCORING GOALS:</b><ol><li>Meet the<b> MQS  
 to move back 10m </b>until you reach your competition distance (see below) 
 </li><li>Meet the <b>MQS </b>to get on the<b> ATCI Indoor and Outdoor Compe
 tition Teams </b>each year<br></li></ol><b>MQS (Minimum Qualifying Scores):
 </b><br><br><b>To move back 10 m </b>until you reach your competition dista
 nce (see below)<b>: </b><br><b>2026: 288 pts </b> in a 36-arrow round on th
 e 122-cm target face <br><b>2027: 297 pts </b> in a 36-arrow round on the 1
 22-cm target face <br><br><b>ATCI Indoor Competition Team (ATCIICT): </b><b
 r><b>2026:  210 pts </b>or <b>410 pts</b> (2 rounds) <b>at 18m</b> <b> </b>
 on 60cm target face (U13/U15) or 40cm target face (U18\, U21\, Seniors 21-4
 9\, Masters 50+) in 30-arrow indoor round (arrow avg: 7.0 pts)<br><b>2027: 
  225 pts or 450 pts </b>(2 rounds) <b>at</b> <b>18m </b>on 60cm target face
  (U13/U15) or 40cm target face (U18\, U21\, Seniors 21-49\, Masters 50+) in
  30-arrow indoor round (arrow avg: 7.5 pts)<br><br><b>ATCI Outdoor Competit
 ion Team  (</b><b>ATCIOCT)</b><br><b>2026 </b><b>: </b><b>260 pts</b> or <b
 >520 pts</b> (2 rounds) At your tournament distance\, 36-arrow round on 122
 -cm target face (arrow avg: 7.22 pts)<br><b>2027 :</b><b> </b><b>270 pts</b
 > or <b>540 pts</b> (2 rounds)<br>At your tournament distance\, 36-arrow ro
 und on 122-cm target face (arrow avg: 7.5 pts)<br><br>Target distances vary
  with each session\, depending on who attends and distances needed.<br>When
  you score <b>288 pts </b><b>you'll move back to the next distance until yo
 u reach your competition distance.</b><br>If you trained outdoors in the 20
 26 season\, during the 2027 outdoor season\, you'll return to the farthest 
 distance you shot in 2026.<br><br><b>70m </b>(U21 + Seniors competition dis
 tance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent practic
 e in between classes.<br><b>60m</b> (U18 + Masters competition distance) <b
 r><b>50m</b><br><b>40m</b> (U15 competition distance) <br><b>30m</b> (U13 c
 ompetition distance)<br><b>20m</b> (for adults who have just graduated out 
 of Indoor 2)<br><b>13.5m</b> (for juniors who have just graduated out of In
 door 2)<br><br>Ideally\, we want to practice with at least two archers/targ
 et to replicate competition conditions  .<br><br><b>TARGET ASSIGNMENTS</b><
 br>Targets are assigned outdoors in advance to reduce confusion and delay o
 n the day\, so <b>add your name next to your distance below</b>. <br>If you
  need help or have questions\, email/text Coach Racae<br>(Dotted lines repr
 esent tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)<br><br>------------------
 ----------------<br>1A. (70m)<br>1B<br><br>2A. (60m)  <br>2B<br><br>3A. (50
 m)  <br>----------------------------------<br>3B<br><br>4A. (40m) <br>4B. <
 br>----------------------------------<br>5A. (30m)<br>5B. <br><br>6A. (30m)
  <br>----------------------------------<br>6B. <br><br>7A. (18m) <br>7B. <b
 r>---------------------------------- <br>8A. (18m) <br>8B.<br><br>9A. (18m)
  <br>----------------------------------<br>9B. <br><br>10A. (13.5m)<br>10B
