 pts              280 pts           -&gt\; Indoor 5 and Outdoor 5 at 30m<br>
    290 pts              300 pts          -&gt\; Indoor  6 and Outdoor 6 at 
 40m<br><br>You can shoot indoors indefinitely and use the range's equipment
 .  When you'd like your own bow\, ask Coach Racae for recommendations.<br><
 br>When you are ready to shoot outdoors in Outdoor 3-9:<br>    * You'll def
 initely need your own bow\, based on Coach Racae's recommendations<br>    *
  You'll be granted access to the ATCI Calendar via an email from Coach Raca
 e\,so you can just add your name directly below under "Registered Archers".
  <br>    * You will also be invited to join the WhatsApp ATCI Community. <b
 r><br>INDOOR CLASS SCHEDULE : (Fees are below) <br>Register for ​​as many a
 s your schedule and budget allows to progress faster:<br>Sat         4:00-5
 :30 pm - INDOOR 2-6<br>Sun        4:00-5:30 pm - INDOOR 2-6<br>Tues       6
 :30-8:00 pm - INDOOR 2-6<br>Wed       5:00-6:30 pm - INDOOR 2-6 Juniors &lt
 \;15 and Parents<br>               6:30-8:00 pm - INDOOR 2-6<br>Thurs     6
 :30-8:00 pm - INDOOR 3+ with own competition recurve bow<br><br>Always chec
 k this calendar just before driving to class in case there are last-minutes
  changes or cancellations!<br><br>USA Archery Level 4 NTS Coach Racae Meyer
  will coach unless otherwise noted above.<br><br>The level of each attendin
 g archer is noted next to their name below\, to help you decide which class
 es to join. (Example: Indoor 2 are beginners\; Outdoor 5+ (O5 @30m\, etc.) 
 are competitive outdoor archers)<br><br>There are 8 places on the shooting 
 line\, but we can accommodate 14. After 8 register\, we'll create another s
 hooting line\, as is done in competitions.<br><br>Sign in/out upon arrival/
 departure <br>Coaching and whistle commands at all times.<br>Instruction in
  the National Training System.<br>Unfair games depending on attendance.<br>
