CREATED:20260924T151701Z
DESCRIPTION:<b>What we worked on:</b><br><b>SET: Posture - Better vertical 
 alignment</b><br><b>SET UP: Raising the bow without raising your shoulders 
 </b><br><ol><li>Knees - Legs - <ul><li><span>Should be straight. Knees not 
 overly locked.</span></li><li><span>Quads tight</span></li></ul></li><li>Hi
 ps / Pelvis<ul><li>Directly below rib cage</li><li>Rotate pelvis down and f
 orward\, instead of up and back</li><li>Do exercises to align back and pelv
 is<ul><li>Small of your back against wall will move pelvis down and forward
 </li><li>On back on floor with feet up against wall\; knees 90 deg\; hips 9
 0 deg.\; push heels into wall</li></ul></li><li>Bottom should not stick out
 \, but rather be tucked in</li><li>Center of gravity should be in core/hips
 /pelvis so you feel grounded\, not top heavy</li><li>Glutes tight - "Coin"<
 /li></ul></li><li>Core tight</li><li>Chest down\, not up<ul><li>Practice ho
 rizontally opening your rib cage in your chest to help keep shoulders down\
 , but scapulae are not squeezed together</li><li>With hand on upper chest\,
  tilt chest until hand is vertical instead of angled up and out</li></ul></
 li><li>Shoulders<ul><li>Reduce tension in upper back</li><li>Shoulders shou
 ld be down and in towards ribs\, not up and rounded forward</li><li>Mentall
 y separate arms away from torso and shoulders<ul><li>Practice making a "T" 
 to remind yourself that shoulders do not have to be raised when arms are ra
 ised. </li><li>Raise the bow with your hands\, not your shoulders!</li></ul
 ></li></ul></li></ol><br>Get tripod with phone attachment and video yoursel
 f at home. (Videos from today's session will be in your Form Album previous
 ly shared with you.)<br><br>Practice with bow in front of mirrors at home\,
  watching vertical alignment and that chest and shoulders do not raise as b
 ow is raised.<br><br>Look at photos in <u>Inside the Archer</u> for underst
 anding of posture and vertical alignment.<br><br>Work at it !
LAST-MODIFIED:20260926T091202Z
