DESCRIPTION:Training classes at this location are reserved for competitive 
 and advanced archers.<br><br>REMINDER:  Everyone needs to come to at least 
 one Training Class per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (All Indoor
  2-6 at 9m classes are training classes.) <br><br>TRAINING CLASS (TC): $57/
 archer/3-hr class<br>(1x/wk required to attend Open Practice)<br>FACILITY F
 EE (FF) (required each month): $75/month/archer due on 1st of the month to 
 attend Open Practice. (USAA Level 3 Coaches do not pay facility fee.)<br>OP
 EN PRACTICE (OP) Included in facility fee (1-2x/wk recommended)<br>PRIVATE 
 LESSON (PL): $125/hr/archer (1x/mo recommended)<br><br>Please add your name
  to the target list below to register<br>Focus primarily on perfecting your
  form\, <br>slowly increasing your physical strength and draw weight\, <br>
 strengthening your mental program\, <br>determining your average and person
 al best\, <br>understanding the spread between the two\, and working on clo
 sing it.<br><br>EQUIPMENT:<br>You need your own equipment: <br>Competition 
 recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side
  rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, fi
 nger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side ro
 ds may not be added until you reach a higher level\, but you should order t
 hem in advance.) <br><br>Wear your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br>WEATHER /
  DAYLIGHT<br>Session times may vary depending on temperature/daylight condi
 tions.<br>During inclement weather (&lt\;52F or 100F heat index&gt\;\, 20 m
 ph winds\, heavy rain\, lightning) class will move to the Indoor 9m range t
 o practice form and be noted on the calendar shortly before the scheduled s
 ession.<br><br>TARGET ARRANGEMENTS<br>May vary each session\, depending on 
 who attends and distances needed.<br>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow r
 ound on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the next distance until 
 you reach your competition distance (see below)<br>If you trained outdoors 
 in the 2025 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.<br><b
 r>Target 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should always stay a
 t 70m so Jake can use it for independent practice in between classes.<br>Ta
 rget 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition distance) <br>Targets 3+4 at 50m<b
 r>Target 5+6 at 40m (U15 competition distance) <br>Target 7+8 at 30m (U13 c
 ompetition distance) <br>Targets 9 at 20m (for adults who have just graduat
 ed out of Indoor 2)<br>Target 10 at 13.5m (for juniors who have just gradua
 ted out of Indoor 2)<br><br>Ideally\, we want to practice with two archers/
 target to replicate outdoor competition conditions.<br><br>TARGET ASSIGNMEN
 TS<br>Targets are assigned outdoors in advance to reduce confusion and dela
 y on the day\, so add your name next to your distance below. <br>If you nee
 d help or have questions\, email/text Coach Racae<br>(Dotted lines represen
 t tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)<br><br>ATCIOCT = 2026 ATCI Ou
 tdoor Competition Team  <br>MQS at your tournament distance\, 36-arrow roun
 ds on 122-cm target face: <br>260 pts or 520 pts (2 rounds)<br>------------
 ----------------------<br>1A. (70m)<br>1B<br><br>2A. (60m)  <br>2B<br><br>3
 A. (50m)  Ethan N (12/12)<br>----------------------------------<br>3B Adria
 nne M. <br><br>4A. (50m) <br>4B. <br>----------------------------------<br>
 5A. (40m)<br>5B. <br><br>6A. (40m) <br>----------------------------------<b
 r>6B. <br><br>7A. (30m) <br>7B. <br>---------------------------------- <br>
 8A. (30m) <br>8B.<br><br>9A. (20m) <br>----------------------------------<b
 r>9B. <br><br>10A. (13.5m)<br>10B
