DESCRIPTION:As confirmation that you are registered for the class\, look fo
 r your name under "Registered Archers" below. (Scroll way down!)\n\nSign up
  for Indoor 2 at 2026 INDOOR 2-6 at 9m Registration Form (https://docs.goog
 le.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfz1Ww1xFc_x-hCgXixX36YxyfAHlfAUMi-Hir24Fy7hLOzbw/v
 iewform?usp=sharing&ouid=104080193312046349991) \n\nPrerequisites for Indoo
 r 2:\nCompletion of Indoor 1. \nAdults do not need a minimum score in Indoo
 r 1 to advance to Indoor 2.\nJuniors <18 need a minimum score of 50 pts in 
 Indoor 1  to advance to Indoor 2.\n\nScores needed at 9m to advance beyond 
 Indoor 2:\nOn 40-cm         On 60-cm\ntarget face        target face\n   23
 0 pts              240 pts           -> Indoor 3 and Outdoor 3 at 13.5m wit
 h own bow\n   250 pts              260 pts           -> Indoor 4 and Outdoo
 r 4 at 18m/20m\n   270 pts              280 pts           -> Indoor 5 and O
 utdoor 5 at 30m\n   290 pts              300 pts          -> Indoor  6 and 
 Outdoor 6 at 40m\n\nYou can shoot indoors indefinitely and use the range's 
 equipment.  \nWhen you'd like your own bow\, ask Coach Racae for recommenda
 tions.\n\nWhen you are ready to shoot outdoors in Outdoor 3-9:\n    * You'l
 l definitely need your own bow\, based on Coach Racae's recommendations\n  
   * You'll be granted access to the ATCI Calendar via an email from Coach R
 acae\,so you can just add your name directly below under "Registered Archer
 s". \n    * You will also be invited to join the WhatsApp ATCI Community. \
 n\n\nINDOOR CLASS SCHEDULE : (Fees are below) \nRegister for ​​as many as y
 our schedule and budget allows to progress faster:\nSat         4:00-5:30 p
 m - INDOOR 2-6\nSun        4:00-5:30 pm - INDOOR 2-6\nTues       6:30-8:00 
 pm - INDOOR 2-6\nWed       5:00-6:30 pm - INDOOR 2-6 Juniors <15 and Parent
 s\n               6:30-8:00 pm - INDOOR 2-6\nThurs     6:30-8:00 pm - INDOO
 R 3+ with own competition recurve bow\n\nAlways check this calendar just be
 fore driving to class in case there are last-minutes changes or cancellatio
 ns!\n\nUSA Archery Level 4 NTS Coach Racae Meyer will coach unless otherwis
 e noted above.\n\nThe level of each attending archer is noted next to their
  name below\, to help you decide which classes to join. (Example: Indoor 2 
 are beginners\; Outdoor 5+ (O5 @30m\, etc.) are competitive outdoor archers
 )\n\nThere is a minimum attendance of 3 registered archers for the class to
  be held.\n\nRegistered archers:\n1. Madison W-S.\, adult\, pd (Indoor 2)\n
 2. Sage V.\, 17\, pd (Indoor 2)\n3. Sid S.\, 11\, on 60-cm target face\, pd
  (Indoor 2)\n4. Paul K.\, adult\, pd (Indoor 2)\n5..Girish P.\, adult\, pd 
 (Indoor 2)\n6. \n7.\n8.\n9.\n10.\n11.\n12.\n\nSINGLE Class Fees per archer 
 for one Indoor 2-6 class\nBook and pay in advance. (All Indoor 2-6 Classes 
 are 1.5 hrs long.)\n$30 for 1 hr (arrive 30 min after class starts or leave
  30 min before class ends)\n$45 for 1.5-hr class\n\nDiscount Fee Packs:\nSt
 arting August 18\, there are no substitutions or credits for days missed\, 
 if you have given us dates and paid for a monthly or multi-class discount p
 ack.\n\nMONTHLY Discount Fee Packs\nPay before the 1st of each month\; book
  dates within the month\n1 class/wk:      $218 (7.5 hrs\; 5 classes/mo)\n2 
 classes/wk: $372 (13.5 hrs\; 9 classes/mo)\n3 classes/wk: $557 (21 hrs\; 14
  classes/mo)\n4 classes/wk: $675 (27 hrs\; 18 classes/mo)\n5 classes/wk: $7
 92 (33 hrs\; 22 classes/mo)\n\nMULTI-CLASS Discount Packets\nPay in advance
  and book dates when you're sure of the dates.\n  9 hours : $257 (6 classes
 )\n 12 hours : $330 (8 classes)\n 18 hours : $477 (12 classes) \n 23 hours:
  $587 (15 classes)\n 27 hours: $675 (18 classes)\n\nThere are 8 places on t
 he shooting line\, but we often have double lines as in competitions\, depe
 nding on attendance.\n\nSign in/out upon arrival/departure\nCoaching and wh
 istle commands at all times.\nInstruction in the National Training System.\
 nUnfair games depending on attendance.\n\nPlease note: Youths <12 y.o. shou
 ld not shoot more than 100 arrows/day!
