DESCRIPTION:Registration form: OUTDOOR 3-9 at 13.5m-70m<br><br>Add your nam
 e to Target Assignment List below or send in the above completed form.<br><
 br>Focus primarily on <br>perfecting your form\, <br>slowly increasing your
  physical strength and draw weight\, <br>strengthening your mental program\
 , <br>determining your average and personal best\, <br>understanding the sp
 read between the two\, and working on closing it.<br><br>You need your own 
 equipment <br>Competition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest
 \, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\,
  armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\,
  etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added until you reach a higher leve
 l\, but you should order them in advance.) <br><br>Wear your ATCI shirt to 
 training.<br><br>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm t
 arget face you'll move back to the next distance until you reach your compe
 tition distance.<br>If you trained outdoors in the 2024 season\, you'll ret
 urn to the farthest distance you shot.<br><br>Target arrangements may vary 
 each session\, depending on who attends and distances needed.<br>Target 1 a
 t 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should always stay at 70m so Jak
 e can use it for independent practice in between classes.<br>Target 2 at 60
 m (U18 + Masters competition distance) <br>Target 3 at 50m<br>Targets 4+5 a
 t 40m (U15 competition distance) <br>Targets 6\, 7\, 8 at 30m (U13 competit
 ion distance) <br>Target 9 at 20m (for those who have shot at 18m indoors o
 r with Coach Racae's approval)<br>Targets 10 at 13.5m (for those who have j
 ust graduated from indoors at 9m)<br><br>Ideally\, we want to practice with
  two archers/target to replicate competition conditions as much as possible
 .<br><br>Target Assignments:<br>Targets are assigned outdoors in advance to
  reduce confusion and delay on the day\,<br>so add your name next to your d
 istance below. <br>If you need help or have questions\, email/text Coach Ra
 cae<br>(Dotted lines represent tent poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)<
 br><br>1.  <b>Luke T</b>\, 16\, USAA\, pd - 1.5 hrs - <i>Worked on: Shot cy
 cle sequence\, esp. Set-Up\, Draw to Load\, up into Anchor. Angular draw ra
 ther than straight drawing. Increase strength and improve sequence before a
 dding any weight. CR </i><br>2. <b>Colby K</b>.\, USAA\, totally paid up\, 
 dude. 1.5 hrs - <i>Worked on: Relaxing\, calm shots\, center of gravity in 
 hips\, not chest. Steadier bow arm. Increase strength and alignment before 
 increasing weight. Trying to get to 40m by end of April and upping to 30#. 
 CR</i><br>3. <b>Anna P\,</b> USAA\, pd - 1.5 hrs - <i>Most positions greatl
 y improved due to working at it all at home with stretchband. Great! CR </i
 ><br>4. <b>Hannah T.\, </b>USAA\, pd - 1.0 hr - <i>Cut carbon arrows\, but 
 unfortunately nocked most of them on the far end of shaft away from the wri
 ting\, so will need to test out the difference in arrow flight between thos
 e and the two that were nocked and cut properly. (Makes no difference which
  end is cut for Avance arrows\, according to Easton tech chat.). </i>
