DESCRIPTION:Training classes at this location are reserved for competitive 
 and advanced archers..<br><br><b>REMINDER</b>:  Everyone needs to come to a
 t least one Training Class per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (Al
 l Indoor 2-6 at 9m classes are training classes.)<br><br>Coach Racae will c
 oach the Outdoor 3-9 Training Class whenever there are at least 5 archers r
 egistered by Fri 9:00 am (for Sat) and Sat 9:00 am (for Sun).   <br><br><b>
 TRAINING CLASS (TC)</b>: <b>$57/archer/3-hr class</b><br>(1x/wk required to
  attend Open Practice)<br><b>FACILITY FEE (FF) </b>(required each month): <
 b>$75/month/archer</b> due on 1st of the month. (USAA Level 3 Coaches do no
 t pay facility fee.)<br><b>OPEN PRACTICE (OP) </b>Included in facility fee 
 (1-2x/wk recommended)<br><b>PRIVATE LESSON (PL)</b>: $125/hr/archer (1x/mo 
 recommended)<br><br><b>Please add your name to the target list below to reg
 ister</b><br>Focus primarily on perfecting your form\, <br>slowly increasin
 g your physical strength and draw weight\, <br>strengthening your mental pr
 ogram\, <br>determining your average and personal best\, <br>understanding 
 the spread between the two\, and working on closing it.<br><br><b>EQUIPMENT
 :</b><br>You need your own equipment: <br>Competition recurve bow\, sight\,
  stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\,
  clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or f
 ield quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added u
 ntil you reach a higher level\, but you should order them in advance.) <br>
 <br>Wear your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br><b>WEATHER / DAYLIGHT</b><br>S
 ession times may vary depending on temperature/daylight conditions.<br>Duri
 ng inclement weather (&lt\;52F or 100F&gt\;\, 20 mph winds\, heavy rain\, l
 ightning) class will move to the Indoor 9m range to practice form and be no
 ted on the calendar shortly before the scheduled session.<br><br><b>TARGET 
 ARRANGEMENTS</b><br>May vary each session\, depending on who attends and di
 stances needed.<br>When you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm
  target face you'll move back to the next distance until you reach your com
 petition distance (see below)<br>If you trained outdoors in the 2025 season
 \, you'll return to the farthest distance you shot.<br><br>Target 1 at 70m 
 (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can 
 use it for independent practice in between classes.<br>Target 2 at 60m (U18
  + Masters competition distance) <br>Targets 3+4 at 50m<br>Target 5+6 at 40
 m (U15 competition distance) <br>Target 7+8 at 30m (U13 competition distanc
 e) <br>Targets 9 at 20m (for adults who have just graduated out of Indoor 2
 )<br>Target 10 at 13.5m (for juniors who have just graduated out of Indoor 
 2)<br><br>Ideally\, we want to practice with two archers/target to replicat
 e outdoor competition conditions.<br><br><b>TARGET ASSIGNMENTS</b><br>Targe
 ts are assigned outdoors in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the da
 y\, so <b>add your name next to your distance below</b>. <br>If you need he
 lp or have questions\, email/text Coach Racae<br>(Dotted lines represent te
 nt poles dividing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)<br><br><b>ATCIOCT</b> = <b>2026 A
 TCI Outdoor Competition Team  </b><br><b>MQS </b>at your tournament distanc
 e\, 36-arrow rounds on 122-cm target face: <br><b>260 pts</b> or <b>520 pts
 </b> (2 rounds)<br>----------------------------------<br>1A. (70m)<br>1B<br
 ><br>2A. (60m)  <br>2B<br><br>3A. (50m)  <br>------------------------------
 ----<br>3B<br><br>4A. (50m) <br>4B. <br>----------------------------------<
 br>5A. (40m) Abby Y<br>5B. <br><br>6A. (40m) <br>--------------------------
 --------<br>6B. <br><br>7A. (30m) Ellie Y<br>7B. <br>----------------------
 ------------ <br>8A. (30m) <br>8B.<br><br>9A. (20m) <br>-------------------
 ---------------<br>9B. <br><br>10A. (13.5m)<br>10B
