DESCRIPTION:<b>What we worked on:</b><br><span><br></span><br><span>Bow til
 t</span><br><ul><li><span>Bow started out tilting up through DRAW to LOAD\,
  and then straightening out at ANCHOR. </span></li><li>Level it up so bow a
 rm is pushing the bow straight into the target and bow arm is level with sh
 oulders.</li><li>Pressure on meaty part of the thumb should not change much
  in the vertical plane\, but bow will still pivot a bit left to right durin
 g DRAW to LOAD.</li><li>Understand it is physically easier to tilt the bow 
 up and then level it out\, but not a good strategy.<ul><li>We need to raise
  the arms in sync to about eye or nose height\, with the draw forearm as ho
 rizontal as possible\, so string is not being drawn down and bow is not til
 ted up. (Elbow never lower than draw shoulder.) </li><li>Both arms come dow
 n together and bow arm remains slightly higher during DRAW to LOAD before A
 IM so sight is never so low the bow needs to be raised into AIM.</li></ul><
 /li></ul><br>Improvement on "leveling it out" and alignments as session wen
 t on\, which means<br><ul><li>Warm up before session</li><li>Focus on one t
 hing for 20-30 arrows or until you get it right\, then move on</li><li>Freq
 uent practice\, so progress is faster\, no two steps forward\, one step bac
 k.</li></ul><br>You're doing great. Lots of subtlety now. Yay!<br>Video you
 rself more.<br>Get that overhead camera in the garage!\n\nJoin with Google 
 Meet: https://meet.google.com/jru-dyrh-eaj\n\nLearn more about Meet at: htt
 ps://support.google.com/a/users/answer/9282720
