DESCRIPTION:Training classes at this location are reserved for competitive 
 and advanced archers..\n\nREMINDER:  Everyone needs to come to at least one
  Training Class per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (All Indoor 2-
 6 at 9m classes are training classes.) \n\nTRAINING CLASS (TC): $57/archer/
 3-hr class\n(1x/wk required to attend Open Practice)\nFACILITY FEE (FF) (re
 quired each month): $75/month/archer due on 1st of the month to attend Open
  Practices. (USAA Level 3 Coaches do not pay facility fee.)\nOPEN PRACTICE 
 (OP) Included in facility fee (1-2x/wk recommended)\nPRIVATE LESSON (PL): $
 125/hr/archer (1x/mo recommended)\n\nPlease add your name to the target lis
 t below to register\nFocus primarily on perfecting your form\, \nslowly inc
 reasing your physical strength and draw weight\, \nstrengthening your menta
 l program\, \ndetermining your average and personal best\, \nunderstanding 
 the spread between the two\, and working on closing it.\n\nEQUIPMENT:\nYou 
 need your own equipment: \nCompetition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, p
 lunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, ches
 t protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, a
 rrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added until you reach 
 a higher level\, but you should order them in advance.) \n\nWear your ATCI 
 shirt to training.\n\nWEATHER / DAYLIGHT\nSession times may vary depending 
 on temperature/daylight conditions.\nDuring inclement weather (<52F or 100F
 > heat index\, 20 mph winds\, heavy rain\, lightning) class will move to th
 e Indoor 9m range to practice form and be noted on the calendar shortly bef
 ore the scheduled session.\n\nTARGET ARRANGEMENTS\nMay vary each session\, 
 depending on who attends and distances needed.\nWhen you score 288 pts in a
  36-arrow round on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the next dist
 ance until you reach your competition distance (see below)\nIf you trained 
 outdoors in the 2025 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you sh
 ot.\n\nTarget 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should always s
 tay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent practice in between classes.\
 nTarget 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition distance) \nTargets 3+4 at 50m\
 nTarget 5+6 at 40m (U15 competition distance) \nTarget 7+8 at 30m (U13 comp
 etition distance) \nTargets 9 at 20m (for adults who have just graduated ou
 t of Indoor 2)\nTarget 10 at 13.5m (for juniors who have just graduated out
  of Indoor 2)\n\nIdeally\, we want to practice with two archers/target to r
 eplicate outdoor competition conditions.\n\nTARGET ASSIGNMENTS\nTargets are
  assigned outdoors in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\, so
  add your name next to your distance below. \nIf you need help or have ques
 tions\, email/text Coach Racae\n(Dotted lines represent tent poles dividing
  Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)\n\nATCIOCT = 2026 ATCI Outdoor Competition Team  \
 nMQS at your tournament distance\, 36-arrow rounds on 122-cm target face: \
 n260 pts or 520 pts (2 rounds)\n----------------------------------\n1A. (70
 m)\n1B\n\n2A. (60m)  \n2B\n\n3A. (50m)  Ethan N\n--------------------------
 --------\n3B\n\n4A. (50m) \n4B. \n----------------------------------\n5A. (
 40m) Abby Y 283+277=560\n5B. \n\n6A. (40m) \n------------------------------
 ----\n6B. \n\n7A. (30m) Emma A.\, 14\n7B. \n-------------------------------
 --- \n8A. (30m) Ellie Y 287+264=551\n8B.\n\n9A. (20m) \n-------------------
 ---------------\n9B. \n\n10A. (13.5m)\n10B
