 hers </b>at 9m on 40-cm target face unless otherwise noted:<u></u><br><u></
 u><br><b>Target Assignments:</b><br><u></u><b><br></b>1. <b>Doug S.\, </b>a
 dult\, pd - <b>96 pts </b>(avg'd) <b>-&gt\; Indoor 2</b><br><br>2. <b>Trent
 on T.\, </b>adult\, pd - <b>118 pts </b>(avg'd) - <b>-&gt\; Indoor 2</b><br
 ><br>3. <br><br>4. <b>Chenille K</b>.\, adult\, pd - <b>43 pts </b>(avg'd)<
 b> -&gt\; Indoor 2</b><br><br>5. <b>Alicia E.\, </b>adult\, pd - <b>94 pts 
 </b> (avg'd) <b>-&gt\; Indoor 2</b><br><br>6. <br><br>7.<b> Lucas B.\, </b>
 13\, on 60-cm target face\, pd (left) - <b>57 pts </b>(avg'd) <b>-&gt\; Ind
 oor 2</b><br><br>8. <b>Craig B.\, </b>adult\, pd (left) - <b>51 pts -&gt\; 
 Indoor 2</b><br><br><b>Nicole B.\, </b>adult\, pd (left) - last min cancell
 ation - fee forfeited<br><br>Space will be limited to 8-16 archers per sess
 ion or in accordance with CDC Guidelines. <br>Each person will have a targe
 t no. assigned as above. <br><br>There may be two lines of 8 archers when t
 he number of participants exceeds 8 archers.<br>Not more than 8 archers wil
 l be on the shooting line at the same time.<br>A = Line A<br>B = Line B<br>
 <br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field 
 until further notice or approved by Coach Racae. <br><br>Parents of juniors
  10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator. <br>Parents of junio
 rs 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their child for gr
 eater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted int
 o each Indoor 1: First-time Class. <br><br>We will accept a limited number 
 of juniors under 12 into the program each semester\, depending on the total
   number of archers in all the classes. If you join before the limit is rea
 ched\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take other 
 Indoor 1 classes as needed and later join Indoor 2. If you are under 12\, a
 nd have registered and paid after the cut off\, your fee will be returned t
 o you. <br><br>Juniors may need to take Indoor 1 two or three times before 
 qualifying for Indoor 2 by scoring 50 pts over 30 arrows.<br>Adults don´t n
 eed a minimum score to graduate into Indoor 2.<br><br>At the end of each In
 door 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a complete 
 round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, because it wil
 l have been averaged by taking your recorded score from your scorecard\, di
 viding it by the number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and th
 en multiplying that by 30 to get a full round score.
