 ustin Business Park in East Oak Hill in Southwest Austin\, 78735 near the i
 ntersection of Mopac (Loop 1) and 290W. <br><br>COME JOIN US AND REGISTER N
 OW !<br><br>Open to adults\, juniors 8+\, and parents! Please read all the 
 info below and in the registration and waivers. <br><br>The composition of 
 the classes are by skill level\, not age.. There is usually about an even s
 plit between adults and juniors in each class.<br><br>More information\, re
 gistration forms and waivers are available at <a href="http://www.archerytr
 ainingcenter.com"><u><u><u><u><u>www.archerytrainingcenter.com</u></u></u><
 /u></u></a>.<br><br>Register here using ONE of these forms:<br><a href="htt
 ps://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeciOgkyuKTLZ5_ZaWCEyQKYSX1fWGpP5qakh
 T6OuAc6jJ_FQ/viewform"><u><u>2023 Indoor 1: First-time Class for Adults</u>
 </u></a>  OR<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSc_bYEFoE
 4oXkcm0T6fZK99fu_q6lL8wZGClXyfa1GZbahh-g/viewform"><u><u>2023 Indoor 1: Fir
 st-time Class for Juniors and Parents</u></u></a><br><br>Sign up for just O
 NE Indoor 1 class\, because most people graduate out of this class into Ind
 oor 2 after the first lesson.<br><br>Your name will be added below and your
  place reserved on a first registered and paid basis and after we receive 3
  things:  <br><b>2023 OUTDOOR 1 REGISTRATION FORM   +  MEMBERSHIP AND WAIVE
 RS PACKET +   FEE</b><b><br></b><u></u><br><b>USA Archery Level 4 NTS Coach
  Racae Meyer and other instructors/coaches.</b><br><b>See </b><a href="http
 s://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/who-we-are"><u><u><u>https://www.archeryt
 rainingcenter.com/who-we-are</u></u></u></a><b><br></b><br><b>Registered ar
 chers </b>at 9m on 40-cm target face unless otherwise noted:<u></u><br><u><
 /u><br><b>Target Assignments:</b><br><b><br></b>1. <b>Todd T.\, </b>adult\,
  pd - <b>51 pts</b><br><br>2.<br><br>3.<br><br>4.<br><br>5.<br><br>6.<br><b
 r>7.<br><br>8.<br><br>Space will be limited to 16 archers per session or in
  accordance with CDC Guidelines. <br>Each person will have a target no. ass
 igned as above. <br><br>There will be two lines of 8 archers when the numbe
 r of participants exceeds 8 archers.<br>Not more than 8 archers will be on 
 the shooting line at the same time.<br>A = Line A<br>B = Line B<br><br>The 
 archer and a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field until fu
 rther notice or approved by Coach Racae. <br><br>Parents of juniors 10+ can
  sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator. <br>Parents of juniors 8-9 y
 ears old need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their child for greater sa
 fety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into each I
 ndoor 1: First-time Class. <br><br>We will accept a limited number of junio
 rs under 12 into the program each semester\, depending on the total  number
  of archers in all the classes. If you join before the limit is reached\, a
 nd are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take other Indoor 1
  classes as needed and later join Indoor 2. If you are under 12\, and have 
 registered and paid after the cut off\, your fee will be returned to you. <
 br><br>Juniors may need to take Indoor 1 two or three times before qualifyi
 ng for Indoor 2 by scoring 50 pts over 30 arrows.<br>Adults don´t need a mi
 nimum score to graduate into Indoor 2.<br><br>At the end of each Indoor 1 c
 lass\, your scores will be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (3
 0 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final score\, because it will have b
 een averaged by taking your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing i
 t by the number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multi
 plying that by 30 to get a full round score.
