DESCRIPTION:<b>What we worked on today:</b><br><b>15 minutes late. Ellie no
 t home. Class ended about 7:36 therefore.</b><br><b>Status: </b>Lots of hom
 ework\, not much time for archery or SPTs lately.<br><b>Form: </b>Looked ve
 ry good overall\, considering amount of practice over the last two weeks. S
 ome positions are becoming automatic.<br>Work on adjusting:<br><ul><li>Head
  moves toward and around string instead of staying still</li><li>Horizontal
  alignment downward instead of horizontal\; bend from waist for lower targe
 ts\, not lower bow arm\; sight needs to align to correct</li><li>Draw upper
  arm and elbow raise unnecessarily too high\, affects alignment</li><li>Rel
 eases are good\, even strong\, directional</li><li>Bow arm stays up pretty 
 well</li><li>Shoulders low\, good</li><li>Draw to Load - Too far back and t
 oo high before Anchor</li><li>Everything needs to be a bit stronger\, tight
 er\, but you're getting there now!</li></ul><br>Not to worry! We'll work on
  it all at 18m and get ready for the Aggie Invitational <b>in 5 weeks !!!</
 b><br>Goal for 2027 Indoor Nationals: 280+<br><b>Homework: Camera on the ce
 iling\, please!</b><br><b><br></b>\n\nJoin with Google Meet: https://meet.g
 oogle.com/pzx-zhzm-kme\n\nLearn more about Meet at: https://support.google.
 com/a/users/answer/9282720
