 d/e/1FAIpQLSfx1RyOwd314Q4zXYiQ9rb_a3oe84E9dIYs8CN35Ginmevfpg/viewform?usp=p
 review</a>)<br><br>Add your name to Target Assignment List below or send in
  the above completed form.<br><br>Focus primarily on <br>    * perfecting y
 our form\, <br>    * slowly increasing your physical strength and draw weig
 ht\, <br>    * strengthening your mental program\, <br>    * determining yo
 ur average and personal best\, <br>    * understanding the spread between t
 he two\, and working on closing it.<br>You need your own equipment <br>Comp
 etition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrow
 s\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, finger
 tab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and
  side rods may not be added until you reach a higher level\, but you should
  order them in advance.) <br><br>Wear your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br>W
 hen you score 288 pts in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm target face you'll 
 move back to the next distance until you reach your competition distance<br
 >If you trained outdoors in the 2024 season\, you'll return to the farthest
  distance you shot.<br>Target arrangements may vary each session\, dependin
 g on who attends and distances needed.<br>Target 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors co
 mpetition distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use it for indepe
 ndent practice in between classes.<br>Target 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters compet
 ition distance) <br>Target 3 at 50m<br>Target 4 at 40m (U15 competition dis
 tance) <br>Target 5 at 30m (U13 competition distance) <br>Targets 6+7+8 at 
 20m (for those who have shot at 18m indoors or with Coach Racae's approval)
 <br>Targets 9 + 10 at 13.5m (for those who have just graduated from indoors
  at 9m)<br><br>Ideally\, we want to practice with two archers/target to rep
 licate competition conditions as much as possible.<br><b><br>Target Assignm
 ents:</b><br>Targets are assigned outdoors in advance to reduce confusion a
 nd delay on the day\,<br>so add your name next to your distance below. <br>
