DESCRIPTION:(Abby ill)<br><b>What we worked on today and you need to do:</b
 ><br><ol><li><b>Training schedule</b> for weeks before tournaments:<ul><li>
 <span>3 days 10 SPTs on Mon/Tues/Thurs</span></li><li><span>3 days shooting
 :  </span><ul><li>3 hrs on Sat (on field)\, </li><li>1.5 hrs Mon (on field)
  or Wed (In garage) </li><li>30 min Fri (in virtual private lesson)</li></u
 l></li></ul></li><li><b>Set shoulders and chest at SET</b><ul><li>Open rib 
 cage in chest to keep shoulders down</li><li>Hand on upper chest should be 
 vertical\, not angled up</li></ul></li><li><b>Maintain posture and weight d
 istribution when raising the bow</b><ul><li>Scoop with the bow arm\, not wi
 th shoulders and torso. </li><li>See notes from last week</li></ul></li><li
 ><b>Set Barrel of the Gun by the end of SET UP\, before DRAW to LOAD</b><ul
 ><li>Shoulders in line with bow arm</li><li>Don't push front shoulder in to
 wards string</li></ul></li><li><b>ANCHOR</b><ul><li>Needs to be stronger<ul
 ><li>Direction is towards neck - under and then up into anchor\, never down
  into anchor</li><li>In as far as you can go and up as high as you can go w
 ith hand into throat\, thumb down along throat\, little finger touching nec
 k</li></ul></li></ul></li><li><b>RELEASE</b><ul><li>Tighten draw arm biceps
  to form tighter "chicken wing" to reduce hand/arm flying out from neck upo
 n release</li><li>Hand should never lose contact with neck</li><li>Wrist st
 raight\, hand does not drop onto shoulder</li></ul></li><li><b>Always say N
 TS Shot Cycle in your head</b> on every shot so it's there to help you when
  you get to the competitions</li></ol><br><b>Before future sessions:</b><br
 ><ol><li><span>Area around target needs to be cleared</span><span> (See not
 es from last week)</span></li><li><span>Need camera on ceiling to analyze a
 lignments</span></li><li>Fletch more arrows for virtual classes</li><li>Loo
 k at form photos in Form Album</li></ol>\n\nJoin with Google Meet: https://
 meet.google.com/pzx-zhzm-kme\n\nLearn more about Meet at: https://support.g
 oogle.com/a/users/answer/9282720
