CREATED:20260326T213634Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><b>SPRING TRAINING PROGRAM - 9 weeks (Mar 23 - May 31)</b> <
 /p><p>We will go through the <b>National Training System (NTS) 11 Steps of 
 Shooting</b> and <b>Building Your Mental Program</b> step-by-step during th
 e regular training classes\, covering each one in sequence during the follo
 wing weeks.. </p><p>Learning\, understanding and doing the NTS and building
  a strong mental program are ongoing quests that all archers are continuous
 ly trying to achieve - even at the highest levels !</p><p><b><i>What if you
  miss some of the weeks?</i></b><i>  </i>We'll do our best to catch you up 
 during your next sessions. </p><p><b><i>Also see more important notes below
 \, under the schedule.</i></b></p><p><b>MARCH / APRIL</b></p><b>Sat 3/28 - 
 Fri 4/3</b><span>  </span><br><ul><li><b>WELCOME </b><span>!  </span><span>
 Understanding  </span></li><li><b>NTS CONCEPTS</b><span> especially TRANSFE
 R </span></li><li><span>Step 1</span><b> STANCE </b>+ Building Your Mental 
 Program</li></ul><p><b>Sat 4/4- Fri 4/10</b><br></p><ul><li>Step 2  <b>NOCK
 </b> + Building Your Mental Program</li><li>Step 3 <b>HOOK &amp\; GRIP</b> 
 + Building Your Mental Program</li></ul><p></p><p><b>Sat</b><b> 4/11 - Fri 
 4/17</b><span> </span><span>  </span></p><p></p><ul><li><span>Step 4</span>
 <b> SET </b><span>+ Building Your Mental Program</span></li><li><span>Step 
 5 </span><b>SET-UP +</b><span> Building Your Mental Program</span></li></ul
 ><p></p><b>Sat 4/18 - Fri 4/24 </b><br><ul><li>Step 6 <b>DRAW</b> to <b>LOA
 D </b>+ Building Your Mental Program</li></ul><b>Sat 4/25 - Fri 5/1 </b><br
 ><ul><li>Step 7 <b>ANCHOR </b>+ Building Your Mental Program</li><li><b>SCO
 RING WEEK for OUTDOOR 3-9</b></li></ul><b>MAY</b><b><br></b><br><b>Sat 5/2 
 - Fri 5/8 </b> <br><ul><li>Step 8<b> </b><b><b>TRANSFER to HOLD</b> + </b>B
 uilding Your Mental Program</li><li>Step 9<b> </b><b>EXPAND / AIM + </b>Bui
 lding Your Mental Program</li></ul><b>Sat 5/9 - Fri 5/15</b> <br><ul><li>St
 ep 10 <b>RELEASE / FO</b><b>LLOW-THROUGH </b><b>+</b> Building Your Mental 
 Program</li><li>Step 11 <b>FEEDBACK +</b> Building Your Mental Program</li>
 </ul><b>Sat 5/16 - Fri 5/22  </b><br><ul><li><b>PUTTING IT ALL TOGETHER FUN
  !</b></li></ul><b>Sat 5/23 - Sun 5/31  </b><br><ul><li><b>SCORING WEEK - A
 TCI SPRING COMPETITION and STAR PIN SHOOT</b></li></ul><p><b>INTRO</b></p><
 p><i>Each week the focus of your lessons will be on one or two particular <
 /i><b><i>Steps of Shooting of the NTS (National Training System) </i></b><i
 >shot cycle\, to help you focus and improve your form\, which\, as we all k
 now\, leads to greater and more consistent precision (tight groups of arrow
 s) and ultimately greater accuracy (tight groups of arrows dead center)</i>
 . <i>Concurrently you will be learning how to build a </i><b><i>strong ment
 al program</i></b><i>\, which will improve your focus\, awareness and confi
 dence for competitions later.</i></p><p><i>The NTS is the </i><b><i>most bi
 omechanically efficient and least injurious method of shooting</i></b><i>\,
  and is highly and continuously researched out at the Elite Athletes Center
  in Chula Vista\, CA. It is what the Olympians do!</i></p><p><i>The 11 NTS 
 Steps are cumulative with each step most successfully completed if the prev
 ious steps have been completed well. As you reach higher levels\, you will 
 learn the NTS Steps in progressively greater detail.</i></p><p><b>Goals by 
 the end of the spring semester (May 31)</b></p><p>Make a list of what you w
 ant to accomplish by the end of the semester. <span>Email it to Coach Racae
 \, so you can discuss it together. </span></p><p>Confidence and consistency
  in form and mind are your two main goals. Replicate the NTS step(s) mindfu
 lly and consistently on every shot\, and build a strong mental program that
  is consistent on every shot. </p><p>Your conscious mind commands your subc
 onscious mind to put your body into position\, after you train your body to
  be in those positions. When you stay in the present\, just doing what you 
 need to do as you need to do it\, your conscious mind will be occupied\, in
 stead of random thoughts entering your head or your being distracted by emo
 tional or environmental elements. </p><p>You´ll need to build up your menta
 l program alongside your form knowledge\, so when your body is trained to s
 hoot excellent shots\, your self image and subconscious support you\, inste
 ad of undermining you. </p><p><i>Improving your training\, practicing\, and
  competition components\, process\, and skills is a perpetual lifetime ques
 t\, which you´ll slowly learn to love. You´ll  realize what is under your c
 ontrol\, and you'll become your own best coach! Those who find all this fun
  and enjoy the journey are the ones who win - the champions!</i></p><p><i>I
  know you can do it -  I'm your biggest fan!</i></p><p><i>​I'm also really 
 looking forward to seeing you improve\, succeed\, and thrive !​</i></p><p><
 b><i>                                                   Coach Racae</i></b>
 </p>
