DESCRIPTION:COME JOIN US AND REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to adults\, juniors
  8+\, and parents! Please read all the info below and in the registration a
 nd waivers. <br><br>The composition of the classes are by skill level\, not
  age.. There is usually about an even split between adults and juniors in e
 ach class.<br><br>More information\, registration forms and waivers are ava
 ilable at <a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com"><u><u><u><u><u>www
 .archerytrainingcenter.com</u></u></u></u></u></a>.<br><br>Register here us
 ing ONE of these forms:<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIp
 QLSeciOgkyuKTLZ5_ZaWCEyQKYSX1fWGpP5qakhT6OuAc6jJ_FQ/viewform"><u><u>2023 In
 door 1: First-time Class for Adults</u></u></a>  OR<br><a href="https://doc
 s.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSc_bYEFoE4oXkcm0T6fZK99fu_q6lL8wZGClXyfa1GZba
 hh-g/viewform"><u><u>2023 Indoor 1: First-time Class for Juniors and Parent
 s</u></u></a><br><br>Sign up for just ONE Indoor 1 class\, because most peo
 ple graduate out of this class into Indoor 2 after the first lesson.<br><br
 >Your name will be added below and your place reserved on a first registere
 d and paid basis and after we receive 3 things:  <br><b>2023 OUTDOOR 1 REGI
 STRATION FORM   +  MEMBERSHIP AND WAIVERS PACKET +   FEE</b><b><br></b><u><
 /u><br><b>USA Archery Level 4 NTS Coach Racae Meyer and other instructors/c
 oaches.</b><br><b>See </b><a href="https://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/wh
 o-we-are"><u><u><u>https://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/who-we-are</u></u>
 </u></a><b><br></b><br><b>Registered archers </b>at 9m on 40-cm target face
  unless otherwise noted:<br><u></u><b><br></b>1  <b>Alayna J.\, </b>adult\,
  pd - <b>125 pts -&gt\; Indoor 2</b><br><br>2. <br><br>3<br><br>4.<br><br>5
 .<br><br>6.<br><br>7.<br><br>8.<br><br><b>Yugan C.\, 11\, </b>on 60-cm targ
 et face\, pd - substituted 9/7<br><b>Devin D.\, </b>adult\, pd - substitute
 d 10/1<br><b>Taurus K</b>.\, adult\, pd - substituted 10/1<br><br>Space wil
 l be limited to 8 archers per session or in accordance with CDC Guidelines.
  <br>Each person will have a target number. <br><br>There will be two lines
  of 8 archers when the number of participants exceeds 8 archers.<br>Not mor
 e than 8 archers will be on the shooting line at the same time.<br>A = Line
  A<br>B = Line B<br><br>The archer and a maximum of one spectator will be a
 llowed on the field until further notice or approved by Coach Racae. <br><b
 r>Parents of juniors 10+ can sign up as an archer or watch as a spectator. 
 <br>Parents of juniors 8-9 years old need to register\, pay\, and shoot wit
 h their child for greater safety.<br><br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ par
 ent) is accepted into each Indoor 1: First-time Class. <br><br>We will acce
 pt a limited number of juniors under 12 into the program each semester\, de
 pending on the total  number of archers in all the classes. If you join bef
 ore the limit is reached\, and are younger than 12\, you´ll stay in the pro
 gram and take other Indoor 1 classes as needed and later join Indoor 2. If 
 you are under 12\, and have registered and paid after the cut off\, your fe
 e will be returned to you. <br><br>Juniors may need to take Indoor 1 two or
  three times before qualifying for Indoor 2 by scoring 50 pts over 30 arrow
 s.<br>Adults don´t need a minimum score to graduate into Indoor 2.<br><br>A
 t the end of each Indoor 1 class\, your scores will be posted. If we did no
 t finish a complete round (30 arrows)\, you may not recognize your final sc
 ore\, because it will have been averaged by taking your recorded score from
  your scorecard\, dividing it by the number of arrows you shot to get an ar
 row average\, and then multiplying that by 30 to get a full round score.
