CREATED:20260913T001403Z
DESCRIPTION:<span>Need camera on ceiling so I can see alignments from overh
 ead.</span><br><span>Fletch more arrows\, so session is not interrupted so 
 often by retrieving arrows.</span><br><span>Cleared away items around targe
 t for safety - more to be done by next week.</span><br><span>Plan for this 
 season (for both girls):</span><br><ul><li>SPTs on weekday mornings</li><li
 >Sat Training at 18m range</li><li>Mon evenings outdoors when Joel is in to
 wn</li><li>Private virtuals</li><li>Aggie Invitational in Nov</li><li>Indoo
 r Nationals in Feb</li></ul><br><b>Abby - 7:00-7:30</b><br>Doing SPTS in th
 e mornings before school<br>Shot at blank bale with no sight\, no target fa
 ce<br>Looking really strong\, dynamic release and follow-through - much imp
 roved!<br>Elbow a bit high\, release sometimes angled down instead of aroun
 d\, <br>but impressive tension and direction towards target.<br>Looking muc
 h more pro ! Well done!<br><span>Next week: </span><br><span>Delve into fin
 er points.</span><br><span>Blank bale until last 10 min\, and then target f
 ace up to see what form changes occur\, if any.</span><br><span><br></span>
 <br><span><b>Ellie - 7:30-8:00</b></span><br>Doing SPTs.<br>Main focus toda
 y: <br>Scooping to keep front shoulder down has been overdone\, so entire t
 orso is scooping. Keep "the pole"\, scoop the bow with the bow arm from the
  shoulder\, but not bending waist and dipping torso to do it.  <br>Main thi
 ng: Focus on what you intend to do after SET. "KEEP" active focus on how yo
 u're scooping until it becomes automatic.<br>Feel the weight shift on the b
 ottom of your feet as you raise the bow\, and try to keep the weight more e
 qual. The bow being pushed out and up will add weight to the front\, and yo
 u need to equalize that more by increasing coiling and back tension on the 
 draw side.<br>Practice watching yourself raise the bow in the mirror.<br>Gr
 eat improvement over the session.<br>Great job\, tonight! <br>See you next 
 time!<br><br>Videos taken and added to Form Video albums\n\nJoin with Googl
 e Meet: https://meet.google.com/btv-ohwx-kon\n\nLearn more about Meet at: h
 ttps://support.google.com/a/users/answer/9282720
