UID:48orcldtrtdmphorjd0lrv9b6k@google.com
X-GOOGLE-CONFERENCE:https://meet.google.com/cmd-nwsk-nuk
CREATED:20260831T233952Z
DESCRIPTION:Concern: Inconsistent release.<br><br>What we worked on today: 
 Focusing on positions that influence release. Thinking about trying to do a
  good release usually is not a good strategy - <br>Better: Build up the pos
 itions before RELEASE and focus on the final position after FOLLOW-THROUGH 
 to obtain a stronger and more consistent RELEASE. Focus on back tension and
  keeping it through the end of the shot. <br><br><b>Clicker </b><br>Trying 
 to get through clicker indicates inconsistent draw and expansion\, so remov
 ed clicker for now.<b><br></b><br><b>Back tension for cleaner release and f
 ollow-through</b><br>Turned target around so practicing at blank bale in or
 der to focus heavily on building back tension\, not all at once at the end 
 of the shot\, but rather gradually during these steps:<br>SET = 40% back te
 nsion<br>SET UP = 60%<br>DRAW to LOAD = 80%<br>ANCHOR - 90%<br>TRANSFER to 
 HOLD = 95%<br>Keeping the back tension and focusing on the final position y
 ou want to be in at RELEASE/FOLLOW-THROUGH (not at AIMING at the target)<br
 >Release should fly back and around upon release as a result of back tensio
 n. Index finger touching back of neck\, wrist straight not bent. <br>Push h
 ard towards the target and around as far as possible with scapula stopping 
 at spine because it can't go any farther = Max stopping point in both direc
 tions.<br>Divide body vertically front and back - tension and direction equ
 al on both sides and maxed out.<br><br><b>Posture - keep torso in position 
 as you raise the bow and draw </b><br>Tighten core\, drop chest\, shoulders
  level\, back and relaxed down.<br>Keep positions as you raise the bow and 
 draw.<br>Video yourself with something in the background to determine when 
 you raise and how much.<br><br><b>Say the Shot Cycle in your head or even b
 etter out loud before each step</b>\, so you don't skip around and over som
 e of the later steps.<br><br>Great session. You did really well! See you ne
 xt time!<br><b><br></b>\n\nJoin with Google Meet: https://meet.google.com/c
 md-nwsk-nuk\n\nLearn more about Meet at: https://support.google.com/a/users
 /answer/9282720
LAST-MODIFIED:20260901T004022Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Virtual Private Lesson with Coach Racae - Ethan N.
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
