DESCRIPTION:Training classes at this location are reserved for competitive 
 and advanced archers..\n\nREMINDER:  Everyone needs to come to at least one
  Training Class per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (All Indoor 2-
 6 at 9m classes are training classes.)\n\nCoach Racae will coach the Outdoo
 r 3-9 Training Class whenever there are at least 5 archers registered by Fr
 i 9:00 am (for Sat) and Sat 9:00 am (for Sun).   \n\nTRAINING CLASS (TC): $
 57/archer/3-hr class\n(1x/wk required to attend Open Practice)\nFACILITY FE
 E (FF) (required each month): $75/month/archer due on 1st of the month. (US
 AA Level 3 Coaches do not pay facility fee.)\nOPEN PRACTICE (OP) Included i
 n facility fee (1-2x/wk recommended)\nPRIVATE LESSON (PL): $125/hr/archer (
 1x/mo recommended)\n\nPlease add your name to the target list below to regi
 ster\nFocus primarily on perfecting your form\, \nslowly increasing your ph
 ysical strength and draw weight\, \nstrengthening your mental program\, \nd
 etermining your average and personal best\, \nunderstanding the spread betw
 een the two\, and working on closing it.\n\nEQUIPMENT:\nYou need your own e
 quipment: \nCompetition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\,
  12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, a
 rmguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, e
 tc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added until you reach a higher level\
 , but you should order them in advance.) \n\nWear your ATCI shirt to traini
 ng.\n\nWEATHER / DAYLIGHT\nSession times may vary depending on temperature/
 daylight conditions.\nDuring inclement weather (<52F or 100F>\, 20 mph wind
 s\, heavy rain\, lightning) class will move to the Indoor 9m range to pract
 ice form and be noted on the calendar shortly before the scheduled session.
 \n\nTARGET ARRANGEMENTS\nThe target arrangements have changed as of 8/22\, 
 because it's the beginning of the indoor season\, so everyone needs to shoo
 t 18m to attend the indoor competitions at Texas A&M in Nov and Feb. Ideall
 y\, you want to alternate between 18m and your outdoor distance each time y
 ou come\, so you continue to improve at the longer distance over the fall a
 nd winter. \n\nIf there is not space at the distance you want to shoot\, sh
 oot at 18m. \nAlternatively\, Targets 6 and 7 can be moved to 30m or 18m an
 d Target 10 to 18m when necessary. \n\nYOUR SCORING GOALS:\n    1. Meet the
  MQS  to move back 10m until you reach your competition distance (see below
 ) \n    2. Meet the MQS to get on the ATCI Indoor and Outdoor Competition T
 eams each year\nMQS (Minimum Qualifying Scores):\n\n\nTo move back 10 m unt
 il you reach your competition distance (see below): \n2026: 288 pts  in a 3
 6-arrow round on the 122-cm target face \n2027 297 pts  in a 36-arrow round
  on the 122-cm target face \n\n\nATCI Indoor Competition Team (ATCIICT): \n
 2026:  210 pts or 410 pts (2 rounds) at 18m  on 60cm target face (U13/U15) 
 or 40cm target face (U18\, U21\, Seniors 21-49\, Masters 50+) in 30-arrow i
 ndoor round (arrow avg: 7.0 pts)\n2027:  225 pts or 450 pts (2 rounds) at 1
 8m on 60cm target face (U13/U15) or 40cm target face (U18\, U21\, Seniors 2
 1-49\, Masters 50+) in 30-arrow indoor round (arrow avg: 7.5 pts)\n\n\nATCI
  Outdoor Competition Team  (ATCIOCT)\n2026 : 260 pts or 520 pts (2 rounds) 
 At your tournament distance\, 36-arrow round on 122-cm target face (arrow a
 vg: 7.22 pts)\n2027 : 270 pts or 540 pts (2 rounds)\nAt your tournament dis
 tance\, 36-arrow round on 122-cm target face (arrow avg: 7.5 pts)\n\nTarget
  distances vary with each session\, depending on who attends and distances 
 needed.\nWhen you score 288 ptsyou'll move back to the next distance until 
 you reach your competition distance.\nIf you trained outdoors in the 2026 s
 eason\, during the 2027 outdoor season\, you'll return to the farthest dist
 ance you shot in 2026.\n\n70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should a
 lways stay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent practice in between cl
 asses.\n60m (U18 + Masters competition distance) \n50m\n40m (U15 competitio
 n distance) \n30m (U13 competition distance)\n20m (for adults who have just
  graduated out of Indoor 2)\n13.5m (for juniors who have just graduated out
  of Indoor 2)\n\nIdeally\, we want to practice with at least two archers/ta
 rget to replicate competition conditions  .\n\nTARGET ASSIGNMENTS\nTargets 
 are assigned outdoors in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\,
  so add your name next to your distance below. \nIf you need help or have q
 uestions\, email/text Coach Racae\n(Dotted lines represent tent poles divid
 ing Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)\n\n----------------------------------\n1A. (70m
 )\n1B\n\n2A. (60m)  \n2B\n\n3A. (50m)  \n----------------------------------
 \n3B\n\n4A. (40m) \n4B. \n----------------------------------\n5A. (30m)\n5B
 . \n\n6A. (30m)\n----------------------------------\n6B. \n\n7A. (18m) Ryan
  R.\, adult\n7B. Abby Y - out sick\n---------------------------------- \n8A
 . (18m) Coraline R.\, 11\n8B. Ellie Y - out sick\n\n9A. (18m) Logan C.\, 9\
 , USAA\, pd (7/18) \n----------------------------------\n9B. Chi C.\, adult
 \, USAA\, pd (8/18)\n\n10A. (13.5m)\n10B
