DESCRIPTION:COME JOIN US AND REGISTER NOW !<br><br>Open to adults\, juniors
  8+\, and parents! Please read all the info below and in the registration a
 nd waivers. <br><br>The composition of the classes are by skill level\, not
  age.. There is usually about an even split between adults and juniors in e
 ach class.<br><br>More information\, registration forms and waivers are ava
 ilable at <a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com"><u><u><u><u><u>www
 .archerytrainingcenter.com</u></u></u></u></u></a>.<br><br>Register here us
 ing ONE of these forms:<br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIp
 QLSeciOgkyuKTLZ5_ZaWCEyQKYSX1fWGpP5qakhT6OuAc6jJ_FQ/viewform"><u><u>2023 In
 door 1: First-time Class for Adults</u></u></a>  OR<br><a href="https://doc
 s.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSc_bYEFoE4oXkcm0T6fZK99fu_q6lL8wZGClXyfa1GZba
 hh-g/viewform"><u><u>2023 Indoor 1: First-time Class for Juniors and Parent
 s</u></u></a><br><br>Sign up for just ONE Indoor 1 class\, because most peo
 ple graduate out of this class into Indoor 2 after the first lesson.<br><br
 >Your name will be added below and your place reserved on a first registere
 d and paid basis and after we receive 3 things:  <br><b>2023 OUTDOOR 1 REGI
 STRATION FORM   +  MEMBERSHIP AND WAIVERS PACKET +   FEE</b><b><br></b><u><
 /u><br><b>USA Archery Level 4 NTS Coach Racae Meyer and other instructors/c
 oaches.</b><br><b>See </b><a href="https://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/wh
 o-we-are"><u><u><u>https://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/who-we-are</u></u>
 </u></a><b><br></b><br><b>Registered archers </b>at 9m on 40-cm target face
  unless otherwise noted:<u></u><br><u></u><br><b>Target Assignments:</b><br
 ><u></u><b><br></b>1A.<br>1B.<br><br>2A.<br>2B.<br><br>3A.<br>3B.<br><br>4A
 .<br>4B.<br><br>5A.<br>5B.<br><br>6A.<br>6B.<br><br>7A.<br>7B.<br><br>8A.<b
 r>8B.<br><br>Space will be limited to 16 archers per session or in accordan
 ce with CDC Guidelines. <br>Each person will have a target no. assigned as 
 above. <br><br>There will be two lines of 8 archers when the number of part
 icipants exceeds 8 archers.<br>Not more than 8 archers will be on the shoot
 ing line at the same time.<br>A = Line A<br>B = Line B<br><br>The archer an
 d a maximum of one spectator will be allowed on the field until further not
 ice or approved by Coach Racae. <br><br>Parents of juniors 10+ can sign up 
 as an archer or watch as a spectator. <br>Parents of juniors 8-9 years old 
 need to register\, pay\, and shoot with their child for greater safety.<br>
 <br>A maximum of one 8-year-old (+ parent) is accepted into each Indoor 1: 
 First-time Class. <br><br>We will accept a limited number of juniors under 
 12 into the program each semester\, depending on the total  number of arche
 rs in all the classes. If you join before the limit is reached\, and are yo
 unger than 12\, you´ll stay in the program and take other Indoor 1 classes 
 as needed and later join Indoor 2. If you are under 12\, and have registere
 d and paid after the cut off\, your fee will be returned to you. <br><br>Ju
 niors may need to take Indoor 1 two or three times before qualifying for In
 door 2 by scoring 50 pts over 30 arrows.<br>Adults don´t need a minimum sco
 re to graduate into Indoor 2.<br><br>At the end of each Indoor 1 class\, yo
 ur scores will be posted. If we did not finish a complete round (30 arrows)
 \, you may not recognize your final score\, because it will have been avera
 ged by taking your recorded score from your scorecard\, dividing it by the 
 number of arrows you shot to get an arrow average\, and then multiplying th
 at by 30 to get a full round score.
