DESCRIPTION:<b>What we worked on:</b><br><ol><li><b>HOOK and GRIP</b><ul><l
 i>Not slightly grabbing bow at the last second</li></ul></li><li><b>SET - P
 osture</b></li></ol><ul><li><ul><li><span>Much better - Getting there</span
 ></li><li><span>Get the basics down really well first</span><ul><li><span>w
 ork in order of shot sequence  </span></li><li><span>lots of reps frequentl
 y - 30 reps on one detail at a time\; 5-6 x wk</span></li><li><span>watch y
 ourself in the mirror </span></li><li><span>video yourself from different a
 ngles</span></li></ul></li><li><span>Work on setting and maintaining positi
 ons</span></li><li>Needs:<ul><li>Chest vertical - Put hand on bony part of 
 chest so that it's vertical\, not angled out and up to indicate chest raise
 d</li><li>Chest position maintained throughout the shot - never raises</li>
 <li>Pelvis down and forward\, not up and back - almost there!</li><li>Core 
 muscles tight to prevent raising  </li></ul></li></ul></li></ul>
