DESCRIPTION:<b>What we worked on today:</b><br><ol><li><b>No bounce</b> - m
 uch improved\, and more consistent</li><li><b>Draw to Load </b>- <b>up into
  ANCHOR</b> <ul><li><span>Draw hand - a little too high on most shots</span
 ><ul><li>come down to shoulder height </li><li>how far back - btwn shoulder
  and neck before DRAW\, then</li><li>into neck - touching at least little f
 inger to throat\, trying for no gap between neck and hand</li></ul></li><li
 >Draw elbow - a little low<ul><li>try not to pull down\, but rather around<
 /li><li>should never be below shoulder height</li></ul></li><li>Bow arm - d
 rops a bit\, sometimes hits body<ul><li>keep your upper bow arm up\, so you
  come down into the target when aiming (never up into it)</li><li>Position 
 bow arm correctly and coil enough\, so swing doesn't hit you</li></ul></li>
 <li>Bow hand - sometimes holds the bow<ul><li>Let it drop and swing</li></u
 l></li></ul></li><li><b>Eyes closed to feel the shot more intensely without
  visual stimulation</b><ul><li>Close eyes after SET</li><li>Open eyes at AI
 M</li></ul></li><li><b>Once you have it down pretty well\, increase flow an
 d rhythm</b></li></ol><br><b>Homework: </b><br><ol><li><b>Video yourself sh
 ooting outdoors\, critique\, correct\, repeat often. </b>(<span>You know wh
 at to do.) </span></li><li><span><b>Shoot for 30 min at least every other d
 ay </b>(or more). At this stage\, number of arrows shot well is much more i
 mportant than number of arrows shot. (Arrow count will increase after the f
 orm is in place and more consistent.)</span></li></ol>\n\nJoin with Google 
 Meet: https://meet.google.com/xxa-mtou-ngn\n\nLearn more about Meet at: htt
 ps://support.google.com/a/users/answer/9282720
LAST-MODIFIED:20260527T200302Z
