DESCRIPTION:Training classes at this location are reserved for competitive 
 and advanced archers..\n\nREMINDER:  Everyone needs to come to at least one
  Training Class per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (All Indoor 2-
 6 at 9m classes are training classes.)   \n\nTRAINING CLASS (TC): $57/arche
 r/3-hr class\n(1x/wk required to attend Open Practice)\nFACILITY FEE (FF) (
 required each month): $75/month/archer due on 1st of the month to attend Op
 en Practices. (USAA Level 3 Coaches do not pay facility fee.)\nOPEN PRACTIC
 E (OP) Included in facility fee (1-2x/wk recommended)\nPRIVATE LESSON (PL):
  $125/hr/archer (1x/mo recommended)\n\nPlease add your name to the target l
 ist below to register\nFocus primarily on perfecting your form\, \nslowly i
 ncreasing your physical strength and draw weight\, \nstrengthening your men
 tal program\, \ndetermining your average and personal best\, \nunderstandin
 g the spread between the two\, and working on closing it.\n\nEQUIPMENT:\nYo
 u need your own equipment: \nCompetition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\,
  plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, ch
 est protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\,
  arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added until you reac
 h a higher level\, but you should order them in advance.) \n\nWear your ATC
 I shirt to training.\n\nWEATHER / DAYLIGHT\nSession times may vary dependin
 g on temperature/daylight conditions.\nDuring inclement weather (<52F or 10
 0F> heat index\, 20 mph winds\, heavy rain\, lightning) class will move to 
 the Indoor 9m range to practice form and be noted on the calendar shortly b
 efore the scheduled session.\n\nTARGET ARRANGEMENTS\nMay vary each session\
 , depending on who attends and distances needed.\nWhen you score 288 pts in
  a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the next di
 stance until you reach your competition distance (see below)\nIf you traine
 d outdoors in the 2025 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you 
 shot.\n\nTarget 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should always
  stay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent practice in between classes
 .\nTarget 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition distance) \nTargets 3+4 at 50
 m\nTarget 5+6 at 40m (U15 competition distance) \nTarget 7+8 at 30m (U13 co
 mpetition distance) \nTargets 9 at 20m (for adults who have just graduated 
 out of Indoor 2)\nTarget 10 at 13.5m (for juniors who have just graduated o
 ut of Indoor 2)\n\nIdeally\, we want to practice with two archers/target to
  replicate outdoor competition conditions.\n\nTARGET ASSIGNMENTS\nTargets a
 re assigned outdoors in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\, 
 so add your name next to your distance below. \nIf you need help or have qu
 estions\, email/text Coach Racae\n(Dotted lines represent tent poles dividi
 ng Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)\n\nATCIOCT = 2026 ATCI Outdoor Competition Team 
  \nMQS at your tournament distance\, 36-arrow rounds on 122-cm target face:
  \n260 pts or 520 pts (2 rounds)\n----------------------------------\n1A. (
 70m)\n1B\n\n2A. (60m)  \n2B\n\n3A. (50m)  \n-------------------------------
 ---\n3B\n\n4A. (50m) \n4B. \n----------------------------------\n5A. (40m) 
 Sara T. (O6 @ 40m)\n5B. Abby Y 292+258=550\n\n6A. (40m) Anna P\n-----------
 -----------------------\n6B. \n\n7A. (30m) akhil C\n7B. Ellie Y 277+276=553
 \n---------------------------------- \n8A. (30m) \n8B.\n\n9A. (20m) \n-----
 -----------------------------\n9B. \n\n10A. (13.5m)\n10B
