DESCRIPTION:Training classes at this location are reserved for competitive 
 and advanced archers..<br><br>REMINDER:  Everyone needs to come to at least
  one Training Class per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (All Indoo
 r 2-6 at 9m classes are training classes.)<br><br>Coach Racae will coach th
 e Outdoor 3-9 Training Class whenever there are at least 5 archers register
 ed by Fri 9:00 am (for Sat) and Sat 9:00 am (for Sun).   <br><br>TRAINING C
 LASS (TC): $57/archer/3-hr class<br>(1x/wk required to attend Open Practice
 )<br>FACILITY FEE (FF) (required each month): $75/month/archer due on 1st o
 f the month. (USAA Level 3 Coaches do not pay facility fee.)<br>OPEN PRACTI
 CE (OP) Included in facility fee (1-2x/wk recommended)<br>PRIVATE LESSON (P
 L): $125/hr/archer (1x/mo recommended)<br><br>Please add your name to the t
 arget list below to register<br>Focus primarily on perfecting your form\, <
 br>slowly increasing your physical strength and draw weight\, <br>strengthe
 ning your mental program\, <br>determining your average and personal best\,
  <br>understanding the spread between the two\, and working on closing it.<
 br><br>EQUIPMENT:<br>You need your own equipment: <br>Competition recurve b
 ow\, sight\, stabilizer\, plunger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-ba
 r assembly\, clicker\, chest protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger slin
 g\, hip or field quiver\, arrow puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may no
 t be added until you reach a higher level\, but you should order them in ad
 vance.) <br><br>Wear your ATCI shirt to training.<br><br>WEATHER / DAYLIGHT
 <br>Session times may vary depending on temperature/daylight conditions.<br
 >During inclement weather (&lt\;52F or 100F&gt\;\, 20 mph winds\, heavy rai
 n\, lightning) class will move to the Indoor 9m range to practice form and 
 be noted on the calendar shortly before the scheduled session.<br><br>TARGE
 T ARRANGEMENTS<br>The target arrangements have changed as of 8/22\, because
  it's the beginning of the indoor season\, so everyone needs to shoot 18m t
 o attend the indoor competitions at Texas A&amp\;M in Nov and Feb. Ideally\
 , you want to alternate between 18m and your outdoor distance each time you
  come\, so you continue to improve at the longer distance over the fall and
  winter. <br><br>If there is not space at the distance you want to shoot\, 
 shoot at 18m. <br>Alternatively\, Targets 6 and 7 can be moved to 30m or 18
 m and Target 10 to 18m when necessary. <br><br>YOUR SCORING GOALS:<br>Meet 
 the MQS  to move back 10m until you reach your competition distance (see be
 low) <br>Meet the MQS to get on the ATCI Indoor and Outdoor Competition Tea
 ms each year <br>MQS (Minimum Qualifying Scores):<br><br><br>To move back 1
 0 m until you reach your competition distance (see below): <br>2026: 288 pt
 s  in a 36-arrow round on the 122-cm target face <br>2027: 297 pts  in a 36
 -arrow round on the 122-cm target face <br><br>ATCI Indoor Competition Team
  (ATCIICT): <br>2026:  210 pts or 410 pts (2 rounds) at 18m  on 60cm target
  face (U13/U15) or 40cm target face (U18\, U21\, Seniors 21-49\, Masters 50
 +) in 30-arrow indoor round (arrow avg: 7.0 pts)<br>2027:  225 pts or 450 p
 ts (2 rounds) at 18m on 60cm target face (U13/U15) or 40cm target face (U18
 \, U21\, Seniors 21-49\, Masters 50+) in 30-arrow indoor round (arrow avg: 
 7.5 pts)<br><br>ATCI Outdoor Competition Team  (ATCIOCT)<br>2026 : 260 pts 
 or 520 pts (2 rounds) At your tournament distance\, 36-arrow round on 122-c
 m target face (arrow avg: 7.22 pts)<br>2027 : 270 pts or 540 pts (2 rounds)
 <br>At your tournament distance\, 36-arrow round on 122-cm target face (arr
 ow avg: 7.5 pts)<br><br>Target distances vary with each session\, depending
  on who attends and distances needed.<br>When you score 288 ptsyou'll move 
 back to the next distance until you reach your competition distance.<br>If 
 you trained outdoors in the 2026 season\, during the 2027 outdoor season\, 
 you'll return to the farthest distance you shot in 2026.<br><br>70m (U21 + 
 Seniors competition distance) should always stay at 70m so Jake can use it 
 for independent practice in between classes.<br>60m (U18 + Masters competit
 ion distance) <br>50m<br>40m (U15 competition distance) <br>30m (U13 compet
 ition distance)<br>20m (for adults who have just graduated out of Indoor 2)
 <br>13.5m (for juniors who have just graduated out of Indoor 2)<br><br>Idea
 lly\, we want to practice with at least two archers/target to replicate com
 petition conditions  .<br><br>TARGET ASSIGNMENTS<br>Targets are assigned ou
 tdoors in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\, so add your na
 me next to your distance below. <br>If you need help or have questions\, em
 ail/text Coach Racae<br>(Dotted lines represent tent poles dividing Targets
  3\, 6\, and 9.)<br><br>----------------------------------<br>1A. (70m)<br>
 1B<br><br>2A. (60m)  <br>2B<br><br>3A. (50m)  <br>-------------------------
 ---------<br>3B<br><br>4A. (40m) <br>4B. <br>------------------------------
 ----<br>5A. (30m)<br>5B. <br><br>6A. (30m) <br>----------------------------
 ------<br>6B. <br><br>7A. (18m) Finn e<br>7B. Emma A<br>-------------------
 --------------- <br>8A. (18m) Rhys e<br>8B.<br><br>9A. (18m) Matt L<br>----
 ------------------------------<br>9B.  Everett Z<br><br>10A. (13.5m)<br>10B
