DESCRIPTION:<h4><b>November 22-24\, 2024 in the Physical Education Activity
  Building at Texas A&amp\;M University</b></h4>The response to the Aggie In
 vitational registration opening on 9/16 at 8:00am has been overwhelming alr
 eady\, so....<b><br></b><br><b>Sign up NOW</b> if you're going to this comp
 etition at Texas A&amp\;M on Nov 22-24.<br>Do not wait to see if you qualif
 y to go or you won't get a place:<br><a href="https://www.usarchery.org/eve
 nts/event-information/45924" target="_blank">https://www.usarchery.org/<u><
 /u>events/event-information/45924</a><br><br><b>Our team shooting time is 1
 :00 pm on Sat.\, Nov 23</b>\, but sign up for any time available or conveni
 ent. (The 1:00 pm Sat may already be full.) The other times are <b>Fri 1:00
  pm\, Fri 6 pm\, Sat 8am\, Sat 6pm\, Sun 9am</b> <br><br><b>Scroll down for
  list of our members and their shooting times.</b><br><br><b>Let me know yo
 ur shooting times</b>\, if I don't have them already as listed below. (Thos
 e not yet registered at the latest time I checked are shown in red.) If you
  do not intend to register\, let me know that\, too\, please.<br><br>More i
 nfo on <a href="http://www.archerytrainingcenter.com/calendar" target="_bla
 nk">www.archerytrainingcenter.com/<u></u>calendar</a> under Aggie Invitatio
 nal on  Nov 22-24.<br><br><b>All that is allowed this year is to sign up fo
 r </b><b>one shooting time of 60 arrows (2 rounds of 30 arrows) on </b><b>a
  40-cm target face (choose single NOT triangular 3-spot). </b><br><br>Pract
 ice outdoors from now on at 18m on <b>40-cm target face only.</b> There are
  no 60-cm target faces at the Aggie Invitational this year. Alternate some 
 days with shooting at your outdoor distance\, so you practice for both indo
 or and outdoor competitions. <br><br><b>Deadline: Sunday\, Nov. 10</b><br>M
 eet one of the <b>MQS</b> (Minimum Qualifying Scores) below to participate 
 more comfortably in the <b>Aggie Invitational. </b><br><br><b>Alternative M
 QS</b>:     <b><u>9m</u>   <u>Arrow avg.</u>    <u>18m</u>   <u>Arrow avg.<
 /u></b><br>          40 cm             270        9.0             210      
  7.0<br>          60 cm             280        9.33           220      7.33
 <br>          Reduced        200        7.0<br><br><b>If you miss making th
 e MQS:</b> <br><ul><li><b>After discussing it with me\,</b> you may decide 
 to notify the TAMU tournament director to release your place so others can 
 attend.</li><li><b>Go to watch instead</b>\, so you'll be more prepared for
  the 2025 Indoor Nationals on February 14-16 in the same location.</li></ul
 ><br><br><b>ATCI Members already signed up:</b><br><br><b><u>Master Male</u
 ></b><br><b>Ted H</b> - 9:00 am\, Sun.\, Nov 24<b><br></b><br><u><b>Senior 
 Female</b></u><br><b>Christine S. - </b>6:00 pm Sat.\, Nov 23<br><b>Erika O
 -G - </b>6:00 pm Sat.\, Nov 23<br><br><u><b>Senior Male</b></u><br><b>Joel 
 Y</b> - 8:00 am Sat.\, Nov 23<br><b>Javier G. - </b>6:00 pm Sat.\, Nov 23<b
 r><b>Nick E.  </b>- 8:00 am Sat.\, Nov 23<br><b>Ji M. - </b>9:00 am Sun.\, 
 Nov 24<br><b>Jake L.</b><br><b>Byron C.</b><br><b>Justin W.</b><b><br></b><
 br><b><u>U18</u></b><br><b>Lily </b>- 1:00 pm Sat.\, Nov 23 <br><b>Kishore 
 </b>- 6:00 pm Sat.\, Nov 23<br><b>Luke - </b>1:00 pm Sat. Nov 23<br><b>Pran
 av </b>- 6:00 pm Sat.\, Nov 23<br><b>Lexi</b> - prior school commitment<b><
 br></b><br><b><u>U15</u></b><br><b>Joseph </b>- 9:00 am Sun.\, Nov 24<br><b
 >Riley</b> - 6:00 pm Sat.\, Nov 23<br><b>Ananya </b>- 6:00 pm Sat.\, Nov 23
 <br><br><b><u>U13</u></b><br><b>Abby -</b> 1:00 pm Sat.\, Nov 23<br><b>Finn
   </b>- 1:00 pm Sat.\, Nov 23<br><b>Gianna </b>- 1:00 pm Sat.\, Nov 23<br><
 b>Rhys  </b>- 1:00 pm Sat.\, Nov 23<br><b>Yugan - </b>1:00 pm Sat.\, Nov 23
 <br><b>Daisy </b>- 6:00 pm Sat.\, Nov 23<br><b>Jacqui </b>- prior family co
 mmitment<b> </b><br><b>Eleonor </b>- schedule conflict (Luke substituted)<b
 r><b>Miles </b>- canceled due to not enough practice due to injury/illness<
 br><b>Bettie</b><br><br><b>Another way to look at it:</b><br><br><b><u>Sat 
 @ 8:00 am</u></b> <br>   Joel Y.\, adult - Level 3 Coach<br>   Nick\, adult
  - Level 3 Coach<br><br><b><u>Sat @ 1:00 pm</u></b> <br>   Lily\, 15 - Leve
 l 1 Instructor<br>   Luke\, 15   <br>   Abby\, 12<br>   Finn\, 12<br>   Yug
 an\, 12<br>   Gianna\, 11<br>   Rhys\, 10<br>   <br><b><u>Sat @ 6:00 pm</u>
 </b><br><b>   </b>Christine\, adult<br>   Erika\, adult<br>   Javier\, adul
 t<br>   Kishore\, 16<br>   Pranav\, 16<br>   Riley\, 13<br>   Ananya\, 13<b
 r>   Daisy\, 9<br><br><b><u>Sun @ 9:00 am</u></b><br><b>   </b>Ted H.\, adu
 lt<br>   Ji M.\, adult<br>   Joseph F\, 13<p>The Aggie Invitational registr
 ation is for all age divisions and you will only be shooting one time (tota
 l of 60 arrows) at a 40-cm target face. Please review the registration deta
 ils for accuracy. Confirm your category and shooting time on the Entry List
 .</p><p>To make any necessary corrections\, contact Texas A&amp\;M archery 
 through <a href="mailto:tamuarcherytournaments@gmail.com" target="_blank"><
 u>tamuarcherytournaments@gmail.com</u></a> </p><p><u><u><strong><b>Parking 
 Information</b></strong></u></u>:</p><p>Parking will be allowed in lot 95 (
 behind the PEAP building) and lot 100 (surrounds Reed Arena) anytime after 
 5pm on Friday through the evening of Sunday. If you arrive to campus before
  5pm on Friday (Friday 1pm shooting time)\, then you will have to pay for p
 arking. Please following the link below to provide you a map of the differe
 nt lots on campus to help further assist you\, as well as the parking websi
 te where you can pay for visitor parking: <a href="https://transport.tamu.e
 du/parkingmap//tsmap.htm?map=vis" target="_blank"><u>https://transport.tamu
 .edu/parkingmap//tsmap.htm?map=vis</u></a></p><p><a href="https://parking.t
 amu.edu/Parking/visitor.aspx" target="_blank"><u>https://parking.tamu.edu/P
 arking/visitor.aspx</u></a></p><p><u><u><strong><b>Awards: </b></strong></u
 ></u></p><p>Aggie Invitational awards will be done on Sunday\, Nov. 24 afte
 r the Sunday 9am line is done. You must either be present to receive your a
 ward or have a representative pick up your award. AWARDS WILL NOT BE MAILED
 !!! Awards will only be given to the top 3 in each division.</p><p><u><u><s
 trong><b>Directions:</b></strong></u></u></p><p><strong><b>From Austin</b><
 /strong></p><p>Take 290 East to Hwy 21\, turn left towards Bryan\, turn rig
 ht on highway 47\, turn left on Highway 60\, turn right on 2818\, turn left
  on George Bush Drive\,  before the railroad tracks make a left onto Olsen 
 Blvd. At the first intersection make a left onto Tom Chandler Rd. At the fo
 ur-way stop make a right onto Penberthy Rd and the PEAP building will be on
  the left side directly across from Reed Arena. It is approximately 100 mil
 es from Austin to College Station. </p>
