DESCRIPTION:Training classes at this location are reserved for competitive 
 and advanced archers..\n\nREMINDER:  Everyone needs to come to at least one
  Training Class per week to be able to attend Open Practice. (All Indoor 2-
 6 at 9m classes are training classes.)\n\nTRAINING CLASS (TC): $57/archer/3
 -hr class\n(1x/wk required to attend Open Practice)\nFACILITY FEE (FF) (req
 uired each month): $75/month/archer due on 1st of the month to attend Open 
 Practices. (USAA Level 3 Coaches do not pay facility fee.)\nOPEN PRACTICE (
 OP) Included in facility fee (1-2x/wk recommended)\nPRIVATE LESSON (PL): $1
 25/hr/archer (1x/mo recommended)\n\nPlease add your name to the target list
  below to register\nFocus primarily on perfecting your form\, \nslowly incr
 easing your physical strength and draw weight\, \nstrengthening your mental
  program\, \ndetermining your average and personal best\, \nunderstanding t
 he spread between the two\, and working on closing it.\n\nEQUIPMENT:\nYou n
 eed your own equipment: \nCompetition recurve bow\, sight\, stabilizer\, pl
 unger\, rest\, 12 carbon arrows\, side rod/v-bar assembly\, clicker\, chest
  protector\, armguard\, fingertab\, finger sling\, hip or field quiver\, ar
 row puller\, etc. (Clicker and side rods may not be added until you reach a
  higher level\, but you should order them in advance.) \n\nWear your ATCI s
 hirt to training.\n\nWEATHER / DAYLIGHT\nSession times may vary depending o
 n temperature/daylight conditions.\nDuring inclement weather (<52F or 100F>
  heat index\, 20 mph winds\, heavy rain\, lightning) class will move to the
  Indoor 9m range to practice form and be noted on the calendar shortly befo
 re the scheduled session.\n\nTARGET ARRANGEMENTS\nMay vary each session\, d
 epending on who attends and distances needed.\nWhen you score 288 pts in a 
 36-arrow round on the 122-cm target face you'll move back to the next dista
 nce until you reach your competition distance (see below)\nIf you trained o
 utdoors in the 2025 season\, you'll return to the farthest distance you sho
 t.\n\nTarget 1 at 70m (U21 + Seniors competition distance) should always st
 ay at 70m so Jake can use it for independent practice in between classes.\n
 Target 2 at 60m (U18 + Masters competition distance) \nTargets 3+4 at 50m\n
 Target 5+6 at 40m (U15 competition distance) \nTarget 7+8 at 30m (U13 compe
 tition distance) \nTargets 9 at 20m (for adults who have just graduated out
  of Indoor 2)\nTarget 10 at 13.5m (for juniors who have just graduated out 
 of Indoor 2)\n\nIdeally\, we want to practice with two archers/target to re
 plicate outdoor competition conditions.\n\nTARGET ASSIGNMENTS\nTargets are 
 assigned outdoors in advance to reduce confusion and delay on the day\, so 
 add your name next to your distance below. \nIf you need help or have quest
 ions\, email/text Coach Racae\n(Dotted lines represent tent poles dividing 
 Targets 3\, 6\, and 9.)\n\nATCIOCT = 2026 ATCI Outdoor Competition Team  \n
 MQS at your tournament distance\, 36-arrow rounds on 122-cm target face: \n
 260 pts or 520 pts (2 rounds)\n----------------------------------\n1A. (70m
 )\n1B\n\n2A. (60m)  \n2B\n\n3A. (50m)  Abby Y\n----------------------------
 ------\n3B\n\n4A. (50m) \n4B. \n----------------------------------\n5A. (40
 m) Sara T. (O6 @ 40m)\, 271+268=539\n5B. \n\n6A. (40m) Abby Y\, 290+260=550
 \n----------------------------------\n6B.  Calla K\n\n7A. (30m) Drew S.\n7B
 . \n---------------------------------- \n8A. (30m) \n8B.\n\n9A. (30m) Ellie
  Y\, 256 + 278=534\n----------------------------------\n9B. \n\n10A. (13.5m
 )\n10B
