DESCRIPTION:<b>Scheduling: Classes were changed to 5:30 Weds from now on.</
 b><br><b>What we worked on:</b><br>Anchor/Transfer/Hold -&nbsp\;<br>Keeping
  draw elbow at or slightly above height of shoulder<br>Increase back tensio
 n to 95% at Transfer (moving tension from arms/shoulders into back to start
  to brace the weight of the bow)<br>Expand/Aim -<br>Keep sight aperture abo
 ve yellow (like in the black at 10-12 o´clock) until Expand and then drop i
 t into yellow at Aim<br>Focus -&nbsp\;<br>Keeping mental focus on form posi
 tions - one at a time - even while physically aiming<br>Keep expanding inte
 rnally by opening chest\, compressing back\, or just waiting later for arro
 w to go through the clicker (I´ll let you know when to put one on your bow)
 <br><b>What to practice:</b><br>Anchor / Transfer / Hold / Expand / Aim&nbs
 p\;<br>Try to determine the movement and direction of your draw elbow (what
  muscles move it up and when)<br>It should move very slightly up at Anchor 
 and then horizontally &lt\;1¨ at Transfer as you build back tension<br>Dete
 rmine when you lose focus:<br>o by backtracking into previous position(s) o
 r distractions - break down\, start over<br>o by focusing on target instead
  of form - break down\, start over<br>Take down target to help with focusin
 g on form instead\, but periodically put it back up to see if you can still
  keep your focus.<br><b>Homework:</b><br>Watch video links sent you&nbsp\;
