UID:cgqmacr56grj6b9hc5hjib9kcosjib9o6pgjgb9gcoomcc9m6osm4or568@google.com
X-GOOGLE-CONFERENCE:https://meet.google.com/ugu-awan-qsz
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Chicago:20260408T130000
CREATED:20260310T030602Z
DESCRIPTION:<b>Progress made:</b><br><ul><li>Shoulders down below arrow lin
 e through shot\, and locked down into place</li><li>Sequence and positionin
 g of SET\, SET-UP much improved\, especially height and path of draw elbow 
 and forearm!</li></ul><br><b>What we worked on:</b><br><br><b>Draw forearm<
 /b><br><ul><li>Keep forearm horizontal throughout SET\, SET-UP\, DRAW to LO
 AD</li><li>Raise only hand and forearm at ANCHOR\, not elbow</li></ul><br><
 b>Draw elbow and draw arm</b><br><ul><li>Start with elbow close to side of 
 chest\, so no gap between chest and upper arm. </li><li>Raise elbow at same
  height as forearm\, as one unit<ul><li>forming almost a 90 deg angle betwe
 en forearm and upper arm and upper arm and chest\, and </li><li>coming out 
 from body like a hinge</li></ul></li><li>Moving elbow during SET-UP\, DRAW 
 to LOAD - several ways to think about it<ul><li>around\, using back shoulde
 r as fulcrum\, or </li><li>along an imaginary wall at end of your elbow\, s
 o not lengthening draw\, or </li><li>along an imaginary line parallel to sh
 ooting line</li></ul></li></ul><b>Bouncing </b><br><ul><li>Reduce bouncing 
 during SET-UP\, which occurs when aiming too early in the shot cycle\, so A
 NCHOR is hard to find because your focus is on the target instead of on for
 m.</li></ul><br><b>Adjusting sight</b><br><ul><li>Always set sight based on
  best positioning at full draw (after HOLD) or sight will dictate your posi
 tions and mess up your form!:<ul><li><b>Good horizontal alignments at HOLD\
 ,</b> <ul><li>forming a "T" as much as possible\, </li><li>keeping arrow li
 ne\, and </li><li>bow arm-shoulders-draw elbow alignment</li><li>head posit
 ion level\, neutral\, turned to left as far as comfortable (work on flexibi
 lity)\, no tilting\, raising\, or dropping</li></ul></li><li><b>Eyes</b> al
 ways on center of target (or aiming point when aiming off) until AIM (Step 
 9)</li><li><b>Sight movement: </b><ul><li>above center of target until AIM 
 (Step 9)</li><li>drops down into center using gravity </li><li>should be in
  the yellow at AIM\, but not before <br></li><li>alignment: <b>left to righ
 t: sight-string-riser </b></li></ul></li></ul></li></ul><br><b>Goals until 
 next time:</b><br>Deep focus on shooting enough arrows to make the above mo
 re consistent\, and therefore forming tighter arrow groups in the target ce
 nter.<br><br><b>Next class: April 22 @ 1:00 pm </b> See you then!<br><b><br
 ></b>\n\nJoin with Google Meet: https://meet.google.com/ugu-awan-qsz\n\nLea
 rn more about Meet at: https://support.google.com/a/users/answer/9282720
LAST-MODIFIED:20260527T200302Z
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Virtual Private Lesson with Coach Racae - Madeline
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
