DESCRIPTION:First-time class for juniors age 8+\, optionally their parents\
 , and other adults who would like to try archery for the first time and joi
 n in future Junior Olympic Archery Development (JOAD) and Adult Training cl
 asses.   \n\nThis class is a prerequisite for all other training classes.  
  \n\nIf you have more than one year experience\, contact us for a placement
  evaluation ($45) instead of attending the Indoor 1 Class.   \n\nIf you wou
 ld like to schedule a birthday party during one of the Indoor 1: First-time
  Class times\, the minimum charge for booking the range is $200 for a max. 
 of 10 archers + $5/archer to cover additional supplies (balloons\, etc.). S
 end your request to racae@archerytrainingcenter.com.  \n\nRegistered archer
 s: \n1.  Rhianna Jes...\, adult\n2.  Todd Black...\, adult\n3.  Lukas Car..
 ...\, 9\n4.  Laura Agu....\, adult\n5.  Jamie Agu....\, adult\n6.  \n7.  \n
 8.  \n9.  \n10.   \nWaiting List:   \n\nIf your name is on the waiting list
 \, you have a choice of  coming to see if a place opens up at the last minu
 te\, or  rescheduling your class for another date/time.  We can only take 1
 0 archers on the shooting line at one time.  The instructor may also create
  two shooting lines\, which may increase the length of the class for everyo
 ne and decrease the number of arrows everyone has time to shoot. \nIf you p
 refer not to be on the waiting list\, please reschedule your class for anot
 her date.
